# Bible lexicon: vocabulary and names drawn from the Bible text, sorted by keyword.
# A row with q is not yet confirmed by a speaker of the language; a row without q is confirmed.
a = (i:1) (t:part) (w:the/a/an) (d:prefix placed before a verb, number or describing word to make a noun phrase, as in {a masa}, the first, {a nihna}, the second, and {a thatpa}, the one who kills) particle prefixed to form nouns
a = (i:2) (t:part) (d:particle prefixed to form verb past tense) (r:43.11.35)
A = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:his/her/its/their) (d:the third person marker <a> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or quoted line; before a noun it shows the possessor, his, her, its or their, and before a verb it marks the subject) (s:ama) (b:a) (q:draft)
A = (i:2) (t:part) (d:the prefix <a> written with a capital at the start of a sentence, before a describing word or a noun made from a verb, as in {A nung ciangin}, afterwards, {A mawkna-in}, in vain, and {A beina}, the end) (b:a) (q:draft, low confidence)
aa = (i:1) (t:part) (w:belonging to/of) (d:placed after a possessor to mean what belongs to it; {keima aa} is mine, {nomau aa} is yours, {ko aa} is ours and {Topa aa} is the Lord's) (q:draft)
aai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lot) (d:<ai> written with a long vowel, a lot cast to decide something; {aai saan} is to cast lots) (b:ai) (q:draft)
aak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:rooster/cock) (d:the male domestic fowl; {aak a khuang} means the rooster crows) (s:ak/aklui) (q:draft)
aam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be jealous/jealous) (d:be jealous, unwilling to share with a rival what is one's own; in the verses said of God toward his people, as in {a aam Pasian}, a jealous God) (s:haza) (q:draft)
Aam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:Jealous) (d:<aam>, jealous, written with a capital as a name of God; {ama min Aam} is whose name is Jealous) (b:aam) (q:draft)
aana = (i:1) (t:n) (w:authority/power) (d:the right and power to rule or command; {ukna aana} is ruling authority, {aana nei} is to have authority and {aana zang} is to exercise it) (s:thuneihna) (q:draft)
aana = (i:2) (t:n) (w:force/compulsion) (d:used in {aana tawh}, by force or under orders; {aana tawh na a sem mite} are forced laborers) (s:zawhthawhna/zawhthawh) (q:draft)
Aaron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aaron) (d:brother of Moses, of the tribe of Levi, and the first high priest of Israel) (r:2.4.14)
Aaronte = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Aaron) (d:<Aaron> with the plural <te>, Aaron and the one named with him; {Moses leh Aaronte} is Moses and Aaron together) (b:Aaron) (r:19.99.6)
aat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reap/harvest) (d:<at> written with a long vowel; cut a standing crop, reap, the opposite of <tuh>, sow) (s:anla) (a:tuh) (b:at) (q:draft)
aat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cut) (d:<at> written with a long vowel; cut with a blade; {aat khia} is to cut off) (b:at) (q:draft)
aate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritance/property/possessions) (d:<aa>, what belongs to someone, with the plural <te>; in Numbers 36.4 the land that a family inherits) (s:neihsate/luahna) (b:aa) (q:draft)
Abaddon = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Abaddon) (d:Hebrew name, meaning destruction, of the angel of the Abyss, who is called Apollyon in Greek) (r:66.9.11)
Abagtha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abagtha) (d:one of the seven eunuchs who served King Xerxes) (r:17.1.10)
aban = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:one after another/in turn) (d:used in {aban banin}, adding one thing to another, step by step) (s:banbanin) (q:draft, low confidence)
Abana = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Abana) (d:river of Damascus, named by Naaman together with the Pharpar) (r:12.5.12)
Abarim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Abarim) (d:mountain range in Moab, east of the Jordan, which includes Mount Nebo) (r:4.33.47) (q:draft)
abat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become like/be like) (d:<bat>, be like, with the prefix <a> written joined; {ciangkhut khat abat} is to become as one stick) (b:bat) (q:draft, low confidence)
Abba = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Abba/Father) (d:Aramaic word for father, used in prayer to God and followed by its translation <Pa>, Father) (s:Pa) (r:45.8.15) (q:draft)
Abda = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abda) (d:name of two men: the father of Adoniram, the officer of Solomon over forced labor, and a Levite, the son of Shammua) (r:11.4.6)
Abde = (t:see) <Abde-el>
Abde-el = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdeel) (d:father of Shelemiah, an officer of King Jehoiakim) (r:24.36.26) (q:draft)
Abdeel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdeel) (d:father of Shelemiah, an officer of King Jehoiakim) (r:24.36.26)
Abdi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdi) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite of the clan of Merari and a descendant of Elam in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.26/13.6.44) (q:draft)
Abdiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abdiel) (d:son of Guni and father of Ahi, of the tribe of Gad) (r:13.5.15)
Abdon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/city) (w:Abdon) (d:name of several men, among them a judge of Israel, the son of Hillel from Pirathon, and of a town of the Levites in Asher) (r:13.8.30/6.21.30)
Abednego = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abednego) (d:Babylonian name given to Azariah, one of the three friends of Daniel who were thrown into the blazing furnace) (r:27.3.30/27.3.16)
abei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:last/final) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with the prefix <a> written joined; {abei ni} is the last day, the opposite of {akipat ni}, the first day) (s:tawp/nunung/khakbel) (a:akipat/masapen) (b:bei) (q:draft)
Abel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abel) (d:second son of Adam and Eve, a shepherd killed by his brother Cain; in 2 Samuel 20.18 the town Abel Beth Maakah) (r:1.4.2/1.4.4)
Abelbeth = (t:see) <Abelbeth-ma>
Abelbeth-ma = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Beth Maakah) (d:town in the far north of Israel; the first part of the name, which is written {Abelbeth-ma-akah} in the text) (r:11.15.20) (q:draft)
Abelbethma = (t:see) <Abelbethma-akah>
Abelbethma-akah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Beth Maakah) (d:town in the far north of Israel, near Dan) (r:12.15.29) (q:draft)
Abelbethmaakah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Beth Maakah) (d:town in the far north of Israel, near Dan) (r:10.20.14/11.15.20)
Abelkeramim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abel Keramim) (d:place in the land of the Ammonites, east of the Jordan) (r:7.11.33)
Abelmaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Abel Maim) (d:town in the north of Israel taken by Ben-Hadad, the same as Abel Beth Maakah) (r:14.16.4)
Abelmeholah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abel Meholah) (d:town in the Jordan valley, the home of the prophet Elisha) (r:7.7.22/11.19.16)
Abelmizraim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Abel-mizraim/Abel Mizraim) (d:place near the Jordan where the Egyptians mourned for Jacob, at the threshing floor of Atad) (r:1.50.11)
Abelshittim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abel Shittim) (d:place in the plains of Moab by the Jordan, where Israel camped before entering Canaan) (r:4.33.49)
Abi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abijah/Abi) (d:mother of King Hezekiah and daughter of Zechariah; {Abi} in the Tedim text and Abijah in the NIV) (q:draft)
Abi-albon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abi-Albon) (d:the Arbathite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.31) (q:draft)
Abiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abijah) (d:one of those who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah; Abijah in the NIV) (q:draft)
Abialbon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abi-Albon) (d:the Arbathite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.31)
Abiasaf = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiasaph) (d:son of Korah, of the tribe of Levi) (r:2.6.24)
Abiathar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiathar) (d:priest, son of Ahimelek, who served David together with Zadok) (r:10.20.25/11.4.4)
Abib = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Abib/Aviv) (d:first month of the Hebrew year, the month of the Passover and of the departure from Egypt) (r:2.13.4)
Abida = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abida) (d:son of Midian, grandson of Abraham and Keturah) (r:1.25.4)
Abidan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abidan) (d:son of Gideoni, leader of the tribe of Benjamin in the wilderness) (r:4.1.11/4.10.24)
Abiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiel) (d:name of two men: the grandfather of King Saul, and the Arbathite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:9.14.51/9.9.1)
Abiezer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiezer) (d:name of two men: a descendant of Manasseh, and a warrior of David from Anathoth) (r:10.23.27/13.11.28)
Abigail = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abigail) (d:name of two women: the wife of Nabal of Carmel who became a wife of David, and a sister of David, the mother of Amasa) (r:10.3.3/9.25.23)
Abigailte = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Abigail) (d:<Abigail> with the plural <te>, Abigail and the one named with her; {Ahinoam leh Abigailte} is Ahinoam and Abigail together) (b:Abigail) (r:9.30.5/10.2.2)
Abihail = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Abihail) (d:name of several men and women, among them the father of Queen Esther and the wife of Abishur) (r:13.2.29/4.3.35)
Abihu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abihu) (d:second son of Aaron, a priest who died with his brother Nadab for offering unauthorized fire) (r:4.3.2)
Abihud = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abihud) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin) (r:13.8.3)
Abijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abijah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Samuel, a son of King Jeroboam, and the son of Rehoboam who was king of Judah) (r:9.8.2)
Abijam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abijah) (d:king of Judah, son of Rehoboam and father of Asa; {Abijam} in the Tedim text of 1 Kings and Abijah in the NIV) (r:11.14.31/11.15.1)
Abilene = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Abilene) (d:region northwest of Damascus, ruled by the tetrarch Lysanias) (r:42.3.1)
Abimael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abimael) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.28)
Abimelek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abimelech/Abimelek) (d:name of two rulers: the king of Gerar in the time of Abraham and Isaac, and the son of Gideon who ruled at Shechem) (r:1.20.2/7.9.22)
Abinadab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abinadab) (d:name of several men, among them the second son of Jesse and a son of King Saul) (r:13.2.13/13.8.33)
Abinoam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abinoam) (d:father of Barak) (r:7.4.12/7.5.1)
Abiram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiram) (d:son of Eliab of the tribe of Reuben, who rebelled against Moses with Korah and Dathan) (r:4.16.1/19.106.17)
Abiramte = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Abiram) (d:<Abiram> with the plural <te>, Abiram and the one named with him; {Dathan leh Abiramte} is Dathan and Abiram together) (b:Abiram) (r:4.16.12/4.16.24)
Abishag = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abishag) (d:young woman from Shunem who attended King David in his old age) (r:11.2.21/11.1.15)
Abishai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abishai) (d:son of Zeruiah, brother of Joab, and a commander in the army of David) (r:13.18.12/13.19.11)
Abishua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abishua) (d:name of two men: the son of Phinehas in the line of the high priests, and a son of Bela of Benjamin) (r:13.6.4/13.8.4)
Abishur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abishur) (d:son of Shammai, of the tribe of Judah, and husband of Abihail) (r:13.2.29/13.2.28)
Abital = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Abital) (d:wife of David and mother of Shephatiah) (r:13.3.3/10.3.4)
Abithar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abiathar) (d:spelling of Abiathar in 1 Samuel 30.7, the priest, son of Ahimelek, who served David) (r:9.30.7)
Abiud = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abihud) (d:son of Zerubbabel in the genealogy of Jesus in Matthew) (r:40.1.13)
Abner = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abner) (d:son of Ner and commander of the army of King Saul) (r:10.2.12/9.14.51)
Abrabia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Arabia) (d:spelling of Arabia in 2 Chronicles 9.14, the land whose kings brought gold and silver to Solomon) (r:14.9.14)
Abraham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abraham) (d:ancestor of the people of Israel, husband of Sarah and father of Isaac, first named Abram) (r:1.21.3)
Abram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Abram) (d:the earlier name of Abraham, before God renamed him) (r:1.13.2)
Abronah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abronah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, before Ezion Geber) (r:4.33.34/4.33.35)
Absalom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Absalom) (d:third son of David, who rebelled against his father and was killed by Joab) (r:10.3.3/10.17.26)
Achzib = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Achzib/Akzib) (d:name of two towns, one in the lowland of Judah and one on the coast of Asher; written <Akzib> in the text)
Acil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beginning) (d:{a cil}, the beginning, written as one word at the start of a sentence; {Acil panin} is from the beginning) (s:kipatna/kipatcil/kipattung) (a:tawpna/beina) (q:draft)
ada = (t:see) <i-ada>
Ada = (t:see) <Ada-iah>
Ada-iah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adaiah) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Jedidah, the mother of King Josiah) (r:16.11.5) (q:draft)
Adadah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Adadah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.22)
adah = (t:see) <La-adah>
Adah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Adah) (d:name of two women: a wife of Lamech, and a wife of Esau, the mother of Eliphaz) (r:1.4.19/1.36.10)
adai = (t:see) <Ma-adai>
Adaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adaiah) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Jedidah, the mother of King Josiah, and a Levite ancestor of Asaph) (r:13.6.41/12.22.1)
Adalia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adalia) (d:one of the ten sons of Haman) (r:17.9.7)
Adam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adam) (d:the first man, husband of Eve and father of Cain, Abel and Seth) (r:13.1.1/46.15.22)
Adamah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adamah) (d:fortified town of Naphtali; in Joshua 3.16 the town near Zarethan that the NIV calls Adam) (r:6.19.36)
Adaminekeb = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Adami Nekeb) (d:place on the border of the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.33)
adang = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for)
adangdangte = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:others/the like) (d:<dang>, other, repeated, with the prefix <a> and the plural <te>; the other things of the same kind, and the like) (s:adangte) (b:dangdangte) (q:draft)
adangte = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:others/the others/the rest) (d:<dangte>, the others, with the prefix <a> written joined; the remaining people or things of a group) (s:adangteng/midangte) (b:dangte) (q:draft)
adangteng = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:the rest/all the others) (d:<dang>, other, with the prefix <a> and <teng>, all of; all the rest, all who remain) (s:adangte) (b:dangteng) (q:draft)
Adar = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Adar) (d:the twelfth month of the Hebrew calendar, in which the feast of Purim is kept) (r:17.3.13) (q:draft)
Adbe = (t:see) <Adbe-el>
Adbe-el = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adbeel) (d:third son of Ishmael) (r:13.1.29) (q:draft)
Adbeel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adbeel) (d:third son of Ishmael) (r:1.25.13)
Addan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Addon/Addan) (d:town in Babylonia from which exiles returned with Zerubbabel, Addon in the NIV) (r:16.7.61) (q:draft)
addar = (t:see) <Ataroth-addar>
Addar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Addar) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin) (q:draft)
Addar = (i:2) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Addar) (d:town on the southern border of Judah) (q:draft)
Addi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Addi) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke, father of Melki) (q:draft)
Addon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Addon) (d:town in Babylonia from which exiles returned with Zerubbabel) (r:16.7.61) (q:draft)
adei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:room/chamber) (d:<dei>, room, with the prefix <a> written joined; {adei tungnung} is apparently the upper court of the temple, where the room of Gemariah was) (s:inndei) (b:dei) (q:draft, low confidence)
adiah = (t:see) <Ma-adiah>
adiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:especially/particularly) (d:<diak>, especially, with the prefix <a> written joined; used in {adiak diakin}, most especially, above all) (s:phadiak) (b:diak) (q:draft)
Adiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adiel) (d:name of several men, among them a leader of Simeon, a priest, and the father of Azmaveth, the treasurer of David) (r:13.9.12/13.4.36)
adik = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:right/just) (d:<dik>, right, with the prefix <a> written joined: that which is right; {adik nate} are things that are right) (s:thutang/aman) (a:akhial) (b:dik) (q:draft)
Adin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adin) (d:head of a family that returned from exile, and a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.16/15.8.6) (q:draft)
Adina = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adina) (d:son of Shiza, a chief of the Reubenites and one of the mighty men of David) (r:13.11.42)
ading = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for) (d:placed after a noun or pronoun: for the benefit or use of, on behalf of) (s:nading/dinga) (b:ding) (q:draft)
Ading = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:to/for) (d:<ading>, for, written with a capital in the quoted altar inscription, to an unknown god) (b:ading) (q:draft)
adinga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for/for the sake of) (d:<ading> with the linking ending <a>, for or for the sake of, used before a following verb or noun phrase) (b:ading) (q:draft)
adingin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for) (d:<ading>, for, with the ending <in>: for the benefit or sake of the one named before it) (b:ading) (r:25.3.25) (q:draft)
adingun = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for) (d:<ading>, for, with the plural ending <un>, used when a group is addressed) (b:ading) (q:draft)
Adithaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Adithaim) (d:town in the lowland of Judah) (r:6.15.36)
Adlai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adlai) (d:father of Shaphat, who was over the herds of David in the valleys) (r:13.27.29)
Admah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Admah) (d:city of the plain near Sodom and Gomorrah, destroyed with them) (r:1.14.8/1.10.19)
Admatha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Admatha) (d:one of the seven nobles of Persia and Media closest to King Xerxes) (r:17.1.14)
Admin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Admin) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke, son of Arni and father of Amminadab) (r:42.3.33)
Adna = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adna) (d:name of two men, one who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra and a priest of the family of Harim) (r:15.10.30) (q:draft)
Adnah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adnah) (d:name of two men, a commander of Manasseh who joined David at Ziklag and a commander of Judah under Jehoshaphat) (r:14.17.14/13.12.20)
Adohijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adonijah) (d:Adonijah, the son of David whom Joab supported, as spelled in 1 Kings 2.28) (r:11.2.28)
Adonibezek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoni-Bezek) (d:Canaanite king of Bezek, defeated and captured by the men of Judah) (r:7.1.5/7.1.6)
Adonijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adonijah) (d:name of several men, among them the fourth son of David, born to Haggith, who tried to make himself king) (r:10.3.4/11.1.18)
Adonikam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adonikam) (d:head of a family that returned from the exile in Babylon) (r:15.8.13)
Adoniram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoniram) (d:son of Abda, the official in charge of forced labour under David and Solomon) (r:11.4.6/10.20.24)
Adonizedek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoni-Zedek) (d:king of Jerusalem who led five Amorite kings against Gibeon and was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.10.1/6.10.3)
Adoram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoniram/Adoram) (d:the official in charge of forced labour, stoned to death when King Rehoboam sent him to Israel, Adoniram in the NIV) (q:draft)
Adoram = (i:2) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adoraim) (d:town in Judah fortified by Rehoboam, Adoraim in the NIV) (q:draft)
Adoriam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adoraim) (d:town in Judah fortified by Rehoboam) (r:14.11.9)
Adorniram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoniram) (d:Adoniram, the official of Solomon in charge of forced labour, as spelled in 1 Kings 5.14) (r:11.5.14)
Adramittium = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adramyttium) (d:seaport in the Roman province of Asia, home port of the ship on which Paul began his voyage to Rome) (r:44.27.2)
Adrammelek = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Adrammelek) (d:name of a god of Sepharvaim to whom children were burned, and of a son of Sennacherib who killed his father) (r:12.17.31/23.37.38)
Adriel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adriel) (d:son of Barzillai of Meholah, to whom Merab the daughter of Saul was given as wife) (r:10.21.8/9.18.19)
Adullam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Adullamite) (d:of Adullam, used with <mi> for a person from that town, as Hirah the friend of Judah) (r:1.38.1/1.38.20)
Adullam = (i:2) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Adullam) (d:town in the lowland of Judah, near the cave where David hid from Saul) (r:9.22.1/6.15.35)
Adummim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Adummim) (d:pass on the border between Judah and Benjamin, on the way up from Jericho) (r:6.15.7/6.18.17)
af = (t:see) <Sha-af>
afas = (t:see) <Kai-afas>
Afek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aphek) (d:name of several towns, among them one in the territory of Asher and one where Ben-Hadad gathered to fight Israel) (r:6.19.30/6.12.18)
Afekah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Aphekah) (d:town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.53)
Afiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aphiah) (d:man of Benjamin, ancestor of King Saul) (r:9.9.1)
Afik = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Aphek) (d:town in the territory of Asher whose people were not driven out) (r:7.1.31)
afrah = (t:see) <Bethle-afrah>
After = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ater) (d:Ater, head of a family of temple gatekeepers that returned from exile, as spelled in Ezra 2.42) (r:15.2.42)
Agabas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agabus) (d:Christian prophet from Judea who foretold a great famine and the arrest of Paul) (r:44.21.10/44.11.28)
Agag = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agag) (d:king of the Amalekites, taken alive by Saul) (r:9.15.8)
agate = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:agate) (d:English loanword for a precious stone, used with <suang>, stone, or <suangmanpha>, precious stone) (r:2.28.19) (q:draft)
Agee = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agee) (d:a Hararite, father of Shammah, one of the mighty men of David) (r:10.23.11)
agik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weight) (d:<gik>, heavy, with the prefix <a> written joined: heaviness, weight; <agik tehna> is the measuring of weight) (s:gikzah/gihna) (b:gik) (q:draft)
Agrippa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agrippa) (d:King Herod Agrippa II, before whom Paul made his defence at Caesarea) (r:44.26.19/44.26.27)
Agur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agur) (d:son of Jakeh, whose sayings are in Proverbs 30) (q:draft)
ah = (i:1) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker indicating place or time) (r:1.1.2)
Ahab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahab) (d:king of Israel, son of Omri and husband of Jezebel) (r:11.22.40) (q:draft)
ahang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:reason/cause) (d:<hang>, reason, with the prefix <a> written joined: its reason, the reason for it; {ahang kan} is to ask the reason why) (b:hang) (q:draft)
Aharah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aharah) (d:third son of Benjamin) (r:13.8.1)
Aharhel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aharhel) (d:son of Harum, ancestor of clans of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.8)
Ahasbai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahasbai) (d:father of Eliphelet, one of the mighty men of David) (r:10.23.34)
ahashtari = (t:see) <Ha-ahashtari>
Ahasu = (t:see) <Ahasu-eras>
Ahasu-eras = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Xerxes/Ahasuerus) (d:king of Persia in the book of Esther, and the father of Darius the Mede in Daniel; the NIV writes Xerxes, older English Bibles Ahasuerus) (r:27.9.1) (q:draft)
Ahasueras = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Xerxes/Ahasuerus) (d:king of Persia in the book of Esther, and the father of Darius the Mede in Daniel) (r:27.9.1/15.4.6)
ahau = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:rich) (d:<hau>, rich, with the prefix <a> written joined: the rich; {ahau azawng} is rich and poor alike) (s:sumhau/hausa) (a:azawng) (b:hau) (q:draft)
Ahava = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ahava) (d:place in Babylonia and the canal named after it, where Ezra gathered the exiles before the journey to Jerusalem) (r:15.8.15) (q:draft)
Ahaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahaz) (d:king of Judah, son of Jotham and father of Hezekiah) (r:23.14.28) (q:draft)
Ahaziah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahaziah) (d:name of two kings, the son of Ahab who ruled Israel and the son of Jehoram who ruled Judah) (r:11.22.40/13.3.11)
Ahaziahte = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ahaziahte/Ahaziah) (d:<Ahaziah> with the plural ending <te>, Ahaziah and the kings named with him) (b:Ahaziah) (r:12.12.18)
Ahban = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahban) (d:son of Abishur and Abihail, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.29)
ahem = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:maimed/deformed) (d:<hem>, deformed, with the prefix <a> written joined: one that is maimed; said of an animal unfit for offering) (s:bui) (b:hem) (q:draft)
ahhong = (t:see) <teembaw-ahhong>
ahi = (i:1) (t:ppm) (d:word indicating nominative case)
Ahi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahi) (d:son of Abdiel, head of a family of the tribe of Gad) (q:draft)
AHI = (i:1) (t:v) (w:is/be) (d:<ahi>, is, written in capital letters in an inscription or a name that is set in capitals) (q:draft)
ahia = (i:1) (t:part) (d:sentence final denoting interrogation or exclamation)
Ahiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiah) (d:one of the leaders who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (q:draft)
ahiam = (i:1) (t:part) (d:sentence final denoting interrogation or exclamation)
Ahiam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiam) (d:son of Sharar the Hararite, one of the mighty men of David) (r:10.23.33/13.11.35)
Ahian = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahian) (d:son of Shemida, of the tribe of Manasseh) (r:13.7.19)
Ahiezer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiezer) (d:son of Ammishaddai, leader of the tribe of Dan in the wilderness) (r:4.1.12/4.7.66)
ahih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen/occur) (d:<a> with <hih>, the form of <hi>, be, used before <ciangin>, <leh>, <manin> and <hangin>: it being so, this having happened)
ahih = (i:2) (t:n) (w:task)
ahih hangin = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:even so/however/still) (s:ahita)
ahih hangin = (i:3) (t:conj) (w:yet) (s:hitaseleh)
ahih hangin = (i:4) (t:conj) (w:nevertheless/nonetheless) (s:ahita)
ahihciangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:therefore/so) (d:{ahih ciangin} written as one word; {tua ahihciangin} is that being so, therefore) (q:draft)
ahihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to be/be the case) (d:<a> with <hih>, the form of <hi>, be, used before a suffix, and <khak>, happen to; {ahihkhak leh} is if it should be so) (s:hikha) (q:draft)
ahihlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:that it is/that it was) (d:{a hih lam} written as one word, the fact of being so, mostly before <thei>, <phawk> or <mu>: know, realize or see that it is) (q:draft)
ahihleh = (i:2) (t:part) (d:particle comparison between verbs to delineate their relationship)
ahihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not be) (d:<hihloh>, not being, with the prefix <a> written as one word; {ahihleh ahihloh} is whether it is so or not, and <ahihloh hangin> is although it is not) (b:hihloh) (q:draft)
ahihlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:not being) (d:<ahihloh>, not being, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact that something is not so, used where English says that it is not) (s:hihlohna) (b:ahihloh) (r:48.1.11) (q:draft)
ahihna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the fact that something is so; placed after a clause that is the object of a verb of knowing, seeing or showing, where English says that) (b:ahih) (q:draft)
ahihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who do/doers) (d:The verb <hih>, do, with the prefix <a> and the plural <te>: the people who do the thing named before it, as in {mawhna ahihte}, those who sin.) (s:bawlte) (b:ahih) (q:draft)
Ahihub = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahihud) (d:spelling of Ahihud in 1 Chronicles 8.7, a man of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.7)
Ahihud = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahihud) (d:name of two men: a leader of the tribe of Asher, son of Shelomi, who helped divide the land, and a man of Benjamin) (r:4.34.27/13.8.7)
Ahijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahijah) (d:name of several men, among them a priest in the time of Saul, the prophet of Shiloh, and one of David's warriors) (r:9.14.3/13.11.36)
Ahikam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ahikam) (d:son of Shaphan, an official of King Josiah who protected Jeremiah, and father of Gedaliah) (r:24.26.24/24.40.6)
ahilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teach/taught) (d:The verb <hilh>, teach, written together with the preceding <a>, the third person marker; it is usually written {a hilh}.) (s:thuhilh/sinsak) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
Ahilud = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahilud) (d:father of Jehoshaphat, the recorder of David and Solomon) (r:10.8.16)
Ahima = (t:see) <Ahima-az>
Ahima-az = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimaaz) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Zadok the priest, and a son-in-law of Solomon who was governor in Naphtali) (r:9.14.50/13.6.8) (q:draft)
Ahima-za = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimaaz) (d:spelling of Ahimaaz in 2 Samuel 18.22, the son of Zadok the priest who ran with news to David) (q:draft)
Ahimaaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimaaz) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Zadok the priest, and a son-in-law of Solomon who was governor in Naphtali) (r:13.6.8)
Ahiman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiman) (d:name of two men: one of the three sons of Anak driven out of Hebron by Caleb, and a Levite gatekeeper) (r:6.15.14)
Ahimelek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimelek) (d:name of two priests: the priest at Nob who helped David and was killed by Saul, and a son of Abiathar) (r:10.8.17)
Ahimoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahimoth) (d:Levite of the line of Kohath, a son of Elkanah) (r:13.6.25)
Ahinadab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahinadab) (d:son of Iddo, one of Solomon's twelve district governors, at Mahanaim) (r:11.4.14)
ahing = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:alive/living) (d:The word <hing>, alive, with the prefix <a> written as one word: who is alive, that lives; {ahing tawntung} is living or lasting for ever.) (s:anungta/nungta/hinglai) (a:sisa) (b:hing) (q:draft)
Ahinoam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Ahinoam) (d:name of two women: a wife of David from Jezreel, the mother of Amnon, and the wife of Saul) (r:9.25.43/10.3.2)
Ahio = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahio) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Abinadab who walked in front of the cart carrying the ark) (r:10.6.3)
ahipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one who is/he who is) (d:The verb <ahi>, is, with <pa>, the male one: it closes a describing phrase and is said of God, as in {Pasian ahipa}, the one who is God.) (s:hipa) (b:ahi) (q:draft)
Ahira = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahira) (d:son of Enan, leader of the tribe of Naphtali in the wilderness) (r:4.1.15/4.10.27)
Ahiram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahiram) (d:son of Benjamin, ancestor of the Ahiramite clan) (r:4.26.38)
Ahisamak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahisamach/Ahisamak) (d:man of the tribe of Dan, father of the craftsman Oholiab) (r:2.31.6)
Ahishar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahishar) (d:official in charge of Solomon's palace; in 1 Chronicles 7.10 the name stands for Ahishahar, a man of Benjamin) (r:11.4.6)
ahita = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:nevertheless/even so) (d:The verb <ahi>, be, with <ta>; it is used in {ahita zongin}, which means even so or nevertheless.) (s:ahih hangin) (b:ahi) (q:draft)
ahite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are/the ones that are) (d:The verb <ahi>, be, with the plural <te>, turning the words before it into a noun: {innkuan lutang ahite} is those who are heads of families, {kham ahite} is the things that are of gold.) (s:hite) (b:ahi) (r:6.22.14) (q:draft)
Ahithofel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahithophel) (d:man of Giloh, David's counselor, who joined Absalom's revolt) (r:10.15.12/10.23.34)
Ahitub = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahitub) (d:name of several priests, among them the grandson of Eli who was the father of Ahimelek, and the father of Zadok) (r:9.14.3/13.6.7)
ahizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to be/be possible) (d:The verb <ahi>, be, with <zo>, be able: {ahizo nawn lo} is no longer able to be, and {ahizo zahzahin} is as far as is possible.) (s:hithei) (b:ahi) (q:draft)
Ahlab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ahlab) (d:town in the territory of Asher whose people were not driven out) (r:7.1.31)
Ahlai = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ahlai) (d:name of two people: a child of Sheshan in the line of Judah, and the parent of Zabad, one of David's warriors) (r:13.2.31/13.11.41)
Ahoah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahoah) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin, ancestor of the Ahohite clan) (r:13.8.4)
Ahoh = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ahoh/Ahohite) (d:ancestor named in {Ahoh-te beh}, the Ahohite clan of Benjamin, to which several of David's warriors belonged) (r:13.11.29/13.27.4)
ahoih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:good/what is good) (d:The word <hoih>, good, with the prefix <a>: that which is good, the good one; {ahoih nate} is good things, and {ahoih ahoih lo} is whether good or bad.) (s:apha/pha) (a:asia/hoihlo/gilo) (b:hoih) (q:draft)
ahoihin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:well/rightly) (d:The word <ahoih>, what is good, with the suffix <in>: in a good way; {ahoihin gamta} is do what is right.) (s:phatakin) (a:sialamin) (b:ahoih) (q:draft)
ahoihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good ones/good things) (d:The word <ahoih>, that which is good, with the plural suffix <te>: the good ones; {gamtatna ahoihte} is good deeds.) (s:phate/hoihnate) (a:siatnate) (b:ahoih) (q:draft)
ahoihzaw = (t:see) <ahoihzaw-in>
ahoihzaw-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:better/even better/even more) (d:The word <hoih>, good, with the prefix <a>, <zaw>, more, and the suffix <in>: in a better way, even better than what is named before <sangin>.) (q:draft)
Ahserah = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Asherah) (d:spelling of Asherah in 2 Kings 13.6, a Canaanite goddess and the wooden pole set up for her worship) (r:12.13.6)
ahsiampi = (t:see) <mai-ahsiampi>
Ahumai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahumai) (d:son of Jahath, of the Zorathite clans of Judah) (r:13.4.2)
ahun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the time/the hour/opportunity) (d:The word <hun>, time, with the prefix <a>: its time, the right time; {ahun hong tung ding} is the time will come, and {ahun hunin} is from time to time.) (b:hun) (q:draft)
Ahuzzam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahuzzam) (d:son of Ashhur and Naarah, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.6)
Ahuzzath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahuzzath) (d:adviser of Abimelek king of Gerar, who came with him to Isaac) (r:1.26.26)
Ahzai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahzai) (d:priest, son of Meshillemoth and ancestor of Amashsai) (r:16.11.13)
ai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lot) (d:A lot cast to decide something; {ai saan} is to cast lots, and {ai a pha} is the one on which the lot falls.) (s:aii/aai/aisaan) (r:19.22.18) (q:draft)
ai = (i:2) (t:n) (w:divination/witchcraft) (d:Divination or witchcraft; {ai saan} is to practise divination, and {ai saan thei} is one who divines or casts spells.) (s:aisan) (q:draft)
Ai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ai) (d:Canaanite city east of Bethel, taken and burned by Joshua) (r:6.8.23) (q:draft)
Ai-ath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aiath) (d:place in Benjamin on the route of the Assyrian army toward Jerusalem, probably the same as Ai) (q:draft)
Aiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aiah) (d:name of two men: a son of Zibeon the Horite, and the father of Rizpah, Saul's concubine) (r:13.1.40/10.21.11)
Aiath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aiath) (d:place in Benjamin on the route of the Assyrian army toward Jerusalem, probably the same as Ai) (r:23.10.28)
aii = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lot) (d:A lot drawn or cast to decide a share, the same word as <ai>; {aii sawk} is to draw lots, and {aii kia} is the lot falls.) (s:ai/aai/aisaan) (q:draft)
Aiialon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Aijalon) (d:spelling of Aijalon in Joshua 19.42, a town in the territory of Dan) (r:6.19.42)
Aija = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aija) (d:town of Benjamin near Bethel where people lived after the exile, probably the same as Ai) (q:draft)
Aijalon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aijalon) (d:name of two places: a Levite town in the territory of Dan with a valley of the same name, and a town in Zebulun where Elon was buried) (r:7.12.12/13.6.69)
aikam = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (s:momai/mom-ai) (q:draft)
aikamte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpions) (s:momaite) (b:aikam) (q:draft)
aikungte = (t:see) <zawl-aikungte>
Ain = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ain) (d:town in the south of Judah, given to Simeon; also a place on the eastern border of Canaan) (r:6.19.7/13.4.32)
Aineas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aeneas) (d:paralysed man at Lydda who was healed by Peter) (r:44.9.33/44.9.34)
Ainon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Aenon) (d:place near Salim with much water, where John baptized) (r:43.3.23)
aisaan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lot/allotment) (d:The lot that is cast to decide something, and the share that falls to someone by it; {aisaan sagihna} is the seventh lot.) (s:ai/aii/aai) (q:draft)
aisaan = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cast lots/divine) (d:To decide or find out something by casting lots; {lai aisaan-in} is by casting lots, and {aisaan man} is the fee for divination.) (q:draft)
aisaana = (i:1) (t:n) (w:casting of lots/lot) (d:A spelling of <aisaanna>, the casting of lots, built on <aisaan>; {aisaana tawh} is by lot.) (s:aisaanna) (b:aisaan) (q:draft)
aisaanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:casting lots/by casting lots) (d:The verb <aisaan>, cast lots, with the suffix <in>: by casting lots; {lai aisaanin} has the same meaning.) (b:aisaan) (q:draft)
aisaanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:casting of lots/lot) (d:The verb <aisaan>, cast lots, with the noun suffix <na>: deciding or sharing out something by lot; {aisaanna tawh} is by lot.) (s:aisaana) (b:aisaan) (r:13.24.7) (q:draft)
Aisaante = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Aisaante) (d:the diviners, written with a capital in {Aisaante’ Tawsaw}, the diviners' tree near Shechem) (r:7.9.37)
aisan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:divination/sorcery/secret arts) (d:Seeking hidden knowledge by lots, omens or magic; {aisan siam}, {aisan thei} and {aisan mi} are a diviner or sorcerer.) (s:ai/mitphial/khongkhai) (b:ai) (r:27.2.27) (q:draft)
aisanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:by divination/by fortune-telling) (d:The word <aisan>, divination, with the suffix <in>: by means of divination or fortune-telling.) (b:aisan) (q:draft)
aisanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:necromancer/divination/casting of lots) (d:<aisan> with the noun suffix <na>: the practice of divination; {aisanna tawh} is by lot) (b:aisan)
aisannate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sorceries/witchcraft) (d:Acts of sorcery or divination, <aisanna> with the plural <te>.) (s:bumnate) (b:aisanna) (q:draft)
aisannu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sorceress/witch) (d:The word <aisan>, divination or sorcery, with <nu> marking a woman: a woman who practises sorcery.) (b:aisan) (q:draft)
aisanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:diviner/soothsayer) (d:The word <aisan>, divination, with <pa> marking a man: a man who practises divination.) (b:aisan) (q:draft)
aisante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:diviners/spiritists/sorcerers) (d:The word <aisan>, divination, with the plural <te>: those who practise divination or magic, often named together with <vankahte>, mediums.) (s:saante/khongkhaite) (b:aisan) (q:draft)
Aisante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:diviners) (d:The word <aisante>, diviners, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a place name, as in the diviners' tree.) (b:aisante) (q:draft)
aitawi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:exorcist/sorcerer) (d:The word <ai>, divination or charm, with <tawi>, hold: one who practises spirit arts; in Acts 19.13 it is said of Jews who went about driving out evil spirits.) (q:draft, low confidence)
aite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:charms/amulets/magic charms) (d:Plural of <ai>: objects worn or tied on for magic or divination.) (b:ai) (q:draft)
aituam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:own/personal/private) (d:It follows a possessor and stresses that the thing belongs to that person alone: {ama aituam} is his own, and {ama aituam dingin} is for himself.) (q:draft)
ak = (i:2) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:raven/crow) (d:The second part of <va-ak>, raven or crow.) (r:19.147.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
