akici = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be called/so-called) (d:The verb <kici>, be called, with the prefix <a> written joined: that is called, so-called; {pasian akici} are those that are called gods.) (b:kici) (q:draft)
akihisak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:proud/arrogant/haughty) (d:Proud or arrogant, from <kihisak>, be proud, with the prefix <a> written joined; {akihisak mite} are the proud.) (a:lungsimniam) (b:kihisak) (q:draft)
akilawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fitting/proper/deserving/reasonable) (d:Fitting, proper or deserved, from <kilawm> with the prefix <a> written as one word; {sihna thuak ding akilawm} is deserving of death, and {akilawm kei hi} is it is not reasonable.) (b:kilawm) (q:draft)
akiman = (t:see) <akiman'na>
akiman'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:use/worth/benefit) (d:<kiman>, be of use, with the prefix <a> and the noun suffix <na>; {bangmah akiman’na om lo} is there is nothing of worth in it) (s:kimanna/phattuamna) (q:draft, low confidence)
akipan = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:from/since/beginning with) (d:marks the starting point in time, place or a list, often after <pan>; {amah akipan a innkuanpihte} means him and all his household) (s:panin/pan) (a:dong/dongin) (b:kipan) (q:draft)
akipanin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:from/since/beginning with) (d:{a kipanin} written as one word; follows the time or thing that is the starting point) (s:panin/pan) (a:dong/dongin) (b:akipan) (q:draft)
akipat = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:first/beginning) (d:<kipat>, begin, with the prefix <a> written joined; {akipat ni} is the first day) (s:masapen) (a:abei) (b:kipat) (q:draft)
akipawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined with/be associated with/go with) (d:<kipawl>, associate, with the prefix <a> written as one word, placed after <tawh> and before a noun: that is joined with, that goes with) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
akisa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be about to/be ready) (d:Be about to do something, from <kisa>, get ready, with the prefix <a> written joined; {thu dong dinga akisa mite} are those who were about to question him.) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prepare/get ready/be about to) (d:the prefix <a> written together with <kisak>, a form of <kisa> get ready; {pai dinga akisak lai takin}, just as he was getting ready to go) (b:kisak) (q:draft, low confidence)
