ankuang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dish/bowl/feeding trough/table) (d:<an>, food, with <kuang>, bowl or trough: the vessel that food is eaten from, and so the table one eats at; {bawng ankuang} is a manger for cattle) (s:kuang) (q:draft)
