Apfia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Apphia) (d:Christian woman greeted in the letter of Paul to Philemon) (r:57.1.2)
apha = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:good) (d:{a pha} written as one word; also stands alone as that which is good) (s:ahoih) (a:asia) (b:pha) (q:draft)
aphuai = (t:see) <bil-aphuai>
apian = (t:see) <apian'cil>
apian'cil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creation/beginning) (d:the time something first came into being: {a pian} come into being, with <cil> beginning; {lei apian'cil a kipan}, since the creation of the world) (s:piancil) (q:draft)
apiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be born/be descended) (d:the prefix <a> written together with <piang>, be born or come into being; {mi thagolte sung panin apiang} is one born from among the giants) (b:piang) (q:draft)
apin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hand over/entrust/deliver) (d:<ap>, give into the charge of someone, with the linking ending <in>, used when another action follows) (b:ap) (q:draft)
apin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:consecrate/dedicate) (d:<ap> in the sense of setting apart for God, with the linking ending <in>) (s:siangthosakin) (b:ap) (q:draft)
Apis = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Apis) (d:the sacred bull god of Egypt, named in the prophecy of Jeremiah against Egypt) (q:draft)
apkhapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:panic/terror) (d:sudden great fear that spreads among many people) (s:patauhna) (q:draft)
apkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dedicate together/consecrate together) (d:<ap>, dedicate, with <khawm>, together: dedicate or consecrate along with other things or people) (b:ap) (q:draft)
apkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hand back/give back/return) (d:<ap>, hand over or entrust, with <kik>, back) (s:piakik) (b:ap) (q:draft)
Apkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dedication/rededication) (d:<apkik>, hand back, with the noun suffix <na>; {Biakinn Apkikna Pawi} is the Festival of Dedication of the temple) (q:draft)
apna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dedication/consecration) (d:the act of giving something over to God or to a sacred use; often written {ki-apna}, being dedicated) (b:ap) (q:draft)
apnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those entrusted) (d:<ap>, hand over or entrust, with <na> and the plural <te>: here the people into whose hands the money was given) (b:ap) (q:draft, low confidence)
Apollion = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Apollyon) (d:Greek name, meaning Destroyer, of the angel of the Abyss, who is called Abaddon in Hebrew) (r:66.9.11)
Apollonia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Apollonia) (d:city in Macedonia through which Paul passed on the way to Thessalonica) (r:44.17.1)
Apollos = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Apollos) (d:learned Jew from Alexandria who taught in Ephesus and Corinth) (r:44.18.24/46.3.6)
appa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who dedicates) (d:<ap>, dedicate, with {-pa}, a man: the man who dedicates something) (b:ap) (q:draft)
