apple = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:apple) (d:English loanword; {apple gah} is the fruit and {apple kung} the tree) (s:epel) (q:draft)
Appolos = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Apollos) (d:spelling of <Apollos> in Titus 3:13, the fellow worker whom Titus is to help on his way) (r:56.3.13)
apsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dedicated/devoted/consecrated) (d:<ap> with <sa>, already done: given over to God or to a sacred purpose) (s:sianthosaksa/tuamkoihsa) (b:ap) (q:draft)
apsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have handed over/cause to entrust) (d:<ap>, hand over or entrust, with <sak>, cause: have something handed over to someone) (b:ap) (q:draft)
apsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dedicated things) (d:<apsa>, dedicated, with the plural <te>: the things that someone has dedicated) (b:apsa) (q:draft)
apte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things handed over/things entrusted/pledges) (d:<ap>, hand over or entrust, with plural <te>: {khapna van a apte} is the things given in pledge, {ka apte} is what I handed over) (b:ap) (r:26.18.16) (q:draft)
aptheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to hand over/be able to present) (d:<ap>, hand over or dedicate, with <theih>, be able, used before <nading>) (b:ap) (q:draft)
