Ashtaroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashtaroth) (d:city in Bashan where King Og reigned, later given to the half-tribe of Manasseh) (r:6.13.12/6.13.31)
Ashtarothah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ashtaroth) (d:<Ashtaroth> with the place marker <ah>: in Ashtaroth, the city of King Og of Bashan) (b:Ashtaroth) (r:6.9.10)
Ashterath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashterath) (d:home town of Uzzia, one of David's mighty warriors, called the Ashterathite in the NIV) (r:13.11.44)
Ashteroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ashteroth-karnaim/Ashteroth Karnaim) (d:first part of {Ashteroth-Karnaim}, a place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Rephaites) (r:1.14.5)
Ashtoreth = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ashtoreth) (d:goddess of the Sidonians, whom Solomon worshipped and for whom he built a high place) (r:11.11.5/12.23.13)
Ashur = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ashur) (d:Assyria, the power named in the oracles of Balaam; also the Ashurites over whom Ish-Bosheth was made king) (r:4.24.22)
Ashurbanipal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashurbanipal) (d:king of Assyria who deported peoples and settled them in Samaria) (r:15.4.10)
Ashvath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashvath) (d:son of Japhlet, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.33)
asia = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:evil/bad/wrong) (d:<sia>, bad, with the prefix <a> written as one word: that which is bad or evil, often paired with <apha>, good; {asia-a gamta} is to act wickedly) (s:gilo/hoihlo) (a:apha/ahoih) (b:sia) (q:draft)
Asia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Asia) (d:the Roman province of Asia in the west of Asia Minor, usually written {Asia gam}) (r:44.2.9) (q:draft)
asiel = (t:see) <Ja-asiel>
Asiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asiel) (d:ancestor of Jehu, a clan leader of the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.35)
Asinkritas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asyncritus) (d:Christian in Rome greeted by Paul) (r:45.16.14)
Asiria = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Assyria) (d:the Assyrian empire, whose king threatened Jerusalem in the days of Hezekiah; also spelled <Assiria>) (r:12.18.30)
Askhelon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashkelon) (d:Philistine city taken by the tribe of Judah; also spelled <Ashkelon>) (r:7.1.18)
Asnah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asnah) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.50)
Aspatha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aspatha) (d:one of the ten sons of Haman killed by the Jews) (r:17.9.7)
Asriel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Asriel) (d:descendant of Manasseh and ancestor of the Asrielite clan) (r:13.7.14/4.26.31)
asseiah = (t:see) <Ma-asseiah>
Asshur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ashur) (d:son of Shem and ancestor of the Assyrians; also the land of Assyria as a trading partner of Tyre) (r:1.10.22)
Asshurim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Ashurites) (d:people descended from Dedan, a grandson of Abraham and Keturah) (r:1.25.3)
Assir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Assir) (d:name of two Levites of the line of Kohath, a son of Korah and a son of Ebiasaph) (r:2.6.24/13.6.22) (q:draft)
Assiri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ashur/Assyria) (d:Assyria, named as the direction in which the land of the descendants of Ishmael lay) (r:1.25.18) (q:draft)
Assiria = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Assyria) (d:empire on the upper Tigris with its capital at Nineveh, which conquered the northern kingdom of Israel) (r:1.2.14)
Assiriate = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Assyrians) (d:the people of Assyria) (b:Assiria) (r:24.2.36/23.14.25)
Assos = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Assos) (d:seaport in the Roman province of Asia where Paul rejoined his companions) (r:44.20.14/44.20.13)
Astaroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ashtaroth) (d:city in Bashan given to the Gershonite Levites; also spelled <Ashtaroth>) (r:13.6.71)
asu = (t:see) <Ja-asu>
asungkuate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:internal organs/entrails/inner parts) (d:<sungkuate>, the inner organs of an animal, with the prefix <a> written together: its internal organs, named in the laws of offerings) (b:sungkuate) (q:draft)
asusia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy) (d:<susia>, destroy, with the prefix <a> written together; {leitung asusia dingin} is in order to destroy the earth) (s:siasak/siatsak) (b:susia) (q:draft)
at = (i:3) (t:v) (w:write/write down/inscribe) (d:put something in writing, used beside <gelh>; with <lai>, writing, it forms {lai-at}, secretary) (s:gelh/laigelh) (q:draft)
Atad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Atad) (d:name attached to a threshing floor near the Jordan where Joseph mourned seven days for Jacob) (r:1.50.10)
atak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truly/especially) (d:<tak>, true, with the prefix <a> written together; {atak takin ci leeng}, to speak truly, introduces a point that is especially true) (s:taktakin) (b:tak) (q:draft, low confidence)
atam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quantity/amount) (d:<tam>, many, with the prefix <a> written together: how much there is, quantity; {atam tehna} is the measuring of quantity) (s:omzah) (b:tam) (q:draft)
Atarah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Atarah) (d:second wife of Jerahmeel and mother of Onam) (r:13.2.26)
Ataroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ataroth) (d:name of several towns, among them one built up by the Gadites east of the Jordan and one on the border of Ephraim) (r:4.32.34/4.32.3)
Ataroth-addar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ataroth Addar) (d:town on the border between Ephraim and Benjamin, on the hill south of Lower Beth Horon) (r:6.16.5) (q:draft)
Atarothaddar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ataroth Addar) (d:town on the border between Ephraim and Benjamin; also written <Ataroth-addar>) (r:6.18.13/6.16.5)
atawntungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:forever/for ever) (d:<tawntungin>, continually, with the prefix <a> written as one word: for all time, forever) (s:paisuak/ngitnget) (a:tawlkhat) (b:tawntungin) (q:draft)
ate = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the linking <a> with plural <te> after a word of place or time, those of or the ones at, as {nuai-ate} those below and {nidang-ate} those of former days) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ater = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ater) (d:name of two men, the ancestor of a family that returned from the exile and a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:15.2.16/16.10.17)
ath = (t:see) <Mefa-ath>
Athaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Athaiah) (d:son of Uzziah, a descendant of Judah who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:16.11.4)
athaim = (t:see) <Kushan-rish-athaim>
athak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:new) (d:<thak>, new, with the prefix <a>, that which is new, the new one; paired with <alui>, the old) (a:alui) (b:thak) (q:draft)
Athak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Athak) (d:a town in Judah to which David sent a share of the plunder) (q:draft)
Athaliah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Athaliah) (d:queen of Judah, mother of King Ahaziah, who seized the throne; also the name of two men) (r:12.11.1)
Atharim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Atharim) (d:place in the Negev on the road by which Israel approached Canaan) (r:4.21.1)
athau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fat/its fat) (d:<thau>, fat, written together with <a>, its: the fat of an animal brought as an offering) (s:sathau) (b:thau) (q:draft)
Athen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Athens) (d:chief city of Greece, where Paul spoke at the Areopagus) (r:44.18.1/44.17.22)
Athlai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Athlai) (d:descendant of Bebai who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.28)
atin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reaping/cutting) (d:<at>, reap or cut, with the linking ending <in>, used before a following verb; {ki-atin} is being cut or circumcised) (a:tuhin/vawhin) (b:at) (q:draft)
atkeh = (t:see) <ki-atkeh>
atkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut off/cut away) (d:<at>, cut, with <khia>, out or off: cut a part off or away) (s:attan/satkhia/tan) (b:at) (q:draft)
atkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut off) (d:<at>, cut, with <khiat>, off or away; the form of <atkhia> used before <sak>, <manin> and similar words) (b:atkhia) (q:draft)
atkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut off) (d:<at>, cut, and <khiat>, off, with <sak>: cut a part off something that belongs to another, as the corner of a robe) (b:atkhiat) (q:draft)
atkhiatsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cutting off/cut off) (d:<at>, cut, with <khiat>, off, <sak>, do to someone, and the suffix <in>: cutting a part off a person) (b:atkhiatsak) (q:draft)
atkhiatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cutting off) (d:<atkhiatsak>, cut off, with the noun suffix <na>: the cutting off of a part, here of garments) (b:atkhiatsak) (q:draft)
atkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:write again/rewrite) (d:<at>, write, with <kik>, again: write something out a second time) (s:gelhkik) (b:at) (q:draft)
atmang = (t:see) <ki-atmang>
atna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:circumcision/cutting) (d:noun of <at>, cut; {vun atna}, cutting of the skin, is circumcision) (s:vunatna) (b:at) (q:draft)
atna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:reaping/harvest) (d:noun of <at>, reap: the reaping of what someone has sown) (s:anlak) (b:at) (q:draft, low confidence)
atnate = (t:see) <sing-atnate>
atnen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut up/chop finely/slice) (d:<at>, cut, with <nen>, fine: cut something up into small pieces) (s:semnen) (q:draft)
atnente = (t:see) <ki-atnente>
Atoroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Atroth) (d:first part of <Atoroth-shofan>, a town built up by the Gadites) (r:4.32.35)
Atoroth-shofan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Atroth Shophan) (d:town east of the Jordan built up by the Gadites) (r:4.32.35) (q:draft)
atpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scribe/secretary/writer) (d:found in {lai-atpa}, from <lai>, writing, and <at>, write, with <pa> marking a man: one who writes, a scribe or secretary) (s:thuvanpipa) (r:13.24.6) (q:draft)
Atroth = (t:see) <Atroth-bethjoab>
Atroth-bethjoab = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Atroth Beth Joab) (d:clan or town of Judah listed among the descendants of Salma) (r:13.2.54) (q:draft)
Atrothbethjoab = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Atroth Beth Joab) (d:clan or town of Judah listed among the descendants of Salma; also written <Atroth-bethjoab>) (r:13.2.54)
Atrothshofan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Atroth Shophan) (d:town east of the Jordan built up by the Gadites; also written <Atoroth-shofan>) (r:4.32.35)
atsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:reaped/harvested/cut) (d:<at>, reap or cut, with <sa>, already done: {buhlom atsa}, cut sheaves; with <vun> and the prefix <ki>, {vun ki-atsa}, circumcised) (b:at) (q:draft)
atsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:circumcise/have cut) (d:<at>, cut, with <sak>, cause: have something cut; with <vun>, skin, it is the expression for circumcise someone) (s:vunat) (b:at) (q:draft)
atsat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut through/sever/hamstring) (d:<at>, cut, with <sat>, strike: cut through; {zagui atsat} is to cut the leg sinew of a horse, hamstring) (s:sattat) (q:draft)
Attai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Attai) (d:name of several men, among them a grandson of Sheshan of Judah and a Gadite warrior who joined David) (r:13.2.36/13.12.11)
Attalia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Attalia) (d:seaport in Pamphylia from which Paul and Barnabas sailed back to Antioch) (r:44.14.25)
attan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut off/sever) (d:cut through so that a part comes off, as thumbs, a tail or a tongue; {ngawng attan} is break or cut the neck) (s:sattan/tan/atkhia) (q:draft)
attatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hamstring/cut through/sever) (d:<at>, cut, and <tat>, sever, with <sak>: cut right through; {a zagui attatsak} is to cut their leg sinews, hamstring) (s:sattat/atsat) (q:draft)
atte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the circumcised) (d:<at>, cut, with the plural suffix <te>, in {vun atte}, those whose skin is cut, the circumcised) (s:vunatte) (b:at) (q:draft)
atte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:reapers/harvesters) (d:<at>, reap, with the plural suffix <te>, those who cut the grain, as in {buh atte} and {an atte}) (s:anlate) (b:at) (q:draft)
atte = (i:3) (t:n) (w:secretaries/scribes/writers) (d:<at>, write, with the plural suffix <te>, second part of {lai-atte}, those who write, the secretaries of a king) (s:laigelhte) (b:at) (q:draft)
attem = (t:see) <sing-attem>
atual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:court/courtyard) (d:<tual>, courtyard, with the prefix <a> written together; {atual sungnung} is the inner court of the temple) (b:tual) (q:draft)
atuam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:different/various/separate) (d:<tuam>, separate, with the prefix <a>; usually doubled as {atuam atuam}, of different kinds, each its own) (s:apawlpawl/pawlpawl) (a:kibang/kikim) (b:tuam) (q:draft)
atuamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:separately/apart/in various ways) (d:<atuam>, separate or different, with the adverb ending <in>; doubled as {atuam atuamin}, each separately, in various ways) (s:tuamtuamin) (a:khawmin) (b:atuam) (q:draft)
atuamte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:various/different) (d:<atuam>, different or separate, with the plural <te>; the doubled {atuam atuamte} means of many different kinds) (b:atuam) (q:draft)
atuamtuam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:various/different/of different kinds) (d:<tuamtuam>, different, with the prefix <a> written together: of different kinds, each one different from the other) (s:apawlpawl/pawlpawl) (a:kibang) (b:tuamtuam) (q:draft)
atul = (t:see) <atul-amakin>
atul-amakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in thousands upon thousands/in countless numbers) (d:in numbers too great to count; <atul> is {a tul}, a thousand, and the part {amak} is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
atung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:above/top) (d:<tung>, top or upper side, with the prefix <a> written together; {atung lam nate} are the things above) (a:nuailam) (b:tung) (q:draft)
Augustas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Augustus) (d:Caesar Augustus, the Roman emperor who ordered the census at the time of the birth of Jesus) (r:42.2.1)
Augustus = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Augustus) (d:name of the Roman emperor; {Augustus pawl} is the Imperial Regiment to which the centurion Julius belonged) (r:44.27.1)
ausan = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:scarlet/crimson) (d:bright red, of dyed yarn and cloth, named together with <dum>, blue, and <dupsan>, purple) (q:draft)
autok = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lobe of the liver) (d:the lobe on the liver of a sacrificed animal, the prefix <a> and <utok> written as one word) (b:utok) (q:draft)
avan = (t:see) <Za-avan>
aven = (t:see) <Beth-aven>
Aven = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Aven) (d:valley in Syria named beside Damascus, in {Aven Kuam}, the Valley of Aven) (q:draft)
Avith = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Avith) (d:city of Hadad son of Bedad, a king of Edom) (r:1.36.35/13.1.46)
Avva = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Avva) (d:place from which the king of Assyria brought settlers to the towns of Samaria) (r:12.17.24)
Avvim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Avvim) (d:town in the territory of Benjamin; also the Avvites, a people who lived in villages as far as Gaza) (r:6.18.23)
aw = (i:1) (t:part) (w:O) (d:vocative particle placed after the name or title of the one addressed) (r:1.49.18)
aw = (i:2) (t:n) (w:voice/sound) (d:the voice of a person or of God, and the sound of an instrument) (s:awging/kamging)
Aw = (i:1) (t:intj) (w:O) (d:exclamation of address, here written with a capital and placed before the one addressed) (s:O) (b:aw) (q:draft)
aw-uun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hushed voice/low voice) (d:a low, hushed voice, from <aw>, voice, with <uun>; {aw-uun duadua} is a faint murmuring voice) (s:awneem) (q:draft, low confidence)
awging = (i:1) (t:n) (w:voice/sound) (d:<aw>, voice, with <ging>, sound: the sound of a voice or of anything that is heard) (s:aw/ging) (q:draft)
awgingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sounds/voices/noises) (d:<awging>, sound or voice, with the plural <te>: the sounds of music, singing, weeping or prayer) (s:awte/gingte) (b:awging) (q:draft)
awh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wear around the neck) (d:said of beads or a necklace, <khi>: {khi awh}, the necklace that is worn, one jewel of your necklace in the NIV; the meaning of {awh} alone is not shown by the verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
awhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put together/join) (d:said of God putting the parts of the body together; the base <awh> is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
awhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chains/necklaces) (d:things worn hung around the neck, <awh> with the plural <te>; {ngawng-awhte}, neck chains) (b:awh) (q:draft, low confidence)
awi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:warm oneself/sit by a fire) (d:with <mei>, fire: {mei awi} is warm oneself at a fire) (q:draft)
awi = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be willing/approve/want/agree to) (d:be willing that something is done or happens; in questions with <hiam>, do you want or do you not mind) (s:thukimpih) (r:42.11.47) (q:draft)
awk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blackness)
awk = (i:2) (t:v) (w:seize/catch/be caught) (d:catch or be caught in a trap, net or snare) (s:man) (a:suakta)
awkcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be snared/be caught fast/be trapped) (d:<awk>, be caught, with <cip>, tightly: be held fast in a trap or snare) (s:awkkha) (a:suakta) (b:awk) (q:draft)
awkcipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trapped/be ensnared) (d:<awk> be caught in a snare and <cip> tight, with the linking suffix <in>: caught fast) (b:awkcip) (q:draft)
awkin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be snared/be caught/be trapped) (d:form of <awk>, be caught in a snare, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:awk) (q:draft)
awkkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trapped/be ensnared) (d:<awk>, be caught in a snare, with <kha>, happen to: get caught, as by a promise one has made) (s:awkcip/awklawh) (a:suakta) (q:draft)
awklawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ensnared/get caught) (d:<awk>, be caught in a snare, with <lawh>, which shows that this comes on someone as a result of something) (s:awkkha) (q:draft)
awklum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hang oneself) (d:die by hanging, from <awk> be caught in a noose) (q:draft)
awkna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:entrapment/snare/trap) (d:<awk>, be caught, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being caught, or the catching itself, as in {awkna ding thang}, a trap to be caught in) (b:awk) (r:54.6.9) (q:draft)
awkpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trapped by/be ensnared by) (d:<awk>, be caught, with <pih>: be caught by means of something, usually by the words or deeds of oneself) (b:awk) (q:draft)
awksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trap/catch/ensnare) (d:<awk>, be caught, with the causative <sak>: cause to be caught in a pit, net or snare) (s:man) (a:suaktasak/khah) (b:awk) (r:19.35.8) (q:draft)
awksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ensnaring/trapping) (d:<awksak>, ensnare, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of causing someone to be caught, as the wicked in the work of their own hands) (b:awksak) (q:draft)
awkte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those caught/those ensnared) (d:<awk>, be caught, with the plural <te>; {a awkte}, those who are caught in a trap) (b:awk) (q:draft)
awl = (t:see) <tang-awl>
awle = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:crocodile/sea monster/Leviathan) (d:large water creature; the verses use it for the monster of the Nile and for Leviathan) (r:18.3.8) (q:draft)
Awle = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:Leviathan/crocodile) (d:<awle>, crocodile, written with a capital for the sea monster Leviathan) (b:awle) (q:draft)
awlin = (t:see) <tang-awlin>
awlmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:heed/care about/pay attention to/consider) (d:mostly used with a negative, not minding or not caring) (s:thudon/don) (q:draft)
awm = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chest/breast) (d:the front of the upper body; {awm beeng} is beat the breast in grief) (r:42.18.13) (q:draft)
awmah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chest/breast) (d:<awm> chest with the place marker <ah>: on the chest) (b:awm) (q:draft)
awmdal = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breastpiece/breastplate) (d:covering worn on the chest, the breastpiece of the high priest or a breastplate of armour) (s:awmdalna) (q:draft)
awmdalah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breastpiece/breastplate) (d:<awmdal> breastpiece with the place marker <ah>: on the breastpiece) (b:awmdal) (q:draft)
awmdalna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breastplate) (d:<awmdal>, chest covering, with the noun suffix <na>: armour worn over the chest) (s:awmdal) (b:awmdal) (q:draft)
awmdalnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breastplates) (d:<awmdalna> breastplate, a covering for the chest, with the plural <te>) (b:awmdalna) (q:draft)
awmgak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sash/chest band) (d:<awm>, chest, with <gak>, tie: a band tied round the chest) (q:draft)
awmtal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crawl/go on the belly) (d:move along the ground on the belly, as a snake does) (s:bokvak) (q:draft)
awn = (i:1) (t:num) (w:million) (d:the number one million; {awn khat} is one million) (q:draft)
awn = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lean/sway/reel/bend) (d:lean, bend or sway to one side, as a hut or a reed in the wind or a drunk person; {awn sak} is cause to lean) (s:hoi) (q:draft)
awn = (i:3) (t:v) (w:give way/give up a place/make room/yield) (d:move aside for someone: give up a seat or a place, or fall back before an enemy) (q:draft, low confidence)
awneem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:soft voice/gentle whisper) (d:<aw>, voice, with <neem>, soft: a soft, gentle voice) (s:aw-uun) (q:draft)
awng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shout/cry out/roar) (d:raise a loud cry, of joy, of battle or of anger) (s:kiko/ot) (a:daih) (q:draft)
awng = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:empty/vacant/unoccupied) (d:empty or free, of a seat or a place with no one in it; {mun awng} is an open space) (s:hawm) (a:dim) (q:draft, low confidence)
awngah = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:open/empty) (d:<awng>, empty or open, with the place marker <ah>; {mun awngah} is in the open place, the public square of a town) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awnggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shout/clamour/cry out loudly) (d:<awng>, shout, with <gawp>, which shows that it is done with force) (s:awngkekgawp) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awnghawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:relieve oneself/ease oneself) (d:go aside to empty the bowels, a polite expression) (q:draft)
awngin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shouting/with a shout) (d:<awng>, shout, with the linking ending <in>: shouting, and then doing something else) (s:kikoin) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awngin = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:empty/unoccupied) (d:<awng> empty with the linking ending <in>, being empty) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awngkeek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thunder/roar) (d:shout with a very loud voice; from <awng> shout) (s:awngkek) (q:draft)
awngkek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cry out/roar/shriek) (d:give a loud cry: roar or thunder, said of the Lord, and cry out in fear) (s:awngkeek) (q:draft)
awngkekgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shout furiously/yell/roar) (d:<awngkek>, shout aloud, with <gawp>, which shows that it is done with force; of an angry crowd) (s:awnggawp) (b:awngkek) (q:draft)
awngkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shout out/cry aloud/raise a shout) (d:<awng>, shout, with <khia>, out) (s:kikokhia) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awngna = (t:see) <mun-awngna>
awngsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make shout/let shout) (d:<awng> shout, with the causative <sak>) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awngsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep shouting/cry out) (d:<awng> shout, with <suak>; said of the prophets of Baal who went on crying out) (q:draft, low confidence)
awngsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thunder/shout down) (d:<awng>, shout, with <suk>, downward: shout down from above, said of the Lord thundering from heaven) (s:hawksuk) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awngte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:empty/deserted) (d:<awng>, empty, with the plural <te>; {mun awngte}, empty places, is used for ruins) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awngthawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cave/hole/gap/vacuum) (s:awngthawlpi) empty space
awngthawl = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:invalid/null/nullified/null and void/empty) (d:empty, with nothing in it or with no use; {a awngthawl mun} is an empty place) (s:awngthawlpi) empty space
awngthawlpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:without form/void) (s:awngthawl/hawmguak) a completely empty space
awngzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shout more/shout louder) (d:<awng> shout, with <zaw> more) (b:awng) (q:draft)
awnna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:open space/square) (d:in {khuapi kulhkongpi mun awnna}, the open place at the city gate; the base <awn> is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
awnsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bruised/bent) (d:<awn> lean, bend over, with <sa> already: already bent; said of a reed) (s:kisunimsa) (b:awn) (q:draft, low confidence)
awnsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:incline/turn/cause to lean) (d:<awn>, lean, with the causative <sak>; used of turning the heart toward something) (b:awn) (q:draft)
awnsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tilt down/lean over) (d:<awn>, lean or tilt, with <suk>, downward: of a pot, tilt over toward someone) (b:awn) (q:draft)
awte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:voices/sounds) (d:<aw>, voice, with the plural <te>: voices, or the sounds of joy, song and prayer) (s:awgingte) (b:aw) (q:draft)
awtna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shouting/uproar) (d:a loud shouting of many people; the same verse also has the spelling <otna>) (s:otna) (q:draft)
awzol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak smoothly/speak cordially) (d:<aw> voice and <zol> coax: speak in a friendly, winning voice) (q:draft, low confidence)
az = (t:see) <Ahima-az>
azah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fold/times as much) (d:the prefix <a> written together with <zah> amount; {azah sagih}, seven times as much) (b:zah) (q:draft)
Azaliah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Azaliah) (d:father of Shaphan the secretary of King Josiah, and son of Meshullam) (r:12.22.3/14.34.8)
Azamveth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Azmaveth) (d:father of Jeziel and Pelet, warriors who joined David; Azmaveth in the NIV) (r:13.12.3)
azaniah = (t:todo) (q:draft, lowercase only as the second part of the hyphenated man's name <Ja-azaniah>, Jaazaniah, in 24.35.3 and 12.25.23; the capitalised {Azaniah} in 16.10.9 is a man's name; a lowercase keyword cannot take type name)
Azaral = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Azarel) (d:a priest in the line of Immer, father of Amashsai; Azarel in the NIV) (r:16.11.13)
