bai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:lame/crippled) (d:unable to walk properly; as a verb, be lame, limp) (s:khebai/khezaw/khelbai) (r:1.32.31) (q:draft)
baihin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:early) (d:<baih> with the adverb ending <in>; {tho baihin} is rising early) (s:tungin) (b:baih) (q:draft)
baihlam = (t:see) <baihlam-a>
baihlam-a = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:easily/hastily/quickly) (d:<baihlam>, easy, with <a>: in an easy or hasty way, said of wealth gained too soon) (q:draft)
baihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ease/quickness) (d:noun form of <baih>, easy or soon, placed after a verb: {zol baihna} is being easy to persuade, {sih baihna} is dying early) (b:baih) (q:draft, low confidence)
baihsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:ready/prepared) (d:usually as {a baihsa-in}, in readiness) (s:kigingsa/kithawisa) (b:baih) (q:draft)
baihta = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:soon) (d:<baih>, soon, with <ta>, which marks that the time has now come; {pai baihta ding}, will come or go soon) (b:baih) (q:draft)
baihte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:quick/easy) (d:<baih>, quick, easy, with the plural <te>; {a heh baihte}, those who are quick to get angry, the hot-tempered) (b:baih) (q:draft)
baihzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:easier/more bearable) (d:<baih>, easy, with <zaw>, more; used after <sangin>, than) (s:olzaw) (a:haksazaw) (b:baih) (r:40.11.22) (q:draft)
baikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:worship/offering) (d:in {baikna tau}, altar; apparently a misprint of <biakna>, as {biakna tau} stands earlier in the same verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
baiknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:offerings) (d:in {meihal baiknate}, burnt offerings; apparently a misprint of <biaknate>) (b:baikna) (q:draft, low confidence)
baina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:laming/crippling) (d:<bai>, be lame, with the noun suffix <na>; <liamna baina> is being wounded and crippled, struck down) (b:bai) (q:draft, low confidence)
baite = (t:see) <khe-baite>
bak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bat) (d:the bat, listed among the unclean flying creatures) (r:5.14.18) (q:draft)
bak = (i:2) (t:n) (w:piece/portion) (d:counting word for a piece of meat: {sa bak khat}, one piece of meat) (s:baak) (q:draft, low confidence)
bak = (i:3) (t:v) (w:hold up to/put to) (d:hold something up against the mouth) (s:tahto) (q:draft, low confidence)
bakbak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:ravenously/greedily) (d:describes greedy, tearing eating; {a ne bakbak}, one that devours ravenously, said of a wild animal) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bakbakkar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bakbakkar) (d:a Levite who lived in Jerusalem after the return from exile) (r:13.9.15)
Bakbuk = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bakbuk) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.51/16.7.53)
Bakbukiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bakbukiah) (d:a Levite in Jerusalem after the exile, who served in the temple worship and as a gatekeeper) (r:16.12.9/16.12.25)
bakkhat = (t:todo) (q:draft, in {bakkhat suahin} of lions crushing their prey, perhaps at one stroke or in one bite, one verse only)
bakte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bats) (d:plural of <bak>, bat) (b:bak) (q:draft)
bakte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:pieces) (d:in the hyphenated word {sa-bakte}, the pieces of meat of an animal that has been cut up) (q:draft, low confidence)
bakuth = (t:see) <Allon-bakuth>
bal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear/rend/tear apart) (d:tear with the hands or teeth; {bal khia} is tear away, {bal nen} is break into small pieces, crumble) (s:balkek/balzan) (a:phop) (q:draft)
Bala = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Balah) (d:town in the territory of Simeon within Judah) (r:6.19.3) (q:draft)
Balaam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Balaam) (d:prophet, son of Beor, whom Balak king of Moab hired to curse Israel) (r:4.22.5/4.24.12)
baladan = (t:see) <Merodak-baladan>
Baladan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Baladan) (d:father of Marduk-Baladan king of Babylon) (r:23.39.1/12.20.12)
Balah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Balah) (d:town in the territory of Simeon, in the south of Judah) (r:6.19.3)
Balak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Balak) (d:king of Moab, son of Zippor, who hired Balaam to curse Israel) (r:4.22.39/4.24.12)
balgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/rip apart/maul) (d:To tear a person or an animal violently to pieces, as a wild beast does to its prey; built from <bal>, tear, and <gawp>, severely.) (s:petgawp/balzan/balthanggawp) (b:bal) (q:draft)
balgawpin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/maul) (d:The verb <balgawp>, tear apart violently, with the linking ending <in>, which joins it to the following verb.) (b:balgawp) (q:draft)
balgawpte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those torn to pieces/torn animals) (d:Animals that wild beasts have torn; <balgawp>, tear to pieces, with the plural <te>.) (s:balzante) (b:balgawp) (q:draft)
balkeek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear/rend/rip) (d:To tear cloth or something like it apart; often {a puan balkeek}, to tear one’s clothes as a sign of grief or horror.) (s:balkek/bal) (a:phop/khui) (q:draft)
balkeekin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear/rend/tear away) (d:The verb <balkeek>, tear, with the linking suffix <in>, which joins it to the next verb; mostly of tearing one’s clothes in grief.) (s:balkekin) (b:balkeek) (r:1.37.34) (q:draft)
balkek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear/rend) (d:To tear cloth apart; in the verses almost always to tear one’s clothes as a sign of grief.) (s:balkeek/bal) (a:phop/khui) (r:18.1.20) (q:draft)
balkekin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear/rend/tear away) (d:The verb <balkek>, tear, with the linking suffix <in>, tearing and then doing something else; often of tearing one’s clothes in grief.) (s:balkeekin) (b:balkek) (q:draft)
balkekna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tearing/rending) (d:The act of tearing one’s clothes, from <balkek>, tear, with the noun suffix <na>; {a balkekna thu} is the news that he had torn them.) (b:balkek) (q:draft)
balkeksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:torn) (d:Torn, of clothes torn as a sign of grief; <balkek>, tear, with <sa>, already done.) (s:kikeeksa) (b:balkek) (q:draft)
balkeksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear off/strip) (d:To tear the clothes off someone; <balkek>, tear, with the causative <sak>.) (b:balkek) (q:draft)
balkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear/tear off) (d:To tear at or tear off a part of the body, said of a lion tearing the arm or head of its prey; <bal>, tear, with <kham>.) (q:draft)
balkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear out/tear away/rip off) (d:To tear something out or away from where it is; <bal>, tear, with <khia>, out.) (s:eukhia) (b:bal) (q:draft)
balkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear away/tear out) (d:The form of <balkhia>, tear away, used before a following word such as <khit>.) (b:balkhia) (q:draft)
balneenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break in pieces) (d:The verb {balneen}, break in pieces, also written <balnen>, with the ending <in> linking it to the following verb.) (s:balnenin) (q:draft)
balnen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break in pieces/break/maul) (d:To break or tear something into pieces; {khomun balnen} is to break bread, and of a lion or bear it is to maul its victim.)
balnenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break in pieces) (d:The verb <balnen>, break in pieces, with the linking ending <in>, which joins it to the following verb.) (s:balneenin) (b:balnen)
balnenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breaking) (d:The act of breaking; <balnen>, break in pieces, with the noun suffix <na>, as in {khomun balnenna}, the breaking of bread.) (b:balnen) (q:draft)
balnensa = (t:see) <balnensa-in>
balnensa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:broken in pieces/crumbled) (d:In the state of having been broken into pieces; <balnen>, break in pieces, with <sa>, already done, and the ending <in>.) (q:draft)
balnensak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear in pieces for) (d:To tear prey in pieces for others, as a lion does for its mate and cubs; <balnen>, break or tear in pieces, with <sak>.) (b:balnen) (q:draft)
baltat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear apart/tear in two/sever) (d:To tear a thing right through so that the parts come apart; <bal>, tear, with <tat>, be severed.) (q:draft)
Balteshazzar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belteshazzar) (d:Babylonian name given to Daniel at the court of Nebuchadnezzar) (r:27.4.9)
balthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear apart/tear to pieces) (d:To tear apart, said of a wild animal tearing its prey.) (s:balzan/balgawp) (q:draft, low confidence)
balthanggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/tear apart) (d:To tear completely to pieces; <balthang>, tear apart, with <gawp>, severely.) (s:balgawp/balzan) (b:balthang) (q:draft)
balzan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/tear apart/tear down) (d:To tear into pieces, as a wild animal does to its prey; of walls and strongholds, to tear down.) (s:balgawp/balthanggawp/petgawp) (r:27.6.24) (q:draft)
balzante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those torn to pieces/torn animals) (d:Animals torn by wild beasts; <balzan>, tear to pieces, with the plural <te>.) (s:balgawpte) (b:balzan) (q:draft)
Bamoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bamoth) (d:stopping place of the Israelites in Moab between Nahaliel and the valley below Pisgah) (r:4.21.19/4.21.20)
Bamoth-baal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bamoth Baal) (d:high place in Moab to which Balak took Balaam to see the Israelite camp) (q:draft)
Bamothbaal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Bamoth Baal) (d:town on the plateau of Moab allotted to the tribe of Reuben, the high place to which Balak took Balaam) (r:6.13.17)
ban = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reach/extend to/stretch to) (d:To reach up to or extend as far as a point, said of height, of borders and of sound.) (s:phak) (q:draft)
ban = (i:2) (t:n) (w:arm) (d:The arm, also written <baan>; a figure for strength or power.) (s:baan) (r:18.4.3) (q:draft)
ban = (i:3) (t:n) (d:What comes next to or on top of something; with the place marker <ah>, {ban-ah}, next to, in addition to.) (q:draft, low confidence)
banah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:in addition to/besides/beside) (d:In addition to or on top of what is named before it; the noun <ban>, what comes next, with the place marker <ah>, as in {tua banah}, besides that.) (b:ban) (q:draft)
Banaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:spelling of Benaiah, here a Levite musician appointed when David brought the ark to Jerusalem) (r:13.15.18/13.16.5)
banbanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:one after another/in succession/in turn) (d:One after another, in a series; usually {a banbanin}, of things that follow each other in order.) (s:aban/khatkhatin) (q:draft)
banbuhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:armlets/bracelets) (d:Rings worn on the arm, named in lists of gold ornaments; <ban>, arm, with <buh>, ring, and the plural <te>.) (s:banbulhte) (q:draft)
banbulh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:armlet/bracelet/arm band) (d:An ornament or band worn on the arm; from <ban>, arm, and <bulh>, put on.) (q:draft)
banbulhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:armlets/arm bands) (d:Ornaments or bands fastened on the arm, <banbulh> with the plural <te>; in Isaiah 3.20 the NIV has anklets, and in Matthew 23.5 they are the phylacteries worn on the arm.) (s:banbuhte) (b:banbulh) (q:draft, low confidence)
bang = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:like) (d:Like, similar to; placed after the thing with which something is compared.)
Bang = (i:1) (t:det) (w:what) (d:The word <bang>, what, written with a capital at the start of a clause; {Bang hang hiam cih leh}, literally if one asks for what reason, means because or for.) (b:bang) (r:24.31.22) (q:draft)
banga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:like/as/such) (d:Like, in the manner of; <bang> with the linking ending <a> before a verb or describing word, often in <tua banga> and {hih banga}, in that way, like this.) (b:bang) (r:1.19.7) (q:draft)
bangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at about) (d:At about, after a measure of distance; <bang>, like or about, with the place marker <ah>.) (b:bang) (q:draft)
bangah = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:in what) (d:In what, in what respect, in a question; <bang>, what, with the place marker <ah>.) (b:bang) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangbang = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:whatever) (d:Whatever, anything at all; often {bangbang hita leh}, whatever it may be.) (s:thuthu)
bangbang = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:as/like) (d:Just as, exactly in keeping with; placed after a verb or noun, as in {a piak zawh bangbang}, as much as he is able to give.)
bangbangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:just as/according to whatever/exactly as) (d:In exactly the way that, in keeping with whatever; placed after a verb or noun.) (b:bangbang) (q:draft)
bangbangin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:however/in whatever way) (d:However, in whatever way; with a following <zongin>, no matter how.) (b:bangbang) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangbangun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:just as/whatever) (d:Just as or whatever, said of several people; <bangbang> with the ending <in> and the plural <u>, as in {a omzia bangbangun}, just as they were, and {a ut bangbangun}, whatever they please.) (b:bangbang) (q:draft)
bangbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:only as/just according to) (d:Exactly as and in no other way; <bang>, like, with <bek>, only.) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangci = (i:2) (t:phrase) (w:how come)
bangcih = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:what/how) (d:The form of <bangci>, how, used before <ding> and <thei>; {bangcih ding} asks what is to be done or what one will do.) (b:bangci) (q:draft)
Bangcih = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Bangcih)
bangcite = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:who/what kind) (d:What sort of person, which one; <bangci>, how, with <te>, as in {a bangcite ahi hiam}, which asks who it is that fits a description.) (b:bangci) (q:draft)
bangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:accordingly) (d:According to, in keeping with what is named before it; {tua mah bangin}, in that same way, accordingly.) (b:bang)
bangin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:therefore) (d:In {tua mah bangin}, so then, therefore, drawing a conclusion from what has been said.)
bangin = (i:3) (t:ppm) (w:like so/like/as) (d:Marker placed after a noun or clause: like, as, in the way of.) (b:bang)
banginah = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:just as/as) (d:Just as; <bangin>, like, with <ah>, introducing the first half of a comparison.) (b:bangin) (q:draft)
bangkeek = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:as if/just as though) (d:<bang>, like, with <keek>; in the same verse also written as two words, {bang keekin}) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangkhat = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:something/anything) (d:Something, anything; often followed by <peuhpeuh> or <teitei>, something or other.) (a:bangmah) (r:41.6.37) (q:draft)
bangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be restored/become as before) (d:To be once more as it was; <bang>, be like, with <kik>, again, usually after {a ngei} or {a ngeina}, its former state.) (b:bang) (q:draft)
bangkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being restored/becoming as before) (d:The verb <bangkik>, be as before, with the linking ending <in>; {a ngei bangkikin}, becoming again as it was.) (b:bangkik) (q:draft)
banglai = (t:todo) (q:draft, in {a them banglai khempeuh}, perhaps every little bit that still remains, one verse only)
banglel = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:just like/no better than) (d:No more than, just like; <bang>, like, with <lel>, merely, placed after a noun and <a>.) (q:draft)
bangmah = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:nothing/anything) (d:With a negative verb, nothing or not anything; <bang>, what, with the emphatic <mah>.) (a:bangkhat) (b:bang) (r:20.21.30) (q:draft)
bangmahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the same way/just so) (d:In that very way, just as; placed after <tua> or after the person whose conduct is followed.) (s:kibangmahin) (q:draft)
bangmahin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:not at all/as nothing) (d:With a negative verb, in no way, as nothing at all.) (b:bangmah) (r:14.9.20) (q:draft)
bangmahpi = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:nothing at all/anything at all) (d:Nothing at all, with a negative verb; <bangmah> with the strengthening suffix <pi>.) (b:bangmah) (q:draft)
bangpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:In {tua bangpi-in}, being like that, that being so; it introduces a question that expects the answer no.) (b:bang) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangpi = (i:2) (t:pron) (w:what) (d:What great thing, what at all; <bang>, what, with the augmentative <pi>.) (b:bang) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangpian = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:something like/a kind of) (d:Something like, something that looks like it; placed after a noun.) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make like/cause to be like) (d:To make like, to cause to be like; <bang> with the causative <sak>, and with <kik>, make as it was before, restore.) (s:kibangsak/batsak) (b:bang) (q:draft)
bangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making like/restoring) (d:The verb <bangsak>, make like, with the linking ending <in>; {a ngei bangsakin}, making as it was before.) (b:bangsak) (q:draft)
bangsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore) (d:To make a thing as it was before, to restore it to its former state; usually after {a ngei}, as before.) (s:batsakkik) (b:bangsak) (q:draft)
bangsakkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restoring) (d:The verb <bangsakkik>, make as it was before, with the linking ending <in>.) (b:bangsakkik) (q:draft)
bangsakkikte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:restorers) (d:Those who restore; <bangsakkik>, restore, with the plural <te>.) (b:bangsakkik) (q:draft)
bangsakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make like) (d:To be able to make like; <bangsak>, make like, with <zo>, be able or succeed.) (b:bangsak) (q:draft)
bangta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have become like/be like now) (d:To have become like; <bang>, be like, with <ta>, which marks a change that has come about.) (s:kibangta) (b:bang) (q:draft)
bangtan = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how long/how much) (d:Question word of extent, how far or how much; with <vei> or <sawt> it asks how long.) (s:bangtanvei) (q:draft)
bangtanvei = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how long) (d:Question word, for how long a time; also written {bangtan vei}.) (s:bangtan) (q:draft)
bangte = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:such ones/such things) (d:People or things like that; <bang> with the plural <te>, used as {tua bangte}, such ones.) (b:bang) (r:42.18.16) (q:draft)
bangteng = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:what/what things) (d:What, of all the things concerned; {hih bangteng}, all this, such things.) (b:bang) (q:draft)
bangtumlo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nonsense/folly) (d:aimless or senseless talk, apparently <bang>, what, <tum>, aim at, <lo>, not) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangtung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lintel) (d:In {bangtung zawl}, the beam over a doorway, the lintel; apparently <bang>, wall, with <tung>, top.) (s:bangtungzawl) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangtungzawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lintel/top of the doorframe) (d:The beam across the top of a door, above the two doorposts.) (s:kongtungzawl/bangtung) (q:draft)
bangun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:as) (d:As, in the way that; the marker <bangin> with the plural <u>, used when the subject is several people.) (b:bang)
bangzaha = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how/how much) (d:How, how much; <bangzah> with <a>, placed before a describing word, as in {bangzaha lian}, how great.) (b:bangzah) (q:draft)
bangzahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how/how much/however much) (d:How, how much, in exclamations and questions of degree; with <hangin>, however much.) (b:bangzah) (q:draft)
bangzahta = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how much/how greatly/however much) (d:Emphatic form of <bangzah>, how much, used in exclamations and questions, and with <hangin> for however much.) (b:bangzah) (q:draft)
bangzahtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how/how much) (d:How, how much, asking about degree; <bangzah>, how much, with <takin>.) (b:bangzah) (q:draft)
bangzahvei = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how much more/how many times) (d:How many times, how much more; <bangzah>, how much, with <vei>, times.) (q:draft)
bangzia = (t:see) <bangzia-in>
bangzia-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the manner/in the way) (d:<bangzia>, manner or way, with the ending <in>; mostly in {hih bangzia-in}, in this way, like this) (s:danin) (q:draft)
Banhadad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Hadad) (d:name of several kings of Aram who ruled in Damascus, among them the one defeated by Ahab at Aphek) (r:11.20.30)
Bani = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bani) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite of the line of Merari and the head of a family that returned from the exile) (r:15.2.10) (q:draft)
banin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reach/border on/touch) (d:<ban>, reach, with the linking ending <in>: reaching to, bordering on or touching; {van banin} is reaching up to the sky) (b:ban) (q:draft)
banin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:one after another/in succession/in turn) (d:used in the expression {a ban banin}: one following the other, in turn, step by step) (s:banbanin/kizomin) (q:draft)
bankap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shoot at) (d:shoot at, said of the archer in {a tuahkhak peuh a bankap}, who shoots at whoever he meets; the second part is <kap>, shoot) (q:draft, low confidence)
banna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:affected part/affected article/place reached) (d:<ban>, reach, with <na>: the thing or place that something has got onto; {natna a banna} is the article or stone affected by the disease or mold) (b:ban) (q:draft, low confidence)
bansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to reach/let overtake/bring upon) (d:<ban>, reach, with <sak>, cause: make something reach or come upon someone) (b:ban) (q:draft)
bansau = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:long-sleeved) (d:<ban>, arm, with <sau>, long; {puantualpi bansau} is the long-sleeved robe of Joseph and of Tamar, the ornate robe of the NIV) (q:draft)
bantan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut off/strike off) (d:of a sword, strike an arm so as to cut it; apparently <ban>, arm, with <tan>, cut off) (q:draft, low confidence)
bante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:arms) (d:<ban>, arm, with the plural <te>) (s:baante) (b:ban) (q:draft)
banto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reach up to/reach) (d:<ban>, reach, with <to>, upward: reach up as far as the sky, the clouds or heaven) (b:ban) (q:draft)
banzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reach/attain/equal/match) (d:<ban>, reach, with <zo>, be able: manage to reach, come up to or be equal to; with <kei> or <lo>, cannot reach, falls short of) (s:batzawh/tunzo) (b:ban) (q:draft)
baptaiz = (i:1) (t:v) (w:baptize) (d:loanword from English: immerse a person in water as the sign of repentance and faith) (s:tuiphum/phum) (q:draft)
Baptaiz = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Baptist) (d:title of John, who baptized in the Jordan; written {Baptaiz-pa Johan}, John the Baptist) (r:40.3.1)
baptaizna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:the act of baptizing or of being baptized; {baptaizna mun} is the place of baptizing) (s:tuiphumna/kibaptaizna/kituiphumna/bataizna) (b:baptaiz) (r:43.1.28) (q:draft)
baptaiznate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baptisms) (d:<baptaizna>, baptism, with the plural <te>; {baptaiznate thuhilhna} is teaching about baptisms) (b:baptaizna) (q:draft)
baptaizpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Baptist/baptizer) (d:<baptaiz>, baptize, with the male ending <pa>: the man who baptizes; title of John the Baptist, written with a capital) (s:tuiphumpa/Tuiphumpa) (b:baptaiz) (r:40.14.8) (q:draft)
Baptaizpa = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Baptist) (d:title of John son of Zechariah, who baptized in the Jordan and prepared the way for Jesus) (b:Baptaiz) (r:40.17.13/40.14.2)
Bar = (t:see) <Bar-Zeisu>
Bar-Zeisu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bar-Jesus) (d:Jewish sorcerer and false prophet at Paphos on Cyprus, also called Elymas) (q:draft)
Barabbas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barabbas) (d:prisoner, a rebel and murderer, whom Pilate released instead of Jesus) (r:42.23.19/40.27.16)
Barak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barak) (d:son of Abinoam from Kedesh in Naphtali, who with Deborah defeated Sisera) (r:7.4.12/7.5.1)
Barakhel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barakel) (d:a Buzite, father of Elihu who spoke to Job) (r:18.32.2)
Barakhiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Berekiah) (d:father of the Zechariah who was murdered between the temple and the altar) (r:40.23.35)
Barekhel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barakel) (d:a Buzite, father of Elihu; another spelling of <Barakhel>) (r:18.32.6)
Bariah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bariah) (d:son of Shemaiah, a descendant of David in the line of Zerubbabel) (r:13.3.22)
Barjesuh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bar-Jesus) (d:Jewish sorcerer and false prophet at Paphos; another spelling of <Bar-Zeisu>) (r:44.13.6)
Barkos = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barkos) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.53/16.7.55)
Barnabas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barnabas) (d:Levite from Cyprus, first named Joseph, who was a companion of Paul on his first missionary journey) (r:44.15.37/44.11.25)
Barnbas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barnabas) (d:another spelling of <Barnabas>, the companion of Paul) (r:44.13.43)
barnea = (t:see) <Kadesh-barnea>
Barsabbas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barsabbas) (d:name of two men: Joseph called Barsabbas, put forward with Matthias, and Judas called Barsabbas, sent to Antioch with Silas) (r:44.1.23/44.15.22)
Bartholomai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartholomew) (d:one of the twelve apostles of Jesus) (r:41.3.18/40.10.3)
Bartholomew = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartholomew) (d:one of the twelve apostles of Jesus; another spelling of <Bartholomai>) (r:40.10.3/41.3.18)
Bartimai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartimaeus) (d:blind beggar, son of Timaeus, whom Jesus healed near Jericho) (r:41.10.46)
Bartimias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bartimaeus) (d:blind beggar whom Jesus healed near Jericho; another spelling of <Bartimai>) (r:41.10.46)
Baruk = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Baruch) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Neriah, scribe of the prophet Jeremiah) (r:24.32.16/16.10.6)
Barzillai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Barzillai) (d:Gileadite from Rogelim who provided for David when he fled from Absalom) (r:10.19.32/10.19.31)
basan = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:lentil) (d:a pulse listed after <bepi>, beans, among the foods brought to David; apparently the same word as <besan>) (s:besan) (q:draft, low confidence)
Basemath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Basemath) (d:name of two women: a daughter of Ishmael who was a wife of Esau, and a daughter of Solomon who married Ahimaaz) (r:1.36.3)
Bashan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bashan) (d:fertile region east of the Jordan and north of Gilead, the kingdom of Og) (r:13.5.11/19.135.11)
Bashante = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bashan) (d:<Bashan> with the plural <te>, in {Gilead leh Bashante}, the lands of Gilead and Bashan) (b:Bashan) (r:6.17.5)
Bashon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bashan) (d:another spelling of <Bashan>, the region east of the Jordan) (r:5.3.10)
Bassha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Baasha) (d:son of Ahijah of the tribe of Issachar, king of Israel who reigned in Tirzah) (r:11.15.33)
Basshebeth = (t:see) <Josheb-Basshebeth>
bat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reach/extend to) (d:form of <ban>, reach, used before a following word such as <mateng>, <dongin> or <loh>: reach as far as a place or point) (q:draft)
bat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be like/resemble/become like) (d:form of <bang>, be like, used before a following word such as <hangin>, <nading> or <kei>) (s:suun) (a:kilamdang) (q:draft)
bat = (i:3) (t:v) (w:owe) (d:form of <ba>, owe, used before a following word: be in debt; {sum bat} is money owed) (q:draft, low confidence)
bataizna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:apparently another spelling or a misprint of <baptaizna>) (s:baptaizna/tuiphumna) (q:draft)
bate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:debtors) (d:<ba>, owe, with the plural <te>: those who owe; {sum bate}, those who owe money) (s:leibate) (a:sumneite) (b:ba) (q:draft)
Bathsheba = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Bathsheba) (d:daughter of Eliam and wife of Uriah the Hittite, later wife of David and mother of Solomon) (r:10.11.3/11.1.16)
Bathshua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Bathshua) (d:Canaanite wife of Judah, mother of Er, Onan and Shelah) (r:13.2.3)
batin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as a debt) (d:<bat>, owe, with <in>: {keima batin seh}, charge it to me as my debt) (b:bat) (q:draft)
batkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become like) (d:<bat>, be like, with <khak>, happen to; {na batkhak loh nadingun}, so that you do not come to be like them) (q:draft, low confidence)
batkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:all be like) (d:<bat>, be like, with <kim>, every one: all become like someone) (q:draft)
batna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:likeness/resemblance) (d:noun of <bang>, be like: the fact of being like something, as in {zukham a batna}, her being like a drunk person) (s:kibatna) (b:bat) (q:draft, low confidence)
batna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:debt) (d:the owing of a debt; {a batna pa} is the one to whom the debt is owed, the creditor) (s:leibatna/leiba) (b:bat) (q:draft, low confidence)
batnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creditors/debts) (d:<batna>, debt, with the plural <te>; {ka lei batnate}, those to whom I am in debt) (s:leibatnate) (b:batna) (q:draft, low confidence)
batsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make like) (d:cause to be like, <bat>, be like, with the causative <sak>; {a ngei batsak kik}, make as it was before, restore) (s:bangsak) (b:bat) (q:draft)
batsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:put on/fasten on) (d:put an ornament on someone, in the verse a ring on the nose) (s:butsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
batsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore) (d:<batsak>, make like, with <kik>, again; {a ngei batsakkik} is to make a thing as it was before) (s:bangsakkik/bawlkik) (b:batsak) (q:draft)
batsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reach down to) (d:<bat>, reach, with <suk>, downward) (b:bat) (q:draft)
battheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to be like/can become like) (d:<bat>, form of <bang>, be like, with <theih>, can; {a battheih nading}, so that one may be like or become like) (b:bat) (q:draft)
battheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<battheih>, can be like, with the noun suffix <na>; {a battheihna dingin}, so that it may become like) (b:battheih) (q:draft)
batzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to reach/attain) (d:<bat>, reach, with <zawh>, manage to; with a negative, be beyond what one can reach) (s:banzo/tunzo) (q:draft)
Bavvai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bavvai) (d:son of Henadad, ruler of half the district of Keilah, who repaired part of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.3.18)
bawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pounce on/swoop on/dart at/rush upon) (d:spring suddenly on prey or at something, of an animal or bird; of fighters, fall suddenly on an enemy or a town) (s:leenlak) (q:draft)
bawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:uproot/pull up) (d:pull a plant up or out of the ground, often with <zung>, root: {zung bawh}, pull up by the roots) (s:bot/botkhia/zunglot) (a:suan) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawhhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rush at/fall upon) (d:spring on a person all together; contains <bawh>, pounce on) (q:draft)
bawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pounce on/seize/snatch) (d:<bawh> with the linking suffix <in>, rushing upon and seizing, followed by another verb) (b:bawh) (q:draft)
bawhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:uproot/pluck out/tear away) (d:<bawh>, pull up or off by force, with <khiat>, out; before <sak>, tear something away from someone) (s:botkhia/zunglot) (a:suan) (b:bawh) (q:draft)
bawhkhiatsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear away from) (d:<bawhkhiat>, tear away, with <sak>, from or for someone, and <in> linking it to the following verb) (b:bawhkhiat) (q:draft)
bawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull out/pluck out) (d:<bawh>, pull up or out, with <sak>: pull out another person's hair) (b:bawh) (q:draft)
bawhsat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/snap) (d:break a cord or rope by pulling; {bawhsat hak}, hard to break) (q:draft)
bawhsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crouch down/bow down) (d:of an animal about to give birth, crouch down to the ground; <suk> shows downward movement) (q:draft)
bawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swell/be swollen) (d:become swollen, said of feet and other parts of the body; of breasts, fill out) (s:pawm) (q:draft)
bawk = (i:2) (t:n) (w:swelling) (d:a raised place on the skin, examined by the priest for skin disease) (q:draft)
bawk = (i:3) (t:n) (w:cluster/bunch/cake) (d:a cluster of fruit, as {leenggah bawk}, a bunch of grapes; also a pressed cake of dried fruit, as {leenggahkeu bawk}, a cake of raisins) (s:bom) (q:draft)
bawkbak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:crawling) (d:in {bawkbak a paite}, those that move crawling on the ground, reptiles) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawkgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swell up) (d:<bawk>, swell, with <gawp>, badly) (b:bawk) (q:draft)
bawkgawpin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swell up) (d:<bawkgawp>, swell badly, with <in> linking it to the following verb) (b:bawkgawp) (q:draft)
bawkin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swell) (d:<bawk>, swell, with <in> linking it to the following verb) (b:bawk) (q:draft)
bawksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give/hold) (d:in {pawi bawksak}, give a feast for someone; possibly a misprint of <bawlsak>, make for) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawkte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:clusters/bunches/cakes) (d:<bawk>, cluster, with the plural <te>: {leenggah bawkte}, clusters of grapes; {leenggahkeu bawkte}, cakes of raisins) (s:bomte) (b:bawk) (q:draft)
Bawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make/create) (d:<bawl>, make, written with a capital of God as Maker: {eite hong Bawl Topa}, the Lord our Maker) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawla = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making/having made/doing) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with the linking ending <a>; another verb follows) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep doing/go on doing/continue/be preparing) (d:<bawl>, do or make, said twice: keep on doing, as in {mawhna bawlbawl}, go on sinning; in some verses be doing or preparing) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:treat roughly/do violently) (d:<bawl>, do, with <gawp>, badly or without restraint; {zahpih bawlgawp}, mock outright) (b:bawl) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlgawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rough treatment/harsh treatment) (d:<bawlgawp> with the noun suffix <na>) (b:bawlgawp) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make/making) (d:form of <bawl> with the linking suffix <in>, making and then going on to the next action) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make/happen to make) (d:<bawl>, make, with <kha>, happen to; {bawlkha kei in}, take care not to make) (q:draft)
bawlkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make/happen to make) (d:form of <bawlkha>, happen to make, used before {loh nading}: take care not to make) (b:bawlkha) (q:draft)
bawlkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have made/have done) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <khin>, already and completely) (s:bawlzo) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:finish doing/have done) (d:<bawl>, do or make, with <khit>, finished; {bawlkhit ciangin}, after doing) (s:sepkhit) (q:draft)
bawlkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prepare/make ready) (d:<bawl>, make, with <khol>, beforehand: get something ready in advance, as a way, a place or a city) (q:draft)
bawlkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prepare/make ready beforehand) (d:form of <bawlkhol> used before a following word such as <khit> or <sak>) (b:bawlkhol) (q:draft)
bawlkholhna = (t:see) <bawlkholhna-in>
bawlkholhna-in = (i:1) (t:n) (w:preparation) (d:<bawlkhol>, make ready beforehand, with the noun suffix <na> and <in>: as a preparing of something in advance) (q:draft)
bawlkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rebuild/restore/repair/remake) (d:make again or put right what was spoiled, from <bawl>, make, and <kik>, again; used of rebuilding a city, restoring a people and undoing a deed) (s:lamkik/puah/bawlpha) (a:susia) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rebuild/restore) (d:<bawlkik>, rebuild, with the linking ending <in>: rebuilding, followed by a further action) (b:bawlkik) (q:draft)
bawlkikzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to repair/be able to restore) (d:<bawlkik>, make again, with <zawh>, be able; {bawlkikzawh nawn loh}, beyond repair) (q:draft)
bawlkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do for each one/do for all) (d:<bawl>, do or make, with <kim>, every one: do the same for each one) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawllai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still do/keep doing/go on doing) (d:<bawl>, do, with <lai>, still) (q:draft)
bawlma = (i:1) (t:v) (w:before making) (d:<bawl>, make, with <ma>, before: before he made) (q:draft)
bawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deed/doing/act/action) (d:what someone does or has done, nominal form of <bawl>; {ka bawlna thu}, what I am doing) (s:hihna/sepna/gamtatna) (b:bawl) (r:4.22.2) (q:draft)
bawlnasa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:had made/had done) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <na> and <sa>, already: what someone did before, or, before <mun>, the place where something was made before) (s:hihsa) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deeds/works/doings) (d:plural of <bawlna>: the things someone has done, often the mighty works of God) (s:gamtatnate/nasepnate/sepnate/hihnate) (b:bawlna) (q:draft)
bawlnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desire to do/wish to commit/urge to do) (d:<bawl>, do, with <nop>, want, and the noun suffix <na>; {mawh bawlnopna}, the desire to do wrong) (s:gamtatnopna/sepnopna) (q:draft)
bawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:maker/one who makes) (d:the one who makes or made something: <bawl>, make, with <pa> marking a man; {paknamtui bawlpa} is a perfume-maker and {savun bawlpa} a tanner) (s:piangsakpa/seekpa) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
Bawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Maker/Creator) (d:title of God written with a capital: the one who made people and all things; often {amah a Bawlpa}, his Maker) (s:Piangsakpa) (b:bawlpa) (r:23.17.7) (q:draft)
bawlpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prepare at once/make immediately) (d:<bawl>, make or prepare, with <pah>, at once) (q:draft)
bawlpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repair/restore/rebuild/strengthen/reform) (d:<bawl>, make, with <pha>, good: mend or strengthen a wall, a gate or a place, or put conduct right) (s:puah/bawlkik) (a:susia) (q:draft)
bawlpha = (i:2) (t:v) (w:work in/be at work in/make effective/make complete) (d:work on a person with good effect, of God, his word or a good quality: bring someone to a good or finished state) (q:draft)
bawlphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore/repair/put right) (d:form of <bawlpha> used before other words and endings; {bawlphat thakna} is renewal) (b:bawlpha) (q:draft)
bawlphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:working/operation/power at work) (d:noun of <bawlphat>, make good: effective working, said of the power of God at work) (b:bawlphat) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlphatna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:renewal) (d:the making new of a person) (b:bawlphat) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do together with/join in making) (d:<bawl>, do or make, with <pih>, together with someone: take part with others in what they do) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<bawlpih>, make together with, with the plural <te>: those with whom something is made, in the verse those with whom the covenant was made) (b:bawlpih) (q:draft)
bawlsa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creation/what is made) (d:what has been made, above all everything that God created: <bawl>, make, with <sa>, already done) (s:piansaksa) (b:bawl) (r:18.14.15)
bawlsa = (i:2) (t:v) (w:prepared/made) (d:already made or prepared: <bawl>, make, with <sa> marking a finished act; placed before a noun it tells what someone has made) (b:bawl) (r:2.23.20)
bawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make for/do for/have make) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <sak>: make or do something for someone, or have someone make it; {kilemna bawlsak} is to make atonement for someone) (s:piangsak) (b:bawl)
bawlsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:making/preparing) (d:noun of <bawlsak>: the making or preparing of something for someone; with <mun>, the place prepared; with <ding>, in order to make) (b:bawlsak) (q:draft)
bawlsaknasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:prepared) (d:<bawlsakna>, making for someone, with <sa>, already: that has been prepared for someone or something) (b:bawlsakna) (q:draft)
bawlsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doer/maker) (d:<bawlsak>, do or make for someone, with <pa> marking a man: he who did something for someone) (b:bawlsak) (q:draft)
bawlsaksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things done for) (d:<bawlsak>, do or make for someone, with <sa>, already done, and the plural <te>: the things that have been done for someone) (q:draft)
bawlsate = (i:1) (t:v) (w:made/things made/works) (d:<bawlsa> with the plural <te>: the things that someone has made or prepared) (b:bawlsa) (r:1.1.31)
bawlsia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:persecute/mistreat/oppress) (d:treat someone cruelly, persecute, mistreat or oppress: <bawl>, do, with <sia>, bad) (s:nengniam/gawt/gimbawl/gawtbawl) (q:draft)
bawlsiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:persecutor/oppressor) (d:the man who mistreats or persecutes, <bawlsia> with <pa> marking a man) (s:nengniampa) (a:bawlsiatpa) (b:bawlsia) (r:20.29.13) (q:draft)
bawlsiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let oppress/allow to mistreat) (d:<bawlsia>, mistreat, with <sak>, cause or allow: let someone mistreat another; in the verses with {nawn kei}, no longer allow it) (b:bawlsia) (q:draft)
bawlsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:persecute/mistreat/oppress) (d:form of <bawlsia> used before nouns and endings; {bawlsiat thuakna}, the suffering of persecution) (s:gimbawl/gawtbawl) (b:bawlsia) (r:48.4.29) (q:draft)
bawlsiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:persecutors/tormentors/oppressors) (d:those who persecute or mistreat, <bawlsia> with the plural ending {-te}) (s:nengniamte) (b:bawlsia) (r:19.119.84) (q:draft)
bawlsiatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:mistreated/oppressed) (d:<bawlsiat>, mistreat, with the ending <in>; {mi’ bawlsiatin}, as ones whom others mistreat) (b:bawlsiat) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:persecution/mistreatment/oppression/abuse) (d:cruel treatment that someone suffers, above all for the sake of faith: noun of <bawlsiat>, mistreat; {bawlsiatna thuak} is to suffer persecution) (s:kibawlsiatna) (q:draft)
Bawlsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oppression/persecution/mistreatment) (d:<bawlsiatna> written with a capital; {bawlsiatna a thuak mite} are the oppressed) (b:bawlsiatna) (q:draft)
bawlsiatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:persecutions/mistreatments/acts of oppression) (d:plural of <bawlsiatna>: acts of persecution or oppression) (b:bawlsiatna) (q:draft)
bawlsiatpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:victim/oppressed man) (d:<bawlsiat>, mistreat, with <pa>, a man; {a bawlsiatpa}, the man who is being mistreated, while the one who mistreats is <bawlsiapa>) (a:bawlsiapa) (b:bawlsiat) (q:draft)
bawlsiatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those oppressed/the tormented) (d:<bawlsiat>, mistreat, with the plural <te>: those whom someone mistreats or torments) (b:bawlsiat) (q:draft)
bawlta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make/do) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <ta>, which marks what has now come about) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawltawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make for oneself/invent/make up) (d:<bawl>, make, with <tawm>, by oneself: make something of one’s own; before a noun it means made by people themselves, man-made, as in {mihingte’ bawltawm thukhamte}, rules made by men) (s:phuahtawm) (q:draft)
bawltawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:man-made things) (d:<bawltawm>, make for oneself, with the plural <te>; {milim bawltawmte}, idols that people made themselves) (b:bawltawm) (q:draft)
bawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doers/makers) (d:those who do or make, <bawl> with plural <te>; {siatna bawlte} are evildoers, {sumbuk bawlte} are traders) (b:bawl) (r:26.17.4) (q:draft)
bawlte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:deeds/things done/works) (d:the things that someone did or made) (s:bawlnate/septe/hihnate) (b:bawl) (r:5.3.21) (q:draft)
bawlthak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:renew/make new) (d:<bawl>, make, with <thak>, new) (s:thakbawl/thaksuaksak/thaksuahsak) (q:draft)
bawlthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can do/be able to do/be able to perform) (d:<bawl>, do or make, with <thei>, be able) (s:hihthei/semthei) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawltheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can do/can make/be able to perform) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <theih>, be able, the form used before <nading> or <ding>) (s:hihtheih) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawltheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those able to do) (d:<bawlthei>, can do, with the plural <te>; {nalamdang bawltheite}, those who can work miracles) (b:bawlthei) (q:draft)
bawlthuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go on holding/hold for longer/do in addition) (d:<bawl>, do or hold, with <thuah>, in addition: go on holding a feast for more days) (q:draft)
bawltuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lawful to do/be right to do) (d:<bawl>, do, with <tuak>, be lawful or proper) (q:draft)
bawlung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ball) (q:draft)
bawlzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:amount made/quota) (d:<bawl>, make, with <zah>, amount: the number of things made) (q:draft)
bawlzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do more/do rather) (d:<bawl>, do, with <zaw>, more or rather: do more than others, or do in one way rather than another) (s:hihzaw) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have made/have done) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <zo> marking an act as carried through) (s:bawlkhin) (b:bawl) (q:draft)
bawlzo = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be able to do/manage to do) (d:<bawl> with <zo> in its sense of be able: {a bawlzo nawn lo} is no longer able to do) (b:bawl) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawnghon = (i:1) (t:n) (w:herd/herds/cattle) (d:a herd of cattle: <bawng>, cow, with <hon>, herd; often paired with <tuuhon>, flock of sheep) (r:2.12.38) (q:draft)
bawnghonte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:herds/herds of cattle) (d:plural of <bawnghon>, herd of cattle; usually paired with <tuuhonte>, flocks) (b:bawnghon) (q:draft)
bawngkhumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cowhouse) (d:a shed or enclosure where cattle are kept: <bawng>, cow, with <khumna>, place of shutting in)
bawngkhumna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:barn)
bawngkhumna = (i:3) (t:n) (w:shed)
Bawngkhumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stall/cowhouse) (d:<bawngkhumna> written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (b:bawngkhumna) (q:draft)
bawngla = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:heifer/young cow) (d:a young female of cattle) (s:bawngnuno) (q:draft)
bawngleeng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ox cart/cart) (d:<bawng>, cow or ox, with <leeng>, cart: a cart drawn by oxen) (q:draft)
bawngnawite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:milk) (d:<bawngnawi>, milk, with the plural <te>) (b:bawngnawi) (q:draft)
bawngno = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:calf) (d:the young of cattle: <bawng>, cow, with <no>, young; also the calf idol that Israel made) (b:bawng) (q:draft)
bawngnote = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:calves) (d:plural of <bawngno>, calf) (b:bawngno) (r:12.10.29) (q:draft)
bawngnuno = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:heifer) (d:<bawng>, cow, with <nu>, female, and <no>, young) (s:bawngla) (q:draft)
bawngpi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:cow) (d:the female of cattle: <bawng> with <pi>, which marks a female or mother animal; the male is <bawngtal>) (a:bawngtal) (b:bawng) (r:1.41.2) (q:draft)
bawngpite = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:cows) (d:plural of <bawngpi>, the female of cattle) (a:bawngtalte) (b:bawngpi) (q:draft)
bawngsa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beef/calf meat) (d:<bawng>, cow, with <sa>, meat) (b:bawng) (q:draft)
bawngtal = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bull/ox/bullock) (d:the male of cattle, a bull, or an ox used for work and for sacrifice: <bawng> with <tal>, male) (a:bawngpi) (r:14.29.33) (q:draft)
bawngtalno = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bull/young bull) (d:a young male of cattle, often named as an animal for sacrifice: <bawngtal>, bull, with <no>, young) (b:bawngtal)
bawngtalno = (i:2) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:calf/fattened calf) (s:bawngno) (b:bawngtal)
bawngtalnote = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young bulls) (d:plural of <bawngtalno>, young bull) (b:bawngtalno) (q:draft)
bawngtalte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:oxen/bulls) (d:plural of <bawngtal>: bulls, or oxen used for work and for sacrifice) (a:bawngpite) (b:bawngtal) (r:19.50.13) (q:draft)
bawngte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cattle/cows/herds) (d:plural of <bawng>: cattle, the cows and oxen that someone owns) (b:bawng) (r:4.31.38) (q:draft)
Bazlith = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bazlith/Bazluth) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile; the same man as Bazluth in Ezra) (r:16.7.54)
Bazluth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bazluth) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.52)
Be = (t:see) <Be-ersheba>
Be-er = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Beer) (d:name of two places: a well in the desert where Israel camped, and a town to which Jotham fled from Abimelek) (r:7.9.21) (q:draft)
Be-era = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beera) (d:a son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37) (q:draft)
Be-erah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beerah) (d:a leader of the Reubenites, taken into exile by Tiglath-Pileser king of Assyria) (q:draft)
Be-eri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeri) (d:name of two men: the Hittite father of Judith, wife of Esau, and the father of the prophet Hosea) (r:1.26.34) (q:draft)
Be-erlahairoi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:well) (w:Beer Lahai Roi) (d:well between Kadesh and Bered where the angel of the Lord found Hagar; Isaac later lived near it) (r:1.24.62) (q:draft)
Be-eroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beeroth) (d:one of the four Gibeonite towns, allotted to the tribe of Benjamin) (r:6.18.25) (q:draft)
Be-ersheba = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beersheba) (d:town in the Negev in the far south of Judah, linked with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob) (r:6.15.28) (q:draft)
Be-eshterah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Be Eshterah) (d:town in Bashan given to the Gershonite Levites from the half-tribe of Manasseh) (q:draft)
Bealiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bealiah) (d:a Benjamite warrior who joined David at Ziklag) (r:13.12.5)
Bealoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bealoth) (d:town in the far south of Judah; the name also stands for a district named with Asher under Solomon) (r:6.15.24)
beba = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:wide open/gaping) (d:describes the mouth opened as wide as it will go, after <kamkat> or {kam ka}, open the mouth; said of gaping in scorn or in greed) (q:draft)
Bebai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bebai) (d:ancestor of a family that returned from the exile, and a leader who sealed the covenant under Nehemiah) (r:15.10.28/16.10.15)
Bedad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedad) (d:father of Hadad, a king of Edom) (r:1.36.35/13.1.46)
Bedan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedan) (d:son of Ulam, a descendant of Manasseh) (r:13.7.17)
Bedciah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedeiah) (d:a descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.35)
Bedeiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bedeiah) (d:a descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.35)
bedolak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bdellium/aromatic resin) (d:a fragrant gum resin, named with <singnai>, resin; manna is said to look like it)
beek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:even/at all/not even) (d:stresses the smallest amount, mostly with a negative: {khat beek} with <kei> means not even one, and {neukha beek} means even a little) (s:nangawn) (q:draft)
beekah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:even in/at least to) (d:<beek>, even, at least, with the place marker <ah>: {khat beekah} with a negative, not even in one; {kiang beekah}, at least to) (b:beek) (q:draft)
Beel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pot/jar) (d:<beel>, pot or jar, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {Beel sekpa} is the potter, the one who shapes pots) (b:beel) (q:draft)
Beel = (i:2) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeliada) (d:first part of the name {Beel-i-ada}, Beeliada, a son of David; not a word by itself) (q:draft)
beela = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cling to/hold on to) (d:<beel>, hold fast to a person, apparently the same word as <bel>, cling to, with <a> linking it to the following verb) (q:draft, low confidence)
Beeliada = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeliada) (d:son of David born in Jerusalem) (r:13.14.7)
beelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take refuge in/cling to/rely on) (d:<bel> written with a long vowel and the linking ending <in>: holding fast to a person or taking shelter in something, and so doing a further action) (s:belin) (q:draft)
beellekuang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vessels/utensils/pots and bowls) (d:<beel>, pot, <le>, and, <kuang>, bowl, written as one word: the vessels of a house or of the temple) (s:umlebeel) (q:draft)
beellekuangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vessels/utensils/dishes) (d:plural of <beellekuang>: the dishes and vessels that belong to a table or a house) (s:kuanglekeute/umlebeelte) (b:beellekuang) (q:draft)
beelmang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:soot/pot black) (d:the black that gathers on a cooking pot; in the verse beauty is smeared with it, that is, made loathsome) (q:draft, low confidence)
beelpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who relies on) (d:<beel>, take refuge in or rely on, with <pa> marking a man: the man who put his trust in something) (q:draft)
beelpei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:griddle/flat pan) (d:flat cooking vessel on which bread is baked; {beelpei kitam} is a broken piece of it, a potsherd; also spelled <belpei>) (s:belpei) (r:3.7.9) (q:draft)
beelpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:large pot/cauldron/vat) (d:<beel>, pot, with <pi>, big; {leenggahzu kholna beelpi} is a wine vat) (b:beel) (q:draft)
beelseek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:potter) (d:one who shapes clay pots, from <beel>, pot, and <seek>, mould; followed by <pa> for a man) (s:beelsekpa/seekpa/sekpa) (r:24.18.4) (q:draft)
beelseekpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:potter) (d:<beelseek>, potter, with <pa> marking a man) (s:beelsekpa/seekpa/sekpa) (b:beelseek) (q:draft)
beelseekte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:potters) (d:plural of <beelseek>: people whose work is making clay pots) (b:beelseek) (q:draft)
beelsekpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:potter) (d:<beel>, pot, and <sek>, shape, with <pa> for a man: the man who shapes pots) (s:beelseekpa/seekpa/sekpa) (q:draft)
beelte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pots/vessels/jars/articles) (d:plural of <beel>: pots, jars and other vessels; {um-le-beelte} is vessels and articles of every kind) (s:belte) (b:beel) (r:19.58.9) (q:draft)
Beelzebub = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Beelzebul/Beelzebub) (d:name given to the prince of demons, by whose power the Pharisees said Jesus drove out demons) (r:40.12.24/40.10.25)
Beelzebul = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Beelzebul) (d:name given to the prince of demons, by whose power the Pharisees said Jesus drove out demons) (r:40.12.24/42.11.15)
beem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:homer/cor) (d:a large measure for grain, equal to ten <bung>; translates the Hebrew homer and cor) (r:26.45.14) (q:draft)
beemlepang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:storehouse/barn/provisions) (d:{beem le pang} written as one word: the bins where grain and food are stored, and so the food kept there) (q:draft)
beempi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:reservoir) (d:in {tui beempi}, a large store made to hold water) (q:draft, low confidence)
beeng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:slap/hit/strike) (d:strike with the open hand, especially on the face) (s:beng/bet) (q:draft)
beeng = (i:2) (t:v) (w:clap) (d:with <khut>, hand: clap the hands, in joy or in scorn) (s:beng) (q:draft)
beenggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strike/smite/slap hard) (d:<beeng>, strike with the hand, with <gawp>, severely) (b:beeng) (q:draft)
beengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:beating/striking) (d:<beeng>, strike, with the linking ending <in>; {awm beengin}, beating the breast, a sign of grief) (b:beeng) (q:draft)
Beer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Beer) (d:a well where Israel camped in the desert, and a town to which Jotham fled; also written <Be-er>) (r:7.9.21) (q:draft)
Beera = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beera) (d:son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37) (q:draft)
Beerah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beerah) (d:leader of the tribe of Reuben, taken into exile by Tiglath-Pileser king of Assyria) (r:13.5.6)
