behlapsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:add to) (d:<behlap>, add, with <sak>: add something to what another has said or has) (b:behlap) (q:draft)
behlapto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:add on/increase further) (d:<behlap>, add, with <to>, upward) (b:behlap) (q:draft)
behlapzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to add) (d:<behlap>, add, with <zawh>, be able) (q:draft)
behlephung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:descent/lineage/clan and family) (d:<beh>, clan, <le>, and, <phung>, family line, written as one word: the family a person descends from) (r:16.7.61) (q:draft)
behnai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:relative/close kin) (d:<beh>, clan, with <nai>, near) (s:tanau) (q:draft)
behnu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kinswoman/female relative) (d:<beh>, clan, with <nu> marking a woman) (b:beh) (q:draft)
behpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kinsman/relative) (d:<beh>, clan, with <pa> marking a man: a male member of the same clan or family) (s:tanaupa) (b:beh) (q:draft)
behtangun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:by their clans/clan by clan) (d:<beh>, clan, with <tang> and the plural ending <un>; of a count of men reckoned by clans) (q:draft, low confidence)
behte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:relatives/clan/kindred/family) (d:people of the same clan; after a name, the clan of that person) (s:tanaute/phungte) (b:beh) (q:draft)
bei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pass/over/come to an end/be finished) (d:come to an end: said of time that passes, of things that are used up, and of people who are no more) (s:tawp) (a:kipan) as {Nitak hong bei-in, zingsang hong tung a}
bei = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:empty/clear/used up/gone) (d:used up or gone, with nothing left) (s:gai) (a:dim)
beibei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pass away/keep passing) (d:<bei>, come to an end, doubled for something that goes on passing) (q:draft)
beikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish together/end together) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <khawm>, together) (b:bei) (q:draft)
beikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be over/be past/be used up) (d:<bei>, be finished, with <khin>, already: be completely gone or past) (s:beikhit) (b:bei) (q:draft)
beikhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be used up/be finished) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <khit>, completed; {a beikhit ciangin}, after it was all gone) (s:beikhin) (q:draft)
beikhitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being used up) (d:<beikhit> with the noun suffix <na>: the fact that something is all gone) (b:beikhit) (q:draft)
beikuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be about to end/near the end) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <kuan>, be on the way to; {leitung beikuan hun}, the time when the world nears its end) (q:draft, low confidence)
beilam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fading/ending) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <lam>: the passing away of something) (q:draft, low confidence)
beilawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lose/spend/perish) (d:<bei>, be finished or used up, with <lawh>, as a result of something: lose or spend all one has for a thing, or perish because of what has happened) (q:draft)
beima = (t:see) <beima-in>
beima-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:before passing away/before coming to an end) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <ma-in>, before: before it ends, before they pass away) (q:draft)
beimang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:vanish/perish/disappear) (d:pass out of existence or out of sight; <bei>, come to an end, with <mang>, away) (s:maimang/mangthang) (r:18.3.3) (q:draft)
beimangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy/wipe out/put an end to) (d:causative of <beimang>, vanish: make something disappear altogether) (s:maimangsak/susiamang) (b:beimang) (q:draft)
beimangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy/wipe out/cut off) (d:<beimangsak>, make disappear, with <in> linking it to the following verb) (b:beimangsak) (q:draft)
beimangsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:destruction/wiping out) (d:<beimangsak> with the noun suffix <na>; with <ding>, in order to destroy) (b:beimangsak) (q:draft)
beimangta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:vanish/disappear) (d:<beimang>, vanish, with <ta> marking a change that has now come about) (s:maimangta) (b:beimang) (q:draft)
beina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:end/outcome) (d:the point where something finishes, and also the way a matter turns out; <bei>, come to an end, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:tawpna) (a:kipatna) (b:bei) (q:draft)
Beinaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:descendant of Parosh who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.25)
beinate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:costs/expenses) (d:<bei>, be used up, with the noun suffix <na> and the plural <te>; {sum beinate}, the money spent) (s:beiteng) (b:beina) (q:draft)
beipak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pass quickly/be fleeting/be short-lived) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <pak>, quickly; of the days of a life) (q:draft)
beisa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:past/former/earlier) (d:gone by, of an earlier time: {a beisa nate} is the former things, <a beisa hun> time past) (b:bei) (q:draft)
beisak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:finish/bring to an end/put an end to) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with the causative <sak>: finish a period of time, or put an end to people or things) (b:bei) Put an end
beisak = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:empty/clear) (d:make empty or clear: use up what someone has, or clear people or things out of a place) (b:bei)
beisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroying/putting an end to/removing) (d:<beisak>, cause to be finished, with the linking ending {-in} before the next verb) (b:beisak) (q:draft)
beisakkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have done away with/have put off) (d:<beisak>, bring to an end, with <khin>, already) (b:beisak) (q:draft)
beisakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring to an end/end) (d:<beisak>, bring to an end, with <kik>, back: end a captivity and so restore the people) (b:beisak) (q:draft, low confidence)
beisakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:annihilate/wipe out) (d:<beisak>, bring to an end, with <mang>, away altogether) (s:susiamang) (q:draft)
beisakmangna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:annihilation) (d:<beisakmang> with the noun suffix <na>; with <ding>, in order to annihilate) (b:beisakmang) (q:draft)
beisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ending/using up) (d:the act of bringing something to an end or using it up, <beisak> with the noun suffix <na>; {hun beisakna}, the passing or wasting of time) (b:beisak) (q:draft)
beisakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:remover/one who puts an end to) (d:<beisak>, put an end to or let pass, with <pa>, a man: the man who takes something away, or who lets a time go by) (b:beisak) (q:draft)
beisakta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put an end to/make cease) (d:<beisak>, put an end to, with <ta>, which marks what now comes about) (b:beisak) (q:draft)
beisiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be wiped out/be completely gone) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <siang>, clean: be gone with nothing left; {beisiang sak}, clear away, purge) (b:bei) (q:draft)
beisiangna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:complete destruction/utter end) (d:<beisiang>, be completely gone, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:beisiang) (q:draft)
beisiangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wipe out/purge/clear away) (d:<beisiang>, be completely gone, with <sak>, cause: remove a thing completely from a place) (b:beisiang) (q:draft)
beita = (i:1) (t:v) (w:has ended/is gone/is finished) (d:<bei> with <ta>, showing that something has now come to an end) (b:bei) (q:draft)
beiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:expenses/all that is spent) (d:<bei>, be used up, with <teng>, all; {sum beiteng}, all the money spent) (s:beinate) (b:bei) (q:draft)
beitum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be consumed/be destroyed/perish) (d:come to a complete end, be used up or destroyed altogether) (q:draft)
beitumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consume/destroy completely) (d:<beitum>, be wholly consumed, with <sak>, cause; said together with <beimangsak>, cause to perish) (b:beitum) (q:draft, low confidence)
beizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have passed away/be gone) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <zo> marking completion) (b:bei) (q:draft)
beka = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:only/merely) (d:<bek>, only, with the ending <a> linking it to the following word: {pualam beka} is only outward, {tungtham beka} only on the surface) (b:bek) (q:draft)
beka = (i:2) (t:n) (w:beka) (d:measure of weight, half a shekel) (q:draft)
bekah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:only in/only at/only to) (d:<bek>, only, with the place marker <ah>: only in, only at or only to that place or person) (b:bek) (r:47.10.17) (q:draft)
bekbak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:thick/heavily) (d:word of manner that strengthens what goes before: {khuamial bekbak}, thick or utter darkness; {man bekbak-in hawl}, drive heavily, with difficulty) (q:draft, low confidence)
bekbakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:with difficulty/heavily) (d:<bekbak>, heavily, with the adverbial ending <in>: {man bekbakin hawl} is to drive slowly and with great difficulty) (b:bekbak) (q:draft, low confidence)
bekbakte = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<bekbak>, thick or hard, with the plural <te>: in the verse the places where the ground has dried hard) (b:bekbak) (q:draft, low confidence)
bekbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:only/nothing but) (d:emphatic doubled form of <bek>, placed after the word it limits: {thusia bekbek} is nothing but evil talk) (s:vive) (q:draft)
bekbekin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:only/solely/nothing but) (d:<bekbek>, only, with the adverbial ending <in>, placed after the word it limits: {a thuman bekbekin} is what is right and that alone) (b:bekbek) (q:draft)
Bekher = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beriah/Beker) (d:a son of Benjamin; also a son of Ephraim, ancestor of a clan) (r:1.46.21/13.7.6)
bekin = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:only/merely) (d:<bek>, only, with <in>, closing a phrase of reason or purpose: {hang bekin} and {man bekin} are only because of, {ading bekin} is only for) (b:bek)
bekin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:just/only/alone) (d:<bek>, only, with the adverbial <in>, limiting the word before it: {keimah bekin} is I alone, {na kam bekin} is just by your word) (s:lelin) (b:bek)
bekinah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in only/within just) (d:<bekin>, only, with the marker <ah>: {nai khat sung bekinah} is within just one hour) (b:bekin) (q:draft)
Bekorath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bekorath) (d:a Benjamite, son of Aphiah and ancestor of King Saul) (r:9.9.1)
bekun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:only/just/merely) (d:<bek>, only, with the ending <un> used when the subject is plural; {man bekun} is only because of, {nading bekun} is only so that) (b:bek) (q:draft)
bel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take refuge in/rely on/cling to) (d:to shelter in or hold on to someone for safety, most often said of trusting in God; also written <belh>) (s:muang) (a:taisan) (q:draft)
bel = (i:2) (t:part) (w:most/very) (d:placed after a word of order or degree to mark the extreme, as in {a masa bel} the very first, {a nunung bel} the very last and {a sang bel} the highest) (q:draft)
Bel = (i:1) (t:part) (w:most) (d:capitalised form of <bel> in titles, as in {Siangtho Bel Mun}, the Most Holy Place, and {Sang Bel Pasian}, God Most High) (s:Pen) (b:bel) (q:draft)
Bel = (i:2) (t:name) (w:Bel) (d:the chief god of Babylon, also known as Marduk) (r:24.51.44/23.46.1/24.50.2) (q:draft)
bela = (i:1) (t:part) (w:very/most) (d:<bel>, which marks the extreme of an order, with <a> joining it to what follows: {a nunung bela piang}, born at the very last) (b:bel) (q:draft)
bela = (i:2) (t:v) (w:built against/adjoining) (d:<bel>, cling to or lean on, with <a>: built against or attached to a wall) (b:bel) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bela = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Bela) (d:a city in the plain of the Jordan, also called Zoar; the same name is borne by several men, among them the firstborn son of Benjamin and a king of Edom) (r:1.14.2/1.14.8)
belapin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:add to) (d:apparently <behlap>, add, written without h, with <in> linking it to the following verb) (s:behlapin) (q:draft, low confidence)
belawi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bean) (d:a kind of bean, named among the grains and pulses used for bread) (s:bepi) (q:draft)
belh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take refuge in/rely on/trust in) (d:to go to someone for shelter and safety, most often said of trusting in God; a form of <bel>) (s:muang) (a:taisan) (q:draft)
belh = (i:2) (t:n) (w:refuge/fortress/stronghold) (d:the one or the place that someone takes refuge in) (s:bukna/hutna/munkip/belhna) (r:19.46.11) (q:draft)
belh = (i:3) (t:v) (w:cling to/hold fast to/stick to) (d:to stay fastened to someone or something, said of holding fast to God and also of a disease that will not leave) (s:toncip/lenkip) (q:draft)
belhin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as a refuge/as shelter) (d:<belh>, refuge, with <in>: {belhin nei}, have as a place of shelter) (b:belh) (q:draft)
belhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:refuge/shelter/hiding place) (d:<belh>, take refuge, with the noun suffix <na>: a place of refuge or the act of taking refuge) (s:bukna/hutna/belh) (b:belh) (q:draft)
belhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:refuge) (d:the one in whom refuge is taken, said of God; <pa> marks a male person) (s:buknapa) (b:belh) (q:draft)
belhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make stick to/cause to cling) (d:<belh>, cling to, with <sak>, cause) (b:belh) (q:draft)
belhtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to take refuge in/can rely on) (d:<belh>, take refuge in, with <theih>, can) (s:muantheih) (b:belh) (q:draft)
beli = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:lentil) (d:a pulse named after <belawi>, bean, among the grains used for bread) (s:basan/besan) (q:draft, low confidence)
Belial = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Belial) (d:a name for the devil, the power of evil set against Christ) (r:47.6.15)
belin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:most/of all/at the most) (d:<bel>, most, with the marker <in>, after a descriptive word: {a masa belin}, first of all; {a nunung belin}, last of all; {a tam belin}, at the most) (b:bel) (q:draft)
belin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cling to/rely on/take refuge in) (d:form of <bel>, cling to or take refuge in, with the linking suffix <in>; also after another verb in <belin nei>, have as the chief thing one relies on or dwells on) (s:beelin) (b:bel) (q:draft, low confidence)
belna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the highest/the highest place/the utmost) (d:<bel>, most, with the noun suffix <na>: {a sang belna} is the highest place) (b:bel) (q:draft)
belnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the highest ones/highest powers) (d:<belna>, the utmost, with the plural <te>; {a sang belnate}, those in the highest places) (b:belna) (q:draft)
belpa = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<bel>, most, with <pa> marking a man; {a masa belpa}, the very first man) (b:bel) (q:draft)
belpei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:griddle/flat pan) (d:flat cooking vessel; {belpei kitam} is a broken piece of it, a potsherd; also spelled <beelpei>) (s:beelpei) (q:draft)
Belshazaar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belshazzar) (d:king of Babylon who saw the writing on the wall and was killed that night; a spelling of <Belshazzar>) (r:27.5.22)
Belshazzar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belshazzar) (d:king of Babylon in the time of Daniel, who saw the writing on the wall and was killed that night) (r:27.5.30/27.8.1)
Beltashazzar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belteshazzar) (d:the Babylonian name given to Daniel; a spelling of <Belteshazzar>) (r:27.4.18/27.4.19)
belte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who take refuge/those who rely on) (d:<bel>, take refuge in, with the plural <te>: the people who shelter in or rely on someone) (b:bel) (q:draft)
belte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:vessels) (d:spelling of <beelte>, pots or vessels, used as a figure for people who receive mercy) (s:beelte) (q:draft, low confidence)
Belteshazzar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Belteshazzar) (d:the Babylonian name given to Daniel by the chief official of King Nebuchadnezzar) (r:27.2.26/27.4.8)
bem = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:round/circular) (d:round in shape; also a round band or rim) (s:vial) (r:14.4.2) (q:draft)
bem = (i:2) (t:adj) (d:in {bem gial}, marked with round spots or rings, said of animals, beside {dung gial} streaked) (q:draft, low confidence)
bemeh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lentil stew/bean stew) (d:<be>, bean or lentil, with <meh>, cooked dish eaten with the staple) (q:draft)
Ben = (t:see) <Ben-Hinnom>
Ben-ammi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Ammi) (d:son of Lot by his younger daughter, ancestor of the Ammonites) (q:draft)
Ben-ejaakan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bene Jaakan) (d:a place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped on the way from Egypt) (r:5.10.6) (q:draft)
Ben-geber = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Geber) (d:one of Solomon's twelve district governors, in charge of Ramoth Gilead) (r:11.4.13) (q:draft)
Ben-Hinnom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Ben Hinnom) (d:a valley on the south side of Jerusalem where children were burned at Topheth; followed by <mualkuam>, valley) (r:24.19.2) (q:draft)
Ben-om = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Oni) (d:the name Rachel gave Benjamin; the spelling {Ben-om} may be a misprint for {Ben-oni}) (q:draft, low confidence)
Benabinadab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Abinadab) (d:one of Solomon's district governors, over Naphoth Dor, married to Solomon's daughter Taphath) (r:11.4.11)
Benaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Jehoiada, commander of David's bodyguard and later of Solomon's army) (r:10.8.18/10.23.30)
Benaiahte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Benaiah) (d:<Benaiah> with <te> closing a list of names, Benaiah and the others; here a temple overseer under King Hezekiah) (b:Benaiah) (r:14.31.13)
Benammi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-ammi/Ben-Ammi) (d:son of Lot by his younger daughter, ancestor of the Ammonites) (r:1.19.38)
Bendeker = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Deker) (d:one of Solomon's district governors, over Makaz, Shaalbim and Beth Shemesh) (r:11.4.9)
Beneberak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bene Berak) (d:a town in the territory of the tribe of Dan) (r:6.19.45)
Benejaakan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bene Jaakan) (d:a place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped on the way from Egypt) (r:4.33.31/4.33.32)
beng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hunt/fish) (d:go after animals or fish to catch them; {sa beng} hunt game, {nga beng} catch fish) (s:gamvak) (q:draft)
beng = (i:2) (t:v) (w:slap/strike/clap) (d:hit with the open hand; {paang beng} slap the cheek, {khut beng} clap the hands, {awm beng} beat the breast) (s:beeng/bet) (q:draft)
bengbengte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who slap) (d:<beng>, slap, repeated to show a repeated action, with the plural <te>) (q:draft)
Bengeber = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Geber) (d:one of Solomon's twelve district governors, in charge of Ramoth Gilead) (r:11.4.13)
bengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:clap/slap) (d:<beng> with the linking suffix <in>: strike with the open hand, {khut beng} clap the hands, {paang beng} slap the cheek; also of <beng>, hunt, as in {sa bengin}, hunting game) (b:beng) (r:14.18.23) (q:draft)
bengkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drive away/scare away/chase off) (d:<beng> with <khia>, away: drive off birds or animals) (s:notkhia) (b:beng) (q:draft)
bengmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hunt down) (d:<beng>, hunt, with <mang>, away altogether) (q:draft)
bengngong = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deaf) (d:unable to hear; {bengngong kei in} is do not be deaf, do not refuse to listen) (s:bilngong/ngong) (q:draft)
Bengngongte = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Bengngongte/the deaf) (d:<bengngong>, deaf, with the plural <te>, deaf people, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (b:bengngong) (r:41.7.37/40.11.5)
bengpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hunter) (d:<beng>, hunt, with <pa> marking a man: one who hunts) (s:sabengpa/sabeng) (b:beng) (q:draft)
bengsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let slap/offer to be slapped) (d:<beng>, slap, with <sak>: let someone slap, hold out the cheek to be slapped) (b:beng) (q:draft)
bengte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fishermen/fishers) (d:<beng>, catch, with the plural <te>: in {ngasa bengte}, those who catch fish) (s:ngabengte) (b:beng) (q:draft)
bengtumsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:beat down/bring low) (d:apparently <beng>, strike, with <tum> and <suk>, downward: strike down, of pride being brought low) (q:draft, low confidence)
Benhadad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Hadad) (d:name of several kings of Aram who ruled in Damascus, among them the son of Hazael) (r:12.13.24/11.20.26)
Benhail = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Hail) (d:an official whom King Jehoshaphat sent to teach in the towns of Judah) (r:14.17.7)
Benhanan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Hanan) (d:a descendant of Judah, son of Shimon) (r:13.4.20)
Benhesed = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Hesed) (d:one of Solomon's district governors, in charge of Arubboth) (r:11.4.10)
Benhur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ben-Hur) (d:one of Solomon's district governors, in the hill country of Ephraim) (r:11.4.8)
Beninu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beninu) (d:a Levite who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.13)
