Binea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Binea) (d:son of Moza, a descendant of King Saul through Jonathan) (r:13.8.37/13.9.43)
bing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:jar/flask/hin) (d:small container for oil; also a liquid measure where the English has hin) (s:biing) (q:draft)
bing = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be closed/be stopped up/be deaf) (d:of the ears, be closed so that one cannot hear) (a:vang) (q:draft, low confidence)
bingphawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:attack by surprise/fall upon) (d:attack an enemy who is off guard) (q:draft)
bingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stop up/close/make deaf) (d:<bing>, be stopped up, with the causative <sak>: close the ears so as not to hear) (s:ngongsak) (b:bing) (q:draft)
Binnui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Binnui) (d:name of several men after the exile, among them a Levite, son of Henadad, who helped repair the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.3.24/15.10.38/16.10.9)
Birsha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Birsha) (d:king of Gomorrah in the time of Abraham) (r:1.14.2)
