Bithynia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Bithynia) (d:Roman province on the Black Sea coast in the north-west of Asia Minor) (r:44.16.7/60.1.1)
bitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:safeguard/safety/security) (d:<bit>, safe, with the noun suffix <na>: something that keeps a person safe) (s:muanhuaina) (a:lauhuaina) (b:bit) (q:draft)
Biziothiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Biziothiah) (d:town in the far south of Judah, listed next to Beersheba) (r:6.15.28)
Biztha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Biztha) (d:one of the seven eunuchs who served King Xerxes) (r:17.1.10)
Blastus = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Blastus) (d:trusted personal servant of King Herod Agrippa, whose support the people of Tyre and Sidon won) (r:44.12.20)
Blatas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Blastus) (d:trusted personal servant of King Herod Agrippa, whose support the people of Tyre and Sidon won) (r:44.12.20)
Boanerges = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Boanerges) (d:name that Jesus gave to James and John, the sons of Zebedee, meaning sons of thunder) (r:41.3.17)
Boaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Boaz) (d:wealthy man of Bethlehem who married Ruth, father of Obed and great-grandfather of David; also the name of one of the two bronze pillars of the temple of Solomon) (r:8.2.1/8.4.21)
Boer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beor) (d:father of the seer Balaam) (r:6.24.9/5.23.4)
Bohan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bohan) (d:son of Reuben after whom a boundary stone between Judah and Benjamin was named) (r:6.15.6/6.18.17)
bok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow down/prostrate oneself/crouch) (d:go down with the face to the ground, in fear, worship or submission; of an animal, crouch) (s:boksuk/maipuk/kunsuk) (a:dingto) (r:6.7.10) (q:draft)
Bokheru = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bokeru) (d:son of Azel, a descendant of King Saul in the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.38/13.9.44)
Bokhim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bokim) (d:place where the angel of the Lord rebuked Israel and the people wept) (r:7.2.5/7.2.1)
bokin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall down/prostrate oneself/bow down) (d:<bok>, fall face down, with the linking ending <in>: falling down before someone, usually followed by <bia>, worship) (s:boksukin/kunin) (b:bok) (q:draft)
boksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make kneel/make fall down/make lie down) (d:<bok>, lie face down, with the causative <sak>: make an animal kneel down, or make a person fall at the feet of another) (b:bok) (q:draft)
boksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow down/prostrate oneself) (d:<bok> with <suk>, downward: throw oneself down with the face to the ground, in worship, fear or pleading) (s:bok/maipuk/kunsuk) (a:dingto) (b:bok) (q:draft)
boksukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow down/prostrate oneself) (d:<boksuk>, fall with the face to the ground, with the linking ending <in>: falling facedown and then doing the next action) (s:bokin/kunin) (b:boksuk) (q:draft)
bokvak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crawl/move along the ground) (d:move along the ground on the belly or on short legs, as snakes, lizards and insects do; {a bokvak ganhing} is a crawling creature) (s:awmtal)
bokvak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:creep/move along the ground) (d:of small animals and reptiles, move close to the ground; {a bokvak ganhingte} are the creatures that move along the ground) (s:hontat)
bokvakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crawl/creeping things/creatures that move along the ground) (d:<bokvak>, creep, with the plural <te>, used as a noun: the creatures that creep on the ground) (b:bokvak) plural form of <bokvak>
bom = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cluster/bunch) (d:a bunch of fruit growing together; {leenggah bom} is a cluster of grapes) (s:bawk) (q:draft)
bomah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the crossroads/at the corner) (d:<bom> with the place marker <ah>; {lamka bomah}, at the place where roads meet, a crossroads or street corner) (q:draft)
