bulllente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bases/sockets) (d:the bases in which the frames of the tabernacle stand; spelling of <bullente> with three l, probably a misprint) (q:draft)
bulom = (i:1) (t:n) (w:heap/lump) (d:in {nin bulom}, a heap or lump of dirt, where the English has dust and ashes; exact sense not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
bulomtang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:heap/pile) (d:in {nin bulomtang}, a heap of rubble or ruins) (q:draft)
bulphuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:base on/rely on/make the foundation) (d:take something as the basis or the main thing) (s:siksan) (q:draft)
bulphuhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:based on/on the basis of) (d:<bulphuh>, take as the basis, with the linking suffix <in>; placed after the thing that is the basis) (b:bulphuh) (q:draft)
bulphuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut down at the root/fell) (d:<bul> base with <phuk> cut down: fell a tree at its foot) (s:phuk) (q:draft)
bulpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foundation/base) (d:the base on which a building or the earth rests; {innkiu suang bulpi} is the cornerstone) (s:innbul/bulkip/tawphah) (b:bul) (q:draft)
bulpipen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:main point/very foundation) (d:<bulpi>, foundation, with <pen>, most: the most basic thing, the heart of a matter) (b:bulpi) (q:draft)
bulpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foundations/bases) (d:<bulpi>, foundation, with the plural <te>) (s:nuaiphahte) (b:bulpi) (q:draft)
bulsel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:branch/shoot/sprout) (d:<bul> base with <sel> sprout: a new shoot growing from the stock; in Isaiah 4.2 the Branch of the Lord) (q:draft)
bulsum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stump) (d:the part of a tree left in the ground after it is cut down) (s:singbul) (q:draft)
bulte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foundations/bases) (d:plural of <bul>, base; {leitung bulte} is the foundations of the earth, and of a wheel the hubs) (b:bul) (q:draft)
buluah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plunder/loot) (d:take all of another's possessions by force) (s:sut) (q:draft)
buluh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raid/attack/plunder) (d:fall on someone to rob) (s:luh) (q:draft)
buluh = (i:2) (t:n) (w:robber) (d:in <guta buluh>, thief and robber) (s:misuam/galgu) (q:draft)
buluhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:robbers/raiders/bandits) (d:<buluh>, robber, with the plural <te>; often paired as {guta buluhte}, thieves and robbers) (s:misuamte/suamte) (b:buluh) (q:draft)
bum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sorcery/magic/spell) (d:magic used to harm or control someone; {bum siam}, enchanter) (s:mibum/bumna) (q:draft)
bum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:bewitch/cast a spell on) (d:put a person under a spell; {mi bum theite} are those who practise sorcery) (q:draft)
bumek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reach into a nest/rob a nest) (d:<bu>, nest, with <mek>: feel in a bird's nest to take what is in it; the same word is also written <bu-mek>) (q:draft, low confidence)
bumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:witchcraft/sorcery) (d:<bum>, bewitch, with the noun suffix <na>; {mi bumna}, casting spells on people) (s:mibumna/khongkhaina) (b:bum) (q:draft)
bumnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sorceries/magic arts) (d:plural of <bumna>, sorcery) (s:aisannate) (b:bumna) (q:draft)
bun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take hold/stick fast/penetrate) (d:of a weapon, bite into what it strikes; of rust or scum, cling so fast that it cannot be cleaned off) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bunah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bunah) (d:son of Jerahmeel, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.25)
bung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hin/bath/ephah) (d:a measure of capacity, used for the Hebrew hin and bath of oil or wine and for the ephah of grain) (q:draft)
bung = (i:2) (t:v) (w:empty/pour out) (d:tip the contents out of a vessel; {bung khia} is empty out) (q:draft, low confidence)
bungbu = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:headlong/head first) (d:used with verbs of falling or pushing) (q:draft)
bungkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pour out/empty out) (d:<bung> tip out with <khia> out: tip the contents out of a vessel or a chest) (s:buakhia/sungkhia) (b:bung) (q:draft)
bungpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bath/large measure) (d:<bung>, a measure for liquids, with <pi> big: a large measure of oil, where the NIV has bath) (b:bung) (q:draft, low confidence)
bungsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:empty into/pour down) (d:<bung>, empty out, with <suk>, downward) (b:bung) (q:draft)
bungte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bottles/boxes/containers) (d:plural of <bung>, here a small container: {paknamtui bungte} are perfume bottles) (b:bung) (q:draft)
Bunni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bunni) (d:name of several men in the time of Nehemiah, among them a Levite who led the people in prayer) (r:16.11.15/16.10.15)
bunzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go deeper/affect more) (d:<bun> go in or take effect, with <zaw> more: sink in more deeply, said of a rebuke) (b:bun) (q:draft)
bunzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pierce/penetrate/take effect) (d:<bun> go in, with <zo> be able: be able to pierce; in the verse negated, of weapons that cannot pierce at all) (s:sunlet/pailet) (b:bun) (q:draft)
bup = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:entire/whole/complete) (d:complete, with no part left out; {a bup-in} is as a whole, entirely) (s:buppi)
bup = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:whole/entire) (d:placed after the noun it describes: {minam bup} is the whole nation) (s:buppi)
bupa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:captain/centurion/officer) (d:commander of a unit of men, <pa> marks a man; {galkap bupa} is a centurion) (s:galkapbu) (q:draft)
bupah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:throughout/over the whole) (d:<bup> whole with the place marker <ah>, after a noun: {leitung bupah} is in the whole earth) (b:bup) (q:draft)
bupin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:wholly/entirely/as a whole) (d:<bup> whole with {-in}; {a minam bupin} is the whole nation, {a bupin hal} is burn it whole) (b:bup) (r:2.29.18) (q:draft)
bupkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one whole/single unit) (d:<bup>, whole, with <khat>, one: one complete piece) (q:draft)
buppi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:whole/entire) (d:<bup>, whole, with <pi>: the whole of something; placed after the noun, as {leitung buppi}, the whole world) (s:bup) (b:bup) (q:draft)
buppiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:offer/give wholly/surrender) (d:<bup> whole with <piak> give: give oneself over completely) (q:draft)
buppite = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:whole/entire) (d:<buppi> whole with the plural <te>, after a noun for a group of people; {mihon buppite} is the whole assembly) (b:buppi) (q:draft)
bupun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as a whole/all together/entirely) (d:<bup>, whole, with the plural ending <un>; follows a group noun: {a innkuan bupun}, his whole household) (b:bup) (q:draft)
busak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hide/conceal) (d:causative of <bu>, hide: put someone into hiding) (s:seel) (b:bu) (q:draft)
busim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hide/lie hidden) (d:<bu>, hide, with <sim>, secretly: hide oneself, stay unnoticed) (s:bu) (q:draft)
butawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hide oneself/hide) (d:<bu>, hide, with <tawm>, do by or for oneself) (s:bu) (q:draft)
bute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:officers/commanders) (d:Plural of <bu>, an officer: {palik bute} are the officers who serve the magistrates, and {galkapte le a bute} are the soldiers and their commanders.) (s:palikbute) (q:draft)
bute = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who hide/those in hiding) (d:<Bu>, hide or take shelter, with the plural <te>: those who are hiding, as in {leihawm sunga bute}, those hiding in caves.) (b:bu) (q:draft, low confidence)
butsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put on/slip on) (d:Put a ring or bracelet on the hand or arm of another person; built with the causative <sak>.) (q:draft)
butsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:putting on/put on) (d:{Butsak}, put a bracelet or ring on another person, with the linking ending <in> that joins it to the next verb.) (b:butsak) (q:draft)
Buz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Buz) (d:name of two men, a son of Nahor the brother of Abraham and a man of the tribe of Gad; also an Arabian people named with Dedan and Tema) (r:1.22.21)
Buzi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Buzi) (d:priest, the father of the prophet Ezekiel) (r:26.1.3)
cangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at that time/then) (d:Found once in {tua cangin}, at that time; probably another spelling or a misprint of <ciangin>.) (s:ciangin) (q:draft, low confidence)
Christian = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Christian) (d:A follower of Christ; the English word taken over unchanged.) (q:draft)
Christiante = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Christiante/Christians) (d:the Christians, followers of Christ) (b:Christian) (r:42.24.9)
ci = (i:1) (t:v) (w:command/order) (d:say as an order; <ci-in> after the quoted words reports the command that was given)
ci = (i:3) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case)
Ci = (i:1) (t:n) (w:salt) (d:{Ci}, salt, written with a capital in place names: {Ci Tuipi} is the Salt Sea or Dead Sea, {Ci Kuam} the Valley of Salt and {Ci Khuapi} the City of Salt.) (b:ci) (r:13.18.12) (q:draft)
cia = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:as big as/the size of/as much as) (d:Placed after a thing to give size or extent by comparison, as in {khut peek cia}, a handbreadth wide; {bang cia-in} asks how big.) (q:draft)
ciahhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be long in returning/return late) (d:{Ciah}, return, with <hak>, slow or late: be a long time in coming back.) (q:draft)
ciahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:returning/going home/coming back) (d:{Ciah}, return or go home, with the linking ending <in>: returned and then did the next thing.) (s:ciahkikin/paikikin) (b:ciah) (q:draft)
ciahkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:return together/go back together) (d:{Ciah}, return, with <khawm>, together: go back together with others.) (b:ciah) (q:draft)
ciahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leave/go away/depart) (d:{Ciah}, go home or return, with <khia>, out: go out and away from a place.) (b:ciah) (q:draft)
ciahkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send away/send off/dismiss) (d:{Ciahkhia}, leave, with the causative <sak>: let or make someone go on his way.) (s:ciahsak/paikhiasak) (b:ciahkhia) (q:draft)
ciahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leave/depart/go away) (d:Form of <ciahkhia>, leave, used before <ding>, <ciangin> and <khit>.) (s:paikhiat) (b:ciahkhia) (q:draft)
ciahkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have returned/have gone back) (d:{Ciah}, return, with <khin>, already done: have gone back.) (b:ciah) (q:draft)
ciahkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:returning/going back/coming back) (d:{Ciahkik}, return, with the linking ending <in> that joins it to the next action: returned and then.) (s:ciahin/paikikin) (b:ciahkik) (q:draft)
ciahkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:return/going back/coming back) (d:{Ciahkik}, return, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of going or coming back.) (s:paikikna) (b:ciahkik) (q:draft)
ciahkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send back/let return/make return) (d:{Ciahkik}, return, with the causative <sak>: send someone back or let him go back.) (s:ciahsakkik/paisakkik/sawlkik) (b:ciahkik) (q:draft)
ciahkiksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:letting return/let go back) (d:{Ciahkik}, return, with the causative <sak> and the linking ending <in>: allowing someone to go back.) (b:ciahkiksak) (q:draft)
ciahkikte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who returned/returned exiles) (d:{Ciahkik}, return, with the plural <te>: the people who came back, said of the exiles who returned from Babylon.) (b:ciahkik) (q:draft)
ciahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who has returned/one who has come back) (d:{Ciah}, return, with <pa>, the man who does it: the man who has come back.) (b:ciah) (q:draft)
ciahpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go home at once/return immediately) (d:{Ciah}, go home, with <pah>, at once: go home straight away.) (q:draft)
ciahpahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:going away at once/returning immediately) (d:{Ciahpah}, go home at once, with the linking ending <in> that joins it to the next action.) (b:ciahpah) (q:draft)
ciahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring back/take back/take home) (d:{Ciah}, go home, with <pih>, together with: take or bring someone or something along to one’s home or back to a place.) (b:ciah) (r:1.14.16) (q:draft)
ciahpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking home/bringing back/carrying off) (d:{Ciahpih}, take home with one, with the linking ending <in>; another verb follows.) (b:ciahpih) (q:draft)
ciahpihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring back/take back) (d:{Ciahpih}, take along home, with <kik>, back: bring or take someone or something back.) (b:ciahpih) (q:draft)
ciahpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:taking back/carrying off) (d:{Ciahpih}, take back with one, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of taking someone away to one’s own place.) (b:ciahpih) (q:draft)
ciahpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things brought home/what is brought in) (d:<ciahpih>, bring home, with the plural <te>: the things one has brought back) (b:ciahpih) (q:draft)
ciahpihto = (t:see) <ciahpihto-in>
ciahpihto-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bringing back up/taking back up) (d:<ciahpih>, bring back, with <to>, upward, and the suffix <in>) (q:draft)
ciahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send away/dismiss/send home) (d:{Ciah}, go home, with the causative <sak>: let or make someone go home; followed by <kik>, send back.) (s:paisak/ciahkhiasak/paikhiasak) (b:ciah) (r:57.1.12) (q:draft)
ciahsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sending away/sending off/sending home) (d:{Ciahsak}, send away, with the linking ending <in> that joins it to the next action.) (b:ciahsak) (q:draft)
ciahsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send back/let return/send away) (d:{Ciahsak}, send home, with <kik>, back or again: send someone back or let him return.) (s:ciahkiksak/paisakkik/sawlkik) (b:ciahsak) (q:draft)
ciahsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sending away/dismissal) (d:{Ciahsak}, send away, with the noun suffix <na>: the sending away of someone, in Isaiah 50.1 of a wife sent away in divorce.) (s:sawlkhiatna) (b:ciahsak) (q:draft)
ciahsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leave/desert/separate from) (d:{Ciah}, go home, with <san>, away from: go off and leave someone behind.) (s:nusia/taisan/paisan) (b:ciah) (q:draft)
ciahsuakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go straight home at once) (d:{Ciah}, return, with <suak>, straight through, and <pah>, at once: go straight home without stopping.) (q:draft)
ciahsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go down home/go home/return down) (d:{Ciah}, go home or return, with <suk>, downward: go down to one’s home.) (a:ciahto) (b:ciah) (q:draft)
ciahto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go up home/go back up/come up) (d:{Ciah}, return, with <to>, upward: return or go home to a higher place.) (a:ciahsuk) (b:ciah) (r:43.6.62) (q:draft)
ciahzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:after returning/have gone home) (d:<ciah>, return, with <zawh>, after finishing: in the verse, counting days from when they had gone) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:growl/snarl) (d:Make the low rough sound of lion cubs.) (q:draft)
ciakciak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:chatter/babble) (d:talk on and on, said of fools who multiply words) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:return/come back) (d:Said of those who came back from captivity; apparently another spelling or a misprint of <ciahkik>.) (s:ciahkik) (q:draft, low confidence)
cial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hire) (d:Engage someone to work or to fight for pay.) (s:guai) (q:draft)
cial = (i:2) (t:n) (w:step/stair/level) (d:One step of a stairway, {kahlei cial}, or one level of a building.) (q:draft)
cialin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hiring/hire) (d:{Cial}, hire, with the linking ending <in>: hiring someone and then going on to the next action.) (b:cial) (q:draft)
cialna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hiring/hire) (d:{Cial}, hire, with the noun suffix <na>: the hiring of people, or what is spent to hire them.) (s:guaihna) (b:cial) (q:draft)
cialpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:employer/one who hires) (d:{Cial}, hire, with <pa>, the man who does it: the one who hires or sends a worker.) (b:cial) (q:draft)
cialte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hired men/mercenaries/hired workers) (d:{Cial}, hire, with the plural <te>: those who are hired; {galkap cialte} are mercenaries.) (s:thacialte) (b:cial) (q:draft)
cialte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:levels/storeys) (d:Plural of <cial>, step or level: the floors of a building.) (b:cial) (q:draft)
ciam = (i:2) (t:v) (w:taste/sample) (d:Try a little food or drink.) (s:ciap) (r:42.14.24) (q:draft)
ciamciam = (t:todo) (q:draft, doubled form after {khemzawh thu mah}, of the treacherous who go on betraying; meaning of the word itself not clear from the verse)
ciamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swearing/promising/vowing) (d:{Ciam}, promise or swear, with the linking ending <in>; often after <thu> or <kam>.) (s:kiciamin/kamciamin) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
ciamin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:tasting/taste) (d:{Ciam}, taste, with the linking ending <in>.) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
ciamkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taste/get a taste of) (d:{Ciam}, taste, with <kha>, which shows that the action comes to happen: get to taste.) (q:draft)
ciamkha = (i:2) (t:v) (w:pledge/promise) (d:{Ciam}, promise, with <kha>: happen to give one’s word, as in {kam ciamkha}.) (q:draft)
ciamkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make a covenant together/vow together) (d:{Ciam}, promise, with <khawm>, together: join with others in making a promise.) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
ciamkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appoint beforehand/fix in advance) (d:{Ciam}, promise, with <kholh>, beforehand; {a ciamkholh ni} is the appointed day.) (q:draft)
ciamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promise/oath/vow) (d:{Ciam} with the noun suffix <na>: what someone has promised or sworn.) (s:kiciamna/kamciamna) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
ciamna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:will/testament) (d:In {sih ciamna}, a will that takes effect at death.) (b:ciam) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciamnasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:promised) (d:{Ciam}, promise, with <na> and <sa>, already done: describes what has been promised, here the place the Lord promised.) (s:kamciamsa) (b:ciamna) (q:draft)
ciamnui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:joke/jest) (d:Speak in fun and not seriously; compare <ciamnuih>, jest.) (q:draft)
ciamnuih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mockery/ridicule/jest) (d:Mockery or joking at someone’s expense: {ciamnuih bawl} is mock or make fun of someone, {ciamnuih-a neih} is treat as a laughingstock.) (q:draft)
ciamnuihbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:mock/ridicule/make fun of) (d:{Ciamnuih}, mockery, with <bawl>, make: make fun of someone.) (s:zahko/nuihsan) (b:ciamnuih) (q:draft)
ciamnuihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:laughingstock/object of ridicule/byword) (d:A person or people that others make fun of.) (b:ciamnuih) (q:draft)
ciamnuihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:joke/jest) (d:Something said or done in fun: {ka ciamnuihna hi} is I was only joking.) (b:ciamnuih) (q:draft)
ciampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who promised/promiser) (d:{Ciam}, promise, with <pa>, the man who does it: he who made the promise, said of God.) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
ciampak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:vow hastily/promise rashly) (d:{Ciam}, promise or vow, with <pak>, quickly: make a vow in haste.) (r:21.8.2) (q:draft)
ciampek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pin/loom pin) (d:The pin of a loom, with which the woven cloth is beaten tight.) (r:7.16.13) (q:draft)
ciampel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break one's word/break a promise/go back on an oath) (d:{Ciam}, promise, with <pel>, miss: fail to keep a promise; mostly negated, as in {ciampel lo}, keep one’s word.) (q:draft)
ciampelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:breaking one's word/treacherous) (d:{Ciampel}, break a promise, with the linking ending <in>; in a list of faults, treacherous.) (b:ciampel) (q:draft)
ciampelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:faithlessness/breach of promise) (d:<ciampel>, break a promise, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:ciampel) (q:draft)
ciamsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:promised/sworn) (d:{Ciam} with <sa> for a completed act: already promised; {na ciamsa bangin} is as you promised.) (s:kiciamsa) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
ciamsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curse) (d:A curse, or an oath that brings harm; {ciamsiatna ngah} is be cursed.) (s:samsiatna/hamsiatna) (q:draft)
ciamsiatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cursed) (d:{ciamsiat}, curse, with <sa>, already done: that has been cursed) (q:draft)
ciamteh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:note/mark/record/consider) (d:Take note of something, keep it in mind or put it on record.) (a:mangngilh) (q:draft)
ciamtehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:noting/recording/marking/registering) (d:{Ciamteh}, note or record, with the linking ending <in> that joins it to the next verb, often <gelh>, write.) (b:ciamteh) (q:draft)
ciamtehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mark/seal/sign) (d:A mark put on something to show whose it is or to close it: a seal on a scroll, a mark on the body, a sign.) (s:ciaptehna) (b:ciamteh) (r:3.19.28) (q:draft)
ciamtehna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:record/register/account) (d:A written record: {khang ciamtehna} is a genealogy and {sum ciamtehna lai} an account of money.) (s:kiciamtehna/thuciamtehna) (b:ciamteh) (q:draft)
ciamtehnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seals/marks/signs) (d:Plural of <ciamtehna>: the seals on a scroll, marks borne on the body, signs set up on a road.) (b:ciamtehna) (r:66.5.2) (q:draft)
ciamtehnate = (i:2) (t:n) (w:records) (d:plural of <ciamtehna>: things noted down and kept) (b:ciamtehna) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciamtehpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who reckons/one who regards) (d:{Ciamteh}, note or consider, with <pa>, the one who does it: said of God, who counts things not yet existing as existing.) (b:ciamteh) (q:draft)
ciamtehsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marked/noted beforehand/predestined) (d:{Ciamteh}, mark, with <sa> for a completed act: already marked out.) (b:ciamteh) (q:draft)
ciamtehsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:mark/count against) (d:{Ciamteh}, mark or record, with <sak>: put a mark on someone, or hold a sin on record against someone.) (b:ciamteh) (q:draft)
ciamtehteh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep remembering/keep on record) (d:{Ciamteh}, note or record, with the last syllable repeated for continued action: go on holding in mind.) (q:draft)
ciamzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:amount promised/promised sum) (d:<ciam>, promise, with <zah>, amount) (q:draft)
ciamzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have sworn/have promised) (d:{Ciam}, swear, with <zo>, done and settled; <thu> or <kam> stands before it.) (s:kiciamzo) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
cian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build up/pile up/heap) (d:Pile up a heap or build up a wall; written with a final apostrophe in the text.) (q:draft)
cian = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:carefully/intently/clearly) (d:Stands after a verb of looking, thinking or knowing: closely and thoroughly.) (q:draft)
ciang = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:as far as/up to/until) (d:Marks the point reached in place or time, often followed by <dong>.) (s:dong/tan) (q:draft)
ciang = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:when) (d:At the time that; a short form of <ciangin>.) (r:20.30.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ciang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scepter/rod/staff) (d:{Ciang}, rod, written with a capital; {ukna ciang} is the scepter of a ruler.) (b:ciang) (q:draft)
cianga = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:when/after/at the time of) (d:<ciang> with <a>, joining a time clause to the words that follow: when; <khit cianga> means after) (b:ciang) (r:24.17.17) (q:draft)
ciangah = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:at/up to/as far as) (d:<ciang> with the place marker <ah>: at or up to the point named, in place or extent) (b:ciang)
ciangbek = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:only up to/only as far as) (d:<ciang>, up to, with <bek>, only: no further than the number or point named) (q:draft)
ciangciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as far as/up to/to the full extent) (d:doubled <ciang>, every point reached: {tu ciangciang} is thus far, {zah ciangciang} is as much as, and {a ciangciang-ah} is on every side) (s:zahzahin) (q:draft)
ciangduai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rod) (d:a rod or stick used for beating as punishment) (s:ciangpum)
ciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:afterwards/later) (d:after <nung> or <khit>: {a nung ciangin} is afterwards, later on) (s:nungciangin/tuazawh)
ciangin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:then) (d:after <tua>, that: {tua ciangin} is then or and then, the usual way to begin the next step of a story) (r:18.3.2)
cianginleitungah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:then on the earth) (d:the two words <ciangin>, when or after, and <leitungah>, on the earth, printed as one word) (q:draft)
ciangka = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pass/entrance) (d:a narrow way through hills or into a place) (s:mualciang) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ciangka = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pass) (d:<ciangka> written with a capital: the narrow way through the hills at Mikmash) (b:ciangka) (q:draft)
ciangkang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stick/rod) (d:a plain stick or dry rod) (s:ciangkhut) (q:draft)
ciangkangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rods/sticks/branches) (d:plural of <ciangkang>; the rods, peeled to show white, that Jacob set before the flocks) (s:ciangkhutte) (b:ciangkang) (r:1.30.38) (q:draft)
ciangkhaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:carrying poles/baskets) (d:plural; apparently <ciang>, stick, with <khai>, hang: a load carried on a pole, where the English has basket) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciangkhut = (i:1) (t:n) (w:staff/rod/stick/scepter) (d:a stick carried in the hand: a walking staff, a shepherd’s rod or a ruler’s scepter) (s:ciangkang) (r:17.8.4) (q:draft)
ciangkhutah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the goad/on the staff) (d:<ciangkhut>, staff, with the place marker <ah>; {ciangkhutah sik phuh}, fix an iron point on a goad) (b:ciangkhut) (q:draft)
ciangkhutin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as a rod/as a club) (d:<ciangkhut>, staff or rod, with the suffix <in>) (b:ciangkhut) (q:draft)
ciangkhutte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:staffs/rods) (d:plural of <ciangkhut>, staff or rod) (s:ciangkangte) (b:ciangkhut) (q:draft)
ciangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rebuild/repair/build up again) (d:build up again a wall that is broken, from <ciang>, build a wall, and <kik>, again) (s:ciangpha/lamkik/bawlkik) (a:sucim) (q:draft)
ciangpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rebuild/repair) (d:<ciang>, build up a wall, with <pha>, good: repair a broken wall and make it sound again) (s:ciangkik/lampha/bawlpha) (a:sucim) (q:draft)
ciangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:basket/measuring basket) (d:a large basket; in the vision of Zechariah 5 the ephah measuring basket) (s:seeng) (q:draft)
ciangpum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rod/cane) (d:a stick used for beating) (s:ciangduai) (q:draft)
ciangtan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:limit/set measure/fixed extent) (d:a fixed limit, especially of time; {hun ciangtan} is an appointed length of time) (q:draft)
ciangtan = (i:2) (t:v) (w:set a limit/determine/fix/ration) (d:fix the measure or limit of a thing, such as the length of a life or a ration of food) (s:khentat) (q:draft)
ciangtang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shuttle) (d:in {siam ciangtang}, the shuttle of a weaver's loom) (q:draft)
ciangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:builders) (d:those who build up a wall, apparently <cian> build up with the plural <te>; {kulh ciangte} is the builders of the wall) (s:lamte) (q:draft)
ciangto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build up/raise) (d:<ciang> build a wall, with <to> upward: build a wall up high) (b:ciang) (q:draft)
ciangun = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:when/after) (d:postpositional marker indicating its been done) (b:ciang) (r:1.3.5)
ciangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to build up) (d:of a wall; apparently <cian>, build up, with <zo>, be able, and not the word <ciang>, until) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciangzum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:goad) (d:<ciang>, stick, with <zum>, pointed: the pointed stick used to drive oxen) (q:draft)
cianna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:building/rebuilding) (d:<cian> build up with the noun suffix <na>; {kulh cianna} is the building of the wall) (s:lamna) (b:cian) (q:draft)
cianpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:siege ramp/mound) (d:<cian>, pile up, with <pi>, great: a great heap of stones raised against a city wall) (b:cian) (q:draft)
ciantakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:clearly/fully/for certain) (d:<cian> carefully or clearly, with <takin> which makes an adverb) (s:teltakin) (b:cian) (q:draft)
ciap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taste) (d:try the taste of food or drink) (q:draft)
ciapkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:after tasting/have tasted) (d:<ciap>, form of <ciam>, taste, with <khit>, after finishing) (q:draft)
ciapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tasting) (d:<ciap> taste, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of tasting) (b:ciap) (q:draft)
ciaptehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mark/seal) (d:a mark or seal put on a thing or a person to show whose it is) (s:ciamtehna) (r:66.13.17) as in put a mark on objects
ciat = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:each/every one) (d:placed after a noun or verb to show that it applies to each one separately) (s:tek/tuak) (q:draft)
ciatah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:each to/each in) (d:to or in each one's own, placed after a noun of place) (b:ciat) (q:draft)
ciatciat = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:own) (d:doubled <ciat>, each: each one’s own, said of every kind or every land separately)
ciatciatin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:to its kind/each according to its kind) (d:<ciatciat> with the ending <in>, after <nam>, kind: each according to its own kind) (b:ciatciat)
ciatin = (i:1) (t:det) (w:each) (d:<ciat>, each, with the ending <in>: each one separately, as in {min ciatin}, each by name) (b:ciat)
ciatin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:according to/each according to) (d:after <nam>, kind, or <beh>, clan: each according to its own) (b:ciat) (r:1.1.11)
ciatna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<ciat>, each, with the noun suffix <na>, placed after a verb: the fact or the way of each one doing it) (b:ciat) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciatte = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:each of them/each one) (d:<ciat> each, with the plural ending <te>: each one of several) (b:ciat) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciatun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:each/every one) (d:<ciat>, each, with the plural ending <un>: each of them in his own way) (s:tek) (b:ciat) (q:draft)
cici = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep saying/say again and again/urge) (d:reduplicated <ci> say; {hong cici kei in} is do not keep telling me) (s:cihcih) (r:19.70.4) (q:draft)
cidamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in good health/healthy/safe and sound) (d:<cidam>, healthy, with the ending <in>: in good health, unharmed) (s:damin) (b:cidam) (r:42.15.27) (q:draft)
cidamkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be healthy again/recover health) (d:<cidam>, healthy, with <kik>, again; with <sak>, restore to health) (b:cidam) (q:draft)
cidamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:health/healing) (d:noun from <cidam> be healthy; {cidamna ngah} is to be healed) (s:damna) (a:cinatna/natna) (b:cidam) (r:24.8.15) (q:draft)
cidamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make healthy/give health/make well) (d:causative of <cidam>, healthy) (s:damsak) (b:cidam) (q:draft)
cidamsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making healthy/giving health) (d:<cidamsak>, make healthy, with the suffix <in>) (b:cidamsak) (q:draft)
cidamsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore to health/make well again) (d:<cidamsak>, make healthy, with <kik>, again) (s:damsakkik) (b:cidamsak) (q:draft)
Cidamsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be healed/become well) (d:<cidam> healthy with <suak> become; here a command, be well) (q:draft)
cidamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the healthy/healthy ones) (d:<cidam> with the plural <te>: those that are healthy, said of people, animals and sound trees) (a:cinate) (b:cidam) (r:42.5.31) (q:draft)
cidamzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:healthier) (d:<cidam>, healthy, with <zaw>, more) (b:cidam) (q:draft)
cih = (i:1) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (r:4.1.48)
cihbangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as said/according to what is said) (d:<cih>, say, with <bangin>, as, written as one word; {na cihbangin}, as you say) (q:draft)
cihcih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep saying/say again and again) (d:<cih>, form of <ci> say, doubled to show repeated or continued saying) (s:cici) (q:draft)
cihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say/declare/tell) (d:<cih> with the suffix {-in}; in the formula {kong cihin ah}, I say to you, introducing a statement) (b:cih) (q:draft)
cihin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:kindling/lighting) (d:of a fire; {mei cih}, light a fire) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihinah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say/tell) (d:<cihin> with <ah>, in the formula {kong cihinah}, I say to you, introducing a statement) (b:cihin) (q:draft)
cihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do to/do anything to) (d:<cih> do or say, with <kha> happen to: used with <bang> or <bangmah>, do something to someone, usually harm) (q:draft)
cihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:might say/happen to say) (d:<cih>, say, with <khak>, form of <kha>, happen to: of something one fears others may say) (s:genkhak) (q:draft)
cihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have said/finish saying) (d:<cih>, form of <ci>, say, with <khit>, finish; before <ciangin> or <phetin>: after or as soon as someone has said; in Acts 10:16 of a thing having been done) (s:genkhit) (q:draft)
cihmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be in distress/be desperate/be in trouble) (d:be at a loss what to do; also used as a noun for distress or heartache) (s:gentheih) (a:cithei) (q:draft)
cihmawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:distress/need/scarcity/hardship) (d:state of being helpless and in want) (s:gentheihna/haksatna/kisapna) (a:cihtheihna) (b:cihmawh) (q:draft)
cihmawhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:needs/distresses/hardships) (d:plural of <cihmawhna> distress or need) (s:haksatnate/kisapnate) (b:cihmawhna) (q:draft)
cihmawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say/happen to say) (d:<cih> say, with <mawk> carelessly or without ground: say something that does not hold, as in even if it should say) (r:46.12.16) (q:draft)
cihmel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nature/what a thing is like) (d:apparently <cih>, say, with <mel>, appearance: {thutang cihmel thei lo}, not know what justice is; exact sense not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:saying/meaning) (d:what someone says or means, noun form of <cih> say) (s:genna/cihnopna) (b:cih) (r:43.13.24) (q:draft)
cihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:that is/called) (d:what a thing is called or means; after a name, {a cihna} gives another name for the same place or person) (b:cih) (r:6.15.8) (q:draft)
cihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sayings/words/things said) (d:plural of <cihna>; placed after quoted words, these sayings) (b:cihna) (q:draft)
cihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to say/mean to say) (d:<cih> say with <nop> want, the form of <nuam> used in dependent clauses) (s:gennop/cinuam) (q:draft)
cihnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:meaning) (d:what someone means or wants to say) (s:khiatna/gennopna/cihna) (r:41.15.22) (q:draft)
cihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one spoken of) (d:the man of whom something is said, <cih>, say, with <pa> marking a man) (s:kigenpa) (b:cih) (q:draft)
cihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say with/say to/join in saying) (d:<cih>, say, with <pih>, together with or to someone: say a thing in agreement with another) (b:cih) (q:draft)
cihsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:said/have said) (d:what has already been said or proposed, <cih> with <sa> for a completed action; {na cihsa bangin}, as you have said) (s:gensa) (b:cih) (q:draft)
cihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say for/tell on behalf of) (d:<cih> say with <sak>, done for another person: {va cihsak un} is go and say it for me; in Galatians 1:7, let a thing be called by a name) (b:cih) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:kindle for/light for) (d:of a fire, light it for someone) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say to/say at/reply) (d:<cih>, form of <ci> say, with <san>, at or toward someone: say something at a person, often to mock or to dismiss them) (b:cih) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihtaak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be worth mentioning/be enough) (d:apparently <cih>, say, with <taak>, worthy: be worth counting, of a small amount among many people) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihtak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:faithful/loyal/true) (d:true and loyal to a person or to God; {cihtak loh} or {cihtak kei} is to be unfaithful, {cihtak lohna} is unfaithfulness) (s:citak) (a:zulhzau) (r:39.2.14) (q:draft)
cihtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truly/utterly) (d:placed between a repeated word, as {hai cihtakin hai}, to say that it is so in the full sense of the word) (b:cih) (q:draft)
cihtaklohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:unfaithfulness/faithlessness) (d:not being faithful, to God or to a spouse: <cihtak> faithful with <loh> not and {-na}) (a:cihtakna) (q:draft)
cihtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:faithfulness/sincerity/honesty) (d:the quality of being faithful and true, <cihtak> with the noun suffix <na>; {cihtakna tawh} is faithfully) (s:thumanna) (a:cihtaklohna) (b:cihtak) (q:draft)
cihtakzawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be more faithful/be more upright) (d:<cihtak>, faithful, with <zawk>, more: surpass others in doing what is right) (q:draft)
cihtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (d:said of firewood, <sing>: apparently get or use for oneself, with <tawm> marking an action done for oneself; the exact sense of <cih> here is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihte = (i:1) (t:part) (w:such things as/those called) (d:plural of <cih>, placed after a list or a name: the things called, what is called) (s:khawngte) (b:cih) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to say/be able to do) (d:<cih>, say or do, with <thei>, can; with <bangmah> and a negative, be unable to say or do anything) (b:cih) (q:draft)
cihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be well off/have plenty) (d:apparently a form of <cithei> prosper; {a cihtheih pen hun} is the time when he is best off) (a:cihmawh) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihtheih = (i:2) (t:v) (d:<cih> say with <theih> can: it can be said; {cihtheih hi lo} is nothing can be said to him, he is past telling) (b:cih) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:well-being/prosperity/plenty/welfare) (d:state of being well off and at peace, the opposite of <cihmawhna>, need) (s:nopsakna) (a:cihmawhna) (b:cihtheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihtuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:distinction/difference) (d:<cih>, say, with <tuam>, separate: a setting apart; {cihtuam om loin} is without distinction, regardless of) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:amount demanded/as much as one says) (d:<cih>, say, with <zah>, amount: whatever amount someone names) (q:draft)
cihzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (d:<cih>, do, with <zawh>, be able: be able to do something to; {bangmah a cihzawh kei leh} is if it can do nothing to it, if the thing is not harmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can do/be able to do) (d:<cih>, do, with <zo>, be able: be able to do something to someone; {bang hong cihzo ding} is what can they do to me) (s:hihzo) (b:cih) (q:draft)
ciik = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:farthest/extreme) (d:placed after <mong>, end: the very end, the outermost edge) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciil = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:aged/matured/fine) (d:of wine, well aged and of the best kind) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciim = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:clear/healthy/sound) (d:Clear: of the eye, healthy and seeing well; of water, settled and clear.) (r:42.11.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wisdom/skill) (d:Wisdom or skill, a clear and discerning mind; <ciim> with the noun ending <na>.) (s:pilna/siamna/lungpilna) (a:haina) (b:ciim) (q:draft)
ciimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make wise/make discerning) (d:<ciim>, clear in mind, with the causative <sak>: make wise or discerning, as in {mi ciimsate ciimsak}, make those who are already wise still wiser) (b:ciim) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciimsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:drench/soak) (d:soak through, in {kawt ciimsak}, said of rain wetting people to the skin) (s:kawtciimsak/kawtsak) (b:ciim) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciimsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the wise/the prudent) (d:<ciim>, here clear in mind or wise, with <sa> already and the plural <te>: people who are already wise) (s:mipilte/mipilsate/pilsate) (a:mihaite) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plant/grow/cultivate) (d:Plant or grow crops; written {ciin’} before a following word or suffix, as in {na ciin’te}, the things you plant.) (s:suan/cin) (q:draft)
ciin = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:continuous/persistent/unceasing) (d:said of rain, {guah ciin} is rain that goes on without stopping) (a:theu) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciing = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:barren/childless) (d:Unable to bear children; said of a woman, and also of animals.) (s:taciing) (q:draft)
ciingin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comb/dress) (d:said of flax thread in {anthul khau ciingin}, where the NIV has combed flax; with the linking ending <in>; not the word <ciing> barren) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciingin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:keep/store up) (d:keep words in the heart so as to use them; with the linking ending <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:growers/planters) (d:those who plant and tend, as in {leenggui ciingte}, vine growers) (q:draft)
ciingte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:barren women/the childless) (d:<ciing>, barren, with the plural <te>, after <numei>, woman) (s:taciingte) (b:ciing) (q:draft)
ciinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:barrenness) (d:the state of a woman who can no longer bear children) (q:draft, low confidence)
cik = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:ever/never) (d:With <mah> and a negative verb, at no time, never: {cik mahin}, {cik mah hunin} and {cik mah ciangin}.) (s:cikmah/cikmahin) (q:draft)
cik = (i:3) (t:n) (w:spring) (d:A spring of water, also as {cik tui} and {cik tuikhuk}.) (s:ciktui/tuinak) (q:draft, low confidence)
cika = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:when) (d:Question word asking about a time in the past, <cik> with the ending <a>: when was it that.) (s:cikin/cikciang/cikciangin) (b:cik) (q:draft)
cikciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:when) (d:question word of time, at what time) (s:cikciangin/cikin/cika) (q:draft)
cikciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:when) (d:question word of time, <cikciang> with the marker <in>) (s:cikciang/cikin/cika) (b:cikciang) (q:draft)
cikha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say/happen to say) (d:<ci> say with <kha>, which marks what might happen: {cikha kei in} is do not say, {cikha thei} is may well say) (s:genkha) (q:draft)
cikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:declare/say out) (d:<ci>, say, with <khia>, out: speak out openly) (s:genkhia/pulak) (b:ci) (q:draft)
cikhuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillar of salt) (d:<ci>, salt, with <khuam>, pillar) (q:draft)
cikhuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:salt pit/salt marsh) (d:<ci>, salt, with <khuk>, pit: a pit or pool where salt is left.) (q:draft)
cikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say again/say back/repeat) (d:<ci>, say, with <kik>, again or back: say once more, or say in reply) (s:genkik) (b:ci) (q:draft)
cikin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:when) (d:question word of time, at what time, from <cik>) (s:cika/cikciang/cikciangin) (b:cik) (q:draft)
cikin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:closely/carefully) (d:after <en>, look: examine closely, watch carefully) (s:limtakin) (q:draft, low confidence)
cikmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:ever) (d:At any time; used with <hun> or <ciangin> and a negative verb, where the whole phrase means never.) (s:cik)
cikmahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:never) (d:<cikmah> with the adverb ending <in>; used with <ngei> and a negative verb for never.) (s:cikmah) (b:cikmah)
ciknawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:marsh/swamp) (d:Marsh or swamp, wet ground where reeds grow.) (s:nawng)
Ciknawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:marsh/swamp) (d:<ciknawng> written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (s:nawng) (b:ciknawng) (q:draft)
ciksa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scoff/hiss) (d:what passers-by do in scorn at a ruined city; the exact action is not clear from the verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
cikte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:springs/fountains) (d:plural of <cik>, spring of water) (s:ciktuite/tuinakte) (b:cik) (q:draft)
ciktui = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seep) (d:Water that seeps or wells up out of the ground.)
ciktui = (i:2) (t:n) (w:natural spring/pulsing spring/seep spring/spring/fountain) (d:A natural spring, a place where water comes up out of the ground; <cik>, spring, with <tui>, water.) (s:cik/tuinak)
ciktuite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seeps/springs) (d:Plural of <ciktui>: springs of water.) (s:cikte/tuinakte) (b:ciktui) see <ciktui>
cikze = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spare/hold back) (d:in {cikze het loin}, without holding back at all, without pity) (q:draft, low confidence)
cikzet = (t:see) <cikzet-huai>
cikzet-huai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:horrifying/dreadful) (d:<cikzet> with <huai>, causing that feeling; with <a> before it, a thing of horror, an object of dread to those who see it) (s:cikzethuai/lauhuai/kihtakhuai) (q:draft)
cikzethuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:horrifying/repulsive/dreadful) (d:causing horror or disgust, {a cikzethuai} is a thing of horror) (s:cikzet-huai/lauhuai/kihtakhuai/dipkuathuai) (r:5.28.37) (q:draft)
cikziat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:loathe/be disgusted) (d:with <huai>, worthy of: {a cikziat huai} is repulsive, loathsome) (q:draft, low confidence)
cil = (i:1) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate nominative case)
cil = (i:2) (t:part) (d:particle suffixed to form verb past tense)
cil = (i:3) (t:conj) (w:beginning/at first) (d:early stage)
cil = (i:4) (t:n) (w:spit/saliva) (d:Spit, the saliva of the mouth; {cil sia} is to spit, and {cil tawh phih} is to spit on someone.) (r:41.8.23)
cila = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the beginning/at first) (d:<cil> the early stage or beginning, with the ending <a>: at the beginning of; {cila kipan} is from the beginning of) (s:cilin) (b:cil) (q:draft)
cilai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still say/yet say) (d:<ci>, say, with <lai>, still: go on to say, say even so) (q:draft)
cilbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be scarce/be sparing) (d:{cilbawl loin an ne} is eat food without scarcity, without having to be sparing; the exact sense is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
cilcil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thresh/tread out) (d:<cil> thresh by treading, repeated to show continuing action: be busy threshing) (s:ancil/buhcil) (q:draft)
cilesa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flesh/body/flesh and blood) (d:The flesh of the body; of kin, {eima cilesa} is our own flesh and blood.) (s:silesa) (a:kha) (q:draft)
cilgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thresh/trample) (d:<cil>, tread or thresh, with <gawp>, thoroughly or violently) (s:tuancil) (q:draft)
cilin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the beginning/in the beginning/at first) (d:<cil>, the beginning, with the ending <in>: at first, in the beginning, often as {a kipat cilin}.) (s:cila) (a:nunungin) (b:cil) (q:draft)
cilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:winepress/press) (d:place of treading; {leenggah cilna} is the place where grapes are trodden for their juice) (s:leenggahcilna/leenggahsukna/sukna) (b:cil) (q:draft)
cilna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:beginning/start/first time) (d:<cil>, the first stage, with the noun ending <na>: the beginning of something, as in {kipat cilna}, the very beginning, and {khualzin cilna}, the first journey) (s:kipatna/patna) (a:tawpna) (b:cil) (q:draft)
cilna = (i:3) (t:n) (w:threshing floor) (d:in {an cilna}, the place where grain is trodden out) (s:ancilna/buhcilna) (b:cil) (q:draft)
cilpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:treader/one who treads) (d:<cil>, tread, with <pa> marking a man: the man who treads grapes in the winepress) (q:draft)
cilphih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spit on/spit at) (d:Spit on someone as an insult; from <cil>, saliva.) (s:cilpih) (r:41.15.19) (q:draft)
cilphihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spitting on) (d:<cilphih>, spit on, with <in> linking it to the following verb) (b:cilphih) (q:draft)
cilphihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spitting) (d:noun form of <cilphih>, spit on: being spat on as an insult) (b:cilphih) (q:draft)
cilphuan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foam/froth/saliva) (d:foam or running spittle at the mouth; {cilphuan bua} is to foam at the mouth) (q:draft)
cilpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spit at/spit on) (d:<cil>, saliva, with <pih>: spit on someone in contempt) (s:cilphih) (b:cil) (q:draft)
cilsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:threshed grain) (d:<cil>, thresh, with <sa>, already done, and plural <te>: what has been threshed) (q:draft)
ciltang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:testicle) (q:draft)
ciltangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:testicles) (d:plural of <ciltang>) (b:ciltang) (q:draft)
cilte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:firstborn) (d:<cil> first with the plural <te>, after <tapa> son: {tapa cilte} is firstborn sons) (s:tacilte) (b:cil) (q:draft)
ciltel = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fine/small) (d:describes the manna lying on the ground, something small and thin like flakes; the exact sense is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
cilun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:when first/at first) (d:<cil> at first, in the early stage, with the plural ending <un>: when they first did something) (b:cil) (q:draft)
cilvui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thresh to powder/grind fine) (d:<cil> thresh or tread, with <vui> fine as dust: thresh grain until it is crushed) (q:draft, low confidence)
cim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall/collapse) (d:Fall down or cave in, said of a city, a wall or a mountain.) (s:puk/kicim) (q:draft)
cim = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be weary of/have enough/be tired of) (d:Have had enough of something, be sated or fed up with it.) (s:cimtak) (q:draft)
cimang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die out/perish/be wiped out) (d:Die out and leave no descendants; said of a person or family whose line comes to an end.) (s:cimit/mangthang) (q:draft)
cimawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:needy/helpless/destitute) (d:In want or distress with no one to help; also used as a verb, be helpless.) (s:zawng/zawngkhal) (a:hau) (q:draft)
cimawhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:helplessly/in distress/desperately) (d:<cimawh> with the adverb ending <in>: in a helpless or distressed way) (b:cimawh) (q:draft)
cimawhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:needy man/the needy) (d:<cimawh>, needy, with <pa> marking a man) (s:zawngpa) (a:haupa) (b:cimawh) (q:draft)
cimawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leave helpless/afflict/fail) (d:make someone helpless or destitute, <cimawh> with the causative <sak>) (s:zawngkhalsak) (b:cimawh) (q:draft)
cimawhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the needy/the poor/the destitute) (d:people who are in need, often as {mi cimawhte}) (s:mizawngte/zawngte/cimmawhte) (a:haute/mihaute) (b:cimawh) (q:draft)
cimbeng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:glaze/silver dross) (d:a coating smeared on an earthen pot, where the NIV has silver dross) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse/fall down) (d:form of <cim> with the linking suffix <in>, collapsing and then going on to the next action) (s:pukin) (b:cim) (q:draft)
cimit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish/be wiped out/die out) (d:be destroyed so that none is left) (s:cimang/mangthang) (q:draft)
cimitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:complete destruction/total ruin) (d:<cimit> come to a complete end, with the noun suffix <na>; in {siat cimitna}, total destruction) (b:cimit) (q:draft)
cimkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make collapse/bring down) (d:<cim>, fall or collapse, with <khia>, out, and causative <sak>: cause a wall to fall down) (s:cimsak) (q:draft)
