dapphah = (t:see) <dapphah-in>
dapphah-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:using as a backing/laying against) (d:<dap>, pad, with <phah>, lay under, and linking <in>: with the door behind the ear as a support) (q:draft, low confidence)
dapphahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:using as a backing/laying against) (d:<dap>, pad, with <phah>, lay under, and linking <in>: with the door behind the ear as a support) (q:draft, low confidence)
dapphahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:saddle blankets/saddle cloths) (d:<dap> pad with <phah> spread and the plural <te>: cloths spread on the back of a horse for riding) (q:draft)
daptakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:silently/speechlessly/in silence) (d:<dap> silent or dumbfounded, with <takin> which makes an adverb: without saying a word, in wonder or dismay) (b:dap) (q:draft)
Dara = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darda) (d:son of Zerah and grandson of Judah) (r:13.2.6)
Darda = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darda) (d:wise man, one of the sons of Mahol, whose wisdom Solomon surpassed) (r:11.4.31)
Darias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darius) (d:name of several kings, among them Darius the Mede in the book of Daniel and the king of Persia under whom the temple was rebuilt) (r:27.9.1/27.5.31)
darik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:daric) (d:a Persian gold coin, used in counting gold given for the temple) (q:draft)
Darius = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darius) (d:name of several kings of Media and Persia, written <Darias> in the Bible text)
Darkon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darkon) (d:ancestor of a family among the descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.56/16.7.58)
Dathan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dathan) (d:son of Eliab of the tribe of Reuben, who rebelled against Moses with Korah and Abiram and was swallowed by the earth) (r:4.16.1/19.106.17)
dau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fortune/prosperity) (d:used with <pai> go in the expression {dau pai}, prosper or fare well; {a dau pai lo} is he does not prosper) (s:maa) (q:draft, low confidence)
daupai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prosper/succeed/do well) (d:be prosperous, secure and at peace; {daupai sak} make someone prosper) (s:maavang/cithei) (q:draft)
daupaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prosperity/success/well-being) (d:the state of doing well and thriving) (s:maavanna/cihtheihna) (a:kamsiatna) (b:daupai) (q:draft)
daupainate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blessings/prosperity/good things) (d:plural of <daupaina> prosperity) (b:daupaina) (q:draft)
daupaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make prosper/give success) (d:cause to succeed or flourish; <daupai> with the causative <sak>) (s:citheisak/tuahphasak/telhsak) (b:daupai) (q:draft)
daupaisakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who makes prosper) (d:<daupaisak>, make prosper, with <pa> marking a man: the one who gives success) (b:daupaisak) (q:draft)
David = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:David) (d:son of Jesse of Bethlehem, the shepherd who became the second king of Israel) (r:19.72.20/8.4.17)
dawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw/pull out/unsheathe) (d:pull something out or back, most often draw a sword from its sheath; {khut dawh tum kik} is to draw the hand back in) (s:dok) (a:siatkik) (q:draft)
dawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:hold out/offer/stretch out) (d:hold out a part of the body or a thing toward someone, to receive or to offer it; {bil dawh}, hold out the ear, is to listen or pay attention, and {ngawng dawh}, hold out the neck, is to risk one's life) (q:draft)
dawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold out/stretch out) (d:form of <dawh>, hold out, with the linking suffix <in>; {khut dawhin ngen}, ask with the hand held out, is to beg) (s:zanin) (b:dawh) (q:draft)
dawhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull out/snatch out) (d:<dawh>, pull, with <khiat>, out: pull or snatch something out, as out of a fire) (s:kaikhia) (b:dawh) (q:draft)
dawhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:revoke/withdraw/recall) (d:<dawh>, pull out, with <kik>, back: take back or cancel a written order) (s:dokkik) (b:dawh) (q:draft)
dawhlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold out also/offer as well) (d:<dawh>, hold out, with <lai>, still or besides: hold out the other one too) (q:draft)
dawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vat) (d:<dawh>, hold out to receive, with the noun suffix <na>; {leenggahtui dawhna} is the vat that catches the juice from the winepress) (b:dawh) (q:draft)
dawhsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:drawn/unsheathed) (d:<dawh>, draw, with <sa>, already done: of a sword, drawn from its sheath) (s:kidoksa) (b:dawh) (r:4.22.31) (q:draft)
dawi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:demon/evil spirit/devil) (d:an evil spirit; {dawi hawlkhia} is to drive out a demon and {dawi lut} is to be possessed by one) (s:dawigilo/dawilawm/khagilo) (q:draft)
dawibia = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:heathen/pagan/uncircumcised) (d:spirit-worshipping, from <dawi> spirit and <bia> worship; used in the Bible for the uncircumcised and for those who do not know God) (q:draft)
dawibiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:demon worship/pagan worship) (d:<dawi>, demon or spirit, with <biakna>, worship; {dawibiakna mun} is a pagan shrine and {dawibiakna tau} a pagan altar) (q:draft)
dawibiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pagans/heathens/Gentiles) (d:<dawibia> with the plural <te>: those who worship spirits, used for the nations who do not know God) (s:lawkite) (b:dawibia) (q:draft)
dawigilo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil spirit/demon) (d:<dawi>, spirit, with <gilo>, evil; {dawigilo lut} is to be possessed by an evil spirit) (s:dawi/dawilawm/khagilo) (r:66.16.16) (q:draft)
dawigilote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:demons/evil spirits/devils) (d:<dawigilo>, evil spirit, with the plural <te>) (s:dawite) (b:dawigilo) (q:draft)
dawilawm = (i:1) (t:n) (w:demon/evil spirit) (d:an evil spirit that takes hold of a person; {dawilawm nei} is to have a demon, to be demon-possessed) (s:dawi/dawigilo/khagilo) (q:draft)
dawilok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disturbed/be alarmed) (d:said of the heart: be shaken, disturbed or frightened; {a sin a dawilok tuan loh} is that its heart is not disturbed at all) (s:patau) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawilutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:demon possession) (d:<dawi> evil spirit, <lut> enter, with the noun suffix <na>; before <mipa>, the man possessed by an evil spirit) (q:draft)
Dawimang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prince of demons/ruler of demons) (d:<dawi> demon with <mang> lord or chief; {dawimang lianpen pa} is the chief ruler of the demons) (q:draft)
dawimangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:devil) (d:the devil, chief of the evil spirits; <dawi> evil spirit and <mang> chief, with <pa> for a male person) (q:draft)
Dawimangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:devil/evil one) (d:the devil, literally the chief of the demons; written with a capital letter as a title or at the start of a sentence) (r:59.4.7) (q:draft)
dawite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:demons/evil spirits) (d:<dawi>, demon, with the plural <te>; {dawite hawlkhia} is to drive out demons) (s:dawigilote) (b:dawi) (r:41.3.11) (q:draft)
dawivai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:demonic) (d:of or from evil spirits) (q:draft)
dawivei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:demon-possessed/possessed) (d:<dawi>, evil spirit: troubled or held by an evil spirit; {dawivei mi} is a person possessed by a demon) (q:draft)
Dawiveite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:demon-possessed people) (d:<dawivei> possessed by a demon with the plural <te>, at the start of a sentence) (q:draft)
dawizek = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:unclean/defiled) (d:ritually unclean, of a thing that may not be eaten or touched) (s:nin) (a:siang) (q:draft)
dawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:project/jut out/stick out/come out) (d:stand out from a surface or line, said of a tower, a cliff, the end of a staff) (s:dawkkhia) (q:draft)
dawk = (i:2) (t:n) (w:bay/inlet) (d:in {tuipi dawk} or {tui dawk}, a part of the sea that juts into the land) (s:tuidawk) (q:draft)
dawkin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:jut out/project/come forward) (d:form of <dawk>, stick out, with the linking suffix <in>; of a crag, stand out toward a place; {mai dawk} is to step forward) (b:dawk) (q:draft)
dawkkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:project/stick out/come out) (d:<dawk> emerge with <khia> out) (b:dawk) (q:draft)
dawkkikto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rise up again/come up again) (d:<dawk> emerge, <kik> again, <to> upward) (q:draft)
dawksa = (t:see) <dawksa-in>
dawksa-in = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bared/exposed/uncovered) (d:<dawk> stick out or show, with <sa> already done and the linking ending <in>: with a part of the body left showing) (q:draft)
dawksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lay bare/expose/put out) (d:make something show or stick out, <dawk> with the causative <sak>) (b:dawk) (q:draft)
dawksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stretch out/put out/extend) (d:<dawk> stick out, with the causative <sak> and the linking ending <in>: holding out the tip of a staff) (b:dawksak) (q:draft)
dawkto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rise up/come up) (d:<dawk> emerge with <to> upward) (a:tumsuk) (b:dawk) (q:draft)
dawktoh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rise up/tower/jut up) (d:<dawk> jut out, with <toh> upward: stand up high above the surroundings, said of a mountain) (b:dawkto) (q:draft)
dawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deck) (d:a deck of a ship, one of the storeys of the ark)
dawl = (i:3) (t:n) (w:level) (d:one of the levels of a building, counted one above another) (s:cial)
dawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spare/deal gently with/be lenient with) (d:treat with care or mercy, hold back from harming; in oaths {hong dawm kei ta hen} is may he not spare me, and {dawm loin} is without mercy) (s:hehpih) (q:draft)
dawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:deal gently with/treat with care) (d:<dawm> treat with care, with the linking ending <in>: gently, considerately) (b:dawm) (q:draft)
dawn = (i:3) (t:n) (w:top/tip/end) (d:the top or tip of something, as in {mual dawn}, mountain top, {ciangkhut dawn}, the tip of a staff, and {vun dawn}, foreskin) (s:khung) (a:bul/taw) (q:draft)
dawna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:top/summit/tip) (d:<dawn>, top, with the ending <a>, at or on the top of; {mual dawna biakpiakna munte} are the hilltop places of worship, the high places) (b:dawn) (r:14.14.3) (q:draft)
dawnah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:on top of/at the top of) (d:<dawn>, top, with the place marker <ah>, placed after the noun) (s:tungah) (a:phungah) (b:dawn) (r:11.7.19) (q:draft)
dawndawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink and drink/keep drinking) (d:<dawn> drink said twice, for drinking freely or again and again) (q:draft)
dawngdawng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep answering/answer again and again) (d:<dawng> answer, doubled: go on answering what is asked) (q:draft)
dawngin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:answer/reply) (d:form of <dawng> with the linking suffix <in>, answering, usually before the words spoken) (s:dawngkikin) (b:dawng) (r:8.3.5) (q:draft)
dawngkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:answer/reply/answer back) (d:<dawng>, answer, with <kik>, back: give an answer in return) (s:dawng) (a:dong) (b:dawng) (q:draft)
dawngkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:answering/replying) (d:<dawngkik> answer back, with the linking suffix <in>: answered and went on to say) (s:dawngin) (b:dawngkik) (q:draft)
dawngthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to answer) (d:<dawng> answer with <thei> can) (b:dawng) (q:draft)
dawnin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink) (d:form of <dawn> with the linking ending <in>, used before a following verb) (b:dawn) (r:21.3.13) (q:draft)
dawnin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:answer/reply) (d:form of <dawng>, answer, with the linking ending <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnin = (i:3) (t:v) (w:meet/welcome) (d:form of <dawn>, meet, with the linking ending <in>) (s:dawntuahin) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawnkei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not drink) (d:<dawn> drink with the negative <kei>, used in a prohibition) (q:draft)
dawnkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get to drink/drink) (d:<dawn> drink with <kha>, which shows that the action comes to happen; with <kei>, never get to drink) (q:draft)
dawnkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink together/drink with) (d:<dawn>, drink, with <khawm>, together; often paired with <nekhawm>, eat together) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawnkhawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drinking together) (d:<dawn> drink, <khawm> together, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:dawnkhawm) (q:draft)
dawnkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bud/sprout/put out shoots) (d:<dawn>, the tip or shoot of a plant, with <khia> out) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawnkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink together with/drink along with) (d:<dawn> drink with <khop> together; here swallow something along with the water) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink again) (d:<dawn>, drink, with <kik>, again) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawnkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:answer/reply) (d:<dawnkik> answer back with the noun suffix <na>) (s:thudawnna) (a:thudotna/dotna) (b:dawnkik) (q:draft)
dawnkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:all drink) (d:<dawn> drink with <kim> all, every one drinks) (q:draft)
dawnna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drinking/drink) (d:the act of drinking, from <dawn> drink; {dawnna hai} is a drinking cup) (s:tuidawnna) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawnna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:meeting/place of meeting) (d:the act or place of going to meet someone, from <dawn> meet, welcome) (b:dawn) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnngeek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tender shoot/tender sprig) (d:<dawn> top or tip with <ngeek> tender, the soft topmost shoot of a tree) (s:dawnngek) (q:draft)
dawnngek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tender shoot/tender sprig) (d:<dawn> top or tip with <ngek> tender, the soft topmost shoot of a tree) (s:dawnngeek) (q:draft)
dawnngekte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shoots/tender shoots) (d:<dawnngek>, the young tender tip of a branch, with the plural <te>) (b:dawnngek) (q:draft)
dawnpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:answer promptly/reply at once) (d:<dawn>, the form of <dawng> answer used before a suffix, with <pah> at once) (q:draft)
dawnpawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:melons) (d:named after cucumbers in the list of the foods of Egypt, where the English has melons; with the plural <te>) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give to drink/make drink) (d:<dawn>, drink, with the causative <sak>: give someone a drink or make someone drink) (s:tulh) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawnsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:giving to drink) (d:<dawn> drink, the causative <sak>, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:dawnsak) (q:draft)
dawnsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink secretly/drink in secret) (d:<dawn> drink with <sim> secretly; of stolen water in the proverb) (q:draft)
dawnte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drinkers/those who drink) (d:<dawn>, drink, with the plural <te>: those who drink; in {an nek tui dawnte} also the eating and drinking itself) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawnte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:tops/tips/ends) (d:<dawn>, top or tip, with the plural <te>, as in {mual dawnte}, mountain tops, {bil dawnte}, ear lobes, and {khutpi dawnte}, tips of the thumbs) (a:bulte) (b:dawn) (q:draft)
dawntheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ability to answer/being able to answer) (d:<dawn>, the form of <dawng> answer used before a suffix, with <theih> can and the noun suffix <na>) (q:draft)
dawntuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet/come to meet/confront) (d:go or come to meet someone; of trouble or death, come upon a person) (s:kimu) (q:draft)
dawntuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet/encounter) (d:<dawntuah> with the linking suffix <in>, meeting someone on the way, followed by another verb) (s:dawnin) (b:dawntuah) (q:draft)
dawntuahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one who meets) (d:<dawntuah> meet, with <pa> marking a man; the one who came to meet him) (b:dawntuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnzang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flat top/top/hearth) (d:<dawn> top with <zang> flat; of an altar, the hearth on its top) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnzangteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the tops/mountaintops) (d:<dawnzang> flat top with <teng> all; after <mual>, all the mountaintops) (b:dawnzang) (q:draft)
dawnzum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:peak/pointed summit) (d:<dawn> top with <zum> pointed; a mountain with many peaks is called rugged in the English) (s:mualvum) (r:19.68.16) (q:draft)
dawt = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stab/thrust through/pierce) (d:drive a sword or dagger into someone) (q:draft)
dawtlet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:run through/pierce through) (d:stab right through with a sword) (s:sunlet) (q:draft)
dawtletin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:running through/piercing through) (d:<dawtlet> stab through, with the linking suffix <in>) (s:sunletin) (b:dawtlet) (q:draft)
de = (t:see) <de-in>
De = (t:see) <De-uel>
de-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lighting/kindling) (d:<de> light a torch or lamp, with the linking suffix <in>; meaning taken from the context of torches and lanterns) (q:draft, low confidence)
De-uel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Deuel) (d:man of the tribe of Gad, father of Eliasaph who led the tribe in the wilderness) (r:4.10.20) (q:draft)
Debir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Debir) (d:Canaanite royal city in the hill country of Judah, earlier called Kiriath Sepher, later given to the Levites; also the name of a king of Eglon) (r:6.15.49/6.21.15)
Deborah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Deborah) (d:name of two women: the prophetess and judge of Israel, wife of Lappidoth, and the nurse of Rebekah) (r:1.35.8/7.4.4)
deda = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:follows a word for something flat or wide, such as <peek>, <zai> or <kizal>, and stresses how broadly it spreads; {a peek deda} is the wide sheet of Acts 10, {lupna zai deda} a wide bed) (r:44.10.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dedan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Dedan) (d:son of Raamah in the line of Cush, and also a son of Jokshan, grandson of Abraham and Keturah; his descendants were a trading people of Arabia) (r:1.10.7)
dedu = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:intently/deeply) (d:placed after <lungngai> think: describes thinking long and hard about something, pondering) (q:draft, low confidence)
deek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bargain/barter/haggle) (d:bargain over a thing in order to buy it) (s:sumdek) (q:draft)
deen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strike/hit/fall on) (d:hit with something that falls or is thrown, such as a stone or hail; written with an apostrophe before the next word) (q:draft)
deeng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw at/pelt/stone) (d:throw something at a person; {suang tawh deeng} is stone someone) (s:deng) (r:44.7.58) (q:draft)
deengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stone/pelt/throw at) (d:<deeng>, throw at or strike, with the linking ending <in>; {suang tawh deengin} is to stone someone) (s:dengin) (b:deeng) (q:draft)
deenglum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stone to death/stone) (d:kill by throwing stones, usually as {suang tawh deenglum}; <deeng> throw at, with <lum>, which shows that the blow kills) (s:denglum/denlup) (q:draft)
deengtan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break off/strip) (d:strike so that it breaks off, said of hail stripping the trees; <deeng> strike with <tan> cut off) (q:draft)
deh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sting/strike) (d:pierce with a sting, said of a scorpion) (s:pet) (q:draft)
dehthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to sting) (d:<deh> sting with <thei> can: have the power to sting) (b:deh) (q:draft)
deidai = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very/intensely) (d:placed after <kha> bitter, to strengthen it: very bitter, as bitter as the venom of snakes) (q:draft, low confidence)
deidan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show favoritism/discriminate/be partial) (d:treat people unequally, favouring some over others; {mi deidan} is to show partiality) (q:draft)
deidanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:partiality/discrimination/favoritism/distinction) (d:<deidan> treat people unequally, with the noun suffix <na>; {mi deidanna} is partiality toward people) (s:angvanna/kideidanna) (b:deidan) (q:draft)
deihdeih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desire/whatever one desires/wish) (d:<deih> want said twice, with <a> before it: the very thing or everything that one wants) (s:deihna) (q:draft)
deihdeihin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as much as one wants/freely/liberally) (d:<deihdeih>, whatever one wants, with the adverb ending <in>: without limit, as much as anyone wishes) (s:ututin) (b:deihdeih) (q:draft)
deihdeihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desires/all that is desired) (d:<deihdeih>, what one desires, with the plural <te>: all that is desired) (s:deihnate) (b:deihdeih) (q:draft)
deihgawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:covet/crave/desire greedily) (d:want strongly something that belongs to another or that is not good to want) (s:duhgawh/iplah) (q:draft)
deihgawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil desire/lust/craving/covetousness) (d:<deihgawh> covet with the noun suffix <na>: strong desire, in the verses mostly evil desire) (s:lunggulhna) (b:deihgawh) (q:draft)
deihgawhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil desires/lusts/cravings) (d:plural of <deihgawhna>: strong, mostly sinful desires) (s:lunggulhnate/deihluatnate) (b:deihgawhna) (q:draft)
deihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:pleasant/pleasing) (d:<deih> want with <huai>, worthy of: good to have or to look at, giving pleasure) (b:deih)
deihhuai = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:satisfying/acceptable/pleasing) (d:found good enough to be accepted, pleasing to the one who receives it; {deihhuai sa} is to find something pleasing) (s:lungkimhuai) (b:deih)
deihhuai = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:attractive/lovely/desirable) (d:worth wanting because of beauty or value; with <zaw>, more desirable than something else) (s:ngaihbaang) (a:muhdahhuai/kihhuai) (b:deih)
deihhuaina = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:desired/desirable) (d:<deihhuai> desirable with the suffix <na>: the quality that makes a thing or person wanted) (b:deihhuai)
deihhuaizaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more desirable/more precious) (d:<deihhuai> desirable with the comparative <zaw>; the thing it is compared with takes <sang> or <sangin>, than) (s:manphazaw) (b:deihhuai) (q:draft)
deihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wanting/desiring/wishing for) (d:<deih> want with the linking ending <in>: wanting something, used before a following verb) (s:lunggulhin) (b:deih) (q:draft)
deihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want again/desire again) (d:<deih> want with <kik> again: want someone or something a second time) (b:deih) (q:draft)
deihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:that one wants/the fact of wanting) (d:<deih> want with <lam>, which turns the clause into the thing that is known: {ka deihlam} is that I want) (q:draft)
deihlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:what is not wanted/ungodliness) (d:<deih> want, <loh> not, with the noun suffix <na>; {Pasian’ deihlohna} is what God does not want, ungodliness) (q:draft)
deihlua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want too much/be greedy for/love excessively) (d:<deih> want with <lua> too much; with <sum>, be a lover of money) (s:deihgawh) (b:deih) (q:draft)
deihluat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want too much/crave/love excessively) (d:form of <deihlua> used before <leh>, <in> and <mahmah> and in dependent clauses; also as a noun, craving) (s:duhluat) (b:deihlua) (q:draft)
deihluatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:desiring too much/loving too much) (d:<deihluat> desire too much, with the linking ending <in>: loving something too much) (b:deihluat) (q:draft)
deihluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:zeal/strong desire/eagerness/excessive love) (d:<deih> want, <luat> too much, with the noun suffix <na>: a very strong desire for something; {sum deihluatna} is the love of money) (s:kinna) (b:deihluat) (q:draft)
deihluatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:excessive desires/lusts) (d:<deihluat> desire excessively, with the noun suffix <na> and the plural <te>) (s:deihgawhnate) (b:deihluatna) (q:draft)
deihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desire/will/wish/purpose) (d:<deih> want with the noun suffix <na>: what someone wants; {Pasian’ deihna} is the will of God and {lungsim deihna} the desire of the heart) (s:utna/lunggulhna) (b:deih) (r:25.3.37) (q:draft)
deihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desires/wishes/will) (d:plural of <deihna>: the things someone wants; {Pasian’ deihnate} is what God wills) (s:lunggulhnate) (b:deihna) (q:draft)
deihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who wants/one who upholds) (d:<deih> want, with <pa> marking a man: the man who wants something; {thutang a deihpa} is the one who wants justice) (b:deih) (q:draft)
deihpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:devote oneself to/be diligent in) (d:meaning taken from the context, set the heart fully on something) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wish for/want for/desire for/care for) (d:want something for another person or want another to do or be something, care for someone’s good; {deihsak-a satna} is beating out of care, discipline) (a:haza) (b:deih) (q:draft)
deihsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wishing for/desiring for) (d:<deihsak>, want something for someone, with the linking ending <in>: wishing it for them) (b:deihsak) (q:draft)
deihsakluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:zeal/jealousy) (d:<deihsak> want for someone, <luat> exceedingly, with the noun suffix <na>; intense concern for someone) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:favor/goodwill/kindness) (d:<deihsak>, wish someone well, with the noun suffix <na>: favor or goodwill shown to someone) (s:maipha) (b:deihsak) (q:draft)
deihsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wishes/will) (d:<deihsak> want for someone, with the noun suffix <na> and the plural <te>; the things one wishes for another) (s:deihsakte) (b:deihsakna) (q:draft)
deihsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wishes/will) (d:<deihsak> want for someone, with the plural <te>; the things one wishes for another) (s:deihsaknate) (b:deihsak) (q:draft)
deihsakzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:would rather/wish more) (d:<deihsak>, want something for someone, with the comparative <zaw>: wish one thing for them more than another) (b:deihsak) (q:draft)
deihtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:earnestly/eagerly/with care) (d:<deih> want with <takin>, which makes an adverb: with real desire, earnestly, or out of care for someone) (b:deih) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who want/those who love/those who desire) (d:<deih> with the plural <te>; after a possessive, the ones someone wants or chooses) (b:deih) (r:43.5.21) (q:draft)
deihteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all that one wants/whatever one wishes) (d:<deih> want with <teng> all; {mi a deihteng} is all the people he wanted) (b:deih) (q:draft)
deihthuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want more/want in addition) (d:<deih> want with <thuah> in addition: desire still more on top of what one has) (q:draft)
deihzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prefer/would rather/like more) (d:<deih>, want, with comparative <zaw>; the thing it is compared with takes <sangin>, than) (s:utzaw/nuamzaw/teelzaw) (b:deih) (q:draft)
deihzawkna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:preference/preferring) (d:<deihzaw> prefer, in the form {deihzawk}, with the noun suffix <na>: liking one more than another) (q:draft)
deina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:partition/division/separation) (d:what divides one space from another; {deina puan} is the dividing curtain of the temple and {deina kulh} a separating wall) (s:khenna) (b:dei) (q:draft)
deipi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:main hall/main room) (d:<dei> room with <pi> great; {biakinn deipi} is the main hall of the temple) (s:inndeipi) (b:dei) (q:draft)
deisung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bedroom/inner room) (d:the inner room where the bed is; {a lupna deisung} is his bedroom) (q:draft, low confidence)
deite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rooms/chambers) (d:plural of <dei>: the rooms or chambers of a building) (s:inndeite) (b:dei)
dek = (i:1) (t:part) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is about to happen or nearly happens: {si dek}, about to die; {hi dek lo} is far from it, not at all) (r:40.26.38) (q:draft)
Dekapolis = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Decapolis) (d:region of ten Greek cities, most of them east of the Jordan and the Sea of Galilee) (r:41.7.31/40.4.25)
dekdak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very) (d:placed after <khum>, sweet, to strengthen it: very sweet, as sweet as honey) (q:draft, low confidence)
dekdek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:placed after a verb, the action is on the point of happening or has just barely happened) (s:dektak) (q:draft)
dekdekte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those about to/those on the point of) (d:<dekdek> almost, about to, with the plural <te>: {a si dekdekte} is those who are about to die, the perishing) (b:dekdek) (q:draft)
deklo = (t:todo) (q:draft, the function of <dek> with <lo> in {phunphun huai pah deklo hi} is not clear from the single verse)
dekna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being about to/being on the point of) (d:<dek> almost, about to, with the noun suffix <na>: {ka sih dekna} is my being close to dying, faint with love in the English) (b:dek) (q:draft)
dektak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:follows the verb or quantity; {si dektak} is at the point of death) (s:dekdek) (r:14.32.24) (q:draft)
dektaka = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly) (d:<dektak> almost, with the linking suffix <a> before a noun phrase) (b:dektak) (q:draft)
dektakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly) (d:<dektak> almost, with the adverb suffix <in>; {let dektakin}, nearly overflowing, to the brim) (b:dektak) (q:draft)
dektakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being almost/nearness) (d:<dektak> almost, with the noun suffix <na>; {sih dektakna}, being close to death) (b:dektak) (q:draft)
dektaksa = (t:see) <dektaksa-in>
dektaksa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly) (d:<dektak> almost, with <sa> already and the adverb suffix <in>; {a si dektaksa-in}, left nearly dead) (q:draft)
dektakta = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:almost now/about to) (d:<dektak> almost, with <ta> marking a change now under way) (b:dektak) (q:draft)
Delaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Delaiah) (d:name of several men, among them a priest in the time of David and an official of King Jehoiakim who urged him not to burn Jeremiah’s scroll) (r:13.3.24/13.24.18)
deldel = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:tremblingly) (d:placed after <ling>, tremble, to picture the shaking: {ling deldel} is to shudder) (q:draft, low confidence)
delh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pursue/chase/go after) (d:run after someone in order to catch or drive them off; also strive after a goal such as peace) (s:nungdelh/nawhdelh) (r:25.3.66) (q:draft)
delhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pursuing/chasing) (d:form of <delh> with the linking ending <in>, used before a following verb) (b:delh) (q:draft)
delhkek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pursue/chase down) (d:<delh> pursue with <kek>, whose force is not clear from the verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drive out/chase away/drag away) (d:<delh> pursue with <khia> out: chase someone out of a place or off a path) (s:hawlkhia) (b:delh) (q:draft)
delhlup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall on and crush/bury under) (d:press down on and cover, said of a tower falling on people; <delh> here means press down, as in <delhphah>) (s:denlup) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:chase away/drive off/frighten away) (d:<delh> chase with <mang> away: chase something until it is gone) (s:taimangsak) (q:draft)
delhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pursuit/pursuing/chasing) (d:<delh> pursue with the noun suffix <na>: the act of chasing after someone; {a delhna panin} means from pursuing) (b:delh) (r:19.35.6) (q:draft)
delhphah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bed/bedding) (d:what is spread under a person to lie on) (s:lupphah) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhphah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lie on/overlay) (d:lie on top of someone; {delhphah kha} is lie on him by accident) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhphahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lying on) (d:<delhphah> with the linking suffix <in>, with one side of the body pressed down, said of lying on the left or right side) (b:delhphah) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhphahkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lie on/overlay) (d:press down on by lying over, with <kha> showing it happened by accident) (q:draft)
delhphahpuan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thick cloth/blanket) (d:a thick cloth of the kind spread on a bed) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to pursue/send after) (d:<delh> pursue with the causative <sak>: make something go after someone, as a sword sent after those who flee) (b:delh) (q:draft)
delhsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:chase down/pursue downward) (d:<delh> pursue with <suk> downward) (b:delh) (q:draft)
delhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pursuers/those who pursue) (d:<delh> pursue with <te>, the ones who pursue) (b:delh) (q:draft)
Delilah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Delilah) (d:woman of the Valley of Sorek whom Samson loved and who betrayed him to the Philistines) (r:7.16.4/7.16.10)
dem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:contend with/defy/challenge) (d:set oneself against someone as a rival or opponent; in many verses, against God) (s:langpang) (q:draft)
Demas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Demas) (d:fellow worker of Paul who later deserted him and went to Thessalonica) (r:55.4.10/51.4.14) (q:draft)
Demetrias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Demetrius) (d:name of two men: a silversmith of Ephesus who stirred up a riot against Paul, and a believer commended in 3 John) (r:44.19.24/44.19.38)
demin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:opposing/defying/contending/striving) (d:<dem>, contend with or rival, with the linking ending <in>) (b:dem) (q:draft)
demlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still oppose/continue to defy) (d:<dem> contend with, defy, with <lai> still: keep on being hostile) (r:3.26.27) (q:draft)
demna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hostility/opposition/rivalry) (d:<dem> contend with, defy, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:langpanna/kidemna) (b:dem) (q:draft)
demnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defiance/obstinacy/rebelliousness) (d:<dem> defy with <nop> want to and the noun suffix <na>: the wish to oppose; {demnopna lungsim} is a defiant, obstinate heart) (q:draft)
demte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:opponents/foes/those who defy) (d:<dem> contend with, defy, with the plural <te>: those who set themselves against someone) (s:langpangte/galte) (b:dem) (q:draft)
demzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to compete with) (d:<dem> compete with <zawh>, a form of <zo> be able) (q:draft)
demzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to stand against/be able to compete with) (d:<dem> contend with, with <zo> be able; {demzo nawn lo} is no longer able to stand against someone) (b:dem) (q:draft)
den = (i:2) (t:v) (w:throw down/hurl/stone) (d:form of <deng> written with a final apostrophe before <ding>, <na> and <nading>: hurl a thing to the ground or strike with stones) (s:deng/deeng) (q:draft, low confidence)
denarias = (i:1) (t:n) (w:denarius) (d:a Roman silver coin; {denarias peek khat} is one denarius) (q:draft)
deng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stone/pelt/throw at) (d:throw something at; {suang tawh deng} is to stone) (s:deeng/den) (q:draft)
dengawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stone/pelt) (d:<den> throw at with <gawp> showing violent or thorough action) (s:denggawp) (b:den) (q:draft)
dengawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:throwing down/dashing down) (d:<dengawp> throw violently, with the noun suffix <na>; with <ding>, will throw down forcefully) (b:dengawp) (q:draft, low confidence)
dengcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall on/bury/crush under) (d:<deng>, strike or fall on, with <cip>, tightly: fall on something and cover it completely, as people call on the hills to fall on them) (s:cipnelh) (b:deng) (q:draft)
denggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:beat down/batter/stone/pelt) (d:<deng>, strike or throw at, with <gawp>, severely: batter a person with stones or, of hail, beat down plants and animals) (s:satgawp) (b:deng) (q:draft)
dengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stoning/throwing at/pelting) (d:<deng>, throw something at, with the linking ending <in>: throwing at someone and going on to a further action; {suang tawh dengin} is stoning) (b:deng) (q:draft)
dengkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hit/strike) (d:<deng>, throw at, with <kha>, which shows that the action reaches its mark: hit someone with something thrown or rolled) (q:draft)
dengkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crack/break open) (d:<deng>, strike, with <kham>, broken: strike a thing so that it cracks, as a millstone dropped on a skull) (q:draft)
dengkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sweep away/beat down/knock away) (d:<deng>, pelt or strike, with <khia>, out or away: said of hail that beats on a shelter and carries it off) (b:deng) (q:draft)
denglum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stone to death/strike dead) (d:kill by throwing or hurling something at a person or animal, from <deng>, throw at, and <lum>, to death; {suang tawh denglum} is stone to death) (s:deenglum) (q:draft)
denglumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stoning to death) (d:<denglum> stone to death, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:denglum) (q:draft)
denglumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have stoned to death/let stone to death) (d:<denglum>, stone to death, with the causative <sak>: have a person stoned to death by others) (b:denglum) (q:draft)
dengnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to stone/wish to stone) (d:<deng>, throw at or stone, with <nuam>, want to) (q:draft)
dengtan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break off/strip/shatter) (d:<deng>, strike, with <tan>, broken off: strike a thing so that it breaks, as hail strips the trees) (q:draft)
dengtanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:striking and breaking/smashing) (d:<dengtan> strike and break, with the linking suffix <in>) (s:dengzanin/satnenin) (b:dengtan) (q:draft)
dengvui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn to dust/crush to dust) (d:<deng>, throw down or strike, with <vui>, dust, as in <leivui>: break a thing down into dust) (q:draft)
dengvuigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush/crush to powder) (d:<dengvui>, strike to dust, with <gawp>, which shows violent or thorough action: crush completely) (s:dengzan) (b:dengvui) (q:draft)
dengzan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dash to pieces/smash/crush) (d:<deng>, throw or strike, with <zan>, broken in pieces: smash a thing to pieces by throwing it down or by falling on it) (s:satnen/dengvuigawp) (q:draft)
dengzanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:smashing/dashing to pieces) (d:<dengzan> dash to pieces, with the linking suffix <in>: smash and go on to the next action) (s:satnenin/dengtanin) (b:dengzan) (q:draft)
denin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:continually/steadily/fixedly) (d:<den>, always, with the ending <in>, placed after a verb: keep on doing it without a break; {en denin} is look with a fixed gaze) (s:gige) (b:den) (q:draft)
denkhap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dash down/smash/shatter) (d:throw a thing down so that it breaks, as a potter dashes a pot or as walls are thrown down) (s:sukham/satkham) (q:draft)
denkhapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dashing down) (d:<denkhap> dash against the ground, with the noun suffix <na>; with <ding>, will dash to the ground) (b:denkhap) (q:draft, low confidence)
denlup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stone/strike down/crush) (d:strike a person down, from <den>, throw at or strike, and <lup>, lie flat; {suang tawh denlup} is stone someone, and of a falling tower it is crush the people under it) (q:draft)
denna = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw/cast/hurl) (d:<den>, throw, with <na>, used as a verb: throw into or cast down; {leilak denna} is cast to the ground and {thong sung denna} is throw into prison) (s:lawn/paai) (b:den) (q:draft)
denna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:stoning/throwing) (d:act of throwing at or throwing down; {suang tawh denna} is stoning) (b:den) (q:draft)
denna = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:endless/perpetual) (d:in {siat denna}, ruin that goes on without end, from <den> always) (q:draft, low confidence)
denpaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:smash/strike down) (d:<den> strike with <paih> away, strike and do away with) (q:draft, low confidence)
densa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:long-standing/lasting/perpetual) (d:<den> always, continually, with <sa> already done: {a sia densa mun} is a place that has lain in ruins all along) (b:den) (q:draft, low confidence)
densak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make remain/keep for ever) (d:<den>, always, with the causative <sak>, placed after a verb: cause to remain so for ever) (b:den) (q:draft)
dep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:choke/smother) (d:of thorns or weeds, grow over a plant and crowd it out; of cares and riches, crowd out the word; often followed by <gawp>, severely) (s:depgawp/deplum) (q:draft)
depgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:choke/smother) (d:<dep>, cover over, with <gawp>, severely: said of thorns that choke young plants, and of cares and riches that choke the word) (s:dep/deplum) (b:dep) (q:draft)
deplum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:choke/smother) (d:<dep>, cover over, with <lum>, to death: said of thorns that grow over plants and kill them) (s:dep/depgawp) (q:draft)
Derbe = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Derbe) (d:city of Lycaonia in Asia Minor, visited by Paul and Barnabas) (r:44.14.6/44.16.1)
det = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:new) (d:said of the moon, {kha det} is the new moon and {kha det ni} the day of the New Moon festival) (q:draft)
deudau = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in a long row/in procession) (d:describes many people or things lined up one after another; used after <kigual>, be arranged in line, and <kizom>, be joined on, as of an army, a procession or a long list of names) (s:diudeu-a) (q:draft, low confidence)
deudaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those in procession/those lined up) (d:<deudau>, in a long row, with the plural <te>: {mihon kigual deudaute} is the crowd of people drawn up in line) (b:deudau) (r:19.45.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
Deuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Deuel) (d:father of Eliasaph, the leader of the tribe of Gad in the wilderness) (r:4.1.14/4.10.20)
deuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:rather/somewhat/a little more) (d:placed after a descriptive word or after <zaw>, more, to show a slightly greater degree: {gamla zaw deuh} is a little farther, {ma deuh} is a little before) (q:draft, low confidence)
deuhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:a little/somewhat/rather) (d:<deuh>, a little more, with the ending <in>; after a describing word it slightly raises or softens the degree) (b:deuh) (q:draft)
deuhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are rather/those who are more) (d:<deuh> rather or somewhat, with the plural <te>; {khangnozaw deuhte}, those who are younger) (b:deuh) (q:draft, low confidence)
diah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dip/soak) (d:put a thing into a liquid for a moment or until it is soaked, as bread in sauce, a finger in water or a cloth in blood) (q:draft)
diah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:hold back/restrain/delay) (d:figurative: hold back anger or judgment, be forbearing) (s:ip) (q:draft, low confidence)
diahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dipping) (d:<diah> dip with the linking ending <in>: dipping, having dipped) (b:diah) (q:draft)
diahkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:finish dipping/finish soaking) (d:<diah> dip or soak with <khit> finish; with <ciangin>, after dipping) (q:draft)
diak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:especially/particularly/exceptionally) (d:placed after a descriptive word or verb to say that it is so to a special degree or more than the rest) (s:phadiak/adiak) (q:draft)
diakah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:just/right) (d:<diak> with the place marker <ah>; in {mai diakah}, right in front of, just ahead of) (b:diak) (q:draft, low confidence)
diakdiakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:especially/in particular) (d:<diak>, especially, doubled and with the ending <in>; in the phrase {a diakdiakin} it stands before the person or thing that is singled out: above all, in particular) (s:adiak) (r:24.44.24) (q:draft)
diakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:especially/particularly/exceptionally) (d:to a special degree, after a descriptive word; {adiak diakin}, above all; {zan diakin}, recently) (b:diak) (q:draft)
diakte = (t:see) <diakte-ah>
diakte-ah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:in the special ones) (d:<diak> especially, with the plural <te> and the place marker <ah>; {a thupi diakte-ah}, for the specially important uses) (q:draft, low confidence)
dial = (i:1) (t:n) (w:banner/flag) (d:a flag raised on a pole as a sign for people to gather; {dial khai} is raise a banner and {dial khuam} is a flagstaff) (s:dialkhai/lan) (q:draft)
dial = (i:2) (t:n) (w:cloth/towel/sash) (d:a strip or band of cloth, as a towel, a sash or a linen wrapping; {saiha dial} is linen) (q:draft)
dialh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:decline/grow dim) (d:of the sun, pass its height and go down toward evening; of light, grow dark) (q:draft, low confidence)
dialkaih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:belt/waistband/loincloth/girdle) (d:a cloth worn around the waist) (s:kawnggak/kawngten) (q:draft)
dialkhai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:standard/flag/banner) (d:the flag of a tribe or army division under which it camps and marches) (s:lan/dial) (q:draft)
dialkhaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:standards/flags/banners) (d:<dialkhai>, standard, with the plural <te>) (s:lante/dialte) (b:dialkhai) (q:draft)
dialkhip = (i:1) (t:n) (w:turban/headband) (d:a cloth wound round the head, named beside {kumpi lukhu}, the royal crown) (s:dialpi/lutuam) (q:draft)
dialkhipte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:turbans/headdresses/tiaras) (d:<dialkhip>, a cloth wound round the head, with the plural <te>) (b:dialkhip) (q:draft)
dialpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:turban/mitre) (d:the cloth headdress wound on the head of the high priest) (s:dialkhip) (q:draft)
dialpuan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:linen cloth) (d:<dial>, strip of cloth, with <puan>, cloth: a linen cloth, as the one in which the body of Jesus was wrapped) (s:puankang) (q:draft)
dialte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:banners/standards/flags) (d:<dial> banner with the plural <te>) (s:dialkhaite/lante) (b:dial) (q:draft)
diam = (i:1) (t:part) (d:sentence-final question word, short for {ding hiam}: will it be so, would you) (q:draft)
diam = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:all together) (d:placed after a verb of gathering, the whole group comes together as one) (q:draft, low confidence)
diamdiam = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb for a gentle movement to and fro, and after verbs with <ki> for doing something to one another in a kindly way: {awn diamdiam} is sway gently, {kihuh diamdiam} is help one another) (q:draft, low confidence)
diamdiamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in harmony/in good order) (d:<diamdiam> with the adverb ending <in>, placed after a verb of agreeing: {a kituak diamdiamin} is all in step together, {ki-it diamdiamin} in love for one another) (b:diamdiam) (q:draft, low confidence)
diamond = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:diamond) (d:English loanword, a very hard precious stone) (q:draft)
dian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leap/skip/jump) (d:form of <diang>, written with a final apostrophe before <nading> and other endings) (q:draft)
Diana = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Artemis/Diana) (d:goddess worshipped at Ephesus, for whom silver shrines were made; called Artemis in the NIV) (r:44.19.28/44.19.24)
diang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leap/jump/leap for joy/rejoice) (d:leap or skip, especially for joy; {nuamin diang}, be jubilant) (q:draft)
dianggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leap for joy/jump about) (d:<diang> jump with <gawp> showing vigorous action) (b:diang) (q:draft)
diangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leaping/jumping) (d:<diang> with the linking suffix <in>, leaping, followed by another verb) (b:diang) (q:draft)
