diangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spring out/leap out/rush out) (d:<diang>, leap, with <khia>, out) (b:diang) (q:draft)
diangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make leap/make skip) (d:<diang>, leap, with the causative <sak>) (b:diang) (q:draft)
dianna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leaping/jumping) (d:<dian> jump with the noun suffix <na>) (b:dian) (q:draft)
Diblaim = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Diblaim) (d:parent of Gomer, the wife of the prophet Hosea) (r:28.1.3)
Dibon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Dibon) (d:town of Moab east of the Dead Sea, built up by the tribe of Gad; also a town of Judah in the time of Nehemiah) (r:24.48.22/4.32.34)
Dibongad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Dibon Gad) (d:place in Moab where the Israelites camped on the way to Canaan) (r:4.33.45/4.33.46)
Dibri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dibri) (d:man of the tribe of Dan, father of Shelomith whose son blasphemed the Name) (r:3.24.11)
dide = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:silently/quietly/still) (d:adverb of stillness after <dai>, <om> and <ngai>, completely quiet and unmoving) (s:hithiat) (r:19.62.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
didi = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:gently/steadily) (d:placed after <luang> flow: describes water running on quietly and steadily) (q:draft, low confidence)
Didimas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Didymus) (d:Greek name, meaning twin, of the apostle Thomas) (r:43.20.24/43.11.16)
dih = (i:1) (t:part) (d:particle after a verb in a command or request, softening or urging it, just, please, now) (q:draft)
dihdiah = (t:see) <dihdiah-in>
dihdiah-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:describes skin hanging on or clinging to the bones; exact sense not clear from the verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
dihdiahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:describes skin hanging on or clinging to the bones; exact sense not clear from the verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
diik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:breathe/inhale/smell) (d:draw in breath or a smell through the nose) (s:naak) (q:draft)
dik = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:gracious/kind/favourable) (d:gracious or kind toward someone, used with <tungah>; of God, gracious) (s:migi) (q:draft)
dikdek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very/thoroughly) (d:intensifier after a descriptive word: {ngek dikdek} very delicate, {vom dikdek} deep black, {kawt dikdek} soaked through) (q:draft, low confidence)
dikdekin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:thoroughly/completely) (d:<dikdek>, an intensifier after a descriptive word, with the suffix <in>; {a kaang dikdekin} is turned quite white or scorched right through, of blighted crops) (b:dikdek) (q:draft, low confidence)
dikin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:righteous/just/true) (d:<dik>, righteous, with the ending <in> that joins it to a following word, as in {a dikin a man}, just and true; also adverbial, rightly) (b:dik) (q:draft)
dikin = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:gracious) (d:<dik> <in> its sense gracious, with the ending in that joins it to a following word; said of God, as in {dikin hehpihna nei}, gracious and compassionate) (b:dik) (r:19.111.4) (q:draft)
dikkisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justification/righteousness) (d:being counted or declared righteous by God; {dikkisakna ngah} is be justified) (s:diksakna/diktansakna) (r:45.10.10) (q:draft)
Diklah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Diklah) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.27)
diklohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:unrighteousness/wrongdoing/injustice) (d:<dik>, right, with <loh>, not, and the noun ending <na>) (a:dikna) (q:draft)
diklote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the unrighteous/wrongdoers/unjust people) (d:<dik> righteous with <lo> not and the plural <te>; used after <mi>, people) (s:thumanlote) (a:midikte) (q:draft)
dikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness/innocence) (d:<dik>, righteous, with the noun ending <na>: being in the right before God or a judge; also innocence) (s:thumanna/diktatna) (a:diklohna) (b:dik) (r:19.54.1) (q:draft)
Dikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness/justice) (d:<dikna> written with a capital in a line of verse, and as a name of the rider on the white horse, Faithful in the NIV) (b:dikna) (r:58.1.8) (q:draft)
diknopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wish to be gracious/desire to show favour) (d:<dik> gracious, kind, with <nop> want to and <na>: {ka diknopna mite} is the people I wish to be gracious to) (q:draft)
dikpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:innocent man/righteous man/just person) (d:<dik>, righteous, with {-pa} marking a man: the one who is in the right, set against <mawhpa>, the guilty one) (s:midikpa/thumanpa) (a:mawhpa) (b:dik) (q:draft)
diksa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pleased with/approve/regard as righteous) (d:<dik>, right, with <sa>, consider: think well of someone, be pleased with; in Romans 3:26 it stands for justify) (s:lungkimpih) (b:dik) (q:draft)
diksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:justify/declare righteous/acquit) (d:<dik>, righteous, with the causative <sak>: declare a person to be in the right, of God justifying sinners or of a judge acquitting) (s:diktangsak) (a:mawhsak) (b:dik) (q:draft)
diksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justification/vindication/righteousness) (d:the state of being declared or shown to be in the right, <diksak> with the noun suffix <na>; {diksakna ngah} is be justified or be proved right) (s:dikkisakna/diktansakna/diktan'sakna) (b:diksak) (q:draft)
diksakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justifier/the one who justifies) (d:the one who declares a person righteous, said of God; <diksak>, justify, with <pa> marking a man) (b:diksak) (q:draft)
diktakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:rightly/uprightly/justly) (d:in a right and upright way; <dik>, right, with <takin>, which makes an adverb) (s:thumanin/thutangin) (b:dik) (q:draft)
diktan = (t:see) <diktan'sakna>
diktan'sakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justification/being made righteous) (d:the act of declaring or making someone righteous; with <ngah>, receive, it means be justified) (s:diksakna/dikkisakna/diktansakna) (q:draft)
diktangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:justify/make righteous) (d:make or declare someone righteous; <diktang>, be righteous, with the causative <sak>) (s:diksak) (a:mawhsak) (q:draft)
Diktanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness) (d:righteousness, written with a capital in the name {Topa, Eite’ Diktanna}, The Lord Our Righteousness, which the NIV gives as The Lord Our Righteous Savior) (s:Diktatna/dikna) (r:24.33.16) (q:draft)
diktansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justification) (d:being made or counted righteous; with <ngah>, receive, it means be justified) (s:diktan'sakna/diksakna/dikkisakna) (q:draft)
diktat = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:faithful/trustworthy/honest/upright) (d:right and reliable in what one does, so that others can trust the person; said of people and of God) (s:citak/muanhuai/thutang) (a:zulhzau) (r:42.16.10) (q:draft)
diktatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness/uprightness/integrity/faithfulness) (d:upright and faithful conduct; <diktat> with the noun suffix <na>) (s:dikna/thumanna/hoihtatna) (a:diklohna/gitlohna) (b:diktat) (q:draft)
Diktatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness) (d:<diktatna> written with a capital within the name The Lord Our Righteousness) (s:Diktanna) (b:diktatna) (q:draft)
DIKTATNA = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness) (d:<diktatna> written in capitals within the name The Lord Our Righteousness) (s:Diktanna) (q:draft)
diktatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the honest/the trustworthy) (d:those who are honest and can be trusted; <diktat>, be honest, with the plural <te>) (b:diktat) (q:draft)
diktatzo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:able to be upright/truly good) (d:<diktat>, upright or honest, with <zo>, be able or manage to; {kuamah a diktatzo om lo} is no one manages to be good) (b:diktat) (r:42.18.19) (q:draft)
dikte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:righteous/upright) (d:<dik> with the plural ending <te>; {mi dikte} is righteous people, the righteous) (a:gilote) (b:dik) (q:draft)
dikzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more righteous/more upright/nobler) (d:<dik>, righteous, with the comparative <zaw>; the one compared takes <sangin>, than) (s:thumanzaw) (b:dik) (q:draft)
dikzo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:able to be righteous/righteous) (d:<dik>, righteous, with <zo>, be able or manage to; used where it is asked or denied that anyone can be righteous before God) (b:dik) (q:draft)
dildel = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after a verb or adjective for something thin, flat or stretched out, {pa dildel} is very thin and {lum dildel} is lying stretched out) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dilean = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Dilean) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.38)
dim = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:filled) (d:made full by something that has been put in or has come in)
dima = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:full/filling) (d:<dim>, full, with the linking suffix <a>; {lungsim dima om} is what the heart is full of) (b:dim) (q:draft, low confidence)
dimdem = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:quietly/expectantly) (d:describes waiting in silence and with attention, after <ngak>, wait) (q:draft, low confidence)
dimdiam = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:closely/evenly/in order) (d:expressive word after a verb for things set closely and evenly together, all in order with none missing) (q:draft, low confidence)
