dimdiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:close fitting/firm joining) (d:the state of being firmly set or closely joined together with no gap; <dimdiam> with the noun suffix <na>) (b:dimdiam) (q:draft, low confidence)
dimin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:multiply) (b:dim)
dimin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:fill/be full) (d:<dim>, full, with the linking suffix <in>: filling something or being filled with something) (b:dim)
dimkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be renewed/be filled again/revive) (d:<dim>, full, with <kik>, again; said of strength that comes back) (b:dim) (q:draft)
dimkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being renewed/returning) (d:<dimkik>, be full again, with the linking suffix <in>; said of strength coming back) (b:dimkik) (q:draft)
dimkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:refresh/fill again) (d:<dimkik>, be full again, with the causative <sak>; said of renewing strength) (s:dimsakkik/thadimsak) (b:dimkik) (q:draft)
dimlah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be short/have too little) (d:fall short of being full, have less than enough; the opposite of <dimval>) (a:dimval) (q:draft)
dimleetin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:full to overflowing/brimming over) (d:<dim>, full, with {leet}, overflow, and the adverb suffix <in>) (q:draft)
dimlet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overflow/be full to overflowing/brim over) (d:<dim>, full, with <let>, over the edge; of a cup, a river in flood, or a heart filled with something) (s:let/letkhia) (q:draft)
dimletin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overflowing/brimming over) (d:<dimlet> with the linking suffix <in>: full to overflowing, said of vats, rivers, tears and the heart) (b:dimlet) (q:draft)
dimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:place full of/fullness) (d:<dim>, full, with the noun suffix <na>: used as {a dimna} between a noun and the place it describes, the place where that thing is in plenty, as {mihing a dimna khuapi}, an inhabited town) (b:dim) (q:draft)
Dimnah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Dimnah) (d:town in the territory of Zebulun given to the Levites of the clan of Merari) (r:6.21.35)
Dimon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Dimon) (d:town in Moab whose waters are full of blood in the prophecy of Isaiah) (q:draft)
