dimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be filled/fill/make full) (d:make something full; <dim>, full, with the causative <sak>) (a:bungkhia/luakkhia) (b:dim)
dimsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:refresh/fill again) (d:<dimsak>, make full, with <kik>, again; said of renewing strength) (s:dimkiksak/thadimsak) (b:dimsak) (q:draft)
dimsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who fill) (d:<dimsak>, fill or make full, with the plural <te>: the people who fill something) (b:dimsak) (q:draft)
dimtak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:full/quite full/in full) (d:<dim>, full, with <tak>, truly: completely full, to the full) (b:dim) (q:draft)
dimtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:fully/to the full/full) (d:<dim>, full, with <takin>: so as to be full, in full measure) (b:dim) (q:draft)
dimval = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be over/have too much) (d:be more than full, have more than enough; <dim>, full, with <val>, exceed; the opposite of <dimlah>) (a:dimlah) (q:draft)
dimzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fuller/more filled) (d:<dim>, full, with the comparative <zaw>; {vangliatna tawh a dimzaw} is more glorious, fuller of glory) (b:dim) (q:draft)
dimzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to fill/be enough to fill) (d:<dim>, full, with <zawh>, a form of <zo>, be able) (q:draft, low confidence)
din = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand) (d:second stem of <ding>, stand, used before endings: {din’na} is a stand or base, or the place where one stands, and {din’ lai tak} is while standing) (q:draft)
Dinah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Dinah) (d:daughter of Jacob and Leah) (r:1.30.21/1.34.1)
dinden = (t:todo) (q:draft, occurs only after <git>, draw a line, in Job 26:10 where a line is marked out at the limit of sight; it may describe the line as straight or fixed but the verse does not make this plain)
ding = (i:1) (t:part) (w:will/shall) (d:particle suffixed to form verb which indicate objective case)
Ding = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand/stand up) (d:<ding>, stand, written with a capital at the start of a quoted command) (s:Tho) (b:ding) (q:draft)
ding-ua = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<ding> marking what is to be done, with the plural <uh> and the linking <a>; {na cih loh ding-ua}, that you, plural, should not say) (q:draft, low confidence)
dinga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for/to) (d:<ding>, marking what is to be, with the linking <a>: joins a verb to the noun that follows, for doing or to be done) (b:ding)
dingah = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:for/to) (d:<ding>, what is to be, with the place marker <ah>: for, towards or at the thing intended, as {a mun dingah}, in its place) (b:ding) (q:draft, low confidence)
dingding = (i:1) (t:v) (w:linger/stand about/keep standing) (d:<ding>, stand, doubled: stay standing where one is instead of going) (b:ding) (q:draft)
dinggaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wither/dry up) (d:of a tree, dry up and die where it stands) (s:keugaw/keutum) (q:draft)
dingin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:to/for/in order to/as) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (b:ding)
dinginah = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:in order to/so as to) (d:<dingin>, in order to, with <ah>: placed after a verb to state the purpose of the main action) (b:dingin) (q:draft)
dingkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand together/stand with) (d:<ding>, stand, with <khawm>, together; the one stood with takes <tawh>) (s:pangkhawm) (q:draft)
dingkhawmsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make stand together) (d:<dingkhawm>, stand together, with the causative <sak>) (b:dingkhawm) (q:draft)
dingkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set out/start out/get up and leave) (d:rise and leave a place; <ding>, stand, with <khia>, out) (s:kuankhia/kuan/kisuan) (b:ding) (q:draft)
dingkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand again/rise again) (d:<ding>, stand, with <kik>, again) (s:thokik) (q:draft)
dingkikzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to stand again/be able to rise again) (d:<dingkik>, stand again, with <zo>, be able) (s:thokikzo) (b:dingkik) (q:draft)
dinglai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still stand/remain standing) (d:<ding>, stand, with <lai>, still) (q:draft)
dinglaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those still standing) (d:<dinglai>, still stand, with the plural <te>; {ankung dinglaite} is the standing grain, not yet cut) (b:dinglai) (q:draft)
dingMoses = (t:todo) (q:draft, not a word, <ding> and Moses printed without a space in Exodus 2.21)
dingpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one who will) (d:the man who will or is to do what the verb before it says, as {luah dingpa} heir and {kheem dingpa} tempter; <ding> with <pa> marking a man) (b:ding) (q:draft)
dingpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get up at once/stand up immediately) (d:<ding>, stand or rise, with <pah>, at once) (s:thopah) (q:draft)
dingpi = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<ding>, will or should, with the emphatic <pi>; marks what is or is not to be so, often set against what is done: {gamtat loh dingpi}, what should not be done; {a mawkna dingpi-in}, though it will be in vain) (b:ding) (q:draft, low confidence)
dingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make stand/set up/raise up) (d:<ding>, stand, with the causative <sak>: make a person stand or set a thing upright; with <kik>, set up again) (s:thosak/phut) (b:ding) (r:4.27.19) (q:draft)
dingsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:setting up/erecting) (d:<dingsak>, make stand, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:dingsak) (q:draft)
dingsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise again/rebuild/set up again) (d:<dingsak>, make stand, with <kik>, again) (s:lamkik/dinsakkik/dingtosakkik) (a:susia) (b:dingsak) (q:draft)
dingsakkikzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to raise again/be able to rebuild) (d:<dingsakkik>, set up again, with <zo>, be able) (b:dingsakkik) (q:draft)
dingtang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand upright/stand up straight/stand firm) (d:<ding>, stand, with <tang>, straight) (a:kun) (q:draft)
dingtangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:upright/erect) (d:<dingtang>, stand upright, with the suffix <in>: standing straight, with the head held high) (b:dingtang) (q:draft)
dingtangto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand up/rise up) (d:<dingtang>, stand upright, with <to>, upward) (s:dingto/thoto) (b:dingtang) (q:draft)
dingte = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<ding> with the plural <te>: those who will or are to, the things to be done) (b:ding) (q:draft)
dingteng = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: all that is to be said or done, everything one has to; <ding> with <teng>, all) (b:ding) (q:draft)
dingto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand up/rise/get up) (d:rise to the feet; <ding>, stand, with <to>, upward) (s:tho/thoto/dingtangto) (a:tusuk) (b:ding) (r:14.20.19) (q:draft)
dingtosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise up/help up/set on the feet) (d:<dingto>, stand up, with the causative <sak>: make or help someone stand up; also raise up what has fallen) (s:thosak/dingsak) (b:dingto) (q:draft)
dingtosakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise up again/restore) (d:<dingtosak>, make stand up, with <kik>, again) (s:dingsakkik/dinsakkik) (b:dingtosak) (q:draft)
dingun = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<ding> with the plural agreement <un>: so that they or you may, for them to; {a neih dingun}, as their possession) (b:ding) (q:draft)
dingvat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand suddenly/appear suddenly) (d:<ding>, stand, with <vat>, suddenly: all at once be standing there) (s:omvat) (q:draft)
dingzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the amount that will/the number that will) (d:<ding>, marking what is to come, with <zah>, amount: how much or how many there will be, as in {a bei dingzah}, the amount it will cost) (q:draft)
dingzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the way something will happen/manner/way) (d:<ding>, will, with <zia>, manner: the way in which something will or should happen; follows a noun ending in <na>) (q:draft)
dingzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to stand/endure) (d:<ding>, stand, with <zo>, be able; with {nawn lo}, no longer able to stand, as a nation that is wiped out) (s:dintheih/kipzo) (b:ding) (q:draft)
Dinhabah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Dinhabah) (d:city in Edom, the city of King Bela son of Beor) (r:1.36.32/13.1.43)
dinkhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand still/stop) (d:<din>, stand, with <khawl>, stop or rest: come to a halt) (q:draft)
dinkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set out) (d:form of <dingkhia> used before words such as <ciangin> and <ni>: get up and leave a place, start a journey) (s:kuankhiat/kisuan)
dinkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repay/reward/recompense/make restitution) (d:give back what is due, whether a reward for good or payment for a wrong) (s:thukkik/lohkik) (a:leitawi) (r:19.18.24) (q:draft)
dinkipna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foothold/firm footing) (d:<din>, stand, with <kip>, firm, and the noun suffix <na>: a place to stand firmly) (s:khesikna) (q:draft)
dinlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<din>, stand, with <lam>, the fact or manner: the fact that someone is standing somewhere) (q:draft, low confidence)
dinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:standing place/place where one stands) (d:<din>, stand, with <na>: the standing, or with <mun> the place where someone or something stands; {a mai-ah ka dinna}, before whom I stand) (b:din) (q:draft)
dinnasa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:had stood) (d:<din>, stand, with <na>, place, and <sa>, already done; {a dinnasa mun} is the place where one had stood) (b:din) (q:draft)
dinsa = (t:see) <dinsa-in>
dinsa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:standing/while standing) (d:<din>, stand, with <sa>, already, and the adverbial <in>: standing where one is) (q:draft, low confidence)
dinsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set up again/restore) (d:<din>, stand, with the causative <sak> and <kik>, again: make stand again, of a ruined building) (s:dingsakkik/dingtosakkik) (q:draft)
dinsih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die/drop dead) (d:the verse has died; apparently <din>, stand, with <sih>, die: die on the spot) (q:draft, low confidence)
dintheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to stand) (d:<din>, stand, with <theih>, be able) (s:dingzo) (b:din) (q:draft)
Dionisias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dionysius) (d:member of the Areopagus council in Athens who became a believer through the preaching of Paul) (r:44.17.34)
Diotrefes = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Diotrephes) (d:church leader who loved to be first and refused to accept the authority of John, the writer of 3 John) (r:64.1.9)
dip = (i:1) (t:n) (w:heart/breast/chest) (d:the heart as the place that pounds with feeling, or the breast; {dip kuasak} is make the heart pound or burn and {dip hum} is beat the breast in grief) (s:awm/lungtang) (q:draft)
dip = (i:2) (t:v) (w:draw/scoop) (d:draw or scoop up water, as in {tui dip}; {tui dip nading} is something to draw water with) (s:tawi) (q:draft, low confidence)
dipkua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be appalled/be horrified/be terrified) (d:be struck with fear or shock; {dipkua sak} is to startle or terrify someone) (s:mulkim/lipkhap/linglawng) (q:draft)
dipkuasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:terrify/startle/horrify) (d:<dipkua>, be appalled or terrified, with the causative <sak>: fill someone with fear or shock) (s:lausak/lauthawng) (b:dipkua) (q:draft)
dipkuat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be terrified/be struck with dread) (d:in the verses always followed by <huai>: {dipkuat huai} is awesome, terrifying) (s:lipkhap/mulkim) (q:draft)
dipkuathuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:awesome/terrifying/dreadful) (d:causing dread or awe, used of God and his deeds and of disasters; <dipkuat>, be terrified, with <huai>, causing) (s:lauhuai/kihtakhuai/lipkhaphuai/mulkimhuai) (q:draft)
dipkuatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:terror/dread/horror) (d:<dipkuat>, be terrified, with the noun suffix <na>: sudden fear that comes upon someone) (s:launa/kihtakna/patauhna) (b:dipkuat) (q:draft)
dipna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scooping/drawing) (d:<dip>, scoop or draw water, with the noun suffix <na>; {tui dipna ding} is something to scoop water with) (b:dip) (q:draft)
dipsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:filling) (d:with <tawh>, filling a container with something, as bags with grain; the causative <sak> and the linking suffix <in> on <dip>, which here seems to mean be full) (s:thunin) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dishan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dishan) (d:son of Seir the Horite and a Horite chief in the land of Edom) (r:1.36.28/13.1.38)
Dishon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dishon) (d:name of two Horites in Edom, a son of Seir who was a chief and a son of Anah) (r:1.36.26/1.36.25)
ditkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:restitution/repayment/compensation) (d:payment made to the owner for something lost, stolen or damaged; {ditkikna bawl} is make restitution) (s:lohkikna/thukkikna) (r:2.22.14) (q:draft)
diudeu = (t:see) <diudeu-a>
diudeu-a = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in a line/in procession) (d:describes people moving one after another in a long line, in {kigual diudeu-a paina}, a procession) (s:deudau) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dizahab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Dizahab) (d:place in the wilderness east of the Jordan, named in the setting of the words Moses spoke to Israel) (r:5.1.1)
do = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fight/attack/make war on) (d:fight against or attack, with the enemy as object; {do dingin} is in order to fight or attack) (s:sim/galdo/galsim) (a:kilem) (r:6.9.2) (q:draft)
Dodai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dodai) (d:Ahohite, commander of the army division for the second month under King David) (r:13.27.4)
Dodanim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Dodanim/Rodanites) (d:descendants of Javan son of Japheth; the NIV reads Rodanites) (r:1.10.4)
Dodavahu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dodavahu) (d:man of Mareshah, father of the prophet Eliezer who spoke against Jehoshaphat) (r:14.20.37)
Dodo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dodo) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Elhanan of Bethlehem and the grandfather of the judge Tola) (r:10.23.24/13.11.26/7.10.1)
Doeg = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Doeg) (d:Edomite, chief shepherd of Saul, who informed on Ahimelek and killed the priests of Nob) (r:9.21.7/9.22.9)
Dofkah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Dophkah) (d:camping place of Israel in the wilderness, between the Desert of Sin and Alush) (r:4.33.12/4.33.13)
doin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fighting/attacking) (d:<do>, fight, with the linking suffix <in>: fighting or attacking and then going on to the next action) (s:simin) (b:do) (q:draft)
dok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw/pull out/withdraw) (d:pull something out or back, as a sword from its sheath or a hand; with <kik>, draw back) (s:kaikhia) (q:draft)
dok = (i:2) (t:v) (w:exact/collect/levy/charge) (d:collect money, tax or interest from people, with {tung panin} for those who must pay) (s:khon/siik) (q:draft)
dokhawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:striving together/fighting together) (d:<do>, fight, with <khawm>, together, and the noun suffix <na>) (q:draft)
dokin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drawing/pulling out) (d:<dok> with <in>, the linking form before a following verb; used of drawing a sword) (b:dok) (r:40.26.51) (q:draft)
dokkhia = (t:see) <dokkhia-in>
dokkhia-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pulling out/drawing out) (d:<dok>, pull, with <khia>, out, and the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft)
dokkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw back/withdraw/take back) (d:pull back a hand, anger, kindness or a word once given; <dok>, pull, with <kik>, back) (s:lakik) (b:dok) (r:45.11.29) (q:draft)
doksa = (t:see) <doksa-in>
doksa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:outstretched/stretched out) (d:<dok> pull out with <sa> and the suffix <in>: with the neck, <ngawng>, held stretched out) (q:draft)
doksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making draw/causing to draw) (d:<dok>, draw a sword, with the causative <sak> and the linking suffix <in>) (b:dok) (q:draft)
dolah = (t:todo) (q:draft, one verse, {sakin dolah nei lo} is said of the hard heart of Leviathan, the meaning of {dolah} is not clear from it)
dom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lift up/hold up/bear up) (d:take up and support with the hands, often as {dom to}, lift up; {nau dom} is to help at a birth) (s:lamto/laamto/phong) (a:khiasuk) (r:19.91.12) (q:draft)
domin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lifting up/carrying/holding up) (d:<dom>, lift or hold up <in> the hands, with the linking ending in; {nau dom} is to help a woman at a birth) (b:dom) (q:draft)
domkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lift out/pull out/take up out of) (d:<dom>, lift up, with <khia>, out) (s:kaikhia) (b:dom) (q:draft)
domsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:midwives) (d:in {nau a domsakte}, those who help a woman deliver a child; <dom>, lift or hold up, with <sak> and the plural <te>) (s:naudomte) (q:draft)
domto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lift up/pick up/raise) (d:<dom>, lift, with <to>, upward: pick up a person or raise someone from a low place) (s:lamto/laamto/phongto) (a:khiasuk) (b:dom) (q:draft)
don = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pay attention/heed/regard/care for) (d:give attention or care to a person or a word; {don lo} is ignore or disregard) (s:thudon/ngai/awlmawh) (q:draft)
dona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fighting/war/warfare/attack) (d:the act of fighting against someone, often as {gal dona}, warfare; <do>, fight, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:galdona/kidona/simna/galkidona) (a:kilemna) (b:do) (q:draft)
dong = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:until/till/as far as) (d:marks the limit reached in time or place, placed after the word or clause it limits; often follows <ciang>) (s:ciang/tan) (a:kipan) (q:draft)
donga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:until/up to/to) (d:<dong>, until, with <a>, joining the phrase to what follows; {tu ni donga a om} is which is there to this day) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:as far as/up to/until) (d:<dong> with the locative suffix <ah>, marking the limit reached; often after <ciang>) (b:dong) (r:1.13.12) (q:draft)
dongin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:until/till/up to) (d:<dong>, until, with the linking suffix <in>: up to a point in time, a place or an amount) (a:kipan) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:block/obstruct/silence) (d:stop or shut off: block a road, or stop the mouth of someone so that he has no answer) (s:khaktan/khakcip) (q:draft)
dongkhakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:silencing/blocking) (d:<dongkhak>, stop or silence, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:dongkhak) (q:draft)
dongkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have asked/be engaged to) (d:<dong>, ask, with <khin>, already; {lawm dongkhin} is having already asked for a woman in marriage) (b:dong) (q:draft, low confidence)
dongkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask again/ask further/ask in return) (d:<dong>, ask, with <kik>, again or back) (a:dawngkik) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to ask) (d:<dong>, ask, with <nuam>, want to) (q:draft)
dongpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inquirer/one who asks) (d:<dong>, ask, with <pa> marking a man: the man who asks or consults) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask/inquire/have someone ask) (d:<dong>, ask, with <sak>: put a question to someone, or send someone to ask on one's behalf) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask privately/ask in secret) (d:<dong>, ask, with <sim>, secretly) (q:draft)
dongtak = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:up to/as far as) (d:<dong>, until, with <tak>, exactly: right up to an amount or point) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongtakin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:right down to/even to) (d:<dong>, until, with <takin>: all the way to, of searching to the very depth) (b:dong) (q:draft, low confidence)
dongtangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hinder/obstruct/hold back) (d:put something in the way so that a person or a work is stopped; with the causative <sak>) (s:khaktan/nawngkaisak) (a:huh) (q:draft)
dongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:collectors) (d:<dong>, ask or demand, with plural <te>: those who demand payment; {phiangsiah dongte} are tax collectors) (s:siahdongte) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:end/outcome) (d:<dong>, until or as far as, with plural <te>; {a thu tawpna dongte} is how their matter goes on to its end, their final destiny) (b:dong) (q:draft, low confidence)
dongtel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:judge/examine/call to account) (d:<dong>, ask, with <tel>, clearly: question closely, test, or pass judgment on) (s:thukhen/entel/kantel) (q:draft)
dongtelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:examining/testing/questioning closely) (d:<dongtel>, find out by asking, examine, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:dongtel) (q:draft)
dongun = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:until/till) (d:<dong>, until, with the plural ending <un>, used when the persons spoken of are more than one) (b:dong) (q:draft)
dongzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask rather/ask instead) (d:<dong>, ask, with <zaw>, rather; here a command to ask in this way instead) (b:dong) (q:draft, low confidence)
donin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:heeding/caring for/paying attention to) (d:<don>, heed, with the linking suffix <in>: heeding or caring for and then going on to the next action; {donin nei lo} is pay no heed to) (b:don) (q:draft)
donkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pay attention to/heed) (d:<don>, heed, with <kha>; {donkha kei} is neglect or fail to attend to) (q:draft)
donkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:care for again/attend to again) (d:<don>, care for, with <kik>, again; the verse says he will never care for them again) (b:don) (q:draft, low confidence)
donnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to heed/care about) (d:<don>, heed, with <nop>, want to) (q:draft)
donzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to care for/be able to attend to) (d:<don>, care for, with <zo>, be able) (b:don) (q:draft)
dop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spare/treat gently/be lenient with) (d:hold back from being hard on someone; {dop bawl} is treat gently) (q:draft)
dopa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one fought against) (d:<do>, fight against, with <pa> marking a male person: he whom one has fought or rebelled against) (b:do) (q:draft)
dopbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:treat gently/spare) (d:<dop>, treat gently, with <bawl>, do or treat) (b:dop) (q:draft)
dopih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fight alongside/join in fighting) (d:<do>, fight, with <pih>, together with someone) (s:simpih/galsimpih) (b:do) (q:draft)
dopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sparing/leniency) (d:<dop>, spare, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:dop) (q:draft)
Dor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Dor) (d:Canaanite city on the coast south of Mount Carmel, allotted to Manasseh, whose people Manasseh did not drive out) (r:7.1.27/6.17.11) (q:draft)
Dorkas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Dorcas) (d:disciple in Joppa, also called Tabitha, known for her good works, whom Peter raised from the dead) (r:44.9.36/44.9.41)
dosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fight for/fight on behalf of) (d:<do>, fight, with <sak>, here doing the action for the benefit of another) (b:do) (q:draft)
dosakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fighting for/fighting on behalf of) (d:<dosak>, fight for someone, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:dosak) (q:draft)
dosakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fighting for/fighting on behalf of) (d:<dosak>, fight for someone, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact of having fought for someone) (b:dosak) (q:draft)
dosakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one who fights for) (d:<dosak>, fight on behalf of, with <pa>, marking a man: he who fights for someone, said of God) (b:dosak) (q:draft)
dosuakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:withstand/resist) (d:with <gal>, be able to hold out in fighting; <do>, fight, with <suak> and <zo>, be able) (s:nangzo) (q:draft, low confidence)
dot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask/question/inquire) (d:form of <dong>, ask, used before <leh>, <hangin>, <ciangin>, <nading> and in dependent clauses) (q:draft)
dote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:adversaries/attackers/enemies) (d:<do>, fight, with the plural suffix <te>: those who fight against someone) (s:galte/langpangte/langte) (b:do) (q:draft)
Dothan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Dothan) (d:town north of Shechem where Joseph found his brothers and where Elisha was surrounded by the Aramean army) (r:1.37.17/12.6.13)
dotin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consulting/inquiring of) (d:<dot>, ask, with <in>; {thu dotin nei} is make a practice of consulting) (b:dot) (q:draft)
dotkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask again/inquire again) (d:<dot>, ask, with <kik>, again) (b:dot) (q:draft)
dotna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:question/asking/inquiry) (d:<dot>, ask, with the noun suffix <na>: a question, or the act of asking; {thu dotna} is an inquiry or a request) (s:thudotna) (a:thudawnna/dawnkikna) (b:dot) (q:draft)
dotnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:questions) (d:<dotna>, question, with the plural <te>) (s:thudotnate) (b:dotna) (q:draft)
dotnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to ask/wish to ask) (d:<dot>, form of <dong> ask, with <nop> want to: {ka dotnop thu} is the thing I want to ask) (q:draft)
dotpen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:asking/consulting) (d:<dot>, ask, with the topic marker <pen>: the asking, as the subject of the sentence) (b:dot) (q:draft, low confidence)
dotsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:inquire for/ask on behalf of) (d:<dot>, ask, with <sak>: ask for someone else; used of inquiring of God for another person) (b:dot) (q:draft)
dotsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:inquiring for/asking on behalf of) (d:<dotsak>, ask for someone else, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:dotsak) (q:draft)
dotte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those consulted/advisers) (d:<dot>, ask, with the plural <te>; {mipil thu dotte} are the wise men whose counsel is asked) (s:thudotte) (b:dot) (q:draft, low confidence)
dottel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:examine/investigate/question closely) (d:<dot>, ask, with <tel>, clearly: question until the matter is clear) (s:kantel) (q:draft)
dozawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to fight) (d:<do>, fight, with <zawh>, form of <zo>, be able; used before <nading>) (q:draft)
dozo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to fight/withstand/oppose) (d:<do>, fight, with <zo>, be able: be strong enough to fight or stand against someone) (s:nangzo) (b:do) (q:draft)
dozo = (i:2) (t:v) (w:wait on/serve) (d:be able to attend to guests, <do> in the sense of receiving guests, with <zo>, be able) (q:draft, low confidence)
Drusilla = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Drusilla) (d:Jewish wife of the Roman governor Felix, who came with him to hear Paul) (r:44.24.24)
duadua = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:faintly/softly) (d:describes a low, hushed voice, after <aw un>) (q:draft, low confidence)
duai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:patient/unyielding/enduring) (d:not giving way easily; with <lung>, heart, {lung duai} means patient and slow to anger, and said of a person it can mean unyielding) (s:lungduai) (a:lungtom/hehbaih/ngot) (q:draft, low confidence)
duang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:figure/stature/build/appearance) (d:the body of a person as it is seen: his figure, build and stature) (s:pumpi) (q:draft, low confidence)
duangvul = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:faint/languishing/weak) (d:<duang>, body, with <vul>, wither: wasting away in body, here faint with longing) (q:draft)
duh = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:thirsty) (d:with <tui>, water: {tui duh} is to be thirsty, to want to drink) (s:dangtak/tuiduh) of water
duh = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:hungry) (d:with <an>, food: {an duh} is to be hungry, to want to eat) (s:gilkial) of food
duhduh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whatever one desires/all one likes) (d:<duh>, desire or crave, doubled: everything that a person wants, said mostly of food) (s:deihdeih) (q:draft)
duhduha = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as much as one likes/to one's heart's content) (d:<duhduh>, whatever one desires, with the adverbial ending <a>: eating as much as one wants) (s:duhduhin) (b:duhduh) (q:draft, low confidence)
duhduhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as one pleases/to one's heart's content) (d:<duhduh>, whatever one craves, with the suffix <in>: eating and drinking as much as one likes) (s:duhduha/ututin) (b:duhduh) (q:draft)
duhgawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crave/covet/long for) (d:want something too strongly, said of food and of what belongs to other people) (s:deihgawh/iplah/duhluat) (q:draft)
duhgawhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:greedily/longingly/with craving) (d:<duhgawh>, crave, with the suffix <in>: with strong craving) (s:huaihamin) (b:duhgawh) (q:draft)
duhgawhkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crave/covet) (d:<duhgawh>, crave, with <kha>, happen to: come to crave something, said of food in the warning {duhgawhkha kei un}, do not crave) (s:duhgawh) (q:draft, low confidence)
duhhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:greed/covetousness/craving) (d:the strong wish to have more and more things) (s:huaihamna/duhluatna) (q:draft)
duhhopte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the greedy/covetous people) (d:people who crave greedily, with the plural <te>; it is joined with <huaiham>, greedy) (s:huaihamte) (q:draft)
duhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thirsting for/hungering for/craving) (d:<duh> with the linking suffix <in>: wanting food or drink, followed by another verb; {tui duhin} is being thirsty and {an duhin} is being hungry) (b:duh) (q:draft)
duhluat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crave/desire too much) (d:<duh>, desire, with <luat>, too much; {duhluat mahmahna} is a very great craving) (s:deihluat/duhgawh) (q:draft)
duhluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:craving/lust/excessive desire) (d:<duhluat>, desire too much, with the noun suffix <na>: a desire that is too strong, named together with <deihluatna>) (s:duhhopna/huaihamna) (b:duhluat) (q:draft)
duhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:appetite/craving/hunger/thirst) (d:the wish for food or drink, and so any strong desire; {an duhna} is hunger and {tui duhna} is thirst) (b:duh) (q:draft)
duhpen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:what one craves most/craving) (d:<duh>, crave or want to eat, with <pen>, most: the thing a person desires most) (b:duh) (q:draft)
dulh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:peel/come off) (d:come off in pieces, said of skin; with <khia>, out, it means peel off) (q:draft, low confidence)
dulhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:peel off) (d:<dulh>, peel, with <khia>, out or off, of skin) (b:dulh) (q:draft, low confidence)
dum = (i:2) (t:n) (w:pit/cistern/hole) (d:a hole dug in the ground, such as a pit to trap something or a cistern to hold water) (s:tuikhuk/gum) (q:draft)
dumah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:to the cistern/at the pit) (d:<dum>, pit or cistern, with the place marker <ah>) (b:dum) (q:draft)
Dumah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dumah) (d:son of Ishmael; also a town in the hill country of Judah) (r:1.25.14)
dumna = (t:see) <dumna-a>
dumna-a = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in a green place/in a meadow) (d:<dum>, be green, with the noun suffix <na> and the place marker <a>; {lopa dumna} is where the grass is green) (q:draft, low confidence)
dumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make green) (d:<dum>, be blue or green, with the causative <sak>: make plants grow green) (b:dum) (q:draft)
dumsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one who makes green) (d:<dumsak>, make green, with <pa> marking a male person) (b:dumsak) (q:draft)
dumte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trenches/siege works) (d:<dum> pit with the plural <te>: apparently ditches dug around a city under siege, where the NIV has siege works) (b:dum) (q:draft, low confidence)
dung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:length) (d:the long side of a thing or its measure from end to end, paired with <vai> for the width) (s:dunglam/sauna) (a:vai/vailam) (q:draft)
dunga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:along/on the shore of) (d:<dung>, length, with <a>: along the length of something; {tuipi dunga} is along the sea, on the coast) (s:dungah) (b:dung) (q:draft)
dungah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:along/alongside) (d:<dung>, length, with the place marker <ah>: along the length of a river, a shore or a border) (s:dunga) (b:dung) (q:draft)
dunglam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:length/long side) (d:<dung>, length, with <lam>, side or direction: the measure or the side along the length of a thing) (s:dung/saulam) (a:vailam/zailam) (q:draft)
dungteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whole length/all along) (d:<dung>, length, with <teng>, all: the full stretch along something, such as the whole coast of the sea) (b:dung) (q:draft)
dup = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dark/blackened/livid) (d:of the face, turned dark; {dup} is also part of colour words such as <dupsan> purple) (q:draft, low confidence)
dupsan = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:purple) (d:the colour purple, said of cloth and yarn and listed with {a dum}, blue, and {a ausan}, scarlet) (s:sandup) (q:draft)
dupsante = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:purple) (d:<dupsan> purple with the plural <te>, which belongs to the whole phrase: {puan dupsante} is purple garments) (b:dupsan) (q:draft)
Dura = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Dura) (d:plain in the province of Babylon where Nebuchadnezzar set up the gold image) (r:27.3.1)
e = (i:1) (t:intj) (d:exclamation placed after a word of address, as in {Nu e}, oh mother, a cry of dismay where the English has how awful) (q:draft, low confidence)
eb = (t:see) <Ze-eb>
Ebal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebal) (d:son of Shobal, a descendant of Seir the Horite; also the mountain near Shechem where the curses were read) (r:1.36.23)
Ebar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eber) (d:son of Shelah and father of Peleg in the genealogy of Jesus in Luke, elsewhere written <Eber>) (q:draft)
Ebed = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebed) (d:name of two men: the father of Gaal, who rose against Abimelek, and a man who returned from Babylon with Ezra) (r:15.8.6) (q:draft)
Ebedmelek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebed-Melek) (d:Cushite official in the palace of King Zedekiah who had Jeremiah lifted out of the cistern) (r:24.38.12/24.38.8)
Ebenezer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ebenezer) (d:place where Israel camped before the Philistines captured the ark; also the stone Samuel set up to mark the help of the Lord) (r:9.5.1/9.7.12)
Eber = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eber) (d:son of Shelah and father of Peleg, an ancestor of Abraham; also the name of several other men) (r:13.1.18/13.1.25)
Ebes = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ebez) (d:town in the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.20) (q:draft)
