Ebiasaf = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebiasaph) (d:Levite of the family of Korah, ancestor of temple singers and gatekeepers) (r:13.6.23/13.6.37)
Ebron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ebron/Abdon) (d:town on the border of the territory of Asher, where the NIV reads Abdon) (q:draft)
Ebronah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abronah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Jotbathah and Ezion Geber) (r:4.33.34/4.33.35)
eden = (t:see) <Beth-eden>
Eden = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Eden) (d:the land in the east where God planted the garden for the first man and woman) (r:1.2.8)
Eder = (i:1) (t:name) (c:tower) (w:Eder) (d:Migdal Eder, the tower beyond which Jacob pitched his tent after Rachel died) (r:1.35.21)
Eder = (i:2) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Eder) (d:town in the far south of Judah; also the name of a Benjamite and of a Levite, son of Mushi) (r:6.15.21)
Edom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Edom) (d:another name of Esau, son of Isaac; also the land and the people descended from him, south of the Dead Sea) (r:1.36.1)
Edomte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Edom/Edomites) (d:the people of Edom, descendants of Esau) (b:Edom) (r:4.24.18)
Edor = (t:see) <Edor-ah>
Edor-ah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Endor) (d:Endor, the town where Saul consulted a medium, written here with the place marker <ah>, at Endor) (q:draft)
Edrei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Edrei) (d:city of Og king of Bashan, where Israel defeated him; also a town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:4.21.33/6.19.37)
ee = (i:1) (t:intj) (d:exclamation of astonishment or scorn uttered by passers-by at a ruin) (s:eh) (q:draft, low confidence)
eek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dung/rubbish) (d:apparently the same word as <ek>, dung, with a long vowel; here of things counted as worthless) (s:ek) (q:draft, low confidence)
eeka = (i:1) (t:n) (w:acre) (d:a measure of land, the English word acre; another spelling of <eka>) (s:eka) (q:draft)
eekkholna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:manure pile/dunghill) (d:<eek>, dung, with <khol>, heap or store, and the noun suffix <na>) (s:ninkholna) (q:draft)
een = (i:1) (t:v) (w:envy/be jealous of) (d:feel ill will because of what another person has or is; written {een’} before a following word, and {een’na} is envy) (s:eng/hazat/haza) (q:draft)
eengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being jealous/envying) (d:<eeng>, a spelling of <eng>, envy, with the linking suffix <in>: being jealous, and so doing a further action) (q:draft)
Efah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephah) (d:son of Midian, grandson of Abraham and Keturah; also the concubine of Caleb and a son of Jahdai) (r:1.25.4/13.2.47)
Efai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephai) (d:man of Netophah whose sons came to Gedaliah at Mizpah) (q:draft)
Efer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Epher) (d:son of Midian, grandson of Abraham and Keturah; also a family head in the half-tribe of Manasseh) (r:1.25.4)
Efesa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ephesus) (d:city in the Roman province of Asia where Paul worked and to whose church he wrote) (r:55.4.12/44.19.28)
Efesdammim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephes Dammim) (d:place in Judah between Sokoh and Azekah where the Philistines camped before David fought Goliath) (r:9.17.1)
Effatha = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ephphatha) (d:Aramaic word spoken by Jesus to a deaf man, meaning be opened) (r:41.7.34)
Efifaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eliphaz) (d:son of Esau and Adah, a spelling of Eliphaz) (r:1.36.4)
Eflal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephlal) (d:man of Judah, descendant of Jerahmeel, son of Zabad and father of Obed) (r:13.2.37)
Efod = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephod) (d:father of Hanniel, the leader of the tribe of Manasseh at the dividing of the land) (r:4.34.23)
Efrah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephrath) (d:older name of Bethlehem, on the road to which Rachel was buried) (r:1.48.7)
Efraim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephraim) (d:younger son of Joseph, ancestor of the tribe of Ephraim; also the tribe and its land) (r:1.41.52/1.46.20)
Efraimte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Ephraim/Ephraimites) (d:the people of the tribe of Ephraim) (b:Efraim) (r:28.13.1/7.12.4)
Efrat = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephrath) (d:older name of Bethlehem, near which Rachel died; also written <Efrath>) (r:1.35.19) (q:draft)
Efrath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ephrath) (d:older name of Bethlehem, near which Rachel died; also the wife of Caleb and mother of Hur) (r:1.35.16/1.48.7)
Efrathah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephrathah) (d:name of the district of Bethlehem in Judah, the home of the family of David) (r:33.5.2)
Efron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephron) (d:Hittite, son of Zohar, who sold Abraham the field and cave of Machpelah) (r:1.23.8/1.23.14)
Eglah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Eglah) (d:wife of David and mother of Ithream) (r:10.3.5/13.3.3)
eglaim = (t:see) <En-eglaim>
Eglaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglaim) (d:town of Moab named in the lament of Isaiah over Moab) (r:23.15.8)
Eglath = (t:see) <Eglath-shelishiah>
Eglath-sheli-shiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglath Shelishiyah) (d:place in Moab named in the oracles against Moab) (q:draft)
Eglath-shelishiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglath Shelishiyah) (d:place in Moab named in the oracles against Moab) (r:23.15.5) (q:draft)
Eglathshelishiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglath Shelishiyah) (d:place in Moab named in the oracles against Moab) (r:24.48.34/23.15.5)
Eglon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Eglon) (d:Canaanite city in the lowland of Judah taken by Joshua; also the king of Moab killed by Ehud) (r:6.15.39/6.10.3)
Egypt = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Egypt) (d:country on the Nile where the Israelites were slaves until the Lord brought them out; also written <Izipt>) (r:2.12.1)
Egypt = (i:2) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Egypt) (d:son of Ham, ancestor of the Egyptians) (r:1.10.6)
eh = (i:1) (t:intj) (d:exclamation of surprise or of correcting oneself, as between two numbers in the sayings of Proverbs 30: three, no, four; also a cry of people shocked at a ruin) (s:ee) (r:46.1.16) (q:draft)
Ehi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ehi) (d:son of Benjamin) (q:draft)
ehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:splitting/chopping) (d:<eh>, the form of <ek> split used before a suffix, with the noun suffix <na>: {sing ehna} is the splitting of logs) (q:draft)
Ehud = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ehud) (d:judge of Israel, a left-handed man of Benjamin who killed Eglon king of Moab) (r:7.3.26) (q:draft)
ei = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:we/us) (d:first person plural including the hearer, the short form of <eite>; before <hong> and <tawh> it is the object, us) (s:eite)
Eijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elijah) (d:the prophet Elijah, as the name is spelled in Matthew 11:14) (r:40.11.14)
Eilishah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elishah) (d:son of Javan, grandson of Japheth) (r:1.10.4)
eima = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:ours) (d:what belongs to us, used with <aa> or {a’}, belonging to: {eima aa hi} is it is ours) (b:ei)
eima = (i:2) (t:det) (w:our/our own) (d:<ei>, we, with <ma>: belonging to us, placed before a noun; {eima adingin} is for ourselves) (b:ei)
eimah = (i:1) (t:det) (w:ours) (d:possessive use of the emphatic pronoun {eimah}: our own, belonging to us ourselves) (b:ei)
eimah = (i:2) (t:pron) (w:our/ourselves/we ourselves) (d:emphatic first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, <ei> with the emphatic <mah>: we ourselves, us; before a noun, our own) (s:eimau) (b:ei)
EIMAH = (t:todo) (q:draft, part of {KEIMAH} printed as {K EIMAH} in Exodus 3.14, <keimah> I myself used for the divine name I AM, not a word by itself)
eimau = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:ourselves/us/our own) (d:emphatic first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer: we ourselves, us, our own; {eimau sungah} means in us, and {eimau san ciatah} each to our own way) (s:eite/eimah) (q:draft)
eimaute = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:we/us/ourselves) (d:<eimau>, the emphatic first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, with the plural ending <te>; English has we, us or our according to its place in the sentence) (s:eite) (b:eimau) (q:draft)
Eite = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:we/us/our) (d:<eite>, the first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a quotation; English has we, us or our according to its place in the sentence) (b:eite) (r:45.9.29) (q:draft)
EITE = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:our/we/us) (d:<eite>, the first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, written in capitals within the name The Lord Our Righteousness) (q:draft)
ejaakan = (t:see) <Ben-ejaakan>
ek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dung/excrement/waste) (d:the solid waste of a person or an animal; {bawng ek} is cow dung, and {mihing ek} human excrement) (s:eklei) (r:26.4.12) (q:draft)
ek = (i:2) (t:n) (w:dross/slag) (d:the waste that is separated from a metal when it is refined; {sik-ek} is the dross of iron) (s:saam-ek) (q:draft)
eka = (i:1) (t:n) (w:acre) (d:a measure of land, from the English word acre; also spelled <eeka> and <ekah>) (s:eeka/ekah) (q:draft)
ekah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:acre) (d:a measure of land, the English word acre; another spelling of <eka>) (s:eeka) (b:eka) (q:draft)
Ekanah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elkanah) (d:name of several Levites of the line of Kohath, usually spelled <Elkanah>) (r:13.6.23/13.6.35)
Ekbatana = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ecbatana) (d:capital city of Media, where the scroll with the decree of Cyrus was found) (r:15.6.2)
ekbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:latrine/toilet) (d:a place used as a toilet; built from <ek>, dung, and <buk>, a hut or shelter) (q:draft)
Eker = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eker) (d:son of Ram and grandson of Jerahmeel, of the tribe of Judah) (q:draft)
ekkeu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dried dung) (d:human or animal dung that has dried, gathered and burned as fuel; built from <ek>, dung, and <keu>, dry) (q:draft)
ekkhamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:chopping up/splitting) (d:chopping or splitting wood into pieces, as for a fire; built from <ek>, split, and <kham>, with the linking ending <in>, and also written as two words, {ek khamin}) (q:draft, low confidence)
eklei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dung/manure) (d:dung, also dung put on the soil to make it fertile; {eklei sung} is to put manure on, to fertilize) (s:ek) (q:draft)
eknel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cud) (d:food that an animal brings back from its stomach to the mouth to chew again; {eknel hai} is to chew the cud) (q:draft)
Ekron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ekron) (d:one of the five chief cities of the Philistines, on the border of Judah and Dan) (r:6.15.45/6.19.43)
ekte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dung/offal/intestines) (d:<ek>, dung, with the plural ending <te>: the dung and waste parts of an animal that are burned outside the camp) (b:ek) (q:draft)
ekte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:splitters) (d:as the second part of {sing-ekte}, those who split wood: <ek>, split, with the plural ending {-te}) (q:draft, low confidence)
el = (i:1) (t:v) (w:envy/be malicious toward/be hostile to) (d:bear ill will toward someone or act as a rival; {mi a el teci} is a malicious witness, and {el pau} is to speak with malice; most occurrences of these letters are not this word but the last part of Hebrew names such as <Beth-el> and <Jezre-el>) (s:een/eng/haza) (q:draft, low confidence)
El = (t:see) <El-Elohe>
El-Elohe = (i:1) (t:name) (w:El Elohe Israel) (d:first part of <El-Elohe-Israel>, the name Jacob gave to the altar he set up) (q:draft)
El-Elohe-Israel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:El Elohe Israel) (d:name that Jacob gave to the altar he set up near Shechem) (r:1.33.20)
El-paran = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:El Paran) (d:place at the edge of the wilderness, the farthest point Kedorlaomer reached in the land of the Horites) (q:draft)
Ela = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ela) (d:father of Shimei, one of the district governors of Solomon) (q:draft)
Ela = (i:2) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Elam) (d:the land of King Kedorlaomer, written {Ela} in one text of Genesis 14:9 and <Elam> elsewhere) (r:1.14.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
Elah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elah) (d:name of several men, among them a king of Israel, son of Baasha, and a son of Caleb) (r:13.4.15) (q:draft)
Elah = (i:2) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Elah) (d:valley in Judah where Israel camped against the Philistines and David fought Goliath; {Elah kuam} is the Valley of Elah) (q:draft)
elaiah = (t:see) <Re-elaiah>
Elam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elam) (d:son of Shem and ancestor of the Elamites; also the name of several other men) (r:1.10.22/13.8.24)
Elasah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elasah) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Shaphan who carried the letter of Jeremiah to Babylon) (r:24.29.3/15.10.22)
Elash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elah) (d:father of Hoshea, the last king of Israel; spelled Elah in the NIV) (r:12.17.1)
Elath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Elath) (d:town on the Red Sea near Ezion Geber, at the southern end of Edom) (r:5.2.8) (q:draft)
Elazar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eleazar) (d:son of Aaron who followed him as high priest, usually spelled <Eleazar>) (r:15.7.5)
Elberith = (i:1) (t:name) (w:El-Berith) (d:god worshipped at Shechem, in whose temple the people of the tower took refuge) (r:7.9.46)
Elbethel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:El-bethel) (d:name that Jacob gave to the place at Bethel where he built an altar) (r:1.35.7)
Elda = (t:see) <Elda-ah>
Elda-ah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eldaah) (d:son of Midian, grandson of Abraham and Keturah) (r:13.1.33) (q:draft)
