Eldad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eldad) (d:one of the two elders who prophesied in the camp in the time of Moses) (r:4.11.26/4.11.27)
Elead = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elead) (d:a son of Ephraim killed by the men of Gath) (q:draft)
Eleadah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eleadah) (d:descendant of Ephraim) (r:13.7.20)
Elealeh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Elealeh) (d:town east of the Jordan near Heshbon, rebuilt by the Reubenites and later held by Moab) (r:4.32.37/4.32.3)
Eleasah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eleasah) (d:name of two men, a descendant of Jerahmeel of Judah and a descendant of King Saul) (r:13.2.39/13.2.40)
Eleash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eleasah) (d:descendant of King Saul through Jonathan; spelled Eleasah in the NIV) (r:13.9.43)
Eleazar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eleazar) (d:name of several men, chiefly the son of Aaron who followed him as high priest) (r:4.3.2)
Eleazer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eleazar) (d:another spelling of <Eleazar>, chiefly the son of Aaron who followed him as high priest) (r:2.6.25/4.26.63)
Eler = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eder) (d:town in the far south of Judah near the border of Edom; spelled Eder in the NIV) (r:6.15.21)
Elhaan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elhanan) (d:son of Dodo from Bethlehem, one of the mighty warriors of David; spelled Elhanan in the NIV) (r:13.11.26)
Elhanan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elhanan) (d:name of two warriors of David, the son of Jair who killed the brother of Goliath and the son of Dodo from Bethlehem) (r:10.23.24/13.20.5)
Eli = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eli) (d:priest at Shiloh who brought up the boy Samuel) (r:9.2.12) (q:draft)
Eliab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eliab) (d:name of several men, among them the leader of Zebulun in the wilderness and the eldest brother of David) (r:4.1.9/4.26.8)
Eliada = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eliada) (d:name of several men, among them a son of David born in Jerusalem) (r:10.5.16/13.3.8)
