emerald = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:emerald) (d:green precious stone, a loanword from English; in Exodus the NIV has turquoise for this stone) (q:draft)
Emerald = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:emerald) (d:<emerald> written with a capital as the name of a precious stone) (b:emerald) (q:draft)
Emim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/people) (w:Emites) (d:people of great height who lived in Moab in ancient times, called Emim by the Moabites) (s:Emin) (r:5.2.10/5.2.11)
emin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bake) (d:<em>, bake, with the linking suffix <in>: bake, said as a command that is followed by another) (b:em) (q:draft)
Emin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Emites/Emim) (d:people of great height living in Shaveh Kiriathaim, defeated by Kedorlaomer) (s:Emim) (r:1.14.5) (q:draft)
emkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bake together) (d:<em>, bake, with <khawm>, together: bake in one oven together) (b:em) (q:draft)
Emmanuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Immanuel) (d:name given to Jesus in the Gospel of Matthew, meaning God with us) (r:40.1.23)
Emmaus = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Emmaus) (d:village about seven miles from Jerusalem, to which two disciples walked on the day of the resurrection) (r:42.24.13)
emna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baking) (d:<em>, bake, with the noun suffix <na>; {moh emna meikhuk} is an oven for baking bread and {emna ding mun} is a place for baking) (b:em) (q:draft)
emsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:baked/broiled/roasted) (d:<em>, bake, with <sa> for a completed act; used alone it means baked food, and {sik emsa} is a hot iron) (b:em) (q:draft)
emsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bake for) (d:<em>, bake, with <sak>, here doing the action for someone else: bake for someone) (b:em) (q:draft)
En = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:En) (d:first part of place names written with a hyphen, such as <En-gedi> and <En-gannim>) (r:6.19.21) (q:draft)
En-eglaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Eglaim) (d:place on the shore of the Dead Sea in the vision of Ezekiel) (s:Eneglaim) (q:draft)
En-gannim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Gannim) (d:town in the territory of Issachar, given to the Levites) (s:Engannim) (r:6.19.21) (q:draft)
en-gedi = (t:todo) (q:draft, the place name <En-gedi>, NIV En Gedi, counted in lowercase where it opens a sentence or a bracket in 26.47.10 and 14.20.2; a lowercase keyword cannot take type name)
En-gedi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Gedi) (d:oasis and town on the western shore of the Dead Sea, where David hid from Saul) (s:Engedi) (r:6.15.62) (q:draft)
enai = (t:see) <Elio-enai>
Enaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Enaim) (d:place on the road to Timnah where Tamar waited for Judah) (r:1.38.14/1.38.21)
Enam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Enam) (d:town in the lowland of Judah) (q:draft)
Enan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enan) (d:father of Ahira, the leader of the tribe of Naphtali in the wilderness) (r:4.1.15/4.10.27) (q:draft)
encian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:look carefully/pay attention/observe) (d:<en>, look, with <cian>, clearly: look at something carefully and take notice of it) (q:draft)
encik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:watch closely/keep an eye on) (d:keep looking at someone carefully, in order to guard or to find fault) (q:draft)
encikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:watching closely/observing carefully) (d:<encik>, watch closely, with the linking suffix <in>: watching closely and so doing the next action) (b:encik) (q:draft)
encikpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:watcher) (d:<encik>, watch closely, with <pa> marking a male person: the one who keeps watching) (b:encik) (q:draft)
Endor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Endor) (d:town in the territory of Manasseh where Saul consulted a medium) (r:6.17.11/9.28.7)
Eneglaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Eglaim) (d:place on the shore of the Dead Sea in the vision of Ezekiel) (s:En-eglaim) (r:26.47.10)
enen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep looking/look on/watch) (d:<en>, look, doubled for an action that goes on) (q:draft)
enenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gazing/looking for a long time) (d:<en>, look, doubled for an action that goes on, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:enen) (q:draft)
eng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:envy/be envious of/be jealous of) (d:feel envy or jealousy toward someone who has what one lacks; {eng kei in} is do not envy) (s:haza/el) (r:19.73.3) (q:draft)
Engannim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:En-gannim/En Gannim) (d:name of two towns, one in the lowland of Judah and one in Issachar given to the Levites) (s:En-gannim) (r:6.15.34)
engdum = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dark blue) (d:a colour named between fiery red and sulphur yellow; <eng> is yellow and <dum> is blue or green, so the exact colour is uncertain) (q:draft, low confidence)
engdup = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:blue) (d:colour of cloth, named beside <sandup> where the English has blue and purple) (q:draft, low confidence)
Engedi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:En Gedi) (d:oasis and town on the western shore of the Dead Sea, where David hid from Saul) (s:En-gedi) (r:9.23.29/6.15.62)
engiau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:peer/peek) (d:look in through a narrow opening) (q:draft, low confidence)
engin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be zealous for/be jealous over) (d:<eng>, envy or be jealous, with the linking suffix <in>; here of people eagerly courting others) (b:eng) (q:draft, low confidence)
engkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:envy/come to envy) (d:<eng> envy with <kha>, which shows the action coming to happen; used with <kei> in warnings not to envy) (s:eng/haza) (q:draft)
Enhaddah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Haddah) (d:town in the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.21)
Enhakkore = (i:1) (t:name) (c:well) (w:En Hakkore) (d:spring at Lehi that God opened for Samson when he was thirsty) (r:7.15.19)
Enhazor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:En Hazor) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.37)
enin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:looking at/looking) (d:<en>, look, with the linking suffix <in>: looking at someone or something and then doing the next action) (s:khuadakin/dakin) (b:en) (q:draft)
enkak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:compare/look at side by side) (d:look at two together to see how they differ; used with <tawh>, with) (s:enteh/tehkak) (q:draft)
enkhong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:look on/merely watch) (d:<en>, look, with <khong>: keep looking on without acting) (s:enen) (q:draft, low confidence)
enluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:envy/bitterness) (d:in {enluatna lungsim}, a heart of envy or bitterness; apparently <eng>, envy, with <luat>, too much, and the noun suffix <na>) (s:enna/hazatna) (q:draft, low confidence)
Enmishpat = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:En-mishpat/En Mishpat) (d:another name for Kadesh) (r:1.14.7)
enna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:envy/jealousy) (d:ill feeling at the good of another, not from <en>, look; {enna lungsim} is an envious mind and {enna mit} an envious eye) (s:hazatna/enluatna/elna) (r:41.7.22) (q:draft)
enneu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:look down on/stare at with contempt) (d:<en>, look, with <neu>, small: look at someone as of little worth) (s:simmawh) (q:draft, low confidence)
Enok = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enoch) (d:son of Jared and father of Methuselah, who walked with God; also the name of a son of Cain) (r:1.5.21)
Enos = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enosh/Enos) (d:son of Seth, named in the genealogy of Jesus; spelled Enosh in the NIV) (s:Enosh) (q:draft)
Enosh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Enosh) (d:son of Seth and father of Kenan) (s:Enos) (r:1.5.6)
enpha = (t:see) <ki-enpha>
Enrimmon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Rimmon) (d:town in Judah where people settled after the exile) (r:16.11.29)
Enrogel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:En Rogel) (d:spring near Jerusalem on the border between Judah and Benjamin) (r:6.18.16/11.1.9)
ensak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let see/make look/show) (d:<en>, look, with the causative <sak>: make or let someone look at something) (s:musak) (b:en) (q:draft)
ensawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:watch in turn/oversee in turn) (d:<en>, look, with <sawn>, passing on: of a higher official who in turn watches those below) (q:draft, low confidence)
