etin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:looking/gazing) (d:<et>, look, with the linking ending <in>; {etin nei} is keep looking at with desire; also the second part of hyphenated words such as {ze-etin}, testing) (b:et) (q:draft)
etkak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:compare) (d:form of <enkak>, compare, used before <ciangin> and in dependent clauses) (s:genteh/tehkak/tehpih/enteh) (q:draft)
etkakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:standard/comparison/figure of speech) (d:<etkak>, compare, with the noun suffix <na>: something to compare with, a standard measure; {etkakna lim-in} is by way of comparison, figuratively) (b:etkak) (q:draft)
etkawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:while looking at) (d:<et>, form of <en>, look, with <kawm>, while, and the linking suffix <in>: looking at someone while doing something else) (q:draft)
etkik = (t:see) <ki-etkik>
