gahin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:bearing fruit/yielding/bear fruit) (d:The verb <gah>, bear fruit, with the linking ending <in>; it often follows the noun <gah>, as in {gah gahin}, bearing fruit.) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to bear fruit/have fruit) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and <khak>, a form of <kha>, happen to; {a gahkhak leh} means in case it has fruit.) (q:draft, low confidence)
gahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:yield/bring forth/produce) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and <khia>, out: bring forth a crop, said of the land.) (s:gahsak/piangsak) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fruitless/not bearing fruit) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and the negative <lo>; said of a branch that bears no fruit.) (a:gahpha) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahpha = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fruitful/bearing well) (d:Built from <gah>, fruit, and <pha>, good; said of a vine or tree that bears much fruit.) (a:gahlo) (q:draft)
gahphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear well/be fruitful) (d:Form of <gahpha>, bear good fruit, used before a noun such as <hun>, time: {a gahphat hun} is the time when it bears well.) (b:gahpha) (q:draft)
gahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:produce/bear/make bear fruit) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and the causative <sak>: make a crop or fruit come, said of the soil or of people.) (s:gahkhia/piangsak) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahta = (t:see) <gahta-in>
gahta-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear fruit/be bearing fruit) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, <ta>, now or already, and the linking ending <in>: the trees are now bearing fruit.) (q:draft)
gahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fruits/crops/produce) (d:Plural of <gah>: the fruits or crops of land, trees or work.) (s:singgahte) (b:gah) (r:1.1.12)
gahteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the fruit/the whole fruit) (d:Built from <gah>, fruit, and <teng>, all: all the fruit of a tree or vine.) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can bear/be able to bear) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and <thei>, can; used in questions about what a tree can bear.) (s:gahzo/gahtheih) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to bear fruit) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and <theih>, be able; the form used before <nading>, so that it can bear.) (s:gahzo/gahthei) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear fruit upward/bear fruit above) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and <to>, upward; set against taking root downward.) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gahzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to bear fruit/manage to bear fruit) (d:Built from <gah>, bear fruit, and <zo>, be able; {bangmah gahzo lo} is bear nothing at all.) (s:gahtheih/gahthei) (b:gah) (q:draft)
gai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:conceive/become pregnant) (d:Conceive a child, become or be pregnant; {gai kik} is conceive again.) (s:naupaai/paii) (r:1.30.5)
Gaia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaius) (d:Gaius of Derbe, a companion of Paul on his journey through Macedonia to Asia) (r:44.20.4) (q:draft)
Gaias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaius) (d:name of several early Christians, among them the host of Paul in Corinth and the friend to whom the third letter of John is written) (r:45.16.23/64.1.1)
gaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:eat up/finish off/consume) (d:eat until nothing is left) (s:netum/nektum/nemang) (q:draft)
gaih = (i:2) (t:v) (d:used after <nungkik>, draw back, in {nungkik gaih-in}, said of people who shrink back or flee from a sight, what {gaih} itself adds is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
gaihgaih = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:placed after <kisat> beat: throbbing or sounding again and again like the strings of a harp, said of a grieving heart) (q:draft, low confidence)
gaihin = (i:1) (t:v) (d:<gaih> with the linking suffix <in>, used after <nungkik>, draw back, of people who shrink back or flee from a sight; what <gaih> itself adds is not clear) (b:gaih) (q:draft, low confidence)
gaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:devour/eat up/consume) (d:<gaih>, eat up, finish off, with <sak>, which here shows the action is done to the loss of another) (s:netum/nektum/nemang) (b:gaih) (q:draft)
gaihsakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:eat up/consume entirely) (d:<gaih>, eat up, with <sak> and <mang>, away: eat up all that belongs to someone else) (q:draft, low confidence)
