galsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:battle/war) (d:<Gal>, war, with <sung>, inside: the battle or the war as the place one is in; {galsung pan} is from the battle and {galsung nazatte} are weapons of war.) (s:galdona/galkidona) (a:galdaihna) (r:26.32.28) (q:draft)
galsunga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in battle/in war) (d:{Galsung}, battle, with the place ending <a>: in battle; {galsunga site} are those who die in battle.) (b:galsung) (q:draft)
galtai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fugitive) (d:<Gal>, enemy, with <tai>, flee: a person who flees from an enemy or from war; {galtai-in} means as a fugitive, in flight.)
galtai = (i:2) (t:n) (w:refugee) (d:A person who has fled from war to find safety in another place.)
galtaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flight/fleeing from the enemy) (d:{Galtai}, flee from the enemy, with the noun suffix <na>: fleeing before enemies.) (s:taina) (b:galtai) (q:draft)
galtaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fugitives/refugees) (d:Plural of <galtai>: people who flee from an enemy or from war.) (b:galtai) (q:draft)
galte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:enemies/foes) (d:Plural of <gal>: enemies, those who fight against or hate someone.) (s:langte/mudahte/langpangte/galbawlte) (a:lawmte) (b:gal) (r:19.7.4) (q:draft)
galvan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weapons/arms/armor) (d:<Gal>, war, with <van>, goods: the equipment of war, weapons and armor; {galvan koihna} is an armory and {galvan puapa} an armor-bearer.) (s:galhiam) (r:16.3.19) (q:draft)
galvante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:armor/weapons/war gear) (d:{Galvan} with the plural <te>: the things worn and carried for battle.) (s:galhiamte) (b:galvan) (q:draft)
galvanteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the weapons/weapons of war) (d:{Galvan}, weapons, with <teng>, all: all the weapons of a soldier.) (b:galvan) (q:draft)
galvil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:watchman/lookout/sentry/guard) (d:<Gal>, enemy, with <vil>, watch: one who keeps watch for the enemy; also the act of keeping watch, as in {galvil koih}, post a guard.) (s:galvilpa/vilpa/khuacing) (q:draft)
galvilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:watch/lookout/guard post) (d:{Galvil}, keep watch, with the noun suffix <na>: keeping watch against an enemy, or the place for it; {galvilna bukno} is a watchtower and {galvilna inndei} a guardroom.) (s:vilna) (b:galvil) (r:14.20.24) (q:draft)
galvilpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:watchman/lookout) (d:{Galvil}, watch, with <pa>, which marks a man: a man who keeps watch for the enemy.) (s:galvil/vilpa) (b:galvil) (r:26.33.3) (q:draft)
galvilte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:watchmen/guards/lookouts) (d:Plural of <galvil>: watchmen or guards who keep watch for the enemy.) (s:vilte/khuacingte/cingte) (b:galvil) (q:draft)
galzak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hear of/hear from afar) (d:<Gal>, from far off, with <zak>, hear: hear about someone or something that is elsewhere.) (q:draft)
galzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:win in war/conquer) (d:<Gal>, war, with <zawh>, the form of <zo>, overcome, used before another word; {galzawh van} is plunder, the goods won in war.) (q:draft)
galzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:victory) (d:{Galzawh}, win in war, with the noun suffix <na>: victory in battle.) (s:gualzawhna/zawhna) (a:guallelhna/lelhna) (b:galzawh) (q:draft)
galzote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conquerors/victors) (d:<Gal>, war, with <zo>, win, and the plural <te>: those who win a war.) (s:gualzote) (q:draft)
galzuih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow at a distance) (d:<Gal>, from afar, with <zuih>, follow: follow at a distance; {nung galzuih} is follow behind someone from far off.) (q:draft)
gam = (i:2) (t:n) (w:territory) (d:The area of land that belongs to a people, a tribe or a ruler.) (r:1.14.7)
gam = (i:3) (t:n) (w:kingdom/realm) (d:The land that a king rules; {kumpi gam} is a kingdom.) (s:kumpigam) (r:5.3.13)
gam = (i:4) (t:n) (w:land) (d:Land as the place where people live; after a name it means the land of, as in {Kanaan gam}, the land of Canaan.) (s:leitang) (r:1.23.12)
Gam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kingdom) (d:{Gam} written with a capital for the kingdom of God or of heaven, as in {Pasian’ Gam} and {Vantung Gam}.) (s:Kumpigam) (b:gam) (q:draft)
gam-bawngtal = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:<Gam>, wild country, with <bawngtal>, bull: a wild ox; also written <gambawngtal>.) (s:gambawngtal/gamsial/zangsial)
gama = (i:1) (t:n) (w:of the land/in the land) (d:<Gam> with the ending <a>, which joins the land to the word that follows: of or in that land.) (b:gam) (q:draft)
Gamad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gammad) (d:place, of uncertain location, whose men guarded the towers of Tyre) (r:26.27.11)
gamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the land/to the land/land/country) (d:<Gam> with the place marker <ah>: in or to the land of.) (b:gam) (r:1.37.1) (q:draft)
Gamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the kingdom/into the kingdom/in the land) (d:<Gam>, the capitalised word for kingdom or land, with <ah>, the marker of place: in or into the Kingdom, as in {Vantung Gamah}, in the kingdom of heaven.) (b:Gam) (q:draft)
Gamaliel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gamaliel) (d:name of two men: the son of Pedahzur, leader of the tribe of Manasseh in the wilderness, and a Pharisee and teacher of the law in Jerusalem) (r:4.7.54/4.10.23)
gambawngtal = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ox)
gambawngtal = (i:2) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:<Gam>, wild country, with <bawngtal>, bull: a wild ox that cannot be made to work.) (s:gamsial/zangsial/gam-bawngtal)
gambulak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wilderness/deserted land) (d:Wild, empty country where no one goes; {lam lianpite gambulak suak} means the highways have become deserted.) (s:gamlakpi) (q:draft, low confidence)
gambup = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the whole land) (d:<Gam>, land, with <bup>, whole: the whole of a land.)
gambup = (i:2) (t:n) (w:the entire country) (d:The whole extent of a country or region, from one border to the other.)
gambuppi = (t:see) <gambuppi-ah>
gambuppi-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the whole land/on the whole land) (d:<Gam>, land, with <bup>, whole, the intensifier <pi> and the place marker <ah>: in or upon the whole land.) (q:draft)
gamdai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:quiet/silent/peaceful) (d:Still and without noise, said of a land at peace or of people who stop speaking; {gamdai takin} is quietly and {gamdai-in om} is keep silent.) (s:dai) (a:gamlum) (r:18.29.10) (q:draft)
gamdaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be quiet/be silent/fall silent) (d:Form of <gamdai>, quiet, used before <nading> and <khit>: become quiet, stop making noise.) (s:daih) (a:gamlum) (b:gamdai) (q:draft)
gamdaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:solitary place/lonely place/desolate place) (d:{Gamdaih}, be quiet, with the noun suffix <na>: quiet country where no one is; often followed by <mun>, place.) (s:mundai) (b:gamdaih) (q:draft)
gamdaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quiet/calm/silence) (d:{Gamdai}, quiet, with the causative <sak>: make people be quiet.) (s:daihsak/daisak) (b:gamdai) (q:draft)
gamdaisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quieting/silencing) (d:{Gamdaisak}, make quiet, with the linking suffix <in>: quieting people before going on to speak.) (b:gamdaisak) (q:draft)
gamdaizaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:quieter/more quiet) (d:{Gamdai}, quiet, with the comparative <zaw>: quieter than before.) (b:gamdai) (q:draft)
gamdang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:foreign/strange) (d:<Gam>, land, with <dang>, other: of another country; {gamdang mi} is a foreigner or stranger and {gamdang pasian} a foreign god.) (s:namdang) (q:draft)
gamdang = (i:2) (t:n) (w:foreign land/foreign country) (d:<Gam>, land, with <dang>, other: a land that is not one’s own; {gamdang khatah} is to another land.) (s:gamdangpi) (q:draft)
gamdangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in a foreign land/to another land/among the nations) (d:{Gamdang}, foreign land, with the place marker <ah>: in or to another land, among other nations.) (b:gamdang) (q:draft)
Gamdangah = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Gamdangah) (d:not a proper name: the word <gamdangah>, in a foreign land, written with a capital at the start of a sentence)
gamdangmi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foreigner/stranger) (d:{Gamdang}, foreign, with <mi>, person: a person from another country.) (s:khualmi/mikhual/minamdang) (a:tualsuak/gammi) (b:gamdang) (q:draft)
gamdangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foreign land/foreign country) (d:{Gamdang}, foreign land, with the intensifier <pi>: a land wholly foreign to a person.) (s:gamdang) (b:gamdang) (q:draft)
gamdangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nations/foreign nations/foreign lands) (d:Plural of <gamdang>: other countries and their peoples, the nations.) (b:gamdang) (r:24.46.1) (q:draft)
gamdong = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as far as the land/down to the realm) (d:<Gam>, land, with <dong>, until: as far as the land or realm of, in the verse the realm of the dead.) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamdung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:length of the land) (d:<Gam>, land, with <dung>, length; paired with <gamvai>, the breadth of the land.) (a:gamvai) (q:draft)
gamgei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:edge of the land/border) (d:<Gam>, land, with <gei>, side or edge; {sehnel gamgei} is the edge of the desert.) (s:gamgi/gammong) (q:draft)
gamgi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:border/boundary/limit) (d:<Gam>, land, with <gi>, boundary: the border or limit of a land, of a city or of the sea.) (s:gi/gammong) (q:draft)
gamgite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:borders/boundaries/territory) (d:Plural of <gamgi>: the borders of a land, and so the land within them.) (b:gamgi) (q:draft)
gamh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage) (d:Land or property that is handed down in a family or tribe; {gamh luah} is to receive an inheritance.) (s:gamhluah/gamluah/luah/luahna) (q:draft)
gamhal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn the land/set fire to the forest) (d:<gam>, land or wild country, with <hal>, burn) (q:draft)
gamhluah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage) (d:{Gamh}, inheritance, with <luah>, inherit: land or possession received as a share to keep.) (s:gamh/gamluah/luahna/gamhluahna) (q:draft)
gamhluah = (i:2) (t:n) (w:heir) (d:The person who inherits.) (s:gamhluahpa/innluahpa) (q:draft)
gamhluahin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as an inheritance) (d:{Gamhluah}, inheritance, with the marker <in>: as an inheritance, for a possession.) (b:gamhluah) (q:draft)
gamhluahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage/property) (d:{Gamhluah} with the noun suffix <na>: the land or place that a person or tribe has inherited.) (s:gamhluah/gamh/luahna) (b:gamhluah) (q:draft)
gamhluahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:heir) (d:{Gamhluah} with <pa>, which marks a man: the man who inherits.) (s:innluahpa) (b:gamhluah) (q:draft)
gamhluahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:heirs) (d:{Gamhluah} with the plural <te>: those who inherit.) (b:gamhluah) (q:draft)
gamhluahte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:inheritance/inherited lands) (d:{Gamhluah} with the plural <te>: the shares of land that pass to the heirs.) (s:gamhte) (b:gamhluah) (q:draft)
gamhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good land) (d:<Gam>, land, with <hoih>, good: the good land that God promised.) (s:gamnuam) (q:draft)
gamhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritances/inherited lands) (d:Plural of <gamh>: the shares of land handed down in a tribe or family.) (s:gamhluahte) (b:gamh) (q:draft)
gamin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:land/country) (d:<Gam> with the marker <in> written together: as a country, or the land as the subject of the sentence.) (b:gam) (q:draft)
gamkeel = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild goat) (d:<Gam>, wild country, with <keel>, goat: a wild goat.) (q:draft)
gamkeelte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild goats) (d:Plural of <gamkeel>: wild goats.) (b:gamkeel) (q:draft)
gamkeu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dry land/parched land) (d:<Gam>, land, with <keu>, dry: land without water.) (s:leikeu/leikeuna) (q:draft)
gamkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kingdom/country) (d:<Gam>, land or kingdom, written together with <khat>, one: one kingdom, a kingdom; <gamkhat leh gamkhat> is kingdom against kingdom.) (q:draft)
gamkhin = (t:see) <gamkhin'na>
gamkhin'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desolation/ruin) (d:The state of a place laid waste; related to <gamkhing>, desolation, and also written <gamkhinna>.) (s:gamkhinna/gamkhing) (q:draft)
gamkhing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desolation/wasteland/desolate place) (d:A land or place laid waste and left without people; {gamkhing suak} is become desolate and {gamkhing suaksak} is make desolate.) (s:gamsia/mundai/gamkhinna) (q:draft)
Gamkhing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Desolate) (d:{Gamkhing}, wasteland, written with a capital as a name given to the land.) (b:gamkhing) (q:draft)
gamkhingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:desolate/as a wasteland) (d:<Gamkhing>, desolate place, with the ending <in>: in a desolate state; with <om> it means lie desolate and with <bawl> make desolate.) (b:gamkhing) (q:draft)
gamkhingpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:most desolate) (d:<Gamkhing>, desolation, with the superlative <pen>: the most desolate of all.) (b:gamkhing) (q:draft)
gamkhinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desolation/ruin) (d:The state of a place laid waste; related to <gamkhing>, desolation, and also written <gamkhin'na>.) (s:gamkhin'na/gamkhing) (q:draft)
gamkuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley) (d:<gam>, land, with <kuam>, valley: a valley region; {Sukkot gamkuam} is the Valley of Sukkoth) (s:kuam/guam/mualkuam) (r:19.108.7) (q:draft)
gamlak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forest) (s:tulak)
gamlak = (i:2) (t:n) (w:field) (s:lolai)
gamlak = (i:3) (t:n) (w:wood)
gamlak = (i:4) (t:n) (w:jungle/wilderness) (d:wild country where no one lives; the land the Israelites crossed after leaving Egypt)
gamlaka = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the field/in the wilderness/in the open country) (d:<gamlak> with the place ending <a>, the short form of <ah>: that is in the field or wilderness; {gamlaka om gamsate} are the beasts of the field) (b:gamlak) (q:draft)
gamlakah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:field/in the field/in the wilderness) (d:<gamlak> with the place marker <ah>: in or into the field, the open country or the wilderness) (b:gamlak) (r:26.39.5)
gamlakpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wasteland/wilderness/desolate place) (d:<gamlak>, wild country, with <pi>, great: land left wild and empty; {gamlakpi suak} is become a wasteland) (s:gamkhing/gamsimtham/gamsia) (b:gamlak) (r:24.50.13) (q:draft)
gamlakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wilderness/deserts/wild places) (d:<gamlak> with the plural <te>: the wild, uncultivated parts of a land) (b:gamlak) (q:draft)
gamlapen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:farthest/most distant) (d:<gamla>, far, with <pen>, most; {leimong gamlapen} is the farthest end of the earth) (a:naipen/kinaipen) (b:gamla) (q:draft)
gamlapi = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:far away/afar/far off) (d:<gamla>, far, with <pi>, great: at, to or from a great distance; {gamlapi-ah} is to a far place, {gamlapi panin} is from afar) (s:pekah/peka) (a:kimnai-a) (b:gamla) (r:18.27.21) (q:draft)
gamlat = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:far/distant) (d:form of <gamla> used before another word; {a gamlat mah bangin} is as far as) (b:gamla) (q:draft)
gamlatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:distance) (d:<gamla> far in its form <gamlat> with the noun suffix <na>: how far away something is) (b:gamlat) (q:draft)
gamlazaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:farther/more distant) (d:<gamla>, far, with the comparative <zaw>) (a:naizaw) (b:gamla) (q:draft)
gamlelei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whole land/land) (d:apparently <gam>, land, <le>, and, <lei>, earth, written as one word: the land and the ground) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamlian = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great nation/great country) (d:<gam>, land, with <lian>, great) (q:draft)
gamluah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage) (d:<gam>, land, with <luah>, inherit: land or a share received as an inheritance) (s:gamh/gamhluah/luah) (q:draft)
gamluahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritance/possession of land) (d:<gamluah>, inheritance, with the noun suffix <na>: the holding of land by inheritance) (s:gamhluahna) (b:gamluah) (q:draft)
gamlum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:noise/uproar/tumult/commotion) (d:loud confused noise of a crowd or of battle) (s:gamlumna/husa/huging) (a:daihna) (q:draft)
gamlum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be in uproar/make a commotion/be noisy) (d:be full of noise and disorder, said of a crowd, an army or a town) (s:kigamlum/kibuai) (a:gamdaih/daai/gamdai) (q:draft)
gamlumin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in an uproar/in confusion) (d:<gamlum> uproar with the suffix <in>; {gamlumin om} is be in an uproar) (b:gamlum) (q:draft)
gamlumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:noise/uproar/tumult/commotion) (d:<gamlum>, uproar, with the noun suffix <na>: the loud noise of a crowd, of rejoicing, of mourning or of a riot) (s:gamlum/husa/huging) (a:daihna) (b:gamlum) (q:draft)
gamlumnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:noises/noise/clamour) (d:plural of <gamlumna>, the loud noise of people, of singing or revelry) (b:gamlumna) (q:draft)
gamlumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause an uproar/start a riot) (d:<gamlum>, uproar, with the causative <sak>) (b:gamlum) (q:draft)
gamlumte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tumult/uproar) (d:<gamlum> with plural <te>; {mi gamlumte} is the peoples in tumult, the turmoil of the nations) (b:gamlum) (q:draft)
gammang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stray/wander/be lost) (d:go astray and be lost, said of animals and of people; before <tulak> it describes wild overgrown land, as in <gammang tulak>, a wild thicket) (s:lampial/vakmang) (q:draft)
gammanpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead astray/cause to wander) (d:take others along in going astray and wandering lost) (s:lampialsak) (q:draft)
gammi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:citizen/native/inhabitant) (d:person belonging to a land; after a place name it names a person of that place, as {Shuah gammi}, the Shuhite) (s:khuami/tualsuak) (a:peemta/gamdangmi/khualmi) (b:gam) (q:draft)
gammite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:people of the land/subjects/citizens) (d:<gammi> with plural <te>, the people who belong to a land or to a ruler) (s:khuamite) (a:khualmite) (b:gammi) (q:draft)
gammong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:end of the land/border/frontier) (d:<gam>, land, with <mong>, end: the farthest part of a country) (s:gamgi) (q:draft)
gammongah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in a remote area/at the end of the land) (d:<gammong>, the farthest part of a land, with the place marker <ah>) (b:gammong) (q:draft)
gamnawl = (t:see) <gamnawl-ah>
gamnawl-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the border/at the edge of the land) (d:<gamnawl>, the border or edge of a land, with the place marker <ah>) (q:draft)
gamneu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:province) (d:<gam> land with <neu> small: one of the smaller lands that make up an empire) (q:draft)
gamneute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:provinces) (d:<gamneu>, province, with the plural <te>) (b:gamneu) (q:draft)
gamnin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:unclean land/polluted land) (d:<gam>, land, with <nin>, unclean) (q:draft)
gamnuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pleasant land/good land) (d:<gam> land with <nuam> pleasant) (s:gamhoih) (a:gamsia) (q:draft)
gampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wilderness/deserted place/lonely place) (d:uninhabited country; in the verses always as {gampa lakah}, in or into the wilderness) (s:gampalak/gamdaihna) (q:draft)
gampalak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wilderness/desert) (d:<gampa>, uninhabited country, written together with <lak>, among: the wilderness) (s:gampa/sehnel) (q:draft)
gampalakah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the wilderness/in the desert) (d:<gampalak>, wilderness, with the place marker <ah>) (b:gampalak) (q:draft)
Gampalakah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the wilderness) (d:<gampalak> wilderness with the marker <ah>, written with a capital) (b:gampalakah) (q:draft)
gampan = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:from the land) (d:<gam>, land, with <pan>, from: from the land or region of a named place) (q:draft, low confidence)
gampi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boundary/border/edge of territory) (d:the limit of a land; the other Bible text has <gamgi> in the same verse) (s:gamgi/gammong) (b:gam) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamsa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:beast) (s:sahang) (a:innsa) (r:26.14.15)
gamsa = (i:2) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wildlife)
gamsa = (i:3) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild animal) (d:<gam>, wild country, with <sa>, animal: an animal that lives in the wild, set against <innsa>, an animal kept at the house) (a:innsa)
gamsai = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wormwood/bitter herb) (d:a bitter plant; {gamsai tawh vak}, feed with wormwood, is a picture of bitter suffering; also the name of the star Wormwood in Revelation) (q:draft)
Gamsai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:star) (w:Wormwood) (d:<gamsai>, wormwood, written with a capital as the name of the star that makes the waters bitter) (b:gamsai) (q:draft)
gamsate = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild animals/beasts) (d:<gamsa>, wild animal, with the plural <te>) (s:sahangte) (a:innsate) (b:gamsa) (r:18.37.8) (q:draft)
gamsia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wasteland/desolate land) (d:<gam>, land, with <sia>, bad or ruined) (s:gamkhing/gamsimtham/gamlakpi) (a:gamnuam/gamhoih) (q:draft)
gamsial = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:<gam>, wild country, with <sial>, the mithun: a strong wild ox, in older English Bibles the unicorn) (s:gambawngtal/zangsial/gam-bawngtal) (q:draft)
gamsialno = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young wild ox) (d:<gamsial> wild ox with <no>, young) (b:gamsial) (q:draft)
gamsialte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild oxen) (d:<gamsial>, wild ox, with the plural <te>) (b:gamsial) (q:draft)
gamsimtham = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wasteland/desolate land) (d:<gam> land with <simtham> desolate: a land left empty with no one living in it) (s:gamkhing/gamsia/gamlakpi) (q:draft)
gamsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:land) (d:<gam>, land, with <sung>, inside: a land or country as an area, often after its name) (s:gam) (r:19.105.33)
gamsung = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:wild) (d:of the open country, said of animals and plants that live or grow wild and of a man who lives outdoors)
gamsunga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the land/in the country) (d:<gamsung>, the inside of <a> land, with the ending a that links it to the words that follow: in the land of, that is in the land) (b:gamsung) (q:draft)
gamsungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the land/into the land) (d:<gamsung> with the place marker <ah>; follows the name of the land) (b:gamsung) (q:draft)
gamta = (i:1) (t:n) (w:motion)
gamta = (i:2) (t:v) (w:act/do/behave/conduct oneself) (d:act or conduct oneself in a certain way; the word before it says how, as in {a manin gamta}, do what is right, and {a sia gamta}, do evil)
gamtaang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:move)
gamtaang = (i:2) (t:v) (w:stir)
gamtaang = (i:3) (t:v) (w:be active)
gamtakha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:act/do/happen to do) (d:<gamta>, act, with <kha>, which shows the act is fallen into or happens to be done; with <kei>, do not act so) (q:draft)
gamtakhial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do wrong/act wrongly) (d:<gamta>, act, with <khial>, err) (q:draft)
gamtakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:act again/do again) (d:<gamta>, act, with <kik>, again or back: go back to a way of acting, whether evil or good) (s:hihkik) (b:gamta) (q:draft)
gamtalai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still act/go on acting) (d:<gamta>, act, with <lai>, still) (q:draft)
gamtang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:moving)
gamtang = (i:2) (t:n) (w:movement)
