Gibeath-haaraloth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gibeath Haaraloth) (d:place near Gilgal where Joshua circumcised the Israelites; the name means hill of the foreskins) (q:draft)
Gibeon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Gibeon) (d:Hivite city north-west of Jerusalem whose people made a treaty with Joshua, later a town of Benjamin given to the Levites) (r:6.9.17/13.9.35)
Giddalti = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Giddalti) (d:son of Heman, a temple musician in the time of David) (r:13.25.4)
Giddel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Giddel) (d:name of two men whose descendants returned from the exile, one among the temple servants and one among the servants of Solomon) (r:15.2.47/15.2.56)
Gideon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gideon) (d:son of Joash of the tribe of Manasseh, the judge who defeated the Midianites with three hundred men; also called Jerub-Baal) (r:7.6.36) (q:draft)
Gideoni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gideoni) (d:father of Abidan, the leader of the tribe of Benjamin in the wilderness) (r:4.1.11/4.10.24)
Gidom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gidom) (d:place in Benjamin as far as which the Israelites pursued the fleeing Benjamites) (r:7.20.45)
gige = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:continually/steadily/always) (d:after a verb, of a state that goes on without a break, as watching, waiting or remaining) (s:den/niloh/ngitnget) (q:draft)
gih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:heavy) (d:form of <gik>, heavy, used before <ciangin> and <na>: {a gih ciangin} is when it grew heavy) (q:draft)
gihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weight/heaviness) (d:<gih>, heavy, with the noun suffix <na>: how much something weighs) (s:gikzah) (b:gih) (r:18.26.8) (q:draft)
Gihon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Gihon) (d:one of the four rivers of Eden, flowing around the land of Cush; also the spring beside Jerusalem where Solomon was made king) (r:1.2.13)
gikin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:weighing/heavy/heavily) (d:<gik>, heavy, with the ending {-in}: after an amount, weighing that much; {a gikin bawl} means make heavy) (b:gik) (q:draft)
