gikpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very heavy/heavy) (d:<gik>, heavy, with <pi>, great; {van gikpi} is a heavy burden) (s:giklua) (b:gik) (q:draft)
giksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make heavy/make heavier) (d:<gik>, heavy, with the causative <sak>: make a load or yoke heavy) (a:zangsak) (b:gik) (q:draft)
gikzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weight) (d:<gik>, heavy, with <zah>, amount: how much something weighs) (s:gihna) (q:draft)
gikzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:heavier) (d:<gik>, heavy, with the comparative <zaw>; the thing compared takes <sangin>, than) (a:zangzaw) (b:gik) (q:draft)
gil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:belly/stomach/womb) (d:the belly or stomach, and also the womb; {gil sungah} is inside the belly, and {gil kial} is be hungry) (s:gilsung)
Gilalai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gilalai) (d:Levite musician who took part in the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem under Nehemiah) (r:16.12.36)
Gilboa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Gilboa) (d:mountain ridge at the edge of the Jezreel valley where Saul and his sons died in battle with the Philistines) (r:9.31.1/13.10.1)
gilead = (t:see) <Ramoth-gilead>
Gilead = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gilead) (d:hill country east of the Jordan settled by Gad, Reuben and half of Manasseh; also the name of a grandson of Manasseh) (r:10.17.26/5.3.15)
Gileah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gilead) (d:spelling of Gilead in some verses, the hill country east of the Jordan and the home of Elijah) (r:11.17.1/33.7.14)
Gilgal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gilgal) (d:place near Jericho where Israel first camped after crossing the Jordan and where Joshua set up twelve stones) (r:6.4.20/6.10.43)
