gilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:evil/wicked/bad) (d:morally bad, wicked or cruel; follows its noun, as in {mi gilo}, a wicked person, and {kha gilo}, an evil spirit) (s:gitloh) (a:hoih/gi) (q:draft)
Gilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:lawless/wicked/evil) (d:<gilo> written with a capital, at the start of a sentence or in the title {Gilo Mi}, the lawless one) (b:gilo) (r:53.2.3) (q:draft)
Gilo = (i:2) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Giloh) (d:town in the hill country of Judah, home of David's counsellor Ahithophel, also written <Giloh>; {Gilo khuami} is the Gilonite) (r:10.23.34/10.15.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Giloh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Giloh) (d:town in the hill country of Judah, home of David's counsellor Ahithophel) (r:6.15.51/10.15.12)
gilohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wickedness/evil) (d:<gilo>, wicked, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:gitlohna/hoihlohna) (a:thumanna) (q:draft)
