Gilopa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the evil one/the lawless one) (d:<gilo>, evil, with {-pa} marking a male person, written with a capital as a title: Satan, or the man of lawlessness who is to be revealed; used as {A Gilopa}) (b:gilopa) (r:53.2.9) (q:draft)
gilopente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the most ruthless/the most wicked) (d:<gilo>, wicked, with <pen>, most, and the plural <te>) (q:draft)
gilote = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wicked/evil) (d:plural form placed after a noun, as in {mi gilote} the wicked and {dawi gilote} evil spirits) (a:hoihte) (b:gilo) (r:44.19.15) (q:draft)
Gilote = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wicked/evil) (d:<gilote> written with a capital in a title; {Numei Gilote}, wicked women, stands for the prostitutes of the English text) (b:gilote) (q:draft)
gilpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:belly/stomach) (d:<gil>, belly, with <pi>, great: the belly or stomach, and the inner organs of an animal) (s:gil) (b:gil)
