giltohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil way/wickedness) (d:paired in the verse with {gamtat khialhnate}, wrong deeds, as what the people must turn from) (s:gitlohna) (q:draft, low confidence)
gilvah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be full/be satisfied/be well fed) (d:have eaten enough, the opposite of <gilkial> be hungry) (s:vah) (a:gilkial) (r:20.27.7) (q:draft)
gilvahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be full/be satisfied) (d:form of <gilvah>, have eaten enough, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:gilvah) (q:draft)
gilvahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:satisfaction/fullness) (d:<gilvah> be full with food with the noun suffix <na>: having eaten enough) (a:gilkialna) (b:gilvah) (q:draft)
gilvahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:satisfy/fill/feed) (d:<gilvah>, be full with food, with the causative <sak>) (a:gilkialsak) (b:gilvah) (q:draft)
gilvahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the full/those who are well fed) (d:<gilvah> be full with plural <te>, the opposite of <gilkialte>, the hungry) (a:gilkialte) (b:gilvah) (q:draft)
gimbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:mistreat/oppress/ill-treat) (d:<gim>, suffer, with <bawl>, do or make: make someone suffer) (s:bawlsia/nengniam/gawt) (b:gim) (q:draft)
gimbawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:oppress/treat harshly) (d:form of <gimbawl>, <gim> suffering with <bawl> do, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:gimbawl) (q:draft)
gimhun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:time of trouble/time of suffering) (d:<gim>, suffering, with <hun>, time) (q:draft)
gimin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be weary/be tired/be exhausted) (d:<gim> with the linking suffix <in>) (b:gim) (q:draft)
