hailuat = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very foolish/too foolish) (d:form of <hailua> used before <man>, because) (b:hailua) (q:draft)
hailuatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great folly/excessive foolishness) (d:<hai> foolish with <luat>, form of <lua> too much, and the noun ending <na>) (b:hailuat) (q:draft)
haina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:folly/foolishness) (d:The state of being foolish, or a foolish act; <hai>, foolish, with the noun ending <na>.) (s:haitatna/haihuaina/pillohna) (a:pilna) (b:hai) (q:draft)
hainate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:follies/foolish things) (d:<haina>, foolishness, with the plural <te>; {thu kidong hainate}, foolish questions or controversies) (b:haina) (q:draft)
haipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fool/foolish man/madman) (d:<hai> foolish with <pa>, marking a man) (s:mihaipa/mihai) (a:mipilpa) (b:hai) (q:draft)
haipa = (i:2) (t:n) (w:glutton/drunkard) (d:in {an hai zu haipa}, a man greedy for food and for wine; this <hai> is to crave food or drink) (s:zuhai) (q:draft, low confidence)
haipau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak foolishly/talk nonsense/play the fool) (d:<hai> foolish with <pau> speak) (q:draft)
haipaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foolish talkers/chattering fools/babblers) (d:<hai> foolish with <pau> speak and <te>, those who: people who talk foolishly or too much) (b:haipau) (q:draft)
haipi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:goblet/large cup/bowl) (d:<hai>, cup, with <pi>, big; in the verses the cup of God's wrath) (b:hai) (q:draft)
haipite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bowls/basins/dishes) (d:<hai> cup or bowl with <pi> large and the plural <te>) (b:haipi) (q:draft)
haisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make foolish/drive mad/make senseless) (d:<hai>, foolish or mad, with the causative <sak>) (s:haitatsak) (b:hai) (q:draft)
haisapi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:as a fool) (d:<hai> foolish with <sa> and <pi>; {ka haisapi mahin}, even as the fool I am taken to be) (q:draft, low confidence)
haitat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:act foolishly/behave like a fool) (d:<hai>, foolish, with <tat>, act; {a haitat ngei} is the foolish thing done before) (q:draft)
haitatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:acting foolishly/foolish) (d:<haitat>, act foolishly, with the linking ending <in>) (b:haitat) (q:draft)
haitatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:folly/foolishness/foolish behaviour) (d:Foolish behaviour or madness; <haitat>, act foolishly, with the noun ending <na>.) (s:haina/haihuaina) (a:pilna) (b:haitat) (q:draft)
haitatnasate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foolish deeds/follies) (d:<haitatna> foolish behaviour with <sa>, already done, and plural <te>: the foolish things someone has done; the English has detestable practices here) (q:draft)
haitatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make foolish/cause to act foolishly) (d:<haitat>, act foolishly, with the causative <sak>) (s:haisak) (b:haitat) (q:draft)
haite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cups/bowls/goblets) (d:Plural of <hai>, cup or bowl: drinking cups, and the bowls used in the temple.) (b:hai) (q:draft)
haite = (i:2) (t:n) (w:fools/the foolish) (d:<hai> foolish with plural <te>, foolish people; {numei haite}, foolish women) (s:mihaite) (a:mipilte/pilte) (b:hai) (q:draft)
haivai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:foolish/senseless/meaningless/absurd) (d:<hai> foolish with <vai> affair: of a foolish kind, making no sense) (s:haihuai) (q:draft)
haizan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:chew/eat solid food) (d:of food, to chew it and get it down; {haizan zo lo} is not yet able to take solid food; how the word is built is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
hak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:slow/hard/difficult) (d:Placed after a verb: slow or hard to do, as in {heh hak}, slow to anger, {tel hak}, hard to understand, and {pai hak}, slow in coming.) (s:haksa) (a:baih) (r:19.103.8) (q:draft)
hak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:open/be open) (d:Of the eyes, to open or be open; {mit hak} is to open the eyes, and of God to look with attention.) (a:mitsi) (q:draft)
Hakaliah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakaliah) (d:father of Nehemiah) (r:16.1.1/16.10.1)
Hakhilah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Hakilah) (d:hill in the Desert of Ziph facing Jeshimon, where David hid from Saul) (r:9.26.1/9.23.19)
hakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be open/open) (d:<hak>, of the eyes be open, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:hak) (q:draft)
hakin = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:slow/hard/dull) (d:<hak> slow or hard to do with the linking suffix <in>; {theih hakin}, being slow to understand) (b:hak) (q:draft)
Hakkatan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakkatan) (d:father of Johanan, the head of the family of Azgad who returned from Babylon with Ezra) (r:15.8.12)
Hakkefirim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hakkefirim) (d:place on the plain of Ono where Sanballat and Geshem asked Nehemiah to meet them; the NIV translates the name as one of the villages) (r:16.6.2)
Hakkofirim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hakkofirim) (d:spelling of <Hakkefirim> in Nehemiah 6:2, a place on the plain of Ono where Sanballat and Geshem asked Nehemiah to meet them) (r:16.6.2)
hakkol = (i:1) (t:n) (w:yoke) (d:The wooden bar laid on the neck of a working animal; also a picture of servitude under a ruler.) (s:kol) (q:draft)
hakkolte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:yokes) (d:Plural of <hakkol>, yoke; breaking the yokes is a picture of setting people free from slavery.) (s:kolte) (b:hakkol) (q:draft)
Hakkoz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakkoz) (d:priest whose family received the seventh priestly division in the time of David; also the grandfather of Meremoth who repaired part of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.3.21/13.24.10)
Hakmoni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakmoni) (d:father of Jehiel who cared for the sons of King David; Jashobeam, chief of David’s mighty warriors, is called a Hakmonite) (r:13.27.32/13.11.11)
hakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:delay/lateness/slowness) (d:<hak> slow with the noun suffix <na>; being slow or late in doing something, placed after the verb) (b:hak) (q:draft)
haknaw = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lead) (d:the heavy soft metal) (q:draft)
haknawte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lead) (d:<haknaw> lead with plural <te>, closing a list of metals) (b:haknaw) (q:draft)
haksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:open/cause to open) (d:<hak>, of the eyes be open, with the causative <sak>: open someone's eyes) (b:hak) (q:draft)
haksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trouble/hardship/harm) (d:noun built on <haksa> hard; a hardship or trouble that one meets) (s:haksatna/lungkhamna) (a:nopna/nopsakna) (q:draft)
haksalua = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:too hard/too difficult) (d:<haksa> hard with <lua>, too much) (b:haksa) (q:draft)
haksapi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very hard/very difficult) (d:<haksa> with <pi>, great; {haksapi-in} and {haksapi-a} mean with great difficulty, by hard toil) (b:haksa) (q:draft)
haksapipi = (t:see) <haksapipi-in>
haksapipi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:with great difficulty/hardly) (d:<haksa>, hard, with <pipi>, very great, and the adverb marker <in>) (q:draft)
haksasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make hard/make bitter/embitter) (d:<haksa> hard with the causative <sak>) (b:haksa) (q:draft)
haksat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trouble/distress/hardship) (d:form of <haksa> used before a noun, as in {haksat hun}, time of trouble) (b:haksa) (q:draft)
haksate = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:hard/difficult/harsh) (d:<haksa>, hard, with plural {-te}, placed after a plural noun: {thudotna haksate}, hard questions) (b:haksa) (r:11.12.4) (q:draft)
haksatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trouble/hardship/difficulty/distress) (d:Trouble or hardship that a person goes through; <haksat>, a form of <haksa>, hard, with the noun ending <na>.) (s:lungkhamna/gentheihna/haksakna) (a:nopna/nopsakna) (q:draft)
haksatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:troubles/hardships/difficulties) (d:plural of <haksatna>) (s:lungkhamnate/cihmawhnate) (a:nopnate) (b:haksatna) (r:55.4.5) (q:draft)
haksazaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:harder/more difficult/worse) (d:<haksa>, hard, with <zaw>, more; used after <sangin>, than) (a:olzaw/baihzaw) (b:haksa) (r:42.10.14) (q:draft)
haktawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wake up/come awake) (d:probably <hak>, be awake or open the eyes, with <tawm>, of oneself; {a haktawm bangin}, as if waking up) (q:draft, low confidence)
hakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hard things/secrets/mysteries) (d:<hak> hard to do with plural <te>; {thu theih hakte}, the things that are hard to know, are the secrets or mysteries) (s:thusimte/thuthukte) (b:hak) (q:draft)
Hakufa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakupha) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.51/16.7.53)
hakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (d:probably <hak>, open the eyes, with <zo>, be able: be able to keep the eyes open; the NIV has their eyes fail) (b:hak) (q:draft, low confidence)
hal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn) (d:Burn something with fire, such as an offering, incense, a house or a town.) (a:phelh/sumit) (q:draft)
Halah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Halah) (d:region of Assyria where the king of Assyria settled the exiled Israelites) (r:12.18.11/12.17.6)
Halak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Halak) (d:mountain rising toward Seir that marked the southern limit of Joshua’s conquests) (r:6.11.17)
Halek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Helek) (d:son of Gilead and descendant of Manasseh, ancestor of the Helekite clan) (r:6.17.2)
Halhul = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Halhul) (d:town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.58)
Hali = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hali) (d:a town in the territory of Asher) (q:draft)
halin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burning/setting on fire) (d:<hal> burn with the linking ending <in>, used when another action follows in the same sentence) (b:hal) (r:11.11.8) (q:draft)
halkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn together/burn along with) (d:<hal>, burn, with <khawm>, together) (b:hal) (q:draft)
hallam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn) (d:<hal> burn with <lam>, the fact that: that someone burns something) (q:draft)
Hallelujah = (i:1) (t:intj) (w:Hallelujah) praise the Lord
Hallelujah = (i:2) (t:n) (w:Praise the Lord)
Hallohesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hallohesh) (d:father of Shallum, the ruler of a half-district of Jerusalem who repaired the wall; also a leader who sealed the covenant under Nehemiah) (r:16.3.12/16.10.24)
hallum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn to death) (d:<hal>, burn, with <lum>, to death) (s:kanglum/katlup) (q:draft)
hallup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn/burn to death/burn up) (d:Burn a person in fire as an offering; probably the form of <hallum>, burn to death, used before <nading>.) (q:draft)
hallupna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:burning) (d:<hallup>, burn in fire, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:hallup) (q:draft)
halna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:burning) (d:the act or place of burning, mostly in {paknamtui halna} the burning of incense) (s:meihalna) (b:hal) (q:draft)
halnelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn down over/burn upon) (d:<hal> burn with <nelh>, over or upon: burn something down on top of someone) (q:draft)
Halohesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hallohesh) (d:spelling of <Hallohesh> in Nehemiah 10:24, a leader who sealed the covenant under Nehemiah) (r:16.10.24)
halpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who burns/burner) (d:<hal> burn with <pa>, the man who does it) (b:hal) (q:draft)
halsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn/burn down/set on fire) (d:<hal> burn with <sak>; {mei tawh halsak}, burn with fire) (b:hal) (q:draft)
halte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who burn) (d:<hal> burn with <te>, the ones who; in the verse those who burned incense) (b:hal) (q:draft)
haltui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:melt/smelt) (d:<hal>, burn, with <tui>, liquid: melt metal by fire) (s:tuisak/suangtui) (q:draft)
haltuina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:smelting/melting) (d:<haltui>, melt by fire, from <hal> burn and <tui> liquid, with the noun ending <na>; {sik haltuina meikhuk} is an iron-smelting furnace) (b:haltui) (q:draft)
haltum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn up/burn down/consume) (d:destroy completely by fire) (s:kangtum/kattum) (r:19.83.14) (q:draft)
haltumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burning up/setting on fire) (d:<haltum>, burn up, with the linking ending <in>) (b:haltum) (q:draft)
haltumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:burning down/destruction by fire) (d:<haltum>, burn up, with the noun suffix <na>; {haltumna thuak} is be burned down) (b:haltum) (q:draft)
haltumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn down/have burned up/destroy by fire) (d:<haltum> burn up with the causative <sak>) (b:haltum) (q:draft)
halungvei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:charging/ranging/raging) (d:said of a bear, set beside a hungry lion: on the prowl or ready to attack; the exact sense and the parts of the word are not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
ham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bray/bellow/low/cry) (d:of an animal or bird, utter its cry) (q:draft)
ham = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:old/aged/elder) (d:advanced in age; {a moi a ham} means young and old) (s:teek/khangham) (a:moi/khangno) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ham) (d:second son of Noah, father of Cush, Egypt, Put and Canaan; the land of Ham is a name for Egypt) (r:1.6.10)
Haman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haman) (d:son of Hammedatha the Agagite, chief official of King Xerxes, who plotted to destroy the Jews) (r:17.7.1) (q:draft)
Hamath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hamathites/Hamath) (d:city and kingdom on the Orontes in Syria, north of Israel; its people, the Hamathites, descended from Canaan) (r:13.1.16)
Hamathzobah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hamath Zobah) (d:city or region north of Israel that Solomon captured) (r:14.8.3)
hamciam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:try/strive/make an effort) (d:the same meaning as <hanciam>, and probably another spelling of it) (s:hanciam/hahkat) (q:draft)
Hamgam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ham) (d:place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Zuzites; <Ham> with <gam>, land) (r:1.14.5)
hamham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cry/chatter) (d:<ham>, of a bird utter its cry, doubled for a repeated or continued sound) (q:draft)
hamin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:old) (d:<ham>, old, with the suffix {-in}; found in the set phrase {a moi a hamin}, young and old alike) (b:ham) (q:draft)
Hammath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hammath) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.35)
Hammeda = (t:see) <Hammeda-tha>
Hammeda-tha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hammedatha) (d:father of Haman, of the Agagites) (r:17.3.1) (q:draft)
Hammedatha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hammedatha) (d:father of Haman the Agagite, the enemy of the Jews in the book of Esther) (r:17.3.10/17.9.24)
Hammolekheth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hammoleketh) (d:sister of Gilead in the tribe of Manasseh, mother of Ishhod, Abiezer and Mahlah) (r:13.7.18)
Hammon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hammon) (d:name of two towns, one on the border of the tribe of Asher and one in Naphtali given to the Levites) (r:13.6.76/6.19.28)
Hammothdor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hammoth Dor) (d:town in the territory of Naphtali given to the Levites) (r:6.21.32)
Hammuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hammuel) (d:son of Mishma, a descendant of Simeon) (r:13.4.26)
hamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bleating/lowing/neighing/cry) (d:the cry of an animal, such as the bleating of sheep, the lowing of cattle or the neighing of horses; <ham>, cry, with the noun ending <na>) (b:ham) (q:draft)
Hamnath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hammath) (d:spelling of <Hammath> in Joshua 19:35, a fortified town of the tribe of Naphtali) (r:6.19.35)
Hamor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hamor) (d:Hivite ruler, father of Shechem, from whose sons Jacob bought a piece of land) (r:1.34.6/1.34.18)
hampen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:oldest/eldest) (d:<ham>, old, with <pen>, most: the oldest of a group, set against <moipen>, the youngest) (s:upen/upapen/teekpen) (a:moipen/neupen/khangnopen) (b:ham) (q:draft)
hampha = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fortunate/blessed/happy) (d:having good fortune or blessing; {mi hampha} is a fortunate or blessed person, and <hampha kisa> is to count oneself fortunate) (s:lungdamhuai) (a:kamsia/tuahsia) (r:21.4.2/11.10.8) (q:draft)
hamphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:benefit/gain/have an advantage) (d:form of <hampha> used before <nading> and <zawkna>; <hamphat nading> means for the benefit of someone, and {hamphat zawkna} is the advantage one has over another) (s:phattuam) (b:hampha) (q:draft)
hamphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:advantage/benefit/right/privilege) (d:<hamphat> with the noun ending <na>: an advantage or benefit that falls to someone, or a right that is due to them) (s:phattuamna/noptuamna/meetna) (a:supna) (b:hamphat) (q:draft)
hamphatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rights/privileges/benefits) (d:plural of <hamphatna>: the rights or benefits that someone is entitled to or receives) (s:phattuamnate) (b:hamphatna) (q:draft)
hamphazaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more fortunate/better off/happier) (d:<hampha>, fortunate, with <zaw>, more: better off or more blessed than another, who is named with <sangin>, than) (b:hampha) (q:draft)
hampheng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hut/booth/shelter) (d:a small rough shelter, as in a field or for livestock) (s:bukno/sawlbuk) (q:draft)
Hamran = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hemdan) (d:son of Dishon, a descendant of Seir the Horite; the NIV writes Hemdan) (r:13.1.41)
hamsia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curse) (d:evil called down on someone, the opposite of <thupha>, blessing; {hamsia ngah} is to be cursed, and {hamsia tawh kiciam} is to swear with a curse) (s:samsia/hamsiatna/samsiatna) (a:Thupha) (q:draft)
hamsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:curse) (d:call down evil on someone; the form of <hamsia> used before endings and other words such as <loin>, <nadingin> and {-in}) (s:haamsiat/phuisam/kosia) (a:thupha) (b:hamsia) (q:draft)
hamsiat = (i:2) (t:n) (w:curse) (d:a curse laid on someone; {hamsiat thuak} means be cursed, be under a curse) (s:hamsiatna/hamsia/samsiatna) (a:Thupha) (b:hamsia) (q:draft)
hamsiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curses) (d:<hamsia>, curse, with the plural <te>) (s:hamsiatnate/samsiatnate/haamsiatnate) (a:thuphate) (b:hamsia) (q:draft)
hamsiatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cursing/curse) (d:<hamsiat>, curse, with the linking ending <in>) (s:samsiatin/phuisamin) (b:hamsiat) (q:draft)
hamsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curse) (d:<hamsiat>, curse, with <na>: a curse or the state of being cursed; {hamsiatna thuak} is be accursed) (s:samsiatna/hamsia/haamsiatna) (a:Thupha) (b:hamsiat) (r:66.22.3) (q:draft)
hamsiatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curses) (d:<hamsiatna>, curse, with the plural <te>) (s:samsiatnate/hamsiate/haamsiatnate) (a:thuphate) (b:hamsiatna) (q:draft)
hamsiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make worse off/put at a disadvantage) (d:probably <hamsia>, unfortunate, with the causative <sak>; the NIV has were you inferior) (q:draft, low confidence)
hamtang = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:deliberately/wilfully/insistently) (d:placed after a verb, shows that the action is done on purpose, with determination or in spite of a warning; with <kei> it makes a firm prohibition) (s:teitei) (q:draft)
hamtang = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:surely/certainly/without fail) (d:placed after a verb, shows that the event is certain to happen) (s:pelmawh/takpi) (q:draft)
hamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cries/calls/cooing) (d:<ham>, of a bird or animal utter its cry, with plural <te>; {vakhu hamte}, the cooing of doves) (b:ham) (q:draft)
hamte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:rough places) (d:in {lei hamte}, the rough or uneven parts of the ground that are to be made smooth) (q:draft, low confidence)
hamu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small coin/small sum of money) (d:a small silver coin or sum of money, perhaps a half as <mat> is a quarter; it stands for the two-drachma temple tax, a day's wage, two pennies and two-thirds of a shekel) (r:9.13.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hamul = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hamul) (d:son of Perez and grandson of Judah, ancestor of the Hamulite clan) (r:13.2.5/4.26.21)
Hamutal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hamutal) (d:daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah, wife of King Josiah and mother of the kings Jehoahaz and Zedekiah) (r:12.23.31/12.24.18)
han = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tomb/grave/sepulchre) (d:the place where a dead person is buried, a tomb or grave; {han sung} is the inside of the tomb and {han kong} its entrance) (s:hankhuk/hanphual/kivuina/dai) (r:42.24.2) (q:draft)
hana = (i:1) (t:n) (w:toothache/aching tooth) (d:<ha> tooth with <na>, pain; the NIV has a broken tooth) (b:ha) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tomb/grave) (d:<han>, tomb, with the place marker <ah>: to the tomb, in the grave) (b:han) (q:draft)
Hanamel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanamel) (d:son of Shallum and cousin of the prophet Jeremiah, who sold Jeremiah his field at Anathoth) (r:24.32.7/24.32.9)
Hanan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanan) (d:name of several men, among them a chief of the tribe of Benjamin and Levites and leaders who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:13.8.23) (q:draft)
Hananel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:tower) (w:Hananel) (d:name borne by a tower on the north wall of Jerusalem, the Tower of Hananel) (r:16.12.39/24.31.38)
Hanani = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanani) (d:name of several men, among them the father of the prophet Jehu, the seer who rebuked King Asa, and a brother of Nehemiah) (r:11.16.1/15.10.20)
Hananiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hananiah) (d:name of many men, among them the false prophet who opposed Jeremiah and the companion of Daniel who was renamed Shadrach) (r:13.3.21/16.10.23)
Hananiahte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hananiah) (d:<Hananiah> with the plural <te>, Hananiah and those with him; here a priest who blew a trumpet at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem) (b:Hananiah) (r:16.12.41)
hanciamciam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep striving/try hard/seek earnestly) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with the last part doubled for effort kept up) (q:draft)
hanciamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:striving/trying hard/making every effort) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with the linking ending <in>: striving, with great effort, while going on to the next action) (b:hanciam) (q:draft)
hanciamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:purpose/plan/scheme/plot) (d:what someone intends and strives to bring about: of God, his purpose or plan; of an enemy, a scheme or plot) (s:ngimna/geelna/tupna) (b:hanciam) (r:49.1.11) (q:draft)
hanciamna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:effort/struggle/striving) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with the noun ending <na>: the act of striving hard, a struggle) (s:hahkatna) (b:hanciam) (q:draft)
hanciamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:efforts/endeavours/intentions) (d:plural of <hanciamna>: things one strives for; in the letters also the purposes or motives of the heart) (s:ngimnate) (b:hanciamna) (r:46.4.5) (q:draft)
hanciampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who strives/one who tries) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with <pa> marking a man: the man who tries to do something) (b:hanciam) (q:draft)
hanciamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make strive/make work hard) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with the causative <sak>) (b:hanciam) (q:draft)
hanciamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who strive/those who seek) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with the plural <te>: people who make an effort for something, used as {a hanciamte} after the thing they seek) (b:hanciam) (q:draft)
hancingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tomb guards/guards) (d:<han>, tomb, with <cing>, guard, and plural <te>: those who guard a tomb) (q:draft)
Hane = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hanes) (d:spelling of <Hanes> in Isaiah 30:4, a town in Egypt to which the envoys of Judah came) (q:draft)
Hanes = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hanes) (d:town in Egypt to which the envoys of Judah came seeking help) (r:23.30.4)
hang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:reason) (d:the reason or cause of something; {bang hang hiam} asks why) (s:ahang)
hang = (i:2) (t:v) (w:complain) of dissatisfaction or annoyance
hang = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:brave/daring/courageous) (d:not afraid in the face of danger; often paired with <thahat>, strong) (s:hangsan) (a:meidawi/lau)
hanga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:because of/for/on account of) (d:<hang>, reason, with <a>, joining it to the noun before; {khialhna hanga biakna} is a sin offering, and <bang hanga> asks why) (b:hang) (r:45.5.15) (q:draft)
hangah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:because of/through/by) (d:placed after a noun to give the reason or the means, like <hangin>) (b:hang) (q:draft)
hangin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:even though/although/though) (d:placed after a verb, shows that what follows happens in spite of it; after a noun the same word means because of)
hanginah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:because of/on account of) (d:<hangin> with the ending {-ah}, placed after a noun to give the reason; {tua thu hanginah} means that is why) (b:hangin) (r:44.26.6) (q:draft)
hanginah = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:although/even though) (d:after a verb: although that was done, what follows is contrary to what might be expected) (s:zongin/napi/hinapi) (b:hangin) (q:draft, low confidence)
hangkeu = (t:see) <hangkeu-in>
hangkeu-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roasted/roasting) (d:<hangkeu>, roast over the fire, with the linking ending <in>: having roasted it; set against meat that is raw or boiled in water) (q:draft)
hangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:brave man/warrior/mighty man) (d:<hang> brave with <pa>, a man; {galkap hangpa} and {gal hangpa} are a valiant warrior) (s:galhangpa/thahatpa/galhang) (b:hang) (q:draft)
hangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make brave/embolden/encourage) (d:<hang>, brave, with the causative <sak>; {lungsim hangsak} means take courage, take heart) (s:thakhauhsak/lungkipsak) (a:lungkiasak/lausak) (b:hang) (q:draft)
hangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking courage/making brave) (d:<hangsak>, make brave, with the linking ending <in>; {na lungsim hangsakin}, taking heart) (b:hangsak) (q:draft)
hangsan = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bravely/dauntlessly/brave/bold) (d:brave and bold; {mi hangsan} is a brave man)
hangsana = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:harshly/fiercely/brazenly) (d:<hangsan>, here harsh or fierce, with <a>, used before a verb; {hangsana kosiate} are those who revile others harshly, the slanderers of the NIV) (b:hangsan) (q:draft, low confidence)
hangsankhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bold/have to be bold) (d:<hangsan>, bold, with <khak>, happen to: come to act boldly or sternly) (q:draft)
hangsante = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fierce/bold) (d:<hangsan>, bold or fierce, with the plural <te>; {gul hangsante}, fierce snakes, the vipers of the NIV) (b:hangsan) (q:draft, low confidence)
hangtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:boldly/fearlessly/bravely) (d:<hang>, brave, with <takin>, which makes an adverb) (a:laukawmin/laukawm) (r:47.3.12) (q:draft)
hangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the brave/mighty ones/warriors) (d:<hang>, brave or strong, with the plural <te>; it follows a noun, as in {galkap hangte}, brave soldiers, and {gal hangte}, warriors) (s:galhangte/thahatte) (q:draft)
hangun = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:because of) (d:<hang>, reason, with the plural ending <un>, placed after a noun when those concerned are several: because of) (b:hang) (q:draft)
hangun = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:although/though) (d:<hang> with the plural ending <un>, placed after a verb when those concerned are several: although they do so, what follows is otherwise) (s:zongin/napi/hinapi) (b:hang) (r:19.49.11) (q:draft)
hanhan = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:fleetingly/swiftly) (d:expressive word after <pai>, go: passing quickly by, as a shadow does) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanhanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:fleetingly/swiftly) (d:<hanhan> with the adverb ending <in>; {pai hanhanin}, passing quickly by like a shadow) (b:hanhan) (q:draft, low confidence)
hankhuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grave/tomb/pit) (d:the pit of a grave, from <han>, grave, and <khuk>, pit) (s:han/hanphual) (r:26.37.13) (q:draft)
Hankhukte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tombs/graves) (d:plural of <hankhuk>, the pit of a grave) (s:hante) (q:draft)
hankuang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:coffin/bier) (d:the box or frame on which a dead body is laid and carried) (q:draft)
hanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:courage/bravery/boldness) (d:<hang>, brave, with the noun ending <na>: courage; {lungsim hanna} is courage of heart, and {hanna bei} is to lose courage) (s:ngamna/kithamuanna) (a:launa/meidawina) (q:draft)
Hannah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hannah) (d:wife of Elkanah and mother of the prophet Samuel) (r:9.1.2/9.1.20)
Hannathon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hannathon) (d:town on the northern border of the territory of Zebulun) (r:6.19.14)
Hanniel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanniel) (d:name of two men: the son of Ephod, leader of Manasseh who helped to divide the land, and a son of Ulla of the tribe of Asher) (r:4.34.23/13.7.39)
Hanok = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanoch/Hanok) (d:name of two men: a son of Midian and grandson of Abraham, and the eldest son of Reuben, ancestor of the Hanokite clan) (r:1.25.4/1.46.9)
hanphual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tomb/grave/burial place) (d:<han> grave with <phual>, place or site) (s:han/hankhuk/kivuina) (q:draft)
hansuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stir up/urge/encourage/exhort) (d:move people to act by words, whether stirring them up to do wrong or urging and encouraging them to do good) (s:hanthawn/hanthot) (q:draft)
hansuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:urging/encouraging/stirring up/inciting) (d:<hansuah> with the linking suffix {-in}; with <zol> it means urge strongly, and it is also used of stirring up a crowd or pressing someone hard) (b:hansuah) (q:draft)
hansuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:exhortation/encouragement/urging) (d:<hansuah>, urge, with the noun ending <na>: words that stir someone up to act or to stand firm) (b:hansuah) (q:draft)
Hansunga = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the grave/in the realm of the dead) (d:<han> grave with <sung> inside and the ending <a>, in or of; written with a capital for the realm of the dead) (q:draft, low confidence)
hante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tombs/graves) (d:<han>, tomb, with the plural <te>) (s:Hankhukte) (b:han) (r:19.49.11) (q:draft)
hanthawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stir up/incite/encourage/urge) (d:move someone to act, whether stirring up to fight or to do wrong, or encouraging in good work) (s:hansuah/hanthot) (a:lungkiasak) (r:14.35.2) (q:draft)
hanthawnin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:encouraging/urging/inciting) (d:<hanthawn>, encourage or stir up, with the linking ending <in>) (b:hanthawn) (q:draft)
hanthot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:urge/encourage/stir up/exhort) (d:push someone on to act, for good or for evil) (s:hanthawn/hansuah) (q:draft)
hanthotna = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strengthened) (b:hanthot)
hanthotnate = (t:see) <hanthotnate-ah>
hanthotnate-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in exhortations/to exhortation) (d:<hanthotna>, exhortation or encouragement, with the plural <te> and <ah>, in or to) (q:draft)
Hanun = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanun) (d:name of several men, chiefly the king of the Ammonites, son of Nahash, who shamed the envoys of David) (r:10.10.1/10.10.4)
hanzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:exploit/brave deed/valour) (d:the way of being brave, with <zia>, manner) (q:draft)
hapaak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:white teeth/teeth) (d:<ha> tooth with <paak>, white) (q:draft, low confidence)
Happizzez = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Happizzez) (d:priest in the time of David to whom the eighteenth lot fell for service in the temple) (r:13.24.15)
Hara = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hara) (d:place in the Assyrian empire to which the king of Assyria exiled the tribes east of the Jordan) (r:13.5.26) (q:draft)
Haradah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Haradah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Mount Shepher and Makheloth) (r:4.33.24/4.33.25)
Haran = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haran) (d:name of two men: the son of Terah, brother of Abram and father of Lot, who died in Ur of the Chaldeans; and a son of Caleb by his concubine Ephah) (r:1.11.28)
Harar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Harar) (d:home of several of the mighty warriors of David, who are called Hararites in the NIV) (r:10.23.33/13.11.35)
Harbona = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harbona) (d:one of the seven eunuchs who served King Xerxes; he pointed out the pole Haman had set up for Mordecai) (r:17.7.9/17.1.10)
Haref = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hareph) (d:descendant of Caleb in the tribe of Judah, founder of Beth Gader) (r:13.2.51)
Harhaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harhaiah) (d:father of Uzziel the goldsmith, who repaired part of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.3.8)
Harhas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harhas) (d:ancestor of Shallum, the husband of the prophet Huldah; called <Hasrah> in 2 Chronicles 34:22) (r:12.22.14)
Harheres = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Mount Heres) (d:place near Aijalon and Shaalbim where the Amorites held out against the Israelites) (r:7.1.35)
Harhur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harhur) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.51/16.7.53)
Harif = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hariph) (d:ancestor of a family that returned from the exile, and a leader of the people who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.19)
Harifa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hatipha) (d:spelling of Hatipha in Nehemiah 7:56, ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:16.7.56)
Harim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harim) (d:name of several men, among them the head of the third division of priests in the time of David and the ancestor of a family that returned from the exile) (r:15.2.32) (q:draft)
Harnefer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harnepher) (d:son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.36)
Harnerfer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harnepher) (d:spelling of Harnepher in 1 Chronicles 7:36, a son of Zophah of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.36)
Harod = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Harod) (d:spring where Gideon and his men camped before the battle with Midian; also the home of Shammah and Elika, two of the mighty warriors of David) (r:7.7.1/10.23.25)
Haroeh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haroeh) (d:descendant of Shobal, the founder of Kiriath Jearim, in the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.52)
Harosheth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Harosheth/Harosheth Haggoyim) (d:town in the north of Canaan where Sisera, the commander of the army of King Jabin, was based; in full Harosheth Haggoyim) (r:7.4.2/7.4.13)
harp = (i:1) (t:n) (w:harp/lyre) (d:stringed instrument, a loanword from English; mostly in {harp lasakna}, the harp as an instrument of music) (r:19.108.2) (q:draft)
harpte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:harps) (d:<harp> with the plural <te>) (b:harp) (q:draft)
Harsha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harsha) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.52/16.7.54)
Harum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harum) (d:father of Aharhel, in the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.8)
Harumaf = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harumaph) (d:father of Jedaiah, who repaired the wall of Jerusalem opposite his own house) (r:16.3.10)
Haruz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haruz) (d:man of Jotbah, father of Meshullemeth and grandfather of King Amon of Judah) (r:12.21.19)
