hatsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who makes strong/giver of strength) (d:<hatsak>, make strong, with <pa> marking a male person) (b:hatsak) (q:draft)
hatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:strong ones/the mighty/champions) (d:<hat>, strong, with the plural <te>: after a noun, the strong ones of that kind; after a verb, those who are quick or good at doing it, as in {a tai hatte}, the fast runners) (s:thahatte) (a:thanemte) (b:hat) (r:30.2.15) (q:draft)
Hattil = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hattil) (d:ancestor of a family of descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.57/16.7.59)
Hattush = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hattush) (d:name of several men, among them a descendant of David who returned from the exile with Ezra, and a priest who returned with Zerubbabel) (r:13.3.22/16.12.2)
hatu = (t:see) <hatu-te>
hatu-te = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fangs) (d:<hatu>, fang, a kind of <ha> tooth, with the plural <te>) (q:draft)
hatute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fangs) (d:<hatu>, fang, a kind of <ha> tooth, with the plural <te>) (q:draft)
hatzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:stronger) (d:<hat>, strong or fast, with <zaw>, more; the thing compared is followed by <sangin>, than) (s:thahatzaw/vanglianzaw) (b:hat) (r:10.13.14) (q:draft)
hatzawpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the stronger one/stronger man) (d:<hatzaw>, stronger, with <pa> marking a man) (b:hatzaw) (q:draft)
hatzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be strong enough/be strong) (d:<hat> strong with <zo>, be able; {a lungsim hatzo nai lote}, those whose mind is not yet strong) (b:hat) (q:draft)
hauh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rich/become rich/grow rich) (d:form of <hau>, be rich, used before words such as <ciang>, <nading>, <nop> and <hangin>) (a:zawn) (b:hau) (r:20.23.4) (q:draft)
hauhlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get rich from/profit by/be enriched) (d:<hauh>, be rich, with <lawh>, as a result: become rich by means of something or someone) (s:kihauhlawh) (q:draft)
