hauhtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to get rich/can become rich) (d:<hauh>, be rich, with <theih>, can; used before <nading>, as in {hauhtheih nading}, in order to be able to get rich) (b:hauh) (q:draft)
hauhtohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:growing rich/gaining of wealth) (d:<hauh>, be rich, with <to>, upward, and the noun suffix <na>: wealth built up step by step) (q:draft, low confidence)
hauin = (i:1) (t:v) (d:in {hu hauin}, said of one who suffers on account of others; the NIV has because of them) (q:draft, low confidence)
haukhin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:already rich) (d:<hau> rich with <khin>, already or completely) (b:hau) (q:draft)
