hawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:corpses/dead bodies) (d:second part of {luang hawmte}, dead bodies; {luang hawm} is a lifeless body, literally an empty body) (s:luanghawmte) (b:hawm) (q:draft)
hawmthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:distribute widely/scatter abroad) (d:<hawm>, share out, with <thang>, spreading far) (q:draft)
hawmthawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:count as too little/be dissatisfied with) (d:in the question {hawmthawh lai na hi hiam}: do you still count it a small thing, is it not enough for you) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawmthawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cherish/care for tenderly/hold dear) (d:of children one has looked after and loved) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawmthawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:counting as too little/not being satisfied with) (d:<hawmthawh> count as too little with the linking ending <in>: as if it were not enough) (b:hawmthawh) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:skin/husk/bark) (d:outer covering of a fruit or of a tree: the skin of a grape, the bark of a fig tree) (q:draft)
haza = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be jealous/envy) (d:feel jealousy or envy toward someone; {a haza Pasian} is a jealous God; with <lo>, not grudge or hold back something) (s:eng/een/aam) (a:deihsak) (q:draft)
Hazael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazael) (d:king of Aram in Damascus who took the throne after Ben-Hadad and oppressed Israel in the days of Jehu and Jehoahaz) (r:12.13.24/12.13.22)
Hazaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazaiah) (d:man of Judah, an ancestor of Maaseiah who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:16.11.5)
Hazaraddar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hazar Addar) (d:place on the southern border of Canaan between Kadesh Barnea and Azmon) (r:4.34.4)
Hazarenan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hazar Enan) (d:place at the north-eastern corner of the promised land, on the border of Damascus) (r:4.34.9/4.34.10)
Hazargaddah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazar-gaddah/Hazar Gaddah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.27)
Hazarmaveth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazarmaveth) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.26)
Hazarshual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazar-shual/Hazar Shual) (d:town in the far south of Judah near Beersheba, allotted to the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.15.28/6.19.3)
Hazarsusah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hazar Susah) (d:town in the south allotted to the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.19.5)
Hazarsusim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hazar Susim) (d:town of the tribe of Simeon, the same place as Hazar Susah) (r:13.4.31)
hazat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be jealous of/envy) (d:form of <haza>, be jealous, used before endings such as <nading> and {uh ciangin}; {hazat nading piangsak} is to stir up jealousy) (b:haza) (r:5.32.16) (q:draft)
hazatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:envy/jealousy) (d:<hazat>, be jealous, with the noun suffix <na>: the feeling of envy or jealousy) (s:enna) (b:hazat) (q:draft)
hazatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be jealous for/be jealous on behalf of) (d:<hazat>, be jealous, with <sak>, here doing it for another person: be jealous for the sake of someone) (b:hazat) (q:draft)
Hazazontamar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazazon-tamar/Hazezon Tamar) (d:place of the Amorites near the Dead Sea, the same as En Gedi) (r:1.14.7/14.20.2)
Hazekiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hezekiah) (d:spelling of Hezekiah in Isaiah 36:4, the king of Judah in the time of Isaiah) (r:23.36.4)
Hazerhattikon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hazer Hattikon) (d:place on the border of Hauran, named on the northern boundary of the land in the vision of Ezekiel) (r:26.47.16)
Hazeroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hazeroth) (d:camping place of Israel in the wilderness after Kibroth Hattaavah, where Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses) (r:4.33.17/4.33.18)
Haziel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haziel) (d:Levite of the clan of Gershon, son of Shimei) (q:draft)
Hazo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hazo) (d:son of Nahor, the brother of Abraham, and Milkah) (r:1.22.22)
Hazor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazor) (d:name of several towns, chiefly the royal Canaanite city in the north whose king Jabin was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.11.1/6.19.36)
Hazorhadattah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hazor-hadattah/Hazor Hadattah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.25)
hazzebaim = (t:see) <Pokereth-hazzebaim>
Hazzelelponi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hazzelelponi) (d:daughter of Etam in the family of Hur of the tribe of Judah, sister of Jezreel, Ishma and Idbash) (r:13.4.3)
Hazzeleponi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hazzelelponi) (d:spelling of Hazzelelponi in one Tedim text, daughter of Etam of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.3)
Heber = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heber) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Beriah and grandson of Asher, and Heber the Kenite, husband of Jael) (r:1.46.17/13.7.32)
Hebron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Hebron) (d:city in the hill country of Judah where Abraham lived and where David first reigned as king; also the name of a son of Kohath and grandson of Levi) (r:1.13.18/6.10.36)
Hebru = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Hebru/Hebrew) (d:a Hebrew, one of the people of Israel, and their language; {Hebru mi} is a Hebrew person and {Hebru pau} the Hebrew language)
Hebrute = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Hebrews) (d:the Hebrews, the people of Israel, as in {Hebrute’ Pasian}, the God of the Hebrews) (b:Hebru) (r:2.9.1/2.5.3)
heek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wring/twist) (d:twist round with force, as the head of a bird at its neck or the neck of an enemy) (q:draft)
heek = (i:2) (t:n) (w:wink) (d:in the compound {mit-heek}, a wink of the eye; {mit-heek pia} is to wink at someone) (s:mitheek) (q:draft, low confidence)
heekcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bind tight/twist tight/grip) (d:<heek>, twist, with <cip>, tightly: wind round and hold fast) (b:heek) (q:draft)
heekgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:twist violently/wrench) (d:<heek>, twist, with <gawp>, violently or thoroughly) (b:heek) (q:draft)
heeksat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wring off/twist off/sever) (d:<heek>, wring, with <sat>, cut: twist right off; in the verse the head is wrung but not severed) (s:heektat) (q:draft)
heektat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wring off/twist off) (d:<heek>, wring, with <tat>, be severed: twist until it comes off) (s:heeksat) (q:draft)
heekte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:accusers/betrayers/those who sue) (d:<heek> with <te>, those who; here <heek> means accuse or hand over, not wring: those who take someone to court, those who betrayed the Righteous One) (s:mawhsakte) (b:heek) (q:draft, low confidence)
heem = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:aside/sideways/indirectly) (d:off the straight line: {a heem lam} is the edge or outer part, {heem pai} is turn aside from the course, {heem gen} is say in a veiled way) (q:draft, low confidence)
heempai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swerve/turn aside) (d:<heem>, aside, with <pai>, go) (s:pial) (q:draft)
heengte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crevices/clefts) (d:plural with <te>; {suangpi heengte} are the clefts in the rocks) (s:kawmte) (q:draft)
Hefer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hepher) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Gilead of the tribe of Manasseh and father of Zelophehad; also a town and district west of the Jordan) (r:4.26.33/4.26.32)
Hefzibah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hephzibah) (d:mother of King Manasseh of Judah, wife of King Hezekiah) (r:12.21.1)
Hegai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hegai) (d:eunuch of King Xerxes who had charge of the women in the palace at Susa) (r:17.2.8/17.2.15)
Heglam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Heglam) (d:in 1 Chronicles 8:7 another name of Gera of the tribe of Benjamin, father of Uzza and Ahihud; the NIV translates the word instead of giving a name) (r:13.8.7)
heh = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:irate)
heh = (i:3) (t:v) (w:irritate/be angry/get angry) (d:be or become angry with someone; {heh kei in} is do not be angry) (s:lungham/thangpai/sinso)
hehbaih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:quick-tempered/hot-tempered/easily angered) (d:<heh>, angry, with <baih>, easy or quick: quick to become angry) (s:lungtom) (a:hehhak/lungduai) (q:draft)
hehgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be furious/rage/pour out wrath) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <gawp>, violently: let anger loose on someone) (s:hehlua/thangpai/lungham) (b:heh) (q:draft)
hehhak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:slow to anger) (d:<heh>, angry, with <hak>, slow or hard: not easily made angry) (s:lungduai) (a:hehbaih/lungtom) (q:draft)
hehhakin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:slow to anger) (d:<hehhak> with the linking ending <in>) (b:hehhak) (q:draft)
hehhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:offensive/provoking anger) (d:<heh> angry with <huai>, causing or worthy of; the NIV has a stumbling block) (q:draft)
Hehiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jehiel) (d:spelling of Jehiel in 1 Chronicles 15:20, a Levite musician who played the lyre before the ark) (r:13.15.20)
hehin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:angrily/in anger) (d:<heh>, be angry, with the linking suffix <in>: being angry, in anger) (s:hehsa-in) (b:heh) (q:draft)
hehkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be angry again) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <kik>, again) (b:heh) (q:draft)
hehlua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be very angry/be furious/rage) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <lua>, too much: be angry beyond measure) (s:hehgawp/thangpai/lungham) (b:heh) (q:draft)
hehluat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be very angry/be furious) (d:form of <hehlua> used before another word, as in {hehluat mahmahna}, great wrath) (b:hehlua) (q:draft)
hehluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wrath/fury/great anger) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <luat>, too much, and the noun suffix <na>: great or fierce anger) (s:thangpaihna/lunghamna/sinsona) (b:hehluat) (q:draft)
hehmai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:angry face/angry look/stern look) (d:<heh>, angry, with <mai>, face) (s:hehmel) (q:draft)
hehmel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:angry look/fierce look) (d:<heh>, angry, with <mel>, appearance; {hehmel a pua} is fierce-looking) (s:hehmai) (q:draft)
hehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:anger/wrath/fury) (d:<heh>, be angry, with the noun suffix <na>: anger, wrath, of people and often of God) (s:thangpaihna/sinsona/lunghamna) (b:heh) (q:draft)
hehnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wrath/anger) (d:plural of <hehna>, here of the outpourings of the wrath of God held in the bowls) (b:hehna) (q:draft)
hehnateng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the anger/full wrath) (d:<hehna>, anger, with <teng>, all: the whole of one’s wrath) (b:hehna) (q:draft)
hehnem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort/console) (d:soothe a person who is sad or in trouble; the form <hehnep> is used before <nading>, <na> and <bangin>) (s:lungnuamsak) (a:dahsak) (q:draft)
hehnemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort/encourage/console) (d:form of <hehnem>, comfort, with the linking suffix <in>: comforting and then going on to the next action) (b:hehnem) (q:draft)
hehnempa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:comforter) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, with <pa>, the man or the one who does it: the one who comforts) (b:hehnem) (q:draft)
hehnemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort/give comfort) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, with the causative <sak>) (b:hehnem) (q:draft)
hehnemta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have comforted/comfort) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, with <ta>, which marks the action as now done) (b:hehnem) (q:draft)
hehnemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:comforters) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, with <te>, those who: people sent to comfort the bereaved) (b:hehnem) (q:draft)
hehnemzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort instead/rather comfort) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, with <zaw>, rather or instead) (b:hehnem) (q:draft)
hehnep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort/console/encourage) (d:form of <hehnem> used before <bangin>, <nading>, <na> and <sawm>) (q:draft)
hehnepna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:comfort/consolation) (d:<hehnep>, comfort, with the noun suffix <na>: comfort given or received) (b:hehnep) (r:18.16.2) (q:draft)
hehnepnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:comforts/consolations) (d:plural of <hehnepna>: comforts, words of comfort) (b:hehnepna) (q:draft)
Hehoahaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jehoahaz) (d:spelling of Jehoahaz in 2 Kings 13:25, king of Israel, son of Jehu and father of Jehoash) (r:12.13.25)
hehpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:angry man) (d:<heh>, angry, with <pa>, a man: a man who is angry; {galkap a hehpa} is an enraged soldier) (b:heh) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have mercy on/pity/have compassion on) (d:feel and show pity or kindness to someone in need; {hong hehpih in}, have mercy on me, is a common prayer) (s:khasiat/lainat) (r:19.103.13) (q:draft)
hehpihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:pitiable/pitiful/wretched) (d:<hehpih>, pity, with <huai>, worthy of: deserving pity, wretched; {hehpihhuai sa} means feel compassion for) (s:khasiathuai) (r:1.41.19) (q:draft)
hehpihhuaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wretchedness/pitiable state) (d:<hehpihhuai>, pitiable, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:hehpihhuai) (q:draft)
hehpihhuaipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:poor man/pitiable man) (d:<hehpihhuai>, pitiable, with <pa>, a man: a man who is to be pitied) (b:hehpihhuai) (q:draft)
hehpihhuaisa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:feel pity/have compassion/take pity) (d:<hehpihhuai>, pitiable, with <sa>, consider: find someone pitiable, be moved with compassion) (s:lainat) (b:hehpihhuai) (q:draft)
hehpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have mercy on/have compassion on/be gracious to) (d:form of <hehpih> with the linking suffix <in>, showing mercy and then doing the next action) (b:hehpih) (q:draft)
hehpihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have compassion again/have mercy again) (d:<hehpih>, have mercy on, with <kik>, again) (b:hehpih) (q:draft)
hehpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grace/mercy/compassion) (d:<hehpih>, have mercy on, with the noun suffix <na>: mercy, compassion, and in the letters the grace of God; {hehpihna thupha} is the blessing of grace) (s:lainatna) (b:hehpih) (q:draft)
Hehpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Favor/grace) (d:<hehpihna>, grace, written with a capital as the name of one of the two staffs of the shepherd in Zechariah) (b:hehpihna) (q:draft)
hehpihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mercies/compassions) (d:plural of <hehpihna>: mercies, acts of compassion) (b:hehpihna) (q:draft)
hehpihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to have mercy on/wish to pity) (d:<hehpih>, have mercy on, with <nop>, the form of <nuam>, want, used before a noun) (q:draft)
hehpihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:merciful one/benefactor) (d:<hehpih>, have mercy on, with <pa> marking a man: the one who shows mercy or kindness) (b:hehpih) (q:draft)
hehpihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have mercy on) (d:<hehpih>, have mercy on, with <sak>; here mercy asked for another person on the behalf of the speaker) (b:hehpih) (q:draft)
hehpihzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to show favour/find favour with) (d:<hehpih>, have mercy on, with <zawh>, the form of <zo>, be able; {nong hehpihzawh a}, if you can show me favour, is a polite opening of a request to a king) (r:17.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehsa = (t:see) <hehsa-in>
hehsa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:angrily/in anger/in a rage) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <sa>, already, and the linking <in>: being angry, in wrath) (s:hehin/hehsapi-in/sinsosa-in) (q:draft)
hehsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:provoke/anger/make angry) (d:<heh>, be angry, with the causative <sak>: make someone angry, provoke; often of provoking God by sin) (s:phin) (a:lungkimsak) (b:heh) (r:11.22.53) (q:draft)
hehsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:provoke/anger/make angry) (d:<hehsak>, make angry, with the linking ending <in>: provoking, and so going on to the next verb) (b:hehsak) (q:draft)
hehsakkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:anger/provoke) (d:<hehsak>, make angry, with <kha>, which marks that the thing came to happen) (q:draft)
hehsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:provocation/provoking) (d:the act of making someone angry, in the verses of provoking God to anger) (s:phinna/hehsuahna) (b:hehsak) (q:draft)
hehsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:offences/provocations) (d:<hehsakna>, making angry, with plural <te>: the things by which others make one angry) (b:hehsakna) (q:draft)
hehsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who anger/those who insult) (d:<hehsak>, make angry, with the plural <te>: the people who do so) (b:hehsak) (q:draft)
hehsapi = (t:see) <hehsapi-in>
hehsapi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in anger/angrily) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <sa>, <pi> and the linking ending <in>: while still in great anger) (s:hehsa-in) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehsuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:provocation/cause of anger) (d:<heh>, anger, with <suah>, bring out, and the noun suffix <na>: what makes someone angry, said of the idol that provokes God) (s:hehsakna) (q:draft)
hehsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be angry/be vexed/be enraged) (d:<heh>, angry, with <suak>, come out or become: break out in anger) (q:draft)
hehtaak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deserving anger/blameworthy) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <taak>, worthy; {hehtaak sa} is to count something worth being angry at, to find fault with it) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are angry) (d:<heh>, angry, with the plural <te>: the people who are angry) (b:heh) (q:draft)
hehtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get angry/be provoked) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <theih>, the form of <thei>, can, used before <nading>; {a hehtheih nadingin bawl} is to act so as to make someone angry) (b:heh) (q:draft)
hehu = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:expressive word after <kising> shake, of a whole town being stirred or in commotion) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehzawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be more angry/be enraged) (d:<heh>, be angry, with <zawk>, the form of <zaw>, more, used before another word) (q:draft, low confidence)
hei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:axe) (d:tool with an iron head for cutting wood) (s:heipi) (r:9.13.20) (q:draft)
hei = (i:2) (t:v) (w:turn/turn aside/pervert) (d:turn something in another direction or over to someone; with <thu> or <thukham>, twist or pervert justice) (q:draft)
hei = (i:3) (t:intj) (w:aha/so) (d:cry of mockery or scorn) (s:ha) (q:draft, low confidence)
heihei = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:to and fro/round about) (d:expressive word after <kikawi>, of a ship being driven this way and that) (q:draft, low confidence)
heikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away/turn aside/pervert/take away) (d:turn something away from its place or right course; of justice, pervert; of the heart, lead astray) (b:hei) (r:11.11.3) (q:draft)
heikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away/pervert) (d:form of <heikhia> used before another word such as <sak>; {thutang heikhiat sak} is to turn justice away from someone) (b:heikhia) (q:draft)
heikhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:perversion/injustice) (d:<heikhiat>, turn away, with the noun suffix <na>; {thuman heikhiatna} is the perverting of justice) (b:heikhiat) (q:draft)
heikhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pervert/turn aside/thwart) (d:cause to turn away from its course: deny or twist justice, bring wisdom to nothing) (b:heikhiat) (q:draft)
heikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn back) (d:<hei>, turn, with <kik>, back; here of the heart turning back to Egypt) (b:hei) (q:draft)
heikikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:turning back) (d:<heikik>, turn back, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:heikik) (q:draft)
heina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rudder/helm) (d:the part a ship is steered with, from <hei> turn) (s:hawhna) (b:hei) (q:draft)
heina = (i:2) (t:n) (d:the place or direction one turns to; {ka heina khempeuh ah}, wherever I turn) (b:hei) (q:draft, low confidence)
heipi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:axe/large axe) (d:<hei>, axe, with <pi>, big) (s:hei) (b:hei) (q:draft)
