hi'ng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:am/I am) (d:<hi>, be, with the first person singular ending <ing> shortened: I am, at the end of a statement) (q:draft)
hia = (i:1) (t:det) (w:that/yonder) (d:points to someone or something away from the speaker; {hia lai-ah} is over there, in contrast with {hih lai-ah}, here) (s:hua) (r:19.36.12) (q:draft)
hial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roll up) (d:roll up, said of a weaver rolling up the finished cloth; <kihial> is be rolled up) (s:zial) (q:draft, low confidence)
hialbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:adjourn/put off/postpone) (d:said of a judge closing a hearing for the time being without giving a decision) (q:draft, low confidence)
hialhial = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:expressive adverb after <omkhawm> or <takhawm> in the picture of twin fawns; paired with <helhel>, it seems to stress being closely together or alike) (s:helhel) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiam = (i:1) (t:part) (d:final particle of an interrogative sentence, collocating with initial particles such as <bang> and <kua>) (r:44.21.22/18.10.4)
hiam = (i:2) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case)
hiamin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sharp) (d:<hiam>, sharp, with the ending <in>; {tat hiamin} and {kitat hiamin} are whet or be whetted until sharp) (a:mawl) (q:draft)
hiamin = (i:2) (t:n) (w:weapon) (d:<hiam>, weapon, with the marker <in>: as a weapon) (s:galhiam) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sharpening) (d:<hiam>, sharp, with the noun suffix <na>; {seek hiamna} is the forging of a tool to make it sharp again) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiamsa = (t:see) <hiamsa-in>
hiamsa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:sharpened/ready sharpened) (d:<hiam> sharp with <sa> already and the ending <in>, in a sharpened state, said of an arrow kept ready for use) (q:draft)
hiamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sharpen) (d:<hiam>, sharp, with <sak>, cause: make sharp) (s:taat) (q:draft)
hiamtawi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:armed) (d:<hiam>, weapon, with <tawi>, carry: bearing weapons; {hiamtawi mite} are the armed men) (q:draft)
hiamtawite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:armed men) (d:<hiamtawi> armed with the plural <te>, those who bear weapons) (b:hiamtawi) (q:draft)
hiamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weapons/arms) (d:plural of <hiam>, weapon: the arms a man carries, such as sword, spear, bow and quiver) (s:galhiamte/galvan) (q:draft)
hiamte = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:sharp) (d:<hiam>, sharp, in the plural after the thing named, as {thaltang hiamte}, sharp arrows, and {namsau hiamte}, sharp swords) (a:mawl) (q:draft)
hiamzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sharper) (d:<hiam>, sharp, with <zaw>, more: sharper, used with <sangin>, than) (q:draft)
hiang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:branch/bough) (d:branch or bough of a tree or vine, also an arm of the lampstand) (s:singhiang) (q:draft)
Hiang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Branch) (d:<hiang>, branch, written with a capital of the promised king from the line of David, the righteous Branch) (s:Sel) (b:hiang) (q:draft)
hiangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the branches/on the branches) (d:<hiang>, branch, with the place marker <ah>: on or in the branches, where birds nest and perch) (b:hiang) (q:draft)
hiangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:plane tree/fir) (d:a kind of tree, used in the Bible for the plane tree and the fir; said with <kung> or <sing>, tree) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiangpha = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:spreading/branching) (d:<hiang>, branch, with <pha>, good or plentiful: having many spreading branches, said of a vine) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:branches/boughs) (d:plural of <hiang>: the branches of a tree or vine) (s:singhiangte) (b:hiang) (q:draft)
hiangteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:branches/all the branches) (d:<hiang>, branch, with <teng>, all of them: all the branches of a tree) (b:hiang) (q:draft)
hiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:calmly/quietly/in peace) (d:after a verb, usually doubled as {hiat-hiat} or <hit-hiat>: in a calm, undisturbed way) (s:hithiat/dide) (q:draft)
hiat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:rub/comb) (d:draw or press something across a surface; {sam hiat} is comb or dress the hair, and in Lamentations 3:16 the face is rubbed on the ground) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiathiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:calmly/quietly/at ease) (d:follows a verb, often of speaking, to show that the action goes on in a calm, even and unhurried way) (s:hithiat/hit-hiat) (a:lualua) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiathiatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:quietly/calmly) (d:<hiathiat> with the adverbial ending <in>; {na sem hiathiatin} is working quietly and steadily) (s:hithiatin) (b:hiathiat) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiau = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb of going, apparently showing that the going is swift and direct, as in {a paikhia hiau hi}, he went straight on his way) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiauhiau = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:gently/softly) (d:expressive word after <nung>, blow: of a wind blowing softly and gently) (s:damtakin) (q:draft, low confidence)
hibek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be only/be merely) (d:<hi>, be, with <bek>, only: is only, is nothing more than) (s:hilel) (q:draft)
hibuang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be after all) (d:<hi> be with the emphatic particle <buang>: whatever else may be said, she is a daughter of a king) (q:draft, low confidence)
hici = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:which is/which means/as in/like this/so) (d:in the Bible text it stands before a verb and points to the manner just seen or spoken of: like this, in this way, so)
Hiddai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hiddai) (d:one of the mighty warriors of David, from the ravines of Gaash) (r:10.23.30)
Hiddekel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Tigris) (d:the third river that flowed out of Eden, running east of Assyria; the Hebrew name of the Tigris) (r:1.2.14)
Hiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hiel) (d:man of Bethel who rebuilt Jericho in the time of King Ahab, at the cost of his sons Abiram and Segub) (q:draft)
Hierapolis = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hierapolis) (d:city in Asia Minor near Laodicea and Colossae, where Epaphras worked) (r:51.4.13)
Hih = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:this/these) (d:<hih>, this, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or of quoted speech) (a:Tua) (b:hih) (r:40.12.23) (q:draft)
HIH = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:this) (d:<hih> written in capitals in the inscription on the cross; {HIH PA} is this man) (q:draft)
hihgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:attack/assault/treat violently) (d:<hih>, do, with <gawp>, roughly or violently: fall upon someone, treat with violence) (s:simgawp) (q:draft)
hihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:doing/by doing) (d:<hih>, do, with the linking ending <in>: doing or by doing, followed by another verb) (b:hih) (q:draft)
hihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to do/do/commit) (d:<hih>, do, with <kha>, which marks an act that happens to be done, by mistake or as something that may come about) (s:gamtakha) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to do/commit/do by mistake) (d:form of <hihkha> used before another word: do something without meaning to; {na hihkhak loh nadingun}, so that you do not come to do it) (s:sepkhak) (b:hihkha) (q:draft)
hihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put forth/stretch out) (d:<hih>, do, with <khiat>, out; {khut hihkhiat} is to put out the hand against someone) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do again/repeat) (d:<hih>, do, with <kik>, again) (s:gamtakik/semkik) (q:draft)
hihkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do completely/do all) (d:<hih>, do, with <kim>, complete: do all of it and leave nothing out) (q:draft)
hihlai = (t:see) <hihlai-ah>
hihlai-ah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:here/in this place) (d:<hih> this with <lai> place and the place marker <ah>; also written {hih lai-ah}) (s:hiah) (a:tuasan) (q:draft)
hihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the fact of being, from <hih> be with <lam>; with <ka>, <na> or <a> before it and <thei> know, <phawk> notice or <um> believe after it, where English says that I am, that you are) (s:hihna) (q:draft)
hihlamtak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (d:<hih>, the form of <hi> be, with <lam> and <tak>: the very fact of being so; {a gelh ka hihlamtak} is that I am indeed one who writes) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihlo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not do) (d:<hih>, do, with the negative <lo> written as one word; {bangmah hihlo} is do nothing) (q:draft)
hihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not do/leave undone) (d:<hih>, do, with <loh>, the form of the negative <lo> used before <nading>, <om> and similar words) (b:hihlo) (q:draft)
hihloh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:not be) (d:<hi>, be, with <loh>: not being, used before <nading> or <hangin>) (s:ahihloh) (q:draft)
hihlohlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the fact of not being or not doing, <hih> with <loh> not and <lam>; with <ka>, <na> or <a> before it and <phawk> notice or <thei> know after it, where English says that I am not, that I was not) (q:draft)
hihlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:not being) (d:<hi>, be, with <loh>, not, and the noun suffix <na>: the fact that someone is not something; {ka hihlohna thu}, that I am not) (s:ahihlohna) (a:hihna) (q:draft)
hihlum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kill/strike down/put to death) (d:<hih>, do, with <lum>, dead: do to death, kill) (s:thatlum) (q:draft)
hihmanun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:because) (d:<hih> with <man> reason and <un>, the plural ending with <in>: because you did or are so; also written {na hih manun} in the same verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be concerned/be anxious/worry) (d:used after <lung> heart, {lung hihmawh}; another spelling of <himawh>) (s:himawh/lunghihmawh) (q:draft)
hihmawhhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:worrying/to be feared) (d:<hihmawh>, be anxious, with <huai>, worthy of; {lung hihmawhhuai hi} is it is a thing to be anxious about) (s:lunghihmawhhuai) (q:draft)
hihna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the fact of being, noun form of <hi> be, used where English says that someone is or will do something, as in {Topa ka hihna} that I am the Lord) (s:hihlam/ahihna) (a:hihlohna) (r:37.2.21) (q:draft)
hihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:deed/doing/action) (d:what someone does, noun form of <hih>, do; {na hihna khempeuh} is all that you do) (s:gamtatna/bawlna) (r:27.9.14/50.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihnasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:what was done/deeds/doings) (d:<hihna>, deed, with <sa>, already done: the things someone has done) (s:gamtatnasa) (b:hihna) (q:draft)
hihnasate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deeds/things done) (d:<hih>, do, with <na>, <sa>, already done, and plural <te>: the things someone has done) (s:gamtatnasate) (b:hihnasa) (q:draft)
hihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deeds/doings/actions) (d:plural of <hihna>; the things someone does or has done) (s:gamtatnate/bawlnate) (b:hihna) (q:draft)
hihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to do/wish to do) (d:<hih>, do, with <nop>, the form of <nuam>, want, used before a noun or <loh>; {na hihnop khempeuh} is all that you want to do) (s:gamtatnop/sepnop) (q:draft)
hihnopte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things one wants to do/wishes) (d:<hihnop>, want to do, with the plural <te>: the things he wants to do) (b:hihnop) (q:draft)
hihnopteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all that one wants to do) (d:<hihnop>, want to do, with <teng>, all of it: everything one wants to do) (b:hihnop) (q:draft)
HIHPA = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:this man/he) (d:<hihpa> written in capitals in the inscription on the cross) (q:draft)
hihpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do quickly/do at once) (d:<hih>, do, with <pak>, at once, used in commands: {hihpak in}, do it without delay) (s:sempah) (q:draft)
hihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be together with) (d:<hih>, the form of <hi> be, with <pih> together with; {sila ka hihpih} is the one who is a servant along with me, my fellow servant) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:had done) (d:<hih>, do, with <sa>, already: what someone has done, placed before the noun it describes or before <khempeuh>, all) (s:bawlnasa)
hihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do for/do to) (d:<hih>, do, with <sak>: do something for or to another person; with <lo>, not let someone act against another) (q:draft)
hihsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deed done for someone/what was done for) (d:<hihsak>, do for, with the noun suffix <na>: what one person has done for another) (b:hihsak) (q:draft)
hihsan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:here/this place) (d:<hih> this with <san> place, used as {hihsan takah}, right here, at this very place) (b:hih) (r:43.6.9) (q:draft)
hihsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deeds/things done) (d:<hihsa> with plural <te>: what someone has done) (s:hihnasate/gamtatnasate) (b:hihsa) (q:draft)
hihtakpi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:really be/truly be) (d:<hih>, be, with <takpi>, truly; {na hihtakpi leh} is if you really are) (q:draft)
hihte = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:these) (s:hite) (a:tuate) (b:hih) (r:1.9.19) plural form of <hih>
Hihte = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:these) (d:<hihte>, these, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or of quoted speech) (b:hihte) (q:draft)
hihthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can do/be able to do) (d:<hih>, do, with <thei>, can) (s:hihzo) (q:draft)
hihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can do/be able to do) (d:form of <hihthei> used before <nading>, <zah> or <leh>; {ka hihtheih zahin}, as much as I can) (s:hihzawh) (b:hihthei) (q:draft)
hihtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ability/power to do/right to do) (d:<hihtheih>, can do, with the noun suffix <na>: what one is able or allowed to do) (s:hihzawhna) (b:hihtheih) (q:draft)
hihzah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:so many/so much/such) (d:<hih>, this, with <zah>, amount: as many or as great as this; {hihzah tak nalamdangte} is miracles as great as these) (s:hizah) (q:draft)
hihzahta = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:so many/this much) (d:<hihzah>, this much, with <ta>: as many as these; {kampau hihzahta} is so many words as these) (s:hizah) (b:hihzah) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do more/do rather) (d:<hih>, do, with <zaw>, more or rather: do more than others, or do one thing rather than another) (s:bawlzaw/semzaw) (q:draft)
hihzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to do/can do) (d:<hih>, do, with <zawh>, the form of <zo>, be able, used before <ding>, <zah> or <nakleh>: what one has the power to do) (s:hihtheih/bawltheih) (q:draft)
hihzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ability/gift) (d:<hihzawh>, be able to do, with the noun suffix <na>: what one is able to do; {Pasian’ piak hihzawhna} is a gift given by God) (s:hihtheihna) (b:hihzawh) (q:draft)
hihzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of doing/doing) (d:<hih>, do, with <zia>, manner: the way someone does a thing) (s:gamtatzia) (q:draft)
hihzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to do/accomplish/manage) (d:<hih>, do, with <zo>, be able: succeed in doing; {hihzo kei} means cannot do) (s:hihthei/semzo/bawlzo) (q:draft)
hikcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grow stiff/freeze/cramp) (d:said of a hand that has grown tired and stiff and stays clenched) (s:khikcip) (q:draft, low confidence)
hikeileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:otherwise/if not/or else) (d:<hi>, be, with <kei>, not, and <leh>, if: if it is not so; usually follows <tua>, that, as <tua hikeileh>, otherwise) (r:5.8.12) (q:draft)
hikha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:may be/turn out to be/happen to be) (d:<hi>, be, with <kha>, which marks what may happen or turn out; {hikha thei} is may well be) (q:draft)
hikhathei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:may be/might be) (d:<hikha>, may be, with <thei>, can: perhaps it is so) (s:hithei) (b:hikha) (q:draft)
hikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be together/be jointly) (d:<hi>, be, with <khawm>, together: be something together with others, or be two things at the same time) (b:hi) (q:draft)
hikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:already be/have become) (d:<hi> be with <khin>, already, marking a state that has been reached) (s:suakkhin) (b:hi) (q:draft)
Hikiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hilkiah) (d:spelling of Hilkiah in some verses; name of several men, among them the father of Eliakim, the palace administrator of King Hezekiah) (r:13.6.13/13.6.45)
hikim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fully/all be) (d:<hi>, be, with <kim>, complete: be so fully, or all be so) (q:draft, low confidence)
hil = (t:see) <sia-hil>
hileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:if/if only) (d:if it were so; closes a conditional clause, if or unless; {tua hileh}, then, in that case; alone after a noun, a wish, if only it were) (s:ahihleh) (r:20.2.9) (q:draft)
hilel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be only/be merely/be just) (d:<hi>, be, with <lel>, only: is nothing more than) (s:hibek) (q:draft)
Hilen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hilen) (d:town in the hill country of Judah given to the descendants of Aaron, called Holon in the book of Joshua) (r:13.6.58)
hileng = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:if I were/if I had) (d:<hi> be with <leng>, the conditional ending for a first person singular subject) (q:draft)
hilha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teach) (d:<hilh> teach with the linking <a> before <kinei>, as {thugen-a kinei} in the same verse: be trying to teach) (b:hilh) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:admonish/warn/instruct) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <bawl>, do: treat someone by instructing or warning him) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhel = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:alongside/parallel) (d:follows <paikhawm> go together, said of a wall that runs along a row of rooms; exact meaning not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhhelh = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:expressive adverb after <dawn> or <dawng>, shoot, picturing young shoots that sprout and spread freely) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhhilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:preach/proclaim/keep teaching) (d:<hilh>, teach, doubled for an action that goes on: keep teaching or preaching) (s:thuhilh/taangko) (q:draft)
hilhhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:that ought to be taught/worthy to be told) (d:<hilh> teach with <huai>, worthy of) (q:draft)
hilhial = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:follows <zol>, said of a healthy, well-fed body, apparently sleek or smooth all over; exact meaning not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teaching/preaching/instructing) (d:<hilh> with the linking ending <in>, used when another verb follows: teaching, and) (s:thuhilhin) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhinah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taught/said in teaching) (d:form of <hilh> teach that closes a clause introducing the words spoken next: he taught them, saying; found in the 1932 text) (b:hilhin) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:proclaim/make known) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <khia>, out: teach or tell out openly) (s:genkhia/taangko) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:proclaim/make known) (d:form of <hilhkhia> used before another word such as <theih>) (s:genkhiat) (b:hilhkhia) (q:draft)
hilhkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:warn/forewarn/tell beforehand) (d:<hilh>, tell, with <khol>, beforehand: tell someone of a danger before it comes) (s:theikholsak) (q:draft)
hilhkhol = (i:2) (t:v) (w:prophesy/testify/foretell) (d:tell a message beforehand, as in {thu hilhkhol}, prophesy; also bear witness against someone) (s:genkhol/kamsang) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:warn/forewarn/tell beforehand) (d:form of <hilhkhol>, tell beforehand, used in dependent clauses and before words such as <bangin>, <nading> and <hangin>) (s:genkholh) (b:hilhkhol) (q:draft)
hilhkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:warning/forewarning) (d:telling of something before it happens; {hilhkholhna lim} is a sign that warns beforehand) (s:thupiakkholhna) (b:hilhkholh) (q:draft)
hilhkholhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:warnings/admonitions) (d:plural of <hilhkholhna>: things taught or told beforehand as a warning) (b:hilhkholhna) (q:draft)
hilhkholhsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:foretold/told beforehand/declared in advance) (d:<hilhkholh> tell beforehand with <sa>, already done) (b:hilhkholh) (r:7.2.15) (q:draft)
hilhkholin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:warning) (d:<hilhkhol>, warn, with the linking suffix <in>, usually before the words spoken) (b:hilhkhol) (q:draft)
hilhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teach again) (d:<hilh> teach with <kik> again) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teaching/instruction/correction) (d:<hilh>, teach, with the noun suffix <na>: what is taught, and also the correction given by a father or teacher) (s:thuhilhna/kihilhna) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhnasa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taught before/preached earlier) (d:<hilh> teach with <na> and <sa> already, placed before a noun of place: where one has taught earlier) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teachings/instructions) (d:plural of <hilhna>: the things that someone teaches) (s:thuhilhnate/kihilhnate) (b:hilhna) (q:draft)
hilhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teacher/instructor/speaker) (d:<hilh>, teach or tell, with {-pa} marking a man: the man who teaches or tells, used as {a hilhpa}) (s:thuhilhpa/siapa) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taught/preached) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <sa>, already done: what has been taught or preached before) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teach/instruct/have someone teach) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <sak>: teach for the good of someone, or cause someone to be taught) (s:sinsak) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:intend to teach/try to teach) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <sawm>, intend or attempt) (q:draft)
hilhsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teach/pass on/teach in turn) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <sawn>, onward: teach to others what one has been taught) (s:gensawn) (q:draft)
hilhsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teach in secret) (d:<hilh> teach with <sim>, secretly) (q:draft)
hilhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teachings/instructions) (d:<hilh>, teach, with plural <te>: the things that someone teaches, as in {kong hilhte}, what I teach you) (s:hilhnate/thuhilhnate) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:teachers/preachers) (d:<hilh>, teach, with plural <te>, used as {a hilhte}: those who teach or preach) (s:thuhilhte/siate) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhtel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:explain/make clear/expound) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <tel>, clear: teach or tell a matter so that the hearer understands) (s:gentel) (q:draft)
hilhtelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:explanation/interpretation) (d:<hilhtel>, explain, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:gentelna) (b:hilhtel) (q:draft)
hilhtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to teach/be able to proclaim) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <theih>, form of <thei>, be able, used before <nading> or <hun>) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
hilhzawhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:teachably) (d:<hilh> teach with <zawh> be able and the ending <in>; {hilhzawhin om lo} is not able to be taught, unteachable, where the NIV has hearts that are hard) (q:draft)
hilhzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have taught/have shown) (d:<hilh>, teach or show, with <zo>, marking an act as carried through) (b:hilh) (q:draft)
Hilkiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hilkiah) (d:name of several men, among them the high priest who found the Book of the Law in the days of King Josiah, and the father of the prophet Jeremiah) (r:13.6.13/13.6.45)
Hillel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hillel) (d:father of Abdon, the judge of Israel from Pirathon) (r:7.12.13/7.12.15)
Hilo = (i:1) (t:part) (w:no/not) (d:<hilo> written with a capital at the start of a reply; {Hilo hi} means no, it is not so) (b:hilo) (q:draft)
hilopi = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:though not so/falsely) (d:<hilo> is not with <pi>; of something that is not so or not rightly so, often as {hilopi-in}, although it is not) (b:hilo) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are not/things that are not) (d:<hi> be with <lo> not and the plural <te>, used after <a>: the ones that are not) (b:hilo) (q:draft)
Himah = (i:1) (t:intj) (w:certainly/yes indeed) (d:<hi> be with the emphatic <mah>; {Himah hi} is a reply meaning it is indeed so) (q:draft)
himaw = (i:1) (t:intj) (d:word expressing surprise, joy or sudden emotion)
himawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be anxious/worry/fear) (d:used after <lung> heart, {lung himawh}, be anxious, afraid or in doubt; usually written as one word, <lunghimawh>) (q:draft)
himawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make anxious/cause concern) (d:<himawh> with <sak> cause, used after <lung> heart: {ka lung hong himawhsak}, it troubled me) (b:himawh) (q:draft)
himawk = (i:1) (t:v) (d:<hi> be with <mawk>, in a question of surprise or reproach at something thoughtless: {bang himawk ahi hiam}, what ever is this; exact force not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
Himenaius = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hymenaeus) (d:false teacher at Ephesus whom Paul names with Alexander and with Philetus in his letters to Timothy) (r:54.1.20/55.2.17)
hin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:live/be alive) (d:shortened form of <hing>, written with an apostrophe before another word, as in {ka hin’ lai teng} as long as I live and {hin’na} life) (s:nuntak/nungta) (a:si) (r:45.8.11) (q:draft)
hin = (i:2) (t:n) (w:life/soul) (d:shortened form written with an apostrophe, the living self) (s:hinna/nuntakna) (a:sihna) (q:draft, low confidence)
hinapi = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:although/though/yet) (d:<hi>, be, with <napi>, though: even though being so; mostly written <hinapi-in> after a noun or a clause) (s:napi) (q:draft)
hing = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:alive/living) (d:living, not dead; {a hing lai mite} are those who are still alive) (s:nungta) (a:sisa)
hingim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be in anguish/be troubled) (d:<hin> soul or life with <gim> be weary or troubled, written together; elsewhere {hin’ gim}) (s:lunggim) (q:draft, low confidence)
hingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:alive/living) (d:<hing> alive with the ending {-in}; {a hingin man} is to capture alive) (s:hingtangin) (b:hing) (q:draft)
hingkhawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spare/leave alive/keep alive) (d:let a person live instead of killing, from <hing> alive and <khawi> keep) (s:hinkhawi/nungtasak) (a:that/thatlum) (q:draft)
hingkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:live together/live with) (d:<hing>, live, with <khawm>, together) (s:hinpih) (a:sikhawm/sihkhawm) (b:hing) (q:draft)
hingkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give birth/bring forth/deliver) (d:<hing>, alive, with <khia>, out: bring a child out alive, be delivered of a child; also used as a figure of speech) (b:hing) (q:draft)
hingkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come back to life/rise again/revive) (d:<hing>, alive, with <kik>, again) (s:thokik/hinkik/nungtakik) (a:si) (b:hing) (r:11.17.22) (q:draft)
hingkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:coming back to life/rising again) (d:<hingkik> with the linking ending <in>, used when another verb follows: come back to life, and) (s:thokikin) (b:hingkik) (q:draft)
hingkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise to life/raise/bring back to life) (d:<hingkik>, come back to life, with <sak>, cause: make someone live again) (s:thokiksak/hinkiksak/hingsakkik/nungtasakkik) (a:sisak) (b:hingkik) (r:44.3.15) (q:draft)
hingkiksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raising to life/bringing back to life) (d:<hingkiksak>, raise to life, with the linking ending <in>: having raised to life) (s:hingsakkikin) (b:hingkiksak) (q:draft)
hinglai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:still alive/living/surviving) (d:<hing>, alive, with <lai>, still: {a hinglai mite} are the living, those still alive) (s:ahing/nungta) (a:sisa) (q:draft)
hingmat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take alive/capture alive) (d:<hing>, alive, with <mat>, catch) (q:draft)
hingmatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking alive/capturing alive) (d:<hingmat>, take alive, with the linking ending <in>: having taken alive) (b:hingmat) (q:draft)
hingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make alive/give life/preserve/sustain) (d:<hing>, alive, with <sak>, cause: make someone live or keep someone alive; with <kik>, bring back to life) (s:nuntaksak/hinsak/nungtasak) (a:sisak/that) (b:hing) (q:draft)
hingsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raising to life/making alive) (d:<hingsak> with the linking ending <in>, used when another verb follows: make alive, and) (b:hingsak) (q:draft)
hingsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring back to life/raise again/revive) (d:<hingsak>, make alive, with <kik>, again) (s:hingkiksak/thokiksak/hinkiksak/nungtasakkik) (b:hingsak) (q:draft)
hingsakkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bringing back to life/reviving) (d:<hingsakkik>, bring back to life, with the linking ending <in>) (s:hingkiksakin) (b:hingsakkik) (q:draft)
hingsakthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:life-giving/able to give life) (d:<hingsak> make alive with <thei> can; {mi a hingsakthei} is that which can make people live) (b:hingsak) (q:draft)
hingsuan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rival wife/rival) (d:a second wife taken while the first is living, here the sister of the wife) (s:zipih) (q:draft, low confidence)
hingtangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:alive/while still living) (d:used as {a hingtangin}: in a living state, without first being killed) (s:hingin) (q:draft)
hingtangun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:alive/while still living) (d:in {a hingtangun}, while still alive, said of more than one who is thrown, burnt or swallowed up without first being killed) (s:hingin) (q:draft)
hingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the living/living ones) (d:<hing>, alive, with plural <te>; {a hingte gam} is the land of the living; also said of green, living plants) (a:misite/sisate) (b:hing) (q:draft)
hinin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in life/alive) (d:<hin> live with the ending <in>; {a sih a hinin}, in death and in life) (b:hin) (q:draft)
hinkep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep alive/preserve) (d:<hin>, live, with <kep>, the form of <kem>, keep, used before another word: keep someone alive) (s:hingsak/nuntaksak) (q:draft)
hinkhawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spare/let live/keep alive) (d:<hin>, live, with <khawi>, keep: leave someone alive and not kill him) (s:hingkhawi/nungtasak) (a:that/thatlum) (q:draft)
hinkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:delivery/bringing to birth) (d:<hin>, live, with <khiat>, out, and the noun suffix <na>: the bringing forth of a child alive) (s:nausuahna) (q:draft, low confidence)
hinkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear/give birth to) (d:<hin> live with <khiat> out and <sak>, bring children forth alive for someone) (q:draft, low confidence)
hinkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:live again/come back to life/rise) (d:<hin>, live, with <kik>, again: rise from death) (s:hingkik/thokik/nungtakik) (a:si) (b:hin) (q:draft)
hinkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:resurrection/coming back to life) (d:noun form of <hinkik>, live again) (s:thawhkikna) (a:sihna) (b:hinkik) (q:draft)
hinkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore to life/raise/bring back to life) (d:<hinkik>, come back to life, with the causative <sak>: bring a dead person back to life) (s:hingkiksak/thokiksak/hinsakkik) (a:sihsak) (b:hinkik) (q:draft)
hinkiksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:raising to life/resurrection) (d:<hinkiksak>, restore to life, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of raising someone from death) (s:thawhkiksakna/thawhsakkikna) (b:hinkiksak) (q:draft)
hinlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be still alive) (d:<hin>, live, with <lai>, still: be still alive; {a hinlai} means while someone was still living) (s:nungtalai) (q:draft)
hinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:life/living) (d:noun form of <hin>, live: life, being alive; {sihna le hinna} is death and life, and {a hinna dingun} means so that they may live) (s:nuntakna) (a:sihna) (b:hin) (q:draft)
Hinnom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Hinnom) (d:valley on the south side of Jerusalem, also called the Valley of Ben Hinnom, where children were sacrificed to Molek at Topheth) (r:12.23.10/6.18.16)
hinpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:live with/remain alive with) (d:<hin>, live, with <pih>, together with: go on living with others, remain alive among them) (b:hin) (q:draft)
hinsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let live/make alive/raise up) (d:<hin>, live, with the causative <sak>: let someone live by sparing his life, or give life to the dead) (s:hingsak/nungtasak/nuntaksak) (a:sihsak/that) (b:hin) (q:draft)
hinsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise up/make alive again) (d:<hinsak>, make alive, with <kik>, again: bring back to life, raise the dead) (s:hinkiksak/thokiksak) (b:hinsak) (q:draft)
hinsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:restoring to life/making alive) (d:<hinsak>, make alive, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of bringing the dead to life) (s:hinkiksakna) (b:hinsak) (q:draft)
hinsuahzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep alive/be able to keep alive) (d:<hin>, live, with <suah> and <zo>, be able: manage to bring through alive, as animals in a drought) (q:draft, low confidence)
hintheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can live/be able to live) (d:<hin> live with <theih>, the form of <thei> can used before <nading>: {na hintheih nadingun}, so that you may live) (s:nungtazo) (b:hin) (q:draft)
hintheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:life/power to live) (d:<hintheih>, can live, with the noun suffix <na>: the power to live; {hintheihna hu} is the breath that gives life) (b:hintheih) (q:draft)
hipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one who is/he who is) (d:<hi>, be, with <pa>, a man: {a hipa} is the one who is so, said of a male and often of God) (s:ahipa) (q:draft)
Hirah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hirah) (d:man of Adullam, the friend of Judah) (r:1.38.1/1.38.12)
Hiram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hiram/Huram) (d:name of the king of Tyre who supplied Solomon with timber for the temple, and of the bronze craftsman Solomon brought from Tyre, called Huram in the NIV) (r:11.7.13) (q:draft)
hisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make be/cause to become/let be) (d:<hi>, be, with the causative <sak>: make someone or something be what is named before it, or let it be so) (s:suaksak) (b:hi) (q:draft)
hisuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become/come to be) (d:<hi>, be, with <suak>, become: come to be; {ama a’ hisuak} is become his own) (q:draft)
hisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be down to/reach down to) (d:<hi>, be, with <suk>, downward: said of a boundary that runs down as far as a place) (q:draft, low confidence)
hit = (t:see) <hit-hiat>
Hit = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Hittite/Heth) (d:people of Canaan descended from Heth; used before <mi> or <mite>, {Hit mi} is a Hittite and {Hit mite} are the Hittites) (r:13.11.41) (q:draft)
hit-hiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:still/quietly/calmly) (d:placed after a verb such as <om>, stay, <dai>, be quiet, or <lum>, lie: staying still, quiet and undisturbed) (s:hithiat/hiat/dide) (q:draft)
hit-hit = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:smoothly) (d:expressive word after {tum suk} go down, of wine going down the throat smoothly) (s:hithit) (q:draft, low confidence)
hita = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:whether/or) (d:<hi>, be, with <ta>, followed by <leh> and repeated after each choice: whether it is this or that, be it this or that) (b:hi) (q:draft)
hita = (i:2) (t:part) (d:<hi>, be, with <ta>, which shows that a state has now come about or is about to: {ka hita hi}, I now am; {hita hen}, let it be so) (b:hi) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitaleh = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:also) (d:<hi>, be, with <ta> and <leh>, repeated after each of two or more choices: both this and also that, whether this or that)
hitaleh = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:even) (d:after one item or the last of several: even if it is, be it even, whatever it may be)
hitalehang = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:though we are/even if we are) (d:<hi> be with <ta>, <leh> if and <hang>, the ending for we including the hearer: however we may be) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitaseleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:although/even though/yet) (d:though it is so; after a statement it means although, and {tua hitaseleh} or {tua bang hitaseleh} opens a sentence as yet or nevertheless) (s:taseleh/hinapi/napi) (q:draft)
hite = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:these) (d:these, these ones, standing at the start of a sentence; a spelling of <hihte>) (s:hihte) (q:draft)
hite = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who are/what is so) (d:<hi>, be, with the plural <te>, used after <a>: those who are, the things that are; {ka gal a hite} is those who are my enemies) (s:ahite) (b:hi) (r:40.5.37) (q:draft)
hithei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be possible/can be/may be) (d:<hi>, be, with <thei>, can: can be, may be, be possible; {a hithei khat hileh} means if it were possible) (s:piantheih/hikhathei) (b:hi) (r:48.4.20) (q:draft)
hithiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at ease/quietly/securely/still) (d:placed after a verb such as <om> or <tu>: staying calm and undisturbed, without care) (s:hit-hiat/hiat/dide/daitakin) (r:19.73.12) (q:draft)
hithiatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:quietly/at rest/peacefully/still) (d:<hithiat> with the ending {-in}, after verbs such as <lum>, lie, and <tu>, sit: staying calmly in that position) (s:daitakin) (b:hithiat) (q:draft)
hithiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:calmness/quietness/ease) (d:noun form of <hithiat>: staying calm and quiet; also the place where people live at ease) (s:daihna) (b:hithiat) (q:draft)
hithit = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:smoothly) (d:describes how wine goes down the throat, smoothly and easily) (s:hit-hit) (q:draft, low confidence)
hito = (i:1) (t:v) (d:<hi> be with <to>, said of a boundary in a description of borders, apparently be or run on as far as a point; exact meaning not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiuhiau = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:strikingly/brightly) (d:placed after a describing word such as <hoih>, beautiful, or <san>, red, to picture a striking, shining look) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hiv = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Hivites/Hivite) (d:people of Canaan descended from Canaan son of Ham; used before <mite>, {Hiv mite} are the Hivites) (r:1.10.17)
hizah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:this many/so many/this much) (d:<hi>, this, with <zah>, amount: this many, as much as this; {mi hizah tak} is so many people as this) (s:hihzah) (q:draft)
hizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rather/be instead) (d:<hi>, be, with <zaw>, rather or more: it is rather this than that, used in contrasts and in either-or questions) (b:hi) (r:24.7.19) (q:draft)
Hizki = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hizki) (d:son of Elpaal in the genealogy of the tribe of Benjamin) (q:draft)
Hizkiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hizkiah) (d:son of Neariah, a descendant of King David through Zerubbabel) (r:13.3.23)
hizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able/can) (d:<hi>, be, with <zo>, be able: manage to be or do so; {ka hizo ding uh hi} means we can) (b:hi) (q:draft)
ho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:talk/speak/converse) (d:talk with someone; {kituam ho} is to talk apart, in private) (s:kiho) (q:draft)
Hobab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hobab) (d:son of Reuel the Midianite and relative of Moses by marriage, whose descendants were the Kenites) (r:4.10.29/7.4.11)
Hobah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hobah) (d:place north of Damascus as far as which Abram pursued the four kings) (r:1.14.15)
Hobaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hobaiah) (d:ancestor of a family of priests who returned from the exile but could not prove their descent) (r:16.7.63)
Hod = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hod) (d:son of Zophah in the genealogy of the tribe of Asher) (q:draft)
Hodaviah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hodaviah) (d:name of several men: a descendant of David, a family head of the half-tribe of Manasseh, and a man of Benjamin) (r:13.3.24/13.5.24)
Hodaviahte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Hodaviah) (d:<Hodaviah> with the plural <te>: the family of Hodaviah, a line of Levites who returned from the exile) (b:Hodaviah) (r:15.3.9/15.2.40)
Hodesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hodesh) (d:wife of Shaharaim of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.9)
Hodevah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hodevah/Hodaviah) (d:ancestor of a family of Levites who returned from the exile, the same as Hodaviah in Ezra 2:40) (r:16.7.43)
Hodiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hodiah) (d:name of several men: a man of Judah who married the sister of Naham, and Levites who explained the law and sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:13.4.19/16.10.18)
Hofni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hophni) (d:son of Eli and priest at Shiloh, killed with his brother Phinehas when the ark was captured) (r:9.1.3/9.4.11)
Hofra = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hophra) (d:Pharaoh of Egypt in the time of Jeremiah) (r:24.44.30)
Hoglah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hoglah) (d:one of the five daughters of Zelophehad of the tribe of Manasseh) (r:4.36.11/4.26.33)
hoh = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after a verb in wishes, requests and regrets, with a sense like just, rather or if only) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hohab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hobab) (d:spelling of <Hobab> in Judges 4:11, the relative of Moses by marriage from whom the Kenites descended) (r:7.4.11)
Hoham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hoham) (d:king of Hebron, one of the five Amorite kings defeated by Joshua) (r:6.10.3)
