hoi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stagger/reel/lean/totter) (d:sway or lean over as if about to fall, like a drunk person or a leaning wall) (s:awn/hoihoi) (r:18.12.25) (q:draft)
Hoih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:Beautiful) (d:<hoih>, good or beautiful, written with a capital in the name of a temple gate: {Hoih Kongkhak} or {Kongpi Hoih}, the Beautiful Gate) (b:hoih) (q:draft)
hoihah = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:good) (d:<hoih> good with the place marker <ah>, which belongs to the whole phrase; {leitang hoihah}, in or into the good land) (b:hoih) (r:5.11.17) (q:draft)
