honsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:openings) (d:plural of <honsakna>: the ways in which a way was opened for someone) (b:honsakna) (q:draft)
hontang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crowd/bunch) (d:in {mihai hontang}, a whole crowd of mad or foolish people; the second part <tang> is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
hontangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:band/gang/crowd) (d:<hontang> with plural <te>, a whole band of people; {migilo hontangte}, a band of evildoers) (b:hontang) (q:draft, low confidence)
hontat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swarm/creep/move along the ground) (d:of small creatures, move about in swarms or crawl; {a hontat ganhing} is a swarming or creeping creature) (s:bokvak) (q:draft)
honte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flocks/herds) (d:groups of animals kept together) (s:ganhonte) (b:hon) (q:draft)
honte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:divisions/hosts/companies) (d:groups of people, as the divisions of a tribe or an assembled community) (s:khente) (b:hon) (r:4.10.27) (q:draft)
honthum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:three bands/three groups) (d:<hon> group with <thum> three) (s:pawlthum) (q:draft)
honzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:protect/shield) (d:apparently <hon> save with <zo> be able; the Tedim says a woman protects a man, where the NIV has return to) (b:hon) (q:draft, low confidence)
hop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:divide/share/distribute) (d:form of <hawm>, share out, used before another word such as <nading>, <zawh> or <theih>) (q:draft)
hopih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak to/talk with/address) (d:talk to or with a person; of God, speak to a prophet) (s:genpih/paupih) (r:24.11.1/24.2.1) (q:draft)
hopih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:greet/salute) (d:speak words of greeting to someone on meeting or in a letter) (q:draft)
hopihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speaking to/greeting) (d:<hopih>, speak to or greet, with the linking ending <in>: speaking to someone, and then) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
hopihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<hopih> speak with, with <lam>: the fact of having talked with someone) (q:draft)
hopihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:speaking to/address) (d:the act of speaking to someone, or what is spoken to them) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
hopihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak to at once/address immediately) (d:<hopih> speak to with <pah> at once) (q:draft)
hopihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak to repeatedly/keep speaking to) (d:<hopih> speak to with its last syllable doubled, said of speaking to someone again and again; {tam veipi} is many times) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
hopihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:greet/give greetings to) (d:<hopih> with <sak>: greet someone on the speaker's behalf, as in the closing greetings of a letter) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
hopihsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak privately to/talk secretly with) (d:<hopih> speak to with <sim> secretly) (q:draft)
hopnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be willing to share/want to share) (d:<hop> share out with <nop> want) (q:draft)
hopnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:willingness to share/generosity) (d:<hopnop> be willing to share with the noun suffix <na>) (s:citna/piaknopna) (b:hopnop) (q:draft)
hopte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those given a share) (d:<hop> share out with plural <te>: those with whom something is shared, here those with whom God shared his glory) (b:hop) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Hor) (d:mountain on the border of Edom where Aaron died, in {Hor Mual}, Mount Hor) (r:4.20.25) (q:draft)
Hor = (i:2) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Horite) (d:the Horites, the people who lived in Seir before the descendants of Esau, in {Hor mite}) (q:draft)
Horam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Horam) (d:king of Gezer who came to help Lachish and was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.10.33)
Horeb = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Horeb) (d:the mountain of God in the wilderness, where God made the covenant with Israel; another name for Mount Sinai) (r:2.3.1/2.33.6)
Horem = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Horem) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.38)
Horesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Horesh) (d:place in the Desert of Ziph where David hid from Saul and made a covenant with Jonathan) (r:9.23.15/9.23.18)
Horhaggidgad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hor Haggidgad) (d:place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped on the way from Egypt) (r:4.33.32/4.33.33)
Hori = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Horites/Hori) (d:the Horites, the people who lived in the hill country of Seir; Hori is also the name of a son of Lotan and of the father of Shaphat of Simeon) (r:1.14.6)
Hormah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hormah) (d:town in the far south of Judah, also counted to Simeon, formerly called Zephath) (r:7.1.17/4.21.3)
Horonaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Horonaim) (d:town in the south of Moab, named in the prophecies against Moab; {Horonaim khuami} renders Horonite, the title of Sanballat) (r:24.48.34/10.13.34)
Horonain = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Horonaim) (d:spelling of <Horonaim> in Jeremiah 48:3 and 48:5, a town in the south of Moab) (r:24.48.3/24.48.5)
Hosah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/place) (w:Hosah) (d:Levite gatekeeper of the family of Merari in the time of David; also a town on the border of Asher near Tyre) (r:13.26.10/6.19.29)
Hosanna = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Hosanna) (d:Hebrew shout of praise meaning save now, cried by the crowd when Jesus entered Jerusalem) (r:41.11.9/41.11.10)
Hosea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hosea) (d:prophet in the northern kingdom of Israel, son of Beeri; also the Bible book that bears his name) (r:28.1.1/28.1.3)
Hoshaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hoshaiah) (d:name of two men: a leader of Judah at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, and the father of Azariah in the time of Jeremiah) (r:16.12.32/24.42.1)
Hoshama = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hoshama) (d:son of Jehoiachin, the exiled king of Judah) (r:13.3.18)
Hoshea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hoshea) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Nun whom Moses renamed Joshua and the last king of Israel, son of Elah) (r:4.13.8)
hot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:row/paddle) (d:move a boat forward with oars; {gunkuang hot} is to row a boat) (q:draft)
hot = (i:2) (t:v) (w:save/rescue/deliver) (d:save someone from danger; often followed by <khiat>, out, as in {hot khiat}, save out of) (s:honkhia/hon/gum) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hotham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hotham) (d:name of two men: a son of Heber of the tribe of Asher, and an Aroerite whose sons were among the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.7.32/13.11.44)
Hothir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hothir) (d:son of Heman, a temple musician in the time of David) (r:13.25.4)
hotkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:save/deliver/rescue/redeem) (d:form of {hotkhia}, save or deliver, used before a following word such as <ding>, <nading> or a noun; {hong hotkhiat ding} is often rendered salvation) (s:honkhia/suaktasak) (r:19.119.166) (q:draft)
hotkhiatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rescue again/save again) (d:<hotkhiat>, rescue, with <kik>, again: rescue someone once more) (b:hotkhiat) (q:draft)
hotkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:salvation/deliverance/rescue) (d:<hotkhiat>, save, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of saving, or the state of being saved from danger or sin) (s:gupna/hotna/gupkhiatna/kihotkhiatna) (b:hotkhiat) (q:draft)
Hotkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Salvation) (d:<hotkhiatna>, salvation, written with a capital as the name given to the walls of Zion) (b:hotkhiatna) (q:draft)
hotkhiatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:redeemed/saved/delivered) (d:<hotkhiat> with <sa>, already done; placed before the noun for the one who has been saved) (s:tatkhiatsa) (b:hotkhiat) (q:draft)
Hotkhiatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the redeemed/the saved) (d:<hotkhiat> save or redeem with the plural <te>: those who are redeemed) (s:tatkhiatsate) (q:draft)
hotna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:saving/salvation/deliverance) (d:<hot>, save, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of saving someone) (s:hotkhiatna/gupna) (b:hot) (q:draft)
hotnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to save/wish to rescue) (d:<hot>, save, with <nop>, want: want to save someone) (q:draft)
hotte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rowers/oarsmen) (d:<hot>, row, with the plural <te>: those who row a boat) (b:hot) (q:draft)
Hovadiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hodaviah) (d:son of Hassenuah of the tribe of Benjamin; spelling of Hodaviah in 1 Chronicles 9:7) (r:13.9.7)
hu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breath) (d:the air that a living being breathes in and out; {nuntakna hu} is the breath of life) (s:husan/husanna) breath of life
hua = (i:2) (t:v) (w:hate/detest/abhor) (d:feel strong dislike for someone or something; the form used before a noun or another verb is <huat>) (s:mudah/kih) (a:it) (q:draft)
huai = (i:1) (t:part) (d:suffix added to a verb or adjective, worthy of or causing that feeling, as in {kihtak-huai} fearsome, <lauhuai> dreadful and <muanhuai> trustworthy) (r:35.1.7) (q:draft)
huaiham = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:greedy/covetous) (d:eager to have more than one needs; also used of greed or craving itself, as in {huaiham luatna}, great greed) (a:cingh) (r:46.6.10) (q:draft)
huaihamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:greedily/in greed) (d:<huaiham>, greedy, with the suffix <in>: in a greedy way, out of greed) (s:duhgawhin) (b:huaiham) (q:draft)
huaihamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:greed/covetousness/craving) (d:<huaiham>, greedy, with the noun suffix <na>: the strong wish to have more than one needs) (s:duhhopna/deihgawhna/duhluatna) (b:huaiham) (r:41.7.22) (q:draft)
huaihamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:greed/covetous desires) (d:plural of <huaihamna>: kinds or acts of greed) (b:huaihamna) (q:draft)
huaihampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:greedy man/covetous man) (d:<huaiham>, greedy, with <pa>, a man: a greedy man) (b:huaiham) (q:draft)
huaihamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the greedy/greedy people) (d:<huaiham>, greedy, with the plural <te>: greedy people) (s:duhhopte) (b:huaiham) (q:draft)
huaina = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the suffix <huai>, worthy of or causing, with the noun suffix <na>: makes a noun for the thing or quality that causes the feeling named, as in {muan huaina}, safety, a place that can be trusted) (b:huai) (q:draft)
huainuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to gather/long to shelter) (d:<huai>, gather under the wings as a hen covers her chicks, with <nuam> want) (r:42.13.34) (q:draft)
huaipi = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<huai>, worthy of or causing a feeling, with <pi> great: {a kihtak huaipi} is a very fearful thing, great terror) (b:huai) (q:draft, low confidence)
huaisa = (t:see) <huaisa-in>
huaisa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:regarding as/deeming) (d:<huai> worthy of with <sa> consider and <in>: {muhthadah huaisa-in} is considering something detestable, hating it) (q:draft, low confidence)
huaisak = (t:see) <muan'huaisak>
huaite = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the suffix <huai>, worthy of or causing a feeling, with plural <te>: those who are, or things that are, fearsome, trustworthy and so on; written joined to the word before or separate) (b:huai) (q:draft)
huaizaw = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<huai>, worthy of or causing, with <zaw>, more: placed after a verb, more worthy of that action, more to be, as in {hehpih huaizaw} more to be pitied and {ngaih huaizaw} more worth listening to) (b:huai) (q:draft)
hualin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rolling/having rolled) (d:<hual>, roll, with the linking ending <in>, used when another verb follows: roll a stone and then do something) (q:draft)
hualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:waves/breakers) (d:plural of <hual>, wave; {tuipi hualte} are the waves of the sea) (s:tuihualte) (q:draft)
huam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:contain/include/take in) (d:hold within itself, as in {huam zo lo}, cannot contain; in lists of towns, take in or include) (q:draft)
huam = (i:2) (t:n) (w:area/bounds/territory) (d:the area that something takes in, in <huam sungah>, within: {gamgi huam sungah}, within the borders of) (q:draft)
huamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:including/covering) (d:<huam>, include, with the linking ending <in>: so as to take in, here one name for each of the twelve tribes) (b:huam) (q:draft)
huamkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:involve/include/take in) (d:<huam> include with <kha> reach, touch: take in or affect all of a group) (q:draft)
huamkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:include/cover/apply to) (d:form of <huamkha> used before another word; {a huamkhak mite} are the people who come under it) (b:huamkha) (q:draft)
huamkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:include all/cover completely) (d:<huam>, include, with <khin>, completely: take in everything, leave nothing out) (b:huam) (q:draft)
huamsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sphere/domain/midst) (d:<huam>, the area that something takes in, with <sung>, inside: the space within the bounds of something) (q:draft)
huamteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whole area/all the territory) (d:<huam> area with <teng> all: everything within the bounds of, here of the city) (b:huam) (q:draft, low confidence)
huan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:garden) (d:a piece of ground, often enclosed, where trees, flowers and food plants are grown; {Eden huan} is the garden of Eden) (s:huansung)
huan = (i:2) (t:n) (w:lawn)
Huan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:garden/paradise) (d:<huan> capitalised in a name: {Eden Huan}, the Garden of Eden; {Pasian’ Huan}, the paradise of God) (b:huan) (q:draft)
huana = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the garden/of the garden) (d:<huan>, garden, with the place marker <a>: that is in the garden) (b:huan) (q:draft)
huanah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the garden/into the garden/in the field) (d:<huan>, garden, with the place ending <ah>: in or into the garden; also of a field or grove where something is grown) (b:huan) (q:draft)
huang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:court/courtyard/enclosure) (d:an enclosed open space beside a building, such as the courts of the temple or the courtyard of a prison; often as {huang sung}, inside the court) (s:huangsung/inntual/tual) (q:draft)
huangsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:courtyard/court/enclosure) (d:the space inside a wall or fence, <huang> with <sung> inside; also the bounds or area set for something) (s:huang/inntual/tual) (q:draft)
huanhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cook/prepare food) (d:<huan>, cook, doubled for an action that is going on: be busy cooking) (s:anhuan) (q:draft)
huanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cooking/boiling) (d:<huan>, cook food by boiling, with the linking ending {-in} before the next verb) (q:draft)
huanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cooking/place for cooking) (d:<huan>, cook or boil, with {-na}: the cooking of food; {a huanna mun} is the place where something is cooked, {a huanna anbuk} a kitchen) (s:anhuanna) (q:draft)
huanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baker/cook) (d:in {an huanpa}, the man who cooks or bakes food: <huan>, cook, with <pa>, a man) (s:anhuanpa) (q:draft)
huanpipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chief baker/chief cook) (d:used as {an huanpipa}, the chief baker or head cook: <huan>, cook, with <pi>, chief, and <pa>, a man) (q:draft)
huansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cooked/baked/prepared) (d:<huan>, cook, with <sa>, already: food that has been cooked; {an huansa}, cooked food) (s:kihuansa) (q:draft)
huansung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:garden/inside of a garden) (d:<huan>, garden, with <sung>, inside: the garden as an enclosed place) (s:huan) (r:12.21.18) (q:draft)
huante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gardens/groves) (d:<huan>, garden, with plural {-te}; {oliv huante} are olive groves) (b:huan) (q:draft)
huantui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:smelt/melt out) (d:melt metal out of ore; apparently <huan> cook, heat with <tui> liquid) (s:haltui) (q:draft)
huat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hate/detest) (d:form of <hua> used before a noun or another verb; {huat mi}, a hated person, {huat bawl}, treat as hateful) (s:muhdah) (b:hua) (q:draft)
huatbawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:treating with contempt/treating hatefully) (d:<huat> hate with <bawl> do, treat and <in>) (q:draft)
huate = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:those) (d:<hua>, that yonder, with plural <te>: those people or things over there) (s:tuate) (a:hihte) (b:hua) (q:draft)
huathuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:hateful/odious/obnoxious) (d:<huat> hate with <huai> worthy of: fit to be hated) (s:mudahhuai/muhthadahhuai) (a:ithuai) (q:draft)
huau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:whisper) (d:speak softly into the ear of someone; {huau-in gen} is say privately in the hearing of) (q:draft)
huausim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:whisper secretly/tell privately) (d:<huau> whisper with <sim> secretly: call or tell someone aside) (q:draft)
hucip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shut/stop up) (d:shut tightly, said of the mouths of lions; compare <humcip>) (q:draft, low confidence)
hucipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stopping up/blocking/closing) (d:<hucip>, stop up or shut by covering, with the linking suffix <in>) (s:khakcipin) (b:hucip) (q:draft)
Hufam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hupham) (d:descendant of Benjamin, ancestor of the Huphamite clan) (r:4.26.39)
huging = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sound/noise/roar) (d:the loud sound of something, such as heavy rain or a crowd) (s:husa/awging/ging) (r:44.2.6) (q:draft)
huh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:assist) (d:work alongside someone and share a task or duty with them)
huh = (i:3) (t:v) (w:aid) (d:come to the aid of someone who is in need or in danger)
huh = (i:4) (t:v) (w:support/uphold/sustain) (d:stand by someone and keep them from falling or failing; {vai huh} is to uphold the cause of someone) (s:panpih) (a:langpang)
Huh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:help) (d:<huh>, help, written with a capital of the Holy Spirit: {note hong Huh ding pa}, the one who will help you, the Advocate in the NIV) (b:huh) (q:draft)
huhau = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:because of/on account of/for the sake of) (d:follows a possessive noun or <tua>, that, and is written {huhau-in}: because of, for the sake of) (s:hanga) (q:draft)
huhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:helping/assisting) (d:<huh>, help, with the linking ending <in>, used before another verb: help and then do something) (b:huh) (q:draft)
huhkhial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fail to help/neglect to help) (d:<huh> help with <khial> miss, err) (q:draft, low confidence)
huhkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:help fully/help completely) (d:<huh> help with <kim> complete) (q:draft)
huhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:help/aid/assistance) (d:<huh>, help, with the noun suffix <na>: what is done or given to help someone; {huhna ngen} is to ask for help) (s:kihuhna/pan'pihna) (b:huh) (r:19.60.11)
huhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:acts of help/aid/gifts) (d:plural of <huhna>: acts of help, also things given as help) (b:huhna) (q:draft)
huhngetna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cry for help/plea for help) (d:<huh> help with <nget> ask and the noun suffix <na>) (q:draft)
huhnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to help) (d:<huh>, help, with <nop>, want: want to help someone) (q:draft)
huhnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eagerness to help/willingness to help) (d:<huh>, help, with <nop>, want, and the noun suffix <na>) (b:huhnop) (q:draft)
huhnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wish to help/be willing to help) (d:<huh>, help, with <nuam>, want, be willing: wish to help someone) (q:draft)
huhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:helper/help) (d:<huh>, help, with <pa>, marking a male person: one who helps; often said of God) (b:huh) (q:draft)
huhpa = (i:2) (t:n) (w:deputy/assistant) (d:an official who assists or stands in for a ruler) (b:huh) (q:draft)
Huhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Advocate/Helper/Comforter) (d:<huhpa>, helper, written with a capital as a title of the Holy Spirit) (b:huhpa) (q:draft)
huhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:help/sustain) (d:<huh> help with <sak>, cause or let something help a person) (b:huh) (q:draft)
huhsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:help in turn/pass on help) (d:<huh> help with <sawn> pass on: give to others the help one has received) (q:draft)
huhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:helpers/those who help) (d:<huh> help with plural {-te}: those who help; {gam ukpi huhte} are the assistants of the governors, the prefects) (b:huh) (q:draft)
huhthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can help/be able to help/be helpful) (d:<huh>, help, with <thei>, can: be able to help, be of real help) (s:huhzo) (b:huh) (q:draft)
huhtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to help) (d:<huh>, help, with <theih>, form of <thei>, be able, used before <nading>) (b:huh) (q:draft)
huhtheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:helpers/those able to help) (d:<huhthei>, be able to help, with the plural <te>: those who are able to help others) (b:huhthei) (q:draft)
huhu = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:with a roar/loudly) (d:sound word for a loud rushing, roaring or blowing noise, placed after a verb: {ging huhu} is roar loudly and {nak huhu} is pant hard) (s:hunhun) (q:draft)
huhzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to help/be able to rescue/save) (d:<huh> help with <zo> be able: manage to help or rescue someone; {a huhzo ding kuamah om kei} means there is no one who can rescue him) (s:honkhiazo) (b:huh) (q:draft)
hui = (t:see) <hui-ah>
hui-ah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:along the edge/at the border) (d:used after <nawl>, edge: {a nawl hui-ah tuh} is to sow a crop along the edge of a field; <hui> is followed by the place marker <ah> and its own meaning is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
huih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:air/wind) (d:air in motion or at rest: the wind that blows and the open air where birds fly; {huih nung} means the wind blows) (s:huihnung)
