hutpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defend/protect/stand up for) (d:<hut>, protect, with <pih>, together with: take the side of someone to protect him or what is his) (s:hut/dal/cing) (b:hut) (q:draft)
hutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make a protection/cause to protect) (d:<hut> protect with the causative <sak>: make something serve as protection) (b:hut) (q:draft)
hutzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:save/be able to save) (d:form of <huzo>, succeed in saving, used before another word) (q:draft)
huu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defend/protect) (d:spelling of <hu>, protect or defend, with a long vowel) (s:hutpih/dal) (q:draft)
huzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:save/preserve/rescue) (d:<hu>, protect or defend, with <zo>, be able: succeed in saving) (s:honkhia/hon/gum/honkhiazo) (a:suplawh/taanlawh) (q:draft)
huzoth = (t:see) <Kiriath-huzoth>
Hymenaias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hymenaeus) (d:false teacher named by Paul, who had turned away from the faith and was handed over to Satan) (r:55.2.17/54.1.20)
i = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:we/our) (d:first person plural including the hearer, placed before a verb or noun) (s:eite) (r:49.5.30)
i-ada = (t:todo) (q:draft, not a word by itself, the end of the name {Beel-i-ada}, NIV Beeliada, in 1 Chronicles 14:7)
i-arib = (t:todo) (q:draft, not a word of its own: the last two parts of the hyphenated man's name {Jo-i-arib}, Joiarib; a lowercase keyword cannot take type name)
iah = (t:see) <Zeru-iah>
iahte = (t:see) <Asa-iahte>
Ibhar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ibhar) (d:son of King David, born in Jerusalem) (r:10.5.15/13.14.5)
Ibleam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ibleam) (d:town of the tribe of Manasseh within the land of Issachar and Asher, near which King Ahaziah was wounded) (r:6.17.11/7.1.27)
Ibneiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ibneiah) (d:Benjamite, son of Jeroham, who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:13.9.8)
Ibnijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ibnijah) (d:Benjamite, ancestor of the Meshullam who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:13.9.8)
Ibri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ibri) (d:a Levite, descendant of Merari through Jaaziah) (q:draft)
Ibsam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ibsam) (d:a son of Tola of the tribe of Issachar) (q:draft)
Ibzan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ibzan) (d:judge of Israel from Bethlehem, who led Israel after Jephthah) (r:7.12.8/7.12.10)
Idalah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Idalah) (d:town in the land of the tribe of Zebulun) (r:6.19.15)
Idbash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Idbash) (d:man of the tribe of Judah, a son of Etam) (r:13.4.3)
Iddo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Iddo) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Ahinadab, an officer of Solomon, and a priest who returned from the exile) (r:11.4.14/16.12.4)
Idumia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Idumea) (d:region south of Judea, the Greek name of Edom) (r:41.3.8)
Iezer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Iezer) (d:son of Gilead of the tribe of Manasseh, ancestor of the Iezerite clan) (q:draft)
Ifdeiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Iphdeiah) (d:Benjamite, a son of Shashak) (r:13.8.25)
Iftah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Iphtah) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.43)
Iftahel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Iphtah El) (d:valley on the border between the lands of Zebulun and Asher) (r:6.19.14/6.19.27)
Igal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Igal) (d:name of several men: the spy from the tribe of Issachar, son of Joseph; a warrior of David, son of Nathan of Zobah; and a son of Shemaiah in the line of David) (r:4.13.7/10.23.36) (q:draft)
Igdaliah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Igdaliah) (d:father of Hanan, whose sons had a room in the temple in the time of Jeremiah) (r:24.35.4)
ihi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:we are) (d:the verb <hi> with the first person plural prefix <i>, including the hearer; {bang cih ding ihi hiam}, what shall we do) (b:hi) (q:draft)
ihih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:we are) (d:<i> we written together with <hih>, the form of <hi> be used before words such as <leh> if, <manin> because and <laitakin> while) (r:63.1.2) (q:draft)
ihihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<i> we with <hihlam>, the fact of being: that we are, followed by <thei> or <kithei> know) (b:hihlam) (q:draft)
ihihna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the fact that we are, noun form of <ihih> we are, used where English says that we are or because we are) (b:ihih) (q:draft)
ihmu = (i:2) (t:v) (w:nap) (s:lusu/mengme)
ihmucip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sleep soundly/be fast asleep) (d:<ihmu>, sleep, with <cip>, fast: sleep deeply; in Psalms 76:5 of the sleep of death) (s:ihmusip/ihsip) (b:ihmu) (q:draft)
ihmucipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sleeping soundly/fast asleep) (d:<ihmucip>, sleep soundly, with the suffix <in>: being fast asleep) (b:ihmucip) (q:draft)
Ihmulum = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ihmulum)
ihmumu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:slumber) (d:<ihmu>, sleep, with its last syllable repeated: go on sleeping, slumber) (s:lusu/mengme) (b:ihmu)
Ihmumu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:slumber/sleep) (d:<ihmumu> written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (b:ihmumu) (q:draft)
ihmusak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put to sleep/make sleep) (d:<ihmu>, sleep, with the causative <sak>: make someone sleep, put to sleep) (a:phong) (b:ihmu) (q:draft)
ihmusip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sleep soundly/be sound asleep) (d:<ihmu>, sleep, with <sip>, deeply: be sound asleep) (s:ihmucip/ihsip) (q:draft)
ihmut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:slept/sleep/be asleep) (d:form of <ihmu>, sleep, used before another word such as <leh>, <hun>, <lai> or <kal>; {ihmut kalin} is while asleep) (r:1.2.21)
ihmutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sleep) (d:<ihmut>, sleep, with the noun suffix <na>: sleep; {a ihmutna panin khanglo} is wake from sleep) (b:ihmut) (q:draft)
ihsip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sleep deeply/be fast asleep) (d:<ih>, sleep, with <sip>, deeply: be in deep sleep) (s:ihmucip/ihmusip) (q:draft)
iik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breast/brisket) (d:the breast of an animal, in the verses the breast portion of a sacrifice, also written {sa-iik}) (q:draft)
iikte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breasts) (d:<iik>, the breast of an animal, with the plural <te>; in the offerings the part that is waved before the Lord) (b:iik) (r:3.9.21) (q:draft)
iim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hide/conceal/cover up) (d:spelling of <im> with a long vowel: hide a matter, keep something from someone) (s:seel) (a:pulak/pholak) (b:im) (q:draft)
Iim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Iyim) (d:town in the far south of Judah, toward the border of Edom) (r:6.15.29)
iimcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cover up/conceal/hide completely) (d:<iim> hide with <cip> tightly; spelling of <imcip> with a long vowel) (s:seelcip) (b:iim) (q:draft)
iip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restrain/hold back/suppress) (d:spelling of <ip> with a long vowel: keep a feeling or words in; {ki-iip} is restrain oneself) (b:ip) (q:draft)
Ijon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ijon) (d:town in the far north of Israel, in the land of Naphtali, taken by Ben-Hadad and later by Tiglath-Pileser) (r:11.15.20/14.16.4)
Ikabod = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ichabod) (d:spelling of <Ikhabod> in 1 Samuel 14:3, the son of Phinehas and grandson of Eli) (r:9.14.3)
Ikhabod = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ichabod) (d:son of Phinehas and grandson of Eli the priest, born when the ark of God was captured) (r:9.4.21/9.14.3)
Ikkesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ikkesh) (d:man of Tekoa, father of Ira, one of the warriors of David) (r:10.23.26/13.11.28)
ikkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring up/belch out/vomit) (d:said of food eaten to excess coming back out, where the NIV has until it comes out of your nostrils; apparently {ik} with <khiat> out) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ikonium = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Iconium) (d:city in the south of Asia Minor where Paul and Barnabas preached) (r:44.13.51/44.14.1)
Ilai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ilai) (d:an Ahohite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (q:draft)
Ilirikum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Illyricum) (d:Roman province on the east coast of the Adriatic Sea, the farthest point of the preaching of Paul) (r:45.15.19)
Illyrikam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Illyrikam/Illyricum) (d:spelling of <Ilirikum>, the Roman province on the east coast of the Adriatic Sea) (r:45.15.18)
im = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hide/conceal/keep secret) (d:keep something from being known or seen; with <tungah>, hide a matter from someone; {ki-im} is be hidden) (s:seel) (a:pulak/pholak/langsak) (r:47.4.2) (q:draft)
imcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seal up/keep hidden/conceal) (d:<im> hide with <cip> tightly: keep completely secret; {ki-imcip} is be kept hidden) (s:seelcip) (a:pholak/pulak) (b:im) (q:draft)
Imlah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imlah) (d:father of the prophet Micaiah) (r:11.22.8/14.18.8) (q:draft)
Immanuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Immanuel) (d:name meaning God with us, given to the child promised as a sign in Isaiah 7:14) (r:23.7.14)
Immer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Immer) (d:name of several men, among them the head of the sixteenth division of priests and the father of the priest Pashhur) (r:24.20.1/13.24.14)
Imna = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imna) (d:a descendant of Asher) (q:draft)
Imnah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imnah) (d:eldest son of Asher, ancestor of the Imnite clan, called {Imnah behte}) (r:13.7.30/4.26.44) (q:draft)
Imrah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imrah) (d:a descendant of Asher, son of Zophah) (q:draft)
Imri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imri) (d:name of two men: the father of Zakkur who helped rebuild the wall of Jerusalem, and a man of Judah descended from Perez) (r:13.9.4) (q:draft)
in = (i:1) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker indicating place or time, equivalent in usage to the prepositions in, at, among) (r:1.1.1)
IN = (i:1) (t:ppm) (d:the marker <in>, which follows the subject or doer of an action, written in capitals in an inscription or title) (q:draft)
inah = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after a verb of saying such as <cih>, <gen> or <hilh>, often joined with a hyphen, to introduce the words that follow: this is what he says) (q:draft)
India = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:India) (d:land at the eastern end of the Persian empire of Xerxes, which reached from India to Cush) (r:17.1.1/17.8.9)
ing = (i:1) (t:part) (d:sentence-final first person singular ending, used in place of <ka> before the verb and <hi> after it, {Hiah om ing} is here I am) (q:draft)
inkipsakna = (t:todo) (q:draft, appears to be the marker <in> joined to <kipsakna>, ordination, in Exodus 29:22, a suspected misprint)
inla = (i:1) (t:part) (d:particle suffixed to a verb to effect politeness)
inla = (i:2) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker indicating future action or state, equivalent in usage to the auxiliary verbs will and shall)
inling = (t:todo) (q:draft, appears to be the marker <in> joined to <ling>, thorn, in Genesis 3:18, a suspected misprint)
inmi = (t:todo) (q:draft, appears to be the marker <in> joined to <mi>, person, in Genesis 6:3, a suspected misprint)
inn = (i:2) (t:n) (w:institution)
Inn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:house/palace) (d:<inn>, house, written with a capital in the names of buildings: {Tulak Inn}, Palace of the Forest; {Galkap Inn}, House of the Heroes) (b:inn) (q:draft)
innah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:home/house) (d:<inn>, house, with the place marker <ah>: to the house, at home) (b:inn) (q:draft)
Innah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imnah) (d:a Levite, father of Kore; apparently a misprint of <Imnah>) (q:draft, low confidence)
innbul = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foundation/base) (d:<inn>, house, with <bul>, base: the base on which a building stands) (s:bulpi/tawphah) (q:draft)
inncin = (t:see) <inncin'na>
inncin'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guarding/guard duty) (d:<inncing>, guard, with the noun suffix <na>: the keeping of guard; {inncin'na inndei} is the guardroom) (s:inncinna) (q:draft)
inncing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guard/palace guard/bodyguard) (d:one who guards a house or palace; {inncing mangpa} is the captain of the guard and {inncing a ukte} the commanders of the guard) (s:cingpa) (q:draft)
inncingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guards) (d:<inncing>, guard, with the plural <te>: the guards of a palace) (s:cingte) (b:inncing) (q:draft)
inncinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guarding/guard duty) (d:<inncing>, guard, with the noun suffix <na>: the keeping of guard; {inncinna inndei} is the guardroom) (s:inncin'na) (q:draft)
inndap = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ceiling/roofing) (d:the boards that cover a room overhead, from <inn>, house, and <dap>, line with boards; {inndap bawl} is to roof or ceil a house) (s:innsun) (q:draft, low confidence)
inndeineu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small room) (d:<inndei>, room, with <neu>, small: a small room) (q:draft)
inndeipi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:main hall/portico/great room) (d:<inndei>, room, with <pi>, great: a large hall; in Ezekiel the main hall or portico of the temple) (s:deipi) (b:inndei) (r:26.41.23) (q:draft)
inndeite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rooms/chambers/storerooms) (d:<inndei>, room, with the plural <te>: the rooms of a building, in the temple also the storerooms) (s:deite) (b:inndei) (r:11.6.29) (q:draft)
inndung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:length of the building) (d:<inn>, house, with <dung>, length: the length of a building, set against its <vai>, the width) (q:draft)
inngualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rows of rooms/rows of houses) (d:<inn> house with <gual> row and plural <te>: rooms or buildings standing in a row) (q:draft)
innhikpi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:chameleon) (s:thankik)
innhikpi = (i:2) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizard/great lizard) (d:a large lizard, named among the unclean creatures that move along the ground) (s:tangteuh)
Innhikte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizards/lizard) (d:a small creature that can be held in the hand and yet lives in the palaces of kings; apparently <innhik> with the plural suffix <te>; the NIV has lizard and older versions spider) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkalte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beams/rafters) (d:the timbers laid across a house to carry the ceiling or roof, with the plural <te>) (s:innkamte) (q:draft)
innkam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beam/rafter/timber) (d:a large beam of wood in the frame of a house) (q:draft)
innkamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beams/rafters/joists) (d:<innkam>, beam, with the plural <te>: the timbers that carry the roof or floor of a house) (s:innkalte) (b:innkam) (q:draft)
innkhangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:neighbours below) (d:those whose houses are on the lower side of one's own; <innsak> and {innkhang} together are the neighbours on either side) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkhuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillar/post/foundation) (d:<inn>, house, with <khuam>, post: the post that carries a house; in the letters of Paul the foundation on which a building is set) (s:khuam/khuampi) (q:draft)
innkhuampi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillar/main pillar) (d:<innkhuam>, house post, with <pi>, great: a main pillar of a house) (s:khuampi) (b:innkhuam) (q:draft)
innkhuamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillars/supports/posts) (d:<innkhuam>, house post, with the plural <te>: the posts or supports of a building) (s:khuamte/khuampite) (b:innkhuam) (q:draft)
innkhumdawn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rooftop/housetop/roof) (d:<innkhum>, roof, with <dawn>, top: the top of the roof of a house) (s:innkhum/innkhumzang) (q:draft)
innkhumzang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:roof/housetop) (d:the flat top of a house, where people can walk or stay) (s:innkhum/khumzang) (q:draft)
innkhumzanga = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the roof/on the housetop) (d:<innkhumzang>, roof, with the place marker <a>) (s:innkhumzangah/khumzanga) (b:innkhumzang) (q:draft)
innkhumzangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the roof/on the housetop/to the roof) (d:<innkhumzang>, the flat roof of a house, with the place ending {-ah}) (s:innkhumzanga/khumzangah) (b:innkhumzang) (q:draft)
innkiim = (t:see) <innkiim-ah>
innkiim-ah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around the house) (d:<innkiim>, the surroundings of a house, with <ah>, at) (q:draft)
innkim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:surroundings of the house) (d:the area all around a house, here the temple; probably the same word as <innkiim>) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkiu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:corner of a house) (d:<inn> house with <kiu> corner; {innkiu suang} is the cornerstone) (q:draft)
innkiunuai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cornerstone/foundation of the corner) (d:<inn> house, <kiu> corner, <nuai> under; {innkiunuai suang} is the cornerstone) (q:draft)
innkongah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the doorway/to the door of the house) (d:<innkong>, the doorway of a house, with <ah>, at or to) (q:draft)
innkuan = (i:2) (t:n) (w:household) (s:innsung/innkuansung) (r:1.20.18)
innkuanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:family by family/by households) (d:<innkuan>, family, with <in>: by family; doubled as {innkuan innkuanin}, one family after another) (s:innkuankuanin/innkuankuan) (b:innkuan) (q:draft)
innkuankuan = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:family by family/by families) (d:<innkuan>, family, doubled: each family in turn; often with {-in} or {-un} added) (s:innkuankuanin/innkuankuanun) (r:4.1.2) (q:draft)
innkuankuanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:family by family/by families/by clans) (d:<innkuankuan>, each family in turn, with {-in}) (s:innkuankuan/innkuankuanun/innkuanin) (b:innkuankuan) (q:draft)
innkuankuanun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:family by family/by their families) (d:<innkuankuan> with <un>, the plural marker <uh> joined with <in>) (s:innkuankuanin/innkuankuan) (b:innkuankuan) (q:draft)
innkuanmi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:household members/people of the household) (d:<innkuan> household with <mi>, person) (b:innkuan) (q:draft)
innkuanpih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:family) (s:innkuan)
innkuanpih = (i:2) (t:n) (w:relative) (d:a person who belongs to the same family; {innkuanpih mite} are the members of a family) (s:tanau)
innkuanpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:families/family members/household) (d:<innkuanpih>, family, with the plural <te>: families, or the members of one family) (s:innkuante) (b:innkuanpih)
innkuanpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:household/whole family/family members) (d:all the members of a household; Genesis 46:31 has {innkuanpite} and <innkuanpihte> side by side for the same thing, so probably <innkuanpih>, family member, with plural {-te}) (s:innkuante/innkuansung) (b:innkuan) (r:5.11.6) (q:draft)
innkuansung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:household/family) (d:<innkuan>, family, with <sung>, inside: those who belong to one house and family) (s:innkuan/innsung) (q:draft)
innkuante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:household/family/house) (d:<innkuan>, family, with the plural <te>: the members of a family or household; {Aaron innkuante} is the house of Aaron) (s:innkuanpite) (b:innkuan) (q:draft)
innlak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:relative/kin) (d:of the father's family; {innlak pa} is an uncle, {innlak nu} an aunt, {innlak sanggampa} a cousin) (s:tanau) (q:draft, low confidence)
innlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:building/house-building/builder) (d:<inn>, house, with <lam>, build: the building of houses, and those who build; {innlam siamte} are skilled builders and {lei-le-suang innlam siamte} stonemasons) (s:innlamna/lamna) (r:44.4.11) (q:draft)
innlam = (i:2) (t:n) (w:way home) (d:the direction of one's house) (q:draft, low confidence)
innlamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:house-building/construction) (d:<innlam> building of houses, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:innlam/lamna) (b:innlam) (q:draft)
innlamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:builders) (d:<innlam>, house-building, with the plural <te>: those who build houses) (s:lamte) (b:innlam) (r:12.22.6) (q:draft)
innlelo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:home/homestead/house and land) (d:<inn> house, <le> and, <lo> field written as one word: a home of one's own with its land; {innlelo nei lo} is homeless) (q:draft)
innliim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:portico/porch/colonnade) (d:the roofed porch at the front of a building, in the verses that of the temple; also spelled <innlim>) (s:innlim) (q:draft)
innlim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:portico/porch) (d:the roofed porch at the front of a building, in the verses that of the temple; also spelled <innliim>) (s:innliim) (q:draft)
innlimah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the portico/to the portico) (d:<innlim> portico with the place marker <ah>) (b:innlim) (q:draft)
innluah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:inherit/be heir) (d:take over the house and property of the family as heir; {innluah mi} or {innluah pa} is the heir and {innluah za} the right of the heir) (s:luah) (q:draft)
innluahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inheritance) (d:<innluah>, inherit, with the noun suffix <na>: what is received as an heir) (s:luahna/gamhluahna) (b:innluah) (q:draft)
innluahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:heir) (d:<innluah>, inherit the house, with <pa>, a man: the son who inherits) (s:gamhluahpa) (b:innluah) (q:draft)
innluahza = (i:1) (t:n) (w:birthright/right of the firstborn) (d:the right of the firstborn son to inherit the house, from <innluah>, inherit, and <za>, rank) (q:draft)
innmong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:end of the house) (d:<inn> house with <mong>, end or edge) (q:draft)
innpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:temple/great house/hall) (d:<inn>, house, with <pi>, great: a great house or main hall; {biakna innpi} is the temple and {Pasian’ innpi} the house of God) (b:inn) (q:draft)
innpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:palaces/great houses) (d:<innpi>, a great house such as a palace or temple, with plural <te>) (b:innpi) (q:draft)
innpua = (t:see) <innpua-ah>
innpua-ah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:outside/outside the house) (d:<innpua>, the outside of a house, with <ah>, at) (s:pualamah) (a:innsunga) (q:draft)
innsa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:livestock) (d:<inn>, house, with <sa>, animal: animals kept at the house, set against <gamsa>, wild animals) (s:gan) (a:gamsa)
innsa = (i:2) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:pet)
innsak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:neighbour above) (d:the house or people on the upper side of one's own; {innsak} and {innkhang} together are the neighbours on either side) (b:inn) (q:draft, low confidence)
innsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:livestock/cattle/domestic animals) (d:<innsa>, animal kept at the house, with plural {-te}; set against <gamsate>, the wild animals) (s:gankhawite) (a:gamsate) (b:innsa) (q:draft)
innsia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ruins/ruined house) (d:<inn>, house, with <sia>, spoiled: houses fallen into ruin; <innsia losia> is ruined houses and fields, a heap of ruins) (q:draft)
innsualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:floors) (d:<inn>, house, with <sual>, floor, and the plural <te>: the floors of the rooms of a house) (s:sualte) (q:draft)
innsun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ceiling/ceiling beam/rafter) (d:the top of a room or the beams there; {sual panin innsun dong}, from floor to ceiling) (s:inndap) (a:sual) (q:draft, low confidence)
innsunga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the house/in the household) (d:<innsung>, the inside of a house or a household, with the place ending <a>; {innsunga om}, who or which is in the house) (s:Innsungah) (a:innpua-ah) (b:innsung) (q:draft)
Innsungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:into the house/in the house/indoors) (d:<innsung>, the inside of the house, with the place marker <ah>, here at the start of a sentence) (s:innsunga) (a:innpua-ah) (q:draft)
innsungmang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:court official/eunuch/palace officer) (d:<innsung>, the inside of the house, with <mang>, officer: an official who serves inside the royal house, in the Bible often a eunuch) (q:draft)
innsungmangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:court officials/eunuchs/attendants) (d:<innsungmang>, court official, with the plural <te>: the officials who serve inside a royal house, often eunuchs) (b:innsungmang) (q:draft)
innsunte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ceiling beams/rafters) (d:<innsun>, ceiling beam, with the plural <te>) (s:innkamte) (b:innsun) (q:draft, low confidence)
innte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:houses/buildings) (d:<inn>, house, with the plural <te>: houses, or the buildings of a town) (b:inn) (q:draft)
innteek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:house owner/householder/master of the house) (d:the person to whom a house belongs; {innteek pa} is the man who owns the house, also the master for whom someone works) (s:teekpa) (q:draft)
inntual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:courtyard/court) (d:<inn>, house, with <tual>, open ground: the open space in front of or enclosed by a house, palace or temple) (s:tual/huang) (r:41.14.66) (q:draft)
inntualah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the courtyard/into the courtyard) (d:<inntual> courtyard, the open space before a house, with the place marker <ah>) (b:inntual) (q:draft)
inntualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:courts/courtyards) (d:<inntual>, courtyard, with plural <te>) (s:tualte) (b:inntual) (q:draft)
inntuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:divide the inheritance/give a share of the property) (d:literally set up a separate house; give a brother his share of the family property) (q:draft, low confidence)
innvengte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:neighbors) (d:plural of <innveng>: people who live in the houses nearby) (s:vengte/veengte) (b:innveng) (q:draft)
innzom = (i:1) (t:n) (w:next door/adjoining house) (d:<inn> house with <zom>, join; {innzom a vengte} are the nearest neighbours) (q:draft)
insek = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:insect) (d:apparently the English word insect; {insek ganhing}, insect creatures, of small winged creatures) (q:draft, low confidence)
Iob = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jashub) (d:third son of Issachar, written Iob in the Hebrew text of Genesis 46:13 and Jashub in the NIV) (r:1.46.13)
ip = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bag/purse/sack) (d:a bag or sack for carrying goods or money; {dangka-ip} is a purse and <thung-ip> a travelling bag) (q:draft)
ip = (i:2) (t:v) (w:hold back/restrain/keep in/conceal) (d:hold in, as words or anger, or keep a matter hidden; {pau ip}, to hold the tongue) (s:im/seel) (a:pulak/genkhia) (q:draft)
ipbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold back/conceal/keep to oneself) (d:<ip>, hold in or conceal, with <bawl>, do: keep something back; {ipbawl loin} is without holding back, openly) (s:im) (a:pulak) (b:ip) (q:draft)
ipcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep hidden/hold back/shut up) (d:<ip> hold in or conceal with <cip>, tightly; {ki-ipcip}, hold oneself back) (s:imcip/seelcip) (a:pholak) (b:ip) (q:draft)
ipcipte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:secrets/hidden things) (d:the things kept hidden; <ipcip> with the plural <te>) (s:thusimte) (b:ipcip) (q:draft)
Iphtah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Iphtah) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah)
ipin = (t:see) <ki-ipin>
ipip = (t:see) <ki-ipip>
ipipna = (t:see) <ki-ipipna>
iplah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:desire/covet/lust after) (d:long for something or someone as too precious to do without) (s:lunggulh/deihgawh/duhgawh) (q:draft)
iplah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:spare/hold dear) (d:value something too much to lose it; {iplah loin} means without sparing, mercilessly) (s:siit) (q:draft, low confidence)
iplahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:coveting/desiring) (d:<iplah>, covet, with the linking suffix <in>: coveting something and then acting on it, as in {iplahin la}, covet and take) (b:iplah) (q:draft)
iplahkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lust after/covet/desire) (d:<iplah>, covet, with <kha>, happen to: come to desire in the heart; used with {kei in} as a prohibition) (s:duhgawhkha) (q:draft, low confidence)
ipna = (t:see) <ipna-in>
ipna-in = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holding in/restraining) (d:<ip> hold in, with the noun suffix <na> and <in>, by or from: from holding it in) (q:draft)
ippi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sackcloth/sack) (d:<ip>, bag, with <pi>, big: a large sack; {ippi puan} is sackcloth, the coarse cloth worn in mourning and repentance) (s:puanham/puanhampi/khautang) (b:ip) (r:27.9.3) (q:draft)
ipsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bag/inside of a bag) (d:<ip>, bag, with <sung>, inside: the inside of a bag, where weights or money are carried) (q:draft)
ipte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bags/sacks/purses) (d:<ip> bag with the plural <te>; {khutkhai ipte}, handbags or purses) (b:ip) (q:draft)
iptheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who can hold back) (d:<ip> hold in, <thei> be able, with the plural <te>; {pau iptheite} are those who can hold their tongue) (q:draft)
ipzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restrain/hold back/keep in) (d:<ip>, hold in, with <zo>, be able: manage to hold back anger or words; {ki-ipzo} is hold oneself back) (b:ip) (r:18.20.2) (q:draft)
ipzote = (t:see) <ki-ipzote>
Ir = (t:see) <Rehoboth-Ir>
Ira = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ira) (d:name of three men in the time of David: Ira the Jairite, his priest, and two of his mighty warriors, Ira the Ithrite and Ira son of Ikkesh from Tekoa) (r:10.23.38) (q:draft)
Irad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Irad) (d:son of Enoch and grandson of Cain, father of Mehujael) (r:1.4.18)
irah = (t:see) <Se-irah>
Iram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Iram) (d:one of the chiefs of Edom descended from Esau) (r:1.36.43/13.1.54)
Iri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Iri) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin, head of a family) (q:draft)
Irijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Irijah) (d:captain of the guard, son of Shelemiah, who arrested the prophet Jeremiah at the Benjamin Gate) (r:24.37.13/24.37.14)
Irnahash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ir Nahash) (d:town in Judah founded by Tehinnah, a descendant of Judah) (r:13.4.12)
iron = (i:1) (t:n) (w:iron)
Iron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Iron) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali; not the English word for the metal) (q:draft)
Irpe = (t:see) <Irpe-el>
Irpe-el = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Irpeel) (d:town in the territory of Benjamin) (r:6.18.27) (q:draft)
Irpeel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Irpeel) (d:spelling of <Irpe-el> without the hyphen, a town in the territory of Benjamin) (r:6.18.27)
Irshemesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ir Shemesh) (d:town in the territory allotted to the tribe of Dan) (r:6.19.41)
Iru = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Iru) (d:eldest son of Caleb son of Jephunneh) (r:13.4.15)
Isaac = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Isaac) (d:son of Abraham and Sarah, husband of Rebekah and father of Esau and Jacob) (r:1.25.5)
Isaak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Isaac) (d:son of Abraham and Sarah, husband of Rebekah and father of Esau and Jacob) (r:13.1.28/1.25.5)
Isaakhar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Issachar) (d:spelling of <Issakhar> in one verse: son of Jacob and Leah, ancestor of the tribe of Issachar) (r:1.46.13)
Isahmael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishmael) (d:spelling of <Ishmael> in one verse: son of Abraham and Hagar, father of Mahalath the wife of Esau) (r:1.28.9)
Isaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Isaiah) (d:prophet in Judah, son of Amoz, in the days of King Hezekiah; also the book of his prophecies) (r:23.13.1/23.38.4)
Isarel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Israel) (d:spelling of <Israel> found in a few verses: the nation and people of Israel) (r:11.22.1/2.17.6)
Ishamael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishmael) (d:spelling of <Ishmael> in one verse: Ishmael son of Nethaniah, who killed Gedaliah the governor of Judah) (r:24.41.9)
Ishbah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishbah) (d:descendant of Judah, son of Mered and founder of Eshtemoa) (r:13.4.17)
Ishbak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishbak) (d:son of Abraham and his wife Keturah) (r:1.25.2)
Ishbibenob = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishbi-Benob) (d:Philistine giant, a descendant of Rapha, who set out to kill David) (r:10.21.16)
Ishbosheth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ish-Bosheth) (d:son of Saul, made king over Israel by Abner after the death of Saul) (r:10.2.12/10.3.15)
Ishhod = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishhod) (d:son of Hammoleketh, of the tribe of Manasseh) (r:13.7.18)
Ishi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishi) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Appaim of the tribe of Judah and a family head of the half-tribe of Manasseh) (r:13.2.31/13.5.24) (q:draft)
Ishma = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishma) (d:a descendant of Judah, son of Etam) (q:draft)
Ishmael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishmael) (d:son of Abraham and Hagar, ancestor of the Ishmaelites; also the name of other men, among them Ishmael son of Nethaniah who killed Gedaliah) (r:1.16.16/13.1.28)
Ishmaelte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishmael) (d:<Ishmael> with the plural <te>, which groups him with the person named before: Abraham and his son Ishmael) (b:Ishmael) (r:1.17.26)
Ishmaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishmaiah) (d:name of two men in the time of David: a warrior from Gibeon who led the Thirty, and the son of Obadiah, officer over the tribe of Zebulun) (r:13.27.19/13.12.4)
Ishmeal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishmael) (d:spelling of <Ishmael> in one verse: a son of Azel, of the tribe of Benjamin and the family of Saul) (r:13.8.38)
Ishmerai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishmerai) (d:a man of the tribe of Benjamin, son of Elpaal) (r:13.8.18)
Ishpah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishpah) (d:a man of the tribe of Benjamin, son of Beriah) (r:13.8.16)
Ishpan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishpan) (d:a man of the tribe of Benjamin, named in the list of family heads who lived in Jerusalem) (r:13.8.22)
Ishvah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishvah) (d:second son of Asher) (r:1.46.17/13.7.30)
Ishvi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishvi) (d:name of two men: a son of Asher, ancestor of the Ishvite clan, and a son of King Saul) (r:1.46.17/13.7.30)
Iskah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Iscah/Iskah) (d:daughter of Haran, sister of Milkah and of Lot) (r:1.11.29)
Iskariot = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Iscariot) (d:second name of Judas, the disciple who betrayed Jesus) (r:43.12.4/42.6.16)
Iskarot = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Iscariot) (d:spelling of <Iskariot> in one verse, the second name of Judas who betrayed Jesus) (r:40.10.4)
Ismakhiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ismakiah) (d:one of the overseers of the temple offerings under King Hezekiah) (r:14.31.13)
Israel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Israel) (d:the name God gave to Jacob, son of Isaac, the ancestor of the twelve tribes) (r:1.32.28/1.35.10)
Israel = (i:2) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Israel) (d:the nation and land of the descendants of Jacob; after Solomon also the northern kingdom as distinct from Judah) (r:9.11.7/10.21.5)
Israelmite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Israelites) (d:<Israel> with <mite>, people: the people of Israel) (b:Israel) (r:11.6.1)
Israelte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Israelites) (d:<Israel> with the plural <te>: the people of Israel) (b:Israel) (r:10.17.26/7.9.22)
Isreal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Israel) (d:misspelling of <Israel> found in a few verses) (r:26.34.14/13.22.9)
Issaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishiah) (d:one of the Korahite warriors who joined David at Ziklag) (r:13.12.6)
Issak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Isaac) (d:spelling of <Isaak> found in a few verses: the son of Abraham and father of Jacob) (r:11.18.36) (q:draft)
Issakhar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Issachar) (d:son of Jacob and Leah, ancestor of the tribe of Issachar; also the tribe and its territory) (r:1.30.18/2.1.3)
Issakharte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Issachar) (d:<Issakhar> with the plural <te>: the people of the tribe of Issachar) (b:Issakhar) (r:13.6.72)
Isshiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishiah) (d:name of several men, among them a chief of the tribe of Issachar and two Levites in the time of David) (r:13.7.3/13.24.21)
Isshijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishijah) (d:descendant of Harim who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.31)
Issiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishiah) (d:a Levite, second son of Uzziel of the family of Kohath) (r:13.23.20)
Itali = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Italy) (d:the land of Italy, spelled as it is said in Zolai) (r:58.13.24)
Italy = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Italy) (d:the land of Italy, where the city of Rome lies) (r:44.27.6/44.27.1)
itbawlin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:lovingly/in love) (d:<it>, love, with <bawl>, treat, and the linking suffix <in>: treating someone with love) (q:draft)
itdiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:love especially/love most) (d:<it> love with <diak>, particularly) (q:draft)
Ithai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithai) (d:one of the mighty warriors of David, from Gibeah in Benjamin) (q:draft)
Ithamar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithamar) (d:youngest son of Aaron, a priest) (r:4.3.2)
Ithiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithiel) (d:a man of the tribe of Benjamin, ancestor of Sallu who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:16.11.7)
Ithlah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ithlah) (d:town in the territory allotted to the tribe of Dan) (r:6.19.42)
Ithmah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithmah) (d:a Moabite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (q:draft)
Ithnan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ithnan) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.23)
Ithra = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithra/Jether) (d:an Ishmaelite, father of Amasa; the NIV has Jether) (q:draft)
Ithran = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithran) (d:name of two men: a son of Dishon the Horite in Edom, and a descendant of Asher) (r:1.36.26/13.7.37)
Ithream = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithream) (d:sixth son of David, born in Hebron to his wife Eglah) (r:10.3.5/13.3.3)
Ithri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Ithrite) (d:name of a clan; {Ithri mi} is an Ithrite and {Ithri mite} the Ithrites) (r:13.2.53) (q:draft)
ithuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:beloved/lovable/dear) (d:<it>, love, with <huai>, worthy of: worthy of love, dear) (q:draft)
itin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:loving/love) (d:<it>, love, with the linking suffix <in>: loving someone and so doing what follows; {itin nei} is hold dear) (a:mudahin) (b:it) (r:62.5.2) (q:draft)
itkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:love again/reaffirm love) (d:<it> love with <kik>, again) (b:it) (q:draft)
itluat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:darling/beloved/dearly loved one) (d:<it>, love, with <luat>, very much: one who is greatly loved; a word of address in love poetry, as {itluat aw}) (s:ngaihno/lungtup) (r:22.4.10/22.2.13) (q:draft)
itluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great love/deep love) (d:<it> love with <luat> very much and the noun suffix <na>; said of the Lord's zeal for Jerusalem, where the NIV has jealousy) (q:draft)
itnakip = (i:1) (t:n) (w:unfailing love/steadfast love) (d:<itna> love with <kip>, firm or lasting) (q:draft)
itnasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:former love/love once shown) (d:<itna> love with <sa> already: the love a person had or showed before) (b:itna) (q:draft)
itnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:love/acts of love) (d:plural of <itna>; {ki-itnate} is love for one another) (b:itna) (q:draft)
itpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beloved/loved one/dear one) (d:<it>, love, with {-pa} for a man: the man whom someone loves) (b:it) (q:draft)
itpa = (i:2) (t:n) (w:the one who loves/lover) (d:<it>, love, with {-pa} for a man: the man who loves someone, as in {ei hong itpa}, he who loved us) (a:mudahpa) (b:it) (q:draft)
itpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dearest/most beloved/favourite) (d:<it>, love, with <pen>, most: the most loved, dearest) (b:it) (q:draft)
Ittai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ittai) (d:man from Gath who stayed loyal to David and commanded part of his army during the revolt of Absalom; also one of the mighty warriors of David, son of Ribai from Gibeah) (r:10.15.19/10.15.22) (q:draft)
itte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beloved/loved ones/dear friends) (d:those who are loved, as in {ka itte}, my beloved) (a:muhdahte) (b:it) (r:24.11.15/61.3.17) (q:draft)
itte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who love) (d:the ones who love someone, as in {kei hong itte}, those who love me) (a:mudahte) (b:it) (r:20.2.8) (q:draft)
itteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the loved ones/all the dear ones) (d:<it> love with <teng>, all; {a lawm itteng}, all his close friends) (b:it) (q:draft)
itthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to love) (d:<it> love with <thei>, be able) (b:it) (q:draft)
Iturea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Iturea) (d:region north-east of Galilee ruled by Philip the tetrarch) (r:42.3.1)
itzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:love more/prefer) (d:<it>, love, with <zaw>, more: love one more than another; the one compared takes <sang> or <sangin>, than) (s:deihzaw) (b:it) (q:draft)
itzawkna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:greater love/loving more) (d:<it> love with <zaw>, more, and the noun suffix <na>: the fact of loving one more than others) (q:draft)
itzawte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who love more) (d:<itzaw> love more with plural <te>, used with <sangin> than) (b:itzaw) (q:draft)
Ivvah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ivvah) (d:city conquered by Assyria, named with Hena and Sepharvaim in the boast of the king of Assyria) (r:12.19.13/23.37.13)
Iyeabarim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Iye Abarim) (d:camping place of the Israelites on the border of Moab, east of the Jordan) (r:4.33.44/4.21.11)
Iyim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Iyim/Iye Abarim) (d:short form of Iye Abarim, a camping place of the Israelites in Moab) (r:4.33.45)
Izhar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Izhar) (d:son of Kohath and grandson of Levi, father of Korah) (r:2.6.21/13.6.38)
Izip = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Egypt) (d:Egypt: a spelling of <Izipt> found in one verse) (q:draft)
Izipt = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Egypt) (d:land on the Nile where the Israelites were slaves until Moses led them out; in the list of nations also a son of Ham) (r:14.9.26)
Izipte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Egyptians) (d:<Izipt> with the plural <te>: the people of Egypt) (b:Izipt) (r:9.6.6)
Iziptpa = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Egyptian) (d:<Izipt> with <pa>, the suffix for a man: an Egyptian man) (b:Izipt) (r:44.7.24/10.23.21)
Iziptte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Egyptians) (d:<Izipt> with the plural <te>: the people of Egypt) (b:Izipt) (r:5.26.6/2.18.11)
Izliah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Izliah) (d:son of Elpaal in the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.18)
Izrah = (t:see) <Izrah-te>
Izrah-te = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Izrahite) (d:<Izrah> with the plural <te>: {Izrah-te beh} is of the Izrah clan, the Izrahite in the NIV, said of Shamhuth, an army commander of David) (q:draft)
Izrahiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Izrahiah) (d:son of Uzzi, a chief in the tribe of Issachar) (r:13.7.3)
Izri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Izri) (d:Levite musician in the time of David, leader of the fourth division of temple singers) (r:13.25.11)
Izziah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Izziah) (d:descendant of Parosh who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.25)
Izzri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Izri) (d:spelling of <Izri>, a Levite musician who led the fourth division of temple singers) (r:13.25.11)
Ja = (t:see) <Ja-azaniah>
Ja-akan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Akan/Jaakan) (d:son of Ezer, a descendant of Seir the Horite; called Akan in the NIV) (r:13.1.42) (q:draft)
Ja-akobath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jaakobah) (d:clan leader in the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.36) (q:draft)
Ja-ala = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jaala) (d:ancestor of a family of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (q:draft)
Ja-alah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jaala/Jaalah) (d:ancestor of a family of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (q:draft)
