Jaddai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jaddai) (d:descendant of Nebo who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.43)
Jaddua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jaddua) (d:name of two men: a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah, and a high priest, son of Jonathan) (r:16.12.11/16.10.21)
Jadon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jadon) (d:man of Meronoth who helped repair the wall of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.3.7)
Jael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Jael) (d:wife of Heber the Kenite, who killed Sisera, the army commander of King Jabin, in her tent) (r:7.4.17/7.5.24) (q:draft)
Jafeth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Japheth) (d:one of the three sons of Noah, brother of Shem and Ham) (r:1.6.10)
Jafethte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Japheth) (d:<Jafeth> with the plural <te>, closing the list of the sons of Noah: Shem, Ham and Japheth) (b:Jafeth) (r:1.10.1)
Jafia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Japhia) (d:name of a king of Lachish defeated by Joshua, and of a son of David born in Jerusalem) (r:6.10.3/13.3.7)
Jaflet = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Japhlet) (d:son of Heber in the tribe of Asher; {Jaflet mite} are the Japhletites, whose land lay on the border of the descendants of Joseph) (r:13.7.32)
Jagur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Jagur) (d:town in the far south of Judah, toward the border of Edom) (r:6.15.21)
Jahath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahath) (d:name of several men, most of them Levites, among them a son of Libni, descendant of Gershon) (r:13.4.2/13.6.43)
Jahaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Jahaz) (d:town east of the Jordan where Israel defeated Sihon king of the Amorites, later a Levite town in Reuben) (r:5.2.32/6.13.18)
Jahaziel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahaziel) (d:name of several men, among them a priest who blew the trumpet before the ark and a Levite, third son of Hebron) (r:13.24.23/13.16.6)
Jahdai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahdai) (d:man in the family line of Caleb in Judah, father of six sons) (r:13.2.47)
Jahdiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahdiel) (d:head of a family in the half-tribe of Manasseh, a brave warrior) (r:13.5.24)
Jahdo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahdo) (d:son of Buz, an ancestor in the tribe of Gad) (r:13.5.14)
Jahle = (t:see) <Jahle-el>
Jahle-el = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahleel) (d:a son of Zebulun, ancestor of the Jahleelite clan) (r:4.26.26) (q:draft)
Jahle-le = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahleel) (d:in {Jahle-le behte}, the Jahleelite clan; apparently a misprint of <Jahle-el>) (r:4.26.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
Jahleel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahleel) (d:son of Zebulun, ancestor of the Jahleelite clan) (r:1.46.14/4.26.26)
Jahmai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahmai) (d:son of Tola, head of a family in the tribe of Issachar) (r:13.7.2)
Jahzah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Jahzah) (d:town on the plateau of Moab east of the Jordan, given to the Levites from the tribe of Reuben; another form of <Jahaz>) (r:24.48.21/13.6.78)
Jahzarah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahzerah) (d:priest of the line of Immer, ancestor of Maasai) (r:13.9.12)
Jahze = (t:see) <Jahze-el>
Jahze-el = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahzeel/Jahziel) (d:first son of Naphtali, ancestor of the Jahzeelite clan; spelled Jahziel in the NIV in Genesis) (r:4.26.48) (q:draft)
Jahzeel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahzeel) (d:first son of Naphtali, ancestor of the Jahzeelite clan) (r:4.26.48)
Jahzeiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahzeiah) (d:son of Tikvah, one of the few who opposed the plan of Ezra about the foreign wives) (r:15.10.15)
Jahzerah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahzerah) (d:priest of the line of Immer, ancestor of Maasai) (r:13.9.12)
