jair = (t:see) <Havvoth-jair>
Jair = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jair) (d:name of several men, among them a descendant of Manasseh who held towns in Gilead, and a judge of Israel from Gilead) (r:7.10.5/4.32.41)
Jairas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jairus) (d:synagogue leader whose daughter Jesus raised from death) (r:41.5.22/42.8.41)
Jakah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Halak) (d:{Jakah Mual} is Mount Halak in the NIV, the mountain rising toward Seir at the southern limit of the conquests of Joshua) (r:6.12.7)
Jakan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jakan) (d:head of a family in the tribe of Gad) (r:13.5.13)
Jakeh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jakeh) (d:father of Agur, whose sayings are in Proverbs) (r:20.30.1)
Jakhin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jachin/Jakin) (d:name of a son of Simeon and of a priest; also the name of the southern bronze pillar of the temple of Solomon) (r:1.46.10/13.9.10)
Jakim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jakim) (d:name of a man of Benjamin, and of a priest to whom the twelfth division fell) (r:13.8.19/13.24.12)
jakinth = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:jacinth) (d:a precious stone, set in the third row of the breastpiece of the high priest; a loan word from the English Bible) (r:2.39.12) (q:draft)
Jakinth = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:jacinth) (d:<jakinth> written with a capital after a comma: a precious stone in the third row of the breastpiece) (b:jakinth) (q:draft)
