Kabze = (t:see) <Kabze-el>
Kabze-el = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kabzeel) (d:town in the far south of Judah near the border of Edom, home of Benaiah) (r:6.15.21) (q:draft)
Kabzeel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kabzeel) (d:town in the far south of Judah near the border of Edom, home of Benaiah) (r:6.15.21/10.23.20)
Kademah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kedemah) (d:youngest son of Ishmael) (r:1.25.15)
kadesh = (t:see) <Meribath-kadesh>
Kadesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kadesh) (d:place in the wilderness on the southern border of Canaan where Israel camped, also called Kadesh Barnea) (r:5.1.46/1.14.7)
Kadesh-barnea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kadesh Barnea) (d:place in the wilderness south of Canaan from which Moses sent men to look over the land) (r:4.32.8/6.10.41) (q:draft)
Kadeshbarnea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kadesh Barnea) (d:place in the wilderness south of Canaan from which Moses sent men to look over the land) (r:5.1.2/4.34.4)
Kadmiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kadmiel) (d:Levite who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel and helped lead the worship) (r:16.12.8/16.10.9)
Kadmon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/people) (w:Kadmonites) (d:one of the peoples whose land God promised to Abraham) (r:1.15.19)
Kaftor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/land) (w:Caphtorim/Caphtor/Caphtorites) (d:the land the Philistines came from, and its people, descended from Egypt; {Kaftor mite} are the Caphtorites) (r:1.10.14)
kah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weep/mourn/lament) (d:form of <kap>, weep, used before other words: {kah hun} is a time to weep, {kah la} is a lament song) (s:thuum) (a:nuih/nui) (r:21.3.4) (q:draft)
Kah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weep/lament) (d:<kah> written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and in <Kah La>, the Laments, a book of lament songs) (a:nuih) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kahbia = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:mongrel/of mixed descent) (d:of people, of mixed or illegitimate birth; {kahbia mite}) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahdan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:how to wail/way of weeping) (d:<kah> weep with <dan>, manner) (q:draft)
kahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:climbing/going up/mounting) (d:<kah>, climb or go up, with the linking ending {-in} before the next verb; also of taking the throne) (s:kahtoin) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kahin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:weeping/mourning) (d:<kah>, weep, with the linking ending {-in}) (s:kapin) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kahkahna = (t:see) <kahkahna-in>
kahkahna-in = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weeping/much weeping) (d:<kah>, form of <kap> weep, doubled for weeping that goes on, with the noun suffix <na> and the marker <in>; by or from continual weeping) (q:draft)
kahkawmin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:while weeping) (d:<kah> weep with <kawm>, while, and <in>) (q:draft)
kahkawmun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:while weeping) (d:<kah>, weep, with <kawm>, while, and <un> marking a plural subject: while they were weeping) (q:draft)
kahkhiato = (i:1) (t:v) (w:climb out/climb up) (d:<kah>, climb, with <khia>, out, and <to>, upward: climb up out of a pit or hole) (q:draft)
kahla = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lament/dirge/song of mourning) (d:<kah>, weep, with <la>, song: a song of mourning for the dead) (s:tamlawhna) (q:draft)
kahlei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stairs/steps/stairway) (d:a flight of steps, a stairway or ladder for going up; {kahlei cial} is a single step) (q:draft)
kahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weeping/crying/wailing) (d:<kah>, weep, with the noun suffix <na>: weeping or wailing; <kahna aw> is the sound of weeping) (s:thuumna) (a:nuihna/lungdamna) (b:kah) (r:40.13.50) (q:draft)
kahnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weeping/mourning) (d:plural of <kahna>) (b:kahna) (q:draft)
kahpihto = (t:see) <kahpihto-in>
kahpihto-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking up/carrying up) (d:<kah> climb with <pih>, together with, <to>, upward, and <in>: climbing up with someone) (s:kahtohpihin) (q:draft)
kahsiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:skilled at wailing) (d:<kah> weep with <siam>, skilful) (q:draft)
kahsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:descend/climb down/go down) (d:<kah> climb with <suk>, downward; {kahsuk kahto}, going down and going up) (s:kumsuk/paisuk) (a:kahto) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mourners/those who weep) (d:<kah> weep with the plural <te>; {misi kahte}, those who mourn the dead) (s:kapte) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kahtoh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go up/climb/ascend) (d:form of <kahto> used before endings such as <ciangin> and {lai takin}) (s:paitoh) (b:kahto) (r:49.4.9) (q:draft)
kahtohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ascent/way up/pass) (d:place where a road climbs, a slope or mountain pass) (s:paitohna) (b:kahtoh) (q:draft)
kahtohpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take up/bring up/lead up) (d:<kahtoh> go up, with <pih>, together with: go up with someone, take a person up to a high place) (b:kahtoh) (q:draft)
kahtohpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking up/bringing up) (d:<kahtohpih> take up, with <in>) (s:kahpihto-in) (b:kahtohpih) (q:draft)
kahtoin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:going up/rising) (d:<kahto> go up, with <in>) (b:kahto) (q:draft)
kahtokik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go back up/ascend again) (d:<kahto> go up, with <kik>, again or back) (b:kahto) (q:draft)
kahtosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have come up/make go up/take up) (d:<kahto> go up, with <sak>, cause: cause or let someone climb up, as into a chariot) (b:kahto) (q:draft)
kahzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weep more) (d:<kah> weep with <zaw>, more) (s:kapzaw) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kahzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to weep/weep for) (d:<kah> weep with <zo>, be able) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kai = (i:2) (t:v) (w:form/gather/come over) (d:of cloud, mist, dew, sweat or a rainbow: form, gather or settle; {meiipi kai} is clouds gather, {daitui kai} is dew falls, {khua-ul kai} is sweat breaks out) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kai = (t:see) <Kai-afas>
Kai-afas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Caiaphas) (d:high priest in Jerusalem at the time of the trial of Jesus, son-in-law of Annas) (r:43.11.49) (q:draft)
Kaiafas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Caiaphas) (d:high priest in Jerusalem at the time of the trial of Jesus, son-in-law of Annas) (r:40.26.57/40.26.3)
kaigawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pulling/pulling together) (d:<kai> pull with <gawm>, together, and <in>; of a new patch pulling on old cloth) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaigawpin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dragging/hauling off) (d:<kai> pull with <gawp>, roughly, and <in>) (q:draft)
kaih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:share/portion/due) (d:the part that a person regularly receives by right, as the priests' share of the offerings) (s:tanh) (q:draft)
kaih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:pull/draw/lead) (d:form of <kai> pull, draw, used before another word, as in {kaih khiat} draw or lead out and {a kaih leeng} the chariot they pull; {leh kaih} is pull back) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kaihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull out/drag out/lead out) (d:form of <kaikhia>, pull or lead out, used before words such as <hun>, <bang>, <khit> and <nading>) (b:kaih) (q:draft)
kaihkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pulling out/means of pulling out) (d:<kaihkhiat> pull out, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kaihkhiat) (q:draft)
kaihkhiatsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pulling off/taking off) (d:<kaihkhiat> pull out, with <sak>, for or from someone, and <in>; of a sandal taken off a man's foot) (b:kaihkhiat) (q:draft)
kaihkhiattoh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull up/bring up) (d:<kaihkhiat> pull out, with <toh>, upward) (b:kaihkhiat) (q:draft)
kaihkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/muster/bring together) (d:form of <kaikhawm> used before another word such as <hun>, <pawi>, <ciangin> or <kik>; {an kaihkhop pawi} is the Feast of Ingathering) (a:thehthang) (q:draft)
kaihkhopkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather again/bring back together) (d:<kaihkhop> gather, with <kik>, again) (s:kaikhawmkik) (b:kaihkhop) (q:draft)
kaihkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ingathering/gathering/gleaning) (d:<kaihkhop>, gather, with the noun suffix <na>: the gathering in of a crop; {kaihkhopna pawi} is the Feast of Ingathering) (b:kaihkhop) (q:draft)
kaihkhoppih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather with/help gather) (d:<kaihkhop> gather, with <pih>, together with: gather along with someone) (a:thehthang) (b:kaihkhop) (q:draft)
kaihkhopsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:gathered/accumulated/collected) (d:<kaihkhop> gather, with <sa>, already done: that has been gathered) (b:kaihkhop) (q:draft)
kaihkhopsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gathering in for/hauling in for) (d:<kaihkhop> gather, with <sak>, for someone, and <in>) (b:kaihkhop) (q:draft)
kaihkhopte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:collection/things gathered) (d:<kaihkhop> gather, with plural <te>: the things that have been gathered; {na milim kaihkhopte} is your collection of idols) (b:kaihkhop) (q:draft)
kaihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw back/bring back/reconcile) (d:<kaih> pull or draw, with <kik>, back) (b:kaih) (q:draft)
kaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pulling/drawing/ploughing) (d:<kaih> pull, with the noun suffix <na>; {lo kaihna kuak} is the furrow drawn in ploughing a field) (b:kaih) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaihnelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hedge in/block/surround) (d:with <ling> thorn, fence in or block the way with thorns) (q:draft)
kaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull/seize/grab) (d:<kaih> pull, with <sak>: take hold of and pull, as a dog by its ears) (b:kaih) (q:draft)
kaihte = (t:todo) (q:draft, in {khedap kaihte pia-in}, gave them sandals; what {kaihte} adds is not clear from the verse)
kaihzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:winning over/drawing to oneself) (d:<kaih> draw, with <zawh>, be able, and the noun suffix <na>; {lawma kaihzawhna}, being able to draw someone as a friend) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaii = (t:see) <kaii-in>
kaii-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forming/appearing) (d:of mist or cloud, forming and hanging; the same word as <kaai>, with <in>) (q:draft)
kaikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather/collect/assemble/bring together) (d:<kai>, draw, with <khawm>, together: bring people or things together in one place) (a:thehthang) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kaikhawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gathering/assembling/bringing together) (d:<kaikhawm> with <in>, gathering and then doing the next action) (b:kaikhawm) (q:draft)
kaikhawmkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather again/gather back) (d:<kaikhawm>, gather, with <kik>, again: bring back together those who were scattered) (s:kaihkhopkik) (b:kaikhawm) (q:draft)
kaikhawmpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who gathers/gatherer) (d:<kaikhawm> gather with <pa>, the man who does it) (b:kaikhawm) (r:47.8.14) (q:draft)
kaikhawmsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather/have gathered) (d:<kaikhawm> gather, with <sak>, cause: have people gathered together, as by sending messengers) (b:kaikhawm) (q:draft)
kaikhawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who gather/gatherers/collectors) (d:<kaikhawm>, gather, with plural {-te}: the people who gather or collect something) (b:kaikhawm) (q:draft)
kaikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull out/draw out/drag out/drag off) (d:<kai>, pull, with <khia>, out: pull, draw or drag someone or something out of a place) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kaikhiato = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull up/lift out/draw up) (d:<kaikhia>, pull out, with <to>, upward) (b:kaikhia) (q:draft)
kaikhop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather/assemble) (d:form of <kaikhawm> used before <khit>) (q:draft)
kaikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw back/pull back again) (d:<kai> pull with <kik>, again; {sila kaikik}, be brought back as a slave) (b:kai) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaikikpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring back at once/lead back shortly) (d:<kai> lead, with <kik>, back, and <pah>, immediately; of an animal led on a rope) (q:draft)
kain = (t:see) <Tubal-kain>
Kain = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cain) (d:eldest son of Adam and Eve, who killed his brother Abel) (r:1.4.1/1.4.6)
Kain = (i:2) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kain) (d:town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.57)
Kainan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cainan/Kenan) (d:name of two men in Luke’s genealogy of Jesus: a son of Arphaxad, and the son of Enosh, called Kenan in Genesis) (r:42.3.36)
kaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make form/bring over/set) (d:<kai>, of cloud form, with <sak>, cause: make clouds or a rainbow form or appear in the sky) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kaisak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:make pull/haul/drag) (d:cause to pull or to be pulled or led, as an ox with a plough, a catch in a net or a horse with its rider) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kaisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making rise/bringing up) (d:<kaisak>, cause clouds to form or rise, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kaisak) (q:draft)
kaisakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to make pull) (d:<kaisak> make pull, with <zo>, be able) (b:kaisak) (q:draft)
Kaisar = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Caesar) (d:Caesar, the title of the Roman emperor, usually written {Kaisar kumpipa}; Augustus and Tiberius are named in Luke) (r:42.2.1) (q:draft)
Kaisaria = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Caesarea) (d:name of two cities: Caesarea on the Mediterranean coast, seat of the Roman governor, and Caesarea Philippi near Mount Hermon) (r:44.10.1/40.16.13)
kaisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hang down/trail down) (d:<kai>, hang or trail, with <suk>, downward: hang down, as a curtain, a beard or braids of hair) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kaisuksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let run down/make hang down) (d:<kaisuk> hang down, with <sak>, cause; of saliva on the beard) (b:kaisuk) (q:draft)
kaisukte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hanging ones) (d:<kaisuk> hang down, with the plural <te>; {samphek kaisukte}, braids of hair that hang down) (b:kaisuk) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaite = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gathered/formed) (d:<kai>, of cloud gather or form, with <te> marking the ones that do so; {meiilum kaite}, the clouds that have gathered) (b:kai) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaito = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull up/draw up/lift up) (d:<kai>, pull, with <to>, upward: pull or lift up, as a person by the hand or a net out of the water) (s:kaikhiato) (a:khaisuk) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kaiton = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pull back/turn back/draw back) (d:in {kaiton kik}, pull back a hand that is stretched out; <kai> is pull) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kaivuan = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Kaivuan) (d:star god worshipped by Israel, named with Sakkuth in Amos 5:26; also written <Kaiwan>) (r:30.5.26)
Kaiwan = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Kaiwan) (d:star god worshipped by Israel, named with Sakkuth in Amos 5:26; also written <Kaivuan>) (r:30.5.26)
kaizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to pull/haul in) (d:<kai> pull with <zo>, be able) (b:kai) (q:draft)
kakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:comparing) (d:in {ki-en kakin}, looking at one another and comparing; the form is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
kal = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kidney) (d:one of the two kidneys of an animal, named among the parts burned on the altar) (r:3.4.9) (q:draft)
kal = (i:2) (t:n) (w:week) (d:week, always after <nipi>: {nipi kal khat} is one week, {nipi kal pawi} is the Festival of Weeks) (s:nipikal) (q:draft)
kal = (i:3) (t:n) (w:step/pace) (d:one stride in walking, also a step of a stairway or sundial) (q:draft)
kal = (i:4) (t:v) (w:demand/require) (d:claim what is owed or due, as a debt, a vow, tribute or obedience; the form before another word is <kalh>) (q:draft)
kala = (t:see) <kala-oh>
kala-oh = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:camel) (d:<kalaoh> written with a hyphen; {kala-oh mul}, camel's hair) (q:draft)
kalah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:on/along/in the course of) (d:in {lam kalah}, on the way, while on a journey; <kal> with the place marker <ah>) (b:kal) (q:draft)
Kalah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Calah) (d:city of Assyria built by Nimrod, near Nineveh) (r:1.10.11) (q:draft)
kalai = (i:1) (t:intj) (w:alas) (s:ala) (r:10.14.5) of expressing grief, pity, or concern
Kalai = (i:1) (t:intj) (w:alas) (d:<kalai>, a cry of grief or distress, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (s:ala) (b:kalai) (q:draft)
kalaoh = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:camel) (d:camel; {kalaoh vasa}, literally camel bird, is the ostrich) (r:15.2.67) (q:draft)
kalaoh-vasapi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ostrich/owl) (d:literally great camel bird; a bird of deserted places, owl in the NIV) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalaohnote = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young camels) (d:<kalaoh> camel with <no>, young, and the plural <te>) (q:draft)
kalaohte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:camels) (d:<kalaoh>, camel, with the plural <te>) (b:kalaoh) (r:38.14.15) (q:draft)
kalaote = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:camels) (d:<kalaoh> camel with the plural <te>, written without h) (q:draft)
Kaleb = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Caleb) (d:son of Jephunneh of the tribe of Judah, one of the twelve spies, who received Hebron; also a son of Hezron in the genealogy of Judah) (r:4.13.6/13.6.56)
kalh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lock/bolt/bar) (d:fasten a door or gate with a bolt, bar or key) (s:kalhcip) (a:hon) (q:draft)
kalh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:demand/require) (d:form of <kal>, demand, used before another word such as <nate> or <masak>) (b:kal) (q:draft)
kalhcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shut up/lock/lock tight) (d:<kalh> lock, with <cip>, tightly: lock or shut a door fast) (s:khakcip) (b:kalh) (q:draft)
kalhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:locking) (d:<kalh> lock, with <in>; {tawh kalhin}, locking with a key) (s:khakin) (b:kalh) (q:draft)
kalhkhapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breaking up/harrowing) (d:the breaking up of ploughed soil; {lei kalhkhapna singka} is the forked wood used for it, a harrow) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalhkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have locked/have already locked) (d:<kalh>, lock, with <khin>, already: have already locked, as a door shut for the night) (b:kalh) (q:draft)
kalhkhum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shut in/lock in/imprison) (d:<kalh>, lock, with <khum>, in: shut someone in so that he cannot get out) (s:khumcip) (q:draft)
kalhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bar/bolt/lock) (d:<kalh>, lock, with the noun suffix <na>: the bar or bolt that a door or gate is fastened with) (b:kalh) (r:16.3.6) (q:draft)
kalhna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:demand/insistent request) (d:<kalh>, demand, with the noun suffix <na>: an insistent demand for something) (b:kalh) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bolts/bars/locks) (d:<kalhna>, bar or bolt, with the plural <te>: the fastenings of a door or gate) (b:kalhna) (r:16.3.15) (q:draft)
kalhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have locked/have barred) (d:<kalh>, lock or bar, with the causative <sak>: have someone lock or bar a door) (b:kalh) (q:draft)
kalin = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:while/during) (d:during the time that: follows a verb or verbal noun, as {ihmut kalin}, while asleep, and {a theih loh kalin}, at a time one does not know) (s:laitakin/kawmin)
kalkakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:astride/straddling) (d:standing with the legs apart, one foot on each of two places, as the angel who stands on both the sea and the land) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalkawm = (i:1) (t:n) (w:navel) (d:a part of the body praised in the Song of Songs; the English versions have navel, the exact part is not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break up/plough up/till) (d:break up ground for sowing, used with <lei>, soil: {lei kalkham}) (q:draft)
kalkhamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:breaking up/ploughing up) (d:<kalkham>, break up soil, with the linking suffix <in>: breaking up the soil and going on to the next action) (b:kalkham) (q:draft)
kalkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reveal/uncover/bring out) (d:bring what is hidden out into the open) (s:kilangsak) (a:seel/seelcip) (q:draft)
Kalkol = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kalkol) (d:wise man named with Ethan, Heman and Darda, with whom the wisdom of Solomon is compared; listed as a son of Zerah of Judah) (r:13.2.6/11.4.31)
Kallai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kallai) (d:priest, head of the family of Sallu in the days of the high priest Joiakim) (r:16.12.20)
kallakah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:meanwhile/in the meantime) (d:in the time between, meanwhile; built from <kal>, interval, and used as {a kallakah}) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kalneh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Calneh/Kalneh) (d:city in Shinar in the kingdom of Nimrod; also a city named by Amos together with Hamath and Gath) (r:1.10.10/30.6.2)
Kalno = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kalno) (d:city conquered by the Assyrians, named together with Carchemish, Hamath and Arpad) (q:draft)
kalohte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:camels) (d:{kaloh}, a spelling of <kalaoh> camel, with plural <te>) (s:kalaohte/kalaote) (q:draft)
kalsagih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seven weeks) (d:<kal>, week, with <sagih>, seven: seven weeks, in {nipi kalsagih}) (q:draft)
kalsawm = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ten steps) (d:<kal>, step, with <sawm>, ten: the ten steps that the shadow moved on the sundial of Ahaz) (q:draft)
kalsuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:step/footstep/walk) (d:<kalsuan>, step, with the noun suffix <na>: a step, and so where and how a person goes) (s:khekhap) (r:18.14.16) (q:draft)
kalsuannate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:steps/footsteps) (d:<kalsuanna>, step, with the plural <te>: the steps a person takes, his course of life) (s:kalsuante/khekhapte) (b:kalsuanna) (q:draft)
kalsuante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:steps) (d:<kalsuan>, step, with the plural <te>: the steps a person takes) (s:kalsuannate/khekhapte) (b:kalsuan) (q:draft)
kaltangnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:willful sins/presumptuous sins) (d:in {mawh kaltangnate}, sins done willfully or presumptuously; <kaltang> with the noun suffix <na> and plural <te>, the meaning of <kaltang> alone is not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kidneys) (d:<kal>, kidney, with the plural <te>: the kidneys of an animal offered in sacrifice) (b:kal) (q:draft)
kalte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:weeks) (d:<kal>, week, with the plural <te>: weeks, as in {Nipi kalte’ pawi}, the Festival of Weeks) (s:nipikalte) (b:kal) (q:draft)
kalteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the whole time/all the while) (d:<kal>, the interval between, with <teng>, all: for as long as) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalthau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kidney fat) (d:<kal>, kidney, with <thau>, fat: the fat around the kidneys of an animal) (q:draft)
kalthum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:three weeks) (d:<kal>, week, with <thum>, three: three weeks, in {nipi kalthum}) (q:draft)
kalun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:while/during) (d:<kal>, interval of time, with the ending <un>, after a verb: while something is going on; {a phawk loh kalun} means while they are unaware, by surprise) (s:laitakin/kawmin) (q:draft)
kam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mouth) (d:the mouth, and so what one says, speech or word; it forms many compounds such as <kamsia>, <kamhoih> and <kammal>) (r:20.16.23)
kam = (i:2) (t:n) (w:void)
kama = (i:1) (t:n) (w:by mouth/in words/of the mouth) (d:<kam>, mouth, with the ending <a>, in or of: by word of mouth, in spoken words) (b:kam) (q:draft)
kamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the mouth/to the mouth) (d:<kam>, mouth, with the place marker <ah>: in or to the mouth) (b:kam) (q:draft)
kamciam = (i:2) (t:v) (w:promise/pledge) (d:give a promise or pledge by word of mouth; <kam>, mouth, with <ciam>, promise) (s:thuciam/kiciam/ciam) (q:draft)
kamciamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:promising/pledging) (d:<kamciam>, promise, with the linking suffix <in>: promising and then going on to the next action) (b:kamciam) (q:draft)
kamciamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promise/oath/word) (d:<kamciam>, promise, with the noun suffix <na>: a promise or oath given by word of mouth) (s:thuciam/kiciamna) (b:kamciam) (q:draft)
kamciamnasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promise already given) (d:<kamciamna>, promise, with <sa>, already done: a promise already given) (b:kamciamna) (q:draft)
kamciamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promises/pledges) (d:<kamciamna>, promise, with the plural <te>: pledges by which a person binds himself) (s:thuciamnate) (b:kamciamna) (q:draft)
kamciamsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:promised/vowed/pledged) (d:<kamciam>, promise, with <sa>, already done: what has been promised or vowed) (b:kamciam) (q:draft)
kamdawn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rumour/report) (d:news that is passed on by word of mouth) (s:kamlengsawn/thuzak) (q:draft)
kamgen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:word/saying) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <gen>, say: what someone has said; {kamgen bangin} is according to the word of) (s:kammal) (q:draft)
kamgenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:word/saying/command) (d:<kamgen> with the noun suffix <na>: what has been spoken) (b:kamgen) (q:draft)
kamgente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/word) (d:<kamgen> with plural <te>: the things a person has said) (s:kammalte/thugente) (b:kamgen) (q:draft)
kamging = (i:1) (t:n) (w:voice) (d:the sound of someone speaking; <kam>, mouth, with <ging>, sound) (s:awging)
Kamging = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/voice) (d:<kamging>, the sound of the voice, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {kamging mawkmawk}, mere words) (b:kamging) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamgingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/voices/sound of words) (d:<kamging> voice, with the plural <te>) (b:kamging) (q:draft)
kamguh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bad language/unwholesome talk/rash words) (d:speech that is harmful or that should not have been said) (s:kamsia/pausia) (a:kamhoih) (q:draft)
kamhanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:big talk/boasting) (d:boastful talk, bragging about what one will do) (s:kisialhna) (q:draft)
kamhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good word/kind word/favorable answer) (d:<kam>, word, with <hoih>, good: a good or kind word, used with <pau>, speak) (a:kamsia) (q:draft)
kamhoihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good words/sound speech) (d:<kamhoih> good word, with the plural <te>) (b:kamhoih) (q:draft)
kamin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the language/by word/with the mouth) (d:<kam> mouth, speech, with the marker <in>: in a language, as {Hebru kamin} in Hebrew, or by a spoken word) (b:kam) (q:draft)
kamka = (i:1) (t:v) (w:open the mouth/gape) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <ka>, open wide: open the mouth to eat or to speak; in Job 6:20 stand gaping at a loss) (q:draft)
kamkaih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bridle/bit) (d:the bit and reins by which a horse or donkey is controlled) (s:kamkaihna) (q:draft)
kamkaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bridle/bit) (d:<kamkaih> bridle, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kamkaih) (q:draft)
kamkat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gape/open the mouth wide) (d:form of <kamka>, <kam> mouth with <ka> open; open the mouth wide at someone in threat or mockery) (b:kamka) (r:19.35.21) (q:draft)
kamkei = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:leopard) (d:a large spotted wild cat, known for its speed) (r:27.7.6) (q:draft)
kamkeite = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:leopards) (d:<kamkei> leopard, with plural <te>) (b:kamkei) (q:draft)
kamkhapte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vows/promises) (d:<kam> word with <khap> pledge and plural <te>: promises made by word of mouth, here vows made to God) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one word/a single word) (d:<kam>, word, with <khat>, one; {kamkhat beek} with a negative verb means not even one word) (q:draft)
kamkhat = (i:2) (t:n) (w:mouthful/morsel/bite) (d:one mouthful of food, as in {khomun kamkhat}, a piece of bread) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamkhauh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:harsh word/harsh speech/bitterness) (d:<kam>, mouth or word, with <khauh>, hard: harsh or bitter speech) (a:kamneem/kamkhum) (q:draft)
kamkhum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sweet words/gentle speech/smooth talk) (d:<kam>, word, with <khum>, sweet: kind or soothing speech, and in a bad sense flattering talk; {kamkhum takin pau} is speak tenderly) (s:kamneel/kamneem) (a:kamkhauh/kamsia) (q:draft)
kamkumin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:plotting/conferring) (d:talking a matter over together; {kamkumin vai hawm}, lay plans by talking together) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamlengsawn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rumour/report) (d:news passed on by word of mouth) (s:kamdawn/thuzak) (q:draft)
kammalte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words) (d:<kammal>, word, with the plural <te>) (s:thugente/kampaute) (b:kammal) (q:draft)
kamneel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:smooth talk/flattering words) (d:<kam>, word, with <neel>, smooth: smooth talk meant to win someone over) (s:kamzol) (q:draft)
kamneem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gentle words/kind words) (d:<kam>, word, with <neem>, soft: gentle or kind words; {kamneem pau} is speak kindly) (s:kamkhum) (a:kamkhauh) (q:draft)
kamnem = (t:see) <kamnem-a>
kamnem-a = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:gently/with gentle words) (d:<kamnem> gentle word, with <a>; {kamnem-a pauna}, gentle speaking) (q:draft)
Kamon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kamon) (d:place in Gilead where the judge Jair was buried) (r:7.10.5)
kampauna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:speech/words/talk) (d:<kampau>, speech, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of speaking or what a person says; the English versions often have lips, mouth or tongue) (s:pauna) (b:kampau) (r:12.2.22) (q:draft)
kampaunate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/speech/utterances) (d:<kampauna>, speech, with the plural <te>: the things a person says; the English versions often have lips) (s:kampaute/kammalte) (b:kampauna) (q:draft)
kampaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/sayings/speech) (d:<kampau>, speech, with the plural <te>: the things a person says) (s:kammalte/kampaunate/thugente) (b:kampau) (q:draft)
kamphen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:interpreter) (d:one who puts the speech of one language into another) (q:draft)
kampi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lips/mouth/mere words) (d:in {a kampi bek}, with the mouth only: words spoken without the heart behind them) (b:kam) (r:28.10.4) (q:draft)
kamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:satisfy) (d:in {na hukna teng na kamsak hi}, you satisfied all your lust; perhaps for <khamsak>, make full) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prophesy) (d:form of <kamsang> written with a final apostrophe before <ding> or the ending {-na}: speak a message from God; with {-na} it means prophecy or prophesying) (s:genkhol) (q:draft)
kamsang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prophesy) (d:speak a message from God; the same word is also the noun prophet, as in {kamsang Haggai}, the prophet Haggai) (s:genkhol)
Kamsang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophet) (d:<kamsang> written with a capital as a title before a name, the prophet) (s:kamsangpa) (b:kamsang) (r:14.32.32) (q:draft)
Kamsanga = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seer/prophet) (d:<Kamsang> prophet with the ending <a>, as; {Kamsanga kineipa} is one who makes himself out to be a prophet) (b:Kamsang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsangin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as a prophet) (d:<kamsang>, prophet, with the suffix {-in}, as; {kamsangin om}, act as a prophet, prophesy) (b:kamsang) (q:draft)
kamsangna = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prophesy)
kamsangnu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophetess/woman prophet) (d:<kamsang>, prophet, with {-nu} marking a woman) (b:kamsang) (q:draft)
kamsangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophet) (d:<kamsang>, prophet, with <pa> marking a man: a man who speaks messages from God) (b:kamsang) (r:24.37.6)
Kamsangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophet) (d:<kamsangpa> written with a capital, the Prophet; <pa> marks a man) (b:kamsangpa) (q:draft)
kamsangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophets) (d:<kamsang>, prophet, with the plural <te>) (b:kamsang) (r:46.14.32) (q:draft)
