kamsia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil speech/harsh words/bad language) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <sia>, bad: evil or hurtful speech) (s:kamguh/pausia) (a:kamhoih/kamkhum) (q:draft)
kamsia = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:unfortunate/unlucky/wretched) (d:having bad fortune, in a wretched state; used in a cry of misery, woe is me) (s:tuahsia) (a:hampha) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsiam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:smooth talk/fine words/compliment) (d:<kam> mouth with <siam> skilled; pleasant or skilful speech, and as a verb speak kindly to or greet) (s:kamkhum/kamzol) (q:draft)
kamsiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eloquence/gracious speech) (d:<kamsiam>, skilled in speech, with the noun suffix <na>: eloquent or gracious speech) (b:kamsiam) (q:draft)
kamsiat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disaster/misfortune/calamity) (d:form of <kamsia>, unfortunate, used before a noun; {kamsiat ni}, the day of disaster) (s:tuahsiatna/kamsiatna) (b:kamsia) (q:draft)
kamsiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:coarse talk/bad words/foul language) (d:<kamsia>, evil or foul speech, with the plural <te>: coarse or indecent talk) (b:kamsia) (q:draft)
kamsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:misfortune/hardship/adversity) (d:trouble or ill fortune that befalls someone; {kamsiatna tuak} is meet with misfortune, and {kamsiatna thuak tahen} is a curse on someone) (s:tuahsiatna/haksatna/gentheihna) (a:daupaina) (b:kamsiat) (q:draft)
kamsiatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:afflictions/misfortunes/hardships) (d:<kamsiatna>, misfortune, with the plural <te>: the troubles a person goes through) (s:tuahsiatnate/haksatnate) (a:daupainate) (b:kamsiatna) (q:draft)
kamsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mouth/inside of the mouth) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <sung>, inside: the inside of the mouth; {kamsung panin} is out of the mouth) (s:kam) (r:66.19.21) (q:draft)
kamtai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:messenger/envoy) (d:one sent to carry a message, a messenger or envoy; {kamtai sawl} is send a messenger) (s:taangmi/palai/laitai) (r:20.13.17) (q:draft)
kamtaipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:messenger) (d:<kamtai>, messenger, with <pa>, the man: the man sent with a message) (s:taangmi) (b:kamtai) (q:draft)
kamtaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:messengers/envoys) (d:<kamtai>, messenger, with the plural <te>; {kamtaite sawl} is send messengers) (s:tangmite/taangmite/laitaite) (b:kamtai) (q:draft)
kamtam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:talkative/loud/noisy) (d:<kam>, mouth or word, with <tam>, many: given to much or noisy talk; {kamtam sak} is make someone loud) (a:dai) (q:draft)
kamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/talk) (d:<kam>, word, with the plural <te>: things said, as in {muhdahna kamte}, words of hatred, and {a mawkna kamte}, empty talk) (s:kammalte/thute) (b:kam) (q:draft)
kamte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:languages/tongues) (d:<kam>, speech, with the plural <te>: the languages spoken by different peoples, and the tongues spoken in the church) (s:paute) (b:kam) (q:draft)
kamthakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in new tongues/in a new language) (d:<kam>, speech, with <thak>, new, and the adverb suffix <in>: speaking in a language new to the speaker) (q:draft)
kamtuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tongues/other language/strange tongue) (d:<kam>, speech, with <tuam>, different: a language not one's own, the speaking in tongues of the New Testament; {kamtuam tawh pau} is speak in tongues) (s:pautuam/paudang) (q:draft)
kamun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mouth) (d:<kam>, mouth, apparently with the plural marker <un>: their mouths, what they say) (b:kam) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamzol = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flattery/flattering words/smooth talk) (d:<kam>, word, with <zol>, persuade: pleasant words used to win someone over or deceive) (s:kamsiam/kamneel/thuzol/mawkphatna) (q:draft)
kan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:search/look for) (d:look for someone or something that is lost or wanted, or look closely into a matter) (s:zon)
kan = (i:2) (t:v) (w:explore) (d:look into something thoroughly in order to understand it) (s:kansim)
kan = (i:3) (t:v) (w:ask) (d:ask or inquire about a matter, often as {thu kan}; {Topa kiangah thu kan} is inquire of the Lord) (s:dong/dot/thukan) (a:dawng)
Kana = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Cana) (d:town in Galilee where Jesus turned water into wine at a wedding) (r:43.2.1) (q:draft)
Kanaan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Canaan) (d:son of Ham and grandson of Noah, ancestor of the Canaanites) (r:1.10.15/13.1.13)
Kanah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Kanah) (d:ravine with a stream on the border between Ephraim and Manasseh, running west to the Mediterranean Sea) (r:6.16.8) (q:draft)
Kanah = (i:2) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kanah) (d:town on the border of the territory of Asher, in the direction of Sidon) (r:6.19.28) (q:draft)
kancip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bind fast/entangle/coil around) (d:of cords, wind around someone and hold tight; <cip> adds the sense of tightly) (s:hencip/gakcip) (q:draft)
Kandake = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Kandake) (d:title of the queen of the Ethiopians, whose treasury official was baptized by Philip) (r:44.8.27)
Kandeis = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Kandake) (d:another spelling of <Kandake>, the title of the queen of the Ethiopians) (r:44.8.27)
kang = (i:2) (t:v) (w:burn/scorch/consume) (d:be burned or scorched by fire; of fire, burn something up) (s:kat/kuang) (q:draft)
kang = (i:3) (t:v) (w:dry up/stop flowing) (d:of water, tears or a flow of blood, dry up or stop flowing) (s:keu) (q:draft)
kangcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dry up/run dry) (d:<kang>, dry up, with <cip>, completely: of streams, rivers and the sea, run completely dry) (s:keucip/keutum) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangcipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drying up/running dry) (d:<kangcip>, dry up completely, with the linking suffix <in>: drying right up) (b:kangcip) (q:draft)
kangcipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dry up/make run dry) (d:<kangcip>, dry up completely, with <sak>, cause: make a river or the sea dry right up) (s:keutumsak/kangsak/keusak) (b:kangcip) (q:draft)
kanggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scorch/sear/burn badly) (d:<kang>, burn, with <gawp>, severely: of the sun or great heat, scorch people badly) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kanghul = (i:1) (t:v) (w:singe/be singed) (d:of hair, be singed or slightly burned by fire) (q:draft)
kangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burning/blazing) (d:<kang>, burn, with the linking suffix <in>, joining it to the next verb: burning, on fire) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangin = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:white/turned white) (d:<kang>, white, with the linking suffix <in>: being or turning white, said of hair or of skin) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangin = (i:3) (t:v) (w:rising/going up) (d:<kang>, rise, with <in> joining it to the next verb) (q:draft, low confidence)
kangkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scorch/burn) (d:<kang> burn, with <kha>, happen to touch: of heat, strike and scorch someone) (q:draft)
kanglum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn to death/consume) (d:<kang> burn, with <lum>, to death: of fire, kill by burning) (q:draft)
kangpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dry up at once/stop at once) (d:<kang> dry up or stop flowing, with <pah>, immediately: said of a flow of blood) (s:khawlpah) (q:draft)
kangsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:white) (d:<kang>, white, with <sa>, already: that which is already white, said of hair) (a:vom) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dry up/make dry) (d:<kang>, dry up, with <sak>, cause: make water or moisture dry up) (s:keusak/kansak) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:burn/set on fire) (d:<kang>, burn, with <sak>, cause: set something on fire so that it burns) (s:halsak/kuangsak) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turning white/making white) (d:<kang> white, with <sak> cause and the connective <in>: making something white, as a skin disease does the hair) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who started the fire) (d:<kangsak> cause to burn, with <pa>, the man who: the man who set something on fire) (b:kangsak) (q:draft)
kangsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gray-haired people/white-haired people) (d:<kangsa> already white, with plural <te>; with <sam> hair, those whose hair is white, the aged) (b:kangsa) (q:draft)
kangtakin = (t:todo) (q:draft, one verse, Job 21:33, where the NIV line does not match the Tedim wording; meaning of <kang> with <takin> here not clear)
kangte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:white/gray) (d:<kang>, white, with the plural <te>, after a noun: {sakol kangte} is white horses, and {sam kangte} is gray hair and so the aged) (a:vomte) (b:kang) (q:draft)
kangto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rise up/lift up) (d:<kang>, rise into the air, with <to>, upward) (q:draft)
kangtum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consume/burn up) (d:<kang>, burn, with <tum>, completely: of fire, burn something up until nothing is left) (s:kattum/haltum/netum) (r:58.12.29) (q:draft)
kangtumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burning up/consuming) (d:<kangtum>, burn up, with the linking suffix <in>: burning something up and going on to the next action) (s:haltumin) (b:kangtum) (q:draft)
kangtummang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn up/consume/burn completely) (d:<kang>, burn, with <tum>, wholly, and <mang>, away: be burned up, or of fire, burn something until nothing is left) (s:kangtum/kattum) (q:draft)
kangtumsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:burned/burned up) (d:<kangtum>, burn up, with <sa>, already done: already burned up) (s:kattumsa) (b:kangtum) (q:draft)
kangtumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn up/consume) (d:<kangtum>, burn up, with <sak>, cause: make something burn up completely, set it on fire and destroy it) (s:haltum/kattumsak) (b:kangtum) (q:draft)
kangtumsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burning up/burning away) (d:<kangtumsak>, burn up, with the linking suffix <in>: said of a refiner burning away the dross) (s:haltumin) (b:kangtumsak) (q:draft)
kangtumthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:able to burn up/scorching) (d:<kangtum> burn up completely, with <thei>, can: able to consume, said of a fire) (b:kangtum) (q:draft)
kangvute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ashes) (d:ashes left from something burnt, here of a heifer; apparently <kang> burn with <vut> ashes and plural <te>) (s:vutte/vute) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:searching/investigating/seeking out) (d:<kan>, search, with the linking suffix <in>: searching or inquiring into something and then going on to the next action) (s:entelin) (b:kan) (q:draft)
kankan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:search out/investigate/ponder/study) (d:<kan>, search or examine, doubled to show continued careful searching) (s:kantel) (q:draft)
kankan = (i:2) (t:adv) (d:follows <liing>, tremble, to picture continued shaking: {liing kankan}, trembling all over) (q:draft, low confidence)
kankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:search out/find out) (d:<kan>, search, with <khia>, out: search a matter through until it is found out) (s:theikhia/kantel) (b:kan) (q:draft)
kankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:find out/search out/sound out) (d:form of <kankhia>, find out, used before {khit ciangin} and similar words) (s:theihkhiat) (b:kankhia) (q:draft)
kankhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:investigation/inquiry) (d:<kankhiat> search out, with the noun suffix <na>: the finding out of a matter) (s:thukanna/kanna) (b:kankhiat) (q:draft)
kankik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come for again/look for again) (d:<kan> search or look for, with <kik>, again or back: seek out again in order to bring back) (s:zongkik) (b:kan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanlai = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how much more/all the more) (d:placed after a verb phrase: even more so) (s:zawkan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:apparently <kan>, a form of <kang> be white, with <lam>, the fact that: that the hair has turned white or gray) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inquiry/investigation/examination) (d:<kan>, search or inquire, with the noun suffix <na>: {thu kanna} is the looking into a matter) (s:thukanna/kankhiatna/thudotna) (b:kan) (q:draft)
kanna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:transgression/breaking) (d:<kan>, cross over or break, with the noun suffix <na>: {thukham kanna} is the breaking of the law) (s:palsatna/thupalsatna) (a:zuihna) (q:draft)
Kanneh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kanneh) (d:city in Mesopotamia that traded with Tyre, named together with Harran and Eden) (r:26.27.23)
kansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dry up/make dry) (d:make water dry up; another spelling of <kangsak>) (s:kangsak/keusak) (q:draft)
kansak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:have someone inquire/have looked into) (d:<kan>, ask or search, with <sak>, cause: have someone find out about a matter) (b:kan) (q:draft)
kansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drying up) (d:<kansak> dry up, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of drying up water, how it was dried up) (b:kansak) (q:draft)
kansim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spy out/investigate secretly) (d:find out about a place or a matter in secret, often as {thu kansim}) (s:ensim/thukansim/vaan) (q:draft)
kansimte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spies) (d:<kansim> spy out, with plural <te>: those who spy out, in {thu kansimte}) (s:thukante/vaante) (b:kansim) (q:draft)
kantan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cross/pass through/pass over) (d:go from one side to the other of a river, a sea, a valley or a land) (s:galkah/paltan) (q:draft)
kantanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:across) (d:<kantan>, cross, with the linking suffix <in>: going across or through to the other side) (b:kantan)
kantanin = (i:2) (t:prep) (w:covering) (d:stretching from one side to the other of something, across its front)
kantanin = (i:3) (t:v) (w:fly) (d:said of birds crossing the sky in flight)
kantansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let pass through/lead across/bring through) (d:<kantan>, cross, with the causative <sak>: let someone pass through a land, or bring someone across) (b:kantan) (q:draft)
kantanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to cross/get across/pass through) (d:<kantan>, cross, with <zo>, be able: manage to get across or through) (b:kantan) (q:draft)
kante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spies/investigators) (d:<kan>, search, with the plural <te>: in {thusim kante}, those who search out matters in secret) (s:kansimte/thukante/vaante) (b:kan) (q:draft)
kante = (i:2) (t:n) (w:roasted grain/parched grain) (d:in {an kante}, grain that has been roasted; {an kan} is roasted grain) (s:ankante) (q:draft, low confidence)
kantel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:examine/search out/investigate) (d:inquire into a matter thoroughly until it is clear) (s:entel/thukan/kankan) (q:draft)
kantelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:investigating/going into in detail) (d:<kantel> examine thoroughly, with the linking suffix <in>: looking closely into) (s:entelin) (b:kantel) (q:draft)
kanzaw = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:even more/exceedingly/surpassing) (d:beyond the usual measure; after a verb, all the more, and {a kanzaw siamna} is an outstanding skill) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leap over/scale/get over) (d:<kan>, cross over, with <zo>, be able: manage to get over a wall) (q:draft)
kap = (i:2) (t:v) (w:shoot) (d:shoot with a bow and arrow, as in {thal tawh kap}, shoot with the bow) (q:draft)
Kapernaum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Capernaum) (d:town on the north shore of the Sea of Galilee where Jesus lived and taught) (r:42.4.31/40.4.13)
kapgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shoot/shoot down) (d:<kap> shoot, with <gawp>, severely: shoot so as to wound badly) (b:kap) (q:draft)
kapia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give/add) (d:in {kapia beh}, be given in addition to; the subject is not first person, so possibly a misprint for <kipia>, be given) (b:pia) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weeping/crying/wailing/mourning) (d:<kap>, weep, with the linking suffix <in>: weeping while doing something else) (s:kahin/thuumin) (b:kap) (q:draft)
