kapkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:split/cleave) (d:said of lightning splitting the earth) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weep aloud/cry out/burst into tears) (d:<kap>, weep, with <khia>, out: break out in weeping; often {a gingin kapkhia}, weep aloud) (b:kap) (q:draft)
kaplet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pierce/shoot through) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <let>, through: shoot with an arrow so that it goes through) (q:draft)
kaplum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shoot dead/kill by shooting) (d:<kap> shoot, with <lum>, to death) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shooting) (d:<kap> shoot, with the noun suffix <na>; {hong kapna thaltang} is the arrows shot at us) (b:kap) (q:draft)
kappa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shooter/archer) (d:<kap> shoot, with <pa>, the man who: the man who shoots arrows) (s:thaltawipa) (b:kap) (q:draft)
Kappadokia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Cappadocia) (d:Roman province in the east of Asia Minor, home of Jews present at Pentecost and of Christians to whom Peter wrote) (r:44.2.9/60.1.2)
Kappadosia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Cappadocia) (d:another spelling of <Kappadokia>, a Roman province in the east of Asia Minor) (r:44.2.9/60.1.1)
kapsa = (t:see) <kapsa-in>
kapsa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:weeping/in tears/mourning) (d:<kap>, weep, with <sa> and the suffix <in>: in a state of weeping, still weeping while doing something else) (q:draft)
