kapsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weep in secret/weep secretly) (d:<kap>, weep, with <sim>, in secret: weep where no one sees) (q:draft)
kapsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:beat down on/shine down on) (d:<kap> shoot, with <suk>, downward: of the sun, strike down on someone with its heat) (b:kap) (q:draft)
kapte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who weep/mourners) (d:<kap>, weep, with the plural <te>, used after <a>: {a kapte}, those who weep or mourn) (s:kahte/dahte) (a:lungdamte) (b:kap) (q:draft)
kapte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who shoot/shooters) (d:<kap>, shoot, with the plural <te>, used after <a>: those who shoot arrows at someone) (b:kap) (q:draft)
kaptuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pierce/hit/strike) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <tuk>: of an arrow or the one who shoots, hit and pierce the one aimed at) (q:draft)
kapzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weep rather/weep more) (d:<kap>, weep, with <zaw>, more or rather: weep for one person rather than for another) (s:kahzaw) (b:kap) (q:draft)
Kar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Carites) (d:the Carites, soldiers who served as guards of the royal house of Judah in the time of the priest Jehoiada; used in the phrase {Kar mite}) (r:12.11.19) (q:draft)
karbankal = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:carbuncle) (d:a precious stone, from English carbuncle, also written <karbankel>; the NIV has beryl in this place) (s:karbankel) (r:2.28.17) (q:draft)
