Kasifia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kasiphia) (d:place in Babylonia where Iddo was leader of the Levites and temple servants, to which Ezra sent for attendants) (r:15.8.17)
Kasluh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Casluhim/Kasluhites) (d:the Kasluhites, a people descended from Egypt, from whom the Philistines came; used in the phrase {Kasluh mite}) (r:1.10.14)
kat = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:sulfur/brimstone) (d:sulfur, the yellow mineral that burns, named together with <mei>, fire, in scenes of judgment; also written <kaat>) (s:kaat) (q:draft)
kat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:burn/consume/burn up) (d:said of fire, burn something or burn it up; also be on fire, and in 1 Corinthians 7:9 burn with desire) (s:kang/kattum) (r:38.11.1) (q:draft)
kat = (i:3) (t:v) (w:be split/be divided) (d:form of <ka>, be split, used before <hangin>: said of a hoof that is cloven, as in {khecin a kat hangin}, though its hoof is divided) (q:draft)
kate = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<ka>, be split or forked, with plural <te>: {khecin kate} are the animals whose hoof is divided) (b:ka) (q:draft)
