kausan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wither/dry up) (d:of green growth, wither and turn dry and brown; said of Mount Carmel in a time of drought) (s:vul/keu) (q:draft)
kausansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blight/wither/strike with mildew) (d:<kausan> wither, with <sak>, cause: make crops wither) (s:keusak) (b:kausan) (q:draft)
kawbia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shovel) (d:a tool named with {tu-ka} among the altar utensils and for tossing fodder; which of the two is the shovel and which the fork is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
kawbiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shovels) (d:plural of <kawbia>: the shovels among the bronze utensils of the altar) (b:kawbia) (q:draft)
kawciik = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:narrow) (d:narrow, of a gate or door that is hard to enter; set against <tanzau>, wide; also written <kawcik>) (s:kawcik) (a:tanzau/zai) (q:draft)
kawcik = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:narrow) (d:narrow, with little room, of a path, a gate or a place; also said of a heart that holds back its affection) (s:kawciik) (a:tanzau/zai) (q:draft)
