kek = (i:3) (t:n) (w:thunderstorm/thunderbolt) (d:seen once, in a phrase for the path of the thunderstorm) (s:keek) (q:draft, low confidence)
keksa = (t:see) <keksa-in>
keksa-in = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:torn) (d:<kek> torn, with <sa>, already, and the linking suffix <in>: with clothes torn, said of men who fled stripped and beaten) (s:balkeksa) (q:draft)
kekseu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rust/corrode/decay) (d:be eaten away by rust or decay, said of stored goods and of gold and silver) (s:keekseu) (q:draft, low confidence)
