Kel = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:goat) (d:{kel} written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {kel hon} is a flock of goats and <keltal> a he-goat) (s:keel) (q:draft)
Kelaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kelaiah) (d:Levite, also called Kelita, who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.23)
Kelita = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kelita) (d:Levite, also called Kelaiah, who helped explain the Law to the people and sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.8.7/16.10.10)
Kelite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kelita) (d:spelling of <Kelita>, the other name of the Levite Kelaiah, in Ezra 10:23) (r:15.10.23)
