kem = (i:2) (t:v) (w:store/place) (d:keep a thing by one, hold it in store or have it in one's charge) (s:khol)
Kem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep/watch over/guard) (d:<kem> written with a capital when it is said of God; {hong Kem pa}, the one who keeps you, stands for Overseer in 1 Peter 2:25) (b:kem) (q:draft)
