kemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep/tend/look after) (d:form of <kem> with the linking suffix <in>, keeping or tending and then going on to the next action) (b:kem) (q:draft)
kemnu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nurse/attendant) (d:a woman who looks after someone; <kem> look after, with <nu> for a woman) (s:cingnu) (b:kem) (q:draft)
kempa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:keeper/guardian/warden) (d:<kem> keep, with <pa> marking a man: one who keeps, guards or looks after; {thong kempa} is a prison warden) (s:keempa/cingpa/hongpa) (b:kem) (q:draft)
kemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:entrust/put in the care of/have guarded) (d:<kem> keep with the causative <sak>: give someone a person or thing to look after) (s:keemsak/kepsak/cingsak) (b:kem) (q:draft)
kemsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep for oneself/keep for good) (d:<kem> keep, with <suak>: hold on to a thing and not give it back) (q:draft)
kemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:keepers/guardians/stewards) (d:<kem> keep with the plural <te>, after <a>: those who look after or are in charge of) (s:keemte/cingte) (b:kem) (q:draft)
Kemuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kemuel) (d:name of three men: a son of Nahor and father of Aram, a leader of Ephraim who helped divide the land, and the father of the Levite Hashabiah) (r:1.22.21/4.34.24)
Ken = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Kenite/Kenites) (d:the Kenites, a people of the south related to Moses by marriage; {Ken mi} is a Kenite and {Ken mite} the Kenites) (r:9.30.29) (q:draft)
Ken = (i:2) (t:n) (w:cliff/precipice) (d:<ken> written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {Ken pang-a} means on the side of a cliff) (s:keen/kensang) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kenan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenan) (d:son of Enosh and father of Mahalalel in the line from Adam to Noah) (r:1.5.12)
