kenkanzo = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:quietly/patiently) (d:<kenkan> quietly, with <zo>, be able: in {ngak kenkanzo}, be able to wait quietly) (b:kenkan) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kenkhrea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Cenchreae) (d:port town east of Corinth, where Paul had his hair cut because of a vow and where Phoebe served the church) (r:45.16.1/44.18.18)
kenkon = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:patiently/persistently) (d:expressive word after a verb: go on doing it with patience, here of bearing with people) (q:draft, low confidence)
kensang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:steep bank/high cliff/precipice) (d:<ken> or <keen>, cliff, with <sang> high: a high steep bank or cliff) (s:keen) (q:draft)
Kente = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Kenites) (d:the Kenites, <Ken> with the plural <te>: a people who had shown kindness to Israel and lived among the Amalekites) (b:Ken) (r:9.15.6)
kep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep/take care of/look after) (d:form of <kem> used before words such as <ding>, <theih> and <hun>) (r:2.22.7) (q:draft)
