khade = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crescent moon/crescent/new moon) (d:the moon in its curved shape; {khade lim tawh a kibang kizepnate} are crescent-shaped ornaments) (q:draft, low confidence)
Khadea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Khadea/Chaldeans/Babylonians) (d:the Chaldeans, the people of Babylon whose army burned Jerusalem; written {Khadea mite}) (r:24.39.8)
khadet = (i:1) (t:n) (w:new moon) (d:the new moon and its festival; {khadet ni} is the day of the new moon, the first day of the month) (r:2.19.1) (q:draft)
Khadet = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Khadet/New Moon) (d:<khadet>, the new moon and its festival, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or as the name of the feast) (r:23.66.23)
khagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be very bitter) (d:<kha> be bitter, with <gawp>, severely: said of drink that has turned bitter) (q:draft)
khagilo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil spirit) (d:<kha>, spirit, with <gilo>, evil: an evil spirit that comes upon a person and troubles him) (s:dawi/dawigilo) (q:draft)
khaging = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sound of wings) (d:<kha>, wing, with <ging>, sound: the noise made by beating wings) (q:draft)
khaguh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:jawbone/jaw) (d:the jawbone or jaw of a person or an animal; {la khaguh} is the jawbone of a donkey) (q:draft)
khaguk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:six months/half a year) (d:<kha>, month, with <guk>, six, written here as one word: six months, in {kumthum leh khaguk}, three years and six months) (q:draft)
khah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:release/set free/let go/spare) (d:let go of someone who is held: release a prisoner, set a captive free, let a person leave, or spare a place from destruction) (s:suaktasak/suahtaksak) (a:mat/khum) (q:draft)
khah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:let loose/send out/send/put in) (d:let something go out or in among others, as a bird from the ark, animals among people or dust into water) (r:4.5.17) (q:draft)
khahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:release/set free/let loose) (d:<khah> with the linking suffix <in>, letting go or setting free before another verb; of a judge, acquitting; of animals or anger, letting loose) (b:khah) (q:draft)
khahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send out) (d:<khah>, let go, with <khia>, out: send out or let loose, as wild animals or anger) (s:sawlkhia)
khahkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:to cause/set free/release/rescue) (d:set free or bring out from the power of another: release a prisoner or a slave, rescue from the hand of an enemy) (s:suaktasak/suahtaksak/honkhia) (a:mat)
