khuampite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillars/posts) (d:plural of <khuampi>: the pillars of a building, the posts of the tabernacle court, and in poetry the pillars of the earth and the sky) (s:khuamte/innkhuamte) (b:khuampi) (q:draft)
khuamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillars/posts) (d:plural of <khuam>: pillars or posts, also the posts of a door frame, {kongkhak khuamte}) (s:khuampite/innkhuamte) (b:khuam) (q:draft)
khuamu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:see/have sight) (d:<khua>, the surroundings, with <mu>, see: have sight; {khuamu thei lo} is unable to see, blind) (s:mu) (q:draft)
khuamuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:see/have sight) (d:<khua>, the surroundings, with <muh>, a form of <mu> see; in the verses always {khuamuh nading}, for seeing) (b:khuamu) (q:draft)
