khukte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knees) (d:plural of <khuk>, knee; weak or shaking knees are a picture of fear and of lost strength) (b:khuk) (q:draft)
khukte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:pits) (d:plural of <khuk> in the sense of pit or hole in the ground; {kultal khukte} are tar pits) (q:draft)
khukzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:weak-kneed/faltering) (d:<khuk>, knee, with <zaw>, weak: {khukzaw mite} are those whose knees give way) (b:khuk) (q:draft)
khul = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw in/cast in/put on the fire) (d:throw or put something into a fire or a furnace) (q:draft)
khulin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throwing in/casting in) (d:<khul>, throw into a fire, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:khul) (q:draft)
khulna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being thrown in/casting in) (d:<khul>, throw into a fire, with the noun suffix <na>; {khulna thuak} is be thrown into the fire) (b:khul) (q:draft)
khulsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw in/cast in) (d:<khul>, throw into a fire, with <sak>: throw into the fire things that belong to someone) (b:khul) (q:draft)
khulte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who throw in) (d:<khul>, throw into a fire, with <te>, those who: the men who threw them in) (b:khul) (q:draft)
khum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:put in/shut in/imprison/insert/pen up) (d:put inside something: a person into prison, an animal into a pen or cage, poles into rings, or words into a book) (s:khumcip/kalhkhum) (a:khah/khahkhia) (q:draft)
khum = (i:3) (t:n) (w:roof/housetop) (d:the top covering of a building; {inn khum} is the roof of a house, and {inn khum nuai}, under the roof, means inside the house) (s:innkhum/khumzang/innkhumzang) (q:draft)
khumah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the roof) (d:<khum>, roof, with the place marker <ah>: {tausang khumah} is on the roof of the tower) (s:khumzangah/innkhumzangah) (q:draft)
khumcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shut in/confine/keep in custody/pen up/isolate) (d:<khum>, put in, with <cip>, tightly: keep a person or an animal shut up, as a prisoner in custody, a sick person apart from others, or a bull in its pen) (s:kalhkhum) (a:khahkhia) (b:khum) (q:draft)
khumcipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking captive/confining) (d:<khumcip>, shut in, with the linking suffix <in>: shutting in, taking captive) (b:khumcip) (q:draft)
khumdawnte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:battlements/pinnacles) (d:<khum>, roof, with <dawn>, top, and the plural <te>: the topmost parts of the walls or roofs of a city) (q:draft, low confidence)
khumdiak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:especially sweet/sweeter) (d:<khum>, sweet, with <diak>, especially: all the sweeter) (s:khumzaw) (q:draft)
khumhak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:hard to put through/hard to put in) (d:<khum>, put in, with <hak>, hard to do: {a khumhak sangin} is than it is hard to put through, said of a camel and the eye of a needle) (r:40.19.24) (q:draft)
khumialna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:darkness/gloom) (d:darkness, named together with distress and gloom; apparently the same word as <khuamialna>) (s:khuamialna/khuamial/mialna) (a:khuavak) (q:draft, perhaps a misprint for <khuamialna>)
khumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:putting in/inserting/shutting in/imprisoning) (d:<khum>, put in, with the linking suffix <in>: the action is followed by another) (b:khum) (q:draft)
khumkhelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:surpass/exceed/excel) (d:be greater than all others; the thing in which one is greater is marked by <tawh>) (s:khumlet/khuplet/khupnelh) (r:14.9.22) (q:draft)
khumlet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:surpass/exceed) (d:be greater than, surpass; the other text of this verse has <khuplet>) (s:khuplet/khumkhelh/khupnelh) (q:draft)
khumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sweetness) (d:<khum>, sweet, with the noun suffix <na>: sweetness of taste, and in {kam khumna} pleasantness of speech) (b:khum) (q:draft)
khumna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:imprisonment/shutting in/confinement) (d:<khum>, put in, with the noun suffix <na>: the act or the place of shutting in; {thong sung khumna} is being put in prison and {bawng khumna} is a cattle stall) (s:thongkiatna) (b:khum) (q:draft)
khumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:imprison/have put in prison/have shut in) (d:<khum>, put in, with the causative <sak>: have someone put in, as into prison) (b:khum) (q:draft)
khumte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sweet/choice) (d:<khum>, sweet, with the plural <te>: {leenggahzu khumte} is the sweet, choice wine) (b:khum) (q:draft)
khumzang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:roof/rooftop/housetop) (d:the flat top of a building, from <khum>, roof; {biakinn khumzang} is the roof of the temple) (s:innkhumzang/innkhum/khum) (r:12.23.12) (q:draft)
khumzanga = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the roof) (d:<khumzang>, roof, with the ending <a>, located on) (s:khumzangah/innkhumzanga/khumah) (b:khumzang) (q:draft)
khumzangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the roof/to the roof/in the vault) (d:<khumzang>, roof or vault, with the place marker <ah>: {kulh kongpi khumzangah} is on the roof of the gateway and {van khumzangah} in the vault of heaven) (s:innkhumzangah/khumah/khumzanga) (b:khumzang) (q:draft)
khumzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sweeter/more delightful) (d:<khum>, sweet, with <zaw>, more: sweeter than something, which is followed by <sangin>) (s:khumdiak) (b:khum) (q:draft)
khun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lean on/walk with) (d:support oneself on a staff or stick; {ciangkhut khun mi} is a person who walks with a stick) (q:draft)
khung = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set/lay across/put up) (d:put something long in position before or across: lay a choice before people, put up a parapet round a roof, stretch chains across a room) (q:draft, low confidence)
khung = (i:2) (t:n) (w:top/upper end) (d:the upper end of something, the opposite of <taw>, the bottom; {a taw panin a khung dongin} is from bottom to top; in Ezekiel 40:6 the top of the steps of a gateway, where the NIV has threshold) (s:dawn) (a:taw) (q:draft, low confidence)
khungah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the top/in the tops) (d:<khung>, top, with the place marker <ah>: at the top, as in the tops of trees) (b:khung) (q:draft)
khungin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:laying across/stretching out/setting in place) (d:form of <khung> with the linking suffix <in>: laying or stretching something long across, such as a beam, a chain or a measuring line) (b:khung) (q:draft)
khungnung = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:uppermost/farthest) (d:<khung>, upper end, with <nung>, last: at the very end; {leilu lam a khungnung pen} is the part farthest to the north, the northern frontier) (r:26.48.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
khungnungpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:farthest/uppermost/outermost) (d:<khungnung>, at the upper end, with <pen>, most: {leilu lam a khungnungpen} is the far north) (b:khungnung) (q:draft, low confidence)
khunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leaning on) (d:<khun>, lean on a staff, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:khun) (q:draft)
khup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cover over/close over) (d:cover something from above so that it is closed in; in the verse with <nelh>, completely) (s:khuhcip) (q:draft, low confidence)
khup = (i:2) (t:v) (w:turn face down/lower/fold down) (d:turn or lay something downward: of wings, lower or fold them; {ka khup lamin} is with my face to the ground) (a:thal) (q:draft, low confidence)
khupcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:close up/shut up) (d:<khup>, cover or close, with <cip>, tightly: {laibu khupcip} is close up the book) (a:hon) (b:khup) (q:draft)
khupin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:closing/folding down/turning down) (d:<khup> with the linking suffix <in>: closing a book, or folding wings down to cover the body) (b:khup) (q:draft)
khuplamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:face down/prone) (d:<khup>, turn face down, with <lam>, side, and <in>: with the face to the ground) (s:maipukin) (q:draft)
khuplet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:surpass/overwhelm/overthrow) (d:get the better of something completely: of wisdom, surpass that of others; of victory, swallow up death; of arguments, overthrow them) (s:khumlet/khumkhelh/khupnelh) (q:draft)
khupna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conclusion/closing/end) (d:<khup>, close, with the noun suffix <na>, what closes or covers a thing: {pawi khupna} the closing of a festival, {khupna suang} the capstone of a building, {thugen khupna} the conclusion of a speech) (s:tawpna/thukhupna) (a:kipatna) (b:khup) (q:draft)
khupnelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:surpass/exceed/overshadow) (d:<khup>, cover, with <nelh>, completely: be greater than all others, overshadow them) (s:khumkhelh/khuplet/khumlet) (q:draft)
khupnelhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:closing over/covering over) (d:<khupnelh>, cover over completely, with the linking suffix <in>; said of the earth closing over people) (b:khupnelh) (q:draft)
khusa = (t:see) <khusa-in>
khusa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wearing on the head/having on the head) (d:<khu>, put on the head, with <sa> for a completed action and the linking ending <in>: having something on the head, such as a hat, a crown or ashes) (q:draft)
khusak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put on the head/crown) (d:<khu>, wear on the head, with the causative <sak>: put a hat or a crown on the head of another person) (s:khuksak) (q:draft)
khusakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:putting on the head of/crowning) (d:<khusak>, put something on the head of another person, with the linking ending <in>) (b:khusak) (q:draft)
khut = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hand) (d:the hand of a person; also said of the power or the work of someone, as in {khut tawh bawl}, make by hand)
khuta = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the hand/on the hand) (d:<khut>, hand, with the ending <a>, in or on: in the hand, on the hand) (b:khut) (q:draft)
khutah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the hand/into the hand/at the hand) (d:<khut>, hand, with the place ending <ah>: in, into or at the hand of someone) (b:khut) (q:draft)
khutbuh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ring/finger ring) (d:a ring worn on the finger, from <khut>, hand; {kham khutbuh} is a gold ring) (s:zungbuh) (q:draft)
khutbui = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:maimed in the hand/one-handed) (d:<khut>, hand, with <bui>, maimed: having a hand cut off or useless; paired with <khebui>, maimed in the foot) (r:41.9.46) (q:draft)
khutcinte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fingernails/nails) (d:<khutcin>, fingernail, with the plural <te>) (q:draft)
khutdawh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:alms/begging) (d:what is asked for with the hand held out, from <khut>, hand, and <dawh>, hold out; {khutdawh ngen} is to beg) (s:ngettawm) (q:draft)
khutdawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:begging) (d:<khutdawh>, alms, with the marker <in>: {khutdawhin ngen} is ask for alms, beg) (b:khutdawh) (q:draft)
khutdim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handful) (d:as much as a hand holds, from <khut>, hand, and <dim>, full) (s:khutkuak) (q:draft)
khute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:smoke/clouds of smoke) (d:<khu>, smoke, with the plural <te>: smoke or a rising cloud, as of incense or of dust) (s:meikhute) (b:khu) (q:draft)
khute = (i:2) (t:n) (w:smoking ones/smoldering) (d:<khu>, give off smoke, with <te>: things that are smoking; {sing tumbang a khute} are smoldering stubs of firewood) (b:khu) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuthawm = (i:1) (t:n) (w:empty hand) (d:<khut>, hand, with <hawm>, empty; in the verses always {khuthawm guakin}, empty-handed) (q:draft)
khutin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:with the hand/by the hand) (d:<khut>, hand, with the marker <in>, showing the hand as the doer or the means of an action) (b:khut) (q:draft)
khutkhai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handbag/purse) (d:<khut>, hand, with <khai>, hang or carry; {khutkhai ip} is a bag carried in the hand) (q:draft)
khutkuak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hollow of the hand/cupped hand/handful) (d:<khut>, hand, with <kuak>, hollow: the hollow of the hand and what it holds) (s:khutdim) (q:draft)
khutlaam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise the hand/swear with uplifted hand) (d:<khut>, hand, with <laam>, lift: raise the hand as the sign of an oath) (q:draft)
khutlamen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:palm reading/soothsaying) (d:apparently reading the hand, a kind of fortune-telling; {khutlamen theite} are those who practise it, where the NIV has mediums) (q:draft, low confidence, kind of divination guessed from <khut> hand and <en> look)
khutlekhe = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hands and feet/limbs) (d:<khut>, hand, <le>, and, <khe>, foot, written as one word: the limbs of the body) (q:draft)
khutlekhezaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:paralyzed/paralytic) (d:{khut le khe}, hand and foot, with <zaw>, weak: unable to move the limbs; {khutlekhezaw mi} is a paralyzed person) (b:khutlekhe) (q:draft)
khutlet = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handle) (d:in the clay's complaint that the thing made has no {khutlet}; the NIV reads has no hands) (q:draft, low confidence, handle or hands)
khutlum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hand/hands) (d:the hand as that which kills or does violence; after a possessive, with <in> or <tawh>: at the hands of) (q:draft)
khutlumin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:by the hand of/at the hands of) (d:<khutlum> with the marker <in>, by means of: after a possessive, killed at the hands of someone) (b:khutlum) (q:draft)
khutme = (i:1) (t:n) (w:finger) (d:a finger of the hand; {taklam khutme} is the finger of the right hand that the priest dips in blood or oil) (q:draft)
khutmeno = (i:1) (t:n) (w:little finger/finger) (d:<khutme>, finger, with <no>, small: the little finger, also a single finger) (b:khutme) (r:40.23.4) (q:draft)
khutmete = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fingers) (d:plural of <khutme>, finger) (b:khutme) (q:draft)
khutngakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:laying on of hands) (d:<khut>, hand, with <ngakna>, the laying on: placing the hands on someone to bless or to appoint) (q:draft)
khutnuai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:subjection/power/control) (d:literally under the hand: the power or rule of someone; {khutnuai mi} is a subject or vassal, and {khutnuai-ah koih} is bring under control) (r:49.5.24) (q:draft)
khuto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rise as smoke/go up in smoke/smoke upward) (d:<khu>, smoke, with <to>, upward: go up as smoke) (b:khu) (r:22.3.6) (q:draft)
khutpeek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:palm/open hand) (d:the flat inner side of the hand, the open hand; {khutpeek zan} is hold out the hands) (q:draft)
khutpeek = (i:2) (t:n) (w:handbreadth) (d:the width of a hand used as a measure; {khutpeek cia} is one handbreadth) (s:khutpeekmai) (q:draft)
khutpeekmai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handbreadth) (d:<khutpeek>, palm, with <mai>, face: the width of the palm as a measure) (s:khutpeek) (q:draft)
khutpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thumb) (d:the big finger of the hand, from <khut>, hand, with <pi>, big; named together with <khepi>, the big toe) (b:khut) (q:draft)
khutpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thumbs) (d:plural of <khutpi>, thumb) (b:khutpi) (q:draft)
khutsiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:skilled/skillful) (d:skilled with the hands, from <khut>, hand, and <siam>, skilled; {khutsiam mi} is a craftsman and {khutsiam nasep} is craft work) (s:siam) (q:draft)
khutsiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:skill/craftsmanship) (d:<khutsiam>, skilled with the hands, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:siamna) (b:khutsiam) (q:draft)
khutsiampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:craftsman/carpenter/skilled workman) (d:<khutsiam>, skilled with the hands, with <pa> marking a man: a man who makes things by hand, especially of wood) (b:khutsiam) (q:draft)
khutsiamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:craftsmen/artisans/carpenters/skilled workers) (d:<khutsiam>, skilled with the hands, with the plural ending <te>: people who make things by hand) (b:khutsiam) (r:13.22.15) (q:draft)
khutsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hand/grasp/power) (d:<khut>, hand, with <sung>, inside: the hand as that which holds, so the grasp or power of someone; mostly in {khutsung panin}, out of the hand of) (r:12.18.29) (q:draft)
khutsunga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the hand/in the palm/held in the hand) (d:<khutsung>, the inside of the hand, with the place marker <a>: in the hand or palm, held by someone) (b:khutsung) (q:draft)
khutte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hands) (d:<khut>, hand, with the plural <te>: the hands, or the arms, of a person) (b:khut) (q:draft)
khuttum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fist) (d:the closed hand; {khuttum zial} is to clench the fist, {khuttum tawh tum} is to strike with the fist, and {khuttum cia} is the size of a fist) (q:draft)
khuttung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hand) (d:<khut>, hand, with <tung>, on: the hand as the place where something is held; {khuttung panin} is from the hand of someone) (s:khutsung) (q:draft)
khutun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in their hands/with their hands) (d:<khut>, hand, with <un>, the plural <uh> joined with the marker <in>: in or with their hands) (b:khut) (q:draft)
khutzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:with a withered hand/paralyzed) (d:<khut>, hand, with <zaw>, weak: having a weak or withered hand; {khutzaw khezaw}, weak in hand and foot, means paralyzed) (b:khut) (q:draft)
khutzepin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:folding the hands/with folded hands) (d:<khut>, hand, with <zep>, fold, and the linking suffix <in>: with the hands folded, doing no work) (q:draft)
Khuza = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Chuza) (d:manager of the household of Herod Antipas and husband of Joanna, one of the women who supported Jesus) (q:draft)
khuzaw = (t:see) <khuzaw-in>
khuzaw-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:smoking/smoldering/burning) (d:<khu>, smoke, with <zaw> and the linking suffix <in>: of anger, smoking or burning against someone like the smoke of a fire) (q:draft, low confidence)
ki = (i:1) (t:n) (w:horn) (d:the horn of an animal; in the visions of Daniel a horn stands for a king) (s:kii/saki) (r:19.98.6) (q:draft)
ki = (i:2) (t:part) (d:prefix on a verb showing that the action is done to oneself or to one another, or that it is passive; it is written with a hyphen before a vowel, as in <ki-it>, love one another) (r:4.18.14) (q:draft)
ki-atkeh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:<at>, cut, and <keh>, split, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: cut one's own body, as was done in mourning for the dead) (s:kikui/kikuiliam) (q:draft)
ki-atmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be mown/be cut away) (d:<at>, cut, with the passive prefix <ki> and <mang>, away or gone: be cut and taken away, as hay from a field) (q:draft)
ki-atnente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pieces/cut pieces) (d:<at>, cut, with <ki>, <nen>, into small bits, and the plural <te>: the pieces into which a slaughtered animal is cut) (s:sanente/sabakte) (q:draft)
ki-enpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:examine oneself/look well at oneself) (d:<en>, look, with <ki>, oneself, and <pha>, well: look carefully at one's own conduct) (s:kisittel/kiteldot) (q:draft)
ki-etkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be searched/be looked at again/be re-examined) (d:<et>, look, with the passive prefix <ki> and <kik>, again: be looked at again, said of records that are searched) (s:kikan) (q:draft)
ki-ettehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comparing oneself) (d:<etteh>, compare, with <ki>, oneself, and the linking suffix <in>: comparing oneself; <tawh> marks the one compared with) (s:kitehin) (q:draft)
ki-eu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hewn/be cut out) (d:<eu>, hew or prise out, with the passive prefix <ki>; {ki-eu khiat} is be cut out of the rock) (s:kikhuak) (q:draft)
ki-ipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restraining oneself/holding oneself back) (d:<ip>, hold in, with <ki>, oneself, and the linking suffix <in>: holding oneself back, keeping one's anger in) (s:kikhamcipin/kikhamcip-in) (q:draft)
ki-ipip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold oneself back/restrain oneself) (d:<ip>, hold in, repeated, with <ki>, oneself: keep holding something in, as anger; {ki-ipip zo nawn lo} is can hold back no longer) (q:draft)
ki-ipipna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holding back/self-restraint/forbearance) (d:<ip>, hold in, repeated, with <ki>, oneself, and the noun suffix <na>: holding oneself in again and again, patience with others) (s:kidekna) (q:draft)
ki-ipzote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who can restrain themselves) (d:{ki-ip}, restrain oneself, with <zo>, be able, and the plural <te>; {kampau a ki-ipzote} are those who can guard their speech) (q:draft)
ki-uatsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boasting) (d:plural with <te> of {ki-uatsakna}, pride or boasting; used beside <kisaktheihna>, pride) (s:kiphatsaknate/kisaktheihna/kiliatsakna) (q:draft)
ki-uktawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:control oneself/be self-controlled) (d:<uk>, rule, with <ki>, oneself, and <tawm>, by oneself: keep one's own body under control) (s:kikemzo) (q:draft)
ki-umcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be enclosed/be shut in/be besieged) (d:<um>, surround, with <cip>, tightly, and the passive prefix <ki>; {a ki-umcip} before a noun means enclosed, as a garden, or besieged, as a city) (s:kiumcih/kikhumcip) (q:draft)
ki-upmawhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:suspicions/mutual suspicion) (d:<upmawh>, suspect, with <ki>, each other, the noun suffix <na> and the plural <te>: suspicions that people have of one another) (q:draft)
kiak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:thistle/brier) (d:a thorny weed that grows on neglected land, usually named together with <ling>, thorn) (s:thangling/sialtalling)
kiakhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall together/fall in together) (d:<kia>, fall, with <khawm>, together: fall into something together; {thong a kiakhawm} is to be in prison together with someone) (s:tukkhawm/pukkhawm) (b:kia) (q:draft)
kiakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall off/fall from/drop off) (d:<kia>, fall, with <khia>, out or away: fall off from a person or place) (b:kia) (q:draft)
kiakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have fallen/have fallen off) (d:<kia>, fall, with <khin>, already or completely: have fallen off) (b:kia) (q:draft)
kiakte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:thistles) (b:kiak) plural form of <kiak>
kial = (i:1) (t:n) (w:famine/hunger) (d:a time when there is no food in the land, and the hunger it brings; {kial tung} is a famine comes) (s:kialpi/gilkialna) (q:draft)
kial = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be hungry/hunger/go hungry) (d:be in need of food, usually in the phrase {gil kial}, the stomach is hungry) (a:gilvah/vah) (q:draft)
kialin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being hungry/going hungry) (d:<kial>, be hungry, with the linking suffix <in>; usually {gil kialin}, being or going hungry) (b:kial) (q:draft)
kiallai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be still hungry) (d:<kial>, be hungry, with <lai>, still: be hungry still, even after eating) (q:draft)
kialna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hunger/starvation) (d:<kial>, be hungry, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being hungry) (s:gilkialna) (b:kial) (q:draft)
kialo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not fall) (d:<kia>, fall, with the negative <lo> written as one word; {lei-ah kialo ding} is will not fall to the ground, said of a hair of the head and of a word that will not fail) (b:kia) (q:draft)
kialpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:famine/severe famine) (d:<kial>, famine, with <pi>, great: a great famine in a land) (s:kial/gilkialna) (b:kial) (q:draft)
kialpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:famines/famine) (d:<kialpi>, famine, with the plural <te>) (b:kialpi) (q:draft)
kiam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:decrease/recede/go down/diminish) (d:become less in amount, number or strength; said of flood water that goes down, of a people or herd that grows fewer, and of flesh that wastes away) (a:pung/khang) (r:1.8.3) (q:draft)
kiamgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:waste away/fail/be greatly reduced) (d:<kiam>, decrease, with <gawp>, severely: of strength or the body, fail or waste away) (b:kiam) (q:draft)
kiamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dwindling/decreasing) (d:<kiam>, decrease, with the linking suffix <in>: dwindling, growing less) (b:kiam) (q:draft)
kiamkiam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep going down/recede steadily) (d:<kiam>, decrease, repeated to show that it goes on little by little) (q:draft)
kiamkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dwindle again/decrease again) (d:<kiam>, decrease, with <kik>, back or again: grow less again, said of wealth quickly gained) (b:kiam) (q:draft)
kiamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reduce/decrease/diminish) (d:<kiam>, become less, with the causative <sak>: make less, or let become fewer) (s:tawmsak/khiam) (a:pungsak/khangsak) (b:kiam) (q:draft)
kiamsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sink/go down/subside) (d:<kiam>, go down, with <suk>, downward: sink or subside, as the Nile after its flood) (a:khangto) (b:kiam) (q:draft)
kiamvat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:subside suddenly/abate at once) (d:<kiam>, decrease, with <vat>, suddenly: go down all at once, said of a fever that leaves) (q:draft)
kiang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:presence/side) (d:the place beside or with someone; mostly in <kiangah>, to, and {kiang panin}, from) (r:44.17.33) (q:draft)
kianga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:to/beside/near/with) (d:<kiang> with the suffix <a>, used where the phrase describes a following noun or verb, as in {pasian kianga thu nget}, praying to God, and {a kianga ding}, standing beside him) (b:kiang) (r:43.18.22) (q:draft)
kiangah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:to/beside/with) (d:<kiang>, presence or side, with the place marker <ah>: to, beside or with a person; it follows the person who is spoken to or approached) (b:kiang) (r:2.6.10/5.2.17)
kiangahhong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:to me) (d:<kiangah>, to or beside, run together with <hong>, toward the speaker; elsewhere written as two words, probably a printing error) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiangpan = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:from) (d:from a person, from the presence of someone; <kiang> with <pan>, more often written {kiang panin}) (q:draft)
kiangpanin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:from/away from) (d:from a person or from the presence of someone; <kiangpan> with the suffix <in>) (b:kiangpan) (q:draft)
kiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to fall/bring down/send down) (d:<kia>, fall, with the causative <sak>: make fall, bring a person down from a high place, or send down hail or birds from the sky) (s:puksak/tuksak) (a:khangtosak) (b:kia) (q:draft)
kiasakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sending down/causing to fall) (d:<kiasak>, cause to fall, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kiasak) (q:draft)
kiasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall down/come down/go down/descend) (d:<kia>, fall, with <suk>, downward: fall or come down from a higher place) (s:tuksuk) (a:kahto/paito) (b:kia) (r:19.104.8) (q:draft)
kiasukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:falling down) (d:<kiasuk>, fall down, with the linking suffix <in>) (s:tuksukin) (b:kiasuk) (q:draft)
kiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall) (d:form of <kia>, fall, used before <leh>, <ciangin>, <sangin>, <manin> and other endings) (b:kia) (r:20.23.27) (q:draft)
kiat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lose heart/falter/grow faint) (d:used with <lung>, heart: {lung a kiat}, the heart falls, means one is discouraged or grows faint) (s:lungkiat/lungkia) (b:kia) (q:draft)
kiat = (i:3) (t:v) (w:shave/shave off/scrape) (d:cut hair off close with a blade, or scrape a surface; {kiat khia} is shave off or scrape away) (s:met/meet) (q:draft)
kiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those that fall/fallen ones/what has fallen) (d:<kia>, fall, with the plural <te>: things that have fallen, as seed, grapes or crumbs) (b:kia) (q:draft)
kiatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shaving/scraping) (d:<kiat>, shave or scrape, with the linking suffix <in>; said of shaving the hair and of scraping the walls of a house) (s:metin) (b:kiat) (q:draft)
kiatkhia = (t:see) <kiatkhia-in>
kiatkhia-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scraping away/scraping off) (d:<kiat>, scrape, with <khia>, out or away, and the linking suffix <in>: scraping something away) (q:draft)
kiatkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scrape off/be scraped off) (d:<kiat>, scrape, with <khiat>, off or away; {a kiatkhiat} is what has been scraped off) (b:kiat) (q:draft)
kiatkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have shaved off/cause to be shaved off) (d:<kiatkhiat>, shave or scrape off, with the causative <sak>: have something shaved off) (b:kiatkhiat) (q:draft)
kiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fall/downfall) (d:the act of falling, from <kiat>, fall, with the noun suffix <na>; {za kiatna} is loss of office and {thong kiatna} is being put in prison) (s:pukna/tukna) (b:kiat) (q:draft)
kiatna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:razor) (d:in {mul kiatna}, a tool for shaving hair, from <kiat>, shave, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:mulkiatna) (b:kiat) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall together with/share a fall with) (d:<kiat>, form of <kia>, fall, with <pih>, together with; {thong kiatpih} is to be in prison together with someone, a fellow prisoner) (b:kiat) (q:draft)
kiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to fall/bring down/send down) (d:<kiat>, fall, with the causative <sak>: make fall or send down; {thong kiatsak} is put in prison and {za kiatsak} is remove from a position) (s:puksak/tuksak) (b:kiat) (q:draft)
kiatsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:having scraped/causing to be scraped) (d:<kiat>, scrape, with the causative <sak> and the linking suffix <in>: having something scraped) (b:kiat) (q:draft)
kiatsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shave clean/shave off) (d:<kiat>, shave, with <siang>, clean: shave away all the hair or beard) (s:metkhia/mettol) (b:kiat) (q:draft)
kiattheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<kiat>, fall, and <theih>, can, with the noun suffix <na>: the possibility of falling; {kiattheihna ding gum} is a pit that one can fall into) (q:draft)
kibaang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put on/be laid on/be worn) (d:<baang>, put on, with the passive prefix <ki>: of a yoke, be laid on an animal; of clothing, be put on a person) (b:baang) (q:draft)
kibalnen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be cut in pieces) (d:<balnen>, tear in pieces, with the passive prefix <ki>; often followed by <gawp>, violently) (s:kibalzan) (b:balnen) (q:draft)
kibalnengawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be cut in pieces) (d:<kibalnen>, be torn to pieces, with <gawp>, violently) (s:kibalzan) (b:kibalnen) (q:draft)
kibalzan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be torn) (d:<balzan>, tear apart, with the passive prefix <ki>: said of a person or animal torn by a wild beast) (s:kibalnen) (b:balzan) (q:draft)
kibang = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:like) (d:be like; the thing compared with is followed by <tawh>, so that <tawh kibang> means is like) (s:kisun)
kibang = (i:3) (t:n) (w:similar) (d:something that is like another; {tawh a kibang khat} is one that looks like) (r:26.10.10)
kibanga = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:like/similar/alike) (d:<kibang>, be alike, with the linking ending <a> before another verb; {tawh kibanga kibawl} means made to be like, as in {ngen tawh kibanga kibawl}, made like a net, the network on the temple pillars) (b:kibang) (q:draft)
kibangbang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:remain the same/stay as it is) (d:<kibang>, be the same, with <bang> repeated: go on being the same, remain as it is) (q:draft)
kibangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:alike/likewise/in the same way) (d:<kibang>, be alike, with the suffix <in>: alike, equally; after <tawh>, in the same way as) (b:kibang) (q:draft)
kibangkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seem/appear like/look like) (d:<kibang>, be like, with <kha>, happen to: after <tawh>, may seem to be) (q:draft)
kibangkim = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:all alike/all the same/equal) (d:<kibang>, same, with <kim>, all: all alike, all the same) (s:kikim) (q:draft)
kibanglai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still be like) (d:<kibang>, be like, with <lai>, still: after <tawh>, still be like) (q:draft)
kibangmah = (t:see) <kibangmah-in>
kibangmah-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the same way/just the same) (d:<kibang> same with the emphatic <mah> and the suffix <in>; another spelling of <kibangmahin>) (s:kibangmahin) (q:draft)
kibangmahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the same way/just the same) (d:<kibang> same with the emphatic <mah> and the suffix <in>) (s:kibangmah-in) (q:draft)
kibangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make equal/make like/make the same) (d:<kibang>, be alike, with the causative <sak>: make or treat one as the same as another; <tawh> marks the one compared with) (s:bangsak/batsak/kikimsak) (b:kibang) (q:draft)
kibangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:likening/making equal/comparing) (d:<kibangsak>, make like, with the linking suffix <in>; <tawh> marks the one compared with) (b:kibangsak) (q:draft)
kibangta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be like now/have become like) (d:<kibang>, be like, with <ta>, marking a state now reached: after <tawh>, have become like) (s:bangta) (b:kibang) (q:draft)
kibangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those that are like/those that seem) (d:<kibang>, be like, with the plural <te>: those that are like or seem; it follows <tawh>) (b:kibang) (q:draft)
kibangzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be more like/be rather like) (d:<kibang>, be like, with <zaw>, more or rather: after <tawh>, be more like) (b:kibang) (q:draft)
kibaptaiz = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:<baptaiz>, baptize, a loanword from English, with the passive prefix <ki>: be baptized) (s:kituiphum/kiphum) (b:baptaiz) (q:draft)
kibaptaizna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:<kibaptaiz>, be baptized, with the noun suffix <na>: the baptism that one receives) (s:kituiphumna/baptaizna/tuiphumna) (b:kibaptaiz) (q:draft)
kibaptaizte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are baptized) (d:<kibaptaiz>, be baptized, with the plural <te>) (b:kibaptaiz) (q:draft)
kibasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:owe one another/be in debt to each other) (d:<ba>, owe, with <ki>, each other, and <sak>: owe one another something) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibat = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:like) (d:used with <tawh>, with: be like someone or something) (s:kibang/kisun)
kibat = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:as) (d:with <tawh>: being as another is, or seeming as if something were so)
kibat = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:similar/alike) (d:alike, the same as each other; {a kibat kei leh} is if they are not alike) (s:kibanga/kisun) (a:tuam)
kibatlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:difference/unlikeness) (d:the fact of not being alike, a difference: <kibat> be alike, <loh> not, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kilamdanna/kideidanna) (a:kibatna) (q:draft)
kibatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:likeness/resemblance/similarity) (d:how one thing is like another, or what two have in common; {tawh a kibatna} is likeness to something) (s:batna) (a:kibatlohna/kilamdanna) (b:kibat) (q:draft)
kibatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:equality/likenesses) (d:<kibatna>, likeness, with the plural <te>: the ways in which one is like or equal to another, as in {Pasian tawh kibatnate}, equality with God) (b:kibatna) (q:draft)
kibatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be like/be alike with/be equal to) (d:<kibat> be like with <pih> together with: be like another; {ka kibatpih ding}, one for me to be like, my equal) (b:kibat) (q:draft)
kibawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made/be prepared/be done) (d:passive of <bawl>, make or do: be made, prepared or done; with <tawh>, made of or prepared with something) (b:bawl) (r:14.4.21) (q:draft)
kibawla = (i:1) (t:v) (w:made/arranged/prepared) (d:<kibawl> be made with the linking <a>; {kibawla a om}, be in a prepared state) (b:kibawl) (q:draft)
kibawlbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make oneself/keep making oneself) (d:<ki> oneself with <bawl> make, repeated: be making oneself into something) (s:kibawltawm) (b:kibawl) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being made/be made/be prepared) (d:form of <kibawl>, be made, with the linking suffix <in>: being made, and then going on to what follows) (b:kibawl) (q:draft)
kibawlkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be prepared/be made ready) (d:passive <ki> with <bawlkhol>, prepare beforehand: be made ready in advance) (b:bawlkhol) (q:draft)
kibawlkholsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:prepared beforehand/made ready) (d:<kibawlkhol>, be prepared in advance, with <sa>, already: prepared and waiting) (s:kithawisa) (b:kibawlkhol) (q:draft)
kibawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doing/making/performing) (d:noun form of <kibawl>, be made or done: the act, place or means of something being done; {pawi kibawlna inn} is a house where a feast is held) (b:kibawl) (q:draft)
kibawlpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be reformed/be renewed/be put right) (d:<bawlpha> put right with <ki>, passive or of oneself: mend one's ways under correction, or be made new) (s:kipuahpha/thaksuak) (b:bawlpha) (q:draft)
kibawlphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be repaired/be rebuilt/reform) (d:form of <kibawlpha> used before <kik>, <hun> and similar words: be put right again, of a broken jar, a ruined city or a person who mends his ways) (s:kilamkik) (b:kibawlpha) (q:draft)
kibawlsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:made/prepared/furnished/already done) (d:<kibawl>, be made, with <sa>, already done: made, prepared or finished beforehand; {a kibawlsa na} is the thing that has been made) (s:kithawisa) (b:kibawl) (r:41.14.15) (q:draft)
kibawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made for/be prepared for) (d:<kibawl>, be made, with <sak>: be made or done on behalf of someone, as atonement made for the people) (b:kibawl) (q:draft)
kibawlsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:that by which something is made for someone: <kibawlsak> be made for, with the noun suffix <na>; of the ram with which atonement is made for a person) (b:kibawlsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibawlsia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be persecuted/be mistreated/be harmed) (d:<bawlsia>, mistreat, with the passive <ki>: be treated badly, harmed or persecuted by others) (s:kibawlsiat/kinengniam) (b:bawlsia) (q:draft)
kibawlsia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:hurt each other/wrong one another) (d:<bawlsia>, mistreat, with <ki> in its sense of each other: hurt or wrong one another) (b:bawlsia) (q:draft)
kibawlsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be persecuted/be mistreated) (d:passive of <bawlsiat>; with <hong>, to be persecuted by others) (s:kibawlsia/kinengniam) (b:bawlsiat) (q:draft)
kibawlsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:persecution/torment/mistreatment) (d:the persecution or torment that people suffer; also of people provoking or harming one another, {khat leh khat kibawlsiatna}) (s:bawlsiatna/gimsakna) (b:bawlsiatna) (r:66.14.11) (q:draft)
kibawlsiatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:acts of mistreatment/wrongs done to one another) (d:<kibawlsiatna> with plural <te>) (b:kibawlsiatna) (q:draft)
kibawltawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make oneself/make oneself out to be) (d:<bawltawm> with <ki>, of oneself: make oneself into something, as unclean by what one touches, or like an angel in appearance) (s:kibawlbawl) (b:bawltawm) (q:draft)
kibawltawm = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:artificial/man-made) (d:{a kibawltawm} before a noun: made by people, not natural) (b:bawltawm) (q:draft)
kibawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things made/carved figures) (d:things that are made, fashioned or carved, as {lim kibawlte} carved figures) (b:kibawl) (q:draft)
kibawlzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have been made/be established) (d:<kibawl> be made with <zawh>, finished; {a kibawlzawh}, after it was made) (q:draft)
kibeh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be related/be kin) (d:<beh> clan with <ki>, one another: belong to the same family; {a kibeh} is a relative) (b:beh) (q:draft)
kibeh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be added/increase) (d:in {kibeh laplap}, keep being added, pile up) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibehlap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be added/be joined) (d:be added to a number or group; <tawh> names what one is added to) (b:behlap) (q:draft)
kibehlaplap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep increasing/be added more and more) (d:<kibehlap>, be added, with its last syllable repeated: keep being added, grow more and more in number or amount) (b:behlaplap) (q:draft)
kibehlapsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:add to/cause to be added) (d:<kibehlap> be added with the causative <sak>: add people to a group) (b:kibehlap) (q:draft)
kibehlapto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be added on/be heaped upon) (d:<kibehlap> be added with <to>, upward or on top) (b:kibehlap) (q:draft)
kibeimangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be wiped out/perish) (d:passive <ki> with <beimangsak>, destroy) (s:kisusia/kisiat) (b:beimangsak) (q:draft)
kibeisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be wiped out/be exterminated/be brought to an end) (d:passive <ki> with <beisak>, bring to an end: be wiped out or made to cease) (s:kiphiat/kibeimangsak) (b:beisak) (q:draft)
kibet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be struck/be slapped) (d:passive <ki> with <bet> strike) (s:kisat) (b:bet) (q:draft)
kibet = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be plucked up) (d:with <khiat>, out: be pulled up out of the ground) (s:kibotkhia/kisuankhia) (a:kisuan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibetkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:uprooting/plucking out) (d:the act of being pulled up or out, with the noun suffix <na>) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be worshipped) (d:passive of <bia>, worship: be worshipped) (b:bia) (q:draft)
kibia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:offer oneself) (d:give oneself as an offering to God) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:worship) (d:the worshipping of God or a god; {kibiakna mun} is the place where he is worshipped, a sanctuary) (s:biakna) (b:biakna) (q:draft)
kibiakna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:offering) (d:what is offered to the Lord in worship) (s:biakna) (b:biakna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibiaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:offerings/sacrifices) (d:<kibiakna> offering with plural <te>: the things offered in worship; {keimah hong kibiaknate}, the offerings made to me) (s:biaknate/kithoihnate) (b:kibiakna) (q:draft)
kibokcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought low/be pressed down) (d:be bowed down flat; used with {kikun}, be bent over) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibokcipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring very low/press down) (d:<kibokcip> be pressed down with the causative <sak>) (b:kibokcip) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hang on/cling to) (d:hang together on something like a bunch, as vessels hung on a peg; perhaps from <bom>, cluster) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibotkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be pulled up/be torn out) (d:passive <ki> with <botkhia>, pull out: be pulled up by the roots, or be torn out of its place) (s:kizunglot/kisuankhia/kidokkhia/kizungbawh) (a:kisuan) (b:botkhia) (q:draft)
kibottat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/snap/be torn apart) (d:of a cord or snare: be pulled until it breaks, from <bot>, pull) (s:kitat/kitan) (q:draft)
Kibrothhattaavah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kibroth Hattaavah) (d:camp of Israel in the wilderness between Sinai and Hazeroth, where the people who craved meat were buried) (r:4.33.16/4.33.17)
Kibrothhattavah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kibroth Hattaavah) (d:camp of Israel in the wilderness before Hazeroth, named graves of craving because the people who craved meat were buried there) (r:4.11.34/4.11.35)
kibu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hidden) (d:passive <ki> with <bu>, hide: be hidden or kept secret) (s:kiseel/kiliah) (a:kilang/kilak) (b:bu) (q:draft)
kibua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be poured out/be shed) (d:passive of <bua>, pour: be poured out or shed, said of blood, water or anger) (s:kibuak/kibuakhia) (b:bua) (q:draft)
kibuai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be in uproar/be in confusion) (d:<buai>, be troubled, with <ki>: be in disorder and noise, said of a crowd) (s:kigamlum/gamlum) (b:buai) (q:draft)
kibuaigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown into confusion) (d:<kibuai> be in confusion with <gawp>, violently) (b:kibuai) (q:draft)
kibuaigawpsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw into confusion/confound) (d:<kibuaigawp> be thrown into confusion with the causative <sak>) (b:kibuaigawp) (q:draft)
kibuaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown into confusion/be troubled) (d:passive <ki> with <buaisak>, trouble, disturb) (b:buaisak) (q:draft)
kibuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sprinkled/be poured/be shed) (d:passive of <buak>: a liquid is poured or sprinkled on someone, blood is shed) (s:kitheh/kibua/kiluan) (b:buak) (r:4.19.13) (q:draft)
kibuak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:sprinkle on oneself/put on oneself) (d:throw dust or ashes over oneself as a sign of grief) (b:buak) (q:draft)
kibuakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be poured out/spill out) (d:<kibua>, be poured, with <khia>, out: be poured or spilled out) (s:kibua/kibuak) (b:kibua) (q:draft)
kibuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sprinkling on oneself/throwing on oneself) (d:<kibuak> with the linking suffix <in>: putting dust or ashes on oneself as a sign of grief) (b:kibuak) (q:draft)
kibuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:place of pouring out/dump/heap) (d:<kibuak>, be poured out, with the noun suffix <na>: the place where something is poured or thrown out; {vut kibuakna} is the ash heap) (b:kibuak) (q:draft)
kibuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raped/be violated/be mistreated) (d:be seized and used with violence; said of women when a city is taken) (s:kibuansak) (q:draft)
kibuansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be violated/be raped/be ravished) (d:<kibuan>, be violated, with <sak>: said of women forced by men) (s:kibuan) (b:kibuan) (q:draft)
kibuasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:shed/poured out) (d:<kibua> be poured out, with <sa> for a completed action; said of blood) (b:kibua) (q:draft)
kibulh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put on/be fastened/be chained) (d:passive <ki> with <bulh>, put on or fasten: be fixed onto something, set in a mounting or grafted in; {kol kibulh} and {sikkol kibulh} mean be put in chains) (s:kihen) (a:kisutkhia) (b:bulh) (r:11.7.28) (q:draft)
kibulhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bound/be chained) (d:<kibulh>, be fastened on, with the linking suffix <in>: being bound, said of chains or fetters put on a person) (b:kibulh) (q:draft)
kibulhsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fastened on/set in place/chained) (d:<kibulh> be put on with <sa>, already: of lamps set on a stand, or of people put in chains) (b:kibulh) (q:draft)
kibulhtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:commit oneself/set oneself/attach oneself) (d:<kibulh> be fastened with <tawm>, of oneself: fix oneself on a course of one's own accord) (q:draft)
kibulphuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken as the basis/be based on) (d:passive <ki> with <bulphuh> base on) (b:bulphuh) (q:draft)
kibuluh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ransacked) (d:passive <ki> with <buluh>, plunder: be raided and stripped of goods) (s:kiluh/kisut) (b:buluh) (q:draft)
kibum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bewitched/be put under a spell) (d:passive <ki> with <bum> bewitch) (b:bum) (q:draft)
kibup = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:wholly/entirely) (d:<ki> oneself with <bup> whole; in {kibup piak}, give oneself wholly, devote oneself, elsewhere written as one word <kibuppiak>) (b:bup) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibuppiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:devote oneself/give oneself wholly) (d:<ki> oneself with <buppiak> give wholly) (s:kipumpiak) (b:buppiak) (q:draft)
Kibzaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kibzaim) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim, given with its pasturelands to the Kohathite Levites) (r:6.21.22)
kici = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be called) (d:passive of <ci>, say: be called by a name or title) (s:kilo/kiphuak) (b:ci)
kici = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be named) (d:have as a name; {a kici min nei} is bearing the name) (s:kiphuak/kilo) (b:ci)
kiciahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought back/be taken home) (d:passive <ki> with <ciahpih>, take home or take along: be taken back, or be taken away to another place; with <kik>, be brought back again) (s:kipuakik) (b:ciahpih) (q:draft)
kiciahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sent back/be sent away) (d:passive <ki> with <ciahsak>, send away) (s:kisawlkhia) (b:ciahsak) (q:draft)
kicial = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:hired) (d:passive of <cial> hire; {a kicial} is a hired hand, {a kicial nasem} a hired worker) (b:cial) (q:draft)
kicialtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hired/hired) (d:of a person who works for wages and is not the owner; {a kicialtawm tuucingpa}, the hired shepherd) (q:draft)
kiciam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swear/take an oath/vow/promise) (d:<ciam>, promise, with <ki>: bind oneself by an oath or vow; {min tawh kiciam} is swear by a name) (s:ciam/thuciam) (b:ciam) (q:draft)
kiciamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swearing/taking an oath/with an oath) (d:<kiciam> with the linking ending {-in}: swearing, with an oath) (b:kiciam) (q:draft)
kiciamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oath/vow/promise) (d:<kiciam>, swear, with the noun suffix <na>: an oath, vow or solemn promise that someone has made) (s:ciamna/kamciamna/khapna/thuciam) (b:kiciam) (q:draft)
kiciamnasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oath sworn/what was sworn) (d:<kiciamna> with <sa>, already done: the oath a person has already made, or the thing sworn about) (b:kiciamna) (r:40.14.9) (q:draft)
kiciamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oaths/vows/covenants) (d:<kiciamna>, oath, with the plural <te>: oaths or vows made, and also covenants between parties) (s:thuciamnate) (b:kiciamna) (q:draft)
kiciampak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swear rashly/vow thoughtlessly) (d:<kiciam> swear with <pak> quickly: take an oath without thinking) (b:ciampak) (q:draft)
kiciampha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swear/make an oath) (d:<kiciam> swear with <pha>; {kiciampha kik}, swear again, reaffirm an oath) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciamsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sworn/vowed/promised on oath) (d:<kiciam> swear with <sa> already: having sworn or vowed; before a noun, that was promised on oath) (s:ciamsa) (b:kiciam) (q:draft)
kiciamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make swear/put under oath) (d:<kiciam>, swear, with the causative {-sak}: make someone take an oath) (b:kiciam) (q:draft)
kiciamsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making swear/putting under oath) (d:<kiciamsak> make swear with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiciamsak) (q:draft)
kiciamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who swear/those who have sworn) (d:<kiciam>, swear, with the plural <te>: the people who take an oath) (b:kiciam) (q:draft)
kiciamteh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be recorded/be listed/be reckoned/be credited) (d:passive <ki> with <ciamteh>, note or record: be written down, listed or remembered, and so be counted as something, as faith is counted as righteousness) (s:kigelh) (b:ciamteh) (r:13.5.7) (q:draft)
kiciamtehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being remembered/being noted) (d:<kiciamteh> be recorded with the linking suffix <in>; {kiciamtehin om}, be kept in mind) (b:kiciamteh) (q:draft)
kiciamtehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:record/register/registration) (d:noun from <kiciamteh> be recorded; what is written down, such as a family list or genealogy) (s:ciamtehna/sazian) (b:kiciamteh) (r:13.7.9) (q:draft)
kiciamtehsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:recorded/written down/marked out) (d:<kiciamteh> be recorded with <sa>, already) (b:kiciamteh) (q:draft)
kiciamtehsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be numbered/be recorded) (d:<kiciamteh> be recorded with <sak>, on someone's behalf) (s:kisim) (b:kiciamteh) (q:draft)
kiciamtehte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those listed/those recorded/those registered) (d:<kiciamteh> be recorded with <te>: the people whose names are written down) (b:kiciamteh) (q:draft)
kiciamzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swear instead/swear rather) (d:<kiciam> swear with <zaw>, rather or instead) (b:kiciam) (q:draft)
kiciamzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have sworn) (d:<kiciam> swear, with <zo> for an action already carried out) (s:ciamzo) (b:kiciam) (q:draft)
kician = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:firm/sure/sound/well-founded) (d:firm and reliable: said of a place that holds, of a plan or a matter that is well grounded, and of a hope or a house that is sure) (s:kip/kiptak) (b:cian) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid/be built up/be built) (d:of stones or a wall, be laid one on another and built up in courses) (s:kilam) (a:kicim) (q:draft)
kiciangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:piled up/lying one upon another) (d:<kiciang>, be laid one on another, with the linking ending <in>; said here of corpses lying in heaps) (b:kiciang) (q:draft)
kiciangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be built up again/be rebuilt) (d:<kiciang>, be built up in courses, with <kik>, again; said of a city wall) (s:kilamkik/kiciankik) (b:kiciang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciangtan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fixed/be set/be determined/be limited) (d:of an amount, a number or a limit, be laid down beforehand; {a kiciangtan zah} is the fixed or allotted amount) (s:kiseh/kisehkhol) (b:ciangtan) (q:draft)
kiciangtansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:appointed/fixed/set) (d:<kiciangtan>, be fixed, with <sa>, already done; {a kiciangtansa hun} is the appointed time) (s:kisehsa/sehsa) (b:kiciangtan) (q:draft)
kiciangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those laid/those built up) (d:<kiciang> be laid with <te>: in {suang kiciangte}, the stones that had been laid in a building) (b:kiciang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciangto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be piled up/be built up high) (d:<kiciang> be built up in courses, with <to> upward; of waters heaped up and of walls rising to the sky) (b:kiciang) (q:draft)
kiciankik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rebuilt/be built again) (d:said of city walls being built up again; perhaps another spelling of <kiciangkik>) (s:kiciangkik/kilamkik) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make sure/ascertain/find out for certain) (d:<kician>, sure, with the causative <sak>: make a matter sure by finding out more about it) (b:kician) (q:draft)
kicici = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be said again and again/keep being said) (d:passive <ki> with <cici>, keep saying) (b:cici) (q:draft)
kicih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be said/be called/be told) (d:form of <kici> used before nouns and endings: {a kicih} is what is said or what someone is called, and {bang kicih ding} is what is to be done with someone) (s:kigen) (b:kici) (q:draft)
kicih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be used as fuel/be burned) (d:be put on a fire as fuel, as in {mei-in kicih}; {sing a kicih mei} is a wood fire) (s:kihal/kikhul) (q:draft)
kiciHebru = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:called Hebrew) (d:<kici>, be called, run together with the name <Hebru>, Hebrew; two words printed as one, probably a printing error) (q:draft, low confidence)
kicihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:name/title/saying) (d:<kici>, be called or be said, with the noun ending <na>: what a person or place is called, or the fact that something is said; {kicihna ngah} is be called, and {a kicihna za} is hear it said) (b:cihna) (q:draft)
kicihnopna = (t:see) <kicihnopna-a>
kicihnopna-a = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:meaning himself/with reference to himself) (d:<ki> oneself, <cihnopna> what one means to say, with <a>: as something meant of oneself) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciing = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cultivated/planted) (d:of an olive tree, grown and tended by people, as opposed to <gamlak>, wild) (q:draft)
kicil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trodden/be trampled/be threshed) (d:passive <ki> with <cil>, tread out: said of grapes in a winepress and of grain on a threshing floor) (q:draft)
kicilgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trampled down/be threshed hard) (d:<kicil> be trodden or threshed with <gawp> severely) (b:kicil) (q:draft)
kicilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:treading/pressing) (d:<kicil> be trodden with the noun suffix <na>; {leenggahzu kicilna phual} is the winepress) (b:kicil) (q:draft)
kicilsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:threshed/trampled/crushed) (d:<kicil> be threshed with <sa> already done) (b:kicil) (q:draft)
kicim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse/fall down/crumble/fall) (d:fall in ruins, said of walls, buildings, cities and the ground) (a:kiciang/kilam) (b:cim) (r:66.14.8) (q:draft)
kicimgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse utterly/crumble/be broken down) (d:<kicim> collapse with <gawp>, completely) (b:kicim) (q:draft)
kicimin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being broken down/collapsing) (d:<kicim> collapse with the linking ending <in>) (b:kicim) (q:draft)
kicimmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse completely/crumble away) (d:<kicim> collapse with <mang>, away or to nothing) (s:cimzan) (q:draft)
kicimsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:broken down/collapsed/fallen) (d:<kicim> collapse with <sa> already done) (s:cimsa) (b:kicim) (q:draft)
kicimsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse down/fall down upon) (d:<kicim> collapse with <suk> downward) (b:kicim) (q:draft)
kicimte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breaches/fallen parts/ruins) (d:<kicim> collapse with the plural <te>: the parts of a wall that have fallen down) (b:kicim) (q:draft)
kicin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be complete/be perfect/be full/be accomplished) (d:be complete or fulfilled; written with a final apostrophe before words such as <nading>, <khit> and <mateng>, and with <na> it forms the noun <kicinna>, completeness) (b:cin) (r:46.13.10) (q:draft)
kicinasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make oneself ill) (d:<ki> oneself with <cinasak> make sick) (b:cinasak) (q:draft)
kicing = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be guarded/be watched) (d:passive <ki> with <cing>, guard: of a tomb, be watched over) (s:kivil/kikemcing) (b:cing) (q:draft, low confidence)
kicinga = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:perfect/complete) (d:<kicing> complete with the linking <a>; {a kicinga a kingaihsun}, considered to be perfect) (b:kicing) (q:draft)
kicingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:fully/completely/in full) (d:<kicing> with the ending <in>: in a complete way, with nothing lacking) (s:cingin) (b:kicing) (q:draft)
kicingkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ready beforehand/be already complete) (d:<kicing> complete with <khol>, beforehand) (q:draft, low confidence)
kicingkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fully supplied/be complete in everything) (d:<kicing> complete with <kim>, all or fully) (q:draft)
kicingsa = (t:see) <kicingsa-a>
kicingsa-a = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fully trained/already complete) (d:<kicing> complete with <sa>, already, and the linking <a>) (q:draft)
kicingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fulfill/complete/make complete/supply/make perfect) (d:<kicing>, complete, with the causative <sak>: make full or perfect, fulfill, supply what is lacking) (s:cingtaaksak/kicinsak/cingsak) (b:kicing) (q:draft)
kicingsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:perfecter/one who makes complete) (d:<kicingsak> make complete with <pa>, the male one who does it) (b:kicingsak) (q:draft)
kicingta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be complete now/be fulfilled) (d:<kicing> complete, with <ta> showing that the state has now been reached; {a hun kicingta}, the time is ripe) (b:kicing) (q:draft)
kicingtaak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:complete/perfect/made complete) (d:<cingtaak>, complete, with <ki>; {a kicingtaak lo} is what is incomplete) (s:kicing) (b:cingtaak) (q:draft)
kicingzah = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:enough/sufficient in number) (d:<kicing> enough with <zah> amount: as many as are needed) (q:draft)
kicingzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more complete/fuller/greater) (d:<kicing> complete with <zaw> more; {a kicingzaw semsemin} is more and more fully) (s:cingtaakzaw) (b:kicing) (q:draft)
kicingzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be enough/be quite sufficient) (d:<kicing> enough with <zo>, fully reached) (b:kicing) (q:draft)
kicinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:perfection/completeness/fullness/integrity) (d:the state of being complete or whole, also integrity of character; {hoih kicinna} is perfect in beauty) (s:cingtaakna) (b:kicin) (q:draft)
kicinsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make complete/supply what is lacking) (d:<kicin> be complete with the causative <sak>) (s:kicingsak/cingtaaksak) (b:kicin) (q:draft)
kicinsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:making complete/perfecting) (d:<kicinsak> make complete with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kicinsak) (q:draft)
kicinzawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become complete/be more complete) (d:<kicin> be complete with <zawk>, more) (q:draft, low confidence)
kicip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse/be broken down/be breached) (d:of a wall, break and fall; {kicipna mun} is a breach in a wall) (s:kicim) (q:draft)
kicipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one called/man named) (d:<kici> be called with <pa>, a male person: the man who is called by the name that stands before it) (b:kici) (q:draft)
kicipna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gap/breach) (d:in {kulh a kicipna mun}, the place where a wall is broken through and has to be closed up; built on <kicip> with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kicip) (q:draft, low confidence)
kicisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let say to oneself/let say to each other) (d:<ki> oneself or each other with <cisak> let say) (b:cisak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kicite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those called/those named/those said to be) (d:<kici> be called with <te> plural, usually as {a kicite}) (s:kilote) (b:kici) (r:2.1.15) (q:draft)
kicizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be called instead/be called rather) (d:<kici> be called with <zaw>, rather or instead) (b:kici) (q:draft)
kidaang = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:apart/aloof) (d:in {kidaang koih}, keep oneself apart from someone, avoid; the 1932 spelling of <kidang>) (s:kidang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidaantah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be punished) (d:passive <ki> with <daantah> punish; {a kidaantah ni} is the day of their punishment) (s:kidaantat/kidantat/kidantah) (b:daantah) (r:24.51.18) (q:draft)
kidaantat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be punished) (d:passive <ki> with <daantat> punish) (s:kidantat/kidaantah/kidantah) (b:daantat) (q:draft)
kidaantatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:punishment/being punished) (d:<kidaantat> be punished with the noun suffix <na>) (s:daantatna/kidantahna) (a:thaman) (b:kidaantat) (q:draft)
kidahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sympathize with one another/grieve with each other) (d:<ki> each other with <dahpih> mourn with) (b:dahpih) (q:draft)
kidahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be grieved/be made to mourn) (d:passive <ki> with <dahsak> grieve) (b:dahsak) (q:draft)
kidai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be silent/be still) (d:<dai>, quiet, with <ki>: be silent; {kidai dide} is be utterly silent) (s:daih/gamdaih) (b:dai) (q:draft)
kidaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defile oneself/disgrace oneself/be profaned) (d:reflexive or passive of <daisak>, profane: defile or disgrace oneself, or of a name, be profaned) (s:kininsak/kinitsak) (b:daisak) (q:draft)
kidal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shield oneself/be protected/be fortified) (d:reflexive or passive of <dal>, screen off: shield oneself, or be protected and fortified) (s:kihu) (b:dal) (q:draft)
kidalin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shielding oneself/being covered) (d:<kidal> shield oneself with the connective <in>: protected with shields and helmets) (b:kidal) (q:draft)
kidalna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shield/protection/shielding) (d:that which screens or protects; {kidalna lum} is a shield, {kidalna puan} the shielding curtain and {kidalna kulh} a wall of protection) (s:hutna/kihutna) (b:kidal) (q:draft)
kidalsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sheltered by/under the lee of) (d:<kidal> be shielded with <sak> cause and the connective <in>; {huih kidalsakin} is letting an island keep off the wind, sailing under its lee) (b:kidal) (q:draft)
kidamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be healed/be cured/recover/heal oneself) (d:<ki> form of <damsak>, heal: be healed, have oneself healed or heal oneself; with {thei lo}, of a wound or of anger that cannot be healed) (s:damkik) (b:damsak) (r:12.9.15) (q:draft)
kidamsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be healed again/be cured) (d:<kidamsak> be healed with <kik>, again or back) (b:kidamsak) (q:draft)
kidamsat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be beaten lightly) (d:passive <ki> with <dam> gently and <sat> beat; with <zawdeuh>, be beaten more lightly) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidang = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:apart/aloof) (d:in {kidang koih}, keep oneself apart from someone, avoid) (s:kidaang) (b:dang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidantah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be punished) (d:passive <ki> with <dantah> punish) (s:kidantat/kidaantah/kidaantat) (b:dantah) (q:draft)
kidantahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:punishment) (d:<kidantah> be punished with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kidaantatna/daantahna) (a:thaman) (b:kidantah) (q:draft)
kidantat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be punished/be condemned) (d:passive <ki> with {dantat}, inflict a penalty: be punished or condemned) (s:kidaantat/kidaantah/kidantah) (q:draft)
kidap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lined/be panelled/be covered/be inlaid) (d:be covered over on the inside or surface with boards, leather or other material) (b:dap) (q:draft)
kidawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pulled out/be drawn out) (d:passive <ki> with <dawh> pull out; {kidawh khiatsak}, have something pulled out and taken away) (s:kidokkhia) (b:dawh) (q:draft)
kidawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be set/be planted) (d:in {so kidawh}, of spikes or pitfalls set in a path beside snares) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidawhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pulled out) (d:passive <ki> with <dawhkhiat> pull out) (s:kidokkhia) (b:dawhkhiat) (q:draft)
kidawhkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be snatched away/be pulled out from under) (d:<kidawhkhiat> be pulled out with <sak>, done to someone) (b:kidawhkhiat) (q:draft)
kidawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear/be exposed/be seen) (d:come into view or be uncovered, so that what was hidden or covered can be seen) (s:kilang/kilak) (a:kiseel) become visible
kidawkkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come to light/be exposed/be detected) (d:<kidawk> appear with <khia>, out) (s:kilangkhia) (b:kidawk) (q:draft)
kidawksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:expose/make appear/lay bare) (d:<kidawk> appear with <sak> cause: make something show) (s:dawksak/pholak) (a:seel) (b:kidawk) (q:draft)
kidawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be careful/beware/take heed/guard oneself) (d:watch oneself so as not to fall into something bad; with <loh nadingin> it is be careful not to, and with an object it is beware of someone) (s:kidop/kikem) (q:draft)
kidawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being careful/taking heed/watchfully) (d:<kidawm> be careful with the connective <in>) (s:kikeemin) (b:kidawm) (q:draft)
kidawng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be answered) (d:passive of <dawng> answer; {hong kidawng lo ding}, will go unanswered) (b:dawng) (q:draft)
kidawng = (i:2) (t:v) (w:answer one another/call to each other/answer oneself) (d:reciprocal or reflexive of <dawng> answer) (b:dawng) (q:draft)
kidawngin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:responsively/answering one another) (d:<kidawng> answer one another with the connective <in>: of singing, one group answering the other in turn) (b:kidawng) (q:draft)
kidawngkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be answered/answer back/reply) (d:<kidawng> with <kik> back: the answer that is given in return to a question) (s:dawngkik) (b:kidawng) (q:draft)
kideek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restrain oneself/hold oneself back) (d:the 1977 spelling; the 1932 text has <kidek>) (s:kidek/ki-ipip) (q:draft)
kideeng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stoned/be pelted) (d:passive <ki> with <deeng> throw at; {suang tawh kideeng lum}, be stoned to death) (s:kideng) (b:deeng) (q:draft)
kideidan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be distinguished/be treated differently) (d:passive <ki> with <deidan> discriminate; {kideidan loin} is without distinction, alike) (s:kikhentel) (b:deidan) (q:draft)
kideidanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:distinction/difference/discrimination) (d:<kideidan> with the noun ending <na>: treating people differently from one another; {kideidanna om lo} is there is no distinction) (s:deidanna/kilamdanna) (b:kideidan) (q:draft)
kideih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be wanted/be desired) (d:passive <ki> with <deih> want; {a kideih lo} is unwanted, rejected) (b:deih) (q:draft)
Kideih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:desire each other/love each other) (d:<deih> want or like with the prefix <ki>, each other; written with a capital in a heading) (b:kideih) (q:draft, low confidence)
kideihsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wishing for one another) (d:<ki> each other with <deihsakin> wishing for; {thupha kideihsakin}, wishing one another well) (b:deihsakin) (q:draft, low confidence)
kideina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:partition/dividing off) (d:<deina> partition with <ki>: the place where a room is divided off, as by the temple curtain) (b:deina) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restrain oneself/hold oneself back) (d:hold oneself back from doing something; {a kidek kei uh hi} is they do not restrain themselves) (s:kideek/ki-ipip) (q:draft)
kidekna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:self-control/self-restraint) (d:<kidek> restrain oneself with the noun suffix <na>) (s:ki-ipipna/khamna) (b:kidek) (q:draft)
kidelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be chased/be hunted/be pursued) (d:passive <ki> with <delh>, chase: be chased or hunted; also of chariots rushing along one after another) (b:delh) (q:draft)
kidelhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being pursued/being chased) (d:<kidelh>, be chased, with the linking ending <in>: being pursued, while being chased) (b:kidelh) (q:draft)
kidem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:compete/contend/vie/race) (d:<dem>, contend with, with <ki>, each other: strive to outdo one another, as in a race or contest; {tai kidem} is run a race) (s:kituh) (b:dem) (q:draft)
kidemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:competing/striving/pressing on) (d:<kidem>, compete, with the linking ending <in>: striving as in a race, here of pressing on toward the goal) (b:kidem) (q:draft)
kidemna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rivalry/competition/envy/selfish ambition) (d:<kidem>, compete, with the noun suffix <na>: striving to outdo one another, rivalry or selfish ambition; <tai kidemna> is a running race) (s:demna) (b:kidem) (q:draft)
kidempih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:compete with/rival/be a rival of) (d:<kidem>, compete, with <pih>, together with: have someone as a rival; {i kidempih} is the one we compete with) (b:kidem) (q:draft)
kidemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:competitors/contestants/runners) (d:<kidem>, compete, with <te>, those who: people who take part in a contest; {tai kidemte} are those who run a race) (b:kidem) (q:draft)
kiden = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be dashed down/throw oneself) (d:<den>, throw down, with <ki>, passive or reflexive: be dashed down or throw oneself down; written {kiden’} before <gawp>, <nading> and <na>, and {leilak kiden’na-in} is throwing oneself to the ground) (s:kikhiasuk/kilawnsuk) (b:den) (r:18.41.28) (q:draft)
kideng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stoned/be pelted) (d:<deng>, throw at, with the passive <ki>: have stones thrown at one; {suang tawh kideng} is be stoned and {kideng lum} is be stoned to death) (s:kideeng/kidenglum) (b:deng) (q:draft)
kidengawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being dashed down/dashing to pieces) (d:<dengawpna>, throwing down violently, with the passive <ki>: being dashed to the ground; with <ding>, will be dashed down) (b:dengawpna) (q:draft)
kidengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being stoned/being pelted) (d:<kideng>, be stoned, with the linking ending <in>; {suang tawh kidengin si} is die by being stoned) (b:kideng) (q:draft)
kidengkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be smashed/be shattered/be dashed to pieces) (d:<dengkham>, from <deng> strike and <kham> break, with the passive <ki>: be smashed to pieces, said of a clay pot) (s:kisukham/kitamkham) (b:dengkham) (q:draft)
kidenglum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stoned to death/be stoned) (d:<denglum>, kill by throwing, with the passive <ki>: be put to death by having stones thrown, usually with {suang tawh}, with stones) (s:kideng/kideeng) (b:denglum) (q:draft)
kidenna = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw oneself down/fall upon/plunge into/be dashed down) (d:hurl oneself or be hurled onto or into something, as into the sea or to the ground; {leilak kidenna} is fall or be thrown to the ground; this is the spelling of the 1932 text, the 1977 text writes {kiden’na}) (b:kiden) (r:41.11.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidiah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dip oneself/be dipped/be soaked) (d:<diah>, dip or soak, with <ki>: dip oneself in water, or be dipped or soaked in a liquid such as water or blood) (b:diah) (r:6.3.15) (q:draft)
kidiahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wallowing/soaked/steeped) (d:<kidiah>, be dipped or soaked, with the linking ending <in>: lying soaked in blood, or being steeped in drink) (b:kidiah) (q:draft)
kidiik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sob/groan) (d:weep or groan aloud; probably the same word as <kidik>) (s:kidik) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sob/weep bitterly/mourn) (d:weep with heavy sobs, often together with <kap>, weep) (s:kidiik/thuum) (q:draft)
kidikdik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep sobbing/go on mourning) (d:<kidik>, sob, said twice to show that the weeping goes on and on) (q:draft)
kidiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consider oneself righteous/justify oneself) (d:<ki>, oneself, with <diksak>, declare righteous: regard oneself as being in the right) (s:kitangsak) (b:diksak) (q:draft)
kidiksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:justifying oneself) (d:<kidiksak>, make oneself out to be in the right, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kidiksak) (q:draft)
kidim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fill/be filled/be full) (d:<dim>, full, with <ki>: be filled or be full, with <tawh> for what fills) (b:dim)
kidimin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being filled/filled with/full of) (d:<kidim>, be filled, with the linking ending <in>: being full of or filled with something, with <tawh> for what fills) (b:kidim) (r:44.6.8) (q:draft)
kidimkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be filled again) (d:<kidim>, be filled, with <kik>, again: become full once more, here of a land full of the noise of many people) (b:kidim) (q:draft)
kidimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being filled/filling) (d:<kidim> be filled with the noun suffix <na>: the fact of being full) (b:kidim) (q:draft)
kidimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fill/be filled) (d:<kidim>, be filled, with the causative <sak>: fill someone or something, or be filled, with <tawh> for what fills) (s:dimsak) (b:kidim) (r:26.9.9) (q:draft)
kidimte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are filled/those full of) (d:<kidim> be filled with the plural <te>: people or things that are full of something, here hands full of bribes) (b:kidim) (q:draft)
kidin = (t:see) <kidin'sak>
kidin'sak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set up/be erected) (d:of a tent or building, be made to stand, be put up; written <kidinsak> in the other text) (s:kidinsak/kidingsak) (q:draft)
kiding = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand/be stood up) (d:<ki> with <ding> stand; {kiding sak} is be made to stand upright) (q:draft)
kidingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set up/be made to stand/be erected) (d:<dingsak>, make stand, with the passive <ki>: of a tent, be set up; of a person, be made to stand before others) (s:kidinsak/kiphut) (b:dingsak) (q:draft)
kidinsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set up/be erected) (d:of a tent or building, be made to stand, be put up) (s:kidingsak/kidin'sak) (q:draft)
kido = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fight/wage war/battle) (d:<do>, fight, with <ki>, each other: fight or be at war, with <tawh> for the opponent; {gal kido} is fight a battle) (s:galkido/galdo/kitawng) (a:kilem) (b:do) (q:draft)
kido = (i:2) (t:v) (w:host one another/show hospitality) (d:in {zin kido}, receive one another as guests, offer hospitality to each other) (b:do) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidoin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fighting each other/contending/opposing) (d:<kido>, fight each other, with the linking ending <in>: fighting, contending with or opposing someone) (b:kido) (q:draft)
kidok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be withdrawn/be revoked/be taken back) (d:<dok>, draw out, with the passive <ki>; {kidok kik} is be taken back again, be revoked, said of a decree or a promise) (s:kidokkik/kikhelkik) (b:dok) (q:draft)
kidokik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fight again/be at war again) (d:<kido>, fight each other, with <kik>, again: go to war once more) (b:kido) (q:draft)
kidokkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pulled up/be pulled out) (d:<kidok>, be drawn, with <khia>, out: be pulled out of the ground, said of tent pegs) (s:kibotkhia/kidawh) (b:kidok) (q:draft)
kidokkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be revoked/be withdrawn/be taken back) (d:<kidok>, be drawn, with <kik>, back: be taken back, said of a sealed decree that cannot be undone) (s:kikhelkik) (b:kidok) (q:draft)
kidoksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:drawn/unsheathed) (d:<kidok> be drawn out, with <sa> for a completed action; of a sword out of its sheath) (s:dawhsa) (b:kidok) (q:draft)
kidom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised) (d:<dom>, lift up, with the passive <ki>: be lifted or raised from the ground) (s:kidomto) (b:dom) (q:draft)
kidomkaang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised off) (d:<kidom> be lifted with <kaang>, raised clear of the ground; followed by <to> upward) (s:kidomto) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidomto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised) (d:<domto>, lift up, with the passive <ki>: be lifted or raised, here of a lid) (s:kidom/kilaamto) (a:kikoihsuk) (b:domto) (q:draft)
kidomto = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lift one another up/encourage one another/spur one another on) (d:<domto>, lift up, with <ki>, one another: build each other up, encourage each other toward what is good) (s:kihanthawn/kihansuah) (b:domto) (q:draft)
kidon = (i:1) (t:v) (w:care for oneself/heed one another) (d:<don> care for, with <ki>, which turns the action on oneself or on each other; {note bek a kidon}, who care only for yourselves; {kidon lohna}, not heeding one another) (b:don) (q:draft)
kidona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:war/battle/fighting) (d:<kido>, fight each other, with the noun suffix <na>: war, a battle or fighting; often {gal kidona}) (s:galkidona/galdona/gal) (a:kilemna) (b:kido) (q:draft)
kidonate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wars/battles/fightings) (d:plural of <kidona>; {gal kidonate} is the fighting of war) (s:galkidonate/galdonate) (b:kidona) (q:draft)
kidong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask one another/question each other/discuss) (d:<dong>, ask, with <ki>, each other: ask or question one another, discuss or argue over a matter) (s:kidot/kikum) (b:dong) (r:41.9.10) (q:draft)
kidong = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be betrothed/be pledged in marriage/be asked in marriage) (d:of a girl, to have been asked for as a wife; {a kidong nai lo nungak} is a virgin not yet betrothed) (s:kingai) (b:dong) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidongin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:questioning one another/disputing/arguing) (d:<kidong>, question one another, with the linking ending <in>: disputing or arguing over a matter) (s:kinialin) (b:kidong) (q:draft)
kidongsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:betrothed/engaged/pledged in marriage) (d:<kidong>, be asked in marriage, with <sa> for a completed action: of a woman already promised to a man) (b:kidong) (q:draft)
kidongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those questioning each other/those debating) (d:<kidong> ask one another with the plural <te>; {thu kidongte} may also be read as the questions that were asked) (b:kidong) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidongzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ask one another/keep asking each other) (d:<kidong> ask one another with <zaw>, which seems to add rather or instead) (s:kidong/kidot) (b:kidong) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be careful/take heed/watch oneself) (d:take care to do or to avoid something; with {nak leh}, if only one is careful to; with {kei leh}, unless one takes care) (s:kidawm/kikem/kingaihsun) (q:draft)
kidophuai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:must be careful/ought to take heed) (d:<kidop> be careful with <huai>, worthy of or needing to be done) (q:draft)
kidopzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to restrain oneself/keep in check) (d:<kidop> be careful with <zawh> be able; with <kampau>, keep control of the tongue) (q:draft)
kidosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set against each other/cause to fight) (d:<kido> fight each other with the causative <sak>) (s:kitawngsak) (a:kilemsak) (b:kido) (q:draft)
kidot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be asked/be questioned) (d:<dot>, ask, with the passive <ki>: be asked or questioned) (b:dot) (q:draft)
kidot = (i:2) (t:v) (w:ask one another) (d:<dot> ask, with <ki> in the sense of each other) (s:kidong) (b:dot) (q:draft)
kidotna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:questioning/controversy/dispute) (d:<kidot>, ask one another, with the noun suffix <na>: questioning or dispute; {thu kidotna} is debate over questions) (s:thukidotna/kinialna) (b:kidot) (q:draft)
Kidron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Kidron) (d:valley with a seasonal stream on the east side of Jerusalem, between the city and the Mount of Olives) (r:43.18.1/10.15.23)
kigaan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plaited/be twisted together/be woven) (d:be plaited or woven together; {ling tawh kigaan lukhu} is a crown plaited of thorns) (s:kigan) (q:draft)
kigaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shudder/be appalled/be horrified) (d:be struck with horror or dread at what one sees or hears, often with <lau>, fear, or {lamdang sa}, be astonished) (s:lipkhap/mulkim/dipkua) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigaih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be chewed/be consumed) (d:of food in the mouth) (b:gaih) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigaihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:startled/appalled/shuddering) (d:<kigaih>, shudder, with the linking ending <in>: startled, struck with horror) (b:kigaih) (q:draft)
