kihah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be forced/be compelled) (d:in {kihah piak}, of drink pressed on a guest) (b:hah) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be foolish/act foolishly) (d:seen in {kihai muan}, trust in oneself foolishly, be conceited, and {thu kihai seelna}, foolish argument) (b:hai) (r:55.2.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihaibawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be deceived/fool oneself) (d:<kihai>, be foolish, with <bawl>, make: make a fool of oneself; negated, do not be deceived) (s:kikheem) (b:kihai) (q:draft)
kihaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sifted/be winnowed) (d:passive of <haih>, sift, with <ki>: be shaken in a sieve) (b:haih) (q:draft)
kihaimuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conceit/presumption/pride) (d:{kihai muan}, trust in oneself foolishly, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kiphatsakna/kisaktheihna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (q:draft)
kihal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be burned/be burnt) (d:passive of <hal>, burn: be burned with fire; {mei tawh kihal biakna} is an offering burned with fire) (s:kikhul) (b:hal) (r:4.15.10) (q:draft)
kihalin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at a distance/far off/apart) (d:<kihal>, keep apart, with <in>: keeping a distance from someone; often with <gamla>, far) (r:40.26.58) (q:draft)
kihalin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be burned/be set on fire) (d:<kihal>, be burned, with the linking ending <in>: being burned) (b:kihal) (q:draft)
kihalkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be burned again) (d:<kihal>, be burned, with <kik>, again) (b:kihal) (q:draft)
kihallum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be burned to death) (d:passive of <hallum>, burn to death, with <ki>; {mei tawh kihallum} is be burned to death with fire) (b:hallum) (q:draft)
kihalna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:burning/place of burning) (d:<kihal>, be burned, with the noun suffix <na>: the burning of something; {kihalna mun} is the place where it is burned, the hearth of an altar) (s:kikhulna/halna) (b:kihal) (q:draft)
kihalna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:distance/gap/space between) (d:the space kept between two things) (s:gamlatna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihalnelhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be burned up/burn oneself up) (d:<kihal> be burned with <nelh>, apparently completely, and <in>: being burned up with the house) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihalsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep apart/leave a space between) (d:make a gap between things, which are named with <kikal>, between) (q:draft)
kihalsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be burned/be set on fire) (d:<kihal>, be burned, with <sak>: be set on fire by someone) (b:kihal) (q:draft)
kihalsan = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:glowing/red-hot/burnished) (d:<kihal>, be burned, with <san>, red: heated in the fire until it glows; said of bronze) (b:kihal) (q:draft)
kihaltum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be burned up/be set on fire/be consumed) (d:passive of <haltum>, burn up, with <ki>: be completely burned) (s:kikhultum) (b:haltum) (q:draft)
kihaltumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being burned/burning) (d:passive <ki> with <haltum> burn up and the noun suffix <na>: being given over to be burned) (b:kihaltum) (q:draft)
kihamsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curse/object of cursing) (d:a person or place that people name when they curse; {kihamsiatna-in zang} is use as a curse) (s:kihaamsiatna/hamsiatna/samsiatna) (b:hamsiatna) (q:draft)
kihanga = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid on a fire/be roasted) (d:said of fish and bread lying on burning coals; exact sense of the root not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihangkeu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be roasted/be parched) (d:of grain, be dried by roasting over fire) (q:draft)
kihangsak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:courage) (d:the call to make oneself brave; {kihangsak in} means take courage) (s:hang) (b:hangsak)
kihangsak = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:brave/plucky/fearless/valiant/valorous/intrepid/heroic) (d:<hangsak>, make brave, with <ki>, oneself: showing courage and not giving way to fear) (s:hang) (a:lau/meidawi) (b:hangsak)
Kihangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be strong/be brave/take courage) (d:<kihangsak>, make oneself brave, at the start of a sentence; {Kihangsak in} is the command be strong) (s:kipasalsak/Kihat) (b:kihangsak) (r:27.10.19) (q:draft)
kihansuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:encourage one another/exhort one another) (d:<hansuah>, urge on, with <ki> in the sense of each other: encourage one another) (s:kihanthawn/kidomto) (b:hansuah) (q:draft)
kihanthawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:encourage one another/spur one another on) (d:<hanthawn>, stir up, with <ki>, one another: urge each other on to do something good) (s:kihansuah/kidomto) (b:hanthawn) (q:draft)
kihanthawn = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be stirred up/rouse oneself) (d:<hanthawn>, stir up, with <ki>, oneself: be roused or rouse oneself to act; often followed by <tawm>, by oneself) (s:kisosuah/thotawm) (b:hanthawn) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihanthawnin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking courage/rousing oneself/encouraging one another) (d:<kihanthawn> with the linking suffix <in>: the person or group gathers courage and then goes on to act) (b:kihanthawn) (q:draft)
kihanthawntawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rouse oneself/stir oneself up) (d:<kihanthawn>, rouse oneself, with <tawm>, by oneself: stir oneself into action; the NIV has take notice here) (s:kisosuah/thotawm) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kihat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be strong/strengthen oneself) (d:<hat>, strong, with <ki>, oneself, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {Kihat sak in} means make yourself strong) (s:kithakhauhsak) (q:draft)
kihatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strengthen oneself/make oneself strong) (d:<hatsak>, strengthen, with <ki>, oneself; with <tawm>, by one's own effort: build up one's own power or position) (s:kithakhauhsak) (b:hatsak) (q:draft)
kihau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be had in plenty/be abundant) (d:<hau>, rich, with <ki>: of grain or a harvest, be got in abundance) (b:hau) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihau = (i:2) (t:v) (w:pretend to be rich) (d:in {kihau sak}, make oneself out to be rich, the opposite of <kizawngsak>, pretend to be poor) (s:kihausak) (a:kizawngsak) (b:hau) (q:draft)
kihauh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plentiful/abound) (d:of food or harvest, be in abundance; {a kihauh kum} is a year of plenty) (b:hauh) (q:draft)
kihauhlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get rich by/be enriched by) (d:<hauhlawh>, get rich from, with <ki>; {kihauhlawh tuan lo} means one is none the richer for it) (a:kizawnlawh) (b:hauhlawh) (q:draft)
kihausak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pretend to be rich/make oneself out to be rich) (d:<hausak>, make rich, with <ki>, oneself: act as if one were rich) (s:kihau) (a:kizawngsak) (b:hausak) (q:draft)
kihawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stripped off/be torn off) (d:passive <ki> with <hawk> strip off; said of skirts) (b:hawk) (q:draft)
kihawkgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be torn off/be stripped off violently) (d:<kihawk> be stripped off with <gawp>, roughly or thoroughly) (b:kihawk) (q:draft)
kihawkkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be robbed/be stripped away) (d:<hawkkhia>, strip off, with passive <ki>: have one's goods taken by force) (s:kisut/kiluh) (b:hawkkhia) (q:draft)
kihawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be driven/be driven out/be banished) (d:passive of <hawl>, drive: usually with <khia>, be driven out of a place; {hong kihawl gawpgawp} is be driven hard) (s:kinotkhia/kinawhkhia/kisawnkhia) (b:hawl) (q:draft)
kihawlkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be driven out/be cut off/be banished) (d:<hawlkhia>, drive out, with passive <ki>: be driven out of a place, or be cut off from one's people) (s:kinotkhia/kinawhkhia/kisawnkhia) (b:hawlkhia) (r:18.30.8) (q:draft)
kihawlkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be driven out/be expelled) (d:form of <kihawlkhia> used before words such as <khit>, <theih> and <nading>) (b:kihawlkhia) (r:42.11.24) (q:draft)
kihawlkhiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:exiles/outcasts/those driven out) (d:<kihawlkhia>, be driven out, with <te>, those who: people driven from their land) (s:hawlkhiatte) (b:kihawlkhia) (q:draft)
kihawlkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being driven out/expulsion) (d:<kihawlkhiat> be driven out, with the noun suffix <na>; before a noun of place, the place from which or to which one was driven) (s:kisuankhiatna) (b:kihawlkhiat) (q:draft)
kihawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be divided/be distributed/be shared out) (d:<hawm>, distribute, with passive <ki>: of land, spoils or goods, be divided and shared out) (b:hawm) (r:17.1.7) (q:draft)
kihawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being distributed/being issued/being sent out) (d:<kihawm>, be distributed, with the linking suffix <in>: said of an order sent out to every province) (b:kihawm) (q:draft)
kihawmkeek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be divided up/be shared out) (d:<kihawm> be divided with <keek>, apart into portions; said of spoils) (q:draft)
kihawmkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be issued/be published/be distributed) (d:<hawmkhia>, give out, with passive <ki>: of an order or letter, be sent out and made known to the people) (b:hawmkhia) (q:draft)
kihawmkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be distributed/be sent out) (d:<kihawm> be distributed with <kik> again or in turn; said of letters sent to each official) (b:kihawm) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sharing/distribution) (d:<kihawm> be shared out with the noun suffix <na>) (s:hawmna) (b:kihawm) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihawmsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be distributed/be divided out/be sent out) (d:passive <ki> with <hawmsak> distribute; of land shared out by lot and of letters sent round) (b:hawmsak) (q:draft)
kihawmsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be emptied/be laid waste) (d:<hawmsuak> become empty with <ki>; {kihawmsuak sakin} is being made utterly empty) (s:kisiacip) (b:hawmsuak) (q:draft)
kihaza = (i:1) (t:v) (w:envy one another/be jealous of one another) (d:<haza> envy with <ki>, one another) (b:haza) (q:draft)
kihazatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:envy of one another/mutual jealousy) (d:<hazatna>, envy, with <ki>, each other: jealousy between people) (b:hazatna) (q:draft)
kihazatnate = (t:see) <kihazatnate-in>
kihazatnate-in = (i:1) (t:n) (w:jealousies/envyings) (d:plural of <kihazatna> envy of one another, with <in>: in or by jealousies) (q:draft)
kihbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scorn/abhor/loathe) (d:<kih>, detest, with <bawl>, do to: treat with loathing) (s:mudah/hua) (b:kih) (q:draft)
kiheek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be twisted/writhe) (d:passive or reflexive of <heek> twist: of cord, be twisted or plaited; of a person in pain, writhe) (s:kihual) (b:heek) (q:draft)
kiheek = (i:2) (t:v) (w:betray one another/be betrayed/be handed over) (d:reciprocal or passive of <heek> in its sense of betraying, handing a person over to those who will harm him) (s:kilehhek/kilehheek) (b:heek) (r:42.9.44) (q:draft)
kiheekgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be twisted/be wrung violently) (d:<ki> with <heek> twist and <gawp>, roughly; with <sak>, cause trees to twist) (b:kiheek) (q:draft)
kiheekheek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:writhe/twist about) (d:<ki> with <heek> twist doubled: twist oneself again and again, as in labour pains) (s:kipeek/kitom) (q:draft)
kiheh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be angry with oneself/be angry at each other) (d:<ki> with <heh> angry; {kiheh tawm} is be angry with oneself) (b:heh) (q:draft)
kihehnem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort oneself/be comforted/comfort one another) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, with <ki>, oneself or one another: be comforted, console oneself, or comfort each other) (s:kinem/kinuamsak) (b:hehnem) (q:draft)
kihehnep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be comforted/be encouraged) (d:passive <ki> with <hehnep> comfort; {lungsim kihehnep nadingin} is so that hearts may be encouraged) (s:kinem) (b:hehnep) (q:draft)
kihehnepna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:comfort/consolation/encouragement) (d:<hehnepna>, comfort, with <ki>: the comfort a person receives, or the comforting of one another) (b:hehnepna) (q:draft)
kihehpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have compassion on one another/be kind to one another) (d:<hehpih> pity with <ki>, one another) (b:hehpih) (q:draft)
kihehpih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be shown mercy/be pitied) (d:passive <ki> with <hehpih> pity; {kihehpih hetloin} is without any mercy) (b:hehpih) (q:draft)
kihehpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:having compassion on one another/being kind to one another) (d:<kihehpih> with the connective <in>) (b:kihehpih) (q:draft)
kihehtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be angry with oneself) (d:<ki> with <heh> angry and <tawm>, toward oneself) (q:draft)
kihei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn/turn round/turn back/return) (d:turn oneself round or toward something; with <lamah> or <kiangah>, turn to a person or direction; {kihei kik} means turn back) (s:kileh) (b:hei) (r:42.9.55) (q:draft)
Kihei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn/turn back) (d:<kihei> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or of quoted speech, mostly as a command) (b:kihei) (q:draft)
kiheihei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn to and fro/keep turning) (d:<hei> turn with <ki>, turn oneself, repeated to show that the action goes on; of a door on its hinges) (b:heihei) (q:draft)
kiheikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away/turn aside/step aside) (d:turn oneself away from a place or person; also turn away in disloyalty) (s:pialkhia) (b:kihei) (q:draft)
kiheikhial = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:perverse/wayward) (d:<kihei> turn with <khial> wrong: turned the wrong way) (q:draft)
kiheikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away/turn aside) (d:form of <kiheikhia> used before <loh>, <theih> and <nading>: turn away from a person, or of anger, turn away from those it rested on) (b:kiheikhia) (q:draft)
kiheikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn back/return/revert/repent) (d:<kihei>, turn, with <kik>, back or again: turn back to a person or away from a way of life) (s:kilehkik) (b:kihei) (r:24.15.7) (q:draft)
kiheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not turn/not turn aside) (d:<kihei> turn with the negative <lo>) (b:kihei) (q:draft)
kiheina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:turning/turn/conversion) (d:<kihei> turn with <na>: a turning, the place one turns to, a turn of events, or a turning to God) (b:kihei) (r:9.14.47) (q:draft)
kiheisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn/make turn/turn back) (d:<kihei> with causative <sak>: cause a person, a heart or an animal to turn toward or away from something; {kiheisak kik} is bring back) (b:kihei) (q:draft)
kiheisan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away from/turn aside from) (d:<kihei>, turn, with <san>, away from someone, leaving him behind) (s:lehngatsan/paisan) (b:kihei) (q:draft)
kiheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who turn) (d:<kihei> turn with <te>, those who: people who turn to God) (b:kihei) (q:draft)
kihel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be mixed/mingle/be mingled) (d:be mixed with something, which is named with <tawh>; also of peoples mingling with each other) (q:draft)
kihel = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be included/take part/join in/be among) (d:be one of a group or join in what it does; {kihel lo} is not counted among, and {kihel loin} is without, apart from) (r:4.23.9) (q:draft)
kihelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:alternate/be set by turns) (d:of two kinds of things, be placed one after the other in turn; a form of <kihel> be mixed) (s:kilaih) (b:kihel) (q:draft)
kihelhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:alternate/set by turns) (d:<kihelh> alternate with causative <sak>: place two kinds of things one after the other) (b:kihelh) (q:draft)
kihelhto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:alternate/follow one after another) (d:<kihelh> alternate with <to>, onward in sequence) (b:kihelh) (q:draft)
kihelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:mingling/joining/being included) (d:<kihel> with the linking suffix <in>; with <tawh> it is mixing with something or joining someone) (b:kihel) (q:draft)
kihelkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be mixed together/be alloyed) (d:<kihel> be mixed with <khawm>, together; of metals melted together) (b:kihel) (q:draft)
kihelkhawm = (i:2) (t:v) (w:take part in together/share in) (d:join in two things at once) (b:kihel) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihelkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fully mixed/be well mixed) (d:<kihel> be mixed with <kim>, completely; of wine mixed with spices) (q:draft)
kihelkim = (i:2) (t:v) (w:take part from each/be included from all) (d:<kihel> take part with <kim>, every: let each group be represented) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihelpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be mixed with) (d:<kihel> be mixed with <pih> together with; {na kihelpih na nin} is the impurity that is mixed in with you) (b:kihel) (q:draft)
kihelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be counted among/let take part/include) (d:<kihel> be included with <sak> cause: cause or allow someone to be included) (b:kihel) (q:draft)
kihelte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those included/those among/those mixed) (d:<kihel> with <te> plural: people counted among a group, or things mixed with something) (b:kihel) (q:draft)
kihem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:depart/turn away/withdraw/separate oneself) (d:move oneself away from a place, a group or evil) (q:draft)
kihemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:departing/moving away/being removed) (d:<kihem> with the linking suffix <in>: the moving away is followed by another action) (b:kihem) (q:draft)
kihemkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:depart/withdraw/turn away) (d:<kihem>, move away, with <khia>, out; with <panin>, move away from a person, a task or evil) (s:pialkhia) (q:draft)
kihen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bound/be tied/be chained) (d:<hen>, bind, with passive <ki>: be tied or chained; also of what is bound in heaven, the opposite of <kiphel>, be loosed) (s:kikhih) (a:kiphel) (b:hen) (r:40.16.19) (q:draft)
kihencip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bound/be tied up) (d:<hencip>, bind fast, with passive <ki>: be tied up tightly; in Job 5:16 of the unjust being silenced) (s:kikhih) (b:hencip) (q:draft)
kihencipna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bondage/being bound/bond) (d:<kihencip> be bound fast with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kihencip) (q:draft)
kihenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being bound/being tied) (d:<kihen>, be bound, with the linking suffix <in>; with <tawh>, being bound to someone) (b:kihen) (q:draft)
kihenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bonds/chains/imprisonment) (d:<kihen>, be bound, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being bound, or the cords and chains that bind) (s:kikhihna/sikkol) (b:kihen) (q:draft)
kihennate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chains/bonds/fetters) (d:plural of <kihenna>, that which binds) (s:kikhihnate) (b:kihenna) (q:draft)
kihensa = (t:see) <kihensa-in>
kihensa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:bound/already bound) (d:<kihen> be bound with <sa> already and <in>: in a bound state) (q:draft)
kihente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bundles/pouches) (d:<kihen> be tied with the plural <te>: things tied up; {sum kihente} are bundles or pouches of money) (b:kihen) (q:draft)
kihep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:part from/separate from) (d:seen only in {kihep khiat}, go away from someone) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihepkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:withdraw/go away/depart) (d:leave a person or place; form used before <ciangin> and <khit>) (q:draft)
kihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:detestable/disgusting/unclean/abominable) (d:so unclean or wicked that it is to be loathed; said of forbidden food, idols and sinful acts) (s:muhdahhuai/nin) (a:siangtho/limci) (r:42.4.33) (q:draft)
kihhuaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:abomination/detestable thing/impurity) (d:<kihhuai>, detestable, with the noun suffix <na>: something disgusting or unclean, or the state of being so) (s:muhdahhuaina/nitna) (a:siangthona) (b:kihhuai) (r:52.4.7) (q:draft)
kihhuainate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:abominations/detestable things/detestable practices) (d:plural of <kihhuaina>: detestable things, acts or idols) (s:kihhuaite) (b:kihhuaina) (r:66.17.5) (q:draft)
Kihhuainate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:abominations/detestable things) (d:<kihhuainate> written with a capital in a title) (b:kihhuainate) (q:draft)
kihhuaisa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:detest/regard as detestable) (d:<kihhuai>, detestable, with <sa>, consider: find something loathsome) (s:mudah/hua) (b:kihhuai) (q:draft)
kihhuaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defile/pollute/make detestable) (d:<kihhuai>, detestable, with causative <sak>: make a thing or oneself unclean) (s:ninsak/nitsak) (a:siansuah/siangthosak) (b:kihhuai) (q:draft)
kihhuaisapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who abhors/one who detests) (d:<kihhuaisa> regard as detestable with <pa>, the man who does so) (b:kihhuaisa) (q:draft)
kihhuaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:detestable things/abominations) (d:<kihhuai> with plural <te>; also follows a noun as detestable, said of several things) (s:kihhuainate) (b:kihhuai) (q:draft)
kihial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rolled up) (d:passive <ki> with <hial> roll up, as a weaver rolls up cloth) (s:kizial) (b:hial) (q:draft)
kihih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be done) (d:<hih>, do, with passive <ki>: something is done, or is done to or for a person, who is named with <tungah>) (s:kisem) (q:draft)
kihihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quarrel/conflict/fight) (d:<kihih>, do to one another, with <na>: a clash or dealings between two sides) (b:kihih) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be proud/boast/be arrogant) (d:carry oneself proudly; {kihihsak pih} is boast in or put trust in something) (s:kiphasak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat) (q:draft)
kihihsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be done for) (d:passive of <hihsak>: something is done for or on behalf of a person, who is named with <ading>) (b:hihsak) (q:draft)
kihihsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/haughtiness) (d:<kihihsak>, be proud, with the noun suffix <na>: pride that makes oneself out to be great) (s:kiphatsakna/kiliatsakna/kisaktheihna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (b:kihihsak) (q:draft)
kihihsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:arrogance/insolence/proud acts) (d:plural of <kihihsakna>, from <kihihsak> be proud) (s:kiphatsaknate) (b:kihihsakna) (q:draft)
kihihsakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trust in/boast in/take pride in) (d:<kihihsak> be proud with <pih>: be proud of something and rely on it) (s:kisaktheihpih/kiphatsakpih/kisialhpih) (b:kihihsak) (q:draft)
kihihthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be done/be permissible) (d:<kihih> be done with <thei> be able) (b:kihih) (q:draft)
kihil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shown/be made known) (d:be shown or made known by a sign, probably a form of <kihilh>, be told; {bang limin hong kihil ding} asks by what sign something will be made known) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taught/be preached/be told) (d:passive of <hilh>, teach: be taught, told or preached; {Lungdamna Thu kihilh} means the gospel is preached) (b:hilh) (r:23.28.26) (q:draft)
Kihilhhilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taught again and again/be rebuked often) (d:<kihilh>, be taught, with <hilh> doubled for a repeated action: be taught or corrected again and again; written with a capital at the start of the sentence) (q:draft)
kihilhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teaching one another/instructing one another) (d:<kihilh> with the linking suffix <in>, here with <ki> in the sense of each other: teaching one another) (b:kihilh) (q:draft)
kihilhin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:being preached/being proclaimed) (d:<kihilh> with the linking suffix <in>, here passive: a message being taught or announced) (b:kihilh) (q:draft)
kihilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:instruction/discipline/correction/teaching) (d:<kihilh>, be taught, with the noun suffix <na>: the teaching or correction that one is given; {thu kihilhna zui} is follow instruction) (s:thuhilhna/hilhna) (b:kihilh) (r:20.10.17) (q:draft)
kihilhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:instructions/teachings) (d:<kihilhna>, instruction, with the plural <te>: the things that are taught to someone) (s:hilhnate/thuhilhnate/kihilhte) (b:kihilhna) (q:draft)
kihilhsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:trained/taught) (d:that has already been taught or trained, <sa> marks a completed action) (s:kiseksa) (b:kihilh) (q:draft)
kihilhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let teach/have oneself taught) (d:<hilhsak> cause to teach with <ki> oneself; the verse follows the older English wording, let your right hand teach you awesome deeds) (b:hilhsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teachings/instruction/things taught) (d:<kihilh> be taught with the plural <te>: the things one is taught) (s:kihilhnate/hilhnate) (b:kihilh) (q:draft)
kihilhtelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:explanation/what has been explained) (d:passive <ki> with <hilhtelna> explanation: the explaining that was given to someone) (b:hilhtelna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilhthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to teach one another/be able to instruct each other) (d:<ki> each other with <hilh> teach and <thei> be able) (b:kihilh) (q:draft)
kihilkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go back/return) (d:meaning taken from the verse, not to go back to Herod; with <kik> back; the relation to <kihil> be made known is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sign/symbol/omen/warning) (d:a sign or indication of what will happen, also a warning that is given, as in a dream; {kihilna lim} in Numbers is an omen sought by divination) (b:kihil) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihing = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kept alive/be made alive) (d:passive of <hing>; {kihing khawi} is to be spared and allowed to live, {kihing kiksak} is to be raised to life again) (a:kithat) (b:hing) (q:draft)
kihingkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised to life again/be made alive again) (d:<ki> with <hingkik> come back to life; followed by <sak>, be raised again) (b:hingkik) (q:draft)
kihingkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised to life/be raised from the dead) (d:passive of <hingkiksak>, make alive again) (s:kihingsakkik/kithokiksak) (b:hingkiksak) (q:draft)
kihingsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised to life/be brought back to life) (d:passive <ki> with <hingsakkik> bring back to life) (s:kihingkiksak/kithokiksak) (b:hingsakkik) (q:draft)
kihisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be proud/be arrogant/be haughty) (d:think much of oneself, be proud or arrogant; {mi kihisak} is a proud person, the opposite of one who humbles himself) (s:kiphasak/kiliansak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (r:20.21.24) (q:draft)
kihisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be arrogant/be proud/be haughty) (d:<kihisak> with the linking suffix <in>) (s:kiphasakin) (a:kiniamkhiatin) (b:kihisak) (q:draft)
kihisakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant/the haughty) (d:<kihisak>, be proud, with the plural <te>: people who think highly of themselves) (s:kiphasakte/kiliansakte) (a:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kihisak) (q:draft)
kiho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:talk together/converse/speak with) (d:talk with one another; the person spoken with is marked by <tawh>, with) (s:kihokhawm/kihopih/kihoho) (r:7.14.7) (q:draft)
kihoho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:converse/talk together/commune) (d:talk with one another at length, <kiho> with <ho> repeated for an action that goes on; in Psalm 77:6 of communing with one's own heart) (s:kiho/kihokhawm) (b:hoho) (q:draft)
kihoin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:talking with/speaking with) (d:<kiho> talk together with the connective <in>) (b:kiho) (q:draft)
kihokhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:talk together/speak with) (d:<kiho> converse with <khawm> together) (s:kiho/kihopih) (b:kiho) (q:draft)
kihon = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be saved/be rescued/be delivered) (d:passive of <hon>, save: be saved or rescued, with <panin> for the enemy or danger) (s:kihonkhia/kihotkhiat) (b:hon) (q:draft)
kihon = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be opened/open) (d:passive of <hon>, open; of a door or a way) (s:kihong) (a:kikhak) (b:hon) (r:44.14.27) (q:draft)
kihona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conversation/talk/talking together) (d:<kiho> talk together with <na>: the talking, or with <mun> the place where they talked) (s:kihopihna) (b:kiho) (q:draft)
kihong = (i:2) (t:v) (w:extend)
kihongin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:opening/being opened) (d:<kihong>, be opened, with the linking suffix <in>: the opening is followed by what happens next) (b:kihong) (q:draft)
kihongkek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken open/burst open) (d:<kihong> open with <kek>, apparently split or wide apart; said of city walls or gates) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihongsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:open/opened) (d:<kihong> be opened, with <sa> for a completed action; {a kihongsa hankhuk}, an open grave) (s:honsa) (a:khaksa) (b:kihong) (q:draft)
kihongsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:open/let open) (d:<kihong> open with causative <sak>: cause to open up) (b:kihong) (q:draft)
kihongtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:open by itself/open of its own accord) (d:<kihong> open with <tawm>, by itself) (q:draft)
kihonkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be saved/be rescued/escape) (d:passive of <honkhia>, rescue: be saved or delivered out of danger) (s:kihon/kihotkhiat) (b:honkhia) (q:draft)
kihonkhiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be delivered/be saved/be safe) (d:<kihonkhia>, be rescued, with <zo> for a completed action: have been delivered, be safe) (b:kihonkhia) (q:draft)
kihonsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be saved by/let save) (d:<honsak>, cause to save, with <ki>: let oneself be saved by someone; used in taunts such as let your idols save you) (b:honsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihontawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:save oneself/deliver oneself) (d:<hon> save with <ki> and <tawm> by oneself) (q:draft)
kihonthahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:slaughter/massacre) (d:apparently <ki> with <hon> in numbers, <that> kill and the noun suffix <na>: killing of many together) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihopih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:greet one another/speak with/have fellowship with) (d:speak with each other; in the letters, greet one another and share fellowship) (s:kiho/kihokhawm) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
kihopihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:greeting one another/talking with one another) (d:<kihopih> speak with each other with the connective <in>) (b:kihopih) (q:draft)
kihopihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:talking with/conversation) (d:<kihopih> speak with and the noun suffix <na>) (s:kihona) (b:kihopih) (q:draft)
kihot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rowed) (d:passive of <hot>, row a boat) (b:hot) (q:draft)
kihot = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be tossed/be stirred up) (d:of water driven about in a storm) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihothei = (t:see) <kihothei-in>
kihothei-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to talk together/have fellowship) (d:<kiho> converse with <thei> be able and <in>; in this verse, having fellowship with one another) (q:draft)
kihotheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fellowship/communion) (d:<kiho> talk together with <theih> can and the noun suffix <na>: being able to speak with one another, fellowship) (q:draft)
kihotkhiana = (i:1) (t:n) (w:salvation/deliverance) (d:being saved, from {hotkhia} save; {ka kihotkhiana ki} is the horn of my salvation) (s:kihotkhiatna/hotkhiatna) (q:draft)
kihotkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be saved/be rescued/be redeemed) (d:<hotkhiat> save with {ki-}, here passive; the form used before words such as <theih> and <ding>) (s:kihonkhia/kihon) (b:hotkhiat) (q:draft)
kihotkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:salvation/deliverance/rescue) (d:being saved or delivered; used also of God as the one who saves) (s:hotkhiatna/gupna/hotna/kihotkhiana) (b:hotkhiatna) (q:draft)
kihozaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak to one another/talk together) (d:<kiho> converse with <zaw>, apparently rather or instead; here speak to each other with a gentle heart) (b:kiho) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fear/be afraid of/dread) (d:be afraid of someone or something, the thing feared standing before the verb; {kihta kei un} means do not be afraid) (s:lau) (r:42.18.2) (q:draft)
kihtak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fear/dread/be afraid of) (d:form of <kihta>, fear, used before nouns and endings: {na kihtak mite} are the people you fear, and {kihtak-huai} is fearsome or awesome) (b:kihta) (q:draft)
kihtakhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:awesome/fearful/dreadful/terrible) (d:causing fear or awe, from <kihtak>, fear, with <huai>, worthy of; said of God, of darkness, wild beasts and judgments) (s:lauhuai/mulkimhuai) (q:draft)
kihtakhuaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dreadfulness/terror) (d:<kihtakhuai> fearful with the noun suffix <na>: the fear one inspires in others) (b:kihtakhuai) (q:draft)
kihtakhuaipen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:most terrible/most fearful/most ruthless) (d:<kihtakhuai>, fearful, with the superlative <pen>) (b:kihtakhuai) (q:draft)
kihtakhuaite = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fearsome/dreadful/dangerous) (d:<kihtakhuai> with the plural <te>, which belongs to the whole phrase: {gamsa kihtakhuaite} are fierce wild beasts) (b:kihtakhuai) (q:draft)
kihtakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fearing/dreading/in fear of) (d:<kihtak> fear with the connective <in>; {kihtakin nei} is hold in dread) (b:kihtak) (q:draft)
kihtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fear/dread/reverence) (d:<kihtak>, fear, with the noun suffix <na>: fear or dread of someone, also reverent fear of God; the one feared stands before the word) (s:launa) (a:hanna) (b:kihtak) (r:45.3.18) (q:draft)
kihtaktak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dread/fear greatly) (d:<kihtak> with its last syllable repeated; {a kihtaktak} is the very thing that someone fears) (s:laulau) (b:kihtak) (q:draft)
kihtakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things feared/what one fears) (d:<kihtak> fear with the plural <te>: the things that someone is afraid of) (b:kihtak) (q:draft)
kihtalua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be very afraid/be terrified) (d:<kihta>, fear, with <lua>, too much or exceedingly) (s:laulua) (b:kihta) (q:draft)
kihtate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who fear) (d:<kihta>, fear, with the plural <te>: the people who fear; {Pasian a kihtate}, those who fear God) (s:laute/zahtakte) (b:kihta) (q:draft)
kihtazaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fear rather/fear more) (d:<kihta>, fear, with <zaw>, more or rather) (b:kihta) (q:draft)
kihtha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:loathe/find repulsive) (d:feel disgust at something, here at food) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be protected/be defended/be rescued) (d:passive of <hu>, defend or shield; {kihu tawm} is defend oneself) (b:hu) (q:draft)
kihuaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:impurity/uncleanness) (d:something disgusting or unclean, here impure motives; apparently <kih>, loathe, with <huai> and the noun suffix <na>) (s:kihhuaina) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihual = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be braided/be twisted) (d:be twisted together like the strands of a rope) (s:kihuiheek/kiheek) (q:draft)
kihual = (i:2) (t:v) (w:unite/be knit together/embrace) (d:be bound up with one another, as hearts that are knit together or as righteousness and peace that embrace) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihualsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roll over/drive over) (d:with <sak> cause: make the wheel of a threshing cart roll round over the grain) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cooked/be boiled) (d:passive of <huan>, to cook; before a noun it means cooked, as in {a kihuan an}, cooked food) (q:draft)
kihuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cooking/being cooked) (d:<kihuan> be cooked with the noun suffix <na>; {a kihuanna leibeel} is the clay pot in which it was cooked) (b:kihuan) (q:draft)
kihuansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:boiled/cooked) (d:<kihuan> be cooked, with <sa> for a completed action; in Ezekiel 27:18 said of iron, apparently worked or wrought) (s:huansa/minsa) (b:kihuan) (q:draft)
kihuau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:whisper/whisper together) (d:speak in a low voice to one another; in the verses always {kihuau sim}, whisper in secret) (s:kihuauhuau) (b:huau) (q:draft)
kihuauhuau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:whisper together/whisper among themselves) (d:<huau> whisper said twice, with <ki> one another) (s:kihuau) (q:draft)
kihuauna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whispering) (d:<kihuau> whisper to one another, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kihuau) (q:draft)
kihubing = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stopped/be shut/be silenced) (d:of the mouth, be stopped up so that it cannot speak) (q:draft)
kihuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be helped/help one another) (d:<huh>, help, with <ki>: passive, be helped, or with <ciat> or {khat leh khat}, help one another) (b:huh) (q:draft)
kihuhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:helping one another) (d:<kihuh> with the linking suffix <in>; after {khat leh khat}, helping each other) (b:kihuh) (q:draft)
kihuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:help/aid/mutual help) (d:help that is given to someone, or helping one another) (b:huhna) (q:draft)
kihuhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let help/have helped) (d:<kihuh>, be helped, with the causative <sak>: let someone be helped by another) (b:kihuh) (q:draft)
kihuhzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:help one another rather/help one another more) (d:<kihuh> with <zaw>, more or rather; after <khatlekhat>, help each other) (b:kihuh) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihui = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:narrow/sloping) (d:of windows, made narrowing or slanting toward the outside) (r:26.41.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihuiheek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be twisted/be interwoven/turn crooked) (d:of chains, be twisted together; of people, warp like a faulty bow) (s:kihuihek/kihual) (b:huiheek) (q:draft)
kihuihek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be twisted/be interwoven) (d:of chains, be twisted or plaited together) (s:kihuiheek) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:closing/covering) (d:passive <ki> with <hukna> cover; {hankhuk kihukna suangtum} is the stone with which the tomb is closed) (b:hukna) (q:draft)
kihupsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be swallowed down/go down) (d:passive <ki> with <hup> suck in and <suk> down) (q:draft)
kihut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defend oneself/protect oneself) (d:form of <kihu> used before <nading>; {kihut nadingin} means for defense, for protection, <panin> marks the danger) (s:kihutawm) (b:kihu) (q:draft)
kihutawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defend oneself/protect oneself) (d:<hu>, protect, with <ki> and <tawm>, do to oneself; {a kihutawm zo lo}, unable to defend itself) (s:kihut) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defence/protection/shield) (d:<kihut>, defend oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: defence or protection, a shield, also a defence spoken in court) (s:hutna/kidalna) (b:kihut) (q:draft)
kihzah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disgusted/loathe) (d:feel disgust toward someone; here of turning away in disgust) (q:draft, low confidence)
kii = (i:1) (t:n) (w:horn) (d:horn of an animal, here a figure for a mighty saviour, the horn of salvation) (s:ki) (q:draft, the verse shown corresponds to Luke 1 verse 69 in the NIV)
kiim = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around) (d:the area around a person or place; follows the noun, often with <ah> or <a>, as in {Gibeah kiim-ah}, around Gibeah) (s:kimkot)
kiima = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:around/surrounding) (d:<kiim> with the place ending <a>, in the area around; mostly {kiima om}, that are around) (s:kiimah) (b:kiim) (q:draft)
kiimah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:around/round about/on every side of) (d:<kiim> with <ah>, placed after the noun) (s:kiima) (b:kiim) (q:draft)
kiimkot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:surround) (d:the space all around; {a kiimkot ah} means all around them, and {kiimkot-a om} means that are on every side)
kiimkotah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:surround)
kiimnai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vicinity/surrounding area/neighbourhood) (d:the area around and near a place) (s:khuakiim/kiimteng) (q:draft)
kiimte = (t:see) <kiimte-ah>
kiimte-ah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:around/round about) (d:<kiim>, surroundings, with the plural <te> and the marker <ah>: at the places all around a wall or a town) (s:kiimah) (q:draft)
kiimteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:region/surrounding area/districts) (d:<kiim>, surroundings, with <teng>, all: the whole area round about a place) (b:kiim) (q:draft)
kiimvelin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around/round about) (d:going all around a place) (s:kimkotin) (q:draft)
kiin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:move/move away/be removed) (d:move away from a place; {kiin lo} is not moved, unshaken) (s:kikhin) (q:draft)
kikah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weep together/weep for each other/be mourned) (d:<kah>, weep, with <ki>: weep for one another, or be wept for when dead) (b:kah) (q:draft)
