kikhuituah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined together/be coupled/be sewn together) (d:<khuituah>, sew together, with the passive <ki>: of cloth or curtains, be fastened one to another to form one set) (b:khuituah) (r:2.36.12) (q:draft)
kikhuituahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined together/be woven together) (d:<kikhuituah>, be joined together, with the linking ending <in>; of the body being put together before birth) (b:kikhuituah) (q:draft)
kikhuk = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:twisted/twined) (d:of thread, twisted together; {a kop-a kikhuk puan hoih} is fine twined linen) (q:draft)
