kikoto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:call out/cry out) (d:<kiko>, cry out, with <to>, upward: cry up from below) (s:kikokhia) (b:kiko) (q:draft)
kikpa = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<kik>, again or back, with <pa>, the male one who: placed after a verb, the one who does it again; {a puah kikpa} is the one who restores) (b:kik) (q:draft)
kiksak = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: cause to do or be again, from <kik>, again or back, with causative <sak>; {nungta kiksak} is bring back to life) (b:kik) (q:draft)
