kikuaitan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/be snapped) (d:<kuaitan>, break in two, with the prefix <ki>; of a bone or a branch) (s:kitan/kikuai-tan) (b:kuaitan) (q:draft)
kikuaitansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:broken/splintered) (d:<kikuaitan>, be broken, with <sa>, already done: that has been broken, of a reed) (s:kitansa) (b:kikuaitan) (q:draft)
kikual = (i:1) (t:v) (w:coil/be coiled) (d:<kual>, ring or around, with <ki>; of a serpent, with <vial>) (s:kikualvial) (b:kual) (q:draft)
