kikuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go/go out) (d:<kuan>, set out for a task, with the prefix <ki> used without a named subject: people go out to work) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kikuangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kept burning) (d:<kuangsak>, make burn, with the passive prefix <ki>: of a fire, be kept burning) (a:kimitsak) (b:kuangsak) (q:draft)
kikuantawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kindled/be aroused/flare up) (d:of anger rising against someone) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:<kui>, cut the skin, with the reflexive prefix <ki>; done to the body as a sign of mourning) (s:kikuiliam/kikuisak) (b:kui) (q:draft)
kikuikham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ripped open/be cut open) (d:said of pregnant women killed in war) (b:kuikham) (q:draft)
kikuiliam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:wound one's own body by cutting) (s:kikui/kikuisak) (b:kuiliam) (q:draft)
kikuisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:<kikui>, cut oneself, with <sak>; {a pumpi a kikuisak} is he cut his own body) (s:kikui/kikuiliam) (b:kikui) (q:draft)
kikum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:discuss/reason together/confer) (d:talk a matter over with one another; <thu kikum> is discuss a matter) (s:kikup/kikumkhawm) (r:44.17.17) (q:draft)
kikumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:confer/discuss/consult together) (d:connective form of <kikum>, usually {thu kikumin}, having talked a matter over) (s:genkhawmin) (b:kikum) (q:draft)
kikumkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reason together/discuss together) (d:<kikum>, discuss, with <khawm>, together) (s:kikum) (b:kikum) (q:draft)
kikumkum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep discussing/talk over/confer) (d:<kikum>, discuss, with the last syllable doubled for continued action: keep talking a matter over) (s:kihoho) (q:draft)
kikumpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:discuss at once/begin to discuss) (d:<kikum>, discuss, with <pah>, straight away) (q:draft)
kikunsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bowed down/be made to stoop) (d:<kun>, bow or stoop, with the prefix <ki> and the causative <sak>) (q:draft)
kikup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:discuss/consult/talk together) (d:talk a matter over with one another, often as <thu kikup>) (s:kikum/kiho) (q:draft)
kikupna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:consultation/discussion/deliberation) (d:noun from <kikup>, talking a matter over together; <kikupna nei> is to hold a consultation) (b:kikup) (q:draft)
kikzo = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<kik>, again or back, with <zo>, be able, after a verb: be able to do again or back; {kikzo nawn lo} is no longer able to do again) (b:kik) (q:draft)
kil = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wavy/curly) (d:of hair; {kil thiuhtheuh} describes long hair that falls in waves) (q:draft, low confidence)
kila = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken/be captured/be seized) (d:<la>, take, with the passive prefix <ki>: be taken or chosen, of a city be captured, also of goods brought in from elsewhere) (s:kilak) (a:kinusia) (b:la) (r:14.9.28) (q:draft)
kilaak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear/present oneself) (d:show oneself before someone, as before God at the yearly feasts) (s:kilak/kilang) (r:23.1.12) (q:draft)
kilaakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear/present oneself) (d:<kilaak>, show oneself, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kilangin/kilakin) (b:kilaak) (q:draft)
kilaam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised) (d:found with <to>, upward: {kilaam to} is be lifted up) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilaamto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised high) (d:<laamto>, lift up, with the prefix <ki>: be lifted up or raised high, said of gates, of a head held high and of tall trees) (s:kilamto/kidomto) (a:kikoihsuk/kiniamkhiat) (b:laamto) (q:draft)
kilah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show oneself/appear/be shown/be revealed) (d:form of <kilak> used before <khit>, <ni>, <leh> and <ciangin>) (s:kilat) (b:lah) (q:draft)
kilahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be revealed/be shown forth) (d:<lahkhiat>, reveal, with the prefix <ki>; the form used before <ding> and <hun>) (s:kilangkhia) (b:lahkhiat) (q:draft)
kilahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:appearing/showing/manifestation) (d:the act of showing oneself or of being shown; {kilahna mun} is the place where someone appeared, and {lim kilahna} is an example shown to others) (s:kilatna/kilakna) (b:kilah) (q:draft)
kilahsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appeared/have appeared) (d:<kilah>, show oneself, with <sa> for a completed action; {a kilahsa bangin}, as he had appeared) (s:kilangsa) (b:kilah) (q:draft)
kilai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fight/struggle/wrestle) (d:fight or wrestle with one another, come to blows; with <tawh>, struggle with someone) (s:kido) (q:draft)
kilaigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:struggle together/jostle) (d:<kilai>, fight with one another, with <gawp>, roughly or violently) (b:kilai) (q:draft)
kilaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be replaced/be exchanged/alternate) (d:passive of <laih>, replace: one thing is put in the place of another; {kilaih sak}, take in turn) (s:kikhek) (b:laih) (q:draft)
kilaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take in turn/alternate) (d:<kilaih>, be exchanged, with the causative <sak>: one is taken from one side and then one from the other) (b:kilaih) (q:draft)
kilailawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fight/struggle with one another) (d:paired with <kitawng>, quarrel) (s:kilai/kido) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fight/fighting/wrestling) (d:<kilai>, fight or wrestle, with the noun suffix <na>: a fight, or the act of wrestling) (s:kidona) (b:kilai) (q:draft)
kilaithang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:attack one another/fight one another) (d:with {khat leh khat}, one another, of people in panic who turn on each other) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear/show oneself/be shown/be revealed) (d:<lak>, show, with the prefix <ki>: show oneself to someone, appear, or be shown and made known) (s:kilang/kilaak) (a:kiseel) (b:lak) (q:draft)
kilak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be taken/be captured) (d:<lak>, take, with the passive prefix <ki>: be taken, said of a city captured in war) (s:kila) (b:lak) (q:draft)
kilakhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken together/be caught up together) (d:<kila>, be taken, with <khawm>, together) (b:kila) (q:draft)
kilakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taken out/be taken away/be removed) (d:<lakhia>, take out, with the passive prefix <ki>: be taken out of or away from a place or a person) (s:kikoihkhia) (b:lakhia)
kilakhia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:draw/be drawn out) (d:be drawn out of something, as milk from the breast or pieces of meat from a pot)
kilakhia = (i:3) (t:v) (w:pull/be pulled out/be snatched away) (d:be pulled up or snatched away from where it was)
kilakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show/appear/present oneself) (d:<kilak>, show or appear, with the linking ending <in>; {khat leh khat tungah kilakin}, showing to one another) (s:kilangin) (b:kilak) (q:draft)
kilakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken away/be removed/be lifted) (d:passive of <lakkhiat>, take away: be taken away, removed or lifted; the form used before a following word such as <ciangin>, <khit>, {kei leh} or <ni>) (b:lakkhiat) (r:53.2.7) (q:draft)
kilakkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken away/be removed) (d:<kilakkhiat>, be taken away, with <sak>; of a kingdom taken from a king and of sin removed) (b:kilakkhiat) (q:draft)
kilakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear again/show oneself again) (d:<kilak>, show oneself, with <kik>, again) (s:kilangkik/kilatkik) (b:kilak) (q:draft)
kilaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not be shown/not be given) (d:<kilak>, be shown, with <lo>, not, written as one word; of a sign that will not be shown) (b:kilak) (q:draft)
kilakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken away/be carried off) (d:be taken so that it is gone, of herds taken as plunder) (q:draft)
kilakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:appearance/appearing/showing oneself) (d:<kilak>, show oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: an appearing, the occasion on which someone shows himself or is made known) (s:kilahna/kilatna) (b:kilak) (q:draft)
kilakna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:taking/charging) (d:the act of something being taken; {leiba ameet kilakna}, the charging of interest on a debt) (s:lakna) (b:kilak) (r:3.16.27) (q:draft)
kilaksa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shown/have been shown) (d:<kilak>, be shown, with <sa> for a completed action; {hong kilaksa bangin}, as it was shown to you) (b:kilak) (q:draft)
kilaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be robbed of/be deprived of/be taken from) (d:have something taken away from one: <laksak>, take from someone, with the passive prefix <ki>; {a no a kilaksak vompi} is a bear robbed of her cubs) (s:kiguksak) (b:laksak) (q:draft)
kilaksakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried off/be taken away) (d:have something taken away for good, said of herds carried off as plunder) (s:kituahmang) (b:laksakmang) (q:draft)
kilaktawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:present oneself/show oneself) (d:go and show oneself to someone of one's own accord) (q:draft)
kilaktoh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken up/be lifted up) (d:be taken upward: of Jesus and Enoch taken up to heaven, and of the cloud lifting from the tent) (s:kilato) (b:kilak) (q:draft)
kilam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be built/be set up) (d:<lam>, build, with the passive prefix <ki>: of a house, a temple or a city, be built) (a:kisusia) (b:lam) (r:2.40.17) (q:draft)
kilamdan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:differ/be different) (d:be different from one another; in the verses it occurs in the noun {kilamdan'na}, difference or distinction) (s:kilamdang) (b:lamdan) (q:draft)
kilamdang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be different/differ/be changed/be transfigured) (d:be or become different from something, with <tawh> for what it differs from; of the face or appearance, be changed) (s:kilamdan) (b:lamdang) (q:draft)
kilamdangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:differently/distinctly/with a distinction) (d:<kilamdang>, be different, with the ending <in>: in a different way, so that one can be told from another) (b:kilamdang) (q:draft)
kilamdangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:transform/make different/confuse/confound) (d:<kilamdang>, be different, with the causative <sak>: of oneself, be transformed; of speech, make it differ so that it is confused) (b:kilamdang) (q:draft)
kilamdanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:difference/distinction) (d:<kilamdan>, differ, with the noun suffix <na>: what makes two things or groups different; {a kilamdanna bawl} is make a distinction) (s:kibatlohna) (a:kibatna) (b:kilamdan) (r:26.44.23) (q:draft)
kilamen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hope/expect/think) (d:<lamen>, hope, with the prefix <ki>: hope or expect for oneself that something will happen, after a clause with <dingin>) (b:lamen) (q:draft)
kilamet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:expect/hope for) (d:<lamet>, hope or expect, with the prefix <ki>) (b:lamet) (q:draft)
kilamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be built/be built up) (d:<kilam>, be built, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:kilam) (q:draft)
kilamkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rebuilt) (d:<lamkik>, rebuild, with the passive prefix <ki>: of a city or temple, be built again) (s:kiciangkik) (b:lamkik) (r:27.9.25) (q:draft)
kilamkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rebuilding/restoration) (d:<kilamkik>, be rebuilt, with the noun suffix <na>: the building again of a house or temple) (s:lamkikna) (b:kilamkik) (q:draft)
kilamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:building/being built) (d:<kilam>, be built, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kilam) (q:draft)
kilamsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:built) (d:<kilam>, be built, with <sa>, already done: that was built, placed before the thing built) (s:lamsa) (b:kilam) (q:draft)
kilamsang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be exalted) (d:lift oneself up high or be lifted up high; the opposite of <kiniamkhiat>, humble oneself) (s:kisangsak/kiliansak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (q:draft)
kilamto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised/be lifted up/be upraised) (d:passive of <lamto>, lift up; of a hand held up, also of trees standing high) (b:lamto) (r:23.9.17) (q:draft)
kilang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear/be revealed/be shown/be seen) (d:become visible or known; of a person or an angel, appear to someone; {a kilang lo} is what is not seen) (s:kilak/kidawk) (a:kiseel) (r:45.1.18) (q:draft)
kilanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:openly/evidently/plainly) (d:<kilang>, appear, with <a>: in a way that can be seen) (b:kilang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilangbawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:opposition/hostility/enmity) (d:<langbawlna>, opposition, with the prefix <ki>: being set against one another, or being opposed by others) (s:kilangneihna/kigalneihna) (a:kilemna) (b:langbawlna) (q:draft)
kilangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:openly/publicly/visibly) (d:<kilang>, appear, with the ending <in>, used as {a kilangin}: in a way that is seen by all, not in secret) (s:langtangin) (a:simthamin/thusimin) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:appear/be revealed) (d:<kilang>, appear, with the linking suffix <in>: appearing and then going on to the next action) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangkhem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pretend/make a false show/be hypocritical) (d:<kilang>, appear, with <khem>, deceive: put on a good appearance that is not true; {a hoihin a kilangkhem} are those who only seem good, hypocrites) (s:kineihkhem) (q:draft)
kilangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be revealed/come to light/be shown) (d:<kilang>, appear, with <khia>, out; {kilangkhia sak}, bring to light, uncover) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear again/reappear) (d:<kilang>, appear, with <kik>, again: come into view once more) (s:kilakkik) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilanglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:not obvious/not apparent/unseen) (d:<kilang>, appear, with the negative <lo>) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangneih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:unfriendly/hostile/at enmity) (d:being enemies of one another, used with <tawh> for the other party)
kilangneihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:enmity/hostility) (d:<kilangneih>, be at enmity, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being enemies of one another) (s:kigalneihna/galneihna/kilemlohna) (a:kilemna) (b:kilangneih)
kilangpang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:oppose each other/be in conflict) (d:<langpang>, oppose, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (b:langpang) (q:draft)
kilangsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appeared/revealed) (d:<kilang>, appear, with <sa>, already done: that has appeared) (s:kilahsa) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reveal/show/make known) (d:<kilang>, appear, with the causative <sak>: make something seen or known) (s:lakkhia) (a:seel) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:revealing/showing/making known) (d:<kilangsak>, reveal, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:kilangsak) (q:draft)
kilangsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make appear again/show again) (d:<kilangsak>, cause to appear, with <kik>, again; of Christ shown alive after his death and of his future appearing) (b:kilangsak) (q:draft)
kilangsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who show/those who make known) (d:<kilangsak>, make known, with the plural <te>) (b:kilangsak) (q:draft)
kilangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things that appear/what is seen) (d:<kilang> appear with <te>, those which; {a pua lama kilangte} is what shows on the outside) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangtuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show oneself separately/appear specially) (d:appear to some apart from others) (q:draft)
kilangzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear more/be more evident) (d:<kilang>, appear, with <zaw>, more) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have appeared/have been revealed) (d:<kilang> appear with <zo>, marking the action as accomplished) (b:kilang) (q:draft)
kilat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear/be revealed) (d:form of <kilang>, appear, used before a following word such as <ciangin>, <ni>, <hun>, <ding> or <nading>) (q:draft)
kilate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things taken/plunder/spoil) (d:<kila> be taken with <te>, those which) (b:kila) (q:draft)
kilate = (i:2) (t:n) (w:channels/canals) (d:in {lei zui-a tui kilate}, waters that are led along the ground) (b:kila) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilatkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exposed/come to light) (d:<kilat>, appear, with <khak>, happen to: of wrong deeds, come to be seen) (s:kipholak) (q:draft)
kilatkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be manifested/be shown forth) (d:<kilat>, appear, with <khiat>, out; {kilatkhiat nading} is for the showing forth, where the English has manifestation) (s:kilahkhiat) (b:kilat) (q:draft)
kilatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appear again/reappear/be revealed again) (d:<kilat> appear with <kik>, again; used of the return of Christ) (s:kilakkik) (b:kilat) (q:draft)
kilatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:revelation/appearing/display/sight) (d:<kilat>, appear, with the noun suffix <na>: the showing or becoming visible of something, also the thing that is seen) (s:kilahna) (b:kilat) (q:draft)
kilato = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken up/be lifted up) (d:<kila>, be taken, with <to>, up: be taken upward, as into heaven) (s:kilaktoh) (b:kila) (q:draft)
kilatosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take up/take away) (d:<kilato>, be taken up, with the causative <sak>; of God taking Enoch) (b:kilato) (q:draft)
kilatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show/reveal/make manifest/demonstrate) (d:<kilat>, appear, with the causative <sak>: make something plain to see, often before <nading>) (s:lakkhia) (a:seel) (b:kilat) (r:47.2.8) (q:draft)
kilatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:showing/proof) (d:<kilatsak>, make plain to see, with the noun suffix <na>; {teci kilatsakna}, the showing of proof, stands where the English has character) (b:kilatsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilausak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be terrified/be made afraid) (d:<lausak>, frighten, with the prefix <ki>) (s:laugawp) (b:lausak) (q:draft)
kilawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread) (d:of a skin disease, spread to other parts of the body) (s:kizelh) (q:draft)
kilawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be picked/be gleaned) (d:of fruit, be gathered; {kilawh kik}, be gone over again, gleaned) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilawhgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break out/spread all over) (d:<kilawh>, spread, of a skin disease, with <gawp>, severely: of boils breaking out on people and animals) (b:kilawh) (q:draft)
kilawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be out of joint/be dislocated/be disabled) (d:of bones or limbs, be put out of place) (s:kilong) (q:draft)
kilawi = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be lacking/be without/be deserted) (d:be missing or empty of something; {kilawi ngei kei} is never be without, and {a kilawi mun} is a deserted place) (s:tasam) (q:draft)
kilawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:suitable/fitting/proper) (d:right or fitting for a person or a purpose; {a kilawm mah bangin} is as is fitting) (s:hoihtuak)
kilawm = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:fit for/worthy/deserving) (d:good enough or deserving to do or receive something; after a verb with <ding>, worthy to do it)
kilawma = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:fittingly/becomingly) (d:<kilawm>, suitable, with <a>; {a mel kilawma om} is of fair appearance) (b:kilawm) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilawmin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:properly/fittingly/decently) (d:<kilawm>, suitable, with the ending <in>, often as {a kilawmin}: in a fitting and proper way) (s:kituakin) (a:kilawmlopi-in) (b:kilawm) (q:draft)
kilawmlopi = (t:see) <kilawmlopi-in>
kilawmlopi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:unjustly/improperly/unfairly) (d:<kilawm>, suitable, with the negative <lo>, <pi> and <in>: in a way that is not right at all) (a:kilawmin) (q:draft)
kilawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fittingness/seemliness/beauty) (d:the quality of being fitting or presentable; {a kilawmna om lo} means it is not fitting) (b:kilawm) (q:draft)
kilawmpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:most worthy/most suitable/fittest) (d:<kilawm>, suitable, with <pen>, most) (b:kilawm) (q:draft)
kilawmtatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fellowship/friendship) (d:being on friendly terms with someone, with <tawh> for the other person) (a:kilangneihna) (q:draft)
kilawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who deserve/those who are due/what is fitting) (d:<kilawm> with the plural <te>; after a verb with <ding>, the people or things for whom the action is fitting) (b:kilawm) (q:draft)
kilawmzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:due amount/as much as is fitting) (d:<kilawm>, fitting, with <zah>, amount: as much as one deserves or ought) (q:draft)
kilawmzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more fitting/more proper) (d:<kilawm>, fitting, with <zaw>, more: more suitable or right; in questions, how much more ought) (s:taakzaw) (b:kilawm) (q:draft)
kilawmzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be worthy/be fit/deserve) (d:<kilawm>, worthy, with <zo>, be able: mostly with a negative, not be worthy to do something) (b:kilawm) (q:draft)
kilawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown/be cast) (d:<lawn>, throw, with the passive prefix <ki>; with <suk>, be thrown down, and with <khia>, be thrown out) (s:kipaai) (b:lawn) (q:draft)
kilawng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be touched) (d:<lawng>, touch, with the prefix <ki>; {khut tawh kilawng}, be touched with the hand) (s:kisukkhak) (b:lawng) (q:draft)
kilawnin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being thrown/thrown) (d:<kilawn>, be thrown, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kilawn) (q:draft)
kilawnkeek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be torn down) (d:of the stones of a building thrown down so that none is left on another; used with <mang>) (s:kiphelkeek) (q:draft)
kilawnkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast out/be hurled out) (d:<lawnkhia>, throw out, with the passive prefix <ki>: be thrown or driven out) (s:kipaaikhia) (b:lawnkhia) (q:draft)
kilawnsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be hurled down/be cast down) (d:<lawnsuk>, throw downward, with the passive prefix <ki>: be thrown down) (s:kikhiasuk) (b:lawnsuk) (q:draft)
kilawnthal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be destroyed) (d:<lawnthal>, overthrow, with the prefix <ki>; of cities thrown down) (s:kisusia) (b:lawnthal) (q:draft)
kilawnto = (t:see) <kilawnto-in>
kilawnto-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown up/be tossed up) (d:<kilawn>, be thrown, with <to>, up, and the linking ending <in>; of sailors lifted high by the waves) (q:draft)
kileh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:return/turn back) (d:turn round and go or come back; often followed by <kik>, back, or <hei>, around) (s:kihei/nungkik/ciahkik) (q:draft)
kileh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:go back and forth/go to and fro) (d:with <kawikawi>, turn this way and that, of people going about and of hills swaying) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilehbulh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be contrary/contradict/be opposite) (d:be the opposite of something, used with <tawh>; here of deeds that go against what is claimed) (s:kilehngat) (q:draft)
kilehbulhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:contrary to/in opposition to) (d:<kilehbulh>, be contrary, with <in>; used with <tawh>) (b:kilehbulh) (q:draft)
kilehdo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:contend with/strive against/rebel against) (d:<lehdo>, rebel, with the prefix <ki>; used with <tawh>) (b:lehdo) (q:draft)
kilehhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be driven back/be routed) (d:of soldiers beaten and forced to turn back) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilehheek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be betrayed/be handed over) (d:<lehheek>, betray, with the passive prefix <ki>) (b:lehheek) (q:draft)
kilehhei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn around/turn back/turn about) (d:turn oneself round; often followed by <kik>, back: turn back from a pursuit or return to a former way) (s:kihei/kilehkik) (b:lehhei) (q:draft)
kilehhek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be betrayed/betray one another) (d:<lehhek>, betray, with the prefix <ki>: be betrayed, or with <khatlekhat>, betray each other) (s:kiheek) (b:lehhek) (q:draft)
kilehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:return/turn back) (d:<kileh>, turn back, with the linking ending <in>: going back and then) (b:kileh) (q:draft)
kilehkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:return/turn back/come back) (d:<kileh> with <kik>, back or again; also of turning back to God) (s:ciahkik/kihei/nungkik) (b:kileh) (q:draft)
kilehkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make turn back/cause to withdraw) (d:<kilehkik>, turn back, with the causative <sak>) (b:kilehkik) (q:draft)
kilehngat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away from/be opposed to/be contrary) (d:face the opposite way from someone or something, used with <tawh>) (s:kilehbulh) (b:lehngat) (q:draft)
kilehngatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:contrary/in opposition/hostilely) (d:facing against someone, used with <tawh> and <pai>: walk contrary to, be hostile toward) (s:kilehbulhin) (b:kilehngat) (q:draft)
kilehsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rush back and forth/go to and fro) (d:<kileh>, go back and forth, with <suk>, down; paired with <kilehto>) (b:kileh) (q:draft)
kilehto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rush back and forth/go to and fro) (d:<kileh>, go back and forth, with <to>, up; paired with <kilehsuk>) (b:kileh) (q:draft)
kilei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bought/be purchased) (d:<lei>, buy, with the passive prefix <ki>: be bought; with <tawh> for the price) (a:kizuak) (b:lei) (q:draft)
kileikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bought again) (d:<kilei>, be bought, with <kik>, again) (b:kilei) (q:draft)
kileina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:purchase/buying) (d:<kilei>, be bought, with the noun suffix <na>: the buying of something; {kileina lai} is a deed of purchase) (s:leina) (b:kilei) (q:draft)
kileinapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seller) (d:the man from whom a thing was bought; <kileina>, purchase, with <pa>, the male one) (s:zuakpa) (b:kileina) (q:draft)
kileipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bought slave/one who is bought) (d:<kilei>, be bought, with <pa> marking a man: a man bought with money, set beside one born in the household) (b:kilei) (q:draft)
kileitawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lend to one another) (d:<leitawi>, loan, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: lend to each other, as in {khatlekhat kileitawi}) (b:leitawi) (q:draft)
kileizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be bought) (d:<kilei>, be bought, with <zo>, be able: used with {hi lo} for what cannot be bought at any price) (s:leizawh) (b:kilei) (q:draft)
kilelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let oneself be defeated/pretend to be beaten) (d:<lelsak>, defeat, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: let oneself be beaten; with <khem>, deceive, pretend to be beaten in order to draw the enemy out) (b:lelsak) (q:draft)
kilem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be at peace/be reconciled/make peace) (d:be on good terms with one another, not at war or in a quarrel; used with <tawh> for the other party, and {kilem nading thu} is an offer of peace) (a:kido/kigal/kihua) (r:40.5.24) (q:draft)
kilemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:at peace/reconciled/in peace) (d:<kilem>, be at peace, with the linking ending <in>: being at peace or reconciled with someone, mostly before <om>, live) (b:kilem) (q:draft)
kilemkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be reconciled/be at peace again) (d:<kilem>, be at peace, with <kik>, again or back: be at peace again after a quarrel or enmity; used with <tawh> for the other party) (b:kilem) (q:draft)
kilemkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be in harmony together/agree all alike) (d:of the parts of the body all being at one with each other, where the English has have equal concern for each other) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilemlo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be at odds/not be at peace/oppose) (d:<kilem>, be at peace, with the negative <lo>: be against someone, used with <tawh>; the English has resist) (a:kilem) (b:kilem) (q:draft)
kilemlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hostility/enmity/discord) (d:the state of not being at peace with one another; {kilemlohna bawl} is rebel, and {kilemlohna that} is put an end to hostility) (s:kilangneihna/kigalneihna/galneihna) (a:kilemna) (q:draft)
kilemna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:atonement/reconciliation) (d:<kilem>, be at peace, with the noun suffix <na>: the putting right of people with God, by sacrifice in the law and through Christ in the letters; <kilemna bawl> is make atonement) (s:mawhphelna) (b:kilem) (r:4.28.22) (q:draft)
kilemsa = (t:see) <kilemsa-in>
kilemsa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:reconciled/at peace) (d:<kilem>, be at peace, with <sa>, already, and the ending <in>: having been put right with someone; the English has justified) (q:draft)
kilemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reconcile/make peace between) (d:<kilem>, be at peace, with the causative <sak>: bring two parties back to peace, often followed by <kik>, again; {hong kilemsak} is he reconciled us) (b:kilem) (q:draft)
kilemsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reconcile/bring back to peace) (d:<kilemsak>, reconcile, with <kik>, again; of the one who makes peace between two parties) (b:kilemsak) (q:draft)
kilemsakkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reconciling/bringing back to peace) (d:<kilemsakkik>, reconcile, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kilemsakkik) (q:draft)
kilemsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:reconciliation) (d:<kilemsak>, reconcile, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kilemna/gallemna) (b:kilemsak) (q:draft)
kilemte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:at peace/secure) (d:<kilem>, be at peace, with the plural <te>: {gam kilemte} are lands that are at peace and feel secure) (b:kilem) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold one another/embrace) (d:<len>, hold, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (s:kikawi) (b:len) (q:draft)
kilenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:holding/being held) (d:<kilen> with the linking suffix <in>; {a khut kilenin} is holding him by the hand) (b:kilen) (q:draft)
kilenkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blown away/be driven away) (d:of smoke made to fly off) (q:draft)
kilensa = (t:see) <kilensa-in>
kilensa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:holding one another/hand in hand) (d:<len>, hold, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>, <sa> for a completed action and the linking ending <in>; {khut kilensa-in}, holding hands) (q:draft)
kiletna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handshake/clasping of hands) (d:found in {khut kiletna}, the giving of the hand to one another as a sign of fellowship) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:nail/fasten) (d:fasten something with nails so that it cannot be moved) (s:khen) (q:draft)
kilhcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:nail fast/crucify) (d:<kilh>, nail, with <cip>, tightly; {singlamteh tungah kilhcip} is nail to the cross) (s:khencip) (b:kilh) (q:draft)
kilhcipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:nailing/nailing fast) (d:<kilhcip>, nail fast, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kilhcip) (q:draft)
kilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:clasp/hook/fastener) (d:<kilh>, fasten, with the noun suffix <na>: a small hook or pin that holds two pieces together, as the gold and bronze clasps of the tabernacle curtains) (b:kilh) (r:2.26.6) (q:draft)
kilhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:clasps/hooks/nails) (d:<kilhna>, fastener, with the plural <te>: the clasps that join the tabernacle curtains, and in one verse the nails of the temple) (b:kilhna) (q:draft)
kiliah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hidden/be concealed) (d:<liah>, cover or hide, with the passive prefix <ki>: be out of sight or kept from someone, with {kiang pan} or <mai-ah> for the one it is hidden from) (s:kiseel/kibu) (a:kilang) (b:liah) (q:draft)
kiliahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being hidden/being covered) (d:<kiliah>, be hidden, with the linking suffix <in>; of the light of understanding, where the English has darkened) (b:kiliah) (q:draft)
kiliahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:veil/covering/screen) (d:<kiliah>, be covered, with the noun suffix <na>: something that screens or hides; {kiliahna puan} is a veil over the face) (s:khuhna/dalna) (b:kiliah) (q:draft)
kiliamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hurt one another/harm/be wounded) (d:<liamsak>, wound, with the prefix <ki>: with {khat leh khat}, hurt one another; of one person, be wounded) (b:liamsak) (q:draft)
kilian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make oneself great/be haughty) (d:<lian>, great, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: found in {kilian sak}, exalt oneself or be arrogant, and {kilian ngaihsut}, think oneself great) (s:kiphasak/kihisak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:lian) (q:draft)
kiliansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be proud/be haughty/be exalted) (d:<liansak>, make great, with the prefix <ki>: make oneself great, be proud or set oneself up against someone; of a name or a kingdom, be made great) (s:kiphasak/kihisak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (b:liansak) (q:draft)
kiliansakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:exalting oneself/being haughty) (d:<kiliansak>, exalt oneself, with the linking suffix <in>: putting oneself forward, behaving haughtily) (b:kiliansak) (r:24.48.29) (q:draft)
Kiliansakin = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Kiliansakin) (d:the verb <kiliansakin>, exalting oneself, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; not a proper name) (r:24.48.29)
kiliansakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who exalt themselves/the proud) (d:<kiliansak>, exalt oneself, with the plural <te>: people who make themselves great, usually as {a kiliansakte}) (s:kiphasakte/kihisakte/kisatheite) (a:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kiliansak) (q:draft)
kiliatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be lifted up) (d:<liatsak>, make great, with the reflexive prefix <ki>; of the heart being lifted up over others) (s:kiliansak/kiphasak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:liatsak) (q:draft)
kiliatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:arrogance/pride/haughtiness) (d:<kiliatsak>, exalt oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: thinking oneself great and looking down on others) (s:kiphatsakna/kihihsakna/kisaktheihna) (a:kiniamkhiatna/kiniamsakna) (b:kiliatsak) (q:draft)
kiliin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sway/shake/tremble) (d:<liin>, tremble, with the prefix <ki>; of a reed moving in the water) (s:kiliing/kiling) (b:liin) (q:draft)
kiliing = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shake/tremble/quake) (d:<liing>, tremble, with the prefix <ki>: shake or be shaken, of the earth, mountains, the powers of heaven or the heart) (s:kiling/liing/kilok) (a:kip) (b:liing) (q:draft)
kiliingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shake/make tremble) (d:<kiliing>, shake, with the causative <sak>) (s:kilingsak/lingsak) (b:kiliing) (q:draft)
Kilikia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Cilicia) (d:Roman province on the south-east coast of Asia Minor, whose chief city was Tarsus, the home town of Paul) (r:48.1.21/44.6.9)
kilikkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rolled away) (d:<likkhia>, roll away, with the passive prefix <ki>: of the stone rolled off from the opening of the tomb) (b:likkhia) (q:draft)
kilim = (t:todo) (q:draft, found only in {thupha hong kilim piak}, be blessed, Deuteronomy 7.14; what {kilim} adds is not clear)
kilin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shake/quake/sway) (d:short form of <kiling>, written {kilin} with an apostrophe before the next word) (s:kiling/kiliing) (q:draft)
kiling = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaken/be moved/shake) (d:be made to shake or lose firmness, of the earth, a mountain, a building or a person; {ka kiling kei ding} is I will not be shaken) (s:kiliing/kilok/liing) (a:kip) (r:19.96.10) (q:draft)
kilinggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaken violently/be shaken/quake) (d:<kiling>, be shaken, with <gawp>, thoroughly: be shaken violently) (s:kilokgawp) (b:kiling) (q:draft)
kilingin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tremble/shake) (d:<kiling>, be shaken, with the linking ending <in>; of the earth trembling) (b:kiling) (q:draft)
kilingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shake/cause to shake/let be shaken) (d:<kiling>, be shaken, with the causative <sak>: make something shake, or let someone be shaken; {a kilingsak zo lo} is that cannot be shaken) (s:lingsak/kiliingsak) (b:lingsak) (q:draft)
kilingsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being shaken) (d:<kilingsak>, cause to shake, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kilingsak) (q:draft)
kilkel = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:intensifier after a descriptive word, with the sense of clear, fresh or gleaming: {siang kilkel} is perfectly clear, {vot kilkel} is cool and clear, {hing kilkel} is fresh and green, {kipuah kilkel} is polished bright) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be called/be named/be mentioned) (d:of a name, be spoken or used: {min kilo} is the name is called or mentioned, {min tawh a kilo} is called by the name of, and {a min-a kilo} is mentioned by name) (s:kici) (q:draft)
kiloh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be paid/be repaid) (d:<loh>, pay off, with the passive prefix <ki>; {kiloh sak} is make someone pay) (b:loh) (q:draft)
kilohsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to pay/be made to repay) (d:<lohsak>, pay for, with the passive prefix <ki>) (b:lohsak) (q:draft)
kilok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaken/be tossed/quake/be rough) (d:be moved to and fro, of the earth quaking or of water stirred up by the wind; {tui kilok} is a wave or rough water) (s:kiling/kiliing/kising) (a:kip) (b:lok) (q:draft)
kilokgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaken violently/be tossed about) (d:<lokgawp>, shake violently, with the passive prefix <ki>: of the earth, a boat or water thrown about by wind or earthquake) (s:kilinggawp) (b:lokgawp) (q:draft)
kilokha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be mentioned/be invoked/be called on) (d:<kilo>, be named, with <kha>: of a name being spoken at all; with {nawn lo}, never be mentioned again) (q:draft)
kilokhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be designated/be called out) (d:<kilo>, be named, with <khia>, out; {a minin a kilokhia}, singled out by name) (b:kilo) (q:draft)
kilokna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:surge/current/tossing) (d:<kilok>, be tossed, with the noun suffix <na>; {tui kilokna} is moving water, a current or surf) (b:kilok) (q:draft)
kiloksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stir up/trouble/shake) (d:<kilok>, be shaken, with the causative <sak>; of stirring the water of a pool) (b:kilok) (q:draft)
kilokzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be shaken) (d:<kilok>, be shaken, with <zo>, be able; with {ngei lo}, can never be shaken) (b:kilok) (q:draft)
kilomin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:huddle together/crowd together) (d:of people gathered close in a heap; compare <lom>, heap) (b:lomin) (q:draft)
kilong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come off/be detached/be dislocated) (d:of an arm coming away from the shoulder, with <khia>, out) (q:draft)
kilongkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come off/fall out of joint) (d:<kilong> with <khia>, out; of an arm coming away from the shoulder) (b:kilong) (q:draft)
kilosa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:named/specified) (d:<kilo>, be named, with <sa>, already done; {a min kilosa}, whose names have been called) (b:kilo) (q:draft)
kilote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those called/those named) (d:<kilo>, be called or named, with plural <te>: those whose names are given, those called by a name) (s:kicite) (b:kilo) (q:draft)
kiluah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be inherited/be passed down) (d:passive of <luah>, inherit: property comes down from parents or from one generation to the next) (b:luah) (q:draft)
kiluan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be poured/flow) (d:<ki> with <luan>, a form of <luang> flow: of molten gold poured for an image; in Joel 2:30 of blood being shed) (b:luan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiluangkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be drained/be made to flow out) (d:<luangkhiasak>, make flow out, with the passive prefix <ki>; of the blood of a slaughtered animal) (b:luangkhiasak) (q:draft)
kiluansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shed/be poured out) (d:<kiluan>, flow, with the causative <sak>; of blood) (b:kiluan) (q:draft)
kiluansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shedding/flowing) (d:with <sisan>, blood: {sisan kiluansakna} is bloodshed, where the English has only blood) (b:kiluansak) (q:draft)
kiluh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ransacked/be looted) (d:<luh>, plunder, with the passive prefix <ki>: of a city, houses or people stripped by raiders; often followed by <gawp>, thoroughly) (s:kisut/kibuluh) (b:luh) (q:draft)
kiluhgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ravaged/be sacked) (d:<kiluh>, be plundered, with <gawp> marking a thorough or violent action) (b:kiluh) (q:draft)
kiluhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be looted) (d:<kiluh>, be plundered, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiluh) (q:draft)
kilui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be served/be set before) (d:<lui>, serve food, with the passive prefix <ki>: of food, be laid out in front of someone to eat, with <mai-ah>, before) (q:draft)
kilukham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid under the head/be used as a pillow) (d:<lukham>, pillow, with the prefix <ki>; of the swords of buried warriors, with <sak>) (b:lukham) (q:draft)
kilukhamsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:having laid under the head) (d:<kilukham> with the causative <sak> and the linking suffix <in>) (b:kilukham) (q:draft)
kilukhuhsa = (t:see) <kilukhuhsa-in>
kilukhuhsa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:with head covered/having covered the head) (d:<lu>, head, and <khuh>, cover, with the reflexive prefix <ki>, <sa> for a completed action and the linking ending <in>; a sign of grief or shame) (q:draft)
kilumlet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be overturned) (d:<lumlet>, overturn, with the passive prefix <ki>; {gam kilumlet} is an uprising in the land) (b:lumlet) (q:draft)
kilumletin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overturned/overturn) (d:<kilumlet>, be turned over, with the linking ending <in>; of a tent knocked over) (b:kilumlet) (q:draft)
kilumletsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn upside down/throw into disorder) (d:<kilumlet>, be overturned, with the causative <sak>) (b:kilumlet) (q:draft)
kilumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to lie down/be laid down to sleep) (d:<lumsak>, make lie down, with the passive prefix <ki>) (b:lumsak) (q:draft)
kilung = (i:1) (t:v) (d:<lung>, heart or mind, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>; found with <tuak>: {kilung tuak} is be of one mind with one another) (b:lung) (q:draft)
kilungdamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pleased/be made glad/rejoice) (d:<lungdamsak>, make glad, with the prefix <ki>: of God, be pleased; of a person, make oneself glad, rejoice) (b:lungdamsak) (q:draft)
kilunggim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be troubled/lose heart) (d:<lunggim>, be troubled, with the prefix <ki>; {kilunggim sak kei in} is do not let yourself be troubled) (b:lunggim) (q:draft)
kilunggimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trouble oneself/make oneself anxious) (d:<lunggimsak>, make heavy in heart, with the reflexive prefix <ki>) (s:kilungkhamsak) (b:lunggimsak) (q:draft)
kilunggulh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lust for one another/desire one another) (d:<lunggulh>, desire, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: desire one another sexually; {kilunggulh luatna}, too much desire of woman and man for each other, is lust) (b:lunggulh) (q:draft)
kilunggulhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lust/desire for one another) (d:<kilunggulh>, desire one another, with the noun suffix <na>; of sexual desire) (b:kilunggulh) (q:draft)
kilunghimawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:worry/be troubled) (d:<lunghimawh>, worry, with the prefix <ki> used without a named subject: one has worry or sorrow) (b:lunghimawh) (q:draft)
kilungkhamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:distress oneself/be upset) (d:<lungkhamsak>, make troubled, with the reflexive prefix <ki>; with {kei in}, do not let yourself be troubled) (s:kilunggimsak) (b:lungkhamsak) (q:draft)
kilungkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be content with one another/be satisfied with each other) (d:<lungkim>, be satisfied, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>; with <lo>, have a grievance against one another) (b:lungkim) (q:draft)
kilungnemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be humbled/be made low) (d:<lungnemsak>, make gentle or lowly in heart, with the passive prefix <ki>: be brought low, where the English has in his humiliation) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilungnuamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort oneself/set one's mind at ease) (d:<lungnuamsak>, make glad or at ease, with the reflexive prefix <ki>) (b:lungnuamsak) (q:draft)
kilungsim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ill will/malice) (d:found in {kilungsim neihna}, holding something in the heart against one another, where the English has malice) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilungso = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fret/be vexed) (d:<lungso>, be hot in heart, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: work oneself into anger or worry; found in {kilungso tawmsak}, make oneself fret) (b:lungso) (q:draft)
kilungsosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fret/vex oneself) (d:<kilungso> fret, with the causative <sak>: make oneself angry or worried) (b:kilungso) (r:19.37.8) (q:draft)
kilungtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:agree together/be of one mind/conspire) (d:<lung>, mind, and <tuak>, agree, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: be of the same mind with one another to do something, here to do wrong) (s:kithukhat/kithukim/kithutuak) (q:draft)
kilup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lain with/be ravished) (d:{Lup}, lie down, with the prefix <ki>; {kilup khoppih} means be lain with, in the sense of sexual intercourse.) (b:lup) (q:draft)
kilutpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought in/be taken in) (d:Passive of <lutpih>, bring in, with the prefix <ki>: be carried or brought into a place, said of goods taken into a town.) (s:kitumpih) (b:lutpih) (q:draft)
kilutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be let in/be admitted/be welcomed in) (d:Passive of <lutsak>, let in, with the prefix <ki>: be allowed to enter or be received into a place.) (b:lutsak) (q:draft)
kim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:surroundings/area around) (d:The area round about a person or place; {kim-ah} or {kim-a} after a noun means around it, as in {khua kim}, the country round a town.) (s:paam) (q:draft)
kim = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:every/all/fully) (d:Placed after a noun or verb: all of them without exception, each one, or the action done in full.) (s:vekpi/vekin) (r:46.12.26) (q:draft)
kim = (i:3) (t:n) (w:half/middle/part) (d:The middle or half of something: {zan kim lai} is the middle of the night, {kim ciang} is halfway up, and {kim khat} is a part of or some of.) (s:kimciang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kima = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:Said of a woman who has been put away by her husband; often listed beside <meigong>, widow.) (s:maksa/kikhensa) (r:4.30.9) (q:draft)
kima-sialh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:Boast about oneself or about what is still to come; compare <kisialh>, boast.) (s:kisialh/kisial/kiphasak) (q:draft)
kimaakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:Divorce, a spelling of <kimakna> with a long vowel; {kimaakna lai} is a certificate of divorce.) (s:kimakna/makna/kikhenna) (q:draft)
kimah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:around/round about) (d:{Kim}, surroundings, with the place marker <ah>, placed after a noun: around it, on every side of it.) (s:kiimah/kiima) (b:kim) (q:draft)
kimai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:face each other/face) (d:{Mai}, face, with the prefix <ki>, each other: written before <ngat>, turn toward, or <tuah>, meet, to say that two parties face each other.) (s:kimaituah/kimaingat) (b:mai) (q:draft)
kimaingat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:face each other/face one another) (d:{Maingat}, face, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: face one another, said of the two cherubim on the ark.) (s:kimaituah/kitang/kigalsai) (b:maingat) (q:draft)
kimaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be forgiven) (d:Passive of <maisak>, forgive, with the prefix <ki>; {mawhna kimaisak} means sins are forgiven, and with {khat leh khat} it means forgive one another.) (s:maitheih) (b:maisak) (q:draft)
kimaisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being forgiven/being pardoned/forgiving one another) (d:{Kimaisak} with the linking suffix <in>: being forgiven or forgiving one another; in Romans 2.15 excusing one another.) (a:kimawhsakin) (b:kimaisak) (q:draft)
kimaisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forgiveness) (d:{Kimaisak}, be forgiven, with the noun suffix <na>; {mawhna kimaisakna} is the forgiveness of sins.) (s:maisakna/mawhmaisakna/maitheihna) (b:kimaisak) (q:draft)
kimaisakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are forgiven) (d:{Kimaisak}, be forgiven, with the plural <te>: those who are forgiven.) (b:kimaisak) (q:draft)
kimaitaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cheer oneself up/put on a cheerful face) (d:{Maitaisak}, make cheerful, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: make one’s own face bright, put on a smile.) (b:maitaisak) (q:draft)
kimaituah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:face each other/meet face to face/confront) (d:stand face to face with someone, as opponents in battle or in court) (s:kimaingat/kitang/kigalsai/kimai) (q:draft)
kimaituahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:facing each other/face to face/opposite each other) (d:{Kimaituah} with the linking suffix <in>: facing one another, face to face.) (b:kimaituah) (q:draft)
kimaizumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be shamed) (d:Passive of <maizumsak>, put to shame, with the prefix <ki>; with <lo>, not be put to shame.) (s:kizahhuaisak/kiminsia-sak/kimindaisak) (b:maizumsak) (q:draft)
kimakai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be led/be guided) (d:{Makai}, lead, with the passive prefix <ki>: be led; {kimakai sak} means let oneself be led, and {kimakai khial sak} let oneself be led astray.) (b:makai) (q:draft)
kimakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:{Makna}, divorce, with the prefix <ki>; {kimakna lai} is a certificate of divorce.) (s:kimaakna/makna/kikhenna) (b:makna) (q:draft)
kimamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be straightened/be made straight) (d:Passive of <mamsak>, straighten, with the prefix <ki>: be made straight.) (s:kitangsak) (b:mamsak) (q:draft)
kiman = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:finished/completed/done) (d:Brought to an end, said of work, an offering or a period of time; {kiman khin} is completely finished.) (s:khinta/zawhsa)
kiman = (i:2) (t:v) (w:arrested/be caught/be captured) (d:Passive of <man>, catch: be caught, arrested or taken captive; {sal-in kiman} is be taken as a captive.) (s:kimat) (a:kikhah)
kimancip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be held captive/be seized) (d:{Mancip}, seize and hold fast, with the prefix <ki>: be held captive; {a kimancip} before a noun means captive.) (b:mancip) (q:draft)
kimang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be of use/be used/be in effect) (d:Be of use or be in use; mostly negative, {bangmah-a kimang lo} is worthless, of no use; also last or stay in use for a time.) (s:phatuam/kizang) (r:20.12.19) (q:draft)
kimangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being used/being in effect) (d:{Kimang}, be in use, with the linking suffix <in>; said of a gift that is in use only for a time.) (b:kimang) (q:draft)
kimangngailh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be forgotten) (d:A spelling of <kimangngilh>: be forgotten, said of past troubles that are no longer remembered.) (s:kimangngilh) (a:kiphawk) (q:draft)
kimangngilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be forgotten) (d:Passive of <mangngilh>, forget, with the prefix <ki>: be forgotten; {kimangngilh bawl} is make oneself forget.) (s:kimangngailh) (a:kiphawk) (b:mangngilh) (q:draft)
kimangngilhkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overlooked/be forgotten by chance) (d:Be forgotten or passed over by chance; said of dead bodies left unburied because no one noticed them.) (q:draft)
kimangpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be used straight on/continue in use) (d:<kimang>, be used, with <pah>, straight away; of the existing priests simply being kept in use) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimangthangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut off/be destroyed) (d:Passive with <ki> of <mangthangsak>, cause to perish: be destroyed, be cut off from one’s people.) (b:mangthangsak) (q:draft)
kimangzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be more useful/be better) (d:{Kimang}, be of use, with <zaw>, more: be of more use, be better.) (b:kimang) (q:draft)
kimanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being caught/being captured/being arrested) (d:{Kiman}, be caught, with the linking suffix <in> that joins it to the next verb: being caught, arrested or captured.) (b:kiman) (q:draft)
kimanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:use/usefulness/value) (d:What something is good for; {a kimanna om lo} or {kimanna nei lo} means useless, worthless.) (s:manphatna) (r:32.2.8) (q:draft)
kimansiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be completed/be finished) (d:{Kiman}, finished, with <siang>, clean: be wholly finished, said of work carried through to the end.) (s:kizawh/kizo) (b:kiman) (q:draft)
kimante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:captives/those captured/prisoners) (d:{Kiman}, be taken, with the plural <te>: those who have been captured; {sal-a kimante} are people taken captive, and after a battle the word also covers the plunder taken.) (s:salte/saltangte/galmatte) (b:kiman) (r:42.4.18) (q:draft)
kimanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be caught) (d:{Kiman}, be caught, with <zo>, be able or enough: said of fish, whether enough could be caught.) (b:kiman) (q:draft)
kimap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spared) (d:Be spared, be left alive; {na nuntakna hong kimap ding} means your life will be spared.) (s:kisiit/kisuaktasak) (q:draft)
kimasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:{Kima}, divorced, with the completive suffix <sa>: said of a woman who has been sent away by her husband.) (s:maksa/kikhensa) (b:kima) (q:draft)
kimat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:arrest/seize/be arrested/be caught) (d:Passive of <mat>, seize, with the prefix <ki>: be arrested, be caught or be taken captive.) (s:kiman) (a:kikhah)
kimat = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:sticky/adhesive/gluey/joined/attached) (d:Holding or sticking to each other; said of parts that are joined or fitted together.)
kimatcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stick fast/be sealed/be tightly joined) (d:{Kimat}, hold together, with <cip>, firmly: be stuck fast or tightly closed, said of a hand stuck to a sword, a sealed book and scales shut together.) (s:kisiincip) (b:kimat) (q:draft)
kimatheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be known beforehand/be foreseen) (d:{Theih}, know, with <ma>, before, and the prefix <ki>: be known beforehand; {a kimatheih lo} is something that cannot be known in advance.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined to/adjoin/be attached to) (d:{Kimat}, be joined, with the linking suffix <in>; after <tawh> it means next to or connected with.) (s:kigizawng) (b:kimat) (q:draft)
kimatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:capture/arrest/seizure) (d:{Kimat}, be caught, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact of being caught or taken.) (s:matna) (b:kimat) (q:draft)
kimatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fasten together/join/couple) (d:{Kimat}, hold to each other, with the causative <sak>: join things so that they hold together, as curtains with clasps.) (s:zom) (b:kimat) (q:draft)
kimatsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fastening together/joining) (d:{Kimatsak}, join things so that they hold together, with the linking suffix <in>; said of foxes tied tail to tail.) (b:kimatsak) (q:draft)
kimawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:condemn oneself/blame oneself/accuse one another) (d:{Mawhsak}, accuse or condemn, with the prefix <ki>: with <amah le amah> condemn oneself, with {khat leh khat} accuse one another.) (a:kimaisak) (b:mawhsak) (q:draft)
kimawhsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:condemning one another/accusing/condemning oneself) (d:{Kimawhsak}, condemn oneself or accuse one another, with the linking suffix <in>.) (a:kimaisakin) (b:kimawhsak) (q:draft)
kimawhsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:accusation/charge/blame) (d:An accusation made against someone; also the condemning of oneself in the heart, a guilty conscience.) (s:mawhsakna/mawhzonna) (b:mawhsakna) (q:draft)
kimawhsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:accusations/charges) (d:{Kimawhsakna} with the plural <te>: the things a person is accused of.) (s:mawhsaknate/mawhzonnate) (b:kimawhsakna) (q:draft)
kimawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:idly/without cause) (d:the prefix <ki> joined to <mawk>, idly or for no reason, and written before the verb that <ki> belongs to: {kimawk tot}, quarrel for no reason; {kimawk hoho}, chat idly with one another; {kimawk phat}, praise oneself emptily) (s:mawk) (b:mawk) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimawkphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flatter oneself) (d:{Mawkphat}, praise idly or flatter, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: flatter oneself.) (b:mawkphat) (q:draft)
kimawksai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spring/go off) (d:of a trap, spring shut with nothing in it) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimawktot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quarrel without cause/accuse for no reason) (d:{Mawk}, idly or without reason, with <kitot>, quarrel: pick a quarrel with someone for no reason.) (q:draft)
kimawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:playing/play) (d:<kimawl>, play, with the linking ending <in>: playing) (b:kimawl) (q:draft)
kimawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:game/contest/sport) (d:<kimawl>, play, with the noun suffix <na>: a contest in which athletes compete) (b:kimawl) (q:draft)
kimawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make perform/make play) (d:<kimawl>, play or perform, with the causative <sak>: have someone perform or hold a contest before onlookers) (b:kimawl) (q:draft)
kimawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who play/ones playing) (d:<kimawl> play, with the plural <te>: the ones who are playing, here of children) (b:kimawl) (r:40.11.16) (q:draft)
kimciang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:middle/halfway/half) (d:The halfway point of the height or extent of a thing; <kim>, middle, with <ciang>, as far as.) (s:kim) (q:draft)
kimeekcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be crushed) (d:Be squeezed or pressed flat, be crushed; passive with the prefix <ki>.) (q:draft)
kimeeltheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be acquainted/know each other) (d:A spelling of <kimeltheih>: know one another by sight, be acquainted; <tawh> marks the other person.) (s:kimeltheih) (q:draft)
kimeetsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shorn/be sheared) (d:Passive with <ki> of <meetsak>, have the wool cut off: be shorn.) (s:kimet) (b:meetsak) (q:draft)
kimeltheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be acquainted/get acquainted/be associated) (d:{Meltheih}, know by face, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: know each other, be acquainted; <tawh> marks the other person.) (s:kimeeltheih) (b:meltheih) (q:draft)
kimemat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be connected/have to do with each other) (d:of two things, belong together or rest on one another; here said of keeping the law and faith, with <lo>: have nothing to do with each other) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimematna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:claim/connection/share) (d:<kimemat> be connected with, with the noun suffix <na>: something that ties a person to a matter and gives a right in it) (b:kimemat) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaved/be shorn) (d:Passive of <met>, shave or shear, with the prefix <ki>: of hair or wool, be cut off.) (s:kikiat/kimeetsak) (b:met) (q:draft)
kimetcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse/sink down/be levelled) (d:said of the age-old hills before God, in parallel with <kitamkham> crumble; how the word is built is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimetmai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaved off/be cut off) (d:Passive with <ki> of <met>, shave: of a beard, be shaved clean away.) (q:draft)
kimettol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/be shaved) (d:Passive of <mettol> with the prefix <ki>: of the head, be shaved completely, as a sign of mourning.) (b:mettol) (q:draft)
kimettolsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/have the head shaved) (d:<kimettol> be shaved bald, with <sak>: have the hair shaved off completely, as a sign of mourning) (b:kimettol) (q:draft)
kimin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:fully/completely/in full/all) (d:{Kim}, complete, with the suffix <in>: the whole of it, with nothing and no one left out; often as {a kimin}.) (s:vekpi/vekin) (b:kim) (q:draft)
kimindaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dishonoured/be disgraced/be put to shame) (d:Passive with <ki> of <mindaisak>, bring a name into disgrace.) (s:kizahhuaisak/kiminsia-sak) (a:kipahtawi) (b:mindaisak) (q:draft)
kiminsia = (t:see) <kiminsia-sak>
kiminsia-sak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be disgraced) (d:Be given a bad name: <min>, name, with <sia>, bad, and the causative <sak>, passive with <ki>.) (s:kizahhuaisak/kimindaisak/kimaizumsak) (a:kipahtawi) (q:draft)
kiminthan = (t:see) <kiminthan'sak>
kiminthan'sak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be glorified/be honoured) (d:Passive of <minthangsak>, glorify; <minthang> is shortened to <minthan> before <sak>.) (s:kiminthangsak/kiminthansak/kithangsak) (a:kimindaisak) (q:draft)
kiminthangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be glorified/be honored) (d:Passive of <minthangsak>, glorify, with the prefix <ki>: be glorified, be honoured.) (s:kiminthansak/kithangsak/kipahtawi) (a:kimindaisak) (b:minthangsak) (q:draft)
kiminthansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be glorified/be made famous) (d:Passive with <ki> of <min>, name, <than>, be renowned, and the causative <sak>: be made famous, be glorified.) (s:kiminthangsak/kithangsak) (a:kimindaisak) (q:draft)
kiminthansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:glorification/display of splendour) (d:{Kiminthansak}, be glorified, with the noun suffix <na>: that by which someone is glorified.) (b:kiminthansak) (q:draft)
kimitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put out/be extinguished/be quenched) (d:Passive of <mitsak>, put out, with the prefix <ki>: of a fire or of anger, be put out; mostly negative, {kimitsak lo ding hi}, it shall not go out.) (s:kisumit/kisukmit) (a:kitawhkuang) (b:mitsak) (q:draft)
Kimittawsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blind oneself/make oneself blind) (d:{Mittaw}, blind, with the prefix <ki>, oneself, and the causative <sak>: make oneself blind.) (q:draft)
kimkhat = (i:2) (t:prep) (w:among) (d:Some among a group, placed after the noun that names the group.)
kimkhatte = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:among) (d:Some among a group, placed after the noun that names the group; also one half, as in {Manasseh minam kimkhatte}, the half-tribe of Manasseh.) (b:kimkhat)
kimkhattte = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:among) (d:A spelling of <kimkhatte> found once, at the start of a sentence: some among them.)
Kimkhattte = (i:1) (t:det) (w:some/others) (d:Some of them, here some of the seed; apparently a misprint of <kimkhatte>.) (b:kimkhattte) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimkot = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around/on all sides/round about) (d:On every side of a person or thing; written after a noun or after <a>, often with the endings <a> or <ah>.) (s:kiim)
kimkota = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:around/surrounding) (d:{Kimkot}, around, with the ending <a> that links it to the following noun: that which is around.) (s:kiima/kiimah) (b:kimkot) (r:26.41.12) (q:draft)
kimkotah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around/on every side) (d:{Kimkot}, around, with the place marker <ah>: on every side of the thing named before it.) (s:kiim) (b:kimkot)
kimkotin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around/round about) (d:{Kimkot}, around, with the suffix <in>; after a noun, going or lying all around it.) (s:kiim) (b:kimkot) (q:draft)
kimkotteng = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:all around/on every side) (d:{Kimkot}, around, with <teng>, all: the whole surrounding of a thing, placed after the thing surrounded.) (b:kimkot) (q:draft)
kimlai = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:while/while still/although) (d:Placed after a descriptive word or clause: while still being so, even though it is so; often followed by {hi napi}, although.) (s:laitakin/laitak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimlaipi = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:even while/while) (d:<Kimlai>, while, with the intensive <pi>: at the very time that something is so.) (b:kimlai) (q:draft)
kimna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<kim> all, complete, with the noun suffix <na>, placed after a verb: the doing of it in full, to every one or in every detail; {tunpih kimna} is the bringing of all of them) (b:kim) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimnai = (t:see) <kimnai-a>
kimnai-a = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:nearby/in the vicinity) (d:{Kim}, around, with <nai>, near, and the place ending <a>; {a kimnai-a om} means which is close by.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimpipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:king) (d:apparently a misprint of <kumpipa>, the king) (s:kumpipa) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:please/satisfy/delight) (d:make the heart content: <kim>, complete, with the causative <sak>, used after <lung> or <lungsim>, heart, as in {ka lung hong kimsak}, it pleases me) (s:lungkimsak) (q:draft)
kimsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:set on edge) (d:of something sour acting on the teeth, as vinegar does) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:fully/completely/in full) (d:<kim>, complete, with <takin>, which makes an adverb: in full, with nothing lacking; usually written {a kimtakin}) (s:kicingin/kimin) (b:kim) (q:draft)
kimte = (i:1) (t:det) (w:all/every) (d:<kim> with the plural <te>, placed after a noun; {minam kimte} is all nations) (b:kim) (r:27.7.14) (q:draft)
kimu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet) (d:see each other, come together with someone: <mu>, see, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>; <tawh> marks the person met) (s:kituah/tuak) (b:mu)
kimuan = (t:see) <kimuan'na>
kimuan'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:confidence/self-confidence/trust) (d:what a person relies on; {ei leh ei kimuan'na} is trust in oneself) (s:kimuanna/muanna) (q:draft)
kimuang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be confident/rely on oneself/trust in oneself) (d:<muang> trust, with the reflexive prefix <ki>; {kimuang takin} is confidently) (b:muang) (q:draft)
kimuangmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:doubt one another/suspect one another) (d:reciprocal <ki> with <muangmawh> doubt, be unsure of) (q:draft)
kimuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:confidence/trust/self-reliance) (d:<muanna>, trust, with the prefix <ki>: trust in oneself, confidence; {kimuanna lungsim} is a confident heart) (s:kimuan'na/muanna) (b:muanna) (q:draft)
kimudah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hated/be detested) (d:passive of <mudah>, hate: be hated by others) (b:mudah) (q:draft)
kimudah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:hate one another/loathe oneself) (d:with {khat leh khat}, hate each other; with <tawm>, loathe oneself) (s:kimuhdah) (b:mudah) (q:draft)
kimudahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hating one another) (d:<kimudah> hate each other, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kimudah) (q:draft)
kimudahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set at odds/cause to hate each other) (d:<kimudah> hate each other, with the causative <sak>) (b:kimudah) (q:draft)
kimudahtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:loathe oneself/hate oneself) (d:<kimudah> hate, with <tawm>, oneself, by oneself) (q:draft)
kimuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be found/be seen/appear) (d:passive form of <muh> see, used before endings such as <theih>, <leh> and <ciangin>) (b:muh) (q:draft)
kimuh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:meet/see each other) (d:form of <kimu> used before endings such as <ciangin>) (b:kimu) (q:draft)
kimuhdah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hate each other) (d:reciprocal <ki> with <muhdah> hate; {kimuhdah sak} is cause to hate each other, set at odds) (s:kimudah) (a:ki-it) (b:muhdah) (q:draft)
kimuhdahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being hated/hatred/bitterness) (d:<kimuhdah> with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being hated or unloved, and also hatred between people) (s:muhdahna) (a:itna) (b:kimuhdah) (q:draft)
kimuhmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overlook/turn a blind eye/ignore) (d:with <bawl>, do: act as if one had not seen a wrong) (q:draft)
kimuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being found/where it is found) (d:<kimuh>, be found or be seen, with {-na}: the place, the person or the way in which something is found or seen) (b:kimuh) (q:draft)
kimuhnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:long to see/wish to meet) (d:<kimuh> meet, see each other, with <nop> wish; used with <tawh> for the person) (q:draft)
kimuhpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet/meet with/come across) (d:<kimuh> meet, with <pih> together with; {na kimuhpih peuhpeuh}, anyone you meet) (b:kimuh) (q:draft)
kimuhsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be seen below/be looked down on) (d:<kimuh> be seen, with <suk> downward; of land that can be seen from a height) (b:kimuh) (q:draft)
kimukhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be found out/be discovered/be discerned) (d:passive of <mukhia>, find out, with the prefix <ki>: come to light, be found out or recognised) (s:kitheikhia/kiphawkkhia) (b:mukhia) (q:draft)
kimukik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be seen again/be found again) (d:passive of <mukik> see again, with the prefix <ki>; {kimukik ngei nawn lo} is never to be found again) (b:mukik) (q:draft)
kimukik = (i:2) (t:v) (w:meet again/see each other again) (d:<kimu> meet, with <kik> again) (b:kimu) (q:draft)
kimusa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:seen/already seen) (d:<kimu> be seen, with <sa> marking what has already happened) (b:kimu) (q:draft)
kimusak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show/let see/be shown) (d:cause people to see a thing) (s:kilangsak) (b:musak) (q:draft)
kimusak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:bring to meet/bring before) (d:<kimu> meet with the causative <sak>, with <tawh> for the person met) (b:kimu) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blown/be sounded) (d:passive of <mut> blow, of a trumpet) (s:kitum) (b:mut) (q:draft)
kimute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things found/things seen) (d:<kimu> be seen or found, with the plural <te>: the things that were found, here the wrongs found in a king) (b:kimu) (q:draft)
kimuthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:visible/seen) (d:that can be seen; the opposite is {kimu thei lo}, unseen) (b:muthei) (q:draft)
kimutheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:visible things/things seen) (d:<kimuthei> visible, with the plural <te>) (b:kimuthei) (q:draft)
kimuzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be found/can be found) (d:passive of <muzo> find; {kimuzo nawn lo}, could no longer be found) (s:kiphawkkhia) (b:muzo) (q:draft)
kimvel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go around/march around/encircle) (d:go all the way round a place, as Israel marched around Jericho for seven days) (q:draft)
kin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:heed/care about/be zealous for/be eager) (d:give attention or care to something, be concerned or eager about it; {kin lo} means ignore or neglect, <kin ngaihsut> means press or treat as urgent) (s:awlmawh/thudon) (r:20.18.2) (q:draft)
kin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:move/shift/move on) (d:change place, go from one spot to another; {nunglamah kin} means draw back) (r:18.38.11) (q:draft)
Kinah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kinah) (d:town in the far south of Judah, toward the border of Edom) (r:6.15.22)
kinai = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:close/near) (d:of kinship, closely related; {a kinai beh}, a close relative) (b:nai) (q:draft)
kinaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw near each other/close in/draw up) (d:<ki> each other with <naih> approach: of two armies, come up close to one another for battle) (b:naih) (q:draft)
kinailua = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:too closely related) (d:<kinai> closely related, with <lua> too much; {si kinailua mi}, a person too near in blood) (b:kinai) (q:draft)
kinaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:relationship/kinship/closeness) (d:<kinai> be near or closely related, with the noun suffix <na>; <tawh> marks the other person) (b:kinai) (q:draft)
kinaipen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:nearest/closest) (d:<kinai>, be near, with <pen>, most; used with <tawh> for the place it is nearest to) (s:naipen) (a:gamlapen) (b:kinai) (q:draft)
kinaipih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:close relative/near kin) (d:one who is closely related, also used before a noun as closely related) (s:tanau) (b:kinai) (q:draft)
kinaipihpen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nearest relative/closest kin) (d:<kinaipih> close relative, with the superlative <pen>) (b:kinaipih) (q:draft)
kinaita = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have come near/be now close) (d:<kinai> be near, with <ta> marking a change now reached) (b:kinai) (q:draft)
kinak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:hard/greatly/tightly) (d:<ki> with <nak>, strongly, placed before a verb: {kinak hawl} be driven hard, {kinak mat} hold fast to each other, {kinak lin} be greatly shaken) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinakko = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shout loudly/cry out) (d:<kinak> strongly with <ko> shout: shout hard; with <semsem>, all the more) (q:draft)
kinam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kiss each other) (d:reciprocal <ki> with <nam> kiss, smell) (q:draft)
kinamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kissing each other/with a kiss) (d:<kinam> with the connective <in>; greeting one another with a kiss) (b:kinam) (q:draft)
kinangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leaning on/supporting oneself on) (d:reflexive <ki> with <nang> prop up, support, and the linking ending in) (q:draft)
kinapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kiss) (d:<napna> kiss, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: the kissing of one another as a greeting) (b:napna) (q:draft)
kinawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hurry) (d:act or come without delay; {hong kinawh in} is hurry here, come quickly) (s:nawhtat) (a:zekai) (r:14.35.21)
kinawh = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:quickly) (d:{kinawh}, hurry, used before another action: in a hurry, at once) (s:manlang)
kinawhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:quickly/in haste/hurriedly) (d:form of <kinawh> with {-in}, hurrying to do the next action) (s:manlangin) (b:kinawh) (q:draft)
kinawhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be driven out/be banished) (d:passive with <ki> of <nawhkhia> drive out) (b:nawhkhia) (q:draft)
kinawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:haste/hurrying) (d:<kinawh> hurry, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kinawh) (q:draft)
kinawhsa = (t:see) <kinawhsa-in>
kinawhsa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in haste/hurriedly) (d:<kinawh> hurry with <sa> and the adverb ending <in>: in a hurried state) (q:draft)
kinawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hurry/make haste/hasten) (d:<kinawh> hurry with <sak>; {va kinawhsak un}, go and have them hurry, said of fetching the wailing women quickly) (b:kinawh) (q:draft)
kinawlkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set aside/be discarded) (d:passive with <ki> of <nawlkhin> put aside, reject) (b:nawlkhin) (q:draft)
kinawmsawm = (t:see) <kinawmsawm-in>
kinawmsawm-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapsing/being brought down) (d:said of those who sink down and fall, with the linking ending <in>; the exact sense of the base is not certain) (s:kinawmsawmin) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinawmsawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapsing/being brought down) (d:said of those who sink down and fall, with the linking ending <in>; the exact sense of the base is not certain) (s:kinawmsawm-in) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinawmvalh = (t:see) <kinawmvalh-in>
kinawmvalh-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being swallowed up) (d:passive with <ki> of <nawmvalh> swallow whole, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kinawmvalhin) (q:draft)
kinawmvalhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being swallowed up) (d:passive with <ki> of <nawmvalh> swallow whole, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kinawmvalh-in) (q:draft)
kinawngkai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disturbed/be troubled) (d:<ki> with <nawngkai> be troubled; {kinawngkai sak}, be caused trouble) (b:nawngkai) (q:draft)
kinawngkaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disturbed/be troubled) (d:passive of <nawngkaisak> trouble, disturb, with the prefix <ki>) (b:nawngkaisak) (r:13.17.9) (q:draft)
kinawtkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be scoured off/be rubbed off/be removed) (d:passive of <nawtkhia>, here in the sense rub or scrape out: of the burnt crust in a cooking pot) (b:nawtkhia) (q:draft)
kinawtngil = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:polished/burnished) (d:rubbed until it shines, said of metal) (s:zutsiang) (q:draft)
kine = (i:1) (t:n) (w:food) (d:what is eaten: <ne>, eat, with the prefix <ki>, used before a noun as in {a kine an}, food that is eaten) (b:ne)
kineh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come close/go near/keep close) (d:<ki> with <neh> press close: get close up to a person or place, with <tawh> for a person) (b:neh) (q:draft)
kinehcipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crowding together/pressing on one another) (d:reciprocal <ki> with <neh> press and <cip> tightly, and the linking ending <in>; of a packed crowd) (q:draft)
kinehkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come close to/get near) (d:<ki> with <neh> come near, press close, and <kha> happen to; used with <tawh> and <kei> as a warning not to get near someone) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinehlua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be too crowded/press too closely) (d:<kineh> press close together with <lua> too much: of a crowd, packed so tight that no one can get through) (b:kineh) (q:draft)
kinei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consider oneself/claim to be) (d:after a word with {-a}: regard oneself as, or set oneself to do, what is named; {mipil-a kinei}, think oneself wise) (s:kisa) (b:nei) (r:29.3.4) (q:draft)
kinei = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be held/be had/be done) (d:passive of <nei>: be had, held or carried out, as a feast, an inquiry or a custom) (b:nei) (q:draft)
kineih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pretend/feign/pose as) (d:make oneself out to be what one is not; follows the thing pretended) (s:kineihkhem) (q:draft)
kineihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pretending/feigning) (d:<kineih> with the linking <in>, pretending to do or be something) (b:kineih) (q:draft)
kineihin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:going to law/disputing) (d:in {thu kineihin}, having a dispute or lawsuit with one another) (q:draft, low confidence)
kineihkhem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pretend/be hypocritical/be false) (d:put on a false appearance to deceive; {mihoih a kineihkhem mi} is a hypocrite, {kamsang kineihkhem} a false prophet) (s:kineih) (q:draft)
kineihkhemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pretending/under false pretences) (d:<kineihkhem> pretend, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kineihkhem) (q:draft)
kineihkhemna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hypocrisy/pretence) (d:<kineihkhem>, pretend, with the noun suffix <na>: a show of goodness that is not real) (s:simtatna/kineihna) (b:kineihkhem) (q:draft)
kineihkhemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pretenders/hypocrites/false ones) (d:plural; those who pretend to be what they are not, as in {kamsang kineihkhemte} false prophets) (s:simtatte) (b:kineihkhem) (q:draft)
kineihlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still claim to be/still pretend to be) (d:<kineih> make oneself out to be, with <lai> still) (q:draft)
kineihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dispute/lawsuit) (d:in {thu kineihna}, a case that people have against one another: {thu neihna}, lawsuit, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (b:neihna) (q:draft)
kineihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:pretence/show) (d:<kineih> pretend, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kineihkhemna) (b:kineih) (q:draft)
kineihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disputes/lawsuits) (d:plural of <kineihna>; {thu kineihnate} are the cases people have against one another) (b:kineihna) (q:draft)
kineihnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to make oneself/claim to be) (d:<kineih> make oneself out to be, with <nuam> want) (q:draft)
kineihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go to law with/dispute with/confront) (d:in {thu kineihpih}, have a case against someone in court: <kineih> as in <kineihna> dispute, with <pih> together with) (q:draft)
kineipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pretender/self-styled man) (d:man who makes himself out to be what is named, <kinei> claim to be with <pa> marking a man; {kamsanga kineipa}, you who call yourself a seer) (b:kinei) (q:draft)
kineite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those regarded as/those considered) (d:<kinei> be held or regarded as, with <te>; the ones who are counted as, or count themselves as, something) (b:kinei) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be eaten) (d:passive of <ne> eat, in the form used before <bang>, <leh> and nouns) (b:nek) (q:draft)
kinek = (i:2) (t:v) (w:devour one another/eat each other) (d:reciprocal of <ne> eat) (b:nek) (q:draft)
kinelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made smooth/be smoothed) (d:<nel> fine or smooth with the causative <sak> and passive <ki>: of rough ground) (q:draft)
kinem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be comforted/be consoled) (d:<nem> soft, gentle, with the prefix <ki>: be soothed; {kinem zo lo} is cannot be comforted) (s:kihehnem) (b:nem) (q:draft)
kinemang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be eaten up/be devoured/be destroyed) (d:passive of <nemang>, eat up, with the prefix <ki>: be grazed bare or devoured, said of a vineyard whose hedge is taken away) (b:nemang) (q:draft)
kinen = (t:see) <kinen'niamna>
kinen'niamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oppression) (d:{nen’niam}, oppress, with the prefix <ki> and the noun suffix <na>: the state of being pressed down by an enemy) (s:kinetniamna/kisukcipna) (a:suahtakna) (q:draft)
kinen'niamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oppressions/acts of oppression) (d:<kinen'niamna> oppression, with the plural <te>) (s:kinenniamnate/kisukcipnate/bawlsiatnate) (q:draft)
kinencip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:oppress each other) (d:<nencip>, press down or oppress, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: people oppress one another) (b:nencip) (q:draft)
kinengcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be crushed/be pressed down) (d:passive of <nengcip>, crush or press hard, with the prefix <ki>: of a person, be utterly crushed; of a measure of grain, be pressed down) (b:nengcip) (q:draft)
kinengniam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be oppressed/be mistreated/be afflicted) (d:passive of <nengniam>, oppress, with the prefix <ki>; {a kinengniam mite} are the oppressed) (s:kinenniam/kibawlsia/kisikcip) (a:suakta) (b:nengniam) (q:draft)
kinengniamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being oppressed/oppressed) (d:<kinengniam>, be oppressed, with the linking ending <in>: being oppressed, followed by another verb) (b:kinengniam) (q:draft)
kinengniamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the oppressed/oppressed people) (d:<kinengniam> be oppressed, with the plural <te>: those who are oppressed) (a:nengniamte) (b:kinengniam) (q:draft)
kinenniam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be oppressed/be afflicted) (d:passive of <nenniam>, press down or oppress, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kinengniam/kisikcip) (b:nenniam) (q:draft)
kinenniamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oppressions/acts of oppression) (d:<kinenniam> be oppressed, with the noun suffix <na> and the plural <te>) (s:kinen'niamnate/kisukcipnate) (b:kinenniam) (q:draft)
kinet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:oppress/press down) (d:first part of {kinet niamna}, oppression, written as two words in one verse; the usual spelling is <kinetniamna> in one word) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinetniamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oppression) (d:<netniamna> oppression with the prefix <ki>: people oppressing one another, or the state of being oppressed) (s:kinen'niamna/kisukcipna) (a:suahtakna) (b:netniamna) (q:draft)
kineu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:little horn/small horn) (d:<ki>, horn, with <neu>, small: the little horn seen in the visions of Daniel) (q:draft)
kineu = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be small in one's own eyes/think oneself small) (d:<neu>, small, with the reflexive prefix <ki>, used with <ngaihsut>, think: {na kineu ngaihsut}, you thought of yourself as small) (b:neu) (q:draft, low confidence)
kineubawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be degraded/be belittled/be humiliated) (d:passive of <neubawl>, make small: be made little of or disgraced in the eyes of others) (a:kipahtawi) (b:neubawl) (q:draft)
kinga = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rest on/be set on/come to rest) (d:be placed so as to rest or lie on something, with <tungah>, on; of a hand, be laid on someone) (q:draft)
kingah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be obtained/be gained/be received/be won) (d:passive of <ngah>, get, with the prefix <ki>: something is got, won or received; with <pan> or <panin>, from) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
kingahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being obtained/being received) (d:<kingah> be obtained, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kingah) (q:draft)
kingahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be received back/be received in reply) (d:<kingah> be obtained, with <kik> back, again) (b:kingah) (q:draft)
kingahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be given/be granted) (d:passive of <ngahsak> cause to receive: be made to receive a share) (s:kipiak) (b:ngahsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spoils/things obtained) (d:<kingah> be obtained, with the plural <te>; {gal sunga a kingahte}, what was taken in war) (b:kingah) (q:draft)
kingahzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be had/can be obtained) (d:<kingah> be obtained, with <zo> be able) (b:kingah) (q:draft)
kingai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be betrothed/be lovers/love each other) (d:love each other as man and woman, be promised to each other in marriage; with <tawh> for the partner) (a:kimudah) (q:draft)
kingai = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be heard/be listened to) (d:passive of <ngai>, listen, with the prefix <ki>: of a prayer or voice, be heard) (s:kiza) (b:ngai) (q:draft)
kingaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:love each other/be lovers) (d:form of <kingai> used as a verbal noun, being in love with someone, with <tawh>: {nang tawh kingaih}, to be in love with you) (b:kingai) (q:draft)
kingaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:love/courtship) (d:the love of a man and a woman for each other) (s:itna) (a:kimuhdahna) (b:kingaih) (r:22.3.5) (q:draft)
kingaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consider oneself/think oneself/regard oneself) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: think of oneself as being something, with a describing word followed by <in> or <bangin>) (s:kisa) (b:ngaihsun) (q:draft)
kingaihsun = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be careful/take heed/watch oneself) (d:as a command, {kingaihsun in} or {kingaihsun un}, watch yourselves; with <loh nadingun>, be careful not to do something) (s:kidawm/kikem) (b:ngaihsun) (q:draft)
kingaihsunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:considering oneself/thinking oneself) (d:<kingaihsun>, consider oneself, with the linking ending <in>; after a phrase with <bangin> or <in> it is regarding oneself as such) (b:kingaihsun) (q:draft)
kingaihsunin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:being remembered/being called to mind) (d:<kingaihsun> in its passive sense, be called to mind, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kiphawkin) (b:kingaihsun) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingaihsut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:think of oneself/think of one another/regard oneself) (d:<ngaihsut> think with <ki>, turned back on oneself or shared between people; form used before <ding>, <nading> and <zawh>) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft)
kingaihsut = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be remembered/be thought of/be understood) (d:passive use; {a kingaihsut nadingin}, so that she is remembered; {a kingaihsut zawh loh}, what cannot be made sense of) (s:kiphawk) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingaihsutna = (t:see) <kingaihsutna-in>
kingaihsutna-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:for one's own sake) (d:<kingaihsutna>, thought or regard for oneself, with <in>, because of: {keimah ka kingaihsutna-in}, for my own sake) (q:draft)
kingaihsutnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thoughts) (d:<kingaihsutna> thought, thinking, with the plural <te>) (s:ngaihsutnate) (b:kingaihsut) (q:draft)
kingaihsutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be counted as/be credited/be reckoned) (d:<kingaihsut>, be considered, with <sak>: be reckoned or counted as something; {piakkhongin kingaihsutsak lo} is not counted as a gift) (b:kingaihsut) (q:draft)
kingak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wait for one another/be waited for) (d:<ngak>, wait, with the prefix <ki>: wait for one another; of a person, be waited for and so be given time) (s:kingakkim) (b:ngak) (q:draft)
kingak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lean on/lean against) (d:form of <kinga>, rest on, used before <theih> and <nading>: lean the weight of the body against something) (s:kingam/kingap) (b:kinga) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingakkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wait for one another) (d:reciprocal <ki> with <ngak> wait and <kim> complete: wait until all are present) (s:kingak) (q:draft)
kingakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stand/base) (d:a stand on which a thing rests, said of the wheeled bronze stands that held the basins of the temple) (b:ngakna) (r:11.7.43) (q:draft)
kingaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stands/supports/bases) (d:plural of <kingakna>, a thing that something rests on; in the verses the movable stands under the temple basins and the base of a table) (b:kingakna) (r:24.27.19) (q:draft)
kingam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lean/lean on/prop oneself) (d:rest the weight of the body on something for support, with <tungah> or <ah> for what is leaned on) (s:kingap/kingak) (q:draft)
kingamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leaning on/leaning against/propped up) (d:<kingam> with the connective <in>: resting one's weight on a person or thing) (b:kingam) (q:draft)
kingap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lean on/rest on) (d:put one's weight on something for support, with <tungah> on) (s:kingam/kingak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leaning) (d:<kingap> lean on, with the noun suffix <na>; before a noun, the one on whom someone leans) (b:kingap) (q:draft)
kingapnapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:man leaned on) (d:<kingapna> leaning, with <pa> marking a man: the officer on whose arm the king leaned) (b:kingapna) (q:draft)
kingawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:forcibly/by force/violently) (d:<ki> with <ngawh> roughly, placed before a verb: {kingawh laksak}, be taken away by force) (b:ngawh) (q:draft)
kingeina = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wear habitually/be accustomed to) (d:be used to a thing, elsewhere written in one word as <kingeinaseh>; here of cursing worn habitually like a garment) (s:kingeinaseh) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingeinaseh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be used to/be accustomed to) (d:be used to or accustomed to a thing; with <lo> or <kei>, not be used to it) (s:kingeina) (q:draft)
kingen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be asked/be requested/be demanded) (d:passive of <ngen>, ask, with the prefix <ki>: be asked for or demanded; {hong kingen} is asked leave of me, {a kingen thungetna} is the prayer that is offered) (b:ngen) (q:draft)
kingensak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pray) (d:in {thu kingensak in}, let prayer be made, let them pray: {thu ngen} pray, with <ki> and <sak> let) (b:kingen) (q:draft)
kinget = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be asked for/be demanded/be prayed) (d:form of <kingen>, passive of <ngen> ask, used before <leh> and <ciangin>) (b:nget) (q:draft)
kingetsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pray for one another/be prayed for) (d:<ngetsak>, ask on behalf of someone, with the prefix <ki>: with <thu>, pray for one another; of prayer or blessing, be asked for someone) (b:ngetsak) (q:draft)
kingim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be purposed/be planned/be determined) (d:passive of <ngim> purpose, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kigeel/kiciangtan) (b:ngim) (q:draft)
kingim = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be aimed at) (d:passive of <ngim> aim at, with the prefix <ki>; of a tree, have the ax aimed at its root) (b:ngim) (q:draft)
kingimzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be aimed at already) (d:<kingim> be aimed at, with <zo> marking completion; of a tree with the ax laid to its root) (b:kingim) (q:draft)
kinial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:argue/dispute/contend) (d:<nial>, dispute, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>: argue with one another; <tawh> marks the other party and <thu> the matter) (s:kiseel/kitot) (a:kithukim) (b:nial) (q:draft)
kinial = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be denied/be disowned/be set aside) (d:passive of <nial>, deny or refuse, with the prefix <ki>) (b:nial) (q:draft)
kinialin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:arguing/disputing/debating) (d:<kinial> argue, with the linking ending <in>; {thu kinialin}, arguing over a matter) (b:kinial) (q:draft)
kinialkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:refuse each other/deprive each other) (d:reciprocal <ki> with <nial> refuse and <kha> happen to) (q:draft)
kinialna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:argument/dispute/quarrel/controversy) (d:<kinial>, argue, with the noun suffix <na>: arguing between people; {Topa a kinialna thu} is the case the Lord brings against his people) (s:kitotna/kiselna/kiseelna) (a:kithukimna/kilemna) (b:kinial) (q:draft)
kinialnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:arguments/disputes/controversies) (d:plural of <kinialna>) (s:kitotnate/kiselnate/kiseelnate) (b:kinialna) (q:draft)
kiniam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought low/be humbled) (d:<niam>, low, with the prefix <ki>; in the verses always with <koih>, put: {kiniam koih} is be brought low, by enemies, hardship or God) (s:kiniamkoih/kiniamkhiat) (a:kilamsang/kipahtawi) (b:niam) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:humble oneself/be humbled/be brought low) (d:<niamkhiat>, bring down, with the prefix <ki>: humble oneself before God or people, or be humbled; before a noun, humble, as in {lungsim kiniamkhiat mite}, the humble in heart) (s:kiniamsak/kiniam/kiniamkoih) (a:kiphasak/kiliansak/kilamsang) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:humbling oneself/humbly) (d:connective form of <kiniamkhiat>, humbling oneself or humbly, followed by another verb) (s:kiniamsakin) (b:kiniamkhiat) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:humility/lowliness/humbling oneself) (d:<kiniamkhiat>, humble oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: a humble attitude toward God and other people) (s:kiniamsakna) (a:kiphatsakna/kiliatsakna) (b:kiniamkhiat) (r:38.9.9) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be humbled/be brought low) (d:<kiniamkhiat> be humbled, with <suk> downward) (s:kiniamkoih) (a:kilamsang) (b:kiniamkhiat) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the humble/the lowly) (d:plural of <kiniamkhiat>, those who humble themselves) (s:kiniamsakte) (a:kiphasakte/kiliansakte/kihisakte) (b:kiniamkhiat) (r:42.18.14) (q:draft)
kiniamkoih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought low/be humbled) (d:be put in a low and helpless state by enemies or hardship) (s:kiniam/kiniamkhiat) (a:kilamsang) (b:niamkoih) (q:draft)
kiniamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:humble oneself/submit/be humble/be made low) (d:<niamsak>, make low, with the prefix <ki>: make oneself low before another, submit; of hills, be made low) (s:kiniamkhiat) (a:kiliansak/kiphasak) (b:niamsak) (q:draft)
kiniamsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:humbling oneself/with humility) (d:<kiniamsak> humble oneself, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kiniamkhiatin) (b:kiniamsak) (q:draft)
kiniamsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:humility/lowliness/humiliation) (d:<kiniamsak>, humble oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: humility, or being brought low; often with <lungsim> or <lung>, heart) (s:kiniamkhiatna) (a:kiphatsakna/kiliatsakna) (b:kiniamsak) (q:draft)
kiniamsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who humble themselves) (d:<kiniamsak> humble oneself, with the plural <te>) (s:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kiniamsak) (q:draft)
kinil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be tossed/be thrown about) (d:passive with <ki> of <nil> throw; {kinil kawikawi}, be tossed to and fro) (b:nil) (q:draft)
kinilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be anointed) (d:passive of <nilh>, anoint, with the prefix <ki>: have oil put on one for an office; {sathau a kinilh siampi} is the anointed priest) (s:kinuh) (b:nilh) (r:4.3.3) (q:draft)
kinilhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being anointed/anointed) (d:<kinilh> be anointed, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kinilh) (q:draft)
kinilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:anointing) (d:<kinilh>, be anointed, with the noun suffix <na>; {sathau kinilhna}, anointing with oil) (s:nilhna) (b:kinilh) (q:draft)
kinilhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:anointed one) (d:<kinilh> be anointed, with <pa> for a man: {sathau kinilhpa}, the one anointed with oil, the Anointed One) (s:nilhpa) (b:kinilh) (q:draft)
kinilkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cast out/be driven away/be exiled) (d:passive of <nilkhia> cast out; {a kinilkhia Israelte}, the outcasts of Israel) (s:kinotkhia) (b:nilkhia) (q:draft)
kinim = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dyed/colourful) (d:of cloth, coloured; {puan kinim}, coloured garments) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinimte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dyed/colourful) (d:<kinim> dyed with the plural <te>, of garments: the coloured ones) (b:kinim) (q:draft)
kinin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be concerned about/care about/give heed to) (d:<kin>, heed, with <in>; {kinin nei} is have concern for something) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kinin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:defile oneself/become unclean) (d:<nin>, unclean, with the reflexive prefix <ki>; {kinin tawmsak} is make oneself unclean) (s:kininsak/kinitsak) (a:kisiangsak/kisiangtho) (b:nin) (q:draft)
kininsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defile oneself/make oneself unclean) (d:<ninsak>, make unclean, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: make oneself unclean, by idols, sexual sin or contact with the dead) (s:kinitsak/kininsaktawm/kidaisak) (a:kisiangsak/kisiansak) (b:ninsak) (q:draft)
kininsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defiling oneself/being defiled/being desecrated) (d:<kininsak> with the linking ending <in>: making oneself unclean, or of a holy place, being made unclean) (b:kininsak) (q:draft)
kininsaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:defiled) (d:<kininsak>, be made unclean, with the completive suffix <sa>; of a woman who has been defiled) (a:siangtho) (b:kininsak) (q:draft)
kininsaktawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defile oneself/make oneself unclean) (d:<ninsak> defile with <ki> and <tawm>, by one's own doing: bring uncleanness on oneself) (s:kininsak) (q:draft)
kinit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defile oneself/make oneself unclean) (d:the form of <kinin> used before <tawmsak>; <ki> with <nit> unclean) (s:kinin) (b:nit) (q:draft)
kinitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defile oneself/be defiled) (d:<nitsak>, make unclean, with the prefix <ki>: make oneself unclean, or of a person or holy place, be made unclean) (s:kininsak) (a:kisiangsak) (b:nitsak) (r:26.20.7) (q:draft)
kinkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:move together/move along with) (d:<kin> move, with <khawm> together) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kinkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:move away/move off/get away) (d:shift out of the place where one is, with <khia> out; as a command, go away; of a mountain, be moved from its place) (b:kin) (r:40.17.20) (q:draft)
kinkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away/move away/depart) (d:<kin> move with <khiat> out, away; used with {kiang pan}, from) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kinlo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not be moved/not be shaken) (d:<kin> move, with the negative <lo> written as one word) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kinloin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:neglecting/not caring about) (d:<kin> heed with <lo> not and the linking ending <in>: without care for, neglecting) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:zeal/concern/eagerness) (d:<kin>, care about or be eager, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kinnamon = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cinnamon) (d:a fragrant spice and the tree it comes from, {kinnamon kung}; the English word) (s:sinnamon) (q:draft)
kinolh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rejected/be turned away) (d:passive of <nolh>, reject, with the prefix <ki>: be turned away in shame) (a:kisan) (b:nolh) (q:draft)
kinomsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be soothed/be softened/be moistened) (d:passive of <nomsak> moisten: of wounds, be softened with oil) (b:nomsak) (q:draft)
kinophuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:name oneself/call oneself/take a name) (d:with {min tawh} and <amahmah>, give oneself an added name; <phuah> is give a name) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinopmawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ill feeling/resentment/discord) (d:ill feeling toward others, a mind that is not at ease with them; {lungsim kinopmawhna} is resentment in the heart, named beside <kitotna>, quarrelling) (s:kilemlohna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pushed/be driven) (d:passive with <ki> of <not>, push or drive; {kinot khia} is be driven out or cut off) (s:kihawl/kisawn) (b:not) (q:draft)
kinotkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be driven out/be driven away/be routed) (d:passive of <notkhia>, drive away) (s:kihawlkhia/kinawhkhia) (b:notkhia) (q:draft)
kinotsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pushed down/be driven down) (d:<kinot> be pushed, with <suk> downward; paired with <kinotto>, be driven this way and that) (b:kinot) (q:draft)
kinotto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pushed up/be driven up) (d:<kinot> be pushed, with <to> upward; paired with <kinotsuk>, be driven this way and that) (b:kinot) (q:draft)
kinsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:move/remove/shift) (d:<kin>, move, with causative <sak>: make something change its place) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kinsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:make heed/cause to care about) (d:<kin>, heed or care about, with causative <sak>; {hong kinsak kei in}, do not let me give my attention to) (b:kin) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swirl/churn) (d:of a storm, whirl round and round, with <nainai>) (r:24.23.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuai = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be fondled/be squeezed/be rubbed) (d:passive with <ki> of <nuai>, rub or press; with <gawp>, roughly) (s:kinuaigawp) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuai = (i:3) (t:v) (w:be subdued/be made subject) (d:in the compound {kinuai-siah}, be put under) (s:kinuaisiah) (b:nuai) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuaigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fondled/be squeezed) (d:passive with <ki> of <nuai> rub, knead, with <gawp> roughly, thoroughly) (s:kinuai) (q:draft)
kinuaisiah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be subdued/be subjugated/be brought low) (d:passive of <nuaisiah>, subdue; {a kinuaisiah mite}, those who are cast down) (s:kizo/kizawh/guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:nuaisiah) (q:draft)
kinuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be glad/be pleased) (d:impersonal <ki> with <nuam> be glad: there is gladness, people rejoice) (b:nuam) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take heart/cheer up/be comforted) (d:with <lung> or <lungsim> heart: <nuamsak> gladden with <ki> oneself, cheer oneself, take courage) (a:lungkia) (b:nuamsak) (q:draft)
kinuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be anointed/rub on oneself/be smeared) (d:passive of <nuh>, rub on: of oil or ointment put on a person or thing; {sathau kinuh} is be anointed or rubbed with oil) (s:kinilh/kizut) (b:nuh) (q:draft)
kinuihsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laughed at/be mocked/be scorned) (d:passive of <nuihsan>; also laugh among themselves) (s:kisimmawh/kizahko/kiphitsan) (b:nuihsan) (q:draft)
kinung = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:later/afterwards) (d:<ki> with <nung>, after, placed before a verb: {kinung theih} be known later, {kinung latsak} show afterwards) (b:nung) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinung = (i:2) (t:v) (w:turn the back) (d:only in {kinung hei}, turn one's back to flee) (s:lehngat) (b:nung) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinungkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be turned back/be driven back) (d:passive of <nungkiksak> turn back) (s:kilehhawl) (b:nungkiksak) (q:draft)
Kinungleh = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Kinungleh)
Kinunglehhei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:look back/turn back) (d:turn oneself round to look back, from <nung> back, <leh> opposite and <kihei> turn; written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and {Kinunglehhei kik lo} is without turning back) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinungsik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:regret afterwards/be sorry later) (d:<nung> after with <kisik> regret: come to regret a thing once it is done) (s:kisik) (q:draft)
kinungta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:live) (d:impersonal <ki> with <nungta>, live: people live, one lives; {sauveipipi kinungta} is people live very long) (b:nungta) (q:draft)
kinusia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be left/be abandoned/be deserted/be forsaken) (d:passive of <nusia>, leave: be left behind when others are taken, or of a city or a wife, be abandoned) (s:kinusiacip/kikoihkhong) (a:kila) (b:nusia) (q:draft)
kinusiacip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be forsaken/be deserted/be abandoned/be neglected) (d:<kinusia> with <cip> completely: be left entirely alone) (s:kinusia/kikoihkhong) (b:kinusia) (q:draft)
kinusiacipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being deserted/being abandoned/left desolate) (d:<kinusiacip> be deserted, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kinusiacip) (q:draft)
kinusiacipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leave deserted/make desolate) (d:<kinusiacip> be left behind for good, with the causative <sak>) (b:kinusiacip) (q:draft)
kinusialai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be still left/remain) (d:<kinusia> be left, with <lai> still) (s:omlai/suaktalai) (q:draft)
kinusiasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:abandoned/desolate/deserted) (d:<kinusia> be left, with <sa> marking what has already happened) (s:simtham) (b:kinusia) (q:draft)
kinusiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be left/be deserted/lie desolate) (d:form of <kinusia>, be left or deserted, used before words such as <sung> and <dong>) (b:kinusia) (q:draft)
kinusiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil/things left behind) (d:goods left behind; {van kinusiate} is the plunder of a captured city) (s:vankinusiate/kilate) (b:kinusia) (r:6.8.27) (q:draft)
kinzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:care more for/love more) (d:<kin> care about, be eager for, with <zaw> more) (s:itzaw) (b:kin) (q:draft)
kiomsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be established/be set in place) (d:passive with <ki> of <omsak> cause to be, put; {kiomsak kik}, be restored) (b:omsak) (q:draft)
kip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be established/stand firm/endure) (d:stand firm and last: of a house, a throne or an inheritance be established; of a word or of love, hold and endure; {kip den} and {kip tawntung} are endure forever) (s:kikip) (a:kiling) (r:58.13.1) (q:draft)
kip = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:steadfast/unfailing/firm/lasting) (d:placed after a noun: {itna kip} is steadfast love and {ngeina kip} a lasting ordinance) (s:kiptak/kician) (q:draft)
kipaai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown/be thrown away/be cast out) (d:passive of <paai>, throw: be thrown down or thrown away; {kipaai mang} is be cast away, and {na kipaai in} is throw yourself) (s:kilawn/kipaih) (b:paai) (q:draft)
kipaaidak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast out and exposed) (d:passive with <ki> of <paai> throw away, with <dak>; of a body left lying in the open) (s:kipaidak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipaaikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken away/be removed/be excluded/be cast out) (d:{ki-} passive form of <paaikhia>; also be cast up on a shore) (s:kilakkhiat/kipaikhia) (b:paaikhia) (q:draft)
kipaaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conception/being conceived) (d:passive <ki> with <paai> carry in the womb and the noun suffix <na>; {kei hong kipaaina naugil}, the womb in which I was conceived) (s:kipaiina/gaina) (q:draft)
kipaaithang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be strewn/be thrown about/lie scattered) (d:of dead bodies, be thrown out and left lying about; also written <kipaithang>) (s:kipaithang/kithehzak) (q:draft)
kipaaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make glad/gladden/give joy) (d:<kipaak>, a spelling of <kipak> rejoice, with the causative <sak>: make someone glad) (s:kipaksak/lungdamsak/nuamsak) (a:dahsak) (q:draft)
kipah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rejoice/be glad) (d:form of <kipak> rejoice used before endings such as <uh> and <nading>) (a:dah) (q:draft)
kipahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gladness/joy/rejoicing) (d:<kipah>, be glad, with <na>; often paired with <lungdamna>) (s:kipakna/lungdamna/nuamna) (a:dahna) (b:kipah) (q:draft)
kipahtawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exalted/be honored/be lifted high) (d:passive form with <ki> of <pahtawi> honor, exalt) (s:kisangsak/kizahtak/kisangtawi) (a:kisimmawh) (b:pahtawi) (r:19.12.8) (q:draft)
kipahtawina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:glory/honor/being honored) (d:<kipahtawi> be honored, honor oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: the honor one receives or gives oneself, also that by which someone is honored) (s:pahtawina/minthanna) (a:minsiatna) (b:kipahtawi) (q:draft)
kipahtawisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring honour to/cause to be honoured) (d:<kipahtawi> be honoured, with the causative <sak>) (a:neusak) (b:kipahtawi) (q:draft)
kipahtawite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:honored ones/the renowned) (d:<kipahtawi> be honored, with the plural <te>: those who are honored) (b:kipahtawi) (q:draft)
kipai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go/set out) (d:<pai> go with the prefix <ki>, used impersonally or passively: one goes, people set out; {kipai khiatpih}, be carried away) (b:pai) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipaidak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast aside/be left lying) (d:be thrown away and left lying in the open, of an unwanted child or of dead bodies) (s:kipaaidak/kilawnkhia) (b:paidak) (q:draft)
kipaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast away/be rejected) (d:passive of <paih>, throw away; mostly with <khia>, out: {kipaih khiatsak} is be thrown out and {kipaih khiatna} is rejection) (s:kipaimang/kilawnkhia/kinolh) (b:paih) (q:draft)
kipaihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast away/be dropped) (d:passive of <paihkhiat>, throw away; form used before words such as <ciangin>, <ding> and <theih>) (b:paihkhiat) (q:draft)
kipaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dumping place/throwing away) (d:<kipaih> be thrown away with the noun suffix <na>; {nin kipaihna phualpi}, a heap where rubbish is thrown) (b:kipaih) (q:draft)
kipaihpehsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crossing) (d:making the hands cross over each other, with the causative <sak> and the linking ending <in>) (s:pehsakin) (q:draft)
kipaii = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be conceived) (d:passive of <paii> conceive, of a child) (b:paii) (q:draft)
kipaiikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown away/be thrown out) (d:passive with <ki> of <paii> throw, with <khia> out) (s:kilawnkhia) (q:draft)
kipaiina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conception/being conceived) (d:<kipaii> be conceived, with the noun suffix <na>; {kei hong kipaiina naugil}, the womb in which I was conceived) (s:kipaaina/gaina) (b:kipaii) (q:draft)
kipaikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be thrown out/be removed/be driven away) (d:be cast away or put out of its place) (s:kipaaikhia/kilawnkhia) (q:draft)
kipaikhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sent away/be drawn out/be made to go out) (d:passive of <paikhiasak> send away, make go out, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kisawlkhia/kiciahsak) (b:paikhiasak) (q:draft)
kipaikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set out/march out) (d:impersonal <ki> with <paikhiat> go out: when the setting out takes place) (s:kuankhiat) (b:paikhiat) (q:draft)
kipaikhiatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken away/be carried off/be led out) (d:passive of <paikhiatpih>; in the verses mostly of people taken away into exile) (s:kipuakhia/kikai) (b:paikhiatpih) (q:draft)
kipaikhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put outside/be sent out) (d:passive with <ki> of <paikhiatsak> make go out) (s:kisawlkhia) (b:paikhiatsak) (q:draft)
kipaimang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown away/be cast away/be discarded) (d:passive of <paimang> throw away, with the prefix <ki>; also written {kipaai mang}) (s:kipaih/kipaai) (b:paimang) (q:draft)
kipaipih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought/be taken) (d:passive of <paipih>, take along: be brought or led to someone or somewhere) (s:kitunpih/kitut) (b:paipih) (r:40.9.32) (q:draft)
kipaipihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being brought/being taken/being led) (d:<kipaipih>, be brought, with the linking ending <in>: being brought, after which another action follows) (b:kipaipih) (q:draft)
kipaipihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being brought/being taken) (d:<kipaipih>, be brought or taken, with the noun suffix <na>; {salin kipaipihna}, being led away as captives) (b:kipaipih) (q:draft)
kipaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sent/be allowed to go) (d:passive of <paisak>, send or let go) (s:kisawl) (b:paisak) (q:draft)
kipaithang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be strewn/be thrown about/lie scattered) (d:of dead bodies, be thrown down and left lying about) (s:kipaaithang/kithehzak) (q:draft)
kipaithangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being strewn/flung about) (d:<kipaithang> be strewn, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kipaithang) (q:draft)
kipak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rejoice/be glad/be joyful) (d:be glad and show it; very often paired with <lungdam>, as in {lungdamin kipak}, rejoice and be glad) (s:lungdam) (a:dah) (r:19.122.1) (q:draft)
kipakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:gladly/joyfully/rejoicing) (d:<kipak>, rejoice, with the linking ending <in>: gladly, with joy; often paired as {lungdamin kipakin}, and {kipakin diang} is leap for joy) (s:lungdamin/lungdamtakin) (a:dahin) (b:kipak) (q:draft)
kipakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gladness/joy/rejoicing) (d:<kipak>, rejoice, with the noun suffix <na>: gladness; often paired as {lungdamna leh kipakna}, joy and gladness) (s:kipahna/lungdamna/nuamna) (a:dahna) (b:kipak) (q:draft)
kipaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make glad/make rejoice/gladden) (d:<kipak> rejoice, with the causative <sak>) (s:kipaaksak/lungdamsak/nuamsak) (a:dahsak) (b:kipak) (q:draft)
kipakta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be approved/be honoured/be esteemed) (d:be well regarded by others, passive of <pakta>) (s:kizahtak/kisangtawi) (a:kisimmawh) (b:pakta) (q:draft)
kipalsat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/be violated/be transgressed) (d:passive of <palsat>, break a law or an agreement) (b:palsat) (q:draft)
kipan = (i:2) (t:prep) (w:from/since) (d:starting from, placed after a time or place word and <a>) (s:akipan/panin/pan) (a:dong) (r:5.9.24) (q:draft)
kipana = (i:1) (t:v) (w:begin) (d:<kipan> begin with the linking <a>: having begun, and then) (b:kipan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be deployed/be stationed) (d:passive of <pangsak> post: of soldiers, be drawn up against an enemy) (b:pangsak) (q:draft)
kipanin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:from/since) (d:postpositional marker equivalent to the locative preposition, "from") (b:kipan)
kipankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come out from/proceed from/begin) (d:<kipan>, begin, with <khia>, out: start out from a place or source, used with <panin>) (b:kipan) (q:draft)
kipankik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:begin again) (d:<kipan> begin, with <kik> again) (b:kipan) (q:draft)
kipanta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have begun) (d:<kipan> begin, with <ta> marking a change now reached) (b:kipan) (q:draft)
kipanto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:start upward/rise from) (d:<kipan> begin, with <to> upward; of rooms that start from a raised base) (b:kipan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be struck/be beaten against) (d:of a boat hit by breaking waves) (s:kisat) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kipasal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:act like a man/be manly) (d:<pasal>, man, with the prefix <ki>; found only with <sak> in {Kipasal sakin}, showing oneself a man, brace yourself like a man in the NIV; also written as one word <Kipasalsakin>) (r:18.38.3) (q:draft)
kipasalsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brave/act like men/be courageous) (d:<pasal> man with <ki> and <sak>: make oneself a man, show courage) (s:Kihangsak) (q:draft)
kipasalsakin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:courageous) (d:<kipasalsak>, show oneself a man, with the linking suffix <in>: bracing oneself like a man) (b:kipasalsak) convey a negative sense
Kipasalsakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:like a man/manfully/bravely) (d:<kipasalsak>, show oneself a man, with the linking suffix <in>; written with a capital at the start of a sentence, brace yourself like a man in the NIV) (s:hangtakin) (b:kipasalsakin) (r:18.38.3) (q:draft)
kipat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:begin/start/open/first) (d:form of <kipan>, begin, used before words such as <ciangin>, <cil> and <ni>; {a kipat cil-in} is in the beginning, and {ni kipat ni} is the first day of the week) (s:kipan/kisin) (a:tawp)
kipatcil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beginning/first) (d:{a kipatcil-in} is in the beginning, {a kipatcil lai} is at first) (s:kipatna/cilna/patna) (a:tawpna) (q:draft)
kipatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:beginning/when beginning) (d:<kipat> begin with the linking ending {-in}; {uk ding a kipatin} means when he began to reign) (b:kipat) (q:draft)
kipatkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:origin/starting point) (d:<kipatkhiat> start out, with the noun suffix <na>; {kipatkhiatna mun}, the place something comes from) (s:piankhiatna) (q:draft)
kipatma = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:before the beginning/before it begins) (d:<kipat> begin, with <ma> before) (q:draft)
kipatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beginning/start) (d:<kipat>, begin, with the noun suffix <na>: the beginning or source of something; {a kipatna leh a tawpna} is the beginning and the end) (s:patna/cilna/kipatcil) (a:tawpna/beina) (b:kipat) (q:draft)
Kipatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beginning) (d:<kipatna> written with a capital as a title of God, the Beginning, standing for Alpha) (a:Tawpna) (b:kipatna) (q:draft)
kipatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:already begun) (d:<kipat> begin, with <sa> marking what has already happened; {hong kipatsa bangin}, as he had already begun) (b:kipat) (q:draft)
kipatthakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:new beginning/fresh start) (d:<kipat> begin with <thak> new and the noun suffix <na>) (q:draft)
kipattung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beginning/very start) (d:<kipat> begin with <tung> at first; {a kipattung lamin}, at the beginning) (s:kipatna/kipatcil) (q:draft)
kipatun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beginning/start) (d:the start of something, here of speaking; probably the same as <kipattung>) (s:kipattung) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak to one another/be spoken) (d:<pau>, speak, with the prefix <ki>: speak with each other; {kipau thei lo}, that cannot be put into words) (s:kiho) (b:pau) (q:draft)
kipawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consort/keep company with) (d:Keep company with someone and live as one of their kind; the companion is marked by <tawh>, with.) (s:kikhawl)
kipawl = (i:2) (t:v) (w:associate/join/belong to) (d:Be on the side of a person or group, join them or belong to them; used with <tawh>, with, as in {Pasian tawh kipawl}, belong to God.) (s:kikhawl/kikholh)
kipawl = (i:3) (t:v) (w:mix) (d:Mix with other people, go among them and share their company.)
kipawlbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become friends/make friends) (d:{Kipawl}, associate, with <bawl>, make or treat as: become friends with each other; its opposite in the same verse is <kigalbawl>, be enemies.) (a:kigalbawl) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:join/ally with/unite/band together) (d:Form of <kipawl> with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb; the partner is marked by <tawh>, with.) (s:kikhawlin) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:join with/get involved with) (d:{Kipawl}, associate, with <kha>, happen to: get involved with someone; mostly negative, as in {kipawlkha kei in}, do not join with them.) (q:draft)
kipawlkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become allies/form an alliance/unite) (d:{Kipawl}, associate, with <khawm>, together: join together as allies.) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlkhawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:alliance/union) (d:{Kipawlkhawm}, become allies, with the noun suffix <na>: an alliance between two parties.) (s:kipawlna) (b:kipawlkhawm) (q:draft)
kipawlkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be already united/have been joined) (d:<kipawl>, join or associate, with <khin>, already done; used with <tawh>, with) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:alliance/treaty/union/fellowship) (d:A joining together of people or nations, an alliance or fellowship; {kipawlna bawl} means make an alliance, and the partner is marked by <tawh>, with.) (s:kipawlkhawmna/kizopna) (a:kikhenna) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
Kipawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Union) (d:<kipawlna>, union, written with a capital as the name of one of the two staffs of the shepherd in Zechariah) (b:kipawlna) (q:draft)
kipawlnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:joints/joinings/connections) (d:plural of <kipawlna>, a joining; here the places where bones and sinews of the body join) (b:kipawlna) (q:draft)
kipawlpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:associate with/ally with/mix with) (d:<kipawl> associate, with <pih> together with; {a kipawlpih}, those one has joined with) (s:pawlpih) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:allies/friends/associates) (d:<kipawlpih>, be allied with, with plural <te>: those who are joined with someone) (s:lawmte) (a:galte) (b:kipawlpih) (q:draft)
kipawlsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:joined/united) (d:<kipawl>, join, with the completive suffix <sa>: having been joined; {Pasian tawh a kipawlsa mite}, people who have been united with God) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:unite/join) (d:<kipawl>, join, with the causative <sak>: cause to be joined with someone) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who belong to/associates/companions) (d:{Kipawl}, belong to or associate with, with the plural <te>: the people who are joined to someone or something, used with <tawh>, with.) (s:kipawlpihte) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipawlthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to associate/can be united) (d:<kipawl> with <thei>, be able to join or have fellowship with; in the 1977 text {Pasian tawh kipawlthei} renders being justified, put right with God) (s:kikhawlthei) (b:kipawl) (q:draft)
kipden = (i:1) (t:v) (w:endure/remain firm/last for ever) (d:{Kip}, be firm, with <den>, always: stand firm for ever, last without end.) (s:kipsuak) (q:draft)
kipeek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roll about/writhe/thrash) (d:Roll or thrash about on the ground, said of a person in a convulsion; with <sawnsawn>, over and over.) (q:draft)
kipeh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be grafted/be grafted in) (d:passive of <peh>, graft: a branch is joined onto another tree) (b:peh) (q:draft)
kipeh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:bite each other) (d:with {khat leh khat}, one another; said of people who attack each other) (s:kipetkha) (q:draft)
kipehthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be grafted/be grafted) (d:<kipeh>, be grafted, with <thei>, be able) (b:kipeh) (q:draft)
kipei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:whirl/spin/swirl) (d:of a whirlwind, turn round and round; <pei> is wheel) (b:pei) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipeksat = (t:see) <kipeksat-in>
kipeksat-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken) (d:passive of <peksat>, break, with the linking ending <in>; said of a treaty or agreement) (s:kipalsat) (q:draft)
kipeksatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken) (d:passive of <peksat>, break, with the linking ending <in>; said of a treaty or agreement) (s:kipalsat) (b:peksatin) (q:draft)
kipelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:escape/be free from/keep away from/avoid) (d:Stay clear of something bad or get away from it; the thing avoided is marked by <tawh>, as in {lungkhamna tawh kipelh}, be kept from trouble.) (s:suakta) (b:pelh) (q:draft)
kipelhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:escape/be free from/avoid) (d:<kipelh>, be free from, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb; used with <tawh> for the thing escaped) (b:kipelh) (q:draft)
kipelhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be released from/be freed from) (d:<kipelh>, be free from, with <khia>, out; used with <tawh> for the thing one is freed from) (b:kipelh) (q:draft)
kipelhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be averted/be turned back/be revoked) (d:<kipelh>, be kept away, with <kik>, back; said of an evil plan that is to be undone) (b:kipelh) (q:draft)
kipelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:avoiding/escape/turning away) (d:{Kipelh}, keep clear of, with the noun suffix <na>: the avoiding of something or escape from it, used with <tawh>.) (s:pelhna) (b:kipelh) (q:draft)
kipelhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep from/spare from/turn away from/take away) (d:cause to pass by or be kept away from someone, from <kipelh>; with a negative, not let go of a promise) (b:kipelh) (q:draft)
kipelhsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sparing/deliverance) (d:<kipelhsak>, keep from, with the noun suffix <na>: being spared from something, with <tawh>) (b:kipelhsak) (q:draft)
kipelhzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rather be spared/rather keep free from) (d:<kipelh>, be free from, with <zaw>, more or rather; used with <tawh>) (b:kipelh) (q:draft)
kipengsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exempted/be made free from) (d:passive of <pengsak>: be released from a duty or a tax) (b:pengsak) (q:draft)
kipetkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bite each other) (d:<ki>, each other, with <pet>, bite, and <kha>, happen to) (s:kipeh) (q:draft)
kiphah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spread/be laid out) (d:be spread or laid flat, as a bed, paving stones or a body on the ground) (b:phah) (q:draft)
kiphal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be allowed/be permitted) (d:Passive of <phal>, allow: be allowed or permitted; with <lo>, not be allowed.) (a:kikham) (b:phal) (q:draft)
kiphamat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow one upon another/overtake one another) (d:in {a ciah leh a kuan kiphamat}, those leaving and those setting out catch up with each other: said of people or messengers coming and going without a break) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphamawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be necessary/be obliged) (d:from <phamawh>, necessary; with {hi lo}, there is no obligation to do something) (s:kisam) (b:phamawh) (q:draft)
kiphamawhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those addicted/those dependent on) (d:people who cannot do without something; {zunek kiphamawhte}, those addicted to drinking wine) (b:kiphamawh) (q:draft)
kiphan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be woven/be embroidered) (d:of cloth, be woven or worked with a pattern) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be proud/be arrogant/boast) (d:Think highly of oneself, be proud or boastful; {a kiphasak mite} are the proud.) (s:kisathei/kihisak/kiliansak/kiphatsak) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (r:19.75.4) (q:draft)
kiphasakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be proud/boast/exalt oneself) (d:<kiphasak> with the linking suffix {-in}, being proud and then doing the next action; also proudly) (b:kiphasak) (q:draft)
kiphasaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pride/boastings) (d:<kiphasak>, be proud, with the noun suffix <na> and the plural <te>) (s:kiphatsaknate) (b:kiphasak) (q:draft)
Kiphasakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:proud man/vain man/foolish person) (d:<kiphasak> be proud or boast, with <pa> marking a man; used in address) (q:draft)
kiphasakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant) (d:<kiphasak> with plural <te>, those who are proud; often {mi kiphasakte}) (s:kihisakte/kisatheite/kiliansakte) (a:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kiphasak) (q:draft)
kiphasakteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the arrogant/all the proud) (d:<kiphasak>, be proud, with <teng>, all: after <mi>, all the people who are proud) (b:kiphasak) (q:draft)
kiphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be praised/be commended) (d:Passive of <phat>, praise: be praised or commended.) (s:kipahtawi) (a:kisamsia) (b:phat) (q:draft)
kiphat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:commend oneself/praise oneself) (d:Reflexive of <phat>, praise: praise or commend oneself, often with <amahmah>, himself, or {amah leh amah}.) (s:kiphattawm) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:phat) (q:draft)
kiphatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being praised/praised) (d:<kiphat> be praised, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiphat) (q:draft)
kiphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:praise/commendation) (d:praise that someone receives; {kiphatna lai} is a letter of recommendation) (s:phatna/minphatna) (b:phatna) (q:draft)
kiphatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:praises) (d:<kiphatna> praise, with the plural <te>) (s:phatnate) (b:kiphatna) (q:draft)
kiphatphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be praised again and again/be praised continually) (d:passive of <phatphat> keep praising) (b:phatphat) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/be arrogant) (d:praise oneself; before <pau> or <gamtat> it means speak or behave proudly) (s:kiphasak/kisathei/kihisak/kisialh) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:kiphat) (r:19.17.10) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cause to be praised) (d:{ki-} form of <phatsak>, let someone or something be praised) (b:phatsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boasting) (d:{Kiphatsak}, be proud, with the noun suffix <na>: a high opinion of oneself, pride or boasting.) (s:kisaktheihna/kihihsakna/kiliatsakna/kisialhna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (q:draft)
kiphatsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boastings) (d:{Kiphatsakna}, pride, with the plural <te>: acts or kinds of pride.) (s:kiphasaknate) (b:kiphatsakna) (r:23.23.9) (q:draft)
kiphatsakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take pride in/boast of) (d:<kiphatsak> with <pih>: be proud on account of something; before a noun or standing alone, the thing one is proud of, the pride) (s:kisaktheihpih) (b:kiphatsak) (q:draft)
kiphattawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:commend oneself/praise oneself/boast) (d:{Kiphat}, praise oneself, with <tawm>, by oneself: praise or commend oneself.) (s:kiphat) (q:draft)
kiphatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who commend themselves) (d:<kiphat>, praise oneself, with the plural <te>) (b:kiphat) (q:draft)
kiphawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be remembered/be missed) (d:Passive of <phawk>, remember: be remembered or be missed; with {nawn lo}, be forgotten.) (a:kimangngilh) (b:phawk) (q:draft)
kiphawkin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be remembered/be realised) (d:<kiphawk>, be remembered or noticed, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:kiphawk) (q:draft)
kiphawkkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be remembered/come to mind) (d:Passive of <phawkkha>, call to mind: be remembered or come to mind; mostly with {nawn lo}, be remembered no more.) (a:kimangngilh) (b:phawkkha) (q:draft)
kiphawkkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be found/be discovered) (d:passive of <phawkkhia>, find out: come to light, here of something found written in a book) (s:kimukhia) (b:phawkkhia) (q:draft)
kiphawkmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overlook/pretend not to notice/hold back) (d:with <bawl>, do: act as if one had not noticed a wrong, let it pass) (s:kimuhmawh) (q:draft)
kiphawkna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:memory/remembrance) (d:the fact of being remembered; with <bei> or <beisak>, the memory of someone is wiped out) (s:phawkna) (b:kiphawk) (q:draft)
kiphawkphawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be long remembered/be remembered continually) (d:Passive of <phawkphawk>, keep remembering: be remembered for a long time.) (a:kimangngilh) (b:phawkphawk) (q:draft)
kiphawksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to be remembered/keep in memory/be remembered) (d:<kiphawk> be remembered with <sak> causative) (b:kiphawk) (q:draft)
kiphawktel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:realise/perceive/know clearly) (d:<phawktel>, realise, with the prefix <ki>) (s:phawktel) (b:phawktel) (q:draft)
kipheek = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:braided/plaited) (d:said of hair, with <sam>) (q:draft)
kiphel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be loosed/be untied/be taken down) (d:Passive of <phel>, undo: be untied or loosed, or of a tent, an altar or a building be taken down.) (a:kihen) (b:phel) (q:draft)
kiphel = (i:2) (t:v) (w:split apart/split open) (d:Written before <kham> in {kiphel kham}, split open, said of the ground; the joined spelling is <kiphelkham>.) (s:kiphelkham) (b:phel) (q:draft)
kiphel = (i:3) (t:v) (w:defend oneself/clear oneself) (d:speak to free oneself from a charge or to prove innocence) (s:kihut/kisut) (b:phel) (q:draft)
kiphelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be quenched/be put out) (d:passive of <phelh> quench, of a fire) (s:kisumit/kimitsak/kisukmit) (a:kitawh) (b:phelh) (q:draft)
kiphelh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:clear oneself/defend oneself) (d:form of <kiphel> used before <nading>: {mawhna kiphelh nading}, to clear oneself of a charge) (b:kiphel) (q:draft)
kiphelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defence) (d:<kiphelh>, clear oneself, with the noun suffix <na>; {mawhna kiphelhna}, clearing oneself of a charge) (s:kiphelna) (b:kiphelh) (q:draft)
kiphelhzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be quenched/can be put out) (d:<kiphelh>, be quenched, with <zo>, be able; with <kei>, unquenchable) (b:kiphelh) (q:draft)
kiphelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:splitting apart/being split) (d:<kiphel> split apart, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiphel) (q:draft)
kiphelkeek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be demolished/be torn down) (d:passive of <phelkeek>, tear down; said of altars) (s:kiphelkek/kiphelkhia) (a:kilam) (b:phelkeek) (q:draft)
kiphelkek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be demolished/be torn down) (d:passive of <phelkek> tear down, of altars and buildings) (s:kiphelkeek/kiphelkhia) (a:kilam) (b:phelkek) (q:draft)
kiphelkekmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be torn down completely) (d:passive of <phelkek>, tear down, with <mang>, away or gone) (q:draft)
kiphelkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be split apart/split open) (d:passive of <phelkham>, split open; said of the ground or the earth) (s:khangkham) (b:phelkham) (q:draft)
kiphelkhamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be divided/be split apart) (d:<kiphelkham> with the linking <in>, being split or divided up) (s:kikhenthang) (b:kiphelkham) (r:11.13.5) (q:draft)
kiphelkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be torn down/come loose) (d:be taken apart or broken off, of stones of a building or of chains) (s:kiphelkek) (b:phelkhia) (q:draft)
kiphellah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defend oneself/clear oneself) (d:apparently <kiphel>, defend oneself against a charge, with <lah>; the verse says there will be nothing to answer for when one is accused) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defense/clearing of oneself) (d:answering an accusation, usually {mawh kiphelna}) (s:kiphelhna) (b:kiphel) (q:draft)
kiphelphel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep defending oneself/defend oneself) (d:<kiphel>, defend oneself, doubled for a repeated action; used with <mawhna>) (q:draft)
kiphelsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:open/opened) (d:<kiphel>, be untied or loosed, with the completive suffix <sa>; said of a scroll that lies open) (b:kiphel) (q:draft)
kiphelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be torn down/be broken down) (d:said of an altar; from <kiphel>, be taken down, with <sak>) (b:kiphel) (q:draft)
kiphen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be opened) (d:passive of <phen>, open; said of a book or scroll) (s:kihon) (b:phen) (q:draft)
kiphenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be open/lie open) (d:<kiphen>, be opened, with the linking ending <in>; said of a book or scroll) (b:kiphen) (q:draft)
kiphiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be swept) (d:be swept clean, said of a house) (b:phiat) (q:draft)
kiphiat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be annulled/be wiped out/be blotted out) (d:be done away with, said of an agreement or of people) (s:kiphiatkhia/kibeisak) (b:phiat) (q:draft)
kiphiatkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be wiped out/be blotted out/be swept away) (d:Passive of <phiatkhia>, wipe out: be wiped out, blotted out or swept away.) (s:kiphiat) (b:phiatkhia) (q:draft)
kiphiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blotted out/be wiped out) (d:<kiphiat> be wiped out with <sak>: let them be wiped out, here of names in a book) (b:kiphiat) (q:draft)
kiphin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:provoke each other) (d:<ki>, each other, with <phin>, provoke) (b:phin) (q:draft)
kiphitsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hissed at/be scorned/be scoffed at) (d:passive of <phitsan>, hiss or scoff at; {simmawhna tawh a kiphitsan}, an object of scorn) (s:kinuihsan/kisimmawh) (b:phitsan) (q:draft)
kipho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spread out/be exposed/be laid bare) (d:passive of <pho> spread out: be laid out in the open where all can see) (s:kipholak) (b:pho) (q:draft)
kiphokhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exposed/be spread out) (d:<kipho>, be spread out, with <khia>, out: be laid out in the open) (s:kipholak) (b:kipho) (q:draft)
kipholaak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disclosed/be revealed/be made known) (d:said of a secret that is brought into the open) (s:kipholak/kilang) (a:kiseel) (q:draft)
kipholak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exposed/be revealed/be uncovered) (d:passive of <pholak>, expose: be laid open for all to see, of sin, shame or a secret; {amah leh amah a kipholak} is expose oneself) (s:kipholaak/kilang/kilangkhia) (a:kiseel/kiseelcip) (b:pholak) (q:draft)
kiphong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be awakened/be woken) (d:passive of <phong>, wake: be woken from sleep) (b:phong) (q:draft)
kiphop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be patched/be mended) (d:passive of <phop> mend; {a kiphop khedap}, a patched sandal) (b:phop) (q:draft)
kiphopte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:patched/mended) (d:<kiphop> be patched, with the plural <te>: the patched ones, here of wineskins) (b:kiphop) (q:draft)
kiphu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collide/run into each other/stumble against) (d:<ki> each other with <phu> push against: knock against one another) (s:kiphukha) (b:phu) (q:draft)
kiphu = (i:2) (t:v) (w:head into/face) (d:with <huih> wind: of a ship, hold its way against the wind) (b:phu) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be named/be given a name) (d:passive of <phuah>, give a name; used with <min>, name) (s:kiphuak) (b:phuah) (q:draft)
kiphuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:naming/being named) (d:<kiphuah>, be named, with the noun suffix <na>; {hong kiphuahna min}, the name by which you are called) (b:kiphuah) (q:draft)
kiphuai = (t:see) <kiphuai-in>
kiphuai-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear at each other/devour each other) (d:said of wild animals attacking one another, with the linking ending <in>; the verse pairs it with <kipetkha>, bite each other, and it is not clear which of the two is bite and which is devour) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be named/be called) (d:passive of <phuak>, give a name: be given a name, usually after <min>, name) (s:kiphuah/kici) (b:phuak) (q:draft)
kiphuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who is named/the man called) (d:<kiphuak> be named, with <pa> for a man: the man to whom a name was given) (b:kiphuak) (r:27.4.8) (q:draft)
kiphuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid/be founded/be set) (d:of a foundation, be laid; of a pillar, be set on its base) (s:kiphut) (b:phuh) (q:draft)
kiphuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:settling/resting) (d:<kiphuh> be set down, with the noun suffix <na>; {a kiphuhna mun}, the place where a thing comes to rest, here of the cloud) (b:kiphuh) (q:draft)
kiphuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut down/be felled) (d:passive of <phuk>, fell: of a tree or a wooden idol, be cut down; {kiphuk tan} is be cut right off) (s:kiphukmang/kiphukpai) (a:kisuan) (b:phuk) (q:draft)
kiphukha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:jostle one another/collide/stumble over one another) (d:<phukha> knock against, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (s:kiphu) (b:phukha) (q:draft)
kiphukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being cut down/cut down and) (d:<kiphuk> be cut down, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiphuk) (q:draft)
kiphukmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut down/be felled) (d:passive of <phukmang>: of trees, be cut down and cleared away) (s:kiphuk/kiphukpai) (b:phukmang) (q:draft)
kiphukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:felling/cutting down) (d:<kiphuk>, be cut down, with the noun suffix <na>; said of trees) (b:kiphuk) (q:draft)
kiphukpai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut down/be felled/be cast down) (d:passive of <phukpai> cut down) (s:kiphuk/kiphukmang) (b:phukpai) (q:draft)
kiphuksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cut down/felled) (d:<kiphuk>, be cut down, with the completive suffix <sa>; said of a tree) (b:kiphuk) (q:draft)
kiphulet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken through/be breached) (d:passive of <phulet>; said of a city wall) (s:kiphutlet) (b:phulet) (q:draft)
kiphum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:passive of <phum>, immerse: be baptized, often with <tui>, water; baptism is <kiphumna>) (s:kibaptaiz/kituiphum) (b:phum) (r:42.12.50) (q:draft)
kiphum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be buried) (d:passive of <phum>, bury: of a dead person, be laid in a grave) (s:kivui/kivuk) (b:phum) (q:draft)
kiphumcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be buried/be hidden/be overwhelmed) (d:passive of <phumcip> bury, submerge, with the prefix <ki>: be covered over completely and so hidden; of a person in sorrow, be swallowed up by it) (s:kivukcip/kiseelcip) (b:phumcip) (q:draft)
kiphumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:<kiphum>, be baptized, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiphum) (q:draft)
kiphumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:burial/grave) (d:being buried; {kiphumna mun} and {kiphumna hankhuk} are the place where someone is buried) (s:kivuina) (b:kiphum) (q:draft)
kiphumna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:plunging in/meddling) (d:throwing oneself into something, such as a quarrel of other people) (b:kiphum) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphumpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be baptized at once) (d:<kiphum>, be baptized, with <pah>, immediately; used with <tui>, water) (q:draft)
kiphumzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to be baptized) (d:<kiphum>, be baptized, with <zo>, be able) (b:kiphum) (q:draft)
kiphunsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grumble against each other/complain against each other) (d:<phunsan>, grumble against, with the prefix <ki>, each other) (b:phunsan) (q:draft)
kiphunsanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:<kiphunsan> grumble against each other, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:phunsanna/phunna) (b:kiphunsan) (r:47.12.20) (q:draft)
kiphupai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stumble over each other/fall over each other) (d:<ki> each other with <phu> push against and <pai> go: run into one another while fleeing) (s:kiphukha/kiphu) (q:draft)
kiphusak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:smash together/dash against each other) (d:<kiphu> collide with the causative <sak>: make people strike against one another) (b:kiphu) (q:draft)
kiphut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set up/be established/be founded) (d:passive of <phut>, set up: of a foundation, be laid; of a throne, be established; of a post, be set firmly in place) (s:kiphuh) (b:phut) (q:draft)
kiphutin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being set up/set firmly) (d:<kiphut> be set up, be established, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiphut) (q:draft)
kiphutkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid again/be set up again) (d:<kiphut>, be set up or founded, with <kik>, again; said of the foundation of the temple) (b:kiphut) (q:draft)
kiphutlet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken through/be breached) (d:said of a city wall; the other Bible text has <kiphulet> in the same verse) (s:kiphulet) (q:draft)
kiphutte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:settings) (d:<kiphut> be set in place, with the plural <te>: the gold settings in which stones are set) (b:kiphut) (q:draft)
kiphuzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to head into) (d:<kiphu>, head into, with <zo>, be able; {huih kiphuzo nawn lo}, no longer able to sail against the wind) (b:kiphu) (q:draft)
kipi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marry/take a wife) (d:take a husband or wife; paired with <kiteeng> or <kiteengsak> for marrying and being given in marriage; {a kipi mo} is a bride being wed) (s:zinei) (q:draft)
kipia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:given/be given/be allotted) (d:passive of <pia>, give: be given, handed over or allotted to someone) (a:kilakhia) (b:pia) (r:1.9.2)
Kipia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:given/dedicated) (d:capitalised in an inscription: {Topa-a’ dingin A Kipia}, given over to the Lord, NIV Holy to the Lord) (b:kipia) (q:draft)
kipiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be given/be handed/be presented) (d:form of <kipia> used before endings such as <ciangin>, <leh> and <ding>) (b:kipia) (r:42.4.17) (q:draft)
kipiakhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be offered together/be given along with) (d:passive of <piakhawm>, give together; said of an offering that goes with another) (b:piakhawm) (q:draft)
kipiakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be given/be given back/be returned) (d:passive of <piakhia>; of property returned to its owner in the jubilee year) (s:kipiakik) (b:piakhia) (q:draft)
kipiakhiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things given/things devoted) (d:<kipiakhia>, be given, with the plural <te>: the things that are given over, here to God) (b:kipiakhia) (q:draft)
kipiakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be given back/be returned/be restored) (d:passive of <piakik> give back, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kipiakhia) (b:piakik) (q:draft)
kipiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gave/giving/self-giving) (d:<kipiak>, be given, with the noun suffix <na>: the giving of an offering or of oneself) (b:kipia)
kipiakna = (i:2) (t:part) (d:particle conveying the meaning "give, given" used in combination with verb)
kipiaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things given/gifts/what was given) (d:<kipiak>, be given, with the noun suffix <na> and plural <te>: gifts offered to God, or with <thu>, the commands given to someone) (b:kipiak) (q:draft)
kipiaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:given/commanded) (d:<kipiak>, be given, with the completive suffix <sa>; {thu a kipiaksa bangin}, as was commanded) (b:kipiak) (q:draft)
kipiaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be given a share/be provided for) (d:<kipiak>, be given, with <sak>; with <lo>, be left out when things are given out) (b:kipiak) (q:draft)
kipiakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:offerings/things given) (d:<kipiak>, be given, with the plural <te>: the things that are given to someone) (b:kipiak) (q:draft)
kipiakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of being given/how something is given) (d:<kipiak>, be given, with <zia>, manner; {gimna a kipiakzia}, how punishment is dealt out) (b:piakzia) (q:draft)
kipialsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be led astray/be turned aside) (d:<pialsak> lead astray with <ki>: {lam kipialsak}, let oneself be turned off the way) (b:pialsak) (q:draft)
kipian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be created/be made) (d:found in {kipian'sak}, be created: <pian>, come into being, with the prefix <ki> and causative <sak>) (b:pian) (q:draft)
kipiangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:create/be created/be made) (d:passive of <piangsak>, create: be brought into being, be made) (s:kibawl) (b:piangsak)
kipiangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:institute/bring about) (d:<kipiangsak>, cause to come into being, with the linking ending <in>; here of the Passover being held for the first time) (b:kipiangsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipiangsaksa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:created thing/creature) (d:<kipiangsak>, be created, with the completive suffix <sa>: what has been created) (b:kipiangsak) (q:draft)
kipiansak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:generation) (b:piansak)
kipiansakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:created) (d:<kipiansak>, be created, with the linking ending <in>: when they were created) (b:kipiansak)
kipiansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creation) (d:<kipiansak>, be created, with the noun suffix <na>: the creating of someone, also the thing from which or the purpose for which one was made) (b:kipiansak)
kipiasa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:given/already given) (d:<kipia> with {-sa} for a completed action; what has been given, often before a noun) (b:kipia) (q:draft)
kipiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make give/impose/let give) (d:have something given: of tribute, impose it on a land; with <lo>, not be allowed to give) (b:kipia) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipiasawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be handed on/be passed on) (d:passive of <piasawn>, pass on; of the law, given on through a go-between) (b:piasawn) (q:draft)
kipiatawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give oneself/give oneself up/sell oneself) (d:hand oneself over for a purpose or for others; also bring a thing on oneself) (s:kipumpiak) (r:11.21.25) (q:draft)
kipiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those given/things given) (d:people or things that are given, handed over or allotted to someone) (b:kipia) (q:draft)
kipiathuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be given more/be added/be given in addition) (d:passive of <piathuah> give in addition, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kibehlap) (b:piathuah) (q:draft)
kipiazah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:amount given/number given) (d:<kipia>, be given, with <zah>, amount: as many as are given or offered) (q:draft)
kipiazaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be given rather/be given more) (d:passive of <piazaw> give rather or more, with the prefix <ki>; {kipiazaw kan ding} is will be given all the more) (b:piazaw) (q:draft)
kipiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have been given/be given) (d:<kipia>, be given, with <zo> marking the action as completed) (b:kipia) (q:draft)
kipilsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be conceited/think oneself wise) (d:<pil>, wise, with <ki> and <sak>: make oneself out to be wise, be wise in one's own eyes) (s:kiphasak) (a:kiniamsak) (b:pilsak) (q:draft)
kipin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:firmly/steadfastly) (d:<kip> with the ending {-in}: standing firm, being established, before the next verb) (s:kiptakin) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kipina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:marrying/marriage) (d:<kipi>, marry, with the noun suffix <na>; paired with {kiteen'na} for marrying and being given in marriage) (b:kipi) (q:draft)
kipkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stand firm/be firmly established) (d:<kip>, be firm, with <khin>, already done) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kipna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:firmness/steadfastness/stability) (d:being firm and lasting; {lung kipna} or {lungsim kipna} is firmness of heart; also what builds a person up) (s:lungkipna) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kipoisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be injured/be hurt) (d:passive of <poisak> injure) (b:poisak) (q:draft)
kipsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:established/made firm) (d:<kip> be established with <sa>, already: standing firm from before) (s:kipsaksa) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:establish/make firm/confirm) (d:<kip>, be firm, with the causative <sak>: make firm, set up to last) (s:phut) (a:susia) (b:kip) (r:24.33.2)
kipsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:establish/strengthen/confirm) (d:<kipsak> with the linking ending <in>: making firm, establishing and) (b:kipsak) (q:draft)
kipsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:strengthening/establishing/confirmation) (d:the act of making someone or something firm) (s:thahatsakna) (b:kipsak) (q:draft)
kipsakna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:ordination/consecration) (d:the setting apart of priests for their office, as in {kipsakna tuutal}, the ram of ordination) (b:kipsak) (q:draft)
kipsaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:supports/stays) (d:<kipsakna> with plural <te>: the parts that hold something firm, as the supports of a stand) (b:kipsakna) (q:draft)
kipsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:establisher/one who makes firm) (d:<kipsak> establish, with <pa> for a male person: he who sets a thing firm, said of God) (b:kipsak) (r:23.45.18) (q:draft)
kipsaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:established/appointed) (d:<kipsak> with <sa>, already done: that has been established) (s:kipsa) (b:kipsak) (q:draft)
kipsaksuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:establish for ever/establish permanently) (d:<kipsak>, establish, with <suak>, right on without end) (q:draft)
kipsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:endure/remain/last forever) (d:stay firm and continue without end) (s:omsuak) (a:beimang) (q:draft)
kiptak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:firm/secure/steadfast) (d:<kip>, firm, with <tak>, truly: really firm, genuine; also used as an adverb, firmly) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kiptaka = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:securely/firmly/at rest) (d:<kiptak>, firm or secure, with the ending <a>) (s:kiptakin) (b:kiptak) (q:draft)
kiptakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:firmly/steadfastly) (d:<kip> with <takin>, which makes an adverb: in a firm, unshaken way) (s:kipin) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kipte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:firm/established/fixed) (d:plural of <kip>; {ngeina kipte}, the established customs, renders decrees, statutes and laws) (b:kip) (r:19.119.138) (q:draft)
kipte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who stand firm) (b:kip) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiptheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to remain/be maintained) (d:<kip>, be established, with <theih>, the form of <thei>, be able, used before <nading>) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kipua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried/be borne) (d:passive of <pua> carry; {kipua khia} is to be carried away) (b:pua) (q:draft)
kipuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be polished/be put in order/be made ready) (d:passive of <puah>: be repaired, tidied or prepared for use) (s:kipuahsiang) (b:puah) (r:42.11.25) (q:draft)
kipuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:adorning oneself/beautifying oneself) (d:<kipuah> put in order, here of women making themselves beautiful, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kipuah) (q:draft)
kipuahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be restored/be repaired again) (d:passive of <puahkik> renovate; of the sanctuary, where the NIV has be reconsecrated) (b:puahkik) (q:draft)
kipuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cosmetics/beauty treatment/adornment) (d:<kipuah>, make oneself ready, with the noun suffix <na>: something used to prepare and beautify the body, such as cosmetics) (s:kizepna) (b:kipuah) (q:draft)
kipuahpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reform/mend one's ways/put right) (d:<puahpha>, repair well, with <ki>, oneself: put one's own conduct right, mend one's ways) (s:kibawlpha) (b:puahpha) (q:draft)
kipuahphasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let oneself be transformed/be made new) (d:<kipuahpha>, put oneself right, with the causative <sak>: let another, here God, put one right) (b:kipuahpha) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipuahphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make amends for/make good/pay for) (d:form of <kipuahpha>, put oneself right, used before <leh> and <ding>; with <mawhna> sin, make amends for it) (b:kipuahpha) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipuahsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be polished/be made clean) (d:passive of <puahsiang>; said of a sword made ready for use) (s:kipuah) (b:puahsiang) (q:draft)
kipuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried/be borne) (d:passive of <puak>, carry: be carried from one place to another) (s:kipua) (b:puak) (q:draft)
kipuak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be sent/be brought/be delivered) (d:passive of <puak>, send or deliver: of a gift, a message or goods, be sent or brought to someone) (s:kisawl/kipaipih) (b:puak) (r:12.17.33) (q:draft)
kipuakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried away/be taken out/be carried off) (d:passive of <puakhia>, carry out: be carried or taken out of a place, often of people and goods taken away to another land) (s:kipuakkhia/kipaikhiatpih) (a:kipuakik) (b:puakhia) (q:draft)
kipuakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried back/be brought back) (d:passive of <puakik>, carry back) (s:kitutkik) (a:kipuakhia) (b:puakik) (q:draft)
kipuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being sent/sent) (d:<kipuak> be sent, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kipuak) (q:draft)
kipuakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried away/be deported/be sent into exile) (d:passive of <puakkhia> carry away) (s:kipuakhia) (a:kipuakik) (b:puakkhia) (q:draft)
kipuakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried away/be taken away/be deported) (d:form of <kipuakkhia> used before endings such as <dong> and <nawn>) (b:kipuakkhia) (q:draft)
kipuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being carried off/deportation) (d:<kipuak> be carried or sent, with the noun suffix <na>; {a kipuakna gam}, the land to which people were carried away as captives) (s:puakkhiatna) (b:kipuak) (q:draft)
kipuasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to carry/be loaded) (d:passive of <puasak> make carry) (b:puasak) (q:draft)
kipuaseh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut off/be excluded/be banned) (d:be put outside and shut out from a place or a people; in the Psalms of the wicked being cut off) (s:kihawlkhia/kikhenkhia) (q:draft)
kipuasehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being cut off/being shut out/banished) (d:<kipuaseh> be shut out, with the linking ending <in>; {a kipuasehin koih}, leave someone in banishment) (b:kipuaseh) (q:draft)
kipuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall/stumble/fall away) (d:fall or stumble; also fall away from faith or come to ruin; built on <puk>, fall) (s:kia/tuk) (a:tho) (b:puk) (q:draft)
kipukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:falling/stumbling) (d:<kipuk> fall, stumble, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kipuk) (q:draft)
kipukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stumbling block/cause of stumbling) (d:<kipuk> stumble with the noun suffix <na>: a thing that makes people fall) (s:puktheihna) (b:kipuk) (q:draft)
kipuksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fallen) (d:<kipuk>, fall, with the completive suffix <sa>) (s:cimsa/kicimsa) (b:kipuk) (q:draft)
kipuksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be dashed to the ground) (d:passive of <puksak>, cause to fall; used with <leitungah>, to the ground) (b:puksak) (q:draft)
kipuksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall on/throw oneself down) (d:<puksuk> fall down with <ki> oneself; with <sak>, let oneself fall on something) (b:puksuk) (q:draft)
kipulaakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:confess to each other) (d:<ki>, each other, with <pulaak>, confess, and the linking ending <in>; <kipulakin> in the other Bible text) (s:kipulakin) (q:draft)
kipulak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be proclaimed/be made known/be confessed/make oneself known) (d:passive or reflexive of <pulak>, declare: be proclaimed or confessed openly; of a person, make oneself known) (s:kitaangko/kitangko) (b:pulak) (q:draft)
kipulakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:confess to each other) (d:<ki>, each other, with <pulak>, confess, and the linking ending <in>) (s:kipulaakin) (b:kipulak) (q:draft)
kipum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be united/be one whole) (d:in {kipum khat}, being as one, in unity) (s:kikhat) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipumpei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reel/shake/tremble) (d:of the earth, shake and rock; perhaps <pum> whole with <pei> turn) (s:kiliing/kiling) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipumpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give oneself/give oneself wholly) (d:give one's whole self for others) (s:kipiatawm/kibuppiak) (q:draft)
kipumsil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bathe/wash the whole body) (d:<pum>, the whole body, with <sil>, wash, and <ki>, oneself: wash one's whole body, bathe) (s:kisil) (q:draft)
kipung = (i:1) (t:v) (w:increase/multiply/be fruitful) (d:<pung> increase with <ki>; {kipung thei lo}, nothing can thrive or bear young, said of a barren land) (b:pung) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipusuahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be taken outside/be put out) (d:passive of <pusuahpih>, bring out) (b:pusuahpih) (q:draft)
kipusuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come out/come forth) (d:<pusuak>, come out, with the prefix <ki>; followed by <sak>, cause to come forth, rouse) (b:pusuak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipusuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought out/be roused) (d:<kipusuak>, come forth, with the causative <sak>: be made to come forth; said of the dead being roused) (s:kithawhthawi) (b:kipusuak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more lasting/firmer/more steadfast) (d:<kip> firm, lasting, with <zaw> more; of a friend, closer) (b:kip) (q:draft)
kipzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to stand/stand firm/endure) (d:<kip> stand firm with <zo> be able; {kipzo lo}, cannot stand) (b:kip) (q:draft)
Kir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kir) (d:land to which the king of Assyria deported the people of Damascus, the earlier home of the Arameans) (r:23.22.6) (q:draft)
Kir = (i:2) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kir) (d:city of Moab, destroyed in a night in the prophecy of Isaiah, probably the same as Kir Hareseth) (q:draft)
Kirhareseth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kir Hareseth) (d:fortified chief city of Moab, the only one left standing when Israel invaded Moab in the time of Elisha) (r:23.16.11/23.16.7)
Kirheres = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kir Hareseth) (d:shorter form of the name Kir Hareseth, the fortified city of Moab, used in Jeremiah) (r:24.48.31/24.48.36)
Kiriath = (t:see) <Kiriath-jearim>
Kiriath-huzoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriath Huzoth) (d:town in Moab to which Balak took Balaam) (q:draft)
Kiriath-jearim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriath Jearim) (d:town on the border of Judah and Benjamin, also called Kiriath Baal, where the ark of the covenant stayed for twenty years) (r:6.15.60) (q:draft)
Kiriath-sannath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriath Sannah) (d:another name of Debir, a town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.49) (q:draft)
Kiriath-sefer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriath Sepher) (d:earlier name of Debir, a town in the hill country of Judah captured by Othniel) (r:6.15.16) (q:draft)
Kiriathaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriathaim) (d:town east of the Jordan rebuilt by the tribe of Reuben and later held by Moab; also a Levite town in Naphtali) (r:24.48.23) (q:draft)
Kiriatharba = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kiriath-arba/Kiriath Arba) (d:old name of Hebron, a city in the hill country of Judah) (r:1.23.2/1.35.27)
Kiriathbaal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kiriath-baal/Kiriath Baal) (d:another name of Kiriath Jearim, a town of the tribe of Judah) (r:6.15.60/6.18.14)
Kiriathhuzoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriath Huzoth) (d:town in Moab to which Balak took Balaam) (r:4.22.39)
Kiriathjearim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kiriath-jearim/Kiriath Jearim) (d:town on the border of Judah and Benjamin, also called Kiriath Baal, where the ark of the covenant stayed for twenty years) (r:6.15.60/6.18.15)
Kiriathsannah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kiriath-sannah/Kiriath Sannah) (d:another name of Debir, a town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.49)
Kiriathsefer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriath Sepher) (d:earlier name of Debir, a town in the hill country of Judah captured by Othniel) (r:7.1.11/6.15.16)
kisa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consider oneself/think oneself) (d:placed after a describing word, as in {pil kisa}, think oneself wise, and {thuman kisa}, think oneself right) (s:kingaihsun/kinei) (q:draft)
kisa = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be sung) (d:of a song, as in {la kisa}) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisaal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pressed out/be cleansed) (d:said of a wound, with <nai>, pus: have the pus pressed out; written <kisal> in the other Bible text) (s:kisal) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisaan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cast) (d:passive of <saan>, cast; used with <ai>, lot) (b:saan) (q:draft)
kisai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:concern/relate to/be about) (d:be connected with; the phrase {tawh kisai} or {tawh kisai-in} means concerning, about) (q:draft)
kisaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:matters concerning/things relating to) (d:<kisai>, concern, with plural <te>; {tawh kisaite}, the things that concern or have to do with) (b:kisai) (q:draft)
kisaizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:depend rather on/relate rather to) (d:<kisai> concern with <zaw> more, rather: {tawh kisaizaw}, has to do with this and not with that) (b:kisai) (q:draft)
kisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be about to/intend/get ready) (d:after a verb with <ding>: be on the point of doing something, mean or prepare to do it; {kisak lai takin} is just as one was about to) (s:kithawi) (r:66.10.4) (q:draft)
kisak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:consider oneself/think oneself/claim) (d:form of <kisa> used before words such as <hangin> and <ciangin>; {thei a kisak} is to think that one knows; {kisak theihna} is pride and {kisak theihpih} is to boast of or take pride in something) (s:kingaihsun/kinei) (b:kisa) (r:23.60.15) (q:draft)
kisak = (i:3) (t:v) (w:be sung) (d:said of a song, <la>) (b:kisa) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:claim/conviction/considering oneself) (d:<kisak> consider oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: what one holds oneself or a thing to be; {thuman kisakna} is the claim to be in the right) (b:kisak) (q:draft)
kisaktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/take pride) (d:think highly of oneself; form used before endings such as <loh> and <nading>) (s:kiphasak/kisathei/kihisak/kiliansak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (q:draft)
kisaktheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pride/boasting/conceit) (d:thinking too highly of oneself and showing it) (s:kiphatsakna/kihihsakna/kiliatsakna/kisialhna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (b:kisaktheih) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast of/be proud of/take pride in) (d:be proud on account of something, such as wealth or strength) (s:kisialhpih/kiphatsakpih/kihihsakpih/angtanpih) (b:kisaktheih) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast of/be proud of) (d:<kisaktheihpih>, take pride in, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kisaktheihpih) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pride/boast/thing boasted of) (d:<kisaktheihpih> take pride in, with the noun suffix <na>: what one is proud of) (b:kisaktheihpih) (q:draft)
kisal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pressed out/be cleansed) (d:said of a wound, with <nai>, pus: have the pus pressed out; written <kisaal> in the other Bible text) (s:kisaal) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisam = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be invited/be called/be summoned) (d:passive of <sam>, call) (s:kilo) (b:sam) (q:draft)
kisamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:call to each other/be called) (d:<kisam>, call or be called, with the linking ending <in>; {khat leh khat kisamin} is calling to one another) (b:kisam) (q:draft)
kisamkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be summoned/be called out/be called up) (d:be called to come out and gather, as men for war) (b:kisam) (q:draft)
kisamkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be called back/be summoned again) (d:passive of <samkik> call back) (b:samkik) (q:draft)
kisamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let be lacking/leave wanting/lose) (d:<kisam>, lack, with causative <sak>; found with <lo> or <kei>: let nothing be lacking, lose none) (b:kisam) (q:draft)
kisamsia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cursed) (d:passive of <samsia>, curse) (b:samsia) (q:draft)
kisamsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:curse/be cursed/be accursed) (d:form of <kisamsia>, be cursed, used before <hi> and <ciangin>; {hong kisamsiat} is you are cursed or we are cursed) (b:samsiat)
kisamsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curse/cursing) (d:<kisamsiat> curse with the noun suffix <na>: a curse spoken against someone) (s:samsiatna/hamsiatna) (b:kisamsiat) (q:draft)
kisamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guests/those invited/those called) (d:<kisam> be invited, be called, with the plural <te>) (s:leenglate/zinte) (b:kisam) (q:draft)
kisamzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:amount needed/as much as is needed) (d:<kisam>, be needed, with <zah>, amount) (q:draft)
kisamzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be more necessary) (d:<kisam>, be necessary, with <zaw>, more) (s:kulzaw) (b:kisam) (q:draft)
kisan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be accepted/be received) (d:written {kisan’} before <theih>, <leh> and similar words; of an offering or a person, be accepted) (a:kinolh) (q:draft)
kisanek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:eat one another's flesh/devour one another) (d:<sa> flesh and <nek> eat, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (s:kinek) (q:draft)
kisang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:accept/be accepted/be acceptable) (d:of an offering or a person, be accepted; {kisang lo} is not accepted and {kisang thei} is acceptable) (a:kinolh)
kisangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exalted/be lifted up/be made high) (d:<sangsak>, make high, with the prefix <ki>: be lifted high or exalted, said of God, of a mountain and of the proud) (s:kipahtawi/kilamsang) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniam) (q:draft)
kisangsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the lofty/the tall ones/those lifted up) (d:<kisangsak> with plural <te>: those that are made high or make themselves high) (b:kisangsak) (q:draft)
kisangtawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exalted/be highly regarded/be honoured) (d:<sang> high and <tawi> hold up, with the prefix <ki>: be held in high regard) (s:kipahtawi/kizahtak) (a:kisimmawh) (q:draft)
kisangthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be acceptable/can be accepted) (d:<kisang>, be accepted, with <thei>, be able; said of an offering) (b:kisang) (q:draft)
kisangtosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised up/be lifted up) (d:passive of <sangtosak>, raise up; said of valleys) (a:kiniamsak) (b:sangtosak) (q:draft)
kisanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:casting) (d:with <ai>, the casting of lots or taking of omens, divination; from <kisaan>, be cast, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:saanna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dyed red/be made red) (d:passive of <sansak>, make red; {a kisansak tuutal vunte}, ram skins dyed red) (b:sansak) (r:2.35.7) (q:draft)
kisap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:need/be needed/lack) (d:form of <kisam>, need, used before nouns and words such as <zah> and <hun>: what someone needs or lacks, or the time when a thing is needed) (q:draft)
kisap = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be called/be invited/be summoned) (d:form of <kisam>, be called, used before <ciangin>, <hangin> and <loh>: be called, invited or summoned; also be called by a name) (s:kilo) (b:sap) (q:draft)
kisapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who considers himself/one who thinks himself) (d:<kisa> with <pa> marking a man; {pil a kisapa} is the man who thinks himself wise) (b:kisa) (q:draft)
kisapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:need/lack/want) (d:<kisap>, need, with the noun suffix <na>: what a person needs or lacks; {kisapna nei lo} is lack nothing) (s:tangsapna/kitangsapna/cihmawhna) (b:kisap) (q:draft)
kisapnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:needs) (d:<kisapna>, need, with the plural <te>: the things a person needs) (s:cihmawhnate) (b:kisapna) (q:draft)
kisasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make oneself feel) (d:<sasak>, cause to feel, with <ki>, oneself; {lamdang kisasak}, be amazed, make oneself wonder) (b:sasak) (q:draft)
kisat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck/be battered) (d:passive of <sat>, beat or strike: be beaten; {khat leh khat kisat} is strike one another; said of the heart, pound or throb) (b:sat) (q:draft)
kisate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who consider themselves) (d:<kisa> with plural <te>, placed after a describing word: people who think themselves so, as {mipil a kisate}, those who think themselves wise) (b:kisa) (q:draft)
kisate = (i:2) (t:n) (w:songs sung) (d:in {la kisate}, the songs that are sung) (b:kisa) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisatgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck hard/strike one another) (d:<kisat>, be beaten, with <gawp> marking a thorough or violent action; {amau le amau kisatgawp}, strike each other down) (b:kisat) (q:draft)
kisathei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/be arrogant) (d:boast or be proud of oneself; {a kisathei mi} is one who boasts, and {Topa sungah kisathei} is boast in the Lord) (s:kiphasak/kihisak/kiphatsak) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (b:kisa) (q:draft)
kisatheikha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be arrogant/become proud) (d:<kisathei>, be proud, with <kha>, happen to: fall into pride; {kisatheikha loin} is without becoming arrogant) (q:draft)
kisatheipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boaster/one who boasts) (d:<kisathei>, boast, with <pa> marking a man: the man who boasts) (b:kisathei) (q:draft)
kisatheisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make proud/puff up) (d:<kisathei>, be proud, with the causative <sak>) (b:kisathei) (q:draft)
kisatheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant/those who boast) (d:<kisathei>, boast or be proud, with the plural <te>: people who are proud or who boast, usually as {a kisatheite}) (s:kiphasakte/kihisakte/kiliansakte) (a:kiniamkhiatte/lungniamsakte) (b:kisathei) (q:draft)
kisatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck) (d:<kisat>, be beaten, with the linking ending <in>: being beaten, and) (b:kisat) (q:draft)
kisatkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be smashed/be broken down/be broken open) (d:passive of <satkham>, smash by striking: be broken down or burst open by blows) (s:kisukham/kidengkham/kisatvui) (b:satkham) (q:draft)
kisatkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken off/be cut off) (d:passive of <satkhia>, strike off: said of branches cut from a tree) (s:kisattan) (b:satkhia) (q:draft)
kisatkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be beaten out/be threshed out) (d:of grain or seed, be knocked out with a stick) (b:satkhia) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisatlum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be struck dead/be killed/be dashed to death) (d:passive of <satlum>, strike dead: be killed by a blow or with the sword) (s:kithat/kithatlum) (b:satlum) (q:draft)
kisatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beating/blow/lash) (d:the act of beating or of being struck; {kisatna ciang} is the rod one is beaten with and {kisatna ma} is a wound from a beating) (s:satna/vuakna) (b:kisat) (q:draft)
kisatnen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be smashed to bits/be shattered) (d:passive of <satnen>, smash into small bits) (s:kisatvui/kisatkham) (b:satnen) (q:draft)
kisatnim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be crushed/be bruised) (d:be beaten down and crushed by blows) (s:kisuzan) (b:satnim) (q:draft)
kisatpuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be struck down/be defeated) (d:passive of <satpuk>, strike down) (s:kizo/guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:satpuk) (q:draft)
kisattan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut off/be cut down) (d:passive of <sattan>, cut off; {a kisattan ankung} is a stalk of grain that has been cut) (s:kisatkhia) (b:sattan) (q:draft)
kisatvui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be smashed to powder/be crushed/be broken down) (d:passive of <satvui>, beat to dust) (s:kisatkham/kisatnen) (b:satvui) (q:draft)
kisatzan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pressed/be beaten/be crushed) (d:passive of <satzan>, beat to pieces; {a kisatzan sathau} is oil from beaten or pressed olives) (s:kisuzan) (b:satzan) (q:draft)
kisatzanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be smashed to pieces/be broken down) (d:<kisatzan> with the linking ending <in>: being smashed to pieces, and) (b:kisatzan) (q:draft)
kisau = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:grasshopper) (d:found in {kauphe kisau}, a kind of locust or grasshopper that may be eaten, the last of the four kinds named in Leviticus 11:22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be leavened/be mixed with/be salted) (d:passive of <sawh>, mix in: {silngo a kisawh} is leavened, made with yeast; {gu kisawh tui} is poisoned water; of salt, be salted) (s:kihelpih) (b:sawh) (q:draft)
kisawhkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:touch/come into contact with/be stained by) (d:with <tawh>, with: come into contact with a thing and so be affected or defiled by it) (s:lawngkha/sukha) (q:draft)
kisawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:revel/carouse) (d:said of men and women at a feast after drinking; the verse has it for indulging in revelry and the exact sense is not certain) (s:gualnuam/noptat) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sent/be ordered) (d:passive of <sawl>, send or order: be sent on an errand or as an envoy, or be given a task to do) (s:kipuak/kipaisak) (b:sawl) (q:draft)
kisawlgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be compelled/be forced) (d:<kisawl>, be sent or ordered, with <gawp>, forcefully) (s:kihah) (b:kisawl) (q:draft)
kisawlkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sent out/be sent away) (d:passive of <sawlkhia>, send out: be sent out or sent on one's way) (s:kiciahsak/kipaikhiasak) (b:sawlkhia) (q:draft)
kisawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:messenger/the one sent) (d:<kisawl>, be sent, with <pa> marking a man: the man who is sent) (s:kamtaipa/kamtai) (b:kisawl) (q:draft)
kisawlsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sent on/be sent in turn) (d:<kisawl>, be sent, with <sawn>, onward: be sent as the one who passes something on) (b:sawlsawn) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those sent/those who are sent) (d:<kisawl>, be sent, with the plural <te>: people who are sent) (b:kisawl) (q:draft)
kisawlteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all that one is told to do) (d:<kisawl>, be ordered, with <teng>, all) (b:kisawl) (q:draft)
kisawlzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have been sent/be sent) (d:<kisawl> be sent, with <zo> marking the action as done) (b:kisawl) (q:draft)
kisawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plotted against/be planned against) (d:passive of <sawm>, intend or plan to do something; in Acts 9:24 of the plan to kill Saul) (b:sawm) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawm = (i:2) (t:phrase) (w:ten horns) (d:<ki> horn and <sawm> ten written as one word) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plot/planned attack) (d:the fact of being aimed at or plotted against, a plan to attack or harm someone) (s:thahsawmna/sawmsimna) (b:kisawm) (q:draft)
kisawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be pushed/be thrust) (d:passive of <sawn>, push, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kinot) (b:sawn) (q:draft)
kisawnkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be driven out/be pushed out) (d:passive of <sawnkhia>, push out: be driven out of a place) (s:kihawlkhia/kinotkhia/kinawhkhia) (b:sawnkhia) (q:draft)
kisawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be washed/be rinsed) (d:passive of <sawp>, wash: said of clothes, vessels and other things; {kisawp siang} is be washed clean) (s:kisilsiang) (b:sawp) (q:draft)
kisawpsa = (t:see) <kisawpsa-in>
kisawpsa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be washed/having been washed) (d:<kisawp>, be washed, with the completive suffix <sa> and the linking ending <in>) (q:draft)
kisawpsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be washed clean/wash away) (d:<kisawp>, be washed, with <siang>, clean; of sins, have them washed away) (s:kisilsiang) (b:kisawp) (q:draft)
kisazaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be considered rather/be thought more) (d:<kisa>, be considered, with <zaw>, more or rather; {mipil kisazaw}, be thought the wiser for it) (b:kisa) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiseek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hammered/be beaten out/be dressed/be carved) (d:be shaped with a tool: of metal hammered into shape, of stone dressed, of an image carved; {a kiseek milim} is a carved image) (s:kisui) (q:draft)
kiseekin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hammered out/be beaten out) (d:<kiseek> with the linking ending <in>: being hammered out, and) (b:kiseek) (q:draft)
kiseel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hidden/be secret) (d:passive of <seel>, hide: be hidden or kept secret; {a kiseel sum} is hidden treasure) (s:kiliah/kibu/kiseelcip) (a:kilang/kipholaak) (b:seel) (q:draft)
kiseel = (i:2) (t:v) (w:argue/dispute/quarrel) (d:argue with one another, often with {khat leh khat}, one another) (s:kisel/kinial/kitot) (q:draft)
kiseelcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hidden/be concealed/be hidden away) (d:passive of <seelcip>, hide completely: be hidden away so that it cannot be seen) (s:kiselcip/kiseel/kiliah/kiseelsim) (a:kilang) (b:seelcip) (q:draft)
kiseelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hidden/hide oneself/be concealed) (d:<kiseel>, be hidden, with the linking ending <in>; {meel kiseelin} is in disguise) (b:kiseel) (q:draft)
kiseelin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:quarrel/dispute/contend) (d:with <tawh>, quarrelling with someone) (b:kiseel) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiseelkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hidden together/be hidden with) (d:<kiseel>, be hidden, with <khawm>, together; used with <tawh>, with) (b:kiseel) (q:draft)
kiseelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quarrel/dispute/argument) (d:<kiseel>, argue, with the noun suffix <na>: a quarrel or dispute between people) (s:kiselna/kitotna/kinialna) (b:kiseel) (q:draft)
kiseelnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quarrels/disputes/arguments) (d:plural of <kiseelna>, quarrel) (s:kiselnate/kitotnate/kinialnate) (b:kiseelna) (q:draft)
kiseelsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be concealed/be kept secret) (d:passive of <seelsim>, hide secretly: be kept out of sight) (s:kiseelcip/kiselcip) (a:kipholaak) (b:seelsim) (q:draft)
kiseelte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hidden things/what is hidden/hidden treasures) (d:<kiseel>, be hidden, with the plural <te>: things that are hidden; {sum kiseelte} are hidden treasures) (s:kiselte/thusimte) (b:kiseel) (q:draft)
kiseepsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:winnowed/threshed) (d:said of grain and, as a picture, of a people who have been crushed; paired with <kicilsa>, trodden out) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiseh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be appointed/be fixed/be assigned) (d:passive of <seh>, appoint or set: be appointed to a task, or of a time be fixed; {a kiseh hun} is the appointed time) (s:kiciangtan) (b:seh) (r:10.24.15) (q:draft)
kiseh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be counted/be reckoned/be valued) (d:be counted or reckoned as something; with {thei lo}, cannot be counted) (s:kisim) (b:seh) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set apart/be allotted/be marked out) (d:<kiseh> with the linking ending <in>: being set apart, and) (b:kiseh) (q:draft)
kisehkhenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:division/grouping) (d:the way people are divided into groups for a duty; built on <sehkhen>, divide and assign, with the prefix <ki> and the noun ending <na>) (q:draft)
kisehkhennate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:divisions/groupings) (d:plural of <kisehkhenna>: the groups into which people are divided for their service) (s:kikhennate) (b:kisehkhenna) (q:draft)
kisehkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set apart/be measured off/be allotted) (d:of land or a share, be marked off from the rest for a purpose) (s:kituamkoih) (b:kiseh) (q:draft)
kisehkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be determined beforehand/be appointed in advance/be decreed) (d:passive of <sehkhol>, appoint beforehand: be decided or fixed in advance) (b:sehkhol) (q:draft)
kisehkholsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:appointed beforehand/predetermined) (d:<kisehkhol> be appointed in advance, with <sa>, already) (b:kisehkhol) (q:draft)
kisehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valuation/value/estimation) (d:the amount at which something is assessed) (s:sehna/manzah) (b:kiseh) (q:draft)
kisehsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:appointed/fixed/prescribed) (d:<kiseh>, be appointed, with <sa>, already: that has been set beforehand, as a time or an amount) (s:kiciangtansa/sehsa) (b:kiseh) (r:27.8.19) (q:draft)
kisehsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those appointed/those destined) (d:<kisehsa> appointed, with the plural <te>: the ones who have been appointed to something) (s:kisehte) (b:kisehsa) (q:draft)
kisehtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:appoint oneself/take upon oneself) (d:<seh> appoint, with the prefix <ki> and <tawm>, by oneself) (q:draft)
kisehte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those appointed/appointed ones/those assigned) (d:<kiseh>, be appointed, with the plural <te>: the ones that are appointed or set; {pawi a kisehte} are the appointed feasts) (s:kisehsate) (b:kiseh) (q:draft)
kisehzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:appointed measure/set amount) (d:<sehzah> set amount, with the prefix <ki>: the amount that has been fixed, here the number of one's days) (b:sehzah) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisehzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be decreed/be appointed/be fixed) (d:<kiseh> be appointed, with <zo> marking the act as completed) (b:kiseh) (q:draft)
kisekin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:train/exercise/discipline oneself) (d:found in {kisekin kisinna}, training by exercise; probably <sek> shape or forge, with the prefix <ki> and the linking ending <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiseksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:trained/disciplined) (d:<sek> shape or forge, with the prefix <ki> and <sa>, already: having been trained; {amau leh amau a kiseksa} is those who have trained themselves) (q:draft)
kiseksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:train oneself/exercise oneself) (d:<sek> shape or forge, with the prefix <ki> and <sak>, cause) (s:kisin) (q:draft)
kiseksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:training/exercise) (d:<kiseksak> train oneself, with the noun suffix <na>; {pumpi ading kiseksakna} is physical training) (s:kisinna) (b:kiseksak) (q:draft)
kisekzo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:disciplined/self-disciplined) (d:<sek> shape or train, with the prefix <ki> and <zo>, be able: able to keep oneself in training) (q:draft)
kisel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:argue/dispute/quarrel) (d:argue with one another; {thu kisel}, dispute a matter or bring a case against someone) (s:kiseel/kinial/kitot/kitawng) (b:sel) (r:33.6.2) (q:draft)
kiselcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hidden/be concealed) (d:passive of <selcip> hide completely, with the prefix <ki>; the same word as <kiseelcip>, written with a single e) (s:kiseelcip/kiliah/kiseelsim) (a:kipholak) (b:selcip) (q:draft)
kiselcipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be covered/be hidden away) (d:<kiselcip> be hidden, with <sak>: of sin, be caused to be covered) (b:kiselcip) (q:draft)
kiselin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:argue/dispute/quarrel) (d:<kisel>, argue, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb; used with <tawh>, with) (b:kisel) (q:draft)
kiselin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:disguise/hide) (d:with <mel>, appearance: hiding what one looks like, disguising oneself) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiselna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dispute/argument/strife/controversy) (d:arguing against one another; {kam kiselna} is a quarrel in words) (s:kiseelna/kitotna/kinialna) (b:kisel) (q:draft)
kiselnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disputes/arguments) (d:<kiselna> dispute, with the plural <te>) (s:kiseelnate/kinialnate/kitotnate) (b:kiselna) (q:draft)
kiselsimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hiding/hiding place) (d:the act or place of hiding oneself secretly; {a kiselsimna mun} is the place where someone hides) (s:bukna) (q:draft)
kiselte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hidden things/what is hidden) (d:<kisel>, be hidden, with the plural <te>: the things that are hidden) (s:kiseelte/thusimte) (q:draft)
kisem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be done/be carried out/be performed) (d:passive of <sem>, work or do, with the prefix <ki>: be done or carried out) (s:kihih/kisep) (b:sem) (q:draft)
kisem = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be cut up/be cut in pieces) (d:in {kisem nen}, be cut into small pieces, said of a slaughtered animal) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be done/be carried on) (d:<kisem> with the linking ending <in>: being done, and) (b:kisem) (q:draft)
kisemkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried out/be accomplished) (d:passive of <semkhia> with the prefix <ki>) (b:semkhia) (q:draft)
kisemnen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut into pieces/be cut up) (d:passive of <semnen> with the prefix <ki>) (b:semnen) (q:draft)
kisemsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:done/have been done) (d:<kisem> be done, with <sa>, already: what has been done) (b:kisem) (q:draft)
kisemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to work/be made to serve) (d:passive of <semsak> make work, with the prefix <ki>) (b:semsak) (q:draft)
kisemsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forced labourers/those made to work) (d:<kisemsak>, be made to work, with plural <te>; {aana tawh na a kisemsakte}, those who are made to work by force) (b:kisemsak) (q:draft)
kisen = (t:see) <kisen'na>
kisen'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:storing place/storage/archive) (d:place where things are kept; {a kisen'na inn} is a house where documents or treasures are stored) (s:kisenna) (q:draft)
kiseng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put in/be deposited/be stored) (d:passive of <seng>; in Ezra 8:33 of silver, gold and vessels handed over in the temple, where the NIV has weighed out) (b:seng) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:storing place/storage/archive) (d:place where things are kept; {a kisenna inn} is a house where documents or treasures are stored) (s:kisen'na) (q:draft)
kisep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be done/be carried out) (d:passive of <sep>, work or do: {na a kisep} is work that is done) (s:kisem/kihih) (b:sep) (q:draft)
kisepna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:work/doing/being done) (d:<kisep>, be done or worked on, with the noun suffix <na>: the carrying out of a work or of deeds) (b:kisep) (q:draft)
kisepsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:serve one another) (d:<sepsak> serve, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>; with <khatlekhat>, one another) (b:sepsak) (q:draft)
kisepsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be served) (d:passive of <sepsak>; {a na a kisepsak pasian} are the gods that were served) (b:sepsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisepsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forced labour/being made to work) (d:<sepsak> make work, with the prefix <ki> and the noun suffix <na>: work that one is made to do) (b:kisepsak) (q:draft)
kisepsep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be at work/keep on working) (d:<sep> work, doubled and with the prefix <ki>, for an action that goes on) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kish = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kish) (d:name of several men, among them a man of Benjamin, the father of King Saul) (r:13.23.21) (q:draft)
Kishi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kishi) (d:Levite of the clan of Merari, father of the temple musician Ethan) (r:13.6.44) (q:draft)
Kishion = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kishion) (d:town in the territory of Issachar given to the Levites) (r:6.21.28/6.19.20)
Kishon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Kishon) (d:river in the north of Israel where the army of Sisera was swept away) (r:7.4.13/7.5.21)
kisi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:face each other/confront/meet in battle) (d:come face to face as opponents, in battle or in court; {khatlekhat kisi ni} is let us face each other) (s:kimaituah) (q:draft)
kisia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:damage) (d:damage or ruin that has come on something; also used as a verb, be ruined or perish) (b:sia)
kisiacip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid waste/be completely ruined/collapse) (d:<kisia>, be ruined, with <cip>, completely: be utterly ruined, said of the earth or a city) (s:kisiagawp) (b:kisia) (q:draft)
kisiagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:corrupt/be ruined/be laid waste) (d:<kisia>, be ruined, with <gawp>, thoroughly: be badly ruined or spoiled; of the earth, be corrupt) (s:kisiacip) (b:kisia)
kisiah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set/be laid) (d:<siah>, set a trap, with the passive prefix <ki>: of a trap or snare, be set; {thang kisiah} is a trap is set) (b:siah) (q:draft)
kisiahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set/be laid) (d:<kisiah>, be set, with the linking ending <in>; {thang kisiahin} is snares being set, and then) (b:kisiah) (q:draft)
kisiahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:setting/laying) (d:<kisiah>, be set, of a trap, with the noun ending <na>; {hong kisiahna ngenthang} is the net that is set for me) (b:kisiah) (q:draft)
kisiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be swept away/be driven out/be banished) (d:be swept or cleared out of a place; found in {kisiak khia}, with <khia>, out) (s:kihawlkhia) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisiakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be corrupted/be ruined) (d:<kisia>, be ruined, with <khin>, already; of a person, warped or corrupted) (b:kisia) (q:draft)
kisiakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be banished/be swept out/be driven out) (d:<kisiak> be swept away, with <khia>, out) (s:kisiakmang/kihawlkhia) (b:kisiak) (q:draft)
kisiakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be banished/be swept away) (d:<kisiak> be swept away, with <mang>, away, out of sight) (s:kisiakkhia/kihawlkhia) (q:draft)
kisial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:speak proudly of oneself or of what one has done) (s:kiphasak/kisathei/kisialh) (a:kiniamkhiat) (q:draft)
kisial = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lie/be laid) (d:lie or be laid down in a place) (q:draft)
kisialh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:form of <kisial>, boast, used before words such as <nading>, <nop>, <taak> and <leh>) (s:kiphasak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:kisial) (r:47.11.30) (q:draft)
kisialhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boasting/arrogance/pride) (d:<kisialh>, boast, with the noun suffix <na>: boasting, proud talk about oneself) (s:kiphatsakna/kisaktheihna/kihihsakna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (b:kisialh) (q:draft)
kisialhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boasts/boastings) (d:<kisialhna>, boasting, with the plural <te>: boasts, proud words) (s:kiphatsaknate) (b:kisialhna) (q:draft)
kisialhpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast of/boast about/take pride in) (d:<kisialh>, boast, with <pih>: boast on account of something or someone) (s:kisaktheihpih/kiphatsakpih) (b:kisialh) (q:draft)
kisialhpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boasting about/pride in) (d:<kisialhpih> with the noun ending <na>: the boasting one does about someone) (b:kisialhpih) (q:draft)
kisialhpihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boaster/one who boasts of) (d:<kisialhpih> boast of, with <pa> for a man: the man who boasts of something) (s:kisatheipa) (b:kisialhpih) (q:draft)
kisialin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boast/show off/taunt) (d:connective form of <kisial>, making much of oneself before others; {kei tungah hong kisialin}, taunting me) (b:kisial) (q:draft)
kisialin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lie/be laid) (d:lying or laid down in something, said of the baby in the manger) (b:kisial) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisialna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:place of lying/being laid) (d:<kisial>, lie or be laid down, with the noun suffix <na>; {a kisialna mun}, the place where he was laid) (b:kisial) (r:41.16.6) (q:draft)
kisialnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to boast/wish to boast) (d:<kisial> boast, with <nuam>, want to) (q:draft)
kisialsial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go on boasting/keep boasting) (d:<kisial> boast, with the second part doubled for an action that goes on) (q:draft)
kisialzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:how it was laid/manner of laying) (d:<sial> lay a body down, with the prefix <ki> and <zia>, manner: the way a body was laid in the tomb) (q:draft)
kisiamai = (t:see) <kisiamai-sate>
kisiamai-sate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:devastated places/ruins) (d:the things or places that have been laid waste; written <kisiamaisate> in the other text) (q:draft)
kisiamaisa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:devastated/ruined/laid waste) (d:<kisia> be ruined, with <mai> and <sa>, already: that has been laid waste) (s:kisiasa) (q:draft)
kisiamaisate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:devastated places/ruins) (d:the things or places that have been laid waste) (s:siasate) (b:kisiamaisa) (q:draft)
kisiamang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ruined/be destroyed/be lost) (d:<siamang> perish, come to complete ruin, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kisiacip) (b:siamang) (q:draft)
kisian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/be sanctified) (d:shortened form of <kisiang>, written with an apostrophe before <tho>, <suah> or <sak>; {kisian’ thosak}, be made holy or clean) (b:sian) (r:26.44.26) (q:draft)
kisian'thosakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:purification/cleansing) (d:shortened spelling of {kisiangthosakna}: making oneself ritually clean; {kisian'thosakna ni} are the days of purification) (s:kisiansuahna) (q:draft)
kisiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/cleanse oneself) (d:<siang> clean, with the prefix <ki>, found with the causative <sak> written apart: {kisiang tawm sak}, have them cleanse themselves; {mei tawh kisiang saksa kham}, gold refined in fire) (b:siang) (q:draft)
kisiangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/purify oneself/consecrate oneself) (d:<siangsak>, make clean, with the prefix <ki>: be made ritually clean, or make oneself clean; {nomau mah kisiangsak tawm un} is consecrate yourselves) (s:kisiansak/kisiansuah/kisiangthosak) (a:kininsak) (b:siangsak) (q:draft)
kisiangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purify oneself/cleanse oneself) (d:<kisiangsak> with the linking ending <in>: purifying oneself, and then) (b:kisiangsak) (q:draft)
kisiangsaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:refined/purified) (d:<kisiangsak>, be purified, with the completive suffix <sa>; of silver and gold that has been refined) (b:kisiangsak) (q:draft)
kisiangtho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purify oneself/consecrate oneself) (d:<siangtho> holy or clean, with the prefix <ki>; found with the causative <sak> written apart, as {kisiangtho sak} and {kisiangtho tawmsak}) (b:siangtho) (q:draft)
kisiangthosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/be made holy) (d:<siangthosak>, make clean or holy, with the passive prefix <ki>; {a kisiangthosak ding mipa} is the man who is to be cleansed) (s:kisiangsak/kisiansak) (b:siangthosak) (r:3.14.29) (q:draft)
kisiangthosak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:purify oneself/sanctify oneself) (d:<siangthosak>, make holy, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: make oneself clean or holy) (s:kisiansuah) (a:kininsak) (b:siangthosak) (r:62.3.3) (q:draft)
kisiangthosakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purifying oneself/cleansing oneself) (d:<kisiangthosak> purify oneself, with <in> linking to the next verb) (b:kisiangthosak) (q:draft)
kisiangthosakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one being cleansed) (d:<kisiangthosak> be cleansed, with <pa> for a man: the man who is to be made clean) (b:kisiangthosak) (q:draft)
kisiangthosaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:purified/refined/consecrated) (d:<kisiangthosak> with <sa>, already: that has been made pure or holy; of metal, refined in fire) (s:kisiangsaksa) (b:kisiangthosak) (q:draft)
kisiansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purify oneself/be cleansed/be pronounced clean) (d:make oneself or be made ritually clean) (s:kisiangsak/kisiansuah) (a:kininsak) (b:siansak) (q:draft)
kisiansak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be refined) (d:of silver or gold, be made pure in the furnace) (b:siansak) (q:draft)
kisiansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:refining/purifying) (d:<kisiansak> be refined, with the noun suffix <na>; {kham a kisiansakna mun} is a place where gold is refined) (b:kisiansak) (q:draft)
kisiansuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consecrate oneself/purify oneself/be consecrated) (d:make oneself or be made ritually holy) (s:kisiangsak/kisiansak/kisiangthosak) (a:kininsak) (b:siansuah) (r:27.9.24) (q:draft)
kisiansuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purify oneself/be purified/be cleansed) (d:<kisiansuah>, purify oneself, with the linking ending <in>: purifying oneself, and then) (b:kisiansuah) (q:draft)
kisiansuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:purification/ceremonial cleansing) (d:the act or rite of making oneself ritually clean) (s:kisian'thosakna) (b:kisiansuah) (q:draft)
kisianthosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified) (d:<sianthosak> with the prefix <ki>; {kisianthosak nading} is for his cleansing) (b:sianthosak) (q:draft)
kisiasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:ruined/desolate) (d:<kisia>, be ruined, with <sa> for a completed state: already ruined, placed before the noun) (s:siasa/kisiamaisa) (b:kisia) (q:draft)
kisiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy oneself/be ruined/be defiled/be corrupted) (d:reflexive or passive of <siasak>; with <tawm>, bring ruin on oneself) (b:siasak) (q:draft)
kisiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/perish/be ruined) (d:form of <kisia>, be ruined, used before words such as <nading>, <ding>, <manin> and <sangin>) (s:mangthang) (b:kisia) (q:draft)
kisiatgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be utterly destroyed) (d:<kisiat> be destroyed, with <gawp>, completely) (s:kisiagawp/kisusiagawp) (b:kisiat) (q:draft)
kisiathei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:perishable/that can perish) (d:<kisia> be ruined, with <thei>, can: that will not last) (s:siathei) (b:kisia) (q:draft)
kisiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:destruction/ruin/perdition) (d:<kisiat>, be destroyed, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being destroyed or ruined; {kisiatna-ah pai} is go to destruction) (s:siatna/kisuksiatna) (b:kisiat) (q:draft)
kisiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:harm one another/ruin one another/do evil to one another) (d:<siatsak> ruin, harm, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (b:siatsak) (q:draft)
kisiatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:harming one another/doing evil to one another) (d:<kisiatsak> with the noun ending <na>) (b:kisiatsak) (q:draft)
kisiatsakna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:defilement/being violated) (d:the fact that someone has been ruined; in Genesis 34:5 of a woman who was defiled) (b:kisiatsak) (q:draft)
kisiatsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:waste away/keep decaying) (d:<kisiat> be ruined, with the second part doubled for a process that goes on) (q:draft)
kisiazan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid in ruins/become rubble) (d:<kisia> be ruined, with <zan>, in pieces: of a city, be reduced to a heap of ruins) (q:draft)
kisiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ruined/lie in ruins) (d:<kisia> be ruined, with <zo> marking the act as completed) (b:kisia) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisiik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be required of/be exacted from) (d:passive of <siik> exact with the prefix <ki>: of blood shed, be demanded from those held responsible) (b:siik) (q:draft)
kisiincip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be covered tight/be sealed/be shut up) (d:<siin> cover with a lid, with the prefix <ki> and <cip>, tightly) (q:draft)
kisiit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be left over/be spared/be kept back) (d:<siit>, keep back, with the passive prefix <ki>: be left over, spared or kept back; {bangmah kisiit lo ding hi} is nothing will be left) (b:siit) (q:draft)
kisiitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kept for/be set aside for) (d:<kisiit> be kept back, with <sak>, for someone) (b:kisiit) (q:draft)
kisikcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trampled/be trodden down/be oppressed) (d:be pressed down underfoot; {a kisikcip mite} are the downtrodden, the oppressed or humble) (s:kisikgawp/kituancil) (q:draft)
kisikgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trampled/be trodden down) (d:passive of <sikgawp> trample with the prefix <ki>) (s:kisikcip/kituancil) (b:sikgawp) (q:draft)
kisikh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be provided) (d:passive with the prefix <ki> of <sikh>, which the same verse uses of God providing) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repenting/repent/turn back) (d:<kisik> with the linking suffix <in>: being sorry and turning from wrong, and then) (b:kisik) (q:draft)
kisikkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trample on one another/tread on) (d:<sik> tread, with the prefix <ki> and <kha>, happen to touch; with <khatlekhat>, step on one another) (q:draft)
kisikkik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:repentance) (d:<kisik>, regret, with <kik>, back: turning back from sin; also used as a verb, repent) (s:kisikna) (b:kisik)
