kisikkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:repentance) (d:<kisikkik>, repent, with the noun suffix <na>: turning back from sin) (s:kisikna) (b:kisikkik) (r:44.11.18)
kisikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:repentance) (d:<kisik>, regret or repent, with the noun suffix <na>: sorrow for sin and turning from it) (s:kisikkikna) (b:kisik)
kisiknuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:relent/be willing to relent) (d:<kisik> regret, with <nuam>, want to: ready to change one's mind about a punishment) (q:draft)
kisikpih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:opponent) (d:the man someone meets hand to hand in a fight) (q:draft)
kisiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead to repentance/cause to repent/grant repentance) (d:<kisik> regret or repent, with the causative <sak>) (b:kisik) (q:draft)
kisikzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to repent) (d:<kisik> regret or repent, with <zo>, be able) (b:kisik) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisilhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be clothed/be robed/clothe oneself) (d:<silhsak>, clothe, with the prefix <ki>: have a garment put on) (b:silhsak) (q:draft)
kisilin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bathe/wash oneself) (d:<kisil> with the linking ending <in>: bathing, and then) (b:kisil) (q:draft)
kisilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:washing) (d:the act of washing oneself, from <kisil>; {kisilna kuang} is a washbasin) (b:kisil) (r:2.40.7) (q:draft)
kisilsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wash one another's/wash for one another) (d:<silsak> wash for someone, with the reciprocal prefix <ki>; said of washing one another's feet) (b:silsak) (q:draft)
kisilsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who have bathed) (d:<kisil> bathe, with <sa>, already, and the plural <te>) (q:draft)
kisilsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wash oneself clean/be washed) (d:<silsiang>, wash clean, with the prefix <ki>: wash oneself clean or be washed clean) (b:silsiang) (q:draft)
kisim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be counted/be numbered) (d:<sim>, count, with the passive prefix <ki>: be counted or numbered) (b:sim) (r:44.19.7) (q:draft)
kisim = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be read) (d:of a letter or writing, be read out) (b:sim) (q:draft)
kisimin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be read) (d:<kisim>, be read, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:kisim) (q:draft)
kisimin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be attacked/be invaded) (d:passive of <sim>, attack, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (q:draft)
kisimkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be counted together/be numbered among) (d:<kisim> be counted with <khawm>, together; with <tawh> or <lakah> for the group) (b:kisim) (q:draft)
kisimkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be read out) (d:passive of <simkhia> read out with the prefix <ki>; of a letter, be read out in a given language) (b:simkhia) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisimkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:counting oneself with/classing oneself with) (d:<simkhawm> count together, with the prefix <ki> and the noun suffix <na>: putting oneself in the same class as others) (q:draft)
kisimmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be despised/be scorned/be shamed) (d:<simmawh>, despise, with the passive prefix <ki>: be looked down on or put to shame) (a:kizahtak) (b:simmawh) (q:draft)
kisimmawhbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dishonoured/be treated with contempt) (d:passive of <simmawhbawl> with the prefix <ki>) (a:kizahtakbawl) (b:simmawhbawl) (q:draft)
kisimmawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being insulted/being despised) (d:<kisimmawh> be despised, with <in> linking to the next verb) (b:kisimmawh) (q:draft)
kisimmawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:insult/scorn/contempt/disrespect) (d:the act of despising or insulting one another, or of being scorned by others) (s:simmawhna/zahkona/kosiatna) (a:zahtakna/pahtawina) (b:kisimmawh) (q:draft)
kisimmawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let oneself be despised) (d:<kisimmawh>, be despised, with <sak>, let: allow others to look down on one; {kuamah kisimmawhsak kei in} means do not let anyone despise you) (b:kisimmawh) (q:draft)
kisimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:census/count/numbering/number) (d:the act or result of counting people) (s:misimna/simna) (b:kisim) (q:draft)
kisimna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:attack/assault) (d:an attack in war, as in {gal kisimna}; of cities, the attacking of them) (s:simna/dona) (q:draft)
kisimte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those counted/those numbered) (d:<kisim> with plural {-te}, the ones who were counted in a census) (s:simte) (b:kisim) (q:draft)
kisimte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:things read/what was read) (d:<kisim> with plural {-te}, the words that were read out from a book) (b:kisim) (q:draft)
kisin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:learn/practise/train oneself) (d:learn or practise something until one can do it, train oneself; <sin>, learn, with the prefix <ki>) (s:sin) (b:sin) (r:50.4.12) (q:draft)
kisin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be covered/be veiled/be closed over) (d:be closed or covered over with a lid, a stone or a veil; passive of <sin> with the prefix <ki>; {kisin cip}, be covered tight) (s:kikhuh/kituam) (a:kihon/kipholak) (b:sin) (q:draft)
kisin = (i:3) (t:v) (w:be beaten/be harvested) (d:of an olive tree, be beaten so that its fruit falls at harvest) (r:23.24.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisincip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be concealed/be covered up/be sealed up) (d:passive of <sincip> cover over tightly, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kiseelcip/kiselcip/kiliah) (a:kilak/kilang/kipholak) (b:sincip) (q:draft)
kising = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quake/shake/be stirred/shake oneself) (d:of the earth, tremble and shake; of a town, be in an uproar; of a person, shake oneself, as from the dust) (s:liing/kiling/kilok/kiliing) (q:draft)
kisingin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shaking/quaking/shaking oneself) (d:<kising> with the linking ending <in>, shaking and) (b:kising) (q:draft)
kisingkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shaken off/be shaken out) (d:passive {ki-} form of <singkhia>, shake something out or off; also said of the earth shaken from its place) (b:singkhia) (q:draft)
kisinin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being veiled/being covered) (d:<kisin> be covered or veiled, with <in> linking to the next verb) (b:kisin) (q:draft)
kisinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:training/exercise/practice) (d:<kisin> train oneself, with the noun ending <na>) (s:sinna/kiseksakna) (b:kisin) (q:draft)
kisinsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have learned/trained) (d:<kisin> learn or train oneself, with <sa>, already: one who has learned) (s:sinsa) (b:kisin) (q:draft)
kisinsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:train/teach/be trained) (d:<kisin>, learn or practise, with causative <sak>: make someone or something learn; also of a person who has been given training) (s:sinsak/hilh) (b:kisin) (q:draft)
kisisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring death on oneself/destroy oneself) (d:<sisak> cause to die, with the reflexive prefix <ki>) (s:kisusiatawm/kisiasak) (b:sisak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be tried/be examined/be tested) (d:be examined, of a case heard in court as {thu kisit}, or of a person tested as by fire) (s:kikan/kize-et/kisittel) (q:draft)
kisitin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be tried/be judged/be examined) (d:<kisit> with the linking ending <in>; {thu kisitin}, when the case is tried, and) (b:kisit) (q:draft)
kisitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:veil/covering) (d:the thing that covers, here the veil over the heart) (s:khuhna/dalna) (q:draft)
kisitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kept for/be set aside for) (d:be kept back for someone; written <kisiitsak> in the other text) (s:kikoihcingsak) (q:draft)
kisittel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:examine oneself/be tested) (d:test or examine oneself, {a kisittel zo lo} is one who fails the test) (s:kize-et/kisit) (b:sittel) (q:draft)
kisosuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flare up/be stirred up/rouse oneself) (d:of anger, flare up, of a person, rouse oneself to act) (s:kihanthawn) (b:sosuah) (q:draft)
kisu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be struck/be touched) (d:passive of <su>, touch or strike; with <kha>: be struck or touched by something, as by the heat of the sun) (s:kisukkhak/kilawng) (b:su) (q:draft)
kisu = (i:2) (t:v) (w:wrong each other/harm each other/fight each other) (d:<su>, strike or harm, with the prefix <ki>, each other; with <khatlekhat>, one another: do wrong to one another or meet one another in battle) (b:su) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisu = (i:3) (t:v) (w:be pounded/be crushed) (d:passive of <su>, pound; {sum sunga a kisu}, what is pounded in a mortar) (b:su) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made into/be divided into/be split into) (d:after a number with <phel> or <khen>: be torn or divided into that many parts) (b:suah) (r:40.27.51) (q:draft)
kisuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being divided into/being made into/forming) (d:<kisuah>, be made into, with the linking ending <in>; after a number of parts: forming that many groups) (b:kisuah) (q:draft)
kisuahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:escape/get away/save oneself) (d:form of <suahtak> with {ki-}, often before <thei> or <zo>, be able to escape) (s:suahtak/suakta/taikhia) (b:suahtak) (r:24.51.45) (q:draft)
kisuai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be portrayed/be drawn/be engraved) (d:of figures and pictures, be drawn or worked on a surface) (q:draft)
kisuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to become/be made into) (d:<suak> become, with the prefix <ki>; found with the causative <sak> written apart, as {innkuan khat kisuak sak}, be made one family) (b:suak) (q:draft)
kisuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make oneself become/turn oneself into) (d:<suaksak> cause to become, with the reflexive prefix <ki>) (b:suaksak) (q:draft)
kisuaktasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be delivered/be set free/be spared) (d:passive of <suaktasak> with the prefix <ki>) (s:kihon) (b:suaktasak) (q:draft)
kisuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be attacked/be assassinated/be struck down) (d:passive of <suam> with the prefix <ki>) (b:suam) (q:draft)
kisuampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the man who was attacked/victim) (d:<kisuam> be attacked, with <pa> for a man: the man who was set upon by robbers) (b:kisuam) (q:draft)
kisuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be planted) (d:passive of <suan>, said of trees, vines and seed) (s:kituh/kivawh) (a:kibotkhia/kizunglot/kisuankhia) (b:suan) (r:26.17.8) (q:draft)
kisuan = (i:2) (t:v) (w:set out/move) (d:said of a camp that breaks up and moves on) (s:kikhin) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuan = (i:3) (t:v) (w:feel guilty/reproach oneself) (d:found with the ending <na> as guilt or fault; {lungsim kisuan'na} is the conscience, a guilty conscience) (r:20.4.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuan'takna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:self-defence/defending oneself) (d:speaking to clear or justify oneself; {kisuan'takna kampau} is words of self-defence) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set on/be placed upon) (d:be set or mounted on top of something, as gold on silver or a wreath on the head) (s:kinga) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuang = (i:2) (t:v) (w:blush/feel shame/feel guilty) (d:feel shame or guilt; {lungsim kisuang het loin} is with a clear conscience) (s:zum) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuangthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to blush/be able to feel shame) (d:<kisuang> with <thei>, can; used with <lo>: not know how to blush) (b:kisuang) (r:24.6.15) (q:draft)
kisuanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry on the shoulder/take up/shoulder) (d:<kisuan>, put a load on one's own shoulder, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:kisuan) (q:draft)
kisuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be driven out/be conquered) (d:be pulled up or driven out of its place, said of a people or city that is uprooted or conquered; passive of <suankhia> with the prefix <ki>) (s:kibotkhia/kizunglot/kihawlkhia) (a:kisuan) (b:suankhia) (q:draft)
kisuankhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being driven out/overthrow) (d:<suankhiatna> driving out, with the passive prefix <ki>) (s:kihawlkhiatna) (b:suankhiatna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:self-reproach/guilty conscience/guilt) (d:the accusing of oneself in the heart for a wrong done) (r:62.3.21) (q:draft)
kisuanna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:planting/place of planting) (d:being planted; {a kisuanna mun} is the place where a thing was planted) (s:suanna) (b:kisuan) (q:draft)
kisuannasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:place where planted/planting) (d:<kisuanna> with <sa>, already; {ama kisuannasa mun} is the place where it had been planted) (b:kisuanna) (q:draft)
kisuantawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring on oneself/incur) (d:of guilt, be laid on oneself by one's own act) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuanto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lift onto/put up on/load on) (d:with {liangko-ah}: lift a load up onto one's own shoulder) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisugawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be crushed/be destroyed/be oppressed) (d:passive {ki-} form of <sugawp>, crush) (s:kitamzan/kisuzan/kinengniam) (b:sugawp) (q:draft)
kisuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be seized/be plundered/be confiscated) (d:passive of <suh> with the prefix <ki>, of goods or animals taken by force) (s:kiluh/kibuluh/kisut) (b:suh) (q:draft)
kisuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plunder/pillage/seizure) (d:<kisuh> with the noun ending <na>; {neihsa kisuhna} is the seizing of what one owns) (s:suhna) (b:kisuh) (q:draft)
kisui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carved/be hewn/be graven) (d:shaped by cutting; {a kisui milim} is a carved image, named beside {a kisung milim}, a cast image) (s:kiseek/kikhuak) (b:sui) (q:draft)
kisuih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stumble/trip) (d:<suih> stumble, with the prefix <ki>; {kisuih khak} is a thing stumbled against, a stumbling block) (s:kipuk) (b:suih) (q:draft)
kisuikha = (t:see) <kisuikha-in>
kisuikha-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stumbling) (d:<sui> stumble, with the prefix <ki>, <kha>, happen to strike, and <in> linking to the next verb) (s:kipukin) (q:draft)
kisuipuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:slip/stumble) (d:of the feet, slip so that one nearly falls) (s:taal/kipuk) (q:draft)
kisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strike against/knock against/hit) (d:in {kisuk khak}, happen to strike against something, said of a foot against a stone) (r:40.4.6) (q:draft)
kisuk = (i:2) (t:v) (w:go down/rush down) (d:<suk> downward, with the prefix <ki>, paired with <kito> go up: {kisuk leh kito}, go down and up, rush back and forth) (b:suk) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisukcipna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oppression/suppression) (d:the state of being pressed down or crushed by others) (s:sukcipna/nenniamna/kinetniamna) (a:suahtakna) (b:sukcipna) (q:draft)
kisukcipnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:oppressions) (d:<kisukcipna> oppression, with the plural <te>) (s:kinenniamnate/nenniamnate) (b:kisukcipna) (q:draft)
kisukgawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:violence/ravaging/destruction) (d:<sukgawpna> with the prefix <ki>: the striking down or ravaging of one another) (s:sukgawpna/kisuksiatna/ngongtatna) (b:sukgawpna) (q:draft)
kisukha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have to do with/associate with/come into contact with) (d:touch or affect one another; with <tawh>, to have dealings with someone, and of a dead body, to come into contact with it) (s:kikholh/kipawlpih/kisawhkha) (b:sukha) (q:draft)
kisukham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/be smashed/be crushed) (d:passive {ki-} form of <sukham>, break in pieces, said mostly of a clay pot) (s:kitam/kitamzan/kisuzan) (a:kibawlphat) (b:sukham) (q:draft)
kisukkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be touched/come into contact/be harmed) (d:passive of <sukkhak>, touch; used with <tawh> for the thing touched; of a person, have a hand laid on him) (s:kilawng/kisu) (b:sukkhak) (q:draft)
kisukmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be wiped out/be annihilated) (d:passive of <sukmang> with the prefix <ki>) (s:kisusiamang/kisumai) (b:sukmang) (q:draft)
kisukmit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put out/be snuffed out/be extinguished) (d:of a lamp or fire, be made to go out) (s:kisumit/kimitsak/kiphelh) (a:kitawh) (q:draft)
kisukmitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be snuffed out/be put out/be extinguished) (d:of a lamp, be made to go out: <kisukmit> with the causative <sak>) (s:kisumit/kimitsak) (a:kitawh) (b:kisukmit) (q:draft)
kisuksiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be ruined) (d:passive of <suksiat>, the form used before <khit>, <loh>, <nading> and similar words) (s:kisusia/kisiat/kisugawp) (a:kilam/kilamkik) (b:suksiat) (q:draft)
kisuksiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:destruction/ruin) (d:the destroying of people or things, also people destroying one another) (s:suksiatna/kisiatna/kisukgawpna) (a:kilamkikna) (b:suksiatna) (q:draft)
kisuksiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be demolished/be ruined) (d:passive {ki-} form of <suksiatsak>, destroy) (s:kisusia/kisuksiat/kisiat) (b:suksiatsak) (q:draft)
kisuktat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut off/be blotted out) (d:passive of <suktat> with the prefix <ki>; of the memory of a person, be wiped from the earth) (s:kiphiatkhia/kitat) (b:suktat) (q:draft)
kisuliam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wound oneself/cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:<su> strike and <liam> wound, with the reflexive prefix <ki>; {no leh no kisuliam} is wound yourselves) (s:kikui/ki-atkeh/kikuiliam) (q:draft)
kisumai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be wiped out) (d:passive of <sumai> destroy with the prefix <ki>) (s:kisukmang/kisusiamang) (b:sumai) (q:draft)
kisumit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put out/be extinguished/be quenched) (d:passive of <sumit>, put out a fire or lamp) (s:kimitsak/kiphelh/kisukmit/mih) (a:kitawh/kuang) (b:sumit) (q:draft)
kisun = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:like) (d:like, resembling in appearance; {a kisun lel ahi hi} means he only looks like him) (s:kibang/kibat)
kisun = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:similar) (d:similar, alike in appearance, said of one person who looks like another) (s:kibat/kibanga) (a:tuam)
kisun'napa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one anointed) (d:the man on whom something has been poured; here the priest on whose head the anointing oil was poured) (q:draft)
kisuncip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be thrust down/be struck down) (d:found with <suk>, down, of people struck down so that they cannot rise) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisunen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ground fine/be pounded fine) (d:<su> pound and <nen> fine, with the prefix <ki>; {a kisunen paknamtui} is finely ground incense) (q:draft)
kisung = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cast/be molten/be made of cast metal) (d:{ki-} form of <sung>, to cast metal; {a kisung} before a noun means cast or molten, as of an idol or object made from melted metal) (b:sung) (r:14.4.2) (q:draft)
kisungin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being poured out/being cast) (d:passive of <sung>, pour, with the linking ending <in>, used of a drink offering, of anger, and of casting metal in a mould) (b:kisung) (q:draft)
kisungkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cast together/be cast in one piece) (d:<kisung> be cast, of metal, with <khawm>, together) (b:kisung) (q:draft)
kisungsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to pay) (d:said of interest on a debt: {na leiba uh a meet hong kisungsak ding}, you will be made to pay the interest on your debt) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisungtawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cast/molten) (d:of an idol, made by pouring metal; {a kisungtawm pasian} is a cast god) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisunimsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bruised/crushed) (d:<sunim> bruise, with the prefix <ki> and <sa>, already) (q:draft)
kisunin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:likeness) (d:likeness; {a kisunin} after <tawh> means in the likeness of, as in {Pasian tawh a kisunin}, in the likeness of God) (s:kibatna/batna) (b:kisun)
kisunnapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one anointed) (d:the man on whom something has been poured; here the priest on whose head the anointing oil was poured) (q:draft)
kisupaisa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:torn down/demolished/broken down) (d:<ki> with <supai> tear down and <sa>, already: that has been torn down) (s:kicimsa/suksiatsa/kisusiasa) (q:draft)
kisusia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be ruined) (d:passive of <susia>, destroy) (s:kisiat/kisuksiat/kisugawp) (a:kilam/kilamkik) (b:susia) (q:draft)
kisusiacip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be completely destroyed/be laid desolate) (d:<kisusia>, be destroyed, with <cip> marking that it is done completely) (s:kisusiamang) (b:kisusia) (q:draft)
kisusiagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be torn down/be utterly destroyed) (d:<kisusia> be destroyed, with <gawp>, completely) (s:kisiatgawp) (b:kisusia) (q:draft)
kisusiamang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be completely destroyed/be wiped out) (d:passive of <susiamang>, destroy completely) (s:kisusiacip/kisukmang/kisumai/siamaimang) (b:susiamang) (q:draft)
kisusiasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:destroyed/broken down/ruined) (d:<kisusia> with <sa>, already: that has been destroyed) (s:kisupaisa/suksiatsa/kisiasa/siasa) (b:kisusia) (q:draft)
kisusiatawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy oneself/ruin oneself) (d:<susia> destroy, with the prefix <ki> and <tawm>, by oneself) (s:kisiasak/kisisak) (q:draft)
kisut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be robbed) (d:passive of <sut>, plunder, with the prefix <ki>: have one’s goods taken away by force) (s:kiluh/kibuluh/kisuh) (b:sut) (q:draft)
kisut = (i:2) (t:v) (w:defend oneself/free oneself) (d:speak or act to get oneself clear of a charge) (s:kiphel/kihut/kihutawm) (b:sut) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisutkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be loosed/be released/be unfastened) (d:passive of <sutkhia> take off, release, with the prefix <ki>; of prisoners, have the bonds come off) (s:kikhah/kiphel/kikhahkhia) (a:kihen) (b:sutkhia) (q:draft)
kisutkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be taken away) (d:passive of <sutkhia> take away by force, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kisut/kiluh) (b:sutkhia) (q:draft)
kisutkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be taken away) (d:<kisutkhia>, be plundered and carried off, in the form used before <sak> and other following words) (b:kisutkhia) (q:draft)
kisutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let oneself be robbed/be deprived of) (d:<kisut>, be robbed, with <sak>: let something be taken from oneself; with {kei un}, do not let yourselves be robbed of it) (b:kisut) (q:draft)
kisutte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:<kisut>, be plundered, with the plural <te>: things taken by force, usually as {van kisutte}, plundered goods) (s:vankisutte) (b:kisut) (q:draft)
kisutuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/come together) (d:of people, come together in one place, for work or to listen) (s:kikaikhawm/kikhop) (a:kithehthang) (q:draft)
kisuvui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ground/be crushed to powder) (d:passive of <suvui> with the prefix <ki>; {a kisuvui mangbuh} is ground wheat) (s:kigawivui) (b:suvui) (q:draft)
kisuzan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken in pieces/be crushed/be shattered/be pressed) (d:passive of <suzan>, break in pieces: of idols and pots, be smashed; of olives, be pressed or beaten for oil) (s:kitamzan/kisukham/kitam) (b:suzan) (q:draft)
kisuzanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being broken to pieces/being smashed) (d:<kisuzan> be broken in pieces, with <in> linking to the next verb) (b:kisuzan) (q:draft)
kisuzante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pressed ones/crushed ones) (d:<kisuzan> with plural <te>: things that have been crushed; {oliv gah a kisuzante} are pressed olives) (b:kisuzan) (q:draft)
kitaaklah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meddle/interfere/be a busybody) (d:busy oneself with matters that are not one's own) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitaangko = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be proclaimed/be announced) (d:passive of <taangko>, proclaim, with the prefix <ki>: be announced aloud for all to hear) (s:kitangko/kipulak) (b:taangko) (q:draft)
kitaangsapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:need/want) (d:what a person is lacking and has to be helped with) (s:kitangsapna/kisapna/tangsapna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitaat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut/be ground) (d:of gemstones, be worked or shaped before setting; <taat> is sharpen or whet) (b:taat) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be applied/be put to/be used on) (d:of a blade being put to something; {mulkiatna kitah lo} is no razor shall touch the head) (b:tah) (r:7.13.5) (q:draft)
kitah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:snap/break) (d:of a thread that parts when fire touches it) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitahkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strike against/hit against/dash against) (d:of a foot or a ship and a stone, knock against each other; ends in <khak>, happen to) (s:suihkhak) (q:draft)
kitai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rebuked/be corrected/admonish one another) (d:<tai>, rebuke, with the prefix <ki>: be rebuked or corrected, or warn and correct one another) (s:kithuhilh) (q:draft)
kitaisan = (t:see) <kitaisan-in>
kitaisan-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being deserted/being forsaken) (d:<taisan> forsake, with the passive prefix <ki> and <in> linking to the next verb) (q:draft)
kitaisanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being deserted/being forsaken) (d:<taisan> forsake, with the passive prefix <ki> and <in> linking to the next verb) (b:taisanin) (q:draft)
kitaitehna = (t:see) <kitaitehna-ah>
kitaitehna-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the race) (d:<kitaitehna> race, running contest, with <ah>, in or at) (q:draft)
kitam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/be shattered) (d:said of pots and other things that break in pieces; {beel kitam} is a broken pot, a potsherd) (s:kitamzan/kisuzan/kisukham) (q:draft)
kitamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:splitting/breaking open/bursting) (d:<kitam> be broken, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kitam) (q:draft)
kitamkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shattered/be broken to pieces/crumble) (d:be broken apart, of mountains, of nations crushing one another and of the heart) (s:kitamzan/kitam) (b:tamkham) (q:draft)
kitamkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burst/break apart) (d:<kitam> be broken, with <khia>, out; {lungsim kitamkhia dektak} is the heart nearly bursting, said of rage) (b:kitam) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitamkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made level/be levelled) (d:<tamkim> level, with the prefix <ki>; found with the causative <sak> written apart) (b:tamkim) (q:draft)
kitamnen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken to pieces/be crushed small) (d:<kitam> be broken, with <nen>, into small pieces) (s:kizangawp) (q:draft)
kitamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:split/break/shatter) (d:<kitam> be broken, with the causative <sak>: make something break; of the heart, break it with grief) (b:kitam) (q:draft)
kitamta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shattered/be broken) (d:<kitam> be broken, with <ta>, now, marking a changed state) (b:kitam) (q:draft)
kitamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:broken ones/broken pieces) (d:<kitam> be broken with the plural <te>, those that are broken; {lungsim kitamte} are the brokenhearted and {beelpei kitamte} are potsherds) (s:kitamzante) (b:kitam) (q:draft)
kitamvui = (t:see) <kitamvui-sak>
kitamvui-sak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grind to powder/crush fine) (d:cause to be broken into dust; written <kitamvuisak> in the other text) (s:gawivui) (q:draft)
kitamvuisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grind to powder/crush fine) (d:<kitam> be broken, with <vui>, dust, and <sak>, cause: cause to be broken into dust) (s:gawivui) (q:draft)
kitamzan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/be shattered/be crushed) (d:be broken in pieces; of the heart or spirit, broken and contrite, as in {lungsim kitamzan mite}, the brokenhearted) (s:kitam/kisuzan/kitamkham) (q:draft)
kitamzante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:broken ones/shattered ones) (d:<kitamzan> with the plural <te>; {lungsim kitamzante} are the brokenhearted) (s:kitamte) (b:kitamzan) (q:draft)
kitan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/break) (d:of a bone, a bow or other long thing, be snapped in two) (q:draft)
kitang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be opposite/face each other) (d:of two things, stand facing each other or lie opposite, often with {khat leh khat}, one another) (s:kimaituah/kimaingat) (q:draft)
kitang = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be kept/be observed) (d:of a holy day that is kept) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitangawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken in pieces/be shattered) (d:<kitan> be broken, with <gawp>, completely) (b:kitan) (q:draft)
kitangcingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made complete/be filled up) (d:of something still lacking, be brought to its full measure) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitangko = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be proclaimed/be announced) (d:passive of <tangko>, proclaim, with the prefix <ki>: be announced aloud for all to hear) (s:kitaangko/kipulak) (b:tangko) (q:draft)
kitangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made straight/be straightened) (d:passive of <tangsak> make straight, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kimamsak) (b:tangsak) (q:draft)
kitangsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:justify oneself) (d:<tangsak> make straight, with the reflexive prefix <ki>: make oneself out to be in the right) (s:kidiksak) (b:tangsak) (q:draft)
kitangsam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be in need/lack/be needy) (d:be without what one needs; {a kitangsam mite} are the needy, {sum kitangsam} is short of money) (s:tasam/kisam) (a:hauh) (q:draft)
kitangsapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:need/lack/want) (d:the state of lacking what one needs, or the thing that is lacking; {kitangsapna nei lo} is lack nothing) (s:kitaangsapna/kisapna/tangsapna) (a:hauhna) (b:tangsapna) (r:11.11.22) (q:draft)
kitanh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be ransomed/be bought back) (d:passive of <tanh>, redeem, with the prefix <ki>: be bought back or set free by payment; {kitanh kik} is be redeemed again) (s:kitankhia/kitat) (a:kizuak) (b:tanh) (q:draft)
kitanhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be bought back/redeem oneself) (d:<kitanh> be redeemed, with <kik> back, again) (s:kitatkik) (b:kitanh) (q:draft)
kitanhkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:allow to be redeemed/let be bought back) (d:<kitanhkik> be redeemed, with <sak>, cause or allow) (b:kitanhkik) (q:draft)
kitanhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let be redeemed/allow to be ransomed) (d:<kitanh> be redeemed, with <sak>, cause or allow) (b:kitanh) (q:draft)
kitanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being broken off/being cut off/snapping) (d:form of <kitan> with {-in}, followed by the result, as in {kitanin kia}, break off and fall) (b:kitan) (q:draft)
kitankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be ransomed) (d:be bought free by payment; {a kitankhia mite} are the redeemed) (s:kitanh/kitatkhiat) (a:kizuak) (b:tankhia) (q:draft)
kitankhiasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:redeemed/ransomed) (d:<kitankhia> with <sa>, already: that has been redeemed) (s:tatkhiatsa/tatsa/hotkhiatsa) (b:kitankhia) (q:draft)
kitankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cut off) (d:<tan> cut off, with the prefix <ki> and <khiat>, off; of a head, be severed) (b:kitan) (q:draft)
kitankhiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be redeemed/be able to be ransomed) (d:<kitankhia> be redeemed, with <zo>, be able) (b:kitankhia) (q:draft)
kitanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being cut off/being broken off) (d:<kitan> be broken or cut off with the noun suffix <na>; {lu kitanna} is beheading) (b:kitan) (q:draft)
kitansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:broken) (d:<kitan> be broken, with <sa> marking a completed state: already broken, said of an arm or a bone) (s:kikuaitansa) (b:kitan) (q:draft)
kitansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/cut/cut off) (d:<kitan>, be broken or cut off, with <sak>, cause: make something break; of a navel cord, have it cut) (s:kuaitan) (b:kitan) (q:draft)
kitante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:broken ones/those broken off) (d:<kitan> with plural <te>; {a hiang kitante} are its broken branches) (b:kitan) (q:draft)
kitap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be torn down/be broken down) (d:in {kitap zan}, be broken to pieces) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitapkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break apart/break up) (d:of a ship, come apart) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitapkhapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gap/breach) (d:a place left empty where one part of a whole is missing, as one tribe out of the twelve) (q:draft)
kitapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:discouragement/brokenness) (d:{lungsim kitapna} is a broken spirit, discouragement) (s:lungkiatna/kitapzanna) (b:kitap) (q:draft)
kitapzanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:breaking down/brokenness) (d:being broken in pieces or torn down; {lungsim kitapzanna} is a broken spirit, discouragement) (s:kitapna/lungkiatna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitasam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lacking/be in want/be missing/fail) (d:of food, water or goods: run short, not be there when needed; usually with <lo>, not be lacking) (s:kisam) (r:20.31.11) (q:draft)
kitat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sharpened/be whetted) (d:of a blade; {kitat hiam}, sharpened to an edge) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be cut off/snap/be severed) (d:of a cord or thread) (b:tat) (q:draft)
kitat = (i:3) (t:v) (w:be redeemed/redeem oneself/be ransomed) (d:<tat>, redeem, with the prefix <ki>: be bought back, or buy oneself free) (s:kitanh/kitankhia/kitatkhiat) (b:tat) (q:draft)
kitatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be severed/snap/break) (d:of a cord or rope, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kitat) (q:draft)
kitatin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:strike against/hit) (d:knock a part of the body against something hard) (s:kitahkhak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitatkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be redeemed/redeem oneself) (d:<tatkhiat>, redeem, with the prefix <ki>: be bought free or buy oneself free; the form found before <nading> and <kei>) (s:kitanh/kitankhia) (b:tatkhiat) (q:draft)
kitatkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:redemption/ransom) (d:<kitatkhiat>, be redeemed, with the noun suffix <na>: redemption, or the price paid; {kitatkhiatna sum} is redemption money) (s:kitatna/tatkhiatna/tatna) (b:kitatkhiat) (q:draft)
kitatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be bought back) (d:passive of <tatkik> with the prefix <ki>) (s:kitanhkik) (b:tatkik) (q:draft)
kitatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:redemption/ransom) (d:the buying back of a person or thing; {kitatna man} is the redemption price and {kitatna sum} is redemption money) (s:kitatkhiatna/tatkhiatna/tatna) (b:kitat) (q:draft)
kitatsat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be interrupted/be broken off/cease) (d:in the verses always with <lo>, not: {kitatsat lo}, unbroken, regular, continual) (b:tatsat) (q:draft)
kitawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kindled/be lit) (d:of fire or anger, be set alight; {kitawh kuang} is be kindled and burn) (s:kitawhkuang) (a:kimitsak) (b:tawh) (r:24.17.4) (q:draft)
kitawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be dug/be dug out/be quarried) (d:of a pit, be dug; {kitawh khiatna} is the place something is dug out from, a mine or quarry) (q:draft)
kitawhkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quarry/place of digging out) (d:<tawh> dig, with the prefix <ki>, <khiat>, out, and the noun suffix <na>: being dug out, or the pit from which something is dug) (s:kitawhna) (q:draft)
kitawhkuang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kindled/blaze up/burn) (d:catch fire and blaze, in the verses always of anger) (s:kitawh) (a:kimitsak) (b:tawhkuang) (q:draft)
kitawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quarry/place of quarrying) (d:<kitawh> be dug or quarried, with the noun ending <na>: the place where stone is dug out) (s:kitawhkhiatna/suangkhuk) (b:kitawh) (q:draft)
kitawhnawina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:confusion/turmoil/panic) (d:a state in which people strike at one another in disorder) (s:buaina/patauhna) (q:draft)
kitawhzauna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:confusion/panic/terror) (d:named with <buaina>, tumult, and {tuatcil gawpna}, trampling, as what comes on a day of disaster) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be held/be carried/be brought) (d:passive of <tawi>, hold or carry) (b:tawi) (q:draft)
kitawi = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be armed/be equipped) (d:bearing weapons, ready for battle) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitawikhai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be weighed) (d:be weighed on scales, passive of <tawikhai>) (s:kitawiteh) (b:tawikhai) (q:draft)
kitawiteh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be weighed/be put on the scales) (d:<tawi> lift or weigh and <teh> measure, with the passive prefix <ki>) (s:kitawikhai) (q:draft)
kitawito = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised up/be elevated/be held high) (d:be built up or lifted higher than what is around, said of a base, a terrace or the head) (b:kitawi) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitawldamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:refresh oneself/rest) (d:<tawldamsak> refresh, with the reflexive prefix <ki>) (s:tawlnga) (b:tawldamsak) (q:draft)
kitawlnga = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stop/come to a halt/be rested) (d:<tawlnga> rest, with the prefix <ki>; of work, be left to stop) (b:tawlnga) (q:draft)
kitawng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quarrel/strive/fight) (d:dispute or fight with one another, in words or with blows) (s:kitot/kido) (a:kilem) (q:draft)
kitawngin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fighting/quarrelling) (d:<kitawng> quarrel, fight, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kitawng) (q:draft)
kitawngpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:begin to quarrel at once/fall into dispute) (d:<kitawng> quarrel, with <pah>, at once) (q:draft)
kitawngsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set against each other/cause to quarrel/stir up strife) (d:<kitawng>, quarrel, with <sak>, cause) (s:kidosak) (b:kitawng) (q:draft)
Kitawngtawng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep quarrelling/quarrel) (d:<kitawng> quarrel with the last syllable repeated, go on quarrelling with one another; {kitawngtawng kawm} is in the midst of quarrelling, where the NIV has with hatred) (q:draft)
kitawphah = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:rocky) (d:used with <suang> stone, {suang kitawphah leilak} is rocky ground, where rock lies under a thin layer of soil) (b:tawphah) (q:draft)
kitawphahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rocky ground/rocky place) (d:<kitawphah> with the noun ending <na>; {suang kitawphahna} is a place where rock lies under a thin layer of soil) (b:kitawphah) (q:draft)
kitawpsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stopped/be brought to an end/be stilled) (d:passive of <tawpsak> with the prefix <ki>) (s:kikhawlsak) (b:tawpsak) (q:draft)
kite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:horns) (d:plural of <ki>; in these verses the horns of the altar) (b:ki) (q:draft)
kiteel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be chosen/be elected) (d:<teel>, choose, with the passive prefix <ki>; {a kiteel mite} are the chosen, the elect) (s:kiteelkhia) (b:teel) (r:55.2.10) (q:draft)
kiteelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being chosen/being selected) (d:<kiteel> be chosen, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kiteel) (q:draft)
kiteelkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be chosen/be selected) (d:be picked out from among others, also placed before a noun, chosen) (s:kiteel) (b:kiteel) (r:66.17.14) (q:draft)
kiteelsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:chosen/elect) (d:<kiteel>, be chosen, with <sa>, already: one that has been chosen; {a kiteelsa kimkhat} is a chosen remnant) (s:teelsa) (b:kiteel) (q:draft)
kiteelte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those chosen/the chosen ones) (d:<kiteel>, be chosen, with the plural <te>: the people who were chosen) (b:kiteel) (q:draft)
kiteelteel = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:choice/select/carefully chosen) (d:<kiteel> be chosen, with <teel> said twice: picked out with care, the best) (s:kitengkhia) (q:draft)
kiteen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marry/be married) (d:short form of <kiteeng>, written with an apostrophe before a suffix or a following word: {kiteen’na}, marriage, {kiteen’sak}, give in marriage) (s:kipi) (b:teen) (r:42.20.34) (q:draft)
kiteen = (i:2) (t:v) (w:dwell/be lived in) (d:in {kiteen’na mun}, a place that is lived in, an abode) (b:teen) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiteeng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marry/be married) (d:of a man and a woman, come to live together as husband and wife; with <tawh>, marry someone) (s:kiteng/kipi) (b:teeng) (q:draft)
kiteengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marrying/marry) (d:<kiteeng> with the linking ending <in>: marrying, and; {kipi kiteengin} is marrying and being given in marriage) (b:kiteeng) (q:draft)
kiteengsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give in marriage/marry off/let marry) (d:<kiteeng> with causative <sak>: cause or allow two people to marry, give a daughter in marriage) (s:kitengsak) (b:kiteeng) (q:draft)
kiteengsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:giving in marriage/give in marriage) (d:<kiteengsak> with the linking ending <in>; {kipi kiteengsakin} is marrying and giving in marriage) (b:kiteengsak) (q:draft)
kiteengte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who marry) (d:<kiteeng> with plural <te>; with <tawh>, those who marry someone) (s:tenpihte) (b:kiteeng) (q:draft)
kiteenkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be snatched out/be pulled out/be plucked out) (d:said of a burning stick taken out of the fire; ends in <khia>, out) (s:kitenkhia) (q:draft)
kiteepsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be suckled/be nursed/be given to suck) (d:passive of <teepsak>, give suck, with the prefix <ki>) (b:teepsak) (q:draft)
kiteeptumlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the fact of being sucked dry, of having one's strength drained; <teeptum> with the prefix <ki> and <lam>) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiteh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be measured) (d:<teh>, measure, with the passive prefix <ki>; {kiteh zo lo} is too much to be measured or weighed) (b:teh) (q:draft)
kiteh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be compared/compare with/be equal to) (d:with <tawh>, be set beside another as a match; {kiteh theih loh} is without equal) (s:kibatpih) (b:teh) (q:draft)
kitehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comparing/measuring against) (d:<kiteh> be compared, with <in> linking to the next verb; with {khat leh khat}, comparing themselves with one another) (b:kiteh) (q:draft)
kitehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:measure/limit/measuring) (d:<kiteh> be measured, with the noun suffix <na>: the measure marked out for someone; {kitehna khau} is a measuring line) (s:tehna) (b:kiteh) (q:draft)
kitehthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be compared/be comparable) (d:<kiteh> be compared, with <thei>, can; with <tawh>, be comparable to someone) (b:kiteh) (q:draft)
kitei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be poured over/be transferred) (d:of wine, be poured from one jar into another) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitel = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:clearly/plainly) (d:with <takin>, {kitel takin}, in a way that is clear to understand) (s:teltakin/kiteltakin/kitelin) (b:tel) (q:draft)
kitel = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be clear/be evident/be verified) (d:of a matter or a statement, become clear or be shown to be so) (s:kitelpha/kitelsiang) (b:tel) (r:46.15.27) (q:draft)
kiteldot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:examine oneself) (d:<teldot> examine, with the reflexive prefix <ki>) (s:kisittel/ki-enpha) (b:teldot) (q:draft)
kitelin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:clearly/distinctly/plainly) (d:<kitel>, be clear, with the adverb ending <in>: in a way that is easy to hear or understand) (s:teltakin/kiteltakin/telin) (b:kitel) (q:draft)
kitello = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:unclear/unintelligible/obscure) (d:<kitel> be clear, with <lo>, not) (s:theihhak) (a:kiteltak) (b:kitel) (q:draft)
kitelpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be clear/become plain) (d:<kitel> be clear, with <pha>, well; with <semsem>, become clearer still) (s:kitel/kitelsiang) (q:draft)
kitelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make clear/reveal/make known) (d:<kitel>, be clear, with the causative <sak>: make a matter clear, show it plainly) (s:kilangsak/langsak/theisak) (b:kitel) (q:draft)
kitelsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be clear/be clearly understood) (d:<kitel> be clear, with <siang>, clean, clear) (s:kitel/kitelpha) (b:kitel) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiteltak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:definite/clear/certain) (d:<kitel>, be clear, with <tak>, truly: clear and certain; {thu a kiteltak} is definite information) (a:kitello) (b:kitel) (q:draft)
kiteltakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:plainly/clearly) (d:<kiteltak> clear, with the adverb ending <in>) (s:teltakin/kitelin) (b:kiteltak) (q:draft)
kiten = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marry/be married/intermarry) (d:form of <kiteng> written {kiten’} before <leh>, <ma>, <na> and other endings) (s:kipi) (b:ten) (q:draft)
kiten = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be settled/be inhabited) (d:passive of <ten>, dwell: of land, be lived in) (b:ten) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kiten = (t:see) <Kiten'pih>
Kiten'pih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:married/be married to) (d:<kiteng> marry with <pih> together with; here given as a name for the land, NIV Beulah) (q:draft)
kiteng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marry/intermarry/be married) (d:with <tawh>, marry someone; from <teng> live, live together as husband and wife) (s:kiteeng/kipi) (b:teng) (q:draft)
kitengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:intermarrying/marrying) (d:<kiteng> marry with the linking ending <in>, used with <tawh>, with) (b:kiteng) (q:draft)
kitengkhia = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:chosen/select/picked/best) (d:picked out from the rest, said of the best troops, chariots or officers) (s:kiteelteel/teelsa) (r:14.13.17) (q:draft)
kitengsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give in marriage/marry off/be given in marriage) (d:cause two people to marry; with <tawh> for the partner) (s:kiteengsak) (b:kiteng) (q:draft)
kitengthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can marry/be free to marry) (d:<kiteng> marry, with <thei> can) (b:kiteng) (q:draft)
kitenkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be snatched out/be pulled out) (d:be taken out of something, said of a stick out of the fire; <khia> is out) (s:kiteenkhia) (q:draft)
kitenpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be married/be taken as wife) (d:passive of <tenpih> with the prefix <ki>; {a kitenpih numei} is a married woman, one who has a husband) (s:pasalnei) (a:kinusia) (b:tenpih) (q:draft)
Kitenpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:married/be married to) (d:<kiteng> marry with <pih> together with; here given as a name for the land, NIV Beulah) (b:kitenpih) (q:draft)
kitep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sapped/be drained) (d:<tep> sap or suck up, with the passive prefix <ki>) (b:tep) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be scattered/be strewn/lie spread) (d:said of dung lying spread on the ground, as a picture of unburied bodies) (s:kithehzak/kipaaithang/kipaithang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithadimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:refresh oneself) (d:<thadimsak> refresh or strengthen, with the reflexive prefix <ki>) (s:kitawldamsak) (b:thadimsak) (q:draft)
kithah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kill/be killed) (d:<thah>, kill, with the prefix <ki>; the form of <kithat> used before <bangin>, <nading>, <hun>, {lai takin} and similar words, where it mostly means be killed) (b:thah)
kithah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:murder) (b:thah)
kithahlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the fact or manner of someone being killed; <kithah> be killed, with <lam> way or fact) (q:draft)
kithahlup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be slaughtered/be killed/be cut down) (d:<thahlup>, slaughter, with the passive prefix <ki>: of many people, be killed and laid low) (s:kithatlum/kisatlum) (b:thahlup) (q:draft)
kithahlupna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:slaughter/slaying) (d:<kithahlup> with the noun ending <na>: the killing of many people) (s:kithahna/kihonthahna) (b:kithahlup) (q:draft)
kithahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:killing/bloodshed/murder/slaughter) (d:<kithah>, be killed, with the noun suffix <na>: the killing of people, bloodshed; before <leitang> or <mun> it names the place where someone was killed) (s:thahna/mithahna/kithahlupna) (b:kithah) (r:26.24.7) (q:draft)
kithahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make kill each other/cause to kill one another) (d:<kithah> kill one another, with the causative <sak>) (b:kithah) (q:draft)
kithakhauhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strengthen oneself/find strength) (d:reflexive of <thakhauhsak>: make oneself strong, take courage) (s:kihatsak) (b:thakhauhsak) (q:draft)
kithakhauhsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strengthen oneself/be strong) (d:<kithakhauhsak> with the linking ending <in>: making oneself strong, and) (b:kithakhauhsak) (q:draft)
kithakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be passed out/be expelled/go out) (d:of food that was eaten, pass out of the body from the stomach; ends in <khia>, out) (q:draft)
kithallot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be brought down/stumble) (d:said of the wicked who meet disaster and do not rise again, set against the good who fall and get up) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithamuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boldness/confidence) (d:trust in one's own strength; {kithamuanna tawh} is boldly) (s:ngamna/hanna) (a:launa) (q:draft)
kithang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be reported/be widely known/spread) (d:of fame or news, be heard of everywhere) (s:kizel) (q:draft)
kithangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be exalted/be made famous/be glorified) (d:of God or his name, be made great and known everywhere) (s:kisangsak/kiminthangsak/kipahtawi) (b:thangsak) (q:draft)
kithat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be killed/be put to death/be slain) (d:passive of <that>, kill) (s:kithatlum/kisatlum) (b:that) (q:draft)
kithatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be killed/be slain) (d:<kithat> with the linking ending <in>: being killed, followed by a further verb such as <puk> or <tuk> fall) (b:kithat) (q:draft)
kithatlum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be slain/be killed/be slaughtered) (d:passive of <thatlum>, kill outright) (s:kithat/kithahlup/kisatlum) (b:thatlum) (q:draft)
kithatlumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let be slain/cause to be killed) (d:<kithatlum> be killed, with the causative <sak>) (b:kithatlum) (q:draft)
kithatnu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the woman who was killed/slain woman) (d:<kithat> be killed, with <nu> marking a woman) (b:kithat) (q:draft)
kithatpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the man who was killed) (d:<kithat> be killed, with <pa> marking a man) (b:kithat) (q:draft)
kithatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:slain/killed) (d:<kithat> with <sa>, already done: one that has been killed) (s:thahsa) (a:hing) (b:kithat) (q:draft)
kithattawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kill oneself) (d:<that> kill, with the prefix <ki> and <tawm>, by oneself) (q:draft)
kithatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the slain/those killed) (d:<kithat>, be killed, with the plural <te> used as a noun: people who have been killed) (s:thahte/site) (a:hingte) (b:kithat) (q:draft)
kithausak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fatten oneself) (d:<thau> fat, with the reflexive prefix <ki> and the causative <sak>) (q:draft)
kithausakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fattening oneself) (d:<kithausak> fatten oneself, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kithausak) (q:draft)
kithausakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fattening of oneself) (d:<kithausak> fatten oneself, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kithausak) (q:draft)
kithawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised/rise) (d:<thawh> rise, with the prefix <ki>; found in {kithawh kiksak}, be raised up again, of rising from the dead) (b:thawh) (q:draft)
kithawhkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised from the dead/be resurrected) (d:passive {ki-} form of <thawhkiksak>, raise up again) (s:kithokiksak/kihingkiksak) (a:kiphum) (b:thawhkiksak) (q:draft)
kithawhthawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stirred up/be roused) (d:be set in motion, said of nations and kings rising for war) (s:kithawithawi/kihanthawn) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prepare/get ready/make ready) (d:get oneself ready for something, often for war; after a verb with <dingin> it means be about to, as in {puk dingin ka kithawi}, I am about to fall) (s:kiging/kigalging/kigingkhol) (r:19.38.17) (q:draft)
kithawina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:readiness/being about to) (d:<kithawi> get ready with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being ready or about to do something) (b:kithawi) (q:draft)
