kithawisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make ready/get ready/prepare) (d:<kithawi> with causative <sak>: have people or things made ready, of a chariot hitch up) (b:kithawi) (q:draft)
kithawisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making ready/having made ready) (d:<kithawisak> make ready, with the linking ending <in>; of a chariot, having it made ready) (b:kithawisak) (q:draft)
kithawithawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be making ready/be preparing/be astir) (d:<kithawi> get ready, with <thawi> doubled to show that the action goes on; said of a nation preparing for war) (s:kithawhthawi) (q:draft)
kithawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:resound/ring out) (d:<thawn> with the prefix <ki>: of a sound, ring out as far as a place) (b:thawn) (q:draft)
kitheh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sprinkled/be spattered/be splashed) (d:<theh>, sprinkle, with the passive prefix <ki>: of blood or water, be sprinkled or splashed on something; {kitheh kha} is be spattered onto) (s:kibuak) (b:theh) (q:draft)
kithehgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spattered/be splashed all over) (d:<kitheh> be sprinkled or spattered, with the intensifier <gawp>) (b:kitheh) (q:draft)
kithehkek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spilled out/be scattered about) (d:burst and scatter, said of intestines) (q:draft)
kithehkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spattered on) (d:be splashed onto something, said of blood on a garment) (q:draft)
kithehkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spattered on) (d:form of <kithehkha> used before <ciangin>) (b:kithehkha) (q:draft)
kithehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sprinkling/application) (d:<kitheh> be sprinkled with the noun suffix <na>: the sprinkling of blood) (s:thehna) (b:kitheh) (q:draft)
kithehthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be scattered/scatter/be dispersed) (d:<thehthang>, scatter, with the prefix <ki>: of people, animals or things, be scattered in all directions) (s:kikhenthang/kizelthang/kithehzak) (a:kikaikhawm/kikaihkhop) (b:thehthang) (q:draft)
kithehthangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being scattered/scattered) (d:form of <kithehthang> with {-in}, linking to what follows) (a:kikaikhawmin) (b:kithehthang) (q:draft)
kithehthangna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scattering/dispersion/place of scattering) (d:<kithehthang> with {-na}; before <mun>, <gam> or <minamte> it means where they were scattered) (s:thehthangna) (a:kikaihkhopna) (b:kithehthang) (q:draft)
kithehthangsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:scattered/dispersed) (d:<kithehthang> be scattered with <sa>, already done: that have been scattered) (b:kithehthang) (q:draft)
kithehthangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scatter/disperse/cause to scatter) (d:<kithehthang>, be scattered, with the causative <sak>: make people or animals scatter, drive them apart) (s:thehthang/khenthang) (a:kaikhawm) (b:kithehthang) (q:draft)
kithehthangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scattered ones/those who are scattered) (d:<kithehthang> be scattered with the plural <te>) (b:kithehthang) (q:draft)
kithehzak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be scattered/be strewn) (d:be scattered about over an area, said of dead bodies left lying in the wilderness) (s:kithehthang/kipaithang/kitha) (q:draft)
kithei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:knew/be known) (d:<thei>, know, with the prefix <ki>: be known, or know something about oneself; {kithei lo} is unknown, not noticed) (a:kiseel) (b:thei) (r:1.3.7)
kithei = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be acquainted with) (b:thei)
Kithei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be known) (d:capitalised in an inscription; {A Kithei lo Pasian} is the unknown God) (b:kithei) (q:draft)
kitheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be known/know/be recognized) (d:form of <kithei> used before {kei leh}, <ciangin> and similar endings; {kitheih theihna lungsim} is conscience) (b:kithei) (q:draft)
kitheihmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disown/ignore deliberately) (d:used with <bawl>: act as if not knowing, so deliberately forget a matter or disown a person) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conscience) (d:in {kitheihna lungsim}, one's own inner knowledge of right and wrong) (b:theihna) (r:46.10.25) (q:draft)
kitheihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:sign/token/assurance) (d:something by which a thing is known or made known) (s:theihsakna/limlahna) (b:kitheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make known/reveal/show) (d:<kitheih> be known with the causative <sak>: make something known, as God making his power known) (s:pulak/langsak/kilangsak) (a:seel/im) (b:kitheih) (q:draft)
kitheihsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:making known/revealing) (d:<kitheihsak> make known with the noun suffix <na>: the making known of something; {damlenat kitheihsakna} is asking after how someone is) (s:latsakna) (b:kitheihsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheihtel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be clearly known/be fully known/be proved) (d:<theihtel> know clearly with the passive prefix <ki>: be clearly known or proved, as obedience that has been fully shown) (b:theihtel) (q:draft)
kitheihthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become widely known/spread abroad/be made public) (d:<theihthang> with the passive prefix <ki>: of news or an order, become known everywhere) (s:kizel/kizeel/kizelh) (b:theihthang) (q:draft)
kitheihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be known/be knowable) (d:<kitheih> be known with <theih> can: able to be known; {a kitheihtheih nading} is the means by which something can be known) (b:kitheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be found out/be comprehended/be understood) (d:<kithei> be known with <khia> out: be found out or fully understood; with {zo lo}, cannot be found out) (s:kimukhia) (b:kithei) (q:draft)
kitheikim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be known to all/be well known/be seen by all) (d:<theikim> know by all with the passive prefix <ki>: be known or seen by everyone) (b:theikim) (q:draft)
kitheisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make known/proclaim/reveal) (d:<theisak> make known with the prefix <ki>: make something known among people; with a person as subject and no object, make oneself known) (s:pulak/langsak/kilangsak/taangko) (a:seel/im) (b:theisak) (q:draft)
kitheisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made known/be proclaimed) (d:<kitheisak> make known with the linking ending <in>: being made known to people, and then the next action follows) (b:kitheisak) (q:draft)
kitheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are known/those well known) (d:<kithei> be known with the plural <te>: people who are known for something, as for good deeds) (b:kithei) (q:draft)
kitheithang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become known/spread/be heard everywhere) (d:of news or a matter, be heard about everywhere) (s:kizel/kizeel/kizelh) (b:theithang) (q:draft)
kitheithangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make known/announce/reveal) (d:<kitheithang> become known with the causative <sak>: make something known openly) (s:pulak/langsak/taangko/kitheisak) (a:seel) (b:kitheithang) (q:draft)
kithoihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sacrifice/offering) (d:an animal sacrifice of which the meat is eaten, named beside {meihal biakna}, burnt offering; {kithoihna bawl} is make a sacrifice) (s:biakpiakna/biakna) (q:draft)
kithoihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sacrifices/offerings) (d:<kithoihna> sacrifice, with the plural <te>) (s:biakpiaknate/thoihnate/biaknate) (b:kithoihna) (q:draft)
kithokiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised to life/be raised from the dead) (d:<thokiksak> raise again with the passive prefix <ki>: be raised again from death) (s:kithawhkiksak/kihingkiksak/kithosak) (b:thokiksak) (q:draft)
kithosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised up/be raised to life) (d:<thosak> raise with the passive prefix <ki>: be raised to life from death, often after {sihna panin}, from death) (s:kithokiksak/kithawhkiksak/kihingkiksak) (b:thosak) (q:draft)
kithu = (i:1) (t:v) (d:found in {kithu tuak}, written apart for <kithutuak>: be of one mind, be in agreement; <thu> word or matter with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (b:thu) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be attached/be fitted with/be joined) (d:of a thing that has another thing fastened to it, <tawh> marks what is attached) (s:kizom) (b:thuah) (q:draft)
kithuah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:accompany/keep company with/go with/join) (d:of people, be together with someone, <tawh> marks the companion) (s:kikhawl/tonpih/kipawl) (b:thuah) (q:draft)
kithuahkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:join/associate with/keep company with) (d:<kithuah> be together with, with <kha> happen to: fall into the company of someone; with {kei in}, do not join them) (s:kikhawl) (q:draft)
kithuahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:accompany/be a companion of) (d:<kithuah> keep company with the ending <pih>, do together with: {a kithuahpih nungakte} are the young women who accompany her) (s:tonpih/kikhawl) (b:kithuah) (r:19.45.13) (q:draft)
kithuahpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:companions/associates) (d:<kithuahpih> accompany with the plural <te>: the people who keep company with someone) (s:lawmte/kikholhpihte/tonpihte) (a:galte) (b:kithuahpih) (q:draft)
kithuahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send along with/cause to accompany) (d:<kithuah> be together with, with the causative <sak>) (s:tonsak/zuisak) (b:kithuah) (q:draft)
kithuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear with one another/be suffered/be endured) (d:<thuak> bear, endure, with the prefix <ki>: put up with each other; {kithuak bawlsiatna} is the persecution being suffered) (b:thuak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bearing with one another) (d:<kithuak> bear with each other, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kithuak) (q:draft)
kithuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to suffer/be afflicted) (d:<thuaksak> make suffer with the passive prefix <ki>: be made to suffer; {gimna hong kithuaksak} is suffering is laid on me) (b:thuaksak) (q:draft)
kithuaksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made to bear/be made to suffer) (d:<kithuaksak> with the linking ending <in>: {maizumna kithuaksakin} is being made to bear shame) (b:kithuaksak) (q:draft)
kithuakzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:endurance/forbearance/patience) (d:ability to bear with one another; <thuakzawhna> endurance, with the prefix <ki>) (s:lungduaina) (b:thuakzawhna) (q:draft)
kithuap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be laid one on another/overlap/be joined together) (d:<thuap> layer with the prefix <ki>: of scales or shields, lie one upon another; of two things, stand together) (b:thuap) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithuapcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined tightly/be close together) (d:<kithuap> with <cip>, tightly: lie one upon another with no gap) (b:kithuap) (q:draft)
kithuapin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:one upon another/laid on top of each other) (d:<kithuap> with the linking ending <in>: of building stones, lying one upon another) (b:kithuap) (r:40.24.2) (q:draft)
kithuapna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the state of lying one upon another; <kithuap> be stacked on each other, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kithuap) (q:draft)
kithuapsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overlap downward/be layered) (d:<kithuap> lie one upon another, with <suk> downward; said of scales) (b:kithuap) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sealed/be stamped) (d:passive of <thuh>: be marked with a seal or signet ring) (b:thuh) (q:draft)
kithuhilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disciplined/be corrected/be instructed) (d:<thuhilh> discipline with the passive prefix <ki>: receive teaching or correction; {kithuhilh ding ut} is to love discipline) (s:kitai) (b:thuhilh) (q:draft)
kithuhilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:correction/instruction/discipline) (d:advice or rebuke given to put a person right) (s:kihilhna/taiina/thuhilhna) (b:kithuhilh) (q:draft)
kithuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:revenge/be avenged/be paid back) (d:<thuk> repay with the prefix <ki>: vengeance is taken or a deed is paid back, on someone or to one another) (s:kithukkik) (a:maisak) (b:thuk)
kithuk = (i:2) (t:n) (w:retaliation) (d:the paying back of a wrong that was done) (s:thuhkikna/thukkikna) (b:thuk)
kithukhat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:conspire/plot together/be of one mind) (d:{thu khat} one matter with <ki>, agree together on one plan, in these verses against someone) (s:kilungtuak/kithutuak) (b:thukhat) (q:draft)
kithukhatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in unity/being of one mind) (d:<kithukhat> be united, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kikhatin) (b:kithukhat) (q:draft)
kithukim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:agree/agree together) (d:<thukim> agree with the prefix <ki>: of several persons, come to an agreement with each other) (s:kithutuak/kithutuah/kilungtuak) (a:kitot/kinial) (b:thukim) (q:draft)
kithukimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:agreement/terms) (d:<kithukim> agree together with the noun suffix <na>: what has been agreed, the terms of a deed) (s:thukimna) (b:kithukim) (q:draft)
kithukkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get revenge/be avenged/be repaid) (d:<thukkik> pay back with the passive prefix <ki>: be avenged, or be paid back for what one has done, good or evil) (s:kithuk) (b:thukkik)
kithukkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:punishment/recompense/retribution) (d:<kithukkik> with the noun suffix <na>: the being paid back for what one has done) (s:thukkikna/gimpiakna) (b:kithukkik) (q:draft)
kithukkim = (i:1) (t:v) (d:in {a kithukkim dingin}, said of a punishment given; perhaps be repaid in equal measure or settle the matter, meaning not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put into/be poured into/be brought in) (d:passive of <thun> put in: be put or poured into a container, as wine into a skin; also of a new thing being brought in) (b:thun) (q:draft)
kithuneihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dispute/case/lawsuit) (d:a matter that people have against each other; {thu neih} have a case, with the prefix <ki> and the noun suffix <na>) (s:kineihna/kinialna/kiselna) (q:draft)
kithuneihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disputes/cases) (d:<kithuneihna> dispute with the plural <te>: the cases people have against one another) (s:kineihnate/kinialnate/kiselnate) (b:kithuneihna) (q:draft)
kithupi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:self-important/important/great) (d:<thupi> important with the reflexive prefix <ki>, said of oneself; <kithupi ngaihsut> is think oneself something, {kithupi bawlna} is pomp) (b:thupi) (q:draft)
kithupisim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be honored/be held in honor/be respected) (d:<thupisim> regard as important, with the passive prefix <ki>) (s:kizahtak/kipahtawi) (a:kisimmawh) (b:thupisim) (q:draft)
kithusim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be respected/be regarded) (d:<thusim> be mindful with the prefix <ki>; {kithusim lohna} is the not being respected, being scorned) (s:kizahtak) (b:thusim) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithusimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shown respect/be honored) (d:<kithusim> be respected with <sak>; in the verse negated: the elders are shown no respect) (s:kizahtakbawl) (a:kisimmawh) (b:kithusim) (q:draft)
kithutuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:agree/be in accord) (d:agree with one another about a matter; in the verse negated, {kithutuah lohna}, dissension) (s:kithutuak/kithukim) (a:kitot) (q:draft)
kithutuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:agree/be in agreement/be of one mind) (d:agree with one another about a matter, <thu>; often found with <lo> or <kei>: disagree, be divided) (s:kithukim/kithutuah/kilungtuak) (a:kitot/kinial/kikhenthang) (q:draft)
kithutuakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in agreement/in harmony/with one accord) (d:<kithutuak> agree with the ending <in>: in agreement with one another, all alike) (s:kikhatin) (b:kithutuak) (q:draft)
kito = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dug/be hewn/be cut down) (d:<to> dig with the passive prefix <ki>; {kito suang} is dressed stone and {kito niam} is be levelled low) (s:kikhuak) (a:kivuk) (b:to) (q:draft, low confidence)
kito = (i:2) (t:v) (d:in {kisuk leh kito}, of chariots, rush down and up or jostle one another) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitokgawpsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw into confusion/stir up) (d:<tok> stir up with <gawp>, thoroughly, and the causative <sak>: throw people into confusion) (s:buaisak) (q:draft)
kitoksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:tossed/turned over/winnowed) (d:of fodder, that has been tossed or spread with fork and shovel; likely <tok> stir with <ki> and <sa>, already done) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitoktok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:battle/keep striking one another) (d:<toktok> with the reciprocal prefix <ki>; said of desires at war within the body) (b:toktok) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitolkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall off/slip off/come off) (d:of chains, come loose and drop from the hands) (s:tolhkhia/pulhkhia/kiakhia) (q:draft)
kitom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:writhe/struggle/thrash about) (d:move with jerks, as a trapped bird trying to get free) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitom = (i:2) (t:adj) (d:in {kauphe kitom}, describing a kind of locust that may be eaten, listed beside {kauphe kisau} and {kauphe zol}) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitomin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:writhing/shrinking) (d:<kitom> with the linking ending <in>; said of the land writhing in pain) (b:kitom) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitomlak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be summed up/be summarized) (d:be put in short form) (q:draft)
kitomsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be shortened/be cut short) (d:<tomsak> shorten with the prefix <ki>, said of days) (b:tomsak) (q:draft)
kitomsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (d:said of boys and firewood, <sing>, before <kipuasak> be made to carry; perhaps being made to bundle or load the wood, meaning not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitomtom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kick about/squirm/welter) (d:of a newborn child, lie kicking and struggling) (q:draft)
kitosa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dug/already dug) (d:<kito> be dug with <sa>, already done: wells that had been dug) (s:khuatsa) (b:kito) (q:draft)
kitotam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be levelled/be made low) (d:of mountains and hills, be dug down flat) (s:kizalhtam/kitamkim) (a:kisangsak) (q:draft)
kitotlawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quarrel/dispute/argument) (d:quarrelling over something, in the verse over the law) (s:kitotna/kinialna/kiselna) (q:draft)
kitotnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:quarrels/arguments/strifes) (d:<kitotna> quarrel with the plural <te>) (s:kinialnate/kiselnate/kiseelnate) (b:kitotna) (q:draft)
kitotpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quarrel with/contend with/dispute with) (d:<kitot> quarrel, with <pih>, together with; {kitotpih pa} is the man one has a dispute with, an adversary) (b:kitot) (q:draft)
kitotpihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:adversary/opponent) (d:<kitotpih> contend with, with <pa>, the man: the man one has a quarrel or dispute with) (s:langpa/galpa/langpang) (a:lawmpa) (b:kitotpih) (q:draft)
Kitron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kitron) (d:town in the territory of Zebulun whose Canaanite inhabitants were not driven out) (r:7.1.30)
Kittim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kittim/Kittites/Cyprus) (d:son of Javan and grandson of Japheth; also the people descended from him and their land, Cyprus) (r:1.10.4)
kituah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet/meet with/encounter) (d:come together with someone, used with <tawh>) (s:kimu/kituak) (b:tuah) (q:draft)
kituah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:meet/join/fit together) (d:of two parts: meet and close on each other) (s:kizom) (b:tuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
kituahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:face to face) (d:in {maitang kituahin} or {mai kituahin}, with faces meeting; <kituah> meet with the suffix <in>) (b:kituah) (q:draft)
kituahin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:meeting/meet together) (d:<kituah> meet with the linking suffix <in>: meeting, coming together, and then) (b:kituah) (q:draft)
kituahkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:coincide/happen to meet) (d:fall together, said of two days; <tuahkhak> with the reciprocal prefix <ki>) (b:tuahkhak) (q:draft)
kituahmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be plundered/be carried off) (d:of goods and treasure, be seized and taken away) (b:tuahmang) (q:draft, low confidence)
kituahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:meeting/meeting place/junction) (d:the meeting of persons or things, with <mun> the place where they meet) (b:kituah) (q:draft)
kituahnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:meeting places/squares/junctions) (d:<kituahna> meeting place with the plural <te>; {lampi kituahnate} are the places where streets meet, the public squares) (b:kituahna) (q:draft)
kituahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet/come upon) (d:<kituah> meet with the ending <pih>: meet with someone or something on the way) (s:kimu) (b:kituah) (q:draft)
kituahpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those met with) (d:the people one happens to meet; <kituahpih> with the plural <te>) (b:kituahpih) (q:draft)
kituak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:go well with/be compatible/be fitting/be suitable) (d:be right or suitable for someone or something; <tawh> marks what it fits)
kituaka = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fitting/proper/right) (d:<kituak> be fitting, with the linking ending <a>) (s:kilawm/akilawm) (b:kituak) (q:draft)
kituakin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:according to/in accordance with/in keeping with) (d:placed after <tawh>; <kituak> with the suffix <in>) (b:kituak) (q:draft)
kituakin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:fittingly/rightly/aptly) (d:<kituak> be fitting with the ending <in>: in a way that fits, rightly; {a kituakin a gen} is spoke rightly) (s:kilawmin) (b:kituak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kituakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the man who met with) (d:the man who encountered something, in the verse robbers; <kituak> meet, with <pa> marking a man) (b:kituak) (q:draft)
kituaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make agree/bring into harmony) (d:<kituak> agree or match, with the causative <sak>) (b:kituak) (q:draft)
kituakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those that agree/things in accord) (d:<kituak> match, agree with, with the plural <te>: the things that agree with something) (b:kituak) (q:draft)
kituakzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fitting measure) (d:the amount that is fitting for someone; <kituak> be fitting, with <zah> amount) (q:draft)
kituam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wrap oneself/cover oneself/be covered) (d:<tuam> cover with the prefix <ki>: wrap or cover oneself, or be covered with something; {kituam nading} is a covering) (s:kikhuh) (b:tuam) (q:draft)
kituamcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be wrapped up/be covered completely) (d:<tuamcip> cover completely with the prefix <ki>: be wrapped in something as in a cloak) (b:tuamcip) (q:draft)
kituamcipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be covered over/have covered) (d:<kituamcip> be wrapped up tight, with <sak>; said of sin) (b:kituamcip) (q:draft)
kituamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being wrapped/wrapped) (d:{Kituam}, be wrapped, with the linking ending <in>: being wrapped, as the hands and feet of a dead body in strips of cloth.) (s:kitunin) (b:kituam) (q:draft)
kituamkoih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be set apart/be set aside) (d:Passive of <tuamkoih>, set apart, with the prefix <ki>: be kept separate from the rest, as a share of land set aside for the Lord, or people who hold themselves apart from others.) (s:kisehkhia) (b:tuamkoih) (q:draft)
kituamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:covering/cloak/veil) (d:{Kituam}, wrap oneself, with the noun suffix <na>: the cloth a person wraps or covers himself with, such as a cloak or a veil; {kituamna puan} is a garment wrapped around the body.) (s:kikhuhna) (b:kituam) (q:draft)
kituancil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be trampled/be trodden underfoot) (d:Passive of <tuancil>, trample, with the prefix <ki>: be trodden down under the feet, said of a vineyard, a crown, the sanctuary or grass.) (s:kisikcip) (b:tuancil) (q:draft)
kituangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being mounted/being made to ride) (d:{Tuangsakin}, making someone ride, with the passive prefix <ki>: couriers being put on horses, after which the next action follows.) (b:tuangsakin) (q:draft)
kituh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sown/be planted) (d:Passive of <tuh>, sow, with the prefix <ki>: of seed, be put into the ground; {khaici kituh} is seed is sown, and {a kituh} is what has been sown.) (s:kivawh/kisuan) (b:tuh) (q:draft)
kituh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:contend/compete/dispute/strive) (d:Strive against one another for something, as for a throne or in a case at law, or strive to be the first to do something.) (s:kidem/kitot/kinial) (q:draft)
kituhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disputing over/contending for) (d:{Kituh}, contend, with the linking ending <in>: disputing over something, which stands before the word.) (b:kituh) (q:draft)
kituhin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:being sown/being planted) (d:{Kituh}, be sown, with the linking ending <in>: of a grain, being put into the ground before something else happens.) (b:kituh) (q:draft)
kituhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sown again) (d:{Kituh}, be sown, with <kik>, again: of seed, be sown once more in land that lay waste.) (b:kituh) (q:draft)
kituhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dispute/contention/lawsuit) (d:{Kituh}, contend, with the noun suffix <na>: a dispute between people; {thu kituhna} is a dispute over a matter, a case at law.) (s:kinialna/kiselna) (b:kituh) (q:draft)
kituhnate = (t:see) <kituhnate-ah>
kituhnate-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in disputes/in arguments) (d:{Kituhnate}, disputes, with the place ending <ah>: in matters that people contend over.) (q:draft)
kituhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things sown/seeds sown) (d:{Kituh}, be sown, with the plural <te>: the things that were sown; {khai kituhte} are the seeds that were sown.) (b:kituh) (q:draft)
kituhteh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:press in/strive eagerly for/force a way in) (d:Of many people, struggle eagerly to get hold of something or to get into it; probably <kituh>, contend, with an intensifying ending.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kituiphum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:Passive of <tuiphum>, baptize, with the prefix <ki>; literally be immersed in water.) (s:kibaptaiz/kiphum) (b:tuiphum) (q:draft)
kituiphumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:{Kituiphum}, be baptized, with the noun suffix <na>: the baptism that a person receives.) (s:kibaptaizna/tuiphumna/baptaizna) (b:kituiphum) (q:draft)
kituisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be melted) (d:Passive of <tuisak>, melt, with the prefix <ki>: said of metal made liquid in a furnace.) (b:tuisak) (q:draft)
kituk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall/topple/stumble) (d:{Tuk}, fall, with the prefix <ki>: of a person, stumble and fall; of an idol, topple over.) (s:puk) (b:tuk) (q:draft)
kitukalhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:confuse/confound) (d:Mix up the speech or the minds of people so that they no longer understand one another or think clearly.) (q:draft)
kitukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stumbling/cause of stumbling) (d:{Kituk}, stumble, with the noun suffix <na>: stumbling, or the thing that makes people stumble, as a stone in the way.) (b:kituk) (q:draft)
kitum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blown/be sounded/sound) (d:Passive of <tum>, blow, with the prefix <ki>: said of a trumpet or horn, or of the signal given with it.) (s:kimut) (b:tum) (q:draft)
kitumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blowing/blast/sounding) (d:{Kitum}, be blown, with the noun suffix <na>: the sounding of a trumpet.) (s:mutna/tumna) (b:kitum) (q:draft)
kitumpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought in/be led in) (d:Passive of <tumpih>, take in with one, with the prefix <ki>: of people or things, be led or carried into a place.) (s:kilutpih) (b:tumpih) (q:draft)
kitun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be wrapped/be bound up/wrap oneself) (d:Be wrapped in cloth, as a baby in cloths or a dead body in grave clothes; also wrap oneself in something; the cloth takes <tawh> or the ending <in>.) (s:kituam) (q:draft)
kitun = (i:2) (t:v) (w:succeed/be accomplished) (d:Written {kitun’} in the phrase {ma kitun’}, make progress, be brought to success; from <tun>, arrive.) (b:tun) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitung = (i:1) (t:v) (w:arrive/reach) (d:Of a group of people, get as far as a place; <dong>, as far as, follows the place.) (b:tung) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitung = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be laid/be set) (d:Of a noose or snare, be laid on the ground to catch someone.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitung = (i:3) (t:v) (w:rise up) (d:Of a cloud of dust or smoke, rise into the air.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitungsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fulfilled/be carried out) (d:Passive of <tungsak>, bring to pass, with the prefix <ki>: said of vows that are carried out.) (s:tangtung) (b:tungsak) (q:draft)
kitunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being wrapped/wrapped up) (d:{Kitun}, be wrapped, with the linking ending <in>: being wrapped in cloth; the cloth takes <tawh>.) (s:kituamin) (b:kitun) (q:draft)
kitunna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wrapping/grave clothes) (d:{Kitun}, be wrapped, with the noun suffix <na>; {a kitunna puan} is the cloth in which a body was wrapped.) (b:kitun) (q:draft)
kitunpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought/be brought to/be led to) (d:Passive of <tunpih>, bring to a place, with the prefix <ki>: of people or things, be taken to someone or into a place.) (s:kipaipih) (b:tunpih) (q:draft)
kitunsa = (t:see) <kitunsa-in>
kitunsa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wrapped around/bound) (d:{Kitun}, be wrapped, with <sa>, already, and the linking ending <in>: having been wrapped, said of a face bound with a cloth.) (q:draft)
kitunsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let oneself be brought into) (d:{Tunsak}, cause to arrive, with the prefix <ki>; in the verse it is said of idols that a person brings into sin.) (b:tunsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitunzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:succeed/be accomplished) (d:Used in the phrase {maa kitunzo}, be able to reach the goal, succeed; <zo> is be able.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:box/fight with fists) (d:Strike each other with the fists, as boxers do; <tawh> marks the opponent.) (q:draft)
kitut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought/be delivered) (d:Be brought to a place or handed over; {zum kitut} is take one another to court, and {kitut kik} is be brought back or restored.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitutkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be brought back/be restored) (d:{Kitut}, be brought, with <kik>, back: said of a land or people restored after war.) (b:kitut) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:place taken to/place of deportation) (d:{Kitut}, be brought, with the noun suffix <na>; {galmatin a kitutna} is the place to which people were taken as captives.) (b:kitut) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:corner/angle) (d:The point where two sides or edges meet, as of a garment, a building or an altar; {kiu li} is the four corners.) (s:kiukawi) (q:draft)
kiu = (i:2) (t:v) (w:knock) (d:Knock on a door to be let in; <kong> or <kongkhak>, door, stands before the word, and the form <kiuh> is used before <ciangin> and <leh>.) (q:draft)
Kiu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Corner/Angle) (d:{Kiu}, corner, written with a capital in the names of parts of the wall of Jerusalem: {a Kiu} is the Angle, and {Kiu Kongpi} the Corner Gate.) (b:kiu) (q:draft)
kiuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:knock) (d:Form of <kiu>, knock, used before <ciangin>, <leh> and similar words.) (b:kiu) (q:draft)
kiuhkeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:thoroughly/completely/utterly) (d:Intensifier placed after a verb or descriptive word: to the full, altogether; with <lo> it means not at all.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiuhkeuhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:utterly/completely/thoroughly) (d:{Kiuhkeuh}, thoroughly, with the adverb ending <in>: completely, to the full, after a verb of ruin or of flourishing.) (b:kiuhkeuh) (q:draft)
kiukawi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:corner) (d:The corner of a building; {kiukawi bul suang} is the cornerstone.) (s:kiu) (q:draft)
kiukeu = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:rounded/roundly) (d:Used after <uk> to describe a round hollow shape like a bowl or goblet.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiukiau = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sparkling/glittering) (d:Describes the crystal vault above the living creatures; whether it refers to the shine or to the arched shape is not confirmed.) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiukiu = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep knocking/knock) (d:<Kiu>, knock, said twice: knock again and again at a door.) (q:draft)
kiuli = (i:1) (t:n) (w:four corners/four quarters) (d:<Kiu>, corner, with <li>, four: the four corners or quarters; {leitung kiuli} is the four quarters of the earth.) (q:draft)
kiumcih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be besieged/be surrounded/be fortified) (d:Passive of <umcih>, besiege, with the prefix <ki>: be surrounded by an army; {kulhpi tawh a kiumcih khuapi} is a city surrounded with walls, a fortified city.) (s:ki-umcip) (b:umcih) (q:draft)
kiumcihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:siege) (d:{Kiumcih}, be besieged, with the noun suffix <na>: the besieging of a city.) (s:umcihna) (b:kiumcih) (q:draft)
kiute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:corners/angles) (d:<Kiu>, corner, with the plural <te>.) (b:kiu) (r:2.36.28) (q:draft)
kiute = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who knock) (d:<Kiu>, knock, with the plural <te>; {a kiute} are the ones who knock at a door.) (b:kiu) (r:42.11.10) (q:draft)
kivaak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fed/be provided for/get a living/be served) (d:{Vaak}, feed, with the prefix <ki>: feed oneself or be fed and supplied by others; {a kivaak nading} is what one has to live on.) (s:kivak) (b:vaak) (q:draft)
kivaikhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be arranged/be ordered) (d:Passive of <vaikhak>, give an order or send word, with the prefix <ki>: be arranged or ordered beforehand.) (b:vaikhak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:feed oneself/support oneself/live on) (d:Provide food for oneself, make a living; the food takes <in> or <tawh>, live on it, and {kivak nading} is what one has to live on.) (s:kivaak) (q:draft)
kivak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be lit/burn/shine) (d:Passive of <vak>, light, with the prefix <ki>: said of a lamp that is lit and gives light; {kivak suak} is be kept burning.) (s:kuang) (b:vak) (q:draft)
kivakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:feeding/nourished/supporting) (d:{Kivak}, feed oneself, with the linking ending <in>: feeding oneself or others, or being nourished by something, which takes <tawh>.) (b:kivak) (q:draft)
kivakin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:burning/lit/shining) (d:{Kivak}, be lit, with the linking ending <in>: said of lamps that are alight.) (b:kivak) (q:draft)
kivakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:feeding/food supply/provision) (d:{Kivak}, feed, with the noun suffix <na>: the giving out or taking of food, or the place of feeding; {nisim kivakna} is the daily distribution of food.) (s:vaakna/vakna) (b:kivak) (q:draft)
kivaksuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be kept burning/stay alight) (d:{Kivak}, be lit, with <suak>, continue: said of a lamp that keeps giving light.) (q:draft)
kivalh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be swallowed) (d:Passive of <valh>, swallow, with the prefix <ki>; {kivalh tum} is be swallowed up completely.) (b:valh) (q:draft)
kivalhtum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be swallowed up/be destroyed) (d:Passive of <valhtum>, swallow up, with the prefix <ki>: be completely destroyed, said of a king and his people.) (b:valhtum) (q:draft)
kivat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be struck down/be struck) (d:Passive of <vat>, strike, with the prefix <ki>; {kivat tuk} is be struck down and fall.) (s:kisat) (b:vat) (q:draft)
kivattuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be struck down/be cut down) (d:Passive of <vattuk>, strike down, with the prefix <ki>: be cut down in battle.) (s:kisatpuk) (b:vattuk) (q:draft)
kivawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sown/be planted) (d:Passive of <vawh>, sow, with the prefix <ki>: of seed or of a word, be sown; of land, be sown with seed.) (s:kituh/kisuan) (b:vawh) (q:draft)
kivawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be saddled/be loaded/be yoked) (d:Of a donkey, horse or ox, have a saddle, load or yoke put on its back.) (b:vawh) (q:draft)
kivawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being sown) (d:{Kivawh}, be sown, with the linking ending <in>.) (b:kivawh) (q:draft)
kivawhin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:being tied/being fastened) (d:{Kivawh}, have something fastened on, with the linking ending <in>: said of a sheet let down with a rope tied at each corner.) (b:kivawh) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiveei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quake/sway) (d:Said of the earth shaking; another spelling of <kivei>, sway.) (s:kivei/kiliing) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be waved) (d:Be waved to and fro before the Lord, said of the part of a sacrifice presented as a wave offering; {a kivei sa-iik} is the breast that was waved.) (s:kiveii) (r:2.29.27) (q:draft)
kivei = (i:2) (t:v) (w:swing/sway/shake) (d:Move to and fro, said of the earth quaking or of men hanging on ropes; {kivei suk kivei to} is swing down and up.) (s:kiveei/kiliing) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiveii = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be waved) (d:Passive of <veii>, wave, with the prefix <ki>; {a kiveii sa-iik} is the breast that was waved before the Lord as an offering.) (s:kivei) (b:veii) (q:draft)
kiveisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swing down/dangle down) (d:{Kivei}, swing, with <suk>, downward; paired with <kiveito> of men who swing down and up on ropes.) (b:kivei) (q:draft)
kiveito = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swing up/dangle up) (d:{Kivei}, swing, with <to>, upward; paired with <kiveisuk> of men who swing down and up on ropes.) (b:kivei) (q:draft)
kivel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be examined/be checked/be searched out) (d:Passive of <vel>, look over, with the prefix <ki>: be checked carefully or searched out.) (s:kikan/kisit) (b:vel) (q:draft)
kivelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show oneself/have oneself examined) (d:{Kivel}, be examined, with <sak>: let someone examine one, said of a healed person who shows himself to the priest.) (s:kilak) (b:kivel) (q:draft)
kiveng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be settled/be decided) (d:Said of disputes that are brought to an end by a ruling; in the verse it is followed by <sak>.) (q:draft)
kivengsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be settled/be decided) (d:{Kiveng}, be settled, with <sak>: of disputes, be decided by the word of the priests.) (b:kiveng) (q:draft)
kivial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:coil around/entwine/be wound around) (d:{Vial}, encircle, with the prefix <ki>: of a snake or of roots, wind around something.) (s:kancip) (b:vial) (q:draft)
kivialgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:entwine/coil around) (d:{Kivial}, wind around, with the intensifier <gawp>: said of roots that twist all around stones.) (b:kivial) (q:draft)
kivil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be guarded/be watched) (d:Passive of <vil>, watch, with the prefix <ki>; {a kivil inn} is a house kept under guard.) (s:kicing/kikemcing) (b:vil) (q:draft)
kivom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be worn/be carried) (d:Passive of <vom>, carry on oneself, with the prefix <ki>; {a kivom aite} are charms worn on the body.) (b:vom) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be buried) (d:Passive of <vui>, bury, with the prefix <ki>: of a dead person, be laid in a grave; the place takes <ah>.) (s:kiphum) (b:vui) (q:draft)
kivuina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:burial place/grave/burial) (d:{Kivui}, be buried, with the noun suffix <na>: the place where someone is buried, usually followed by <mun>, place, or <han>, tomb.) (s:hanphual/kiphumna) (b:kivui) (q:draft)
kivuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be covered/be buried/be filled in) (d:Passive of <vuk>, cover, with the prefix <ki>: be covered over with earth; {kivuk dim}, said of a valley, is be filled up.) (b:vuk) (q:draft)
kivukcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be filled up/be blocked up/be buried) (d:{Kivuk}, be covered, with <cip>, completely: of a valley, be filled or blocked up; the English of this verse follows another reading.) (s:kivukdim) (b:kivuk) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivukdim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be filled in/be filled up) (d:{Kivuk}, be covered, with <dim>, full: said of a valley filled up with earth.) (s:kivukcip) (q:draft)
kiza = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be heard/sound) (d:Passive of <za>, hear, with the prefix <ki>: of a sound, voice or cry, be heard; {awging kiza} is a sound is heard.) (b:za) (r:24.50.22) (q:draft)
kizahhuaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be disgraced) (d:Passive of <zahhuaisak>, put to shame, with the prefix <ki>.) (s:kimaizumsak/kimindaisak) (a:kipahtawi) (b:zahhuaisak) (q:draft)
kizahko = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be insulted/be mocked) (d:Passive of <zahko>, mock, with the prefix <ki>: have insults thrown at one.) (s:kikosiat/kinuihsan) (b:zahko) (q:draft)
kizahkona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disgrace/reproach/insults) (d:{Zahkona}, ridicule, with the prefix <ki>: the state of being mocked, or the insulting of one another.) (s:mindaina/simmawhna) (b:zahkona) (q:draft)
kizahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be respected/be honored/be esteemed) (d:Passive of <zahtak>, respect, with the prefix <ki>: of a person or a name, be held in honor; {hong kizahtak mahmah} is highly esteemed.) (s:kipahtawi) (a:kisimmawh) (b:zahtak) (q:draft)
kizahtakbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be honored/be treated with respect) (d:{Kizahtak}, be respected, with <bawl>, treat: be treated with honor by others.) (s:kipahtawi) (a:kisimmawhbawl) (b:kizahtak) (q:draft)
kizahtakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being respected/being honored) (d:{Kizahtak}, be respected, with the linking ending <in>: being respected, followed by another verb.) (b:kizahtak) (r:41.6.4) (q:draft)
kizahtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fear/reverence/respect) (d:The fear or respect in which someone is held; {Topa a kizahtakna} is the fear of the Lord, and {khat leh khat kizahtakna} is respect for one another.) (s:kikihtakna/kihtakna) (a:simmawhna) (b:zahtakna) (q:draft)
kizak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be heard/be reported) (d:Form of <kiza>, be heard, used before <ciangin>, <hun>, {nawn loh} and other dependent endings.) (b:kiza) (q:draft)
kizakim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be equal/be of equal rank) (d:Be equal to or on the same level as another, used with <tawh>; of two workers, count the same) (q:draft)
kizakim = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be heard everywhere/be heard all around) (d:Be heard everywhere, said of news: <kiza> be heard with <kim>, all around) (s:kizaza) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be informed/be told) (d:Be informed or told of something: <zaksak> make hear with the passive prefix <ki>) (b:zaksak) (q:draft)
kizal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be spread out/be outstretched) (d:of wings or a covering, stretched out wide; {a kizal} is also a thing spread overhead, a canopy) (b:zal) (q:draft)
kizalhtam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be levelled/be made a plain) (d:of rough and stony ground, be laid out flat) (s:kitamkim) (b:zalhtam) (q:draft)
kizalin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:outspread/spread out) (d:<kizal> be spread out with the linking ending <in>; {kha a kizalin} is the wings when spread out, the wingspan) (b:kizal) (q:draft)
kizalsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stretch out/spread wide) (d:<kizal> be spread out with the causative <sak>, said of tent curtains) (b:kizal) (q:draft)
kizan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stretched out/stretch out/straighten up) (d:Be stretched out, said of a hand or arm, or of the body, straighten up; {a kizan khut} is an outstretched arm) (s:kizankhia) (q:draft)
kizan = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be crushed/be broken to pieces) (d:Be smashed to pieces, often as {kizan gawp}; of the heart, be broken) (s:kizangawp/kitamzan/kisuzan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be used/be practised/be the custom) (d:Be used: <zang> use with the passive prefix <ki>; {kizang lo} is not used, not the custom, and {a kizang thei} is useful) (s:kimang) (b:zang) (r:2.27.19) (q:draft)
kizanga = (i:1) (t:v) (w:used/being used) (d:<kizang> be used, with the linking ending <a>) (b:kizang) (q:draft)
kizangawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be crushed/be broken to pieces) (d:<kizan> be crushed with <gawp>, thoroughly) (s:kitamzan/kisuzan) (b:kizan) (q:draft)
kizangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be used) (d:<kizang> be used with the linking ending <in>: being used, and then the next action follows) (b:kizang) (q:draft)
kizangsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:used/made use of) (d:<kizang> be used, with <sa> already) (b:kizang) (q:draft)
kizangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be used up/be spent/be wasted) (d:<kizang> be used with <sak>; {a mawkna-in kizangsak} is be used to no purpose, wasted) (b:kizang) (q:draft)
kizankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stretched out/outstretched) (d:<zankhia> stretch out, with the prefix <ki>; said of the arm) (s:kizan) (b:zankhia) (q:draft)
kizanlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be still stretched out/be still upraised) (d:of the hand, <kizan>, be stretched out, with <lai>, still) (r:23.10.4/23.9.21) (q:draft)
kizap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blown/be fanned) (d:<zap> fan with the prefix <ki>; {pum a kizap} is the bellows are worked) (b:zap) (q:draft)
kizapkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blown away) (d:<kizap> be fanned with <khiat>, out, away: be driven off like chaff by the wind) (b:kizap) (q:draft)
kizaptel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be limber/be agile) (d:said of arms; in the verse followed by <sak>) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizaptelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make limber/make agile) (d:<kizaptel> with the causative <sak>; said of arms) (b:kizaptel) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizapzap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blown again and again/keep being fanned) (d:<kizap> be blown with <zap> doubled for a repeated action, said of bellows) (q:draft)
kizasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be made heard/be reported/let be heard) (d:Be made heard: <zasak> make hear with the prefix <ki>; of a voice or sound, let it be heard, and of news, be reported) (b:zasak) (q:draft)
kizasakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making heard/causing to be heard/proclaiming) (d:<kizasak> be made heard, let be heard, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kizasak) (q:draft)
kizat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be used) (d:form of <kizang> used before <nading>, <ciangin> and similar words; {kizat nading} is what a thing is to be used for) (s:kimang) (b:zat) (r:23.54.16) (q:draft)
kizatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:use/usage) (d:the use made of something, or the thing in which a material is used) (s:zatna) (b:kizat) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizato = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be heard up to/rise up) (d:said of a sound; <kiza> be heard, with <to> upward) (b:kiza) (q:draft)
kizawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be finished/be completed) (d:passive of <zawh> finish, said of work, a harvest or a building) (s:kikhit) (b:zawh) (q:draft)
kizawh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be subdued/be conquered) (d:passive of <zawh> overcome, said of a land or people) (s:guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:zawh) (q:draft)
kizawhgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be utterly defeated) (d:<kizawh> be overcome, with the intensifier <gawp>) (b:kizawh) (q:draft)
kizawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:in {Eufrates gun lang khat a kizawhna gam}, the territory beyond the Euphrates; perhaps <kizawh> be subdued with the noun suffix <na>, the land that was conquered, meaning not confirmed) (b:kizawh) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:say to one another/urge one another/invite one another) (d:with {khat leh khat}, one another; said of people calling each other to come along and hear) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizawn = (i:2) (t:v) (w:become poor/come to poverty) (d:in {kizawn’lawh}, become poor as a result: <zawn>, form of <zawng> poor, with the prefix <ki> and <lawh>) (b:zawn) (q:draft)
kizawng = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be carried) (d:be carried along by bearers; in these verses Solomon comes carried on a royal litter, <luai>) (s:kipua) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizawngsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pretend to be poor/make oneself poor) (d:<zawng> poor with the prefix <ki> and <sak>: make oneself out to be poor; the opposite in the verse is <kihausak>) (a:kihausak) (q:draft)
kizawnlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become poor/come to poverty) (d:become poor as a result of what one does; <zawn> poor, with <lawh> as a consequence) (a:kihauhlawh) (q:draft)
kizaza = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be heard everywhere/be heard again and again/be widely heard) (d:<kiza> be heard, with <za> doubled to show that it goes on or happens widely; of a name, be famed) (s:kizakim) (b:zaza) (q:draft)
kizazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be heard) (d:<kiza> be heard, with <zo> be able) (b:kiza) (q:draft)
kize = (t:see) <kize-et>
kize-et = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be tested/be tried/be put to the test/be tempted) (d:Be tested or tried, as metal is tried in fire, or be tempted: <ze-et> test with the passive prefix <ki>) (s:kisit) (q:draft)
kize-etna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:testing/test/trial) (d:<kize-et> be tested with the noun suffix <na>) (s:ze-etna) (q:draft)
kize-etsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:tested/tried) (d:that has been tested; <ze-et> test with the prefix <ki> and <sa>, already done) (q:draft)
kizeel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread/spread abroad) (d:of news or a smell, go out over a whole area) (s:kizel/kizelh) (b:zeel) (q:draft)
kizeelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spreading/spreading out) (d:<kizeel> spread, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kizelin/kizelhin) (b:kizeel) (q:draft)
kizeelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread/spread abroad/make known everywhere) (d:<kizeel> spread, with the causative <sak>: make news or a smell go out over a whole area) (s:kizelsak/thangsak) (b:kizeel) (q:draft)
kizeem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dressed/be adorned/adorn oneself/be decorated) (d:Be dressed in fine clothes or adorn oneself, and of a thing, be decorated with something: <zeem> with the prefix <ki>) (s:kizem/kizep) (b:zeem) (q:draft)
kizeemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:adorned/being adorned) (d:<kizeem> be adorned, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kizemin) (b:kizeem) (q:draft)
kizeemsa = (t:see) <kizeemsa-in>
kizeemsa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:adorned/dressed) (d:having been adorned; <kizeem> with <sa> already and the linking ending <in>) (q:draft)
kizeemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:decorations/adorned things) (d:things that are decorated; <kizeem> be adorned, with the plural <te>) (b:kizeem) (q:draft)
kizekaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:delay/put off) (d:<zekaisak> make late, with the prefix <ki>) (b:zekaisak) (q:draft)
kizel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread/be spread abroad) (d:Of news, a message or a reputation, go out through a whole region) (s:kizeel/kizelh) (b:zel) (r:44.6.7) (q:draft)
kizelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread/be spread) (d:of mould, disease or news, extend over a wider area) (s:kizel/kizeel) (b:zelh) (r:44.4.17) (q:draft)
kizelhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spreading/having spread) (d:<kizelh> spread, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kizeelin/kizelin) (b:kizelh) (q:draft)
kizelhthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread widely/spread abroad) (d:Spread out widely in every direction, said of a people growing in number) (s:kizelthang) (q:draft)
kizelin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spreading/being spread abroad) (d:Spreading, said of news, a teaching or a people: <kizel> spread with the linking ending <in>) (s:kizeelin/kizelhin) (b:kizel) (q:draft)
kizelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread/cause to spread) (d:<kizel> be spread, with the causative <sak>) (s:kizeelsak) (b:kizel) (q:draft)
kizelthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread out/be scattered/spread abroad) (d:of peoples or descendants spreading over the earth in every direction) (s:kizelhthang) (q:draft)
kizem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be adorned/be decorated/be embroidered/adorn oneself) (d:Be adorned or decorated: <zem> with the prefix <ki>; of cloth, be embroidered, and of people, put on ornaments) (s:kizeem/kizep) (b:zem) (r:66.18.16) (q:draft)
kizemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being adorned/dressed/decorated) (d:connective form of <kizem>, adorning oneself or being adorned with fine clothes, gold or jewels) (s:kizeemin) (b:kizem) (q:draft)
kizemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:adorn oneself) (d:<kizem> be adorned, with the causative <sak>) (b:kizem) (q:draft)
kizemte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:embroidered/decorated/carved) (d:<kizem> with plural {-te}, said of several decorated things, as embroidered cloth or carved work) (b:kizem) (q:draft)
kizen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:diligent/industrious/hardworking) (d:careful and busy at work) (s:thanuam) (a:thadah) (q:draft)
kizen = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be cut into strands) (d:in Exodus 39:3 only, of beaten gold made into thread; sense uncertain) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:adorn oneself/deck oneself/dress up) (d:put ornaments or fine things on oneself; {na kizep nading}, for your adornment) (s:kizem/kizeem) (b:zep) (q:draft)
kizepna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ornament/adornment/jewelry/decoration) (d:a thing worn or set to make beautiful; also the setting of a stone) (s:zepna) (b:kizep) (q:draft)
kizepnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ornaments/jewelry/finery) (d:Ornaments or jewelry worn on the body: <kizepna> ornament with the plural <te>) (s:zepnate) (b:kizepna) (q:draft)
kizia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stretch out/sprawl/lounge) (d:lay the body down at ease, as a person lounging on a couch or a lion settling down to rest) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rolled up/roll up) (d:passive of <zial>: be rolled like a scroll; {lai kizial} is a rolled book, a scroll) (s:kihial) (b:zial) (q:draft)
kizialcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be rolled up/be rolled shut) (d:<kizial> be rolled, with <cip> tight) (b:kizial) (q:draft)
kizialin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being rolled up/rolled up) (d:<kizial> be rolled up, with the linking ending <in>) (b:kizial) (q:draft)
kizialto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roll upward/billow up/rise up) (d:<kizial> roll, with <to> upward, said of smoke rising in rolls) (b:kizial) (q:draft)
kizim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be hemmed/be edged) (d:of the opening of a garment, be bound round with a woven edge so that it does not tear) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be defeated/be subdued/be overcome) (d:Be defeated or overcome, said of enemies, a people or a ruler: <zo> overcome with the passive prefix <ki>) (s:guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:zo) (q:draft)
kizo = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be finished/be completed) (d:Be finished or completed, said of a building or a piece of work) (s:kikhit) (b:zo) (r:14.8.16) (q:draft)
kizogawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be utterly defeated) (d:<kizo> be defeated, with the intensifier <gawp>) (b:kizo) (q:draft)
kizolsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be led astray/let oneself be enticed) (d:<zol> entice with the prefix <ki> and <sak>; {kuamah kizolsak kei un} is do not let anyone lead you astray) (q:draft)
kizolsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be smeared/be covered) (d:of a sword, be coated or made slick with fat) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined/be connected/be attached/join) (d:be joined to or connected with something, usually after <tawh>; also belong to, have to do with or share in) (s:kituah) (a:kikhenkhia) (b:zom) (r:14.3.12) (q:draft)
kizom = (i:2) (t:v) (w:continue/endure/go on) (d:go on without a break, one thing following the next; {a kizom a kizomin} is in order, one after another) (a:tawp) (b:zom) (r:20.27.24) (q:draft)
kizoma = (i:1) (t:v) (w:connected/in succession) (d:<kizom> be joined, with the linking ending <a>; in the verse of descent from the fathers) (b:kizom) (q:draft)
kizomin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:joined together/in order/in succession) (d:<kizom> with the linking ending <in>; {a kizom a kizomin}, one thing after another in order) (s:kizomzomin/banbanin) (b:kizom) (q:draft)
kizomin = (i:2) (t:prep) (w:concerning/in connection with) (d:Concerning or in connection with, used after <tawh>) (s:tungtangin/tungtangah) (b:kizom) (q:draft)
kizomkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:join again/come together again) (d:<kizom> be joined with <kik>, again: of bones, come back together; of people, join with others again) (s:kigawmkik) (b:kizom) (q:draft)
kizompih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined with/be next to) (d:<kizom> be joined with the ending <pih>; {a kizompih} is the one that a thing adjoins, its neighbour) (b:kizom) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizomsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:join/unite/cause to continue) (d:<kizom> be joined, continue, with the causative <sak>: join one thing to another, or make a name carry on) (b:kizom) (q:draft)
kizomsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:continue/endure) (d:go on without a break, said of a reign) (b:zomsuak) (q:draft)
kizomtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:join oneself to/yoke oneself to) (d:attach oneself to someone of one's own accord, used with <tawh>) (q:draft)
kizomte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those joined to/those who belong to/those united with) (d:<kizom> with plural <te>, after <tawh>: the people connected with someone) (b:kizom) (q:draft)
kizomto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:continue upward) (d:<kizom> be joined or continue, with <to> upward) (b:kizom) (q:draft)
kizomzomin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in order/consecutively) (d:one thing following another) (s:kizomin/banbanin) (q:draft)
kizong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be searched/be sought/be looked for) (d:Be searched for or looked for, and of a place, be searched: <zong> seek with the passive prefix <ki>) (s:kikan) (b:zong) (q:draft)
Kizongkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sought out/be sought after) (d:<zong> seek with the prefix <ki> and <khia> out; used as a name given to Zion, Sought After) (q:draft)
kizop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be joined/be attached/be connected) (d:form of <kizom> used before words such as <theih> and <khawm>; {kei tawh na hong kizop uh} is you remain joined to me) (b:zop) (q:draft)
kizop = (i:2) (t:v) (w:continue/be carried on) (d:go on without a break, as a family line) (b:zop) (r:41.12.19) (q:draft)
kizopkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have contact with/be involved with) (d:Have contact or dealings with something, used after <tawh>; built on <kizop> be joined) (q:draft)
kizopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:relationship/connection/fellowship/alliance) (d:a being joined together with others, by dealings, marriage or trade) (s:kipawlna) (b:kizop) (q:draft)
kizopsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:continue/preserve/keep going) (d:<kizop> be joined with <sak>, cause, make a line go on; {suan-le-khak kizopsak} is preserve the family line) (b:kizop) (r:1.19.34) (q:draft)
kizosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let prevail/let overcome) (d:allow someone or something to win, in the verses always negated, do not let them prevail) (b:kizo) (q:draft)
kizuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sold/sell oneself) (d:Be sold, or sell oneself to someone: <zuak> sell with the prefix <ki>) (a:kilei) (b:zuak) (r:12.7.16) (q:draft)
kizuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being sold/be sold) (d:<kizuak>, be sold, with the linking suffix <in>, which joins it to the next action: being sold for a price) (b:kizuak) (q:draft)
kizuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:selling/sale) (d:<kizuak>, be sold, with the noun suffix <na>: selling; {van kizuakna phualpi} is the place where goods are sold, the market square) (s:zuakna) (a:leina) (b:kizuak) (q:draft)
kizuaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sold) (d:<kizuak>, be sold, with <sa>, already done: having been sold; {sal-a kizuaksa} is sold as a slave) (s:zuaksa) (a:leisa) (b:kizuak) (q:draft)
kizuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sell/cause to be sold) (d:<kizuak>, be sold, with the causative <sak>: have someone sold, sell) (s:zuak) (b:kizuak) (q:draft)
kizualsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be tamed/be made tame) (d:<zualsak>, tame, with the prefix <ki>: be tamed; {a kizualsak zo lo} is one that cannot be tamed, stubborn) (b:zualsak) (q:draft)
kizuansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be gathered to/be made to go to) (d:passive of <zuansak> with the prefix <ki>; {a pu a pate kiang kizuansak} is be gathered to the ancestors, die) (b:zuansak) (q:draft)
kizui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:accord with/be in keeping with/agree with) (d:<zui>, follow, with the prefix <ki>: be in keeping with something; the phrase {tawh kizui-in} means according to) (b:zui) (r:19.119.149) (q:draft)
kizuih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be followed/be obeyed/be kept) (d:passive of <zuih>: be followed, obeyed or observed, of a word, a law, advice or an agreement) (a:kipalsat) (b:zuih) (q:draft)
kizuihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:keeping/observance) (d:<kizuih> be kept, be observed, with the noun suffix <na>: the keeping of an agreement) (s:zuihna) (b:kizuih) (q:draft)
kizuisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take along/make accompany/cause to go with) (d:have a person or animal go along; also of an offering that is to go together with another) (s:tonpih) (b:kizui) (q:draft)
kizuizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be accompanied all the more) (d:<kizui> go together with, accord with, and <zaw> more; {minthanna tawh kizuizaw} is come with still greater glory) (b:kizui) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizung = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be uprooted) (d:<zung> root with the prefix <ki>, used in {kizung bawh}, be pulled up by the roots) (s:kizungbawh/kizunglot/kibotkhia) (a:kisuan) (b:zung) (q:draft)
kizungbawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be pulled up by the roots) (d:passive of <zungbawh> uproot, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kizunglot/kibotkhia/kizung) (a:kisuan) (b:zungbawh) (q:draft)
kizunglot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be rooted out) (d:passive of <zunglot> uproot, with the prefix <ki>) (s:kizungbawh/kibotkhia) (a:kisuan) (b:zunglot) (q:draft)
kizunglotin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being uprooted/uprooted) (d:<kizunglot> be uprooted with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kizunglot) (q:draft)
kizut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be coated/be overlaid/be smeared/be plastered) (d:passive of <zut>: be covered with a layer of oil, metal, paint, whitewash or plaster) (s:kinuh) (b:zut) (q:draft)
kizutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:overlay/coating/plaster) (d:<kizut> with the noun suffix <na>: what is smeared or laid on a surface, as the plaster of a wall or the metal overlay of a post top; also the act of smearing) (s:zutna) (b:kizut) (q:draft)
kizutnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plaster/coatings) (d:<kizutna> plaster with the plural <te>: all that a house is plastered with) (b:kizutna) (q:draft)
kizutnelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:degrade/defile) (d:in the verse, of a woman who ruins her own beauty; likely smear and soil oneself, exact sense not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
Klandia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Claudia) (d:Christian woman in Rome whose greetings Paul sends to Timothy) (r:55.4.21)
Klaudia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Claudius) (d:Roman emperor who ordered all Jews to leave Rome) (q:draft)
Klaudias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Claudius) (d:name of two men in Acts, the Roman emperor Claudius and the commander Claudius Lysias) (r:44.11.28/44.23.26)
Klaudis = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Claudius) (d:Claudius Lysias, the Roman commander in Jerusalem who sent Paul to the governor Felix) (r:44.23.26)
Klement = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Clement) (d:fellow worker of Paul at Philippi) (r:50.4.3)
Kleopas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cleopas) (d:one of the two disciples who met the risen Jesus on the road to Emmaus) (r:42.24.18)
Klopas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Clopas) (d:husband of one of the women named Mary who stood by the cross of Jesus) (r:43.19.25)
ko = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:we/us) (d:first person plural pronoun that leaves out the person spoken to; the English form, we, us or our, depends on its place in the sentence) (s:kote/komau)
Ko = (t:see) <Ko-laiah>
Ko-laiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kolaiah) (d:father of the false prophet Ahab in the time of Jeremiah) (r:24.29.21) (q:draft)
Koa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Koa) (d:a people named together with Pekod and Shoa among those brought against Jerusalem; {Koa mite} is the men of Koa) (r:26.23.23) (q:draft)
kobawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:insult/revile/hurl insults at) (d:<kobawl>, abuse someone with words, with the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft)
kobawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:taunt/insult/abuse) (d:<kobawl>, abuse with words, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kosiatna/zahkona/simmawhna) (a:phatna) (q:draft)
koh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:express/offer/give) (d:say or present something to someone; with <lungdam> or <lungdamna> it means give thanks) (q:draft)
koh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:report/appeal/bring up) (d:bring a matter or complaint before someone, cry to someone for help) (s:zasak) (q:draft)
Kohath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kohath) (d:second son of Levi, ancestor of the Kohathite clans of the Levites) (r:1.46.11/13.6.1)
Kohathte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Kohathites) (d:the Levite clans descended from Kohath, who carried the holy things of the tabernacle) (b:Kohath) (r:4.3.29/4.3.27)
kohkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:<koh> utter or offer with <khit> finish; in the verses always {lungdamna a kohkhit ciangin}, after he had given thanks) (q:draft)
kohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:expressing/announcing/giving notice) (d:act of reporting or expressing, from <koh>; {lungdam kohna} is thanksgiving, {patau kohna} an alarm or warning) (b:koh) (q:draft)
koiah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:where) (d:<koi>, where, with the place marker <ah>: at what place) (s:koi/koilai) (b:koi) (r:43.11.34) (q:draft)
koici = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how/in what way) (d:question word asking the manner of an action, how, in what way; {koici bang} asks how a matter stands) (s:bangci) (q:draft)
koih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put) (s:omsak) (a:lakhia) put in a particular position.
koih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:place) (d:set something or someone in a certain spot or position) (s:omsak) (r:1.1.17)
koih = (i:3) (t:v) (w:deposit) (d:leave something in a safe place or with someone for keeping, as a writing before the Lord or money in a bank)
koih = (i:4) (t:v) (w:lay down) (d:set a person or thing down, as a body on a bed or in a tomb; also lay a foundation) (s:sial)
koihcing = (i:1) (t:v) (w:store up/reserve/keep/save) (d:put something by and keep it safe for later use) (s:khol/koihkhol) (q:draft)
koihcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:isolate/shut up/keep shut away/confine) (d:<koih>, put, with <cip>, tightly closed: put away and keep closed in; also of keeping the hand held back in the fold of the garment) (s:khakcip) (a:khahkhia) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihdakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leaving neglected/neglect) (d:the leaving of a thing as it is without caring for it; {a siapi-in na koihdakna} is your leaving it in ruins) (q:draft, low confidence)
koihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put/place/set) (d:<koih> with the linking suffix <in>, joining it to the next action) (b:koih) (r:3.1.7) (q:draft)
koihkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put together/join/place with) (d:<koih>, put, with <khawm>, together) (s:gawm) (a:koihtuam/khenkhia) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put out/remove/take away/get rid of) (d:<koih>, put, with <khia>, out: put someone out, or take away and get rid of something such as an idol or a sin) (s:lakhia/paaikhia) (a:koihkik) (b:koih) (r:12.3.2) (q:draft)
koihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have put/finish putting) (d:<koih> put with <khit>, finished: the putting is completed) (s:koihzo) (q:draft)
koihkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:store up/lay up/keep in advance) (d:<koih> put with <khol>, beforehand: put aside or prepare for a later time) (s:koihcing) (q:draft)
koihkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lay down beforehand/set down in advance) (d:form of <koihkhol>; {thu koihkholh} is a word laid down or declared beforehand) (b:koihkhol) (q:draft, low confidence)
koihkhong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leave alone/let be/leave as is) (d:leave a person as he is without doing anything about it) (s:koihmawk/khahkhong) (q:draft)
koihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put back/return/restore/replace) (d:<koih>, put, with <kik>, again, back: put a thing back where it was, or restore a person to a former place or office) (a:koihkhia) (b:koih) (r:15.5.15) (q:draft)
koihkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore/put back/replace) (d:<koihkik> put back with the linking suffix <in>) (b:koihkik) (q:draft)
koihleh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:store/keep) (d:apparently <koih>, put or store, written together with <leh>, and: the storing of valuables and) (q:draft, low confidence)
koihmawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tolerate/let be/leave alone) (d:<koih> put, leave, with <mawk> carelessly; with <lo>, not put up with) (s:koihkhong/khahkhong) (q:draft)
koihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:storehouse/store/holder) (d:place where something is put or kept, as in {humpinelkai koihna} lions' den and {meivak koihna} lampstand) (s:vankoihna/kholna) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:storehouses/treasuries/stores) (d:<koihna> with the plural <te>: places where things are kept; {van manpha koihnate} are treasuries) (s:vankoihnate/sumkoihnate) (b:koihna) (r:14.32.28) (q:draft)
koihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who appointed/one who put/man appointed) (d:<koih>, put, with <pa> for a male person: the one who put, set or appointed, or the man who was put in a post) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:laid up/stored up/set/placed) (d:<koih> with {-sa}, already put; {a koihsa} before a noun is that which someone has put, set or laid down) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put for/place for/set up for) (d:<koih>, put, with <sak>: put or appoint something for someone, or cause it to be put) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep for/set up for) (d:<koihsak> put for someone with the linking ending <in>: keeping something for someone, and then the next action follows) (b:koihsak) (q:draft)
koihsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hide/set secretly) (d:<koih> put with <sim>, secretly: lay a trap where it is not seen) (s:seel) (q:draft)
koihsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put down/set down/put under) (d:<koih> put with <suk>, down) (a:koihto) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those placed/things set aside) (d:<koih>, put, with the plural <te>: people or things that someone has put, stationed, kept or set aside) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put up/set on top/build up) (d:<koih> put with <to>, upward: set something up on top of another) (a:koihsuk) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihtuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set apart/set aside) (d:<koih> put with <tuam> separate: put apart from the rest for a special use) (s:tuamkoih/khenkhiat) (a:koihkhawm) (q:draft)
koihzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put instead/put rather) (d:<koih> put with <zaw>, rather: put in one place rather than another) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koihzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have put/have placed/have set ready) (d:<koih> put with <zo>, which shows that the action is done) (s:koihkhit) (b:koih) (q:draft)
koilai = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:where/whereabouts/which place) (d:question word for place; {koilai panin} is from where, and repeated as {koilai mun koilai gam} it means in whatever place) (s:koi/koiah) (q:draft)
koilam = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:where/which way) (d:<koi>, where, with <lam>, direction: to which place, in which direction) (s:koi) (q:draft)
koimah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:anywhere/nowhere/everywhere) (d:<koi> where with <mah>: with a negative verb, nowhere or not anywhere; {koimah peuh}, anywhere at all, everywhere) (s:koimahah) (b:koi) (q:draft)
koimahah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:anywhere/nowhere) (d:<koimah> with the place marker <ah>; used with a negative verb: not anywhere, nowhere) (s:koimah) (b:koimah) (q:draft)
koin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:expressing/giving) (d:apparently <ko>, utter or express, with the linking suffix <in>, elsewhere written {ko-in}; {lungdamna koin} is giving thanks) (q:draft, low confidence)
koipan = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:from where/whence) (d:<koi> where with <pan> from) (q:draft)
kol = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shackles/chains/fetters/stocks) (d:iron or wooden restraint put on a prisoner; {kol bulh} is put in chains) (s:sikkol) (q:draft)
kol = (i:2) (t:n) (w:yoke) (d:wooden yoke laid on the neck of a working animal) (s:hakkol) (q:draft)
kol = (i:3) (t:v) (w:come loose/hang loose/loosen) (d:come loose or hang slack, of a belt, a rope or something tied on) (q:draft)
Kolaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kolaiah) (d:name of two men, a Benjamite ancestor of Sallu and the father of the false prophet Ahab) (r:16.11.7/24.29.21)
kolbulh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fetters/shackles/irons) (d:<kol>, shackles, and <bulh>, put on: fetters fastened on the feet of a prisoner) (s:kol/sikkol) (q:draft)
kolbulh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:shackle/put in fetters) (d:<kol>, shackles, with <bulh>, put on: fasten the feet of someone in fetters) (q:draft)
kolbulhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stocks/shackling/fetters) (d:<kolbulh> put in fetters with the noun suffix <na>: the being put in fetters, or the stocks in which a prisoner is held) (s:singkol) (b:kolbulh) (q:draft)
koleko = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:ourselves) (d:<ko> we, repeated with <le> and: we ourselves as the object of our own action, excluding the hearer) (s:komau) (q:draft)
kolh = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bald/bare) (d:bare of hair or of growth; {tal kolh} is a bald forehead and {mual kolh} a bare hilltop; of plants or forest it is stripped bare) (s:tol) (q:draft)
kolhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:baldness/bareness) (d:<kolh> bald or bare with the noun suffix <na>; {lu kolhna} is baldness of the head and {mun kolhna} a bare, ruined place) (b:kolh) (q:draft)
Kolhozeh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kol-Hozeh) (d:father of Shallun who repaired the Fountain Gate, and an ancestor of Maaseiah of Judah) (r:16.3.15/16.11.5)
kolhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make bald/strip bare) (d:<kolh> bald or bare with <sak>, cause) (s:tolsak) (b:kolh) (q:draft)
kolhsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stripped bare/be laid flat) (d:<kolh> bare with <siang> clean: of a forest, be cleared completely) (b:kolh) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kolose = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Colossae) (d:city in Phrygia in Asia Minor, to whose church Paul wrote the letter to the Colossians) (r:51.1.2/51.1.1)
kolsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:relent/let go) (d:of God, turn from punishing; likely <kol> come loose with the causative <sak>, loosen) (b:kol) (q:draft, low confidence)
koltan = (t:see) <koltan'na>
koltan'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:slavery/bondage) (d:<koltan>, be in bonds, with the noun suffix <na>; {koltan’na Izipt gam} is Egypt the land of slavery) (s:koltanna/salsuahna) (a:suahtakna) (q:draft)
koltanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:slavery/bondage) (d:<koltan>, be in bonds, with the noun suffix <na>; {koltanna Egypt gam} is Egypt the land of slavery) (s:koltan'na/salsuahna) (a:suahtakna) (q:draft)
kolte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:yokes) (d:<kol>, yoke, with the plural <te>: yokes of working oxen, also the yoke of bondage) (s:hakkolte) (b:kol) (q:draft)
kolte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:shackles/fetters) (d:<kol>, shackles, with the plural <te>: irons fastened on the hands or feet of a prisoner) (s:sikkhaute) (b:kol) (q:draft)
komau = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:ourselves/we/us/our) (d:first person plural excluding the hearer, emphatic form of <ko>, we ourselves; before a noun, our own; the English form depends on its place in the sentence) (s:koleko/ko) (r:47.3.5) (q:draft)
komdep = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hollow place/hollow) (d:a hollow or basin in the ground or rock; in Judges 15.19 God split one open at Lehi and water came out of it) (q:draft)
kona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scorn/reproach) (d:reproach or scorn that a person has to bear, in {kona thuak}, bear reproach; likely <ko>, shout at, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kosiatna/simmawhna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kona = (i:2) (t:n) (w:crying out/shouting) (d:second part of {kiko-kona}, <kiko> cry out with <ko> doubled and the noun suffix <na>: continual crying out) (q:draft, low confidence)
Konaniah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Konaniah) (d:name of two Levite leaders: the overseer of the temple offerings under King Hezekiah, and a chief of the Levites under King Josiah) (r:14.31.12/14.35.9)
konate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:insults/reproaches) (d:<kona> reproach with the plural <te>) (s:simmawhnate) (b:kona) (q:draft)
kong = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:of which/I to you) (d:placed before a verb when I or we do something to you: {nang kong it hi}, I love you; note {kong pia hi}, I give to you) (r:1.1.29) particle prefixed to form verb
konga = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the entrance/at the door) (d:<kong> door, entrance, with the suffix <a>, at or of) (s:kongkhakah) (b:kong) (q:draft)
kongah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the door/at the entrance) (d:<kong>, door or entrance, with the place marker <ah>) (b:kong) (q:draft)
kongbiang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gate/door/doorway) (d:the gate or doorway by which a house is entered; {kongbiang dongin hong nai} is near, right at the door) (s:kongkhak/kongvang) (q:draft)
kongbiangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the gate/at the door) (d:<kongbiang> gate with <ah>, at) (s:kongkhakah) (b:kongbiang) (q:draft)
kongcin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gatekeeping/charge of the gates) (d:apparently the work of a <kongcing> gatekeeper, guarding the gates of a building) (q:draft, low confidence)
kongcing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gatekeeper/doorkeeper) (d:person who guards a door or gate, of a house, a palace or the temple) (s:kongcingpa)
Kongcingin = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Kongcingin) (d:<kongcing> gatekeeper with the ending <in>, as gatekeepers, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; not a proper name)
kongcingnu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gatekeeper/doorkeeper) (d:woman who keeps the door of a house: <kongcing> gatekeeper with <nu>, female) (b:kongcing)
kongcingpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gatekeeper/doorkeeper) (d:man who keeps a door or gate: <kongcing> gatekeeper with <pa>, male) (s:kongcing) (b:kongcing)
kongcingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gatekeepers/doorkeepers) (d:<kongcing> gatekeeper with the plural <te>: those who guard the gates of the temple or the city) (b:kongcing)
konghon = (t:see) <konghon'na>
konghon'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:key) (d:<kong> door with <hon> open and the noun suffix <na>: the thing a door is opened with) (s:tawhtang) (q:draft)
konghonna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:opening of the door) (d:<kong> door with <hon> open and the noun suffix <na>; {konghonna tawhtang} is a key) (q:draft)
kongka = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doorway/door) (d:the opening of a door; {kongka lai-ah} is in the doorway) (s:kongvang) (q:draft)
kongkalai = (t:see) <kongkalai-ah>
kongkalai-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the doorway) (d:<kongka> doorway with <lai>, middle, and <ah>, at) (q:draft)
kongkaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:convulse/become rigid) (d:of a person seized by a spirit, have a fit in which the body stiffens and shakes; {kongkaw sak} is throw into a convulsion) (s:kongkawcip) (q:draft, low confidence)
kongkawcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become rigid/stiffen) (d:<kongkaw> convulse, stiffen, with <cip>, firmly, completely) (b:kongkaw) (q:draft)
kongkawcipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:throw into convulsions/convulse) (d:<kongkaw> convulse with <cip>, tightly, and the causative <sak>) (s:kongkawsak/linsakgawp) (q:draft)
kongkawsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:convulse/throw into convulsions/shake violently) (d:<kongkaw> with causative <sak>: said of an evil spirit that makes a person's body go into a fit) (s:kongkawcipsak/linsakgawp) (b:kongkaw) (r:41.1.26) (q:draft)
kongkawtsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:convulse/throw into convulsions) (d:form of <kongkaw> convulse with the causative <sak>: make someone convulse) (s:kongkawsak) (q:draft)
Kongkhak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gate/door) (d:<kongkhak>, door or gate, written with a capital in the names of gates, as {Hoih Kongkhak}, the Beautiful Gate, and {Tuu Kongkhak}, the Sheep Gate, and at the start of a sentence) (s:Kongpi) (b:kongkhak) (q:draft)
kongkhakah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the door/at the entrance) (d:<kongkhak> door with the place marker <ah>: at the door or entrance of a house or tent) (s:kongvangah/konga) (b:kongkhak) (q:draft)
kongkhakmung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doorpost) (d:<kongkhak> door with {mung}: the post of a door) (s:kongkhuam) (q:draft)
kongkhakpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gate/great door) (d:<kongkhak> door with <pi>, great) (s:kongpi) (b:kongkhak) (q:draft)
kongkhakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doors/gates) (d:<kongkhak> door with the plural <te>: the doors of a house or temple, or the gates of a city) (s:kongte/kongpite) (b:kongkhak) (r:26.41.24) (q:draft)
kongkhuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doorpost) (d:<kong> door with <khuam> post; named together with <kongzawlte> in Ezekiel 43.8, where the English has threshold and doorposts) (s:kongkhakmung) (q:draft, low confidence)
kongkhuamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doorposts/gateposts) (d:<kongkhuam> doorpost, with the plural <te>) (b:kongkhuam) (q:draft)
kongkiu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:street corner/corner) (d:the corner of a street or lane) (q:draft)
konglak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:neighborhood/street) (d:the street or open public place among the houses of a town; {konglak buannawng} is the mud of the streets) (s:kongzing)
konglak-a = (i:1) (t:n) (w:neighborhood/in the street) (d:<konglak>, street, with the ending <a>, in or of: in the street) (b:konglak)
konglak-a = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:among us)
konglakah = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:among us)
konglekong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:gate and gate) (d:{kong le kong} written as one word; {konglekong kikal} is the distance from one gate to the other) (q:draft)
kongpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gate/gateway/doorway) (d:main gate of a city, court or building, <kong> door with <pi>, great; {sihna kongpi} is the gates of death) (s:kulhkongpi/kongkhakpi) (b:kong) (q:draft)
Kongpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gate) (d:<kongpi> gate written with a capital in the names of city gates, as {Sakol Kongpi}, the Horse Gate, and {Tuu Kongpi}, the Sheep Gate, and at the start of a sentence) (s:Kulhkongpi/Kongkhak) (b:kongpi) (q:draft)
kongpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:I give you) (d:<piak> give with <kong> before it, which marks I as the doer and you as the receiver) (q:draft)
kongpimai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:front of the gate) (d:<kongpi> gate with <mai>, front: the place before a gate) (q:draft)
kongpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gates/doors) (d:<kongpi> gate with the plural <te>: the main gates of a city, wall or building) (s:kulhkongpite/kongkhakte) (b:kongpi) (q:draft)
kongpuankhai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:curtain/hanging/door curtain) (d:cloth hung at an entrance: <kong> door, <puan> cloth, <khai> hang) (s:puankhai) (q:draft)
kongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doors/doorways/gates) (d:<kong> door with the plural <te>: doors, doorways or gates; {vantung kongte} is the doors of heaven) (s:kongkhakte) (b:kong) (q:draft)
kongtual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gate/gate court) (d:the open place at a gate, where people sit and cases are heard; {kumpipa’ kongtual} is the king’s gate) (q:draft, low confidence)
kongtualah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the gate) (d:<kongtual>, the open place at a gate, with <ah>, at) (b:kongtual) (q:draft)
kongtungzawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lintel/doorframe) (d:apparently the beam above a door, from <kong> door and <tung> above; in the verse it is the part of the door smeared with blood) (s:bangtungzawl) (q:draft, low confidence)
kongvang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doorway/entrance/door) (d:the opening of a door, gate or tomb, the place where one goes in) (s:kongka) (r:26.41.11) (q:draft)
kongvangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the entrance/in the gateway/at the mouth) (d:<kongvang> doorway, with the place marker <ah>; {Leinuai’ kongvangah} is at the mouth of the grave) (b:kongvang) (q:draft)
kongvangneu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sloping/narrow/small/window) (d:window, a small opening in the wall of a house or ship: <kongvang> opening with <neu>, small) (s:tawlet) of window
kongvangneute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:windows/small windows/floodgates) (d:<kongvangneu> window with the plural <te>; {vantung kongvangneute} is the windows or floodgates of heaven) (s:tawlette) (b:kongvangneu) (r:11.6.4) (q:draft)
kongzawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (d:parts of a doorway, plural; <kong> door with <zawl> bar or beam; named with <kongkhuam> doorpost in Ezekiel 43.8, where the English has threshold and doorposts) (q:draft, low confidence)
kongzing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:street) (d:street or open public place of a town; {kongzing lakah} is in the streets) (s:lamdung/konglak) (q:draft)
Kongzing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:street) (d:<kongzing> street written with a capital, in the street name {Kongzing Tang}, Straight Street, and at the start of a sentence) (b:kongzing) (q:draft)
kongzingah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the street/in the square) (d:<kongzing> street with the place marker <ah>: in the street or square of a town) (b:kongzing) (r:20.26.13) (q:draft)
kongzingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:streets) (d:<kongzing> street with the plural <te>: the streets of a town) (s:lamzingte) (b:kongzing) (q:draft)
Koniah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jehoiachin/Coniah) (d:son of Jehoiakim, king of Judah; Coniah is a short form of the name Jehoiachin) (r:24.37.1) (q:draft)
kop = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pair) (d:two of a kind taken together, counted as {kop khat}, one pair, {kop sagih}, seven pairs; {a kop-a kikhuk} is twisted double, said of thread) (r:1.7.3)
kopa = (t:see) <kopa-a>
kopa-a = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:doubled/in plies) (d:apparently <kop> pair with <a>: of threads twisted together, in {kopa-a kikhuk}, finely twisted) (q:draft, low confidence)
kopin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:together/jointly/in pairs) (d:<kop> pair with the ending <in>: joined with another, together with, after <tawh>; of animals, in pairs) (s:khawmin) (a:tuamin) (b:kop) (q:draft)
kopin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:twined/doubled) (d:of thread twisted two together, in {a kopin a kikhuk puan}, where the English has finely twisted linen) (b:kop) (q:draft, low confidence)
kopkopin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in pairs/two by two) (d:<kop> pair said twice with the ending <in>) (q:draft)
koplen = (i:1) (t:v) (d:said of war horses made ready for an attack; perhaps prance or rear, meaning not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
koplenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:galloping/prancing) (d:<koplen>, said of war horses, with the noun suffix <na>; {sakol koplenna kheging} is the sound of the hooves of galloping horses) (s:koptaina) (b:koplen) (q:draft, low confidence)
koppih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:side with/support/stand by) (d:be on the side of someone, stand by and support; likely <kop> pair with the ending <pih>, do together with) (s:panpih) (a:langpan) (b:kop) (q:draft)
koptaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:galloping/prancing) (d:the galloping of horses and the sound of it; apparently <kop> pair and <tai> run, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:koplenna) (q:draft, low confidence)
kopte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pairs) (b:kop) (r:2.37.21) (q:draft)
Korah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Korah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Esau and the Levite, son of Izhar, who rebelled against Moses and from whom temple singers and gatekeepers descended) (r:2.6.21/4.26.11)
Korahte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Korahites) (d:the Levite clan descended from Korah son of Izhar) (b:Korah) (r:2.6.24)
korban = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Corban) (d:loanword from Hebrew: a thing given to God, explained in the text as {Pasian a’ ding}) (q:draft)
Kore = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kore) (d:name of two Levites: the father of the gatekeeper Shallum, and the son of Imnah who kept the East Gate in the days of Hezekiah) (r:14.31.14/13.26.1) (q:draft)
Korenelias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cornelius) (d:Roman centurion at Caesarea to whom Peter was sent; another spelling of <Kornelias>) (r:44.10.7)
Korin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Corinth) (d:city in Greece where Paul stayed and founded a church) (r:44.18.1/47.6.11)
Kornelias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cornelius) (d:Roman centurion of the Italian Regiment at Caesarea, to whom Peter was sent) (r:44.10.25/44.10.27)
Kos = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kos) (d:island in the Aegean Sea, reached by Paul’s ship the day before Rhodes) (r:44.21.1) (q:draft)
Kosam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cosam) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke, son of Elmadam) (r:42.3.28)
kosia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blaspheme/slander/curse/scoff) (d:speak abusively or mockingly against someone, especially against God) (s:gensia) (a:phat) (q:draft)
kosiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:slander/insult/speak evil of/revile) (d:form of <kosia> used before {uh hangin}, <ciangin> and {uh a}) (s:gensiat) (b:kosia) (q:draft)
kosiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:slanderers/revilers) (d:<kosia> slander, revile, with the plural <te>: those who speak abusively) (s:gensiate) (b:kosia) (q:draft)
kosiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:insult/reproach/curse/disgrace) (d:abusive speech against someone, or the disgrace of being so spoken of) (s:simmawhna/kona) (a:phatna) (b:kosiat) (q:draft)
kot = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around/round about/in a circuit) (d:with <pai>, go round from place to place or circle about; of events, come round in turn) (q:draft)
Kote = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:we/us/our) (d:<kote>, first person plural excluding the hearer, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; English we, us or our depends on its place in the sentence) (b:kote) (q:draft)
kotegel = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:the two of us/we two) (d:<kote> we, not including the hearer, with <gel>, both) (q:draft)
Koz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Koz) (d:man of the tribe of Judah, father of Anub and Hazzobebah) (r:13.4.7) (q:draft)
kozaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:call all the more) (d:<ko> call, name, with <zaw> more; here of calling someone by a bad name) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kozbi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Kozbi) (d:Midianite woman, daughter of the chief Zur, who was killed with an Israelite man at Peor) (r:4.25.15/4.25.18)
Kozeba = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kozeba) (d:town in Judah where descendants of Shelah son of Judah lived) (r:13.4.22)
Kresen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Crescens) (d:companion of Paul who left him to go to Galatia) (r:55.4.10)
Krete = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Crete) (d:large island in the Mediterranean Sea, where Paul left Titus to appoint elders) (r:56.1.12/44.2.11)
Krispas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Crispus) (d:ruler of the synagogue at Corinth, who believed with his household and was baptised by Paul) (r:44.18.8/46.1.14)
kristal = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:crystal) (d:loanword from English: a clear, bright precious stone, used in comparisons for what is clear and shining) (q:draft)
Kristal = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Kristal/crystal) (d:<kristal>, crystal, written with a capital in {Kristal suangmanpha}, crystal gem; a kind of clear stone, not a personal name) (r:66.21.11/66.4.6)
ku = (i:1) (t:v) (w:howl/snarl/growl) (d:of dogs, howl or snarl; {ui bangin ku} is howl like a dog) (r:19.59.14) (q:draft)
kua = (i:1) (t:num) (w:nine) (d:the number nine; {kum kua} is nine years, and {sawmkua-le-kua} is ninety-nine)
kuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strap on/gird on/wear) (d:fasten a weapon at the waist, or wear it there; in the verses almost always with <namsau>, sword) (q:draft)
kuahawm = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pit/den/cave) (d:a hollow in the ground or in rock, such as the den where a lion hides; {kuahawm thukpi}, the very deep pit, is the Abyss) (q:draft)
kuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strapping on/carrying/bearing) (d:<kuah>, strap on, with the linking ending <in>: wearing a weapon at the waist while the next action follows, as in {lum leh namsau kuahin}, carrying shield and sword) (b:kuah) (q:draft)
kuahkuah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:strutting) (d:descriptive word placed after <pai>, walk, for the proud strutting walk of a rooster) (s:kuankuan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who puts on/one who girds on) (d:<kuah> strap on, gird on, with <pa>, the man who does it; {galhiam a kuahpa} is one who puts on his armor) (b:kuah) (q:draft)
kuai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bend/bow down/droop) (d:bend over, as ripe grain heavy on the stalk; {kuai tan} is break by bending, snap) (q:draft)
kuai = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be captivated) (d:in {lung kuai}, of the heart, be won over or moved with longing) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/snap) (d:form of <kuai> bend, used in {kuaih tan}, break in two) (b:kuai) (q:draft)
kuaihtan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/snap) (d:break a rigid thing in two, said of a yoke or a rod; in the verses always followed by <sak>) (s:kuaitan/sutan) (q:draft)
kuaihtansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/shatter/snap off) (d:cause to break in two, of an arm, a branch or a tree, from <kuaihtan>) (s:kuaitan/sutan) (b:kuaihtan) (q:draft)
kuaitan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/snap/break in two) (d:break something long and rigid in two, such as a staff, an arm, a leg, a bow or a yoke) (s:kuaihtan/sutan) (r:38.11.10) (q:draft)
kuaitanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/snap/shatter) (d:connective form of <kuaitan>, breaking a long thing such as a bow, a leg bone or a yoke bar in two) (b:kuaitan) (q:draft)
kuaitanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have broken/manage to break) (d:<kuaitan> break with <zo>, showing the act is achieved or completed) (b:kuaitan) (q:draft)
kuak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hollow/cavity) (d:a hollow or bowl-shaped space: {khut kuak} is the hollow of the hand, {lo kaihna kuak} a furrow; {a kuak-in} means hollow inside) (r:2.38.7) (q:draft)
kuakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:hollow) (d:<kuak> hollow with the ending <in>; {a kuakin bawl} is make something hollow inside) (b:kuak) (q:draft)
kuakte = (t:see) <ma-kuakte>
kuakua = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:whoever/whosoever) (d:<kua> who doubled; {kuakua ahih hangin} is whoever he may be) (s:peuhmah) (q:draft)
kual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ring) (d:a ring or loop, such as the gold rings that hold poles or chains) (r:2.39.17) (q:draft)
kual = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:around/roundabout) (d:going round in a circuit or curve rather than straight: {kual pai} is go around, and of a boundary it means curve or turn) (q:draft)
kualah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:to the ring/at the ring) (d:<kual> ring with <ah>, at or to) (b:kual) (q:draft)
kualin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:around/round about) (d:<kual>, around, with the ending <in>: going round in a circle or curve; {kawi kualin} is turning round) (b:kual) (q:draft)
kualpai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go around/go round about) (d:<kual> around with <pai> go: go by a roundabout way; {kualpai sak} is send around) (q:draft)
kualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rings) (d:plural of <kual>, ring: the rings on the ark, the table and the altar through which the carrying poles pass) (b:kual) (r:2.25.14) (q:draft)
kualte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:rims) (d:rims of wheels) (b:kual) (q:draft)
kuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley/gorge/plain) (d:low ground between hills: a valley, gorge or plain; {kuam sung} is the inside of the valley) (s:guam/mualkuam) (a:mual) (q:draft)
Kuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley) (d:<kuam>, valley, written with a capital as part of a place name, as in {Zered Kuam} and {Ci Kuam}, the Valley of Salt) (b:kuam) (q:draft)
kuama = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:anyone/no one) (d:form of <kuamah> used before a noun as a possessive or before a verb it governs, mostly in negative clauses) (s:kuamah) (r:24.41.4) (q:draft)
Kuama = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley) (d:<Kuam> valley with <a>, in the Valley; {Aven Kuama teng mi} are those who live in the Valley of Aven) (b:Kuam) (q:draft)
kuamah = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:no one/nobody) (d:no one, nobody: used with a negative verb, so that {kuamah om lo} is there is no one; {kuamah in} marks it as the subject) (s:kuama) (a:mikim/mikhempeuh) (r:2.23.26)
Kuamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley) (d:<Kuam>, valley as part of a place name, with the place marker <ah>: in the Valley or to the Valley) (b:Kuam) (q:draft)
kuamahdang = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:no one else/nobody else) (d:<kuamah>, anyone, no one, with <dang> other; used with a negative) (q:draft)
kuamahpeuh = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:anyone)
kuami = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:who/what people) (d:<kua> who with <mi> person: asks who someone is or where he belongs) (b:kua) (q:draft)
kuamkeu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley/dry valley) (d:<kuam>, valley, with <keu>, dry: a dry valley; in Psalm 84 it stands for the Valley of Baka)
Kuamkeu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dry valley) (d:<kuam> valley with <keu> dry; used as a place name, NIV Valley of Baka) (b:kuamkeu) (q:draft)
kuampi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley/great valley) (d:<kuam>, valley, with {-pi}, great: a large or deep valley) (b:kuam) (q:draft)
kuampi = (i:2) (t:n) (w:abyss/bottomless pit) (d:the deep pit in which Satan is shut up) (s:kuamthuk) (b:kuam) (q:draft)
kuampite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valleys) (d:<kuam> valley with <pi>, great, and the plural <te>) (s:kuamte/guamte) (a:mualte) (b:kuampi) (q:draft)
kuamsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley/plain) (d:the inside of a valley, low ground between hills, set against <mualtung>, the hilltop) (s:kuam) (a:mualtung) (q:draft)
kuamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valleys/plains/ravines) (d:plural of <kuam>: valleys, ravines or plains) (s:guamte/kuampite) (a:mualte) (b:kuam) (q:draft)
kuamthuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:abyss/deep pit/bottomless pit) (d:<kuam> valley, hollow, with <thuk> deep) (s:kuampi) (q:draft)
Kuamthuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley/deep valley) (d:<kuam> valley with <thuk> deep) (b:kuamthuk) (q:draft)
kuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out/set out/march/go to war) (d:set out for a task: go out to war against an enemy, or go out to work in the field) (s:kuankhia) (a:ciahkik) (r:7.20.21) (q:draft)
kuana = (i:1) (t:num) (w:ninth) (d:<kua> nine with the ordinal ending {-na}; {sawm-le-kuana} is nineteenth) (b:kua) (q:draft)
kuancil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set out/first set out) (d:<kuan> set out, go to war, with <cil>, at the beginning) (q:draft)
kuang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:basin/bowl/trough) (d:an open vessel: a bowl for food, a basin for washing, or a trough) (q:draft)
kuang = (i:2) (t:v) (w:burn/blaze) (d:burn with a flame, blaze; also said of anger that burns like fire) (s:kang) (q:draft)
kuanga = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burning) (d:<kuang> burn with the linking suffix <a>) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the pouch/in the bowl) (d:<kuang> bowl with the place marker <ah>; {saili kuangah} is in the pouch of a sling) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangdaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plates/dishes) (d:<kuangdai> with plural {-te}, the flat dishes of the table in the tabernacle) (b:kuangdai) (q:draft)
kuangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn/blaze/break out) (d:<kuang>, burn with flame, with the linking suffix {-in}) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blaze out/flare up/burn forth) (d:<kuang> burn with <khia> out) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn again/flame up again) (d:<kuang> burn with <kik>, again) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangkuang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burn/keep burning/blaze) (d:<kuang> burn, doubled for an action that goes on) (q:draft)
kuanglekeute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vessels/utensils/dishes) (d:household vessels and utensils of all kinds, a pair-word built on <kuang>, bowl, with plural <te>) (q:draft)
kuangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:large basin/basin/Sea) (d:<kuang> basin with <pi> big; {tui kuangpi} is the great bronze basin of the temple, called the Sea) (s:tuikuangpi) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kindle/set on fire/make burn) (d:<kuang> burn with causative <sak>; also of anger, make it blaze) (s:kangsak/tawhkuang/halsak) (a:sumit/phelh/mitsak) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set ablaze/kindle) (d:<kuangsak> make burn with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kuangsak) (q:draft)
kuangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bowls/basins/trays/troughs) (d:plural of <kuang>: bowls, basins or trays) (b:kuang) (q:draft)
kuangtuahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sistrums/castanets) (d:a percussion instrument played in worship, listed between timbrels and cymbals; plural <te>) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuangzalzal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flash/blaze in flashes) (d:<kuang> burn with <zalzal>, flashing repeatedly) (q:draft)
kuangzawn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trough/watering trough) (d:long trough filled with water for animals to drink from) (s:tuikuang) (q:draft)
kuanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out/set out) (d:<kuan> with the linking suffix <in>, going out and then) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuanin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:by families/household by household) (d:in the phrase {innkuan kuanin}, family by family, where the last part of <innkuan> is repeated) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuankha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to go/chance to come) (d:<kuan> go out with <kha>, showing the thing happened by chance) (s:paikha) (q:draft)
kuankhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out together/march together/go with) (d:set out together, to war or to work) (s:kuankhop) (b:kuan) (r:14.25.7) (q:draft)
kuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out/set out/march out) (d:<kuan>, set out, with <khia>, out: go out from a place to work or to battle) (s:kuan) (a:ciahkik) (b:kuan) (r:41.4.3) (q:draft)
kuankhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send out/march out) (d:<kuankhia> set out, with the causative <sak>: make soldiers go out to war) (b:kuankhia) (q:draft)
kuankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out/march out/set out) (d:form of <kuankhia> used before words such as <ciang> and <khit> or before a noun) (b:kuankhia) (q:draft)
kuankhiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who set out/those who go out) (d:<kuankhia>, set out, with plural <te>: the people who set out) (b:kuankhia) (q:draft)
kuankhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:going out/setting out/undertaking) (d:<kuankhiat> go out with the noun suffix <na>, a going out to battle or to a task) (s:kuanna) (a:ciahkikna) (b:kuankhiat) (q:draft)
kuankhiatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead out/march out with) (d:<kuankhiat>, set out, with <pih>, together with: go out to war at the head of others) (a:ciahpih) (b:kuankhiat) (q:draft)
kuankhiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have come out/have set out) (d:<kuankhia> go out with <zo>, showing the act is completed) (b:kuankhia) (q:draft)
kuankhop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out together/go along with) (d:<kuan>, set out for work, with <khop>, together) (s:kuankhawm) (q:draft)
kuankik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go again/go back/return) (d:<kuan> set out with <kik>, again or back) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuankikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set out again/go again) (d:<kuankik> set out again with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kuankik) (q:draft)
kuankuan = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:strutting) (d:descriptive word after <pai> walk, of the proud walk of a rooster) (s:kuahkuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuankuanta = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:apparently shows that something is steadily on its way to happening, with <ta>, now; {maimang kuankuanta} is now passing away, coming to nothing) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuanlamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:on the way in/when going) (d:<kuan> set out, go, with <lamin>, in the direction or at the time of) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:setting out/marching out/coming) (d:the act of setting out, especially to war; {hong kuanna lampi}, the way by which he came) (s:kuankhiatna) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send out/send into battle/bring against) (d:<kuan>, set out, with the causative {-sak}: make someone set out, especially to war) (s:sawlkhia) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuansak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:set ablaze/kindle) (d:make something burn, apparently from <kuang>, burn, with the causative {-sak}) (s:kuangsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuansakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sending out/sending) (d:<kuansak> send out, with the linking ending <in>, sending out and then doing the next action) (b:kuansak) (q:draft)
kuansaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make go out/send out to work) (d:<kuansak> make someone go, with <sak> repeated; {lo kuansaksak} is make someone go out to work the field) (b:kuansak) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuansanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go off to/go away to) (d:<kuan> go out with <san>, leaving something behind, and the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft)
kuansuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go down/come down/march down) (d:<kuan>, set out, with <suk>, downward; often of going down to battle) (s:paisuk) (a:kuanto) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuansukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come down/go down/march down) (d:<kuansuk> go down with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kuansuk) (q:draft)
kuanta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be about to/be on the point of) (d:<kuan>, set out, with <ta>, now; placed after another verb, the action is just about to happen, as in {ni tum kuanta}, the sun is about to set) (b:kuan) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who march out/those coming to attack) (d:<kuan>, set out, with plural <te>; after another verb, as in {a si kuante}, those who are about to do it, the dying) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuanto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go up/march up) (d:set out upward, often to attack) (s:paito/kahto) (a:kuansuk) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuantoh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go up/march up) (d:form of <kuanto> used before <ding>) (s:paitoh/kahtoh) (b:kuanto) (q:draft)
kuantohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:coming up/marching up) (d:<kuantoh> go up, march up, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:kuantoh) (q:draft)
kuantokik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come up again/go up again) (d:<kuanto> go up with <kik>, again) (b:kuanto) (q:draft)
kuantosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send up/make go up) (d:<kuanto> go up with the causative <sak>) (s:paitosak) (b:kuanto) (q:draft)
kuantosakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send up/make go up) (d:<kuantosak> send up with the linking suffix <in>) (b:kuantosak) (q:draft)
kuanun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:by families/family by family) (d:in {a innkuan kuanun}, family by family, by households; the last part of <innkuan>, household, said again with the ending <un>) (q:draft)
kuanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to go out) (d:<kuan> go out to fight with <zo>, be able) (b:kuan) (q:draft)
kuaphete = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:locusts) (d:apparently a misprint of <kauphete>, the plural of <kauphe> locust, which stands in the same verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kuartas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Quartus) (d:Christian in Corinth, called a brother, whose greetings Paul sends to the church in Rome) (r:45.16.23)
kuasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make pound/set burning/stir) (d:said with <dip>, the heart: make the heart pound or burn with strong feeling) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuate = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:who/which people) (d:plural of <kua>: which people, who all) (s:kuateng) (b:kua) (q:draft)
kuate = (i:2) (t:num) (w:nine) (d:<kua>, nine, with plural {-te}; {sawmkua leh kuate} means the ninety-nine) (b:kua) (q:draft)
kuateng = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:who/which ones) (d:<kua> who with <teng> all: which persons out of a group) (s:kuate) (b:kua) (q:draft)
kuavang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mouth/opening) (d:the opening of a pit or hole, with <vang>, opening) (q:draft)
kuavangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the hole/at the mouth of the den) (d:<kuavang>, the opening of a hole, with <ah>, at) (b:kuavang) (q:draft)
Kue = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kue) (d:region in Cilicia, in the south-east of Asia Minor, from which the merchants of Solomon bought horses) (r:11.10.28/14.1.16)
kui = (i:1) (t:n) (w:corner/edge/brow) (d:outer edge or corner of something: {vantung kui li}, the four corners of heaven; {mual dawn kui}, the brow of a hill) (s:kiu) (q:draft, low confidence)
kui = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cut/slash/gash/scratch) (d:cut, tear or scratch a surface: the skin of the body or hands in mourning, flesh torn with thorns, marks scratched on a door) (s:kuikek/at) (q:draft)
kuigawpin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scratch all over/scrawl on) (d:<kui> cut, scratch, with <gawp>, badly or all over, and the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft)
kuih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plow/furrow) (d:form of <kui>, cut, used before <bang>: cut furrows in the ground) (b:kui) (q:draft)
kuikeek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gash/tear up/plow up) (d:cut long gashes or furrows in a surface, built on <kui>, cut) (s:kuikek) (q:draft)
kuikek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gash/slash/furrow) (d:cut long lines into something, as a plough does the soil or as mourners cut their hands) (s:kuikeek/kui) (q:draft)
kuikham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tear/gash/lacerate) (d:cut or tear the flesh, built on <kui>, cut; stands beside <petkham>, chew, in the same verse) (q:draft)
kuiliam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash) (d:<kui> cut with <liam> wound: cut the body so that it is wounded, as was done in mourning) (q:draft)
Kuirinias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Quirinius) (d:Roman governor of Syria at the time of the census during which Jesus was born) (r:42.2.2)
kulgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bent over/be bent double) (d:of the back, be badly bent, with <gawp>, severely) (q:draft)
kulh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wall/fortification) (d:wall of a city or stronghold; {kulh a nei khuapi} is a fortified city and {kulh kongpi} a city gate) (s:kulhpi/khuakulh) (q:draft)
Kulh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wall) (d:<kulh>, wall, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in names of parts of Jerusalem: {Kulh Zai} is the Broad Wall, {Ngasa Kulh kongpi} the Fish Gate) (b:kulh) (r:16.12.38) (q:draft)
kulhhuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:area within the walls) (d:<kulh> wall with <huam>, the area taken in: the space enclosed by a city wall) (q:draft)
