kulhkongpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gates/city gates) (d:plural of <kulhkongpi>: the gates of a walled city or of the temple) (s:kongpite/khuakongpite) (b:kulhkongpi) (q:draft)
kulhnei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fortified/walled) (d:having a wall, <kulh> wall with <nei> have; said of cities) (q:draft)
kulhneite = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fortified/walled) (d:<kulhnei>, having a wall, with plural <te>, which belongs to the whole phrase {khuapi kulhnei}, fortified cities) (b:kulhnei) (q:draft)
kulhpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wall/city wall/fortress) (d:<kulh>, wall, with <pi>, great: the great wall round a city, and so a fortress or stronghold) (s:kulh/khuakulh) (b:kulh) (r:23.22.10) (q:draft)
Kulhpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wall/fortress) (d:<kulhpi> written with a capital in the place name {Kiu Kulhpi} in the wall of Jerusalem, where the NIV has Corner Gate) (b:kulhpi) (q:draft)
kulhpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:walls/strongholds/fortresses) (d:plural of <kulhpi>: the great walls of a city, or its strongholds) (s:kulhte) (b:kulhpi) (r:26.19.7) (q:draft)
kulhpua = (t:see) <kulhpua-ah>
kulhpua-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:outside the wall) (d:<kulh> wall with <pua> outside and <ah>, at) (q:draft)
kulhsia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:broken wall/ruined wall) (d:<kulh> wall with <sia>, ruined) (q:draft)
