laamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dancing/dance) (d:<laam>, dance, with the noun suffix <na>: dancing, a dance) (s:lamna) (b:laam) (q:draft)
Laamna = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Laamna) (d:the noun <laamna>, dancing, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (r:19.149.3)
laamsa = (t:see) <laamsa-in>
laamsa-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dancing) (d:<laam> dance with <sa-in>, while doing) (q:draft)
laamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make float) (d:<laam> float with the causative <sak>) (b:laam) (q:draft)
laamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dancers/those who dance) (d:<laam> dance, with the plural <te>; {a laamte}, the ones who are dancing) (b:laam) (r:22.6.13) (q:draft)
laamto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lift up/raise) (d:lift something up, as the hands in prayer or a staff; also lift a person out of trouble, and of water, bear a boat upward) (s:domto/phongto) (q:draft)
laamtosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make float up/make rise) (d:<laam> float with <to>, upward, and the causative <sak>) (b:laamto) (q:draft)
laano = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:donkey/young donkey) (d:<laa> donkey with <no>, young or small; in the verse a wild donkey in heat) (s:lano) (b:laa) (q:draft, low confidence)
laate = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:donkeys) (d:<laa> with plural <te>; {gamlak laate} is wild donkeys) (s:late) (b:laa) (q:draft)
Laban = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Laban) (d:brother of Rebekah and father of Leah and Rachel, for whom Jacob worked in Haran) (r:1.29.26)
Labanon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Lebanon) (d:mountain range and region north of Israel, famous for its cedar trees) (r:5.3.25/26.27.5)
Ladan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ladan) (d:name of two men: a Levite of the clan of Gershon, and an Ephraimite ancestor of Joshua) (r:13.23.7/13.7.26) (q:draft)
Lael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lael) (d:a Levite, father of Eliasaph the leader of the Gershonites) (r:4.3.24)
lah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show/display) (d:form of <lak>, show, used before <ding>, <nading>, <theih> and nouns: let someone see a thing, or make a quality such as power or kindness known) (s:muhsak) (a:seel/im) (r:45.9.23) (q:draft)
lah = (i:2) (t:part) (d:emphatic particle after a noun or verb that sets one fact beside another: indeed, as for, and yet) (r:18.32.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lahad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lahad) (d:a man of Judah, son of Jahath, of the clans of the Zorathites) (r:13.4.2)
lahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reveal/show forth/bring out) (d:form of <lakkhia> used before <loh>, <ding>, <nading> and nouns: show openly, make known, bring a person out before others) (b:lah) (q:draft)
lahkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foreshadowing/showing beforehand) (d:<lah> show with <kholh>, beforehand, and the noun suffix <na>; {lim lahkholhna} is a shadow or picture shown in advance) (q:draft)
lahkimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:full depiction/detailed showing) (d:<lah> show with <kim>, every part, and the noun suffix <na>; {lahkimna lim} is a sketch that shows every detail) (q:draft)
Lahmam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Lahmam/Lahmas) (d:town in the western lowland of Judah, listed with Kabbon and Kitlish) (r:6.15.40)
Lahman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Lahmas) (d:town in the western lowland of Judah, listed with Kabbon and Kitlish; another spelling of <Lahmam>) (r:6.15.40)
Lahmi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lahmi) (d:brother of Goliath the Gittite, killed by Elhanan son of Jair) (r:13.20.5)
lahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:showing/display/demonstration) (d:<lah>, show, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of showing or making known, or the thing that shows it; {lim lahna} is the showing of a sign) (s:latsakna/muhsakna) (b:lah) (q:draft)
lahnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things shown/signs) (d:<lahna> showing with the plural <te>, the things someone has shown; {lam lahnate} are guideposts) (b:lahna) (q:draft)
lahnopmi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one I wish to show) (d:the person to whom one wants to show something; <lah> show, with <nop> want and <mi> person) (q:draft)
lahnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:representation/intended meaning) (d:what something is meant to show or stand for; <lah> show, with <nop> want and the noun suffix <na>) (q:draft, low confidence)
laho = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:nettle) (d:a wild stinging or thorny plant that overgrows ruins, named together with <thangling>, thistle) (q:draft, low confidence)
lahpi = (t:see) <lahpi-a>
lahpi-a = (t:todo) (q:draft, said of deer fleeing before hunters in Lamentations 1:6, the meaning of <lahpi> cannot be told from one verse)
lahsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shown/have shown) (d:<lah>, show, with <sa> for a completed action: have shown; before a noun, that which was shown) (s:lakkhin) (b:lah) (q:draft)
lahsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shake at/raise against) (d:<lah>, show, with <san>, toward: hold up the fist against someone) (b:lah) (q:draft)
lahsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things shown/what was shown) (d:<lahsa> shown, with the plural <te>) (b:lahsa) (q:draft)
lahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things shown) (d:<lah> show with the plural <te>, making a noun, the things that someone shows; {nalamdang lahte} are the signs shown) (b:lah) (q:draft)
lahtel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show clearly/prove/demonstrate) (d:<lah>, show, with <tel>, clearly: make something plain or prove it; {lahtel nading} is evidence or proof) (s:laktel) (q:draft)
lahtelnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:declarations/explanations) (d:<lahtel>, show clearly, with <na> and plural <te>: things set out plainly) (b:lahtel) (q:draft)
lahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to show/can show) (d:<lah>, show, with <theih>, be able; {lahtheih nadingin} means so that one may show) (s:lakthei) (b:lah) (q:draft)
lai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:writing) (d:written words, a document or anything set down in writing) of a composing text
Lai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Scripture/writing) (d:<lai>, writing, with a capital in {Lai Siangtho}, Holy Scripture, the Bible) (b:lai) (q:draft)
