lakhiakhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take away together with) (d:<lakhia> take out, with <khawm> together) (b:lakhia) (q:draft)
lakhiakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take away again/take back) (d:<lakhia> take out, with <kik> again or back) (b:lakhia) (q:draft)
lakhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have brought out/cause to bring out) (d:<lakhia>, take out, with <sak>, cause) (b:lakhia) (q:draft)
lakhiasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring down/take down) (d:<lakhia> take out, with <suk> downward) (b:lakhia) (q:draft)
lakhiato = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring up/lift out) (d:<lakhia>, take out, with <to>, upward) (b:lakhia) (q:draft)
lakhiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to take out/deliver) (d:<lakhia> take out, with <zo> be able) (s:honkhiazo) (b:lakhia) (q:draft)
Lakhish = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Lachish) (d:fortified city in the lowlands of Judah, taken by Joshua and later besieged by the kings of Assyria and Babylon) (r:24.34.7/6.10.3)
lakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take back/get back/bring back/restore) (d:<la>, take, with <kik>, back or again: take or bring back what was given, lost or sent away) (s:lakkik/ngahkik) (a:piakik) (b:la) (q:draft)
lakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:showing/pointing out) (d:<lak>, show, with the linking ending <in>: showing or pointing out, of showing a thing to someone and of making a matter known) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lakkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to take/take wrongly) (d:<lak> take, with <khak>, by chance or by mistake) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reveal/show forth/make known) (d:<lak>, show, with <khia>, out: bring out into view what was hidden or unseen) (s:langsak/kilangsak/pulak) (a:seel/im) (b:lak) (r:18.36.9) (q:draft)
lakkhial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:mislead/lead astray) (d:<lak>, show, with <khial>, wrong: show the way wrongly, as in {lam lakkhial}, lead astray) (s:lampialsak/pialsak/khialsak) (a:lamlak) (q:draft)
lakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take/take out/take away) (d:the form of <lakhia>, take out, used before endings and following words)
lakkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:taking out/removal) (d:<lakkhiat> with the noun suffix <na>; before <gam>, the land from which someone was taken away) (b:lakkhiat) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:taken away/taken out) (d:<lakkhiat>, take out, with <sa>, already done; before a noun, that which someone has taken away) (b:lakkhiat) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:took/taken out/take away from) (d:<lakkhiat>, take out, with <sak>: take something away from someone) (b:lakkhiat) (r:66.22.19)
lakkhiatsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking away from/stripping of/removing) (d:<lakkhiatsak>, take something out or away from someone, with the linking ending <in>) (b:lakkhiatsak) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take back out of/make give back) (d:<lakkhiatsak> with <kik> back: take out again what another has taken) (b:lakkhiatsak) (q:draft)
lakkhiatte = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<lakkhiat>, take away, with plural <te>: here the people from whom something is taken away) (b:lakkhiat) (q:draft)
lakkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have shown/have revealed) (d:<lak>, show, with <khin>, already: have shown or revealed something to someone) (s:lakzo/lahsa) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lakkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have taken/have received) (d:<lak> take, with <khit> finished; {lakkhit ciangin} is after receiving) (s:sankhit/ngahkhit) (q:draft)
lakkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show beforehand/reveal in advance) (d:<lak> show, with <khol> beforehand) (q:draft)
lakkholzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have shown beforehand/reveal in advance) (d:<lakkhol> with <zo>, marking the action as accomplished) (b:lakkhol) (q:draft)
lakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take back/take again/bring back) (d:<lak>, take, with <kik>, again or back: take up again or bring back; {phu lakkik} is take revenge) (s:lakik) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lakkiksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:taken back/reclaimed) (d:<lakkik>, take back, with <sa>, already done) (b:lakkik) (q:draft)
Lakkum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Lakkum) (d:town on the border of the territory of Naphtali, near the Jordan) (r:6.19.33)
laklak = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after {dian’}, leap, for the bounding of a deer) (q:draft, low confidence)
laklawhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in between/halfway/lukewarm) (d:being neither one thing nor the other, here neither cold nor hot) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:taking/extortion) (d:<lak>, take, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of taking; {sumgolh lakna} is taking a bribe, {a meet lakna} taking interest, {phu lakna} taking revenge, and {tui lakna} a channel that draws water) (r:19.62.10) (q:draft)
laknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:taking/takings) (d:<lakna> taking, with the plural <te>; {sumgolh laknate} is the taking of bribes, {sakol a laknate} the horses he obtained) (b:lakna) (q:draft)
laknop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to take/want to marry) (d:<lak> take, with <nop> want; here of taking a woman as wife) (q:draft)
lakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who shows/adviser/guide) (d:the one who shows, <lak> with {-pa} marking a male person; {lam a lakpa}, one who shows the way, is a guide or adviser) (q:draft)
lakpan = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:from among/out of) (d:<lak>, among, with <pan>, from) (s:lakpanin/sungpan) (q:draft)
lakpanin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:from among/out of) (d:<lakpan> with the linking suffix <in>) (s:lakpan/sungpanin) (b:lakpan) (q:draft)
laksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:taken/captured/seized) (d:<lak>, take, with {-sa}, already taken; {a laksa} before a noun is what someone has taken or captured) (b:lak) (q:draft)
laksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take away from/seize/plunder) (d:<lak>, take, with <sak>: take something away from someone, by force or as plunder) (s:sut) (a:pia) (b:lak) (q:draft)
laksak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:take for/get for) (d:<lak>, take, with <sak>: take or get something on behalf of another, as a wife for a son) (b:lak) (q:draft)
laksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking away/seizing/robbing) (d:<laksak> take from someone with the linking ending <in>: taking away, having seized) (s:sutin) (b:laksak) (q:draft)
laksakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take away completely/plunder) (d:<laksak> take away from, with <mang>, so that it is gone) (q:draft)
laksakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who take away/those who seize) (d:<laksak>, take away from, with plural <te>) (b:laksak) (q:draft)
laksakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to plunder/be able to take away) (d:<laksak> take away from, with <zo> be able) (s:sutzo/luhgawpzo) (b:laksak) (q:draft)
laksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:captives/those captured) (d:<laksa>, taken, with plural <te>: the people someone has taken) (s:galmatte/salte) (b:laksa) (q:draft)
laksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take down/bring down) (d:<lak> take, with <suk> downward) (a:lato) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things taken/plunder/takings) (d:<lak> take or get with the plural <te>: the things or people taken or received; {na lakte}, things taken, plunder) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lakte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who show/guides/counselors) (d:<lak> show with the plural <te>; {thu hong lakte}, those who show me what to do) (s:lamlakte) (q:draft, low confidence)
laktel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show clearly/make plain/prove/point out) (d:make something plainly known, as the truth of a word or the fault of a person) (s:lahtel/telsak) (a:seel) (q:draft)
laktelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let show clearly/make plain to) (d:<laktel> show clearly, with <sak> cause or allow) (b:laktel) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all that was taken) (d:<lak> take, with <teng> all; {a galvan lakteng} is all the goods he has taken, his spoil) (b:lak) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to show/prove) (d:<lak> show with <thei> can) (b:lak) (q:draft)
laktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to take/be able to capture) (d:<lak> take with <theih>, the form of <thei> can before <nadingin>, so that one can take; {phu laktheih} is be able to take revenge) (b:lak) (q:draft)
laktheih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be able to present/be able to show) (d:<lak> show with <theih>, the form of <thei> can before <nadingin>) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lakthuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take in addition/marry also) (d:<lak>, take, with <thuah>, in addition: take another wife besides the one already had) (s:lathuah) (q:draft)
lakto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise/lift up/hold up) (d:<lak> with <to>, up: hold something up high to be seen, as a banner) (s:laamto) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lakzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:conquest/capture) (d:<lak> take, with <zawh> succeed and the noun suffix <na>: the taking of a town) (q:draft)
lakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have shown/make known) (d:<lak> show, with <zo>, marking the action as accomplished) (b:lak) (q:draft)
lal = (i:1) (t:v) (w:migrate/move/wander/sojourn) (d:move from one place to live in another, or wander from place to place; {lal-a om} is to live as a sojourner away from home, and {lal hun} the season when birds migrate) (s:peem/kikhin) (q:draft)
lalcin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lantern) (d:a lamp carried in the hand to give light at night, named beside <meilah>, torch) (q:draft)
lalsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:move/resettle/cause to migrate) (d:<lal>, migrate, with <sak>, cause) (b:lal) (q:draft)
lam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way) (d:the way a person goes or lives; {lam pial} is to turn off the way and {lam hilh} to teach someone the way) (s:lampi)
lam = (i:2) (t:n) (w:path) (s:lampi/lamzin)
lam = (i:3) (t:n) (w:direction) (d:the side toward which someone goes or something faces; after a place name, toward that place) (s:lamsang) (r:1.2.8/4.3.29)
Lam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:road/way) (d:<lam>, road or way, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {Lam kawi} is a crooked road, {Lam lianpi} a main road and {Lam gei} the roadside) (b:lam) (q:draft)
lam-ethuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:worth hoping for/to be looked forward to) (d:{lam-et} hope, with <huai> worthy of) (s:lamethuai) (q:draft)
lama = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:on the side of/toward/facing) (d:<lam>, side or direction, with the suffix <a> joining it to what follows; {nisuahna lama om} is that is on the east side) (b:lam) (q:draft)
lama = (i:2) (t:ppm) (d:<lam> with the suffix <a>, showing time or manner; after a verb, at the time of doing, as {a kuan lama}, as he goes in; {nitak lama} is in the evening and {a sia lama} in a bad way) (b:lam) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lama = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:why) (d:Aramaic word quoted untranslated in the cry of Jesus on the cross, NIV lema) (q:draft)
lamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:direction) (d:<lam>, direction, with the marker <ah>: toward, in the direction of) (b:lam)
lamah = (i:2) (t:n) (w:side/area) (d:<lam>, side, with the marker <ah>: on the side of, in the part lying that way) (b:lam) (r:1.3.24)
lambaangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:turning aside/stopping on the way) (d:leaving one's road to call on someone; the exact sense of <baang> is not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
lambehte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:side rooms/annexes) (d:rooms built on against the wall of a house; plural <te>) (q:draft)
lamdan = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wonderful/marvellous/amazing) (d:<lamdang> written short, with an apostrophe, before <mahmah>) (q:draft)
lamdang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:surprise) (d:the feeling that something is strange or unexpected; {lamdang sa} is to feel surprise at something)
lamdang = (i:2) (t:n) (w:shock)
lamdang = (i:3) (t:v) (w:astonish/amaze/nonplus/startle/astound/stun) (d:be wonderful or astonishing; with <sa>, {lamdang sa}, be astonished at something)
lamdangdang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:strange/various strange) (d:<lamdang>, strange, with its last syllable repeated: strange things of many kinds) (q:draft)
lamdangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:wonderfully/marvellously/strangely) (d:<lamdang>, wonderful or strange, with <in>: in a wonderful or strange way; {pau lamdangin} is in a strange tongue) (b:lamdang) (q:draft)
lamdanglua = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:too wonderful/too amazing) (d:<lamdang> with <lua>, too much) (b:lamdang) (q:draft)
lamdangpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very strange/marvellous/foreign) (d:<lamdang> with the intensifier <pi>; {thu lamdangpi} is a strange thing, {a lamdangpi khatin} is in a wonderful way) (b:lamdang) (q:draft)
lamdangpipi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very marvellous/most wonderful) (d:<lamdangpi> with <pi> repeated for emphasis; {na lamdangpipi} are marvellous things) (b:lamdangpi) (q:draft)
lamdangsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be amazed/be astonished/be surprised/wonder) (d:find something strange or wonderful, <lamdang> with <sa>) (b:lamdang) (q:draft)
lamdangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be surprised at/find strange/wonder at) (d:form of <lamdangsa> used before <ding> and <huai>: {lamdangsak ding hi lo hi}, it is no wonder) (b:lamdangsa) (r:30.5.13) (q:draft)
lamdangsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spectacle/astonishment/wonder/amazement) (d:<lamdangsak> with the noun suffix <na>: the feeling of wonder or astonishment; {lamdangsakna tawh en} is look at in astonishment) (b:lamdangsak)
lamdangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wonders/wonderful deeds/marvels) (d:plural of <lamdang> wonderful, after <na> thing or <nasepna> deed) (s:nalamdangte) (b:lamdang) (q:draft)
lamding = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build) (d:<lam>, build, with <ding> written as one word: to build, going to build) (b:lam) (q:draft)
lamdung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:street/roadside/wayside) (d:the length of a road: the streets of a town where people pass, or the ground along the side of a path) (s:lampidung) (r:20.7.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lamdungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:along the road/along the path/on the street) (d:<lamdung>, the length of a road, street, with the marker <ah>; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (q:draft)
Lamek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lamech) (d:name of two men: a descendant of Cain who had two wives, and the son of Methuselah and father of Noah) (r:1.5.28)
lamen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hope for/expect/look forward to) (d:look ahead to something with hope or expectation; the form <lamet> is used before endings such as <leh>, <loh>, <ding> and <na>) (q:draft)
lamenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hoping for/expecting/waiting for) (d:<lamen> with the linking ending <in>, hoping or expecting while another action follows) (b:lamen) (q:draft)
