leitungte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:worlds/universe) (d:plural of <leitung>, earth, world; in the verse, the whole created universe) (b:leitung) (q:draft)
leitungteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the whole earth/all the earth) (d:<leitung>, earth, with <teng>, all of: the whole earth, every part of it) (s:leitungbup/leipi) (b:leitung) (q:draft)
leivang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hole in the ground/hole) (d:<lei> ground with <vang>, opening: a hole or hollow in the earth used as a hiding place) (q:draft)
leivui = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dust) (d:fine dry earth; also the dust of the ground from which man was made and to which he returns) (r:1.2.7)
leivui = (i:2) (t:n) (w:dirt) (d:loose earth picked up from the ground and thrown)
Leivui = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dust) (d:<leivui> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse) (b:leivui) (q:draft)
leivuineel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fine dust) (d:<leivui>, dust, with <neel>, fine: very fine dust that the wind carries off) (q:draft)
leivuite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dust) (d:plural form of <leivui>; English uses the singular) (b:leivui) (q:draft)
leivuithem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:speck of dust/refuse/scum) (d:<leivui> dust with <them>, a small bit; in the verse a picture of something worthless) (q:draft, low confidence)
leivumte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ridges/mounds of earth) (d:<lei> earth with <vum>, heaped up, and plural <te>: the raised ridges of a ploughed field) (q:draft)
leizang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flatland/plain) (d:<lei>, land, with <zang>, flat: a plain, a wide stretch of flat low land) (s:zanglei)
leizang = (i:2) (t:n) (w:level ground) (d:ground that is even, where the foot stands firm)
leizangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:on the plains/in the plain) (d:<leizang>, plain, with the ending <ah>, at or in: on the plains) (b:leizang) (q:draft)
leizawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be bought/be able to buy) (d:<lei> buy with <zawh>, be able; with {hi lo}, cannot be bought) (q:draft)
leizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to buy/can buy) (d:apparently <lei> buy with <zo> be able, in a proverb: only skin can buy skin; the NIV has skin for skin) (q:draft, low confidence)
leizum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cape/headland/point of land) (d:apparently <lei> land with <zum> pointed, a point of land running into the sea; the NIV names only Salmone) (s:leidawk) (q:draft, low confidence)
lek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weigh enough/have weight) (d:of something put on a balance: be heavy enough to bring the scale down; {lek lo} and {lek zo kei} are too light, found wanting; also written <leek>) (s:leek) (q:draft)
Lekah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Lekah) (d:place in Judah whose founder was Er son of Shelah, named only in the genealogy of Judah) (r:13.4.21) (q:draft)
leklek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:skipping along/bounding) (d:placed after <diang> leap, of a flock of goats moving down a hill, skipping along, bounding again and again) (r:22.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
lekuana = (i:1) (t:num) (w:nineteenth) (d:second part of {sawm lekuana}, the nineteenth: <le> and, <kua> nine, with the ordinal ending <na>) (q:draft)
lel = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:only/merely/just) (d:placed after a verb or a noun phrase: nothing more than that; most often as {hi lel}, is merely, and {bang hi lel ahi hiam}, what is it after all) (s:bek) (q:draft)
lela = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:brightly/radiantly) (d:placed after <taang> shine or <taangsak> make shine) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overcome/be no match for/fail) (d:form of <lel>: lose to someone, or be unable to manage a load or a duty) (s:guallelh) (a:gualzawh) (b:lel) (q:draft)
lelhlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defeat/being beaten) (d:<lelh> be overcome, with <lam>, the fact or state of: {a lelhlam a kitheih ciangin} is when he saw that he was beaten) (q:draft)
lelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defeat) (d:<lelh>, be overcome, with the noun suffix <na>: defeat; {lelhna thuak} is suffer defeat, be defeated) (s:guallelhna) (a:zawhna/gualzawhna) (b:lelh) (q:draft)
lelhpipi = (t:see) <lelhpipi-un>
lelhpipi-un = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:staggering/barely managing) (d:<lelh>, be unable to manage a load, with <pipi> and the ending <un>: of boys carrying loads too heavy for them) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelhtaak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:begin to lose to/begin to fall before) (d:<lelh>, be overcome, lose to someone, with <taak>; spelling of <lelhtak>; of the person before whom one has begun to fall) (s:lelhtak) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelhtak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:begin to lose to/begin to fall before) (d:<lelh>, be overcome, lose to someone, with <tak>; of the person before whom one has begun to fall) (s:lelhtaak) (b:lelh) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelhtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be overcome by/be no match for) (d:<lelh>, lose, with <tuak>, meet with: find an enemy too strong) (q:draft)
lelin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:merely/just/only) (d:<lel> with the adverbial suffix <in>; {bang lelin} means as no more than) (s:bekin) (b:lel) (q:draft)
lellelte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:mere) (d:<lel> only, merely, doubled and with the plural <te>: {mihing lellelte} is those who are no more than human, mere mortals) (s:lelte) (q:draft)
lelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being only/being merely) (d:<lel>, only or merely, with the noun-forming ending <na>, the fact of being merely so, as in {mi ahih lelna}, their being only human) (b:lel) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:condemn/make lose/deny justice) (d:<lel> lose, with the causative <sak>: make someone lose his case before the judges) (s:mawhsak) (a:diksak) (b:lel) (q:draft)
leltak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:merely/just/mere) (d:emphatic form of <lel>, only, often in questions that make little of something, {bang hi leltak ahi hiam}, what are they really) (b:lel) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:mere/no more than/only) (d:<lel>, only or merely, with plural {-te}: those that are nothing more than what is said, as {mihing ahi lelte}, mere humans) (s:lellelte) (b:lel) (q:draft)
lelun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:just/merely) (d:<lel>, only, merely, with the ending <un> used for a plural subject; {a gen bang lelun}, just in the way they spoke of) (b:lel) (q:draft, low confidence)
lem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repair/caulk/mend) (d:in the verse, of craftsmen who repair or caulk a ship) (q:draft, low confidence)
lemin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:unrolling/opening) (d:<lem> with the ending <in>; in the verse, of opening or unrolling a book or scroll) (s:phenin) (q:draft, low confidence)
lemkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take away/remove/roll away) (d:in the verses, move the stone away from the mouth of a tomb) (q:draft)
lemtuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reconciling/bringing to agreement) (d:<lemtuah>, bring two sides into agreement, with the linking ending <in>) (s:kilemsakkikin) (q:draft)
Lemuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lemuel) (d:king whose mother’s teaching is recorded in Proverbs 31) (r:20.31.1/20.31.4)
len = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold/take hold of/grasp) (d:take or keep in the hand; also of a ring that holds a carrying pole, and of holding on to what is good or to God; {kip takin len} is hold firmly) (s:tawi) (a:khah/khahsuah) (q:draft)
Len = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold/hold back/handle) (d:<len> written with a capital at the start of a quoted command) (b:len) (q:draft)
lencip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold fast/grip/bind/cling to) (d:<len>, hold, with <cip>, tightly: hold and not let go) (s:lenkip/letcip/letkip) (a:khahsuah) (b:len) (r:24.49.24) (q:draft)
lencipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:holding fast/holding back) (d:<lencip>, hold tightly, with the linking ending <in>) (s:lenkipin) (b:lencip) (q:draft)
leng = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:if) (d:if I, should I; conditional ending for a first person singular subject, matching <leh> for other persons) (q:draft)
lenggah = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:grape) (d:shorter spelling of <leenggah>; {lenggah lo} is a vineyard) (s:leenggah) (q:draft)
lenggahte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:grapes/vines) (d:plural of <lenggah>) (s:leenggahte) (b:lenggah) (q:draft)
lenggahzu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wine) (d:strong drink made from grapes) (s:leenggahzu) (q:draft)
lengin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flying/soaring) (d:<leng>, also written <leeng>, fly, with the ending <in>) (s:leengin) (q:draft)
lengkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:revolt/rebel/break away) (d:break away from the rule of another) (s:leengkhia/lehdo) (q:draft)
lengkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:gush out/flow out) (d:said of water coming out with force) (s:luangkhia/phulkhia) (q:draft, low confidence)
lengkhiamang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee away/vanish/come right off) (d:<lengkhia>, break away or come out, with <mang>, gone: go off and disappear; also of skin rubbed off the shoulders) (q:draft)
lenglua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overwhelm/overcome) (d:in the verse, said of a face or look that is too much for the one who sees it; <lua> is too much, the first part is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
lengmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fly away/be blown away) (d:<leng> fly with <mang>, gone: fly off or be carried off out of sight) (s:leengmang) (q:draft)
lengmasel = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:mint) (d:a garden herb of which a tenth was given; also written <leengmasel>) (s:leengmasel) (q:draft)
lengpei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wheel) (d:wheel of a cart or chariot, also written <leengpei>) (s:leengpei/pei) (q:draft)
lengsawn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rumour/report/hearsay) (d:in {kam lengsawn}, word that flies on from one person to another) (s:kamlengsawn/kamdawn) (q:draft)
lengsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come out through/pass right through) (d:of a spear, go through the body and come out on the other side) (q:draft)
lengsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fly down/swoop down) (d:<leng>, also written <leeng>, fly, with <suk> downward; paired with <lengto>) (s:leengsuk) (a:lengto) (q:draft)
lengto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fly up/soar up) (d:<leng>, also written <leeng>, fly, with <to> upward; paired with <lengsuk>) (s:leengto) (a:lengsuk) (q:draft)
lengzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:even if/even though) (d:<leng>, if I, with <zong>, even: even if I, for a first person subject) (q:draft)
lenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking hold of/holding/grasping/seizing) (d:<len> with the linking suffix {-in}, taking hold of and then doing the next action) (b:len) (r:10.13.11) (q:draft)
lenkawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:while holding) (d:<len> hold with <kawm>, while, and the ending <in>) (q:draft)
lenkhiatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sweep away/carry off/blow away) (d:of a strong wind, carry something off with it) (q:draft)
