lensak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to be carried off/make fly) (d:with <huih>, wind: let the wind carry someone away; apparently <leng> fly with <sak> cause) (s:leensak) (q:draft, low confidence)
lenuai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:armpit/underarm) (q:draft)
Leshem = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Leshem) (d:city in the far north taken by the tribe of Dan and renamed Dan, also called Laish) (r:6.19.47)
let = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overflow/flood) (d:of water, rise and spill over) (s:dimlet/letkhia) (a:kiam) (q:draft)
let = (i:2) (t:v) (w:hold/hold back/keep) (d:form of <len>, hold, used in dependent clauses) (a:khah) (q:draft)
let = (i:3) (t:adv) (w:through/right through) (d:placed after a verb of stabbing or shooting: so that the weapon passes through the body) (q:draft, low confidence)
