leteh = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:if/if only) (d:placed after a verb: if one does so, should one do so; also used in wishes and polite requests) (q:draft)
Lethusim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Letushites) (d:people descended from Dedan, a grandson of Abraham and Keturah) (r:1.25.3)
letin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:through/right through) (d:<let> with the linking ending <in>, after a verb of stabbing, so as to go through, {sun letin}, {dawt letin}, run through) (b:let) (q:draft)
letin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:overflowing/to overflowing) (d:after <dim>, full, so full that it runs over) (b:let) (q:draft)
letkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overflow/flood over) (d:<let> overflow with <khia>, out: of water rising over its banks) (s:dimlet) (b:let) (q:draft)
letkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blow away/drive away/sweep away) (d:of the wind carrying something off; {huih letkhiat ansi} is chaff the wind blows away) (s:mutkhiat/letmang) (q:draft)
letkhiatmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry away/blow away) (d:of the wind, carry clouds off so that they are gone; <mang> is away, lost) (s:mutmang/leenmang) (q:draft)
letkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blow away/carry off) (d:<letkhiat>, blow away, with the causative <sak>: of wind carrying off blossoms) (b:letkhiat) (q:draft)
letkip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold firmly/hold fast) (d:<let>, form of <len> hold, with <kip> firm) (s:letcip/lenkip/lencip) (a:khahsuah) (q:draft)
letmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blow away/carry off) (d:of wind: carry something off out of sight; {huih letmang}, blown away by the wind) (s:mutmang/leenmang) (q:draft, low confidence)
letmat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inch) (d:a small unit of length in the 1932 text, which gives cubits as <pi> feet and {letmat}; {letmat kua}, nine, stands for a span and {pi nih le letmat thum} for a cubit and a half) (q:draft, low confidence)
letmatthuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:signet ring/signet/seal) (d:a ring worn on the hand and used to stamp a seal or signature) (s:zungbuh/minthuhna) (q:draft)
letna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hold/grasp) (d:<let>, form of <len> hold, with the noun suffix <na>; {kumpi aana a letna}, his hold on the royal power) (b:let) (q:draft)
letsan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handle) (d:apparently the handle of a plow, the part that is held, in {lokhawhna leeng letsan len}, hold the plow) (q:draft, low confidence)
letsongin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as a gift/as an offering) (d:<letsong>, gift, with the ending <in>: given or sent as a gift) (s:piakkhongin) (b:letsong) (q:draft)
