Levi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Levi) (d:third son of Jacob and Leah and ancestor of the tribe of Levi, the tribe set apart for the service of the sanctuary; also the tax collector whom Jesus called, and two ancestors of Jesus) (r:1.35.23)
Levite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Levites) (d:the members of the tribe of Levi, who served at the tabernacle and the temple and assisted the priests) (b:Levi) (r:43.1.19/2.6.19)
li = (i:1) (t:num) (w:four) (d:the number four; it follows the noun it counts, and {sawm-le-li} is fourteen) (r:41.8.9)
liah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cover/overshadow/shade/hide) (d:come between something and the light, heat or sight, so as to shade, shield or hide it) (s:khuh/tuam) (q:draft)
