Maath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maath) (d:an ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke) (r:42.3.26)
maavang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prosper/succeed/be successful) (d:to prosper or succeed, said of a person or of work that goes well, from <maa>, success, and <vang>; also written <mavang>) (s:mavang/maapai/daupai/vang) (q:draft)
maavanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:success/prosperity) (d:success or prosperity, from <maavang>, prosper, in the form {maavan} before the noun suffix <na>) (s:daupaina/maa) (q:draft)
Maaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maaz) (d:son of Ram, the firstborn of Jerahmeel, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.27) (q:draft)
Maaziah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maaziah) (d:head of the twenty-fourth division of priests in the time of David; also a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.8/13.24.18)
maban = (i:1) (t:n) (w:continuation/what lies ahead/the rest) (d:the part still ahead of a work or course already begun; <maban zom> is carry on what others began, {maban sem} is go on with the work ahead) (q:draft, low confidence)
Madai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Madai) (d:son of Japheth, ancestor of the Medes) (r:1.10.2)
madawk = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:foremost/at the front) (d:being at the front or the nearest edge; {a madawk teng} is the foremost part, in Numbers the outskirts of the camp as seen from a height) (q:draft, low confidence)
madawkah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the front/in the front line) (d:<madawk> foremost with <ah>, at: at the very front, in the verse of a battle) (s:madawkin) (b:madawk) (q:draft)
madawkin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:forward/in front/at the front) (d:<madawk> foremost with <in>; {hong madawkin} is coming forward) (s:madawkah) (b:madawk) (q:draft)
madawkte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:front ranks/those in front/vanguard) (d:<madawk> foremost with plural <te>; the front part of an army, set against <nungdalte> the rear) (a:nungdalte) (b:madawk) (q:draft)
madiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:just before/shortly before) (d:<ma> before with <diak>: a little short of, just before reaching a place) (q:draft)
madiakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:just before/shortly before) (d:<madiak> just before with <in>; {a tun madiakin} is when he had almost arrived) (b:madiak) (q:draft)
Madmannah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Madmannah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.31/13.2.49)
Madmen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Madmen) (d:a town of Moab named in the prophecy of Jeremiah against Moab) (r:24.48.2) (q:draft)
Madmenah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Madmenah) (d:town north of Jerusalem whose people fled before the Assyrian advance) (r:23.10.31)
Madon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Madon) (d:Canaanite royal city in the north whose king Jobab joined Jabin of Hazor against Joshua) (r:6.11.1)
Magadan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Magadan) (d:place on the shore of the Sea of Galilee to which Jesus went by boat) (r:40.15.39)
Magbish = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Magbish) (d:town whose people returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.30)
Magdala = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Magdala) (d:town on the western shore of the Sea of Galilee, home of Mary Magdalene) (r:40.27.61/41.15.47)
Magdalene = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Magdalene) (d:byname of Mary of Magdala, a follower of Jesus from whom seven demons had gone out) (r:42.8.2/42.24.10)
Magdiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Magdiel) (d:one of the chiefs of Edom descended from Esau) (r:1.36.43/13.1.54)
Magog = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/land) (w:Magog) (d:son of Japheth; also the land of Gog in the prophecy of Ezekiel) (r:1.10.2)
Magpiash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Magpiash) (d:one of the leaders of the people who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.20)
mah = (i:1) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case)
mah = (i:2) (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate selective case)
mahah = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:right in/right at) (d:emphatic <mah> with the place marker <ah>, in, at or upon that very place or person) (b:mah) (q:draft)
Mahalab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mahalab) (d:town on the border of the territory of Asher, near Akzib) (r:6.19.29)
Mahalale = (t:see) <Mahalale-el>
Mahalale-el = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalalel) (d:son of Kenan and father of Jared in the line from Adam to Noah, an ancestor of Jesus) (q:draft)
Mahalaleel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalalel) (d:son of Kenan and father of Jared in the line from Adam to Noah, an ancestor of Jesus) (r:42.3.37)
