Mahalate = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalate/Mahalalel) (d:first part of {Mahalate-el}, a spelling of Mahalalel, the father of Jared, in the genealogy of Luke) (r:42.3.37)
Mahalath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Mahalath) (d:name of two women: a daughter of Ishmael whom Esau married, and a granddaughter of David who married Rehoboam) (r:1.28.9)
Mahalelel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalalel) (d:son of Kenan and father of Jared in the line from Adam to Noah) (r:1.5.16)
Mahanaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mahanaim) (d:town east of the Jordan in Gilead, where Ish-Bosheth ruled and where David stayed during the revolt of Absalom) (r:6.13.26/11.4.14)
Mahanasim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mahanaim) (d:a spelling of Mahanaim, the town east of the Jordan in Gilead) (r:6.13.30)
Mahanehdan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mahaneh Dan) (d:place between Zorah and Eshtaol, west of Kiriath Jearim, where the men of Dan camped; the name means camp of Dan) (r:7.13.25/7.18.12)
Maharai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maharai) (d:one of David's mighty warriors, from Netophah, commander of the army division for the tenth month) (r:10.23.28/13.11.30)
Mahath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahath) (d:name of two Levites, a Kohathite son of Amasai and a temple overseer in the time of Hezekiah) (r:14.29.12/14.31.13)
Mahavah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mahavah/Mahavite) (d:place from which Eliel, one of David's mighty warriors, came; the NIV has Eliel the Mahavite) (r:13.11.46)
Mahazioth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahazioth) (d:son of Heman, a temple musician in the time of David) (r:13.25.4)
Mahershalahashbaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maher-Shalal-Hash-Baz) (d:son of the prophet Isaiah, whose name means quick to the plunder, swift to the spoil) (r:23.8.3/23.8.1)
Mahershalalhasbaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maher-Shalal-Hash-Baz) (d:son of the prophet Isaiah, whose name means quick to the plunder, swift to the spoil) (r:23.8.3/23.8.1)
Mahil = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahli) (d:son of Merari and grandson of Levi, a spelling of Mahli) (r:13.6.29)
mahin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (w:very/same/just) (d:emphatic <mah> with the marker <in>; after a time word, on that very day, at that very time, just now) (b:mah) (q:draft)
Mahlah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Mahlah) (d:eldest of the five daughters of Zelophehad of the tribe of Manasseh; also a child of Hammoleketh in the same tribe) (r:4.36.11/4.26.33)
Mahli = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahli) (d:name of two Levites, a son of Merari and a son of Mushi) (r:13.6.47)
Mahlon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahlon) (d:son of Elimelek and Naomi, the first husband of Ruth) (r:8.1.2/8.1.5)
mahmah = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:exactly) (d:marks the word before it as exactly the one meant: that very night, the very word, I myself) (s:teekteek)
mahmah = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:only/just)
mahmaha = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very/exceedingly/greatly) (d:<mahmah>, very, with <a> linking it to the verb that follows) (s:mahmahin/nakpi/nakpitakin) (b:mahmah) (q:draft)
mahmahah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:right at/at the very) (d:<mahmah>, exactly, with the place marker <ah>: at the very place, right in or on) (s:takah) (b:mahmah) (q:draft)
mahmahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very/exceedingly/greatly) (d:<mahmah>, very, with the adverb suffix <in>, after a describing word or verb: very, greatly) (s:mahmaha/nakpi/nakpitakin) (b:mahmah) (r:4.11.10) (q:draft)
mahmahin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:on that very) (d:after a time word: {tua ni mahmahin} is on that very day, <tu mahmahin> is right now) (b:mahmah) (q:draft)
mahmahlam = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how very) (d:<mahmah> very with <lam> way, manner, after a descriptive word: how very much it is so) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahmahna = (i:1) (t:part) (d:intensifier <mahmah> with the noun-forming suffix <na>; the phrase before it becomes a noun meaning great or extreme, as in {heh mahmahna}, great anger) (b:mahmah) (q:draft)
mahmahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the very one) (d:<mahmah> very, truly with <pa> marking a man: the man who truly did what the verb before it says) (b:mahmah) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahmahpi = (t:see) <mahmahpi-in>
mahmahpi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:exceedingly/very greatly) (d:<mahmah> very with <pi> great and <in> making an adverb, after a descriptive word) (s:mahmahin) (q:draft)
mahmahsa = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very much/greatly) (d:<mahmah> very, with <sa>, already: of a state fully reached) (s:mahmahin) (b:mahmah) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahmahte = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very) (d:<mahmah> with the plural <te> after a descriptive word: those that are very much so, as in {a lungkham mahmahte}, those in great anguish) (b:mahmah) (q:draft)
Mahol = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahol) (d:father of Heman, Kalkol and Darda, wise men with whom Solomon is compared) (r:11.4.31)
Mahseiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahseiah) (d:father of Neriah and grandfather of Baruch and Seraiah in the time of Jeremiah) (r:24.32.12/24.51.59)
mahun = (i:1) (t:part) (d:emphatic <mah> with the ending <un>, placed after a phrase where the doers are several: right, just, the very; {a suah tung mahun}, from the very time of birth) (b:mah) (q:draft, low confidence)
mai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:face) (d:the front of the head; {mai kun} is bow the face down and {mai tuam} is cover the face) (s:maitang) (r:1.4.5)
mai = (i:2) (t:n) (w:ahead) (d:the place in front of someone; {a mai pai} is go ahead of him, set against {a nung zui}, follow behind) (s:mailam) (a:nung)
mai = (i:3) (t:n) (w:future) (d:the time ahead, most often as {mai lamah}, in the future) (s:mailam)
mai-ahsiampi = (t:todo) (q:draft, two words run together in the text: <mai-ah>, before, and <siampi>, priest)
maiah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:before/in front of/in the presence of) (d:<mai>, face, with the place ending <ah>: placed after a noun, in front of or in the sight of someone) (a:nungah) (b:mai) (q:draft)
Maiakah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Maakah) (d:home or people of Ahasbai, the father of Eliphelet, one of the mighty warriors of David; the NIV has the Maakathite) (r:10.23.34)
maigum = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:gloomy/downcast/sullen) (d:with a dark, sad face; set against <maitai>, cheerful) (s:dahmai/maimial) (a:maitai) (q:draft)
maigumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gloom/sadness) (d:<maigum> gloomy-faced with the noun suffix <na>) (a:maitaina) (b:maigum) (q:draft)
maigumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make gloomy/sadden) (d:<maigum> gloomy-faced with the causative <sak>: make the face downcast) (s:gumsak) (a:maitaisak) (b:maigum) (q:draft)
maihem = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:disfigured) (d:with a marred or defective face, one in a list of bodily defects) (q:draft, low confidence)
maikhin = (t:see) <maikhin'na>
maikhin'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sullenness/sulking) (d:a sullen, displeased face; noun in <na>) (s:maikhinna) (q:draft)
maikhing = (i:1) (t:v) (w:look sad/be downcast/be dismayed) (d:<mai> face with <khing>: have a sad or fallen face) (a:maitaii) (q:draft)
maikhingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:with a downcast face/gloomily/sullenly) (d:<maikhing> with <in>: with a face that shows sorrow, shame or displeasure) (b:maikhing) (q:draft)
maikhingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make downcast/dismay/put to shame) (d:<maikhing> be downcast, with the causative <sak>) (s:maizumsak/maisiasak) (b:maikhing) (q:draft)
maikhinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sullenness/sulking) (d:a sullen, displeased face; noun in <na>) (s:maikhin'na) (q:draft)
maikun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bow down/bow with the face to the ground) (d:<mai> face with <kun> bend, stoop) (s:maipuk/boksuk) (q:draft)
maikunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bowing down/bowing with the face to the ground) (d:<maikun> bow the face down with the linking <in>) (b:maikun) (q:draft)
mailam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:future) (d:the time ahead; {mailam thu gen} means prophesy, speak of things to come) (s:mai) (q:draft)
mailam = (i:2) (t:n) (w:front/ahead/forward) (d:the side or direction in front) (s:mai) (a:nunglam) (q:draft)
Mailamah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:ahead/in the future/in time to come) (d:<mailam>, future or front, with the marker <ah>; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (s:tunung) (q:draft)
maim = (t:see) <Mishrefoth-maim>
maimai = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:merely/just) (d:placed after a verb: do something only so-so, without aim or fullness) (s:lel) (q:draft, low confidence)
maiman = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish/vanish/be blotted out) (d:form of <maimang> written with an apostrophe before <loh>, <nadingin> and <na>; {maiman’na} is destruction) (s:beimang/mangthang) (r:23.51.19) (q:draft)
maimang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish/vanish/be wiped out) (d:be lost completely; after another verb it adds the sense utterly, completely) (s:beimang/mangthang) (q:draft)
maimangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perishing/wasting away) (d:<maimang> perish, with the linking ending <in>) (b:maimang) (q:draft)
maimangpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:vanish quickly/disappear soon) (d:<maimang> vanish with <pak> quickly) (s:thengpak) (q:draft)
maimangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wipe out/blot out/destroy/make vanish) (d:<maimang>, perish, with the causative {-sak}) (s:susia/siasak) (b:maimang) (q:draft)
maimangta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have vanished/be gone/disappear) (d:<maimang> with <ta>, which marks a change that has now come about) (s:beimangta/thengta) (b:maimang) (q:draft)
maimankhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lost/come to nothing) (d:<maiman> vanish with <khak>, happen to: end up lost, said of greatness) (q:draft)
maimanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:destruction/ruin) (d:<maiman> perish with the noun suffix <na>) (s:siatna) (b:maiman) (q:draft)
maimansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy/wipe out) (d:<maiman> perish with the causative <sak>) (s:susia/siasak) (b:maiman) (q:draft)
maimawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fail/come to nothing/go to waste/perish) (d:come to nothing: of a promise, fail to come true; of people and land, be lost or laid waste) (q:draft)
maimial = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sad-faced/gloomy/dark) (d:<mai> face with <mial>, dark: looking sad; of a day, gloomy) (s:maigum/dahmai) (a:maitai) (q:draft)
maimom = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:spider) (d:{maimom khau} is a spider’s thread or web, {maimom bu} a spider’s nest or web) (r:23.59.5) (q:draft)
mainawhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:resolutely/with the face set toward) (d:setting the face toward a place and pressing on; <mai> is face) (q:draft)
mainawt = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go forward/advance/move on) (d:<mai> front with <nawt> push on) (s:maipai) (a:nungkik/nungkin) (q:draft)
mainawtin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:press forward/advance) (d:<mainawt> go forward with the linking suffix <in>) (b:mainawt) (q:draft)
maingalsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:comfort/embolden) (d:make someone feel less ashamed) (q:draft, low confidence)
maingat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:face/turn the face toward/look toward) (d:<mai> face with <ngat> turn toward; the opposite is <nungngat> turn the back; {maingat lo} is with the face turned away) (a:nungngat) (r:24.50.5) (q:draft)
maingatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:facing/with the face toward) (d:with the face turned toward something; {lei maingatin} is face to the ground) (b:maingat) (q:draft)
maingatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:facing) (d:<maingat> face toward with <sa>, already in that state: with the face already turned that way) (b:maingat) (q:draft, low confidence)
mainul = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handkerchief/cloth) (d:<mai> face with <nul>, wipe: a cloth for wiping the face) (s:mainulna) (q:draft)
Mainul = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Mainul)
mainulna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:handkerchief) (d:<mainul> with the noun suffix <na>: what the face is wiped with; {mainulna puan} is a face cloth) (s:mainul) (b:mainul) (q:draft)
mainulpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:towel) (d:<mainul> with <pi>, large) (b:mainul) (q:draft)
maipai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go forward/advance) (d:<mai> front with <pai> go; the opposite is <nungkik> go back) (s:mainawt) (a:nungkik) (q:draft)
maipha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:favor)
maipha = (i:2) (t:n) (w:favor/esteem) (d:goodwill shown to someone; <maipha ngah> and <maipha mu> mean find favor) (s:maiphatna/deihsakna) (r:1.6.8)
maiphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:esteem/good standing/favor) (d:being well regarded; {maiphatna a ngah mi} is one held in high regard) (s:maipha) (q:draft, low confidence)
maiphut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:confront/face/come against) (d:<mai> face with <phut>: meet someone head on; of the wind, blow against) (q:draft)
maipuak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:look/countenance) (d:the look on the face, facial expression; with <zia>, manner) (s:maiput/maisuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
maipuakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:appearance/look/expression) (d:how the face is carried: the look of a person or thing) (s:maiput/maisuah) (q:draft)
maipuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow with face to the ground) (d:go down with the face to the ground, in a fall or to show respect) (s:boksuk/maikun) (q:draft)
maipukin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:face down/prostrate) (d:<maipuk> fall on the face with <in>: bowing with the face to the ground) (s:khuplamin) (b:maipuk) (q:draft)
maipuksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow with face to the ground) (d:<maipuk> fall facedown with <suk> downward) (s:boksuk) (b:maipuk) (q:draft)
maiput = (i:1) (t:n) (w:look on the face/countenance/expression) (d:<mai> face with <put>, bear: the look that the face shows) (s:maisuah/maipuak) (q:draft)
maisa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:devastated/lying in ruins) (d:follows <kisia> be ruined; <mai> after a verb with <sa>, already in that state: left ruined) (q:draft, low confidence)
maisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forgive/pardon) (d:let go of a wrong done, most often with <mawhna>, sin; also cancel a debt) (s:mawhmaisak/maisiangsak) (a:mawhsak) (r:19.85.2) (q:draft)
maisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forgive/pardon/cancel) (d:<maisak> with the ending <in>, which links it to the following verb: forgiving a sin or cancelling a debt and then doing something more) (b:maisak) (q:draft)
maisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forgiveness/remission/cancelling of debt) (d:<maisak>, forgive, with {-na}; of sins and also of debts) (s:mawhmaisakna/maitheihna) (b:maisak) (r:51.1.14) (q:draft)
maisaknop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to forgive/be willing to forgive) (d:<maisak> forgive with <nop> want) (q:draft)
maisaksa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have forgiven/pardoned) (d:<maisak> forgive with <sa>, already done) (b:maisak) (q:draft)
maisakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who forgive) (d:<maisak> forgive with plural <te>) (b:maisak) (q:draft)
maisia = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:ashamed/confounded/disgraced) (d:<mai> face with <sia> bad: with the face spoiled by shame; {maisia sak} is put to shame) (s:maizum) (q:draft)
maisiangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pardon/forgive) (s:maisak/mawhmaisak) (q:draft)
maisiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put to shame/confound) (d:<maisia> ashamed with the causative <sak>) (s:maizumsak/maikhingsak) (b:maisia) (q:draft)
maisiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set the face against/turn against/oppose) (d:show displeasure toward someone, said of God turning against a wrongdoer) (b:maisia) (q:draft)
maisiatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set one's face against/be hostile to) (d:<maisiat> with the linking suffix <in>) (b:maisiat) (q:draft)
maisuah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:countenance/expression/look) (d:the look on the face that shows what one feels) (s:maiput/maipuak) (q:draft)
maitai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cheerful/radiant/bright-faced) (d:of a bright, glad face; <maitai takin> is cheerfully; in Proverbs 7:13 of a bold face put on) (a:maigum/maimial) (q:draft)
maitaii = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cheerful/brighten) (d:of the face, be bright and glad) (a:maikhing) (q:draft)
maitaiina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:brightness/cheerfulness) (d:<maitaii> be bright of face with the noun suffix <na>) (s:maitaina) (a:maigumna) (b:maitaii) (q:draft)
maitaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cheerfulness/cheerful look/brightness) (d:<maitai> cheerful, bright of face with the noun suffix <na>; in Amos 5:20 brightness as opposed to gloom) (s:maitaiina) (a:maigumna) (b:maitai) (q:draft)
maitaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:brighten the face/make cheerful) (d:<maitai> cheerful, with the causative <sak>) (s:taiisak) (a:maigumsak) (b:maitai) (q:draft)
maitang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:face) (d:the face of a person or of God; {maitang kituahin} is face to face) (s:mai)
maitang = (i:2) (t:n) (w:surface) (d:the outer face of a thing, most often {lei maitang}, the surface of the ground)
maitangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the presence of/before/on the face) (d:<maitang> face with the place marker <ah>) (b:maitang) (q:draft)
maitangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:faces) (d:<maitang> face with plural <te>) (b:maitang) (q:draft)
maitheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be forgiven/be pardoned) (d:<mai> forgive with <theih>, can; {mawhna a maitheih nading} is for the forgiveness of sin) (s:kimaisak) (q:draft)
maitheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forgiveness/atonement) (d:<maitheih> be forgiven with the noun suffix <na>; {mawhnate a maitheihna ding} is for the forgiveness of sins) (s:maisakna/mawhmaisakna) (b:maitheih) (q:draft)
maivil = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek the favour of/court) (d:come to someone with gifts to win his goodwill) (q:draft)
maizum = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:ashamed) (d:feeling shame, from <mai>, face, and <zum>, be ashamed; {maizum sak} is put to shame) (s:maisia) (r:56.2.8)
maizumhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:shameful/disgraceful) (d:<maizum> be ashamed with <huai> for what causes a feeling) (s:zumhuai/mindaihuai) (q:draft)
maizumhuaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace) (d:<maizumhuai> shameful with the noun suffix <na>) (s:zumhuaina/maizumna) (b:maizumhuai) (q:draft)
maizumin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in shame/ashamed) (d:<maizum>, ashamed, with the ending <in>: feeling shame, in shame) (b:maizum) (q:draft)
maizumlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be put to shame by/be ashamed because of) (d:<maizum> ashamed with <lawh>, suffer on account of something) (q:draft)
maizumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace) (d:<maizum>, ashamed, with the noun suffix <na>; {maizumna thuak} and {maizumna ngah} mean be put to shame) (s:zumna/mindaina/zahhuaina) (a:pahtawina) (b:maizum) (q:draft)
maizumpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:humiliated/greatly ashamed) (d:<maizum> ashamed with <pi> great; with <in>, in great shame) (b:maizum) (q:draft)
maizumpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ashamed of) (d:<maizum> ashamed with <pih>: be ashamed about someone or something) (b:maizum) (q:draft)
maizumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shame/put to shame/humiliate) (d:<maizum> ashamed with the causative <sak>; in Luke 9.26 be ashamed of someone) (s:zumsak/maisiasak/mindaisak) (b:maizum) (q:draft)
mak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:son-in-law) (d:the husband of a daughter; {a mak ding} is a man who is going to marry the daughter) (s:makpa)
makaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead/guide) (d:go before others and show them the way; the verb that belongs to <makai>, leader) (s:lamkaih/lamlak) (a:zui) (b:makai) (q:draft)
makaihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leading/lead/guide) (d:<makaih> lead with the linking ending <in>: leading someone, after which the next action follows) (b:makaih) (q:draft)
makaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leadership/direction/supervision/guidance) (d:the act of leading, <makaih> lead with the noun ending <na>; {makaihna tawh} and {makaihna nuai-ah} mean under the leadership of someone) (s:lamlahna) (b:makaih) (q:draft)
makaihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leader/director) (d:<makaih> lead with <pa> marking a man: the one who leads, in the verse the director of the musicians) (s:makaipa/makai) (b:makaih) (q:draft)
makaihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leaders/guides) (d:<makaih> lead with the plural <te>: those who lead or guide a people) (s:makaite/lamlakte) (b:makaih) (q:draft)
makaipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leader/chief) (d:<makai> leader with <pa> marking a man: the man at the head of a tribe or group) (s:makai/makaihpa) (b:makai) (q:draft)
makaipi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chief leader/chief/champion) (d:<makai> leader with <pi> great: the foremost leader, as a champion among warriors; {la makaipi} is the chief musician) (s:makaipipa) (b:makai) (q:draft)
makaipipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chief/leader/head) (d:<makaipi> chief leader with <pa> marking a man: the head man of a place or of a group of workers) (s:makaipi/makaipa) (b:makaipi) (q:draft)
makaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leaders/chiefs/princes) (d:<makai> leader with the plural <te>: the leaders, chiefs or princes of a people) (s:uliante/ukpite/makaihte) (b:makai) (r:2.35.27) (q:draft)
Makaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Makaz) (d:town in the second district of Solomon, governed by Ben-Deker) (r:11.4.9)
Makbannai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Makbannai) (d:warrior of the tribe of Gad, the eleventh of those who joined David in the wilderness) (r:13.12.13)
Makbenah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Makbenah) (d:town in Judah founded by Sheva, a descendant of Caleb) (r:13.2.49)
Makedonia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Macedonia) (d:Roman province in the north of Greece, with the cities of Philippi, Thessalonica and Berea, where Paul founded churches) (r:47.8.1/44.27.2)
makeng = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:tamarisk) (d:the tamarisk, a tree of dry country; {makeng kung} is a tamarisk tree) (q:draft)
Makhael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Michael) (d:spelling of Michael in this verse: a man of Benjamin, son of Beriah) (r:13.8.16)
makhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send away together/divorce together) (d:apparently <ma>, divorce or send away, with <khawm>, together: the wives are sent away together with their children) (q:draft, low confidence)
makhelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:outrun/overtake) (d:get ahead of someone who is running the same way) (q:draft)
makhelhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:outrunning/outrun) (d:<makhelh> outrun with the linking ending <in>: getting ahead of someone, after which the next action follows) (b:makhelh) (q:draft)
Makheloth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Makheloth) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Haradah and Tahath) (r:4.33.25/4.33.26)
Makhi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maki) (d:father of Geuel, the man of Gad sent to spy out Canaan) (r:4.13.15) (q:draft)
Makhijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkijah) (d:spelling of Malkijah: name of several men, among them a Levite ancestor of Asaph and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:13.6.40/16.10.3)
Makhir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Machir/Makir) (d:son of Manasseh and father of Gilead; also the son of Ammiel of Lo Debar who sheltered Mephibosheth) (r:1.50.23)
Makhiram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkiram) (d:spelling of Malkiram, a son of King Jehoiachin of Judah) (r:13.3.18)
Makhirte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Makir/Makirites) (d:the clan descended from Makir son of Manasseh, who took Gilead) (b:Makhir) (r:4.32.39)
Makhishua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malki-Shua) (d:spelling of Malki-Shua, a son of King Saul) (r:13.9.39)
Makkedah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Makkedah) (d:Canaanite royal city in the lowland of Judah, with the cave where five Amorite kings hid from Joshua) (r:6.10.16/6.15.41)
makna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:the putting away of a wife, <mak> divorce with the noun ending <na>; {makna lai} is a certificate of divorce) (s:kimakna/kikhenna) (q:draft)
Maknadebai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maknadebai) (d:man of the family of Binnui who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.40)
makpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:son-in-law) (d:a son-in-law, and more widely a man related to a family by marriage; <mak> with <pa> marking a man) (s:mak) (b:mak) (q:draft)
Makpelah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Machpelah) (d:the field with a cave near Mamre at Hebron that Abraham bought as a burial place for his family) (r:1.23.17/1.23.19)
Makri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikri) (d:spelling of Mikri, a man of Benjamin whose descendant Elah lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:13.9.8)
maksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:<mak> divorce with <sa> marking a completed act: divorced, as in {a maksa numei}, a divorced woman; not the word <mak>, son-in-law) (s:kimasa/kikhensa) (q:draft)
maksim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:divorce quietly/divorce) (d:put away a wife or betrothed; the verse shows a divorce without public disgrace, and <sim> may add the sense secretly) (q:draft, low confidence)
makte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:son-in-law/sons-in-law) (b:mak) plural form of <mak>
Makte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sons-in-law) (d:<makte> written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (b:makte) (q:draft)
maktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:may divorce/can divorce) (d:<mak> divorce with <theih> can, be allowed) (s:mathei) (q:draft)
mal = (i:1) (t:n) (w:item/unit/single one/number) (d:a single one of things that are counted, such as an article, a word or a strand; {a mal sim} is to count one by one, {a mal zah} the full number, and {mal khat} a single word) (q:draft, low confidence)
Malakhi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malachi) (d:prophet through whom the Lord spoke to Israel after the exile; the last book of the Old Testament bears his name) (r:39.1.1)
malam = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb, apparently for doing something readily or straight off, as {na sang malam}, you so readily accept) (q:draft, low confidence)
maleep = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deposit/pledge/guarantee/first instalment) (d:something given in advance as assurance that the rest will follow; in the verses always said of the Holy Spirit) (q:draft)
malgol = (i:1) (t:n) (w:large drop/drop) (d:a big drop of liquid; {sisan malgol} is drops of blood) (q:draft)
malin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:one by one/individually/by number) (d:<mal> a single counted one with <in>: taken one at a time, person by person or item by item; {a mi malin} is man by man) (s:khatkhatin) (b:mal) (q:draft)
Malkam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkam) (d:man of Benjamin, a son of Shaharaim and his wife Hodesh) (r:13.8.9)
Malkhas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchus) (d:servant of the high priest whose right ear Peter cut off when Jesus was arrested) (r:43.18.10)
malkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one item/one word) (d:<mal> a single item with <khat> one; {malkhat khit malkhat} is one item after another, where the English has rule on rule or precept upon precept) (r:23.28.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
Malkhiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkijah) (d:name of two men in Jeremiah: the father of Pashhur, an official of King Zedekiah, and the son of the king who owned the cistern into which Jeremiah was thrown) (r:24.21.1/24.38.6) (q:draft)
Malkhiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchiel/Malkiel) (d:son of Beriah and grandson of Asher, ancestor of the Malkielite clan) (r:1.46.17/13.7.31)
Malkhijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchijah/Malkijah) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite ancestor of Asaph, the head of the fifth division of priests and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:13.6.40/16.10.3)
Malkhiram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkiram) (d:son of King Jehoiachin of Judah) (r:13.3.18)
Malkhishua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malki-Shua) (d:son of King Saul, killed with his father and brothers by the Philistines on Mount Gilboa) (r:9.14.49/13.8.33)
Malkhus = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchus) (d:servant of the high priest whose right ear Peter cut off when Jesus was arrested) (r:43.18.10)
Mallothi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mallothi) (d:son of Heman, head of the nineteenth division of temple musicians in the time of David) (r:13.25.4)
Malluk = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluk) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite of the family of Merari and a priest who returned from exile with Zerubbabel) (r:13.6.44/16.12.2)
Mallukhi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluchi/Malluk) (d:priestly family in the days of the high priest Joiakim, headed by Jonathan) (r:16.12.14)
malneu = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fine/thin) (d:<mal> a single strand with <neu> small: thin or fine, said of cord in {khau malneu}; the exact sense is not clear from one verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
Malta = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Malta) (d:island in the Mediterranean Sea south of Sicily where Paul and his companions came ashore after the shipwreck) (r:44.28.1)
malte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/letters/items) (d:<mal> a single one with the plural <te>: the single words of a song or writing, or the items of a list) (s:kammalte) (b:mal) (q:draft)
Maluk = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluk) (d:name of several men, among them a descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife and a priest who returned from exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.10.29/16.12.2)
Maluk = (i:2) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluch/Malluk) (d:name of several men, among them a descendant of Harim who had married a foreign wife and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:15.10.32/16.10.4)
Malukhi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluk) (d:priestly family in the days of the high priest Joiakim, headed by Jonathan) (r:16.12.14)
malzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:number/total number/count) (d:<mal> a counted one with <zah> amount: how many there are of things that are counted one by one) (s:phazah/nambat/omzah) (q:draft)
mam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:straight/smooth) (d:said of legs, where the English has straight) (a:kawi) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mamre = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mamre) (d:place near Hebron with great trees where Abraham lived and built an altar; also the name of an Amorite who was an ally of Abram) (r:1.35.27/1.18.1) (q:?)
mamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:straighten/make straight) (d:<mam> straight with the causative <sak>: make straight what is crooked or uneven) (s:tangsak) (b:mam) (q:draft)
mamsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:straighten again/make straight again) (d:<mamsak> straighten with <kik> again, back) (b:mamsak) (q:draft)
man = (i:4) (t:v) (w:seize/arrest/catch/capture) (d:take hold of with the hand, or catch and arrest a person) (a:khah) (r:14.23.15) (q:draft)
Man = (t:see) <Man-a>
man'suahsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:lost) (d:that had been lost, <mansuah> lose with <sa> already) (s:mansuahsa/mangsa) (q:draft)
Man-a = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:because of/on account of) (d:<man> reason or cause with <a>; in the section heading {Kikhen Man-a Lunggimna}, distress because of parting) (q:draft, low confidence)
man-unah = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:because) (d:<man> because, with <un> for a plural subject and <ah>: because they or because you, placed at the end of the clause that gives the reason) (s:manunah) (q:draft)
mana = (i:1) (t:n) (w:manna) (d:the food God gave Israel in the wilderness) (s:manna) (q:draft)
mana = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:because/because of) (d:<man> reason with <a>; follows the clause that gives the reason, like <manin>) (b:man) (r:48.5.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
Manaen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manaen) (d:prophet and teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch) (r:44.13.1)
manah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:rightly/in the right way) (d:<man> right with the place marker <ah>: in the right way; {lampi manah} is on the right path) (b:man) (q:draft)
Manahath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manahath) (d:son of Shobal, a descendant of Seir the Horite; also a place to which men of Benjamin were deported) (r:1.36.23/13.1.40)
Manaseeh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Manasseh) (d:spelling of Manasseh in this verse: the tribe descended from the elder son of Joseph) (r:66.7.6)
Manason = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mnason) (d:spelling of Mnason, a man from Cyprus and an early disciple, in whose house Paul stayed on the way to Jerusalem) (r:44.21.16)
Manasseh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manasseh) (d:elder son of Joseph and ancestor of the tribe of Manasseh; also a king of Judah, the son of Hezekiah) (r:1.41.51/1.46.20)
Manassehte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Manasseh) (d:<Manasseh> with the plural <te>: the people of the tribe of Manasseh) (b:Manasseh) (r:7.12.4/6.17.7)
manawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:head for/go toward/make for) (d:go in the direction of a place or an end; often after <lam>, direction) (s:zuan) (q:draft)
manawhin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:toward/in the direction of/heading for) (d:<manawh> head for with the linking ending <in>: in the direction of, usually after <lam>, direction) (b:manawh) (q:draft)
mancip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seize/grip/hold fast) (d:<man> seize with <cip> tightly; said of anguish, fear or trembling taking hold of people) (s:lencip) (b:man) (q:draft)
Manean = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manaen) (d:spelling of Manaen, a prophet and teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch) (r:44.13.1)
manek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:eat first/eat ahead) (d:<ma> before with <nek> eat: eat ahead of others without waiting) (q:draft)
mang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey) (s:zui/thumang/thungai) obey an order; listen to advice
mangbuh = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wheat) (r:10.17.28)
mangbuh = (i:2) (t:n) (w:wheat flour) (s:mangbuhnel)
Mangbuhci = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wheat seed/grain of wheat) (d:<mangbuh> wheat with <ci> seed) (q:draft)
mangbuhham = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:barley) (r:2.9.31)
mangbuhhamte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:barley) (d:<mangbuhham> barley with plural <te>, the barley plants) (b:mangbuhham) (q:draft)
mangbuhhum = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wheat grain/kernel of wheat) (d:<mangbuh> wheat with <hum>; counted with <tang>, grain) (q:draft)
mangbuhman = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:spelt) (d:a grain named in a list after wheat, barley and millet) (q:draft)
mangbuhmante = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:spelt) (d:plural of <mangbuhman>, a grain named beside <mangbuh> wheat and <mangbuhham> barley) (b:mangbuhman) (q:draft)
mangbuhnel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wheat flour/fine flour) (d:flour ground from wheat, used for bread and for the grain offering) (q:draft)
mangbuhte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wheat/grain) (d:wheat as a crop or as a stock of grain, with the plural ending <te>) (b:mangbuh) (q:draft)
mangbuhvui = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:head of wheat/ear of grain) (d:<mangbuh>, wheat, with <vui>, ear: the head of a wheat plant, which holds the grain) (s:buhvui/anvui) (q:draft)
mangbuhvuite = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:heads of grain/ears of wheat) (d:<mangbuhvui>, head of wheat, with the plural <te>) (s:buhvuite/anvuite) (q:draft)
mangbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tavern/inn) (d:a roadside inn or tavern; in the Bible only in the place name {Mangbuk Thum}, Three Taverns)
Mangbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tavern/inn) (d:<mangbuk>, tavern, written with a capital in the place name {Mangbuk Thum}, Three Taverns, a stopping place on the road to Rome) (b:mangbuk) (q:draft)
mangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:listen to/pay attention/obey) (d:<mang>, obey, with the linking ending <in>: obeying, and then; {thu mangin} is obeying what someone says) (b:mang) (r:1.28.7)
manginn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:governor's residence/praetorium/palace) (d:<mang>, ruler, with <inn>, house: the governor's official residence, the Praetorium; {manginn tual} is its courtyard) (q:draft)
mangkawlsing = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:pomegranate) (d:the pomegranate, both the tree and its fruit; also the pomegranate shapes that decorated the temple pillars) (q:draft)
mangkawlsingte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:pomegranates) (d:plural of <mangkawlsing>, pomegranate; here the bronze pomegranates around the capital of a pillar) (b:mangkawlsing) (q:draft)
mangkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give in to/yield to/heed) (d:<mang>, obey, with <kha>, happen to: come to follow what someone says, be won over by persuasion or pressure) (q:draft)
mangkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:interpret dreams) (d:<mang>, dream, with <khiat>, bring out: explain the meaning of a dream; {mangkhiat siamna} is skill in interpreting dreams) (q:draft)
mangkhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:completely/utterly/away) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is finished and the thing is gone, as in {bei mangkhin}, come to an end altogether) (b:mang) (q:draft)
mangkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey again) (d:<mang>, obey, with <kik>, again, and the linking ending <in>: obeying once more) (q:draft)
manglian = (i:1) (t:n) (w:commander/high officer) (d:<mang>, officer, with <lian>, great: a high officer; {galkap manglian} is the field commander of an army) (s:mangpa/galkapmang) (q:draft)
mangliante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:officials/rulers/governors) (d:plural of <manglian>, a high official or ruler) (s:uliante/mangpite/mangte) (b:manglian) (q:draft)
mangman = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:one who has dreams and tells what they mean; <mang>, dream, with <man>, catch, as in {mang man}, have a dream; often followed by <pa>, {mangman pa}, the dreamer) (s:mangmanpa) (q:draft)
mangmanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:<mangman> dreamer with <pa> marking a man) (s:mangman) (b:mangman) (q:draft)
mangmat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dream) (d:a dream seen in sleep; <mang>, dream, with <mat>, the second form of <man>, catch, as in {mang man}, have a dream) (q:draft)
mangmatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vision/dream) (d:<mangmat> dream with the noun suffix <na>: what is seen in a dream or vision) (s:mangmuhna/maangmuhna) (b:mangmat) (q:draft)
mangmatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:visions/revelations) (d:plural of <mangmatna>: visions or revelations received from God) (s:mangmuhnate/maangmuhnate) (b:mangmatna) (q:draft)
mangmu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tribute/tax/levy) (d:a payment required by a ruler or for the house of God, named together with <siah>, tax, and <losap>, duty) (s:siah/phiangsiah) (q:draft)
mangmu = (i:2) (t:v) (w:see a vision/fall into a trance) (d:<mang>, dream, with <mu>, see: see a vision while awake, fall into a trance) (q:draft)
mangmuh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vision) (d:what is seen as in a dream, a prophetic vision; <mang> dream with <muh>, the form of <mu> see) (s:maangmuh/mumaang) (b:mangmu) (q:draft)
mangmuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vision/revelation) (d:<mangmuh>, vision, with the noun suffix <na>: something seen in a dream or in a vision from God) (s:maangmuhna/mangmatna) (b:mangmuh) (q:draft)
mangmuhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:visions) (d:plural of <mangmuhna>: the visions seen by a prophet or in sleep) (s:maangmuhnate/mangmatnate) (b:mangmuhna) (r:23.1.1) (q:draft)
mangna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:noun form of <mang>, away or completely, after a verb: {a suksiat mangna} is their destroying completely) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangngilhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forget) (d:<mangngilh>, forget, with the linking ending <in>: forgetting, and then) (a:phawkin) (b:mangngilh) (q:draft)
mangngilhkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to forget/forget) (d:<mangngilh>, forget, with <kha>, happen to: come to forget) (q:draft)
mangngilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forgetting/forgetfulness/oblivion) (d:<mangngilh> forget with the noun suffix <na>; {mangngilhna gam} is the land of oblivion) (a:phawkna) (b:mangngilh) (q:draft)
mangngilhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who forget) (d:<mangngilh> forget with the plural <te>: the ones who forget) (b:mangngilh) (q:draft)
mangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:commander/captain/officer/chief) (d:a man in command or in office: {galkap mangpa} is an army commander or centurion, {inncing mangpa} the captain of the guard, {thukhen mangpa} a judge) (s:galkapmang/ukpa) (r:41.15.45) (q:draft)
Mangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:official/governor/lord) (d:capitalised form of <mangpa> used as a title: the Ethiopian official of Acts 8, the governor Festus, and Christ as the author or prince of life) (b:mangpa) (q:draft)
mangpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disappear at once/vanish) (d:<mang>, disappear, with <pah>, at once: vanish in a moment) (q:draft)
mangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:governor) (d:<mang>, ruler, with <pi>, great: the governor of a land under the emperor) (s:mangpipa) (q:draft)
mangpipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:governor) (d:<mangpi>, governor, with <pa> marking a man) (s:mangpi/menzipa) (q:draft)
Mangpipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:governor/His Excellency) (d:<mangpipa>, governor, written with a capital as a title before or after the name, as {Mangpipa Feliks}, Governor Felix) (b:mangpipa) (q:draft)
mangpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:governors/officials/high officers) (d:plural of <mangpi>, a high official) (s:mangliante/uliante) (b:mangpi) (q:draft)
mangsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:lost) (d:<mang>, be lost, with <sa>, already: that has gone missing; {a mangsa} is the lost one) (s:mansuahsa) (q:draft)
mangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drive away/get rid of/waste/make vanish) (d:<mang>, disappear, with the causative <sak>: make disappear, get rid of or waste; often follows another verb, as {mut mangsak}, blow away, and {tum mangsak}, plunge into ruin) (s:maimangsak/mangthangsak) (q:draft)
mangsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who lose) (d:<mangsak> cause to be lost, lose, with <te>, the people who do so) (b:mangsak) (q:draft)
mangsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:practise sorcery/divine) (d:in {mangsan theite}, where the English has sorcerers; perhaps divining by dreams) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:officials/officers/commanders/magistrates) (d:plural of <mang>, officer: men in office or command, as {galkap mangte}, army commanders, and {thukhen mangte}, magistrates) (s:uliante/ukte/mangpite) (b:mang) (q:draft)
mangte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:dreams) (d:plural of <mang>, dream) (b:mang) (q:draft)
mangte = (i:3) (t:n) (w:those who obey/those who accept) (d:<mang>, obey, with the plural <te>: {a mangte}, the ones who obey or accept a word) (s:zuite/mangzote) (b:mang) (q:draft)
mangthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disappear/vanish/perish/pass away) (d:go out of sight or out of existence: disappear, be lost, perish) (s:maimang/beimang) (a:kilang) (q:draft)
mangthangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disappear/vanish) (d:<mangthang>, disappear, with the linking ending <in>: disappearing, and then) (b:mangthang) (q:draft)
mangthangpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disappear quickly/vanish soon) (d:<mangthang> disappear with <pak>, quickly, for a short while) (q:draft)
mangthangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lose/destroy/make vanish) (d:<mangthang>, be lost, with the causative <sak>: lose something, or cause it to perish) (s:mangsak/maimangsak) (a:gum) (b:mangthang) (q:draft)
mangthangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the lost/lost ones) (d:<mangthang> be lost or perish, with plural <te>: those who are lost) (b:mangthang) (q:draft)
mangthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:obedient) (d:<mang> obey with <thei> able: who obeys; {thu a mangthei naupangte}, obedient children) (b:mang) (q:draft)
mangza = (t:see) <mangza-ah>
mangza-ah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:under authority/in a rank of authority) (d:<mangza>, rank or position of authority, with the place marker <ah>) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey rather/obey more) (d:<mang> obey with <zaw>, more, rather) (s:manzawk) (b:mang) (q:draft)
mangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to obey/obey) (d:<mang> obey with <zo>, be able, manage to) (b:mang) (q:draft)
mangzote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who obey) (d:<mangzo>, manage to obey, with the plural <te>: those who have obeyed the teaching, NIV those trained by it) (s:zuite) (b:mangzo) (q:draft)
manin = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:as of)
manin = (i:3) (t:conj) (w:reason being/because of) (d:gives the cause of what follows; {tua ahih manin}, that being so, is therefore)
maninah = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:because/because of) (d:<manin>, because, with <ah>: placed at the end of the clause that gives the reason, often as {ahih maninah}) (b:manin) (q:draft)
mankhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seize together/take along with) (d:<man> seize with <khawm> together: seize along with other things) (q:draft, low confidence)
mankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seize and bring out/hunt down/catch) (d:<man> seize with <khia> out: catch and take out of a hiding place) (q:draft)
mankhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:finish/complete/be finished) (d:<man>, finish, with <khin>, already: have finished, be completed) (s:khinta) (b:man) (q:draft)
mankhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:finish/have finished) (d:<man> finish with <khit>, which marks the action as completed; {a mankhit ciangin} is when he had finished) (s:zawhkhit) (q:draft)
mankim = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:all true/wholly true) (d:<man> true with <kim>, all, every one) (q:draft)
manlah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be busy/be occupied) (d:be taken up with work, with no time left for other things) (q:draft)
manlahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:busily/being busy) (d:<manlah> be busy, with <in>; {manlahin om} is to be busy, taken up with one's affairs) (b:manlah) (q:draft)
manlahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be busy with/occupy oneself with/devote oneself to) (d:<manlah> be busy, with <pih> which adds the thing one is busy with) (b:manlah) (q:draft)
manlan = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:quickly) (d:form of <manlang> quick, used before <pak>) (q:draft)
manlangin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:at once/right away/quickly) (d:with <a> before it, {a manlangin}: at once, without delay) (b:manlang) (r:66.3.11)
manlangin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:immediately/quickly/in a hurry) (d:<manlang>, quick, with <in>: quickly, in a hurry, placed before the verb) (s:thakhatin) (a:damdamin) (b:manlang)
manlangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are quick) (d:<manlang> quick with the plural <te>; here of feet quick to do evil) (b:manlang) (q:draft)
manlo = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:worthless) (d:in {bangmah manlo mite}, good-for-nothing men) (b:man) (q:draft, low confidence)
manlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wrong/untruth/falsehood) (d:<man> true or right with <loh> not and the noun suffix <na>: what is not right; NIV evil) (a:manna) (q:draft, low confidence)
manlote = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:false) (d:plural of <manlo>; {pasian manlote} are false gods, idols) (s:zuaute) (b:manlo) (q:draft)
manman = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:regular/due/proper) (d:of what comes at its fixed time or in its fixed amount; {a hun manman} is the appointed time) (r:12.25.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
manmanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:regularly/at the proper time/continually) (d:at each set time without fail, as of daily meals or regular offerings; {a hun manmanin} is at the proper time) (b:manman) (r:12.25.30) (q:draft)
manna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:manna) (d:the food God gave Israel in the wilderness, the Hebrew word kept in Zolai) (s:mana/maana) (q:draft)
manna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:truth/uprightness/integrity) (d:<man>, true or right, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact of being true, or uprightness of heart) (s:thutak) (a:manlohna/zuauna) (b:man) (q:draft)
mannop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be willing to listen/be willing to obey) (d:<man>, the form of <mang> obey, with <nop> want; in the verses always with <kei>, refuse to listen) (q:draft)
Manoah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manoah) (d:man of Zorah of the tribe of Dan, the father of Samson) (r:7.13.2/7.13.19)
manpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:catcher/one who catches) (d:<man> catch with <pa>, a man: the man who catches an animal in hunting) (b:man) (q:draft)
manpa = (i:2) (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:in {mang manpa}, the man who has dreams; {mang man} is to dream a dream) (s:mangmanpa/mangman) (b:man) (q:draft)
manpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seize at once/arrest immediately) (d:<man> seize or arrest, with <pah> at once) (q:draft)
manpha = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:precious/valuable/costly) (d:of great worth or dearly valued; {suang manpha} is a precious stone, and {manpha zaw} is more valuable) (s:amanpha) (a:mawkna) (r:19.116.15) (q:draft)
manphapen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:most precious/most valuable) (d:<manpha> precious with the superlative <pen>) (b:manpha) (q:draft)
manphat = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:precious/dear/valuable) (d:form of <manpha> used before {mah bangin} and other endings) (b:manpha) (q:draft)
manphate = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:precious/valuable) (d:plural of <manpha>, placed after the noun it describes; {van manphate} are valuable goods, treasures) (b:manpha) (r:14.36.10) (q:draft)
manphateng = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:all precious/all valuable) (d:<manpha> precious with <teng>, all of: {na manphateng}, all the valuable things) (b:manpha) (q:draft)
manphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:value/worth/preciousness) (d:<manphat>, precious, with the noun suffix <na>: how much something is worth or how precious it is) (s:man) (b:manphat) (r:18.28.17) (q:draft)
manphazaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more valuable/more precious/worth more) (d:<manpha>, precious, with the comparative <zaw>: worth more; used with <sangin>, than) (b:manpha) (q:draft)
mansa = (t:see) <mansa-in>
mansa-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:ready/already prepared) (d:<man>, finish, with <sa>, already, and <in>: in a finished state, ready) (s:kigingin) (q:draft)
mansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have seized/cause to catch/hand over) (d:<man> seize with causative <sak>: have someone caught, or let someone capture; {mang mansak} is to make someone dream) (b:man) (q:draft)
mansakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have arrested/have seized) (d:<man> seize with the causative <sak> and the linking suffix <in>: having had someone arrested) (b:man) (q:draft)
mansiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:finish completely/complete) (d:<man>, finish, with <siang>, clean: finish completely) (s:zosiang/zawhkhit) (b:man) (q:draft)
mansuahsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:lost) (d:<mansuah> lose with <sa>, already done: that has been lost) (s:mangsa) (b:mansuah) (q:draft)
mantak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:true/real/right) (d:<man>, true, with <tak>, real: true, genuine; {a mantak} is what is true, the truth) (s:man) (a:manlo) (b:man) (q:draft)
mantak = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:truly/in truth) (d:in truth, really; {a mantak a kong genin-ah}, truly I tell you, opens a solemn saying of Jesus) (s:takpi/taktak) (b:man) (q:draft)
mantakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truly/truthfully/honestly) (d:<mantak>, true, with the adverb ending <in>: {a mantakin kong genin-ah} and {a mantakin ci lehang} open a solemn statement, very truly I tell you) (s:takpi/taktak) (b:mantak) (r:20.24.26) (q:draft)
mantakpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:certainly/indeed/of course) (d:<mantak>, true, with the intensifier <pi>: most certainly, of course) (s:takpi) (b:mantak) (q:draft)
mantaktak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:really true/true) (d:<mantak>, true, with <tak> repeated for emphasis: really true; {a mantaktak a gen} is tell the real truth) (s:mantak) (b:mantak) (q:draft)
mante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:captors/catchers) (d:<man>, catch or seize, with the plural <te>: those who catch or hold someone captive; {mi mante} is catchers of people, fishers of men) (a:salte) (b:man) (q:draft)
mante = (i:2) (t:n) (w:prices/values) (d:<man>, price, with the plural <te>: the prices of things, the money they are worth) (b:man) (q:draft, low confidence)
manthan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:vanish/disappear/pass away) (d:form of <mangthang>, vanish, used before words such as <ding>, <hun>, <ciangin> and <bangin>: pass away, cease to exist) (s:maimang/beimang) (r:18.7.9) (q:draft)
mantheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to obey/obey) (d:<man>, the second form of <mang>, obey, with <theih>, be able: be able to obey; used with <thu>, word, before <nading> or <lai-in>) (s:zuihtheih/mangzo) (q:draft)
manun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:because/since) (d:<manin>, because, in the form used when the subject is plural: placed at the end of the clause that gives the reason) (s:manunah) (b:man) (q:draft)
manunah = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:because/since) (d:<manun>, because, with <ah>: placed after a clause whose subject is plural, because they; after <lau>, fear, it is for fear that) (s:manun) (b:manun) (r:43.7.13) (q:draft)
manzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:value/price/worth) (d:<man>, price, with <zah>, amount: how much a thing is worth, the value set on it) (s:man) (q:draft)
manzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more right/more true) (d:<man>, right, with <zaw>, more: the more right of two things) (b:man) (q:draft)
manzawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey rather/listen to rather) (d:{thu man}, the second form of {thu mang} obey, with <zawk> more; said of two choices) (q:draft, low confidence)
manzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to catch/capture/manage to catch) (d:<man>, catch, with <zo>, be able: manage to catch or capture) (q:draft)
Maok = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maok) (d:father of Achish, king of Gath, to whom David fled) (r:9.27.2)
Maon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Maon) (d:town in the hill country of Judah with a wilderness around it where David hid from Saul; also a descendant of Caleb) (r:6.15.55)
mapai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go ahead/go before/go in advance) (d:<ma>, before, with <pai>, go: go ahead of someone else, go on in advance) (s:masuan) (a:nungzuih) (q:draft)
mapaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send ahead/send on before) (d:<mapai>, go ahead, with the causative <sak>: send someone on ahead) (b:mapai) (q:draft)
mapek = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:before/long before) (d:<ma> before with <pek>, far back: placed after a clause, before that happened) (q:draft)
mapekin = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:before/even before) (d:<ma>, before, with <pek>, far back, and <in>: placed after a verb, already before something happened) (b:mapek) (q:draft)
mapi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leader/chief/chief officer) (d:the one at the front, the head of a group; {nasem mapi} is a foreman, {a mapi-in om} is be in the lead) (s:makai/makaipa) (b:ma) (q:draft)
mapi = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lead/go before) (d:go at the front of a people and lead them) (s:makaih/lamkaih) (q:draft)
mapiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give beforehand/give in advance) (d:<ma> before with <piak> give: give ahead as a pledge of what is to come; NIV put as a deposit) (s:piakhol) (q:draft)
mapite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:overseers/foremen/leaders) (d:those who stand in front and direct the work of others; {nasem mapite}, foremen over the workers) (s:makaite) (b:mapi) (q:draft)
Mara = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Mara) (d:name meaning bitter, which Naomi asked to be called after the loss of her husband and sons) (r:8.1.20) (q:draft)
Marah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Marah) (d:place in the wilderness where Israel camped after crossing the sea and found the water bitter) (r:2.15.23/4.33.8)
Marari = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Merari) (d:third son of Levi, ancestor of the Merarite clan of Levites) (r:1.46.11)
mard = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nard) (d:a costly perfume, the English word nard as written in this text) (s:nard) (q:draft)
Mareal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Maralah) (d:place on the western border of the territory of Zebulun) (r:6.19.11)
Mareshah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mareshah) (d:town in the lowlands of Judah, fortified by Rehoboam; also a descendant of Caleb) (r:6.15.44/14.11.8)
Mari = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Mary) (d:name of several women, among them the mother of Jesus and the sister of Martha and Lazarus) (r:42.1.46) (q:draft)
Marioth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Meraioth) (d:priest, son of Ahitub, in the family line of Azariah) (r:13.9.11)
Marka = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mark) (d:John Mark, companion of Paul and Barnabas, later with Peter) (r:55.4.11) (q:draft)
Markaboth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Markaboth/Beth Markaboth) (d:second part of Beth Markaboth, a town of the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.31) (q:draft)
Maroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Maroth) (d:town in Judah named in the lament of Micah) (r:33.1.12)
Marsena = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Marsena) (d:one of the seven nobles of Persia and Media closest to King Xerxes) (r:17.1.14)
