Mary = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Mary) (d:name of several women, among them the mother of Jesus; the same name as <Mari>) (r:40.1.16/42.1.46)
masa = (i:1) (t:num) (w:first) (d:first in order or time; {a masa pen} is the first one) (s:khatna) (r:42.13.30)
masa = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:initial/first/earlier/former) (d:that comes or happens before the others: {ta masa} is the firstborn child, {thuciamna masa} the first covenant) (a:nunung/nununga)
masabel = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very first/first/foremost) (d:<masa> first with the superlative <bel>; {a gah masabel} is the firstfruits, {a masabel} at the head of a clause is first of all) (s:masapen) (a:nunungpen) (q:draft)
masak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:first/before others) (d:placed after a verb: do first, before anything else or before someone else) (s:phot/masazaw) (b:masa) (r:21.10.10) (q:draft)
masak = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:first/former/earlier) (d:placed after a verb to describe a noun: the first or earlier one that was made, born or done) (a:nunung) (b:masa) (q:draft)
masakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:first) (d:<masak> first with the adverb suffix <in>: doing first, before the rest) (b:masak) (q:draft)
masakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:first/first time) (d:<masak>, do first, with {-na}: the place or occasion where something was first done, translated first or at first) (a:nunungna) (b:masak) (q:draft)
masakpen = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very first/first of all) (d:<masak>, first, with <pen>, most: the very first; after a verb, the first that was made or done) (b:masak) (q:draft)
masakun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:first/the first time) (d:<masak> first with <un>, the plural <uh> joined with <in>: when they first did something; {a khualzin masakun}, on their first journey) (b:masak) (q:draft, low confidence)
masala = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:spice/caraway/dill) (d:a small seed that is sown and beaten out with a rod and used as seasoning, caraway or dill; also spice as trade goods) (q:draft)
masalate = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:caraway/spices) (d:plural of <masala>) (b:masala) (q:draft)
masapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:first one/first man) (d:<masa> first with <pa> marking a man; {a gen masapa} is the first to speak) (b:masa) (q:draft)
masapen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:first/very first/foremost) (d:<masa> first with the superlative <pen>: first of all) (s:masabel) (a:nunungpen) (b:masa) (q:draft)
masapente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the first ones/the very first) (d:<masapen>, first of all, with the plural <te>) (a:nunungte) (b:masapen) (q:draft)
masasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do first/let be done first) (d:<masa> first with the causative <sak>: have something done before anything else) (b:masa) (q:draft)
masate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:first ones/former ones) (d:those who are or were first, plural of <masa>; {a teeng masate} are the earlier inhabitants, {pu pa masate} the first forefathers) (a:nunungte) (b:masa) (q:draft)
masawlin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send ahead/send before) (d:<ma> before with <sawl> send and the linking suffix <in>: sending on ahead) (q:draft)
masazaw = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:first/ahead/before others) (d:<masa> first with the comparative <zaw>; placed after a verb: do it first, or before someone else does) (s:masak/phot) (b:masa) (q:draft)
