mawkmawkte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:simple ones/ordinary people/common people) (d:<mawkmawk>, ordinary or without understanding, with the plural <te>; said after <mi>, person) (s:nautangte) (b:mawkmawk) (r:2.30.32) (q:draft)
mawkna = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:vain/worthless/futile/empty) (d:of no use or value; {a mawkna-in}, in vain) (b:mawk) (q:draft)
mawkna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:nothing/vanity) (d:<mawk>, in vain, with the noun suffix <na>: something empty that comes to nothing; {a mawkna suak} is come to nothing, {a mawkna suaksak} bring to nothing) (s:hawmpi/thumawkna) (b:mawk) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawknapi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:meaningless/vain/futile/utterly empty) (d:<mawkna> with the strengthening suffix {-pi}, usually as {a mawknapi}, a thing that is utterly meaningless) (b:mawkna) (r:21.1.14) (q:draft)
mawknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vanities/vain things) (d:<mawkna> with the plural <te>; {kisaktheih mawknate}, empty boasting, NIV the pride of life) (b:mawkna) (q:draft)
