metkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shave off/cut off) (d:<met>, shave, with <khia>, out or off: shave hair off completely) (b:met) (q:draft)
metna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shearing/shaving) (d:<met>, shear or shave, with the noun suffix <na>: the shearing of sheep or the shaving off of hair) (b:met) (q:draft)
metna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:profit/gain/benefit) (d:<met>, profit, with the noun suffix <na>: gain or benefit; {bang metna om ahi hiam} is what is gained) (s:met/meetna/phattuamna) (a:supna) (b:met) (q:draft)
metsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shave/shave off/have shaved) (d:<met>, shave, with the causative <sak>: shave another person's hair or beard, or have one's own hair cut off) (b:met) (q:draft)
mette = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shearers) (d:<met>, shear, with the plural <te>: those who shear; used after <mul>, hair or wool, as in {tuumul mette}, sheepshearers) (s:meette/mulmette) (b:met) (q:draft)
mettol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shave/shave bald) (d:<met>, shave, with <tol>, bare: shave the head completely bald, often as a sign of mourning) (q:draft)
mettolna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shaving/shaving bald) (d:<mettol>, shave bald, with the noun suffix <na>; {sam mettolna} is shaving off the hair in mourning) (b:mettol) (q:draft)
mettom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crop/cut short/shave short) (d:<met> shave or cut hair with <tom> short; {a sam uh a mettom} are those who crop their hair, where the NIV has those in distant places) (s:tommet) (q:draft, low confidence)
Meunim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Meunites) (d:people living south of Judah who were defeated by the men of Simeon and by King Uzziah) (r:14.26.7/13.4.41)
Mezahab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Me-Zahab) (d:grandparent of Mehetabel, the wife of King Hadad of Edom) (r:1.36.39/13.1.50)
Mi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:person/man/one) (d:<mi>, person, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a title such as {Mi Siangtho}, the Holy One) (b:mi) (r:44.3.14) (q:draft)
miaimuai = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in throngs/in a great crowd) (d:descriptive word for a countless crowd standing close together) (q:draft, low confidence)
mial = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:without being able to see or continuous)
mial = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:dark) (d:without light; {khua mial} is it is dark, and of the eyes {mial} means dim) (r:19.35.6)
mial = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:invisible)
mial = (i:4) (t:adj) (w:lose face)
miala = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dark) (d:<mial> dark with the linking <a>, and: {khua miala}, it was dark and) (b:mial) (q:draft)
mialcipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:darken completely/shroud in darkness) (d:<mial> dark, <cip> completely and the causative <sak>: make wholly dark) (s:mialsak) (a:khuavaksak) (q:draft)
mialin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dark/become dark/grow dark) (d:<mial>, dark, with the linking suffix {-in}: being or becoming dark, followed by another verb) (b:mial) (q:draft)
mialna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:darkness/dark place) (d:<mial>, dark, with the noun suffix <na>: darkness; {mialna mun} is a dark place) (s:khuamial/khuamialna/khim) (a:khuavak/khuavakna) (b:mial) (q:draft)
mialpha = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very dark/deeply dark) (d:<mial> dark with <pha>; said of how great a darkness is) (q:draft, low confidence)
mialsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:darken/make dark/dim) (d:<mial>, dark, with the causative <sak>: make dark, take the light away; of the eyes, make dim) (s:zingsak/ziingsak) (a:khuavaksak/vaaksak) (b:mial) (q:draft)
mialta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become dark/be darkened) (d:<mial> be dark, with <ta> which marks a change that has now come about; {khua hong mialta} is it had grown dark) (b:mial) (q:draft)
mialzawt = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grope/feel one's way) (d:<mial> dark with <zawt> feel about with the hands: grope as in the dark) (s:zawt/zawtzawt) (q:draft)
miamua = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:describes insects settled close together in a swarm, after <bawm>) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mibhar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mibhar) (d:son of Hagri, one of David's mighty warriors) (r:13.11.38)
Mibsam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mibsam) (d:name of two men: a son of Ishmael, and a descendant of Simeon) (r:13.1.29/13.4.25)
mibum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sorcery/enchantment/spell) (d:<mi> person with <bum> bewitch: casting spells on people; {mibum theite} are enchanters, {mibum siamna} is skill in spells) (s:bum/mibumna/bumna) (q:draft)
mibumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sorcery/witchcraft/magic spell) (d:<mibum> cast spells on people, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:bumna/mibum/khongkhaina/aisan) (b:mibum) (q:draft)
mibuppite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whole people/all the people) (d:<mi> people with <bup> whole, <pi> great and the plural <te>) (s:minambup) (q:draft)
Mibzar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mibzar) (d:chief of Edom descended from Esau) (r:1.36.42/13.1.53)
micinate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sick people/the sick) (d:<mi> person with <cina> sick, plural <te>) (s:cinate/veite) (q:draft)
micing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guard/watchman) (d:<mi> person with <cing> keep watch) (s:galvil/cingpa) (q:draft)
micitakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:faithful people/faithful ones/saints) (d:<mi> person with <citak> faithful, plural <te>) (q:draft)
midang = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:other/another/someone else) (d:another person, someone else; {midang'} before a noun is another person's) (r:46.14.17) of people
midangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stranger/outsider/foreigner) (d:<midang> other person with the intensive <pi>: a complete stranger) (s:khualmi/mikhual/gamdangmi) (b:midang) (q:draft)
midangte = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:others) (d:<midang>, another person, with the plural <te>: other people, the others) (s:adangte) (b:midang) of people
Middin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Middin) (d:town in the wilderness of Judah) (r:6.15.61)
Midian = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/people/land) (w:Midian) (d:son of Abraham and Keturah, and the people and land named after him) (r:1.25.2/1.25.4)
Midiante = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Midianites) (d:<Midian> with the plural <te>: the people of Midian, a desert people who oppressed Israel until Gideon defeated them) (b:Midian) (r:7.6.1/7.6.7)
midik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteous person/upright person/the righteous) (d:<mi>, person, with <dik>, right: a person who does what is right, one who is righteous before God) (s:mipha/midikpa) (a:migilo/misia) (q:draft)
Midik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteous person/the righteous/Righteous One) (d:<midik>, righteous person, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in the title {Midik Pa}, the Righteous One) (b:midik) (q:draft)
midikin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as righteous) (d:<midik> righteous person with <in>: as a righteous person; {midikin sang} is to count as righteous) (b:midik) (q:draft)
midikpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteous man/the righteous) (d:<midik> righteous person with <pa> marking a man) (s:dikpa/thumanpa/mihoihpa) (a:migilopa/gilopa) (b:midik) (q:draft)
midiktatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:upright people/the blameless/the righteous) (d:<mi> person with <diktat> upright, plural <te>) (s:midikte/mihoihte/thumante) (a:migilote) (q:draft)
midikte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the righteous/the upright/righteous people) (d:<midik>, righteous person, with the plural <te>: the righteous, often set against <migilote>, the wicked) (s:mihoihte/thumante/miphate/midiktatte) (a:migilote/misiate) (q:draft)
Mifibosheth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mephibosheth) (d:son of Jonathan and grandson of Saul, lame in both feet, who ate at King David's table; a spelling of <Mefibosheth>) (r:10.9.13)
Migdalel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Migdal El) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.38)
Migdalgad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Migdal-gad/Migdal Gad) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.37)
Migdel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Migdol) (d:town in northern Egypt where Jews settled after the fall of Jerusalem; a spelling of <Migdol>) (r:24.44.1)
Migdol = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Migdol) (d:place in northern Egypt near which the Israelites camped before they crossed the sea; later a town where Jews lived) (r:4.33.7/2.14.2)
migi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:kind/good/gracious) (d:good and kind in character, gracious; {migi tuucing} is the good shepherd; in Matthew 5:48 it stands for perfect) (a:gilo) (r:56.2.5) (q:draft)
migilo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wicked person/the wicked/evildoer) (d:<mi>, person, with <gilo>, evil: a wicked person, one who does evil) (s:misia/gilomi/gilopa) (a:midik/mipha) (q:draft)
migiloin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as wicked/as evil) (d:<migilo> wicked person with <in>: as a wicked person) (b:migilo) (q:draft)
migilopa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wicked man/the wicked) (d:<migilo> with <pa> marking a man, the wicked one) (s:gilopa) (a:midikpa/dikpa) (b:migilo) (q:draft)
migilote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the wicked/evildoers/sinners) (d:<migilo>, wicked person, with the plural <te>: the wicked, evildoers; in the Gospels also sinners) (s:misiate/gamtatsiate) (a:midikte/mihoihte) (b:migilo) (r:20.10.29) (q:draft)
migina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:worthy man/man of standing/respectable person) (d:<mi> person with <gina> worthy; {migina lo} is a nobody, a worthless person) (q:draft)
miginalo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:worthless person/scoundrel/good-for-nothing) (d:<migina>, a worthy person, with the negative <lo>: a worthless or bad person; in Hebrews 5:3 it is said of a weak, imperfect man) (a:migina) (b:migina) (q:draft)
miginate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the blameless/people of integrity/worthy people) (d:plural of <migina>: people of worth and good character, the blameless) (s:ginate/mawhbaanglote) (a:migilote) (b:migina) (q:draft)
migit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show favor/be gracious/be kind) (d:the form of <migi>, kind, used before <hangin>, <nading> and <mahmahna>: be kind or gracious to someone, the person taking <tungah>) (b:migi) (q:draft)
migitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kindness/goodness/benefit) (d:<migit>, be kind, with the noun suffix <na>: kind and generous dealing with others; {migitna lak} is show kindness) (s:gitna) (b:migit) (q:draft)
Migron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Migron) (d:place in Benjamin near Gibeah, on the Assyrian line of march toward Jerusalem) (r:9.14.2/23.10.28)
mih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out/be quenched/be extinguished) (d:of fire, go out; the form of <mit>, go out, used in {mei a mih ngei lohna}, where the fire never goes out) (q:draft)
mihai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fool/foolish person/madman) (d:<mi>, person, with <hai>, foolish: a fool, the opposite of <mipil>, a wise person) (s:mimawl) (a:mipil) (q:draft)
mihaipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fool/foolish man) (d:<mihai>, fool, with <pa> marking a man: a foolish man, often set against <mipilpa>, the wise man) (s:haipa) (a:mipilpa) (b:mihai) (r:18.5.2) (q:draft)
mihaipi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great fool/fool/stupid person) (d:<mihai>, fool, with <pi>, great: a great fool, a thoroughly stupid person) (b:mihai) (q:draft)
mihaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fools) (d:plural of <mihai>: fools, often set against <mipilte>, the wise) (s:haite/pillote) (a:mipilte) (b:mihai) (r:21.10.6) (q:draft)
mihatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the strong/strong men/the mighty) (d:<mi>, person, with <hat>, strong, and the plural <te>: strong or mighty people) (s:thahatte/hatte) (a:thanemte) (q:draft)
mihau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rich person/wealthy person) (d:<mi>, person, with <hau>, rich: a rich or wealthy person, the opposite of <mizawng>, a poor person) (a:mizawng) (q:draft)
mihaupa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rich man) (d:<mihau>, rich person, with <pa> marking a man) (s:haupa) (a:mizawngpa) (b:mihau) (r:20.13.8) (q:draft)
mihaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the rich/rich people) (d:plural of <mihau>: rich people, often set against <mizawngte>, the poor) (s:haute) (a:mizawngte) (b:mihau) (q:draft)
mihing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:human/human being) (s:mi)
mihing = (i:2) (t:n) (w:man/mankind) (r:1.1.26) where it is not necessarly referring to just a male man
Mihing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Man) (d:<mihing>, man, written with a capital in the title {Mihing Tapa}, the Son of Man) (b:mihing) (r:43.3.14) (q:draft)
mihingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as a human/as a human being/as a man) (d:<mihing>, human, with the marker <in>: as a human being, in human life) (b:mihing) (q:draft)
mihingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:humans/human beings/mankind) (b:mihing) (r:19.78.60) plural form of <mihing>
mihoih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:righteous) (s:thuman/dik) (a:gilo) (r:20.25.26)
mihoih = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:upright) (s:thutang/diktat)
mihoihin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:righteous) (d:<mihoih>, a good or righteous person, with the marker <in>: as righteous; with <sang>, accept, it says that God counts someone righteous) (b:mihoih)
mihoihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good man/righteous man/the righteous) (d:<mihoih>, good person, with <pa> marking a man, often set against <migilopa>, the wicked man) (s:midikpa/miphapa) (a:migilopa) (b:mihoih) (q:draft)
mihoihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the righteous/the upright/good people) (d:plural of <mihoih>: good or righteous people, often set against <migilote>, the wicked) (s:midikte/miphate) (a:migilote/misiate) (b:mihoih) (r:20.10.7) (q:draft)
mihoihteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the good/all good people) (d:<mihoih>, good person, with <teng>, all: all the good people there are) (b:mihoih) (q:draft)
Mihon = (i:1) (t:n) (w:assembly/congregation/crowd) (d:<mihon> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse) (b:mihon) (q:draft)
mihonpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crowd/multitude) (d:<mihon>, crowd, with <pi>, great: a large crowd, a multitude) (s:honpi/mipi) (b:mihon) (r:40.23.1) (q:draft)
mihonpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crowds/multitudes) (d:plural of <mihonpi>: great crowds, multitudes) (s:mipite/mihonte) (b:mihonpi) (q:draft)
Mihonpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crowds/multitudes/hosts) (d:<mihonpite> written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {Mihonpite’ Pasian} is the God of hosts, NIV God Almighty) (b:mihonpite) (q:draft)
mihonte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crowds/assembly/community/congregation) (d:plural of <mihon>: crowds, or the whole body of a community or assembly) (s:mihonpite/mipite) (b:mihon) (q:draft)
Mijamin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mijamin) (d:name of several men, among them the head of the sixth priestly division and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.7/16.12.5)
Mika = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mika) (d:name of several men, among them the young son of Mephibosheth and a Levite who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:10.9.12/16.11.22) (q:draft)
Mikah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Micah) (d:name of several men, among them an Ephraimite who made a shrine in the days of the judges and the prophet from Moresheth) (r:7.17.12/13.5.5)
Mikaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Micaiah) (d:name of several people, among them the prophet, son of Imlah, who foretold the death of Ahab, and the son of Gemariah who reported what Baruch read) (r:24.36.11/24.36.13)
Mikhael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Michael) (d:name of several men, and of the chief angel who fights for Israel) (r:4.13.13/13.6.40)
Mikhal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Michal) (d:younger daughter of King Saul and wife of David) (r:10.6.23/9.18.28)
mikhat = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:someone/anyone/a person) (d:<mi>, person, with <khat>, one, written as one word: someone, anyone; with <suak> or <ahi> it means one people, one and the same) (r:46.8.3) (q:draft)
mikheemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deceivers/impostors) (d:<mi>, person, with <kheem>, deceive, and the plural <te>: deceivers, impostors) (s:mikhemte/kheemte/khemte) (q:draft)
mikhem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:deceive people/be deceitful/cheat) (d:<mi> person with <khem> deceive; {mikhem theite} and {mikhem hatte} are deceivers, the treacherous) (q:draft)
mikhempeuh = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:everyone/all people/everybody) (d:<mi> person with <khempeuh> all, written as one word; usually written {mi khempeuh}) (s:mikim/milip) (a:kuamah) (q:draft)
mikhemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deceivers/deceitful people) (d:<mikhem> deceive people, with plural <te>: those who deceive) (s:khemte/kheemte/mikheemte) (b:mikhem) (q:draft)
mikhial = (i:1) (t:n) (w:falsehood)
mikhialte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:falsehoods) (b:mikhial)
Mikhialte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deceitful people/false people) (d:<mi> person with <khial> go wrong and the plural <te>; in the verse the people the psalmist does not sit with, the deceitful in the NIV) (s:mikhemte/kheemte) (b:mikhialte) (q:draft, low confidence)
mikhual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stranger/foreigner/sojourner) (d:<mi>, person, with <khual>, guest: a person from elsewhere who stays among others, often paired with <peemta>) (s:khualmi/peemta/gamdangmi) (a:tualsuak/gammi) (q:draft)
mikhualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:complete stranger/utter stranger) (d:<mikhual> stranger with the intensifying <pi>) (s:midangpi) (b:mikhual) (q:draft)
mikhualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:strangers/foreigners/sojourners) (d:plural of <mikhual>: foreigners who live among another people, paired with <peemtate>) (s:khualmite/peemtate/khualte) (b:mikhual) (q:draft)
mikician = (i:1) (t:n) (w:capable person/able man/reliable person) (d:<mi> person with <kician> sound, reliable; in the verse of several men) (s:misiam) (q:draft)
mikim = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:each one/everyone/each person) (d:<mi>, person, with <kim>, every: each person, everyone; {mikim tungah} is to each one) (s:milip/mikhempeuh) (q:draft)
Mikloth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikloth) (d:Benjamite of Gibeon, father of Shimeah, in the family line of King Saul) (r:13.9.38/13.9.37)
Mikmas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mikmash) (d:town of Benjamin north of Jerusalem, also written <Mikmash>) (r:15.2.27) (q:draft)
Mikmash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mikmash) (d:town of Benjamin north of Jerusalem, where Jonathan attacked the Philistine outpost at the pass) (r:9.13.23/16.11.31)
Mikmethath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mikmethath) (d:place east of Shechem on the border between Ephraim and Manasseh) (r:6.17.7/6.16.6)
Mikneiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikneiah) (d:Levite gatekeeper who played the harp when David brought the ark to Jerusalem) (r:13.15.21/13.15.18)
Mikonah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mekonah) (d:town in the south of Judah settled again after the exile) (r:16.11.28)
Mikri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikri) (d:Benjamite, ancestor of Elah who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:13.9.8)
miksite = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ants) (d:plural of <miksi>, ant) (q:draft)
Milalai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Milalai) (d:musician in the procession at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem under Nehemiah) (r:16.12.36)
Miletas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Miletus) (d:port city on the west coast of Asia Minor, where Paul met the elders of the church of Ephesus) (r:44.20.17/44.20.15)
milian = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great person/the great) (d:<mi>, person, with <lian>, great: a person of high standing or power, the opposite of <mineu>) (s:lianpa) (a:mineu) (r:58.7.7) (q:draft)
milianin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great person/the great) (d:<milian> great person with the marker <in>, here as or into: made them great) (b:milian) (q:draft)
milianpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great man/very great person/somebody) (d:<milian>, great person, with the intensive <pi>: a very great person, somebody of importance) (b:milian) (q:draft)
miliante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nobles/great men/princes) (d:plural of <milian>: great or high-ranking people, nobles) (s:uliante/mithupite) (a:mineute) (b:milian) (r:13.17.8) (q:draft)
Miliante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the great/the exalted/nobles) (d:<miliante> written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (b:miliante) (q:draft)
milim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:idol/image) (d:<mi>, person, with <lim>, likeness: an image made to be worshipped, an idol; <milim biakna> is idolatry) (s:lim) (r:27.3.3) (q:draft)
milimin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:into an idol/as an idol) (d:<milim> idol, image with the marker <in>; {milimin bawl} is make something into an idol) (b:milim) (q:draft)
milimte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:idols/images) (d:plural of <milim>: idols, images made to be worshipped) (s:limte) (b:milim) (r:23.2.18) (q:draft)
milip = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:each one/everyone/every man) (d:each person individually, usually as {a milip-in}, each of them) (s:mikim) (r:2.32.27) (q:draft)
milipin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:one by one/per head/individually) (d:person by person, counting or assessing each individual; used with <a> before it, {a milipin}) (s:mimi-in/khatkhatin/malin) (q:draft)
milipun = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:each one/every one/all of them) (d:<milip> everyone with the plural ending <un>; usually {a milipun}, each and every one of them) (b:milip) (q:draft)
Milkah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Milcah/Milkah) (d:wife of Nahor, the brother of Abraham, and grandmother of Rebekah; also one of the five daughters of Zelophehad) (r:1.11.29/1.24.24)
Milkom = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Milkom/Molek) (d:god of the Ammonites, called Molek in the NIV) (r:11.11.5/36.1.5)
Millo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Millo) (d:part of the defences of the City of David in Jerusalem, built up by David and Solomon; the NIV has the terraces, and Beth Millo for {Millo inn}) (r:11.9.24/12.12.20) (q:draft)
milmel = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:tender) (d:after <moi> young, tender: {a moi milmel}, delicately tender) (q:draft, low confidence)
milmial = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:dimly/dully/faintly) (d:not clear or bright: of seeing, dimly; after a colour word, dull, as {a kang milmial}, dull white) (q:draft)
mimah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:man/human being) (d:<mi> person with the emphatic <mah>: himself a man, truly human) (b:mi) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimal = (i:1) (t:n) (w:individual/person/number of people) (d:<mi> person with <mal> single unit: individual persons; in the verse the number of members that grows) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:captive/prey) (d:<mi> person with <mat> seize: a person taken; {galte’ mimat}, captive of the enemy) (s:sal/galmat) (q:draft)
mimawh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sinner/guilty person/the guilty) (d:<mi>, person, with <mawh>, sin: a sinner, a guilty person; {mimawh lo} is an innocent person) (s:mawhnei/mawhneimi) (a:midik) (q:draft)
mimawhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sinners/the guilty) (d:plural of <mimawh>: sinners, guilty people, often set against <midikte>, the righteous) (s:mawhneite) (a:midikte) (b:mimawh) (q:draft)
mimawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:senseless person/fool) (d:<mi>, person, with <mawl>, dull: a senseless person, paired with <mihai>, fool) (s:mihai) (a:mipil) (q:draft)
mimi = (t:see) <mimi-in>
mimi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:man by man/person by person/one by one) (d:<mi> person doubled, with <in>: each person in turn, like {a behbehin} clan by clan and {a innkuankuanin} family by family) (s:milipin/khatkhatin) (q:draft)
miminthang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:celebrity)
mimkhau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thread) (d:a thread, a thin strand of spun fibre used for weaving and sewing) (q:draft)
Min = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Name) (d:<min>, name, written with a capital for the name of God, as in {Min Siangtho}, the holy Name, and at the start of a sentence) (b:min) (q:draft)
mina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mina) (d:a unit of weight for silver and gold, sixty shekels in Ezekiel 45:12) (s:minas) (q:draft)
minam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:native) (s:tualsuak)
minam = (i:2) (t:n) (w:ethics)
minambup = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whole nation/whole people/whole community) (d:<minam> nation with <bup> whole) (q:draft)
minamdang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foreigner)
minamdang = (i:2) (t:n) (w:immigrant)
minamdangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:other nations/nations/foreign peoples) (d:<minamdang> foreigner, another people, with plural <te>) (s:namdangte/gamdangte) (b:minamdang) (q:draft)
minamin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nation/people) (d:<minam>, nation, with the marker <in>: as a nation, into a nation, nation by nation; {minamin bawl} is make into a nation) (b:minam) (q:draft)
minamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nations/peoples) (d:plural of <minam>: the nations or peoples of the world) (s:mipawlte) (b:minam) (q:draft)
minamte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:tribes) (d:plural of <minam> used for the tribes of Israel) (b:minam) (r:26.48.2) (q:draft)
Minamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tribe/people of a tribe) (d:capitalised form of <minamte> placed after a tribal name in the land allotments of Ezekiel 48, as in {Asher Minamte} the tribe of Asher) (b:minamte) (q:draft)
minas = (i:1) (t:n) (w:minas/mina) (d:unit of weight for gold and silver, written as in English) (s:mina) (q:draft)
minautangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:common people/ordinary people) (d:{mi nautang}, common people, with the plural <te>; {minautangte’ tutna mun}, the seat of the common people, is the lowest place at a feast) (s:nautangte/mineute) (a:miliante) (q:draft)
mindai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disgraced/be put to shame) (d:lose one's good name, be shamed before others; often {mindai-in} together with <maizum>, be ashamed) (s:minsiat/zahhuai) (a:kipahtawi) (q:draft)
mindai = (i:2) (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace/dishonor) (d:loss of one's good name; {mindai ni} is a day of disgrace) (s:mindaina/minsiatna/maizumna) (a:minphatna/pahtawina) (q:draft, low confidence)
mindaihuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:shameful/disgraceful/detestable) (d:<mindai>, be disgraced, with <huai>, deserving of: shameful, said of detestable conduct) (s:zumhuai/maizumhuai/kihhuai/muhdahhuai) (q:draft)
mindaihuaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:detestable things/shameful things) (d:<mindaihuai>, shameful, with the plural <te>: shameful or detestable deeds) (s:kihhuaite/kihhuainate) (b:mindaihuai) (q:draft)
mindaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disgrace/shame/dishonor/reproach) (d:<mindai>, be disgraced, with the noun suffix <na>: the loss of one's good name; {mindaina tun} is to bring dishonor on someone) (s:maizumna/minsiatna/zumna) (a:minphatna/pahtawina) (b:mindai) (q:draft)
mindainate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disgraces/shame) (d:plural of <mindaina>: the disgraces a people has suffered or brought on itself) (b:mindaina) (q:draft)
mindainateng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the disgrace/disgrace) (d:<mindaina>, disgrace, with <teng>, all: the whole of one's disgrace) (b:mindaina) (q:draft)
mindaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disgrace/dishonor/put to shame) (d:<mindai>, be disgraced, with the causative <sak>: bring shame or dishonor on someone) (s:minsiasak/maizumsak/zahhuaisak/zumsak) (a:minthangsak/pahtawi) (b:mindai) (q:draft)
mindaisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scorn/insult/shaming) (d:<mindaisak>, put to shame, with the noun suffix <na>: the scorn or insults by which others shame someone) (s:simmawhna/kosiatna) (b:mindaisak) (q:draft)
mindang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:other name/another name) (d:<min>, name, with <dang>, other: a second name of a person, or a name other than the one just mentioned) (s:minno) (q:draft)
mineu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lowly person/the small/common person) (d:<mi>, person, with <neu>, small: a person of low standing, usually paired with <milian>, the great) (s:miniam) (a:milian) (q:draft)
mineupen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the least/lowliest person/least person) (d:<mineu> lowly person with the superlative <pen>) (b:mineu) (q:draft)
mineute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the lowly/the small/common people) (d:plural of <mineu>, people of low standing, the opposite of <miliante>) (s:miniamte/nautangte/minautangte) (a:miliante) (b:mineu) (r:19.62.9) (q:draft)
miniam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lowly person/person of low position) (d:<mi>, person, with <niam>, low: a person of low position; {miniam i hih laitak} is when we were lowly) (s:mineu) (a:milian) (q:draft)
Miniam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lowly person/humble person) (d:<miniam>, lowly person, written with a capital at the start of a verse; {Miniam ihih laitakin} is when we were lowly) (s:mineu) (b:miniam) (q:draft)
Miniamin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Miniamin) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite under King Hezekiah and a priest in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.12.41/16.12.17)
miniamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the humble/the lowly/humble people) (d:plural of <miniam>: people of low position or humble spirit, whom God lifts up) (s:mineute/kiniamkhiatte) (a:kiphasakte) (b:miniam) (q:draft)
minih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:two men/two people) (d:<mi> person with <nih> two, written as one word) (q:draft)
minin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:by name/in the name of/name) (d:<min>, name, with the marker <in>: by name or in the name of someone; also as subject, the name is) (b:min) (q:draft)
mininte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the unclean/unclean people) (d:<mi>, person, with <nin>, unclean, and the plural <te>; paired with <misiangte>, the clean) (a:misiangte) (q:draft)
minkhem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:figurative name/byname/nickname) (d:a name borne in place of the real one; in the verse the city is figuratively called Sodom and Egypt) (q:draft, low confidence)
minlian = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:exalted/renowned/great in name) (d:<min>, name, with <lian>, great: having a great name, exalted) (s:minthang) (q:draft)
minliat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be honoured/be great in name) (d:form of <minlian> used before <nading>: {na minliat nading}, your being honoured) (q:draft)
minliatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:majesty/glory/honour/renown) (d:<minliat>, be great in name, with the noun suffix <na>: majesty, the greatness and honour of a king or of God) (s:minthanna/vangliatna) (a:mindaina) (b:minliat) (r:19.111.3) (q:draft)
minmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ripen/be ripening) (d:<min> ripe, doubled: beginning to ripen, said of figs) (q:draft, low confidence)
minnei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:named/called) (d:<min>, name, with <nei>, have: bearing the name, placed after a personal name) (q:draft)
Minni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Minni) (d:kingdom summoned with Ararat and Ashkenaz to make war on Babylon) (r:24.51.27) (q:draft)
Minnith = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Minnith) (d:place east of the Jordan, as far as which Jephthah struck down the Ammonites) (r:7.11.33)
minno = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nickname/other name) (d:<min>, name, with <no>, small: a second name by which a person is known) (s:mindang) (b:min) (q:draft)
minpha = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good name/good reputation) (d:<min>, name, with <pha>, good: a good name, a good reputation) (a:minsia) (q:draft)
minphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:praise/honor/be praised) (d:<min>, name, with <phat>, praise: praise the name of someone; {minphat ding}, to be praised, is set against {minsiat ding}, to be disgraced) (a:minsiat) (q:draft)
minphathuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:praiseworthy/approved/of good repute) (d:<minphat>, praise, with <huai>, worthy of: deserving praise, well thought of) (s:phathuai) (q:draft)
minphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:honor/good name/praise) (d:being well spoken of, the opposite of <mindaina>) (s:pahtawina/minthanna/phatna) (a:mindaina/minsiatna) (b:minphat) (r:20.8.18) (q:draft)
minphatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:honors/greatness) (d:plural of <minphatna>: the honors given to a person) (b:minphatna) (q:draft)
minsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cooked/boiled/prepared) (d:of meat or food, already cooked: <min>, cooked or ripe, with <sa>, already; the opposite of <sial>, raw) (s:huansa) (a:sial) (q:draft)
minsia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bad name/disgrace/ill repute) (d:<min>, name, with <sia>, bad; {minsia tun} is to bring a bad name on someone and {minsia sak} is to disgrace) (s:minsiatna/mindai/mindaina) (a:minpha) (q:draft)
minsiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disgrace/dishonor/shame/defame) (d:<minsia>, bad name, with the causative <sak>: give someone a bad name, bring disgrace on someone) (s:mindaisak/maizumsak/zahhuaisak) (a:minthangsak) (b:minsia) (q:draft)
minsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be disgraced/get a bad name) (d:form of <minsia>, bad name, used as a verb before <ding>: get a bad name; set against <minphat>, be praised) (s:mindai) (a:minphat) (b:minsia) (q:draft)
minsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disgrace/dishonor/shame/reproach) (d:the spoiling of one's name, loss of good reputation) (s:mindaina/maizumna/zumna/minsia) (a:minphatna) (b:minsiat) (q:draft)
minta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ripe/have ripened) (d:<min>, ripe, with <ta>, now: has become ripe, said of fruit ready for harvest) (q:draft)
minte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:names) (d:plural of <min>, name) (b:min) (q:draft)
minthak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:new name) (d:<min>, name, with <thak>, new; {minthak phuah} is to give a new name) (q:draft)
minthan = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:glorious/famous/renowned) (d:form of <minthang>, famous or glorious, used before a suffix; found mostly in {minthan’na}, glory or honour) (s:minthang/minlian) (r:48.1.5) (q:draft)
minthang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:popular/famous/well known) (d:known and spoken of by many people, held in honor among them) (s:minlian)
minthang = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:renown/renowned/glorious/majestic) (d:of great name, glorious, said of a city, a throne or the name of God)
minthang = (i:3) (t:n) (w:fame/renown) (d:a great name known far and wide) (s:minthanna)
Minthang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:glorious/majestic/renowned) (d:<minthang>, glorious, written with a capital in titles of God: {Minthang Kumpipa} is the King of glory and {Vanglian Minthang pa} the Majestic Glory) (b:minthang) (r:19.24.9) (q:draft)
minthangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:gloriously/in glory/famously) (d:<minthang>, glorious, with the suffix <in>: in a glorious way, with honor) (b:minthang) (q:draft)
minthangsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:renowned/once famous) (d:<minthang>, famous, with <sa>, already: that has been famous, once renowned) (b:minthang) (q:draft)
minthangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:glorify/exalt/honor) (d:<minthang>, famous or glorious, with the causative <sak>: give glory or honor to someone) (s:pahtawi/thangsak/liansak) (a:mindaisak/minsiasak) (b:minthang) (q:draft)
minthangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:renown/famous men/the renowned) (d:plural of <minthang>: famous people; {mi minthangte} are men of renown) (b:minthang)
minthanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:glory/splendor/fame/honor) (d:<minthan>, glorious, with the noun suffix <na>: glory, splendor or fame, of God or of a person; also written {minthan’na}) (s:minliatna/vangliatna/pahtawina) (a:mindaina) (b:minthan) (q:draft)
minthannate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:glories/glory/splendor) (d:<minthanna>, glory, with the plural <te>: glories, all the splendor of a person or kingdom) (b:minthanna) (r:19.145.12) (q:draft)
minthanzawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be more honoured/have greater glory) (d:<minthang>, renowned, with the comparative <zaw>, in the form used before {mah bangin}: have greater honor than) (q:draft)
minthuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seal/signet) (d:<min>, name, with <thuh>, stamp, and the noun suffix <na>: a seal for stamping a name on a document; {minthuhna zungbuh} is a signet ring) (q:draft)
minu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:woman) (d:<mi>, person, with <nu> marking a female) (s:numei) (a:mipa)
minuamsa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blessed person/happy person/fortunate person) (d:<mi>, person, with <nuamsa>, happy or at ease: a person who is well off, blessed) (q:draft)
minun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:by name) (d:<min> name with <un>, the plural marker joined to <in>: by their names) (b:min) (q:draft)
mipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:man) (d:<mi>, person, with <pa> marking a male: a man, the man just spoken of) (s:pasal) (a:minu/numei) (b:mi)
Mipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:man) (d:<mipa>, the man, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or as a title of Christ, the Man from heaven) (b:mipa) (q:draft)
Mipaktat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:adulterous person/immoral person) (d:<mi>, person, with <paktat>, sexually immoral: an adulterous person, here of an unfaithful generation) (q:draft)
mipawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nation/people/group of people) (d:<mi>, person, with <pawl>, group; {mipawl khempeuh}, all nations) (s:minam) (q:draft)
Mipawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nation/people) (d:<mipawl>, nation, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {Mipawl khempeuh} is all nations) (b:mipawl) (q:draft)
mipawlpawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nations/peoples/groups of people) (d:<mi>, person, with <pawl>, group, doubled, and the plural <te>: the various peoples, the nations) (q:draft)
mipawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:people/peoples/nations) (d:a people or nation taken together, or groups of people; plural of <mipawl>) (s:minamte) (b:mipawl) (q:draft)
mipha = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good person/the good/righteous person) (d:<mi>, person, with <pha>, good: a good or upright person; the opposite of <misia>) (s:midik) (a:misia/migilo) (q:draft)
miphak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leper) (d:<mi>, person, with <phak>, leprosy: a person who has leprosy) (s:phakpa/miphakpa) (q:draft)
miphakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leper) (d:<miphak>, leper, with <pa> marking a man) (s:phakpa/miphak) (b:miphak) (q:draft)
miphakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lepers/people with leprosy) (d:<miphak>, leper, with the plural <te>) (s:phakte) (b:miphak) (q:draft)
miphapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good man/innocent man) (d:<mipha>, good person, with <pa> marking a man: a good or innocent man) (s:mihoihpa/dikpa/phapa) (b:mipha) (q:draft)
miphate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the righteous/good people/the upright) (d:plural of <mipha>, a good person: those who are good or faithful, set against <migilote>, the wicked) (s:midikte/mihoihte) (a:migilote/misiate) (b:mipha) (r:42.5.32) (q:draft)
mipi = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:noble/generous) (d:in {mipi lungsim}, a noble or great-hearted mind) (q:draft, low confidence)
mipih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fellow countryman/own people/kinsman) (d:a person or people of the same nation as oneself; the suffix <pih> marks sharing, like English fellow) (b:mi) (r:27.9.20) (q:draft)
mipihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fellow countrymen/own people/kinsmen) (d:plural of <mipih>: people of one's own nation, tribe or kind) (q:draft)
mipil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wise person/wise man) (d:<mi>, person, with <pil>, wise: a wise person; {mipil suak} is to become wise) (s:mipilpa) (a:mihai) (r:20.10.19) (q:draft)
mipilin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wise person) (d:<mipil>, wise person, with the marker <in>; {mipilin bawl} is to make someone wise) (b:mipil) (q:draft)
mipilpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wise man) (d:<mipil>, wise person, with <pa> marking a man; set against <mihaipa>, the fool) (s:mipil) (a:mihaipa) (b:mipil) (q:draft)
mipilpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:very wise person/great sage) (d:<mipil> wise person with the augmentative <pi>) (a:mihaipi) (b:mipil) (q:draft)
mipilsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the wise/wise people) (d:<mi>, person, with <pilsa>, already wise, and the plural <te>: those who are already wise) (s:mipilte) (q:draft)
mipilte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the wise/wise men) (d:plural of <mipil>: wise people; also the wise men, the Magi, whom Herod called) (s:pilte/lungpilte) (a:mihaite) (b:mipil) (r:20.15.24) (q:draft)
mipilteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the wise men/wise men) (d:<mipil> wise person with <teng>, all of them) (b:mipil) (q:draft)
mipite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:people/crowds/multitude) (d:<mipi>, the public, the mass of people, with the plural <te>) (s:mihonte/mihonpite) (b:mipi) (q:draft)
Mipite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the people/the public) (d:{Mipite’ Kongpi} is the Gate of the People) (b:mipite) (q:draft)
mipoite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the crippled/the maimed) (d:people with injured or disabled bodies, named with the lame and the blind) (q:draft)
mipum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:human body/flesh) (d:<mi> person with <pum> body: a person in bodily form; {mipum bangin}, in the flesh) (q:draft)
Miriam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Miriam) (d:sister of Moses and Aaron, daughter of Amram, a prophetess who led the women in song after the crossing of the sea) (r:2.15.20/4.12.1)
Mirmah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mirmah) (d:son of Shaharaim and Hodesh, head of a family of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.10)
mirrah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:myrrh) (d:a fragrant resin used as perfume and in preparing a body for burial; often {mirrah paknamtui}, myrrh perfume) (s:mor/myrrh) (q:draft)
Mirrah = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Mirrah/myrrh) (d:myrrh, a fragrant resin, written with a capital; {Mirrah paknamtui} is myrrh perfume) (r:20.7.17/1.37.25)
Mishael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishael) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Uzziel the Levite and the companion of Daniel who was renamed Meshach) (r:2.6.22)
Mishal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mishal) (d:town in the territory of Asher, given to the Levites) (r:6.21.30/6.19.26)
Misham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Misham) (d:son of Elpaal of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.12)
Mishamannah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishmannah) (d:warrior of the tribe of Gad who joined David in the wilderness, fourth in rank) (r:13.12.10)
Mishma = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishma) (d:name of two men, a son of Ishmael and a descendant of Simeon) (r:1.25.14)
Mishmannah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishmannah) (d:warrior of the tribe of Gad who joined David in the wilderness, fourth in rank) (r:13.12.10)
Mishrai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Mishraite) (d:one of the clans of Kiriath Jearim in Judah) (r:13.2.53)
Mishrefoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Misrephoth) (d:first part of the name <Mishrefoth-maim>, a place near Sidon at the northern limit of the land) (r:6.13.6)
Mishrefoth-maim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Misrephoth Maim) (d:place near Sidon, named with Lebanon as the northern limit of the land still to be taken) (q:draft)
misi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dead person/the dead/corpse) (d:<mi>, person, with <si>, die: someone who has died, or the body of a dead person; {misi vui} is bury the dead) (s:sipa/siluang) (q:draft)
misia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bad person/wicked person/the wicked) (d:<mi>, person, with <sia>, bad: a bad or wicked person, the opposite of <mipha>, a good person) (s:migilo) (a:mipha) (q:draft)
misiam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:skilled man/able man/capable person) (d:<mi>, person, with <siam>, skilled: a skilled or capable person) (s:mikician) (q:draft)
misiamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:capable men/skilled people/the learned) (d:<misiam>, skilled person, with the plural <te>: capable men, and in the Gospels the learned) (b:misiam) (q:draft)
misiangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the clean/clean people) (d:<mi>, person, with <siang>, clean, and the plural <te>: those who are ritually clean, paired with <mininte>, the unclean) (a:mininte) (q:draft)
misiangtho = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holy person/saint/holy one) (d:<mi>, person, with <siangtho>, holy: a holy person, one who belongs to God; {Pasian’ misiangtho} is a holy man of God or the Holy One of God) (s:siangthopa) (r:49.1.15) (q:draft)
Misiangtho = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Holy One/holy person) (d:<misiangtho> written with a capital, of the Holy One of God or at the start of a sentence) (b:misiangtho) (q:draft)
misiangthote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:saints/holy people/God’s people) (d:<misiangtho>, holy person, with the plural <te>: the people who belong to God) (q:draft)
misiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ruined man/broken man/wretched man) (d:<mi> person with <sia> bad, ruined, and <pa> marking a man) (b:misia) (q:draft, low confidence)
misiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bad people/the evil/the wicked) (d:<misia>, bad person, with the plural <te>; set against <mihoihte> and <miphate>, good people) (s:migilote) (a:mihoihte/miphate) (b:misia) (q:draft)
misiluang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dead body/corpse) (d:<misi>, dead person, with <luang>, body: a dead body) (s:siluang/luanghawm) (q:draft)
Misiluangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:corpses/dead bodies/carcasses) (d:<misiluang>, dead body, with the plural <te>, here with a capital at the start of a sentence) (s:siluangte/luanghawmte) (q:draft)
misimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:census/counting of people/numbering) (d:<mi>, person, and <sim>, count, with the noun suffix <na>: a count of the people; {misimna bawl} is take a census) (s:kisimna) (q:draft)
misimtatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hypocrites) (d:<mi>, person, with <simtat>, as in <simtatna>, hypocrisy, and the plural <te>: people who pretend to be good) (s:simtatte/kineihkhemte) (q:draft, low confidence)
misipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dead man) (d:<misi> dead person with <pa>, a man: the dead man) (s:sipa) (b:misi) (q:draft)
misite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the dead/dead people) (d:<misi>, dead person, with the plural <te>; {misite’ gam} is the land of the dead, the grave) (s:site) (a:nungtate) (b:misi) (r:18.26.5) (q:draft)
Misite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the dead) (d:<misite> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in the name {Misite’ Gam}, the Land of the Dead, Hades) (b:misite) (r:66.20.13) (q:draft)
Mispah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mizpah) (d:region at the foot of Mount Hermon where the Hivites lived in the time of Joshua) (r:6.11.3)
Mispar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mispar) (d:one of the leaders who returned from exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.2)
Mispereth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mispereth) (d:one of the leaders who returned from exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel, called Mispar in the book of Ezra) (r:16.7.6)
Misrefothmaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Misrephoth Maim) (d:place near Sidon as far as which Joshua pursued the kings of the north) (r:6.11.8/6.13.6)
misuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:robber/bandit/insurrectionist) (d:one who attacks people with violence: a robber, and in the Gospels a rebel such as Barabbas) (s:buluh/galgu) (q:draft)
misuam = (i:2) (t:v) (w:riot/rebel/make an insurrection) (d:rise up and attack people, take part in an uprising) (q:draft)
misuampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:robber/insurrectionist/bandit) (d:<misuam> robber, rebel, with <pa> marking a man) (b:misuam) (q:draft)
misuamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:robbers/bandits/rebels) (d:<misuam>, robber or rebel, with the plural <te>: men who attack and rob) (s:buluhte/suamte) (b:misuam) (q:draft)
Misusia = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Misusia) (d:word addressed to Babylon in Psalm 137, written with a capital: <mi>, person, with <susia>, destroy; the NIV has doomed to destruction) (r:19.137.8)
mit = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eye) (d:the organ of sight; {mit tawh en} is look with the eyes) (s:mittang) (r:1.19.11)
mit = (i:2) (t:v) (w:put out/go out) (d:of a fire or a lamp, go out; also put a fire out) (s:mitsak/sumit)
mit = (i:3) (t:adv) (w:off)
mit = (i:4) (t:v) (w:kill)
mitah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the eyes/in the sight/on the eyes) (d:<mit>, eye, with the place marker <ah>: on the eyes or in the eyes; after <Topa> or a pronoun it means in the sight of) (b:mit) (q:draft)
mitang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eye/eyesight) (d:apparently the same as <mittang>, eye) (s:mittang) (q:draft, low confidence)
mite = (i:1) (t:v) (w:people) (b:mi) (r:1.4.26) plural form of <mi>
Mite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:people) (d:<mite> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a title: {Jew Mite’ Kumpipa}, King of the Jews; {Mite’ Kongpi}, Gate of the People) (b:mite) (q:draft)
mitei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:discerning person/person of insight) (d:<mi>, person, with <tei>, clever: a person of insight, paired with <mipil>, wise person) (q:draft, low confidence)
miteite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the intelligent/the clever) (d:<mi>, person, with <tei>, clever, and the plural <te>: clever or learned people, named beside <mipilte>, the wise) (q:draft)
mitepen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:people/men) (d:<mite> people with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word) (b:mite) (q:draft)
mithagolte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:giants) (d:<mi>, person, with <thagol>, big and strong, and the plural <te>: the giants of Gath, where the NIV has Rapha and Rephaites) (s:thagolte) (r:13.20.4) (q:draft)
Mithagolte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Mithagolte/Rephaites) (d:the giants, a race of very big men in Philistia, called Rapha or the Rephaites in the NIV; <mithagolte> written with a capital) (r:10.21.16)
mithah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bloodshed/murder/killing) (d:<mi>, person, with <thah>, kill: the killing of a person; {mithah mawhna} is the guilt of bloodshed) (s:mithahna/thahna) (q:draft)
mithahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:murder/killing/bloodshed) (d:<mithah>, killing of a person, with the noun suffix <na>: murder, bloodshed) (s:thahna/kithahna/mithah) (b:mithah) (q:draft)
mithak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:new person/new self/new creation) (d:<mi>, person, with <thak>, new: the new self of one who is in Christ) (q:draft)
mithat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:murderer/killer) (d:<mi>, person, with <that>, kill: one who kills people, a murderer; the NIV has bloodthirsty and criminal) (s:thatpa) (q:draft)
mithatpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:murderer/killer) (d:<mithat> murderer with <pa> marking a man) (s:thatpa) (b:mithat) (q:draft)
mithatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:killers/manslayers/murderers) (d:<mithat>, killer, with the plural <te>; {mithatte’ bukna khuapi} is a city of refuge for those who have killed someone) (s:thatte) (b:mithat) (r:6.21.38) (q:draft)
mitheek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wink/signal with the eye) (d:<mit>, eye, with <heek>: a sign made with the eye; {mitheek pia} is wink at someone) (q:draft)
Mithkah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mithkah) (d:place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped between Terah and Hashmonah) (r:4.33.28/4.33.29)
Mithni = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Mithni) (d:home or clan of Joshaphat, one of the mighty warriors of David, who is called the Mithnite in the NIV) (r:13.11.43)
Mithredath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mithredath) (d:name of two Persian officials: the treasurer of King Cyrus, and a man who wrote to King Artaxerxes against Jerusalem) (r:15.1.8/15.4.7)
mithumante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the righteous/upright people) (d:<mi> person with <thuman> truthful, upright, plural <te>) (s:midikte/thumante) (a:migilote) (q:draft)
mithupite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nobles/important people/dignitaries) (d:<mi> person with <thupi> important, plural <te>) (s:miliante) (q:draft)
Mitilena = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mitylene) (d:chief city of the island of Lesbos, where the ship of Paul called after Assos; also spelled <Mitylene>) (r:44.20.14)
mitin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:with the eyes/with one's own eyes) (d:<mit>, eye, with the marker <in>, showing the eye as the means of seeing: with the eyes) (b:mit) (q:draft)
mitkhu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eyelid) (d:<mit> eye with <khu> cover; {mitkhu mul}, the hair of it, stands for the eyebrows in Leviticus 14:9) (q:draft)
mitkhuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eye socket) (d:<mit> eye with <khuk> pit, hollow) (s:mitkua) (q:draft)
mitkhute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eyelids) (d:<mitkhu> eyelid with plural <te>) (b:mitkhu) (q:draft)
mitkua = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eye socket) (d:<mit> eye with <kua> hole) (s:mitkhuk) (q:draft)
mitlawt = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lose one's sight/have the eyes fail) (d:<mit> eye with <lawt>; {mitlawt dongin kap}, weep until the eyes fail) (q:draft, low confidence)
mitmangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grow dim/lose one's sight) (d:<mit> eye with <mang> lost, dim, and the linking marker <in>: the eyes growing dim) (q:draft, low confidence)
mitnauta = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pupil of the eye/apple of the eye) (d:the pupil of the eye, used in comparisons for something guarded with great care: {mitnauta bangin kem}, keep as the apple of the eye) (q:draft)
mitpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out suddenly/be snuffed out) (d:<mit> go out, of a light, with <pak> at once) (q:draft)
mitphial = (i:1) (t:n) (w:magic/sorcery/witchcraft) (d:magic arts that deceive the eye; {mitphial siamte} are magicians and {mitphial bawl} is practise sorcery) (r:27.2.2) (q:draft)
mitphiat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blink/twinkling of an eye/moment) (d:the closing and opening of the eyelid, hence a very short time: {mitphiat kal} and {mitphiat sung}, in a moment) (s:tomkha) (q:draft)
mitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quench/extinguish/put out) (d:<mit>, go out, with the causative <sak>: make a fire or lamp go out) (s:sumit/phelh) (b:mit) (q:draft)
mitsi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:close the eyes/shut the eyes) (d:of the eyes, be shut; with <sak>, make someone's eyes shut so that he cannot see) (q:draft)
mitsicip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shut the eyes tight/close the eyes) (d:<mitsi> close the eyes with <cip> tightly) (b:mitsi) (q:draft)
mitsuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:look to/fix the eyes on/watch) (d:keep the eyes on someone or something, in trust or attention) (q:draft)
mitsuanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:with eyes fixed on/looking to) (d:<mitsuan> fix the eyes on, with <in>; {mitsuanin nei} is to keep the eyes fixed on, to hold in view) (b:mitsuan) (q:draft)
mitta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out/have gone out) (d:<mit> go out, of fire or a lamp, with <ta> marking a change that has come about) (b:mit) (q:draft)
mittang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eye) (d:the eye, the eyeball; a fuller word for <mit>) (s:mit) (r:27.7.8) (q:draft)
mittangin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:with the eye/by sight) (d:<mittang> eye with the marker <in>: with the eyes) (b:mittang) (q:draft)
mittangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eyes) (d:<mittang>, eye, with the plural <te>) (s:mitte) (b:mittang) (q:draft)
mittaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:blind) (d:<mit>, eye, with <taw>, blind: blind; also used as a noun for a blind person) (s:taw) (q:draft)
mittawpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blind man) (d:<mittaw>, blind, with {-pa}, marking a man) (b:mittaw) (q:draft)
mittawpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blind ones/the blind) (d:<mittaw> blind with <pi> and the plural <te>: the ones that are blind, here of animals brought as offerings) (b:mittaw) (q:draft)
mittawsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:blind/formerly blind) (d:<mittaw> blind with <sa>, already: one who had been blind) (b:mittaw) (q:draft)
mittawsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:blind/make blind) (d:<mittaw> blind with the causative <sak>) (s:tawsak) (b:mittaw) (r:23.29.9) (q:draft)
mittawt = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be blind/become blind) (d:form of <mittaw> blind used before <nading> and before a joined word) (b:mittaw) (q:draft)
mittawte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the blind/blind people) (d:<mittaw>, blind, with the plural <te>: blind people) (s:tawte) (b:mittaw) (q:draft)
Mittawte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the blind/blind people) (d:<mittawte> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line) (b:mittawte) (q:draft)
mittawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blindness) (d:<mittawt>, be blind, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being blind) (b:mittawt) (q:draft)
mitte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eyes) (s:mittangte) (b:mit) (r:1.3.5) plural form of <mit>
mituam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:special people/own people) (d:<mi> person with <tuam> separate: a people set apart; said by God of Israel where the English has Virgin Israel) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mitylene = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mitylene) (d:chief city of the island of Lesbos, where the ship of Paul called after Assos) (r:44.20.14)
mitzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go out/be quenched) (d:<mit> go out with <zo> be able; with <lo>, cannot be quenched) (b:mit) (q:draft)
mitzung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:eyesight/sight) (d:<mit> eye with <zung> root; {ka mitzung zaw} is my eyes grow weak) (q:draft, low confidence)
mivanglianpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mighty man/hero) (d:<mi> person with <vanglian> mighty and <pa> marking a man) (q:draft)
mivomte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:black people) (d:<mi> person with <vom> black and the plural <te>; {Ethiopia mivomte} is the Ethiopians) (q:draft)
Mizar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Mizar) (d:hill or mountain in the region of Mount Hermon, named in Psalm 42) (r:19.42.6)
mizawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:poor person/the poor/beggar) (d:<mi>, person, with <zawng>, poor: a poor person or a beggar; also used to say that someone is poor) (s:zawngpa) (a:mihau) (r:18.29.12) (q:draft)
mizawngin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:poor person) (d:<mizawng> poor person with the marker <in>, here as: became poor) (b:mizawng) (q:draft)
mizawngpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:poor man/beggar) (d:<mizawng> poor person with <pa> marking a man) (s:zawngpa) (a:mihaupa) (b:mizawng) (q:draft)
mizawngpen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:poorest people/the poorest) (d:<mizawng> poor person with the superlative <pen>) (b:mizawng) (q:draft)
mizawngte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the poor/poor people/the needy) (d:<mizawng>, poor person, with the plural <te>: poor people, the opposite of <mihaute>, the rich) (s:zawngte/cimawhte/gentheite) (a:mihaute) (r:18.34.28) (q:draft)
Mizpah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mizpah) (d:name of several places, among them the town in Benjamin where Samuel gathered Israel and the place in Gilead where Jacob and Laban made their covenant) (r:16.3.19/1.31.49)
Mizpeh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mizpah) (d:spelling of <Mizpah> used for a town in the lowland of Judah, a town in Benjamin and a place in Moab where David took his parents) (r:6.18.26/6.15.38)
Mizuau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:liar) (d:<mi> person with <zuau> lie; {Mizuau tecite} are false witnesses) (q:draft)
mizuaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:liars) (d:<mi> person with <zuau> lie and plural <te>, people who tell lies) (s:zuaugente/zuautheite) (q:draft)
Mizzah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mizzah) (d:son of Reuel and grandson of Esau, a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.13/13.1.37)
Mnanhath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Manahath) (d:place to which men of Benjamin living in Geba were deported; the NIV spells it Manahath) (r:13.8.6)
Mnason = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mnason) (d:man from Cyprus, an early disciple, at whose house Paul stayed on the way to Jerusalem) (r:44.21.16)
mo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bride) (d:a woman who is being married; {mo la} is to take a bride, so a wedding, and {mo-man} is the bride price) (s:mothak) (r:1.34.12) (q:draft)
mo = (i:2) (t:n) (w:daughter-in-law) (d:the wife of one’s son) (s:monu) (q:draft)
Mo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bride) (d:<mo>, bride, written with a capital, in Revelation for the bride of the Lamb and at the start of a sentence) (s:Mothak) (b:mo) (q:draft)
Moab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Moab) (d:son of Lot by his elder daughter and ancestor of the Moabites; also the land of his descendants east of the Dead Sea) (r:1.19.37)
Moabte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Moab/Moabites) (d:the people of Moab, descendants of Lot, living east of the Dead Sea) (b:Moab) (r:12.3.23/4.21.28)
Moadiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Moadiah) (d:head of a priestly family in the days of the high priest Joiakim) (r:16.12.17)
Moan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Maon) (d:spelling of <Maon>, the desert in the hill country of Judah where David hid from Saul) (r:9.23.25)
mohbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bake bread/make bread) (d:<moh>, bread, with <bawl>, make: make bread; {mohbawl pa} is the baker) (b:moh) (q:draft)
mohin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:into cakes/into loaves) (d:<moh>, cake or loaf, with the marker <in>: into cakes or loaves, as in {mohin bawl}, make into loaves) (b:moh) (q:draft)
mohkeu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dry bread/dry crust) (d:<moh>, bread, with <keu>, dry: a dry piece of bread, a crust) (q:draft)
mohlawh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:basket of bread/bread basket) (d:<moh>, bread, with <lawh>, basket: a basket of bread) (q:draft, low confidence)
mohneu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small loaf/little cake) (d:<moh>, bread, with <neu>, small: a small loaf or cake) (q:draft)
mohpheng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wafer/thin cake/thin loaf) (d:<moh>, cake, with <pheng>, flat: a thin flat cake of bread, a wafer) (s:pheng) (q:draft)
mohphengte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thin cakes/wafers/flat loaves) (d:plural of <mohpheng>: thin flat cakes or wafers of bread) (s:pheengte) (b:mohpheng) (q:draft)
mohte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cakes/loaves) (d:plural of <moh>: cakes or loaves; {thei mohte} are cakes of pressed figs) (b:moh) (q:draft)
moilai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:young/youthful) (d:still in the time of youth, said of a boy or young man) (s:khangno) (q:draft)
moipen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:youngest) (d:<moi>, young, with <pen>, most: the youngest of a group, the opposite of <hampen>, the oldest) (s:khangnopen) (a:hampen/teekpen) (b:moi) (q:draft)
moisuahin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:youthful/in the bloom of youth) (d:<moisuah> newly grown up, in full youth, with the linking marker <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
moken = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dowry/wedding gift) (d:a gift given with a bride at her marriage, from <mo>, bride) (q:draft)
mokenin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as a wedding gift/as a dowry) (d:<moken>, wedding gift, with the marker <in>: as a wedding gift) (b:moken) (q:draft)
mokhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give in marriage/send off as a bride) (d:<mo>, bride, with <khak>, send: give a daughter in marriage to another family) (q:draft)
Moladah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Moladah) (d:town in the far south of Judah, allotted to the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.28/16.11.26)
molakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:<mo>, bride, with <lak>, take, and the noun suffix <na>: the taking of a bride, a wedding; {molakna puan} is wedding clothes) (s:mopina) (q:draft)
molakpawi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wedding feast/wedding banquet) (d:<mo>, bride, with <lak>, take, and <pawi>, feast: a wedding feast) (s:mopawi) (q:draft)
Molek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Molech/Molek) (d:god of the Ammonites, to whom children were sacrificed) (r:3.20.4/3.18.21)
molhtum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:club/rod/cudgel) (d:a heavy stick used as a weapon or for beating, a club) (r:2.21.20) (q:draft)
molhtumin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as a club/club) (d:<molhtum>, club, with the marker <in>: as a club) (b:molhtum) (q:draft)
molhtumte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:clubs/cudgels) (d:plural of <molhtum>; {kulh sukkhap nading molhtumte} are battering rams) (b:molhtum) (q:draft)
moliah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:best man/groomsman/wedding companion) (d:one who attends the bridegroom at his wedding; {moliah pa}, the man who does so) (q:draft)
moliahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:best man/groomsman/wedding companion) (d:<moliah> with <pa> marking a man: the companion who attends the bridegroom) (b:moliah) (q:draft)
Molid = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Molid) (d:son of Abishur and Abihail, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.29)
Molok = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Molek) (d:spelling of <Molek> in Acts, the god to whom Israel carried a shrine in the wilderness) (r:44.7.43)
mom = (t:see) <mom-ai>
mom-ai = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (d:a small creature with a poisonous sting in its tail, also written <momai>) (s:momai/aikam) (q:draft)
momai = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (d:a small creature with a poisonous sting in its tail, also written <mom-ai>) (s:mom-ai/aikam) (q:draft)
momaite = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpions) (d:plural of <momai>, scorpion) (s:aikamte) (b:momai) (q:draft)
moman = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bride-price/dowry) (d:<mo>, bride, with <man>, price: the price paid to the father of a bride) (q:draft)
mong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:end/edge/hem/corner) (d:the far end, outer edge or corner of something; {puan mong} is the hem of a garment and {mong nei lo} is without end) (q:draft)
monga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the edge/at the end) (d:<mong>, edge, with the place marker <a>, a short form of <ah>: at the edge or end of a place) (s:mongah) (b:mong) (q:draft)
mongah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the end/at the edge/at the corner) (d:<mong>, end or edge, with the place marker <ah>: at the end, edge or far part of a place) (s:monga) (b:mong) (q:draft)
mongciik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:farthest end/extremity/uttermost part) (d:the very edge of a land; {leitaw lam mongciik}, the southernmost part) (s:mongdong) (q:draft)
mongdong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:end/farthest end) (d:<mong>, edge, with <dong>, as far as: the farthest end; {lei mongdong} is the ends of the earth) (s:mongciik) (q:draft)
mongin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:by the hem/by the edge) (d:<mong>, edge or hem, with the marker <in>: by the edge, said of what is taken hold of) (b:mong) (q:draft)
mongkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one end/one edge) (d:<mong>, end or edge, with <khat>, one: one end; {mongkhat panin mongkhat dong} is from one end to the other) (q:draft)
mongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ends/edges/corners/hems) (d:plural of <mong>: the ends of poles, the edges of a beard, the corners or hem of a garment) (b:mong) (q:draft)
mongteep = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hem/edge/fringe) (d:the border or fringe at the edge of a garment; {puan mongteep} is the edge of a cloak) (s:puanmongteep) (q:draft)
monu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:daughter-in-law) (d:<mo>, bride or son’s wife, with <nu> marking a woman: the wife of one’s son) (s:mo) (b:mo) (q:draft)
monute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:daughters-in-law) (d:plural of <monu>: the wives of the sons of a family) (s:mote) (b:monu) (q:draft)
mopina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:a wedding, the taking of a bride; {mopina pawi} is a wedding feast) (s:molakna/zipina) (q:draft)
mopipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:the man who is taking a bride) (s:zipipa/zineipa)
Mopipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:<mopipa>, bridegroom, written with a capital) (s:zipipa/zineipa) (b:mopipa) (q:draft)
mor = (i:1) (t:n) (w:myrrh) (d:a fragrant resin used as a spice and perfume, in {mor paknamtui}, myrrh spice) (s:mirrah/myrrh) (q:draft)
Mordekai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mordecai) (d:Jew of the tribe of Benjamin living in Susa, cousin and guardian of Queen Esther) (r:17.2.5/17.2.7)
Moreh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Moreh) (d:place near Shechem known for its great tree; also a hill in the Valley of Jezreel near which Midian camped) (r:5.11.30/7.7.1)
Moreseth = (t:see) <Moreseth-gath>
