Moseste = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Moses) (d:<Moses> with the plural <te>: Moses and the one named with him, here Aaron and Moses) (b:Moses) (r:2.6.26)
mot = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:idly/aimlessly/senselessly) (d:without thought, sense or purpose; {mot pau} is to talk idly or foolishly and {mot om} is to live on aimlessly) (s:mawk) (q:draft)
mote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:daughters-in-law) (d:plural of <mo>: the wives of the sons of a family) (s:monute) (b:mo) (q:draft)
mothak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bride) (d:<mo>, bride, with <thak>, new: a newly married woman, a bride; {mothak nu} is the bride) (s:mo) (q:draft)
Mothak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bride) (d:<mothak> written with a capital for the bride of the Lamb) (s:Mo) (b:mothak) (q:draft)
