Mual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Mount/Mountain) (d:<mual>, mountain, written with a capital after the name of a mountain, as in {Sinai Mual}, Mount Sinai) (a:Kuam) (b:mual) (r:2.19.20) (q:draft)
muala = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the mountain/of the mountain) (d:<mual> mountain with the ending <a>, at or on: {Lebanon muala om}, that are on Mount Lebanon) (s:mualah) (b:mual) (q:draft)
Muala = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Mount/mountain) (d:<Mual> with <a>, of or on the Mount; {Oliv Muala lam} is the road on the Mount of Olives) (b:Mual) (q:draft)
mualah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the mountain/to the mountain) (d:<mual> mountain or hill with the place marker <ah>, on, at or to the mountain) (s:muala) (b:mual) (q:draft)
Mualah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:to the Mount/at the Mount) (d:<Mual> Mount with the place marker <ah>, in {Oliv Mualah}, to or at the Mount of Olives) (b:Mual) (q:draft)
mualbo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hill/hilltop/knoll) (d:a hill or rise of ground, used after the name of the hill, as {Ofel mualbo}, the hill of Ophel) (s:mualno/mualneu) (q:draft)
mualciang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pass/mountain pass) (d:the place where a line of hills is crossed, from <mual> hill) (s:ciangka) (q:draft)
mualdawn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hilltop/mountain top/high place) (d:<mual> hill with <dawn> top; also the high places where offerings were made) (s:mualvum) (q:draft)
mualdawnzang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mountaintop/hilltop) (d:<mual> hill with <dawn> top and <zang> level ground: the open top of a hill) (s:mualdawn) (q:draft)
mualh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fade/grow dim) (d:of a mark, stain or colour: become faint, fade) (q:draft)
mualin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:faded/dim) (d:said of a spot on the skin that has grown faint, in {mualin om} be faded; not the word <mual> mountain) (r:3.13.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
mualkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fade away/pass away/vanish) (d:<mual> disappear from sight with <khin> already; said of the fading brightness of the face of Moses) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mualkolh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bare hilltop/bare hill) (d:<mual> hill with <kolh>, apparently bare) (s:mualpawn) (q:draft, low confidence)
mualkuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley/ravine) (d:low ground between hills, from <mual>, hill, and <kuam>, valley; also used in the names of valleys) (s:guam/kuam) (a:mual) (r:24.7.31) (q:draft)
Mualkuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valley) (d:<mualkuam>, a valley between hills, written with a capital in the names of valleys such as {Ben-Hinnom Mualkuam}, the Valley of Ben Hinnom, and at the start of a sentence) (s:Kuam) (b:mualkuam) (r:24.32.35) (q:draft)
Mualkuamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:to the Valley/in the Valley) (d:<Mualkuam>, valley, with the place marker <ah>: to or in the Valley, as in {Ben-Hinnom Mualkuamah}, to the Valley of Ben Hinnom) (s:Kuamah) (b:Mualkuam) (q:draft)
mualleguamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hills and valleys) (d:<mual>, hill, <le>, and, <guam>, valley, with the plural <te>: the hills and valleys, the shape of the land that daylight makes stand out) (q:draft)
mualliante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mountains/great mountains) (d:<mual>, hill, with <lian>, great, and the plural <te>: the great mountains, often set beside <mualneute>, the hills) (s:mualsangte) (a:mualneute) (q:draft)
mualmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fade away/lose luster/grow dull) (d:<mual>, fade, with <mang>, away: lose its brightness altogether, said of something that once shone) (s:mualkhin) (q:draft)
mualmual = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:indistinctly/in a mutter) (d:doubled word after <pau> speak: speaking in a low unclear voice, muttering) (q:draft)
mualneu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hill/small hill) (d:<mual>, hill, with <neu>, small: a hill as against a great mountain) (s:mualno) (a:mualpi/mualsang) (q:draft)
mualneute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hills/small hills) (d:<mualneu>, hill, with the plural <te>: the lower hills, often set beside <mualliante>, the great mountains) (a:mualliante/mualsangte) (b:mualneu) (q:draft)
Mualneute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hills/small hills) (d:<mualneute>, the hills, written with a capital at the start of a clause) (a:mualliante) (b:mualneute) (q:draft)
mualno = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hill/small hill) (d:<mual>, hill, with <no>, small: a small hill; {Areopagas mualno} is the hill of the Areopagus in Athens, Mars Hill) (s:mualneu) (a:mualpi) (b:mual) (q:draft)
mualpang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hillside/mountainside/slope/ridge) (d:the side or slope of a hill or mountain, also a ridge of land; {mualpang khatah} is on one side of the mountain) (q:draft)
mualpangah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the hillside/at the hillside) (d:<mualpang> hillside with the place marker <ah>) (b:mualpang) (q:draft)
mualpawn = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bare hill/barren height) (d:<mual>, hill, with <pawn>, bare: a hill or height with no trees on it) (q:draft)
mualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great mountain/mountain) (d:<mual>, mountain, with <pi>, great: a great mountain) (s:mualsang) (a:mualneu/mualno) (b:mual) (q:draft)
mualsang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:high mountain/height/high hill) (d:<mual>, mountain, with <sang>, high: a high mountain or hill, a height) (s:mualpi) (a:mualneu) (q:draft)
mualsangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:high hills/heights/high mountains) (d:plural of <mualsang>: the high hills or heights, often as places where offerings were made) (s:mualliante) (a:mualneute) (b:mualsang) (r:24.17.2) (q:draft)
mualsuang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:memorial stone/pillar/tombstone) (d:a stone set up in memory of someone, as over a grave; <suang> is stone) (q:draft)
mualsuangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:memorial stones/pillars/monuments) (d:plural of <mualsuang>: the monuments of the dead, and the sacred pillars of Egypt) (b:mualsuang) (q:draft)
mualtan = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:viper/poisonous snake) (d:a poisonous snake; in the verses always in the address {mualtan’ suante}, brood of vipers) (r:42.3.7) (q:draft)
mualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mountains/hills) (d:plural of <mual>: mountains or hills) (s:mualtungte) (a:guamte/kuamte) (b:mual) (q:draft)
mualteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the mountains/all the hills) (d:<mual>, hill, with <teng>, all: all the hills, paired with <guamteng>, all the valleys) (b:mual) (q:draft)
Mualteng = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Mualteng)
mualtung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hill/mountain/hill country) (d:the top of a hill or the high land, from <mual>, hill, and <tung>, top; {mualtung gam} is hill country) (s:mual) (a:kuam/zanglei) (r:18.24.8) (q:draft)
Mualtung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Mount/hill country/mountains) (d:<mualtung> written with a capital, in a place name such as {Seir Mualtung}, Mount Seir, or at the start of a sentence) (b:mualtung) (q:draft)
mualtunga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:on the hill/on the hilltop) (d:<mualtung> with the place marker <a>: located on a hill; {mualtunga biaknate} are the high places of worship) (b:mualtung) (q:draft)
mualtungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:on the mountain/in the hill country/to the hills) (d:<mualtung>, hill or mountain, with the place marker <ah>: on or to the mountain, in the hill country) (b:mualtung) (q:draft)
mualtungte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mountains/hills) (d:<mualtung> with the plural <te>: the mountains or hills of a land, as in {Israel mualtungte}, the mountains of Israel) (s:mualte) (b:mualtung) (r:26.35.12) (q:draft)
mualvum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mountain top/summit/peak) (d:the top of a mountain, its summit) (s:mualdawn) (q:draft)
mualzang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plateau/tableland) (d:level high ground, from <mual>, hill, and <zang>, flat: a plateau) (q:draft)
muam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hold in the mouth/keep in the mouth) (d:keep something in the mouth without swallowing it; doubled as {muam muam}, go on holding it there) (q:draft)
muammuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep in the mouth/savour) (d:<muam> hold in the mouth, doubled: go on holding and tasting something) (q:draft, low confidence)
muamua = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in great numbers/in swarms/teeming) (d:follows a verb to picture many people or creatures moving or gathered together) (s:muaimuai/mua-mua) (q:draft)
muan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trust/rely on/put hope in) (d:second stem of <muang>, trust, used before endings such as <nading>; {muan’na} is trust or confidence, and {muan’huai} is trustworthy) (a:muanlah) (r:19.71.5) (q:draft)
