Naham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naham) (d:man of Judah whose sister was the wife of Hodiah) (r:13.4.19)
Naharai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naharai) (d:man of Beeroth, armor-bearer of Joab and one of David’s mighty warriors) (r:13.11.39/10.23.37)
Nahash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahash) (d:king of the Ammonites who besieged Jabesh Gilead and was defeated by Saul; also the name of other men) (r:13.19.1/10.17.27)
Nahath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahath) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Reuel and grandson of Esau, and a Levite descended from Kohath) (r:13.1.37/13.6.26)
Nahbi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahbi) (d:son of Vophsi, the spy sent from the tribe of Naphtali to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.14)
nahoih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good thing/good things) (d:<na>, thing, with <hoih>, good: a good thing or good things, such as food or what God has promised) (b:hoih) (q:draft)
Nahor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahor) (d:name of two men: the son of Serug and grandfather of Abraham, and a brother of Abraham) (r:1.11.22)
nahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stubble/chaff) (d:dry stalks or husks that the wind carries off; {nahpa keu} is dry stubble) (q:draft)
Nahshon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahshon) (d:son of Amminadab, leader of the tribe of Judah in the wilderness and ancestor of David) (r:4.1.7/13.2.11)
nahteh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:leaves/fallen leaves) (d:{nah} and <teh> both mean leaf; {nahteh muat} is rotten leaves, used where the English has scum and refuse) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahthel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dry leaf) (d:a dry or fallen leaf that the wind blows about)
Nahum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahum) (d:prophet from Elkosh whose vision about Nineveh is the book of Nahum; also an ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke) (r:34.1.1/42.3.25)
nai = (i:1) (t:part) (d:particle prefixed to a verb to convey a negative sense, as not yet) (r:43.2.4)
nai = (i:2) (t:n) (w:watch) (d:a watch or clock, the instrument that shows the hour)
naih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:approach/draw near/come near) (d:form of <nai> near used as a verb with an object or before endings such as <ciangin>) (s:neh) (a:kihem) (b:nai) (q:draft)
