nangin = (i:2) (t:conj) (w:in order to/so that) (d:after a verb, for the purpose of; apparently a short form of <nadingin>) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nangma = (i:1) (t:det) (w:your/you) (d:<nangma> written with a capital, for God or at the start of a line; your before a noun, you before <sungah>, <hang> and the like) (b:nangma) (r:19.3.8) (q:draft)
nangmah = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:you/yourself) (d:emphatic form of <nang>: you yourself, you and no other; common in prayer) (s:nang) (b:nang) (r:19.123.1)
nangmah = (i:2) (t:det) (w:your) (d:{nangmah} used before a noun as a possessive, more often written <nangma>) (s:nangma)
Nangmah = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:you/yourself) (d:<nangmah>, emphatic you, written with a capital when God is addressed and at the start of quoted speech) (b:nangmah) (r:24.36.29) (q:draft)
nangmahmah = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:you yourself/yourself) (d:emphatic form of <nangmah>, one person addressed) (s:nangpipi) (b:nangmah) (q:draft)
nangnawn = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:even) (d:placed after the word or phrase it stresses; another spelling of <nangawn>) (s:nangawn) (q:draft)
nangnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to withstand/be willing to resist) (d:<nang>, stand up against, with <nuam> want; said of the spirit that is willing to resist temptation) (q:draft)
nangpipi = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:you yourself) (d:<nang> you with the emphatic <pipi>: one as great as you, you in person) (s:nangmahmah) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangun = (i:1) (t:part) (d:seen once after <theih>, be able, apparently a short form of <nadingun>, in order that, so that) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:withstand/resist/stand against) (d:<nang>, resist, with <zo>, be able: be able to withstand; mostly used with a negative) (s:thuakzo/dozo) (b:nang) (q:draft)
nangzote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who persevere/those who withstand) (d:<nangzo> withstand with the plural <te>: the ones who stand firm under trial) (b:nangzo) (q:draft)
nanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:support/prop) (d:<nan> support with the noun suffix <na>: a part that holds something up, as the supports of a basin stand or the ledges that carry beams) (b:nan) (q:draft)
nanna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:resistance/withstanding) (d:<nan> withstand with the noun suffix <na>: holding out against something, as against a siege) (b:nan) (q:draft, low confidence)
nannan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:manna/coriander) (d:in the Bible text the plant whose small round seed manna is compared to: {nannan tang} is coriander seed)
nannate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:supports/props) (d:plural of <nanna>, a part that holds something up) (b:nanna) (q:draft)
nanzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:withstand/resist/stand against) (d:<nan> withstand with <zawh> be able; the form of <nangzo> used before <ding> and <nading>) (s:thuakzo/dozo) (q:draft)
Naomi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Naomi) (d:wife of Elimelek of Bethlehem and mother-in-law of Ruth) (r:8.1.3/8.1.2)
nap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kiss) (d:touch with the lips as a greeting or a sign of love) (s:tawp) (q:draft)
nap = (i:2) (t:v) (w:smell/sniff) (d:take in a smell through the nose) (s:diik) (q:draft)
nap = (i:3) (t:n) (w:nasal mucus/snot) (d:in {nap nit}, blow the nose at, a gesture of contempt; rendered sniff at in English) (s:naptui) (q:draft, low confidence)
napa = (t:see) <pian'napa>
napi = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:though/although/yet/but) (d:placed after a verb, often as <napi-in>: even though this is so) (s:hinapi) (q:draft)
napia = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:you give) (d:<na>, you, and <pia>, give, written as one word; {napia kei ding} is you shall not give) (b:pia) (q:draft)
napna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kiss) (d:<nap>, kiss, with the noun suffix <na>: a kiss, especially one given as a greeting) (s:kinapna) (b:nap) (q:draft)
nappa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one kissed) (d:<nap> kiss with <pa>, the man: {ka nappa} is the man I kiss) (b:nap) (r:41.14.44) (q:draft)
Naptali = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naphtali) (d:son of Jacob and Bilhah, ancestor of the tribe of Naphtali) (r:1.46.24)
naptui = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nasal mucus) (d:used in the pair <khitui naptui>, tears and running nose, for bitter weeping) (s:nap) (q:draft)
nard = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:nard/spikenard) (d:a fragrant plant and the costly perfume made from it, a loanword) (s:mard) (q:draft)
Nariah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Neriah) (d:father of Baruch, the scribe of Jeremiah, and son of Mahseiah) (r:24.32.12)
Narkissas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Narcissus) (d:man in Rome whose household Paul greets) (r:45.16.11)
Narsissas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Narcissus) (d:man in Rome whose household Paul greets; another spelling of <Narkissas>) (r:45.16.11)
nasa = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the endings <na> and <sa> together on a verb, written after an apostrophe or hyphen, marking the place where something was or was done before; {teen’nasa mun}, the place once lived in) (q:draft)
nasaepna = (t:see) <nasaepna-a>
nasaepna-a = (i:1) (t:n) (w:service/work) (d:seen once, in the service of the tabernacle; apparently <nasepna>, work or service, with the ending <a>, in, and ae probably a misprint for e) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:afflict/hurt/cause pain) (d:<na>, be painful or ill, with the causative {-sak}: make a part of the body hurt or sick) (q:draft)
nasak = (i:2) (t:phrase) (d:{na sak} written as one word, you consider or you feel; {hoih nasak leh} means if it seems good to you) (q:draft)
nasakna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (d:{na sak}, you consider, with the noun ending <na>; {hoih nasakna mun} is the place that seems good to you) (b:nasak) (q:draft)
nasate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:former ways/things done before) (d:the endings <na> and <sa> with the plural <te> after a verb: the things formerly done; {gamtat nasate}, the ways walked before) (b:nasa) (q:draft, low confidence)
naseemte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:servants) (d:<nasem>, servant, with the plural <te>, here spelled with ee; the same verse also has <nasemte>) (s:nasemte) (q:draft)
nasem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:servant/worker) (d:one who works for or serves another, from <na>, work, and <sem>, do; also a hired worker) (s:nasempa/sila) (a:topa) (b:sem) (q:draft)
Nasem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:servant) (d:<nasem> written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and once of Jesus as the Servant of God) (b:nasem) (q:draft)
