neupen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:smallest/least/youngest) (d:<neu>, small, with <pen>, most: the smallest of all, the least in rank, or the youngest) (s:neubel/ngekpen) (a:lianpen/golpen) (b:neu) (q:draft)
neupente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the smallest/the least/the lowliest) (d:<neupen>, smallest, with the plural <te>: those who are smallest or lowest of all, whether people or things) (a:lianpente) (b:neupen) (q:draft)
neusak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make small/humble/bring low) (d:<neu>, small, with the causative <sak>: make small in number, or bring low in standing) (s:neubawl/niamsak/niamkhiat) (a:liansak/liatsak) (b:neu) (q:draft)
neuseekin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making smaller) (d:reducing the size of something, here a measure for grain, with the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
neuta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become small/be brought low) (d:<neu>, small, with <ta>, marking a change of state: become small, be brought low from a high standing) (s:kiniam) (a:liat) (b:neu) (q:draft)
neute = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:small/little) (d:<neu>, small, with the plural <te>, said of several things: {khua neute} are villages, {ta neute} little children, {thu neute} small matters) (a:liante) (b:neu) (r:62.5.21) (q:draft)
