ng = (t:see) <na'ng>
nga = (i:1) (t:num) (w:five) (d:the number five; it follows the thing that is counted, as in {tul nga}, five thousand) (r:26.41.9)
nga = (i:3) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bird) (s:va/vasa) usually found in lyric
ngaam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grow weak/waste away) (d:lose strength and waste away; in the verse it is said of the bones of a suffering person) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngabeng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fisherman) (d:a person who catches fish: <nga>, fish, with <beng>, hunt; compare <sabeng>, hunter) (q:draft)
ngabengte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fishermen/fishers) (d:<ngabeng>, fisherman, with the plural <te>) (s:bengte) (b:ngabeng) (r:40.4.18) (q:draft)
ngah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive/get/obtain) (d:come to have something that is given or gained, such as a blessing, an inheritance, wages or favour) (a:pia)
ngahbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive as well/gain in addition) (d:<ngah> receive with <beh> in addition) (s:ngahthuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahbuang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get at least) (d:<ngah> get with the limiting particle <buang>, get at least or after all) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive/get/obtain/find) (d:<ngah>, receive or get, with the linking ending <in>: used when another verb follows, receiving something and then doing something else) (b:ngah) (r:54.2.4) (q:draft)
ngahkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to get/incur) (d:<ngah>, get, with <khak>, by chance: come to get something unwanted; with {loh nading}, so as not to incur) (s:ngahlawh/tuaklawh/thuaklawh) (q:draft)
ngahkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive together/share in/receive along with) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <khawm>, together: receive along with others, share in what they receive) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have received/have already received) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <khin>, already done) (s:ngahkhit/sankhit) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have received) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <khit>, finish: have received; {ngahkhit ciangin} is after receiving) (s:ngahkhin/sankhit) (q:draft)
ngahkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive together/share in) (d:form of <ngahkhawm>, receive together with others) (q:draft)
ngahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:regain/recover/get back/receive back) (d:<ngah>, get, with <kik>, again: get back what was lost, taken away or given up) (s:neikik/lakik) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:getting back/recovering/receiving back) (d:<ngahkik> get back, with the linking ending <in>) (b:ngahkik) (q:draft)
ngahkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:regaining/recovery) (d:<ngahkik> get back, with the noun suffix <na>; {a ngahkikna dingin} is in order to regain) (b:ngahkik) (q:draft)
ngahkim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:all receive/receive in full) (d:<ngah> receive with <kim> complete, every one receives) (q:draft)
ngahlah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fail to obtain/fall short of) (d:<ngah> get with <lah> fail to) (q:draft)
ngahlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive besides/still receive) (d:<ngah> receive with <lai> still, further) (q:draft)
ngahlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:incur/get as a result/bring upon oneself) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <lawh>: receive trouble or harm as a consequence) (s:ngahkhak/thuaklawh/tuaklawh) (q:draft)
ngahmun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ford/crossing) (d:a shallow place where a river is crossed on foot, as on the Jordan, the Jabbok and the Arnon) (q:draft)
ngahmunah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the ford/at the crossing) (d:<ngahmun> ford with the place marker <ah>) (b:ngahmun) (q:draft)
ngahmunte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fords/crossings) (d:<ngahmun>, ford, with the plural <te>; with <ah> it means at the fords) (b:ngahmun) (q:draft)
ngahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gain/getting/obtaining) (d:<ngah>, get, with the noun suffix <na>: the getting of something or the means of getting it; {thuman lo-a ngahna} is ill-gotten gain and {pahtak ngahna} is a way to honour) (s:meetna) (a:taanna/supna) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to get/wish to receive) (d:<ngah>, get, with <nop>, want; found before <man>, because, as in {sum ngahnop manin}, because of wanting money) (q:draft)
ngahnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desire to get/greed for) (d:<ngahnop> want to get with the noun suffix <na>; {sum ngahnopna}, desire for money) (b:ngahnop) (q:draft)
ngahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:receiver/finder/one who gets) (d:<ngah>, get, with <pa>, the man: the man who receives, gets or finds something; {cidamna a ngahpa} is the man who was healed) (s:sangpa) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get soon/quickly receive) (d:<ngah> get with <pak> quickly) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:received/obtained/acquired) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <sa>, already done: what has been received or gained; it stands before a noun, or alone after a possessor) (s:sansa) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to receive/bring/grant/give) (d:<ngah>, receive, with the causative <sak>: make someone get or have something, whether good or bad) (s:neihsak/pia) (b:ngah) (r:5.8.17) (q:draft)
ngahsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:causing to receive/inflicting) (d:<ngahsak> cause to receive with the linking suffix <in>; {gim ngahsakin}, making someone suffer) (b:ngahsak) (q:draft)
ngahsakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to give/enable to receive) (d:<ngahsak> cause to receive with <thei> be able) (b:ngahsak) (q:draft)
ngahsakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:manage to get for) (d:<ngahsak> cause to receive with <zo> be able, succeed in getting something for someone) (b:ngahsak) (q:draft)
ngahsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive in turn/receive a share from) (d:<ngah> receive with <sawn> onward, receive out of what another has received) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahsunte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those gained/converts) (d:the ones who have been won, from <ngah> get, with plural <te>) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:received) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <ta>, marking that the action has now taken place)
ngahtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get by oneself) (d:<ngah> get with <tawm> by oneself, without the help of another) (q:draft)
ngahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who receive/recipients) (d:<ngah>, receive, with the plural <te>: the people who receive or have something; {gupna ngahte} are those who are saved) (s:sangte) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:things received/gains) (d:<ngah>, receive, with the plural <te>: the things that have been received or taken, as in {na ngahte uh}, what you receive) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to receive/can get) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <thei>, can: be able to receive or get) (s:ngahzo/sangthei) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
ngahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to receive/can obtain/may get) (d:form of <ngahthei>, be able to receive, used before <nading>: so that one may receive) (s:ngahzawh) (b:ngah) (r:56.2.11) (q:draft)
ngahtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:obtaining/means of getting) (d:<ngahtheih> be able to get, with the noun suffix <na>; {sum ngahtheihna ding} is in order to get money) (s:ngahna) (b:ngahtheih) (q:draft)
ngahthuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gain in addition/gain more) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <thuah>, in addition) (s:ngahbeh) (q:draft)
ngahthuap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive regularly/receive as allowance) (d:receive a portion again and again; <ngahthuapna> is an allowance) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahthuapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:allowance/provision) (d:what a person is regularly given to live on) (b:ngahthuap) (q:draft)
ngahtoto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep gaining/receive more and more) (d:<ngah> receive with <toto>, going on and increasing) (q:draft)
ngahzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:portion/share) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <zah>, amount: the amount a person receives, a share or portion, also pay) (s:tanh/seh) (q:draft)
ngahzahzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whatever one gets/as much as one gets) (d:<ngah> get with <zahzah> as much as) (q:draft)
ngahzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:receive/receive more/get more) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <zaw>, more: receive or get more than others; the others are followed by <sangin>, than) (b:ngah)
ngahzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:win/gain/obtain/manage to get) (d:<ngah>, get, with <zawh>, form of <zo>, be able: succeed in getting; this form is used before <nading> and {nak-uhleh}) (s:ngahtheih) (q:draft)
ngahzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to get/obtain/attain) (d:<ngah>, get, with <zo>, be able or succeed: manage to get, obtain) (s:ngahthei) (b:ngah) (q:draft)
Ngai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:listen/hear/pay attention) (d:<ngai> written with a capital at the start of a call) (s:don/ngaihsak) (b:ngai) (q:draft)
ngaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:listen/hear/heed) (d:form of <ngai> used before words such as <lai>, <ding> and <loh>) (b:ngai) (q:draft)
ngaih = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:lovely/charming/beloved) (d:{ngaih baang} means lovely or attractive, and {lawm ngaih} is a beloved) (s:ngaihhuai/etlawm) (a:melsia) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihbaan = (t:see) <ngaihbaan'na>
ngaihbaan'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:loveliness/charm) (d:{ngaih baang} lovely with the noun suffix <na>; the English versions have breasts here) (s:ngaihbaanna/ngaihban'na) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihbaang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:beautiful/handsome/lovely/attractive) (d:pleasing to look at, said of women and of men) (s:melhoih/etlawm/ngaihhuai) (a:melsia) (q:draft)
ngaihbaangin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:lovely/handsome/attractive) (d:<ngaihbaang>, pleasing to look at, with <in>, linking to what follows) (s:melhoihin) (b:ngaihbaang) (q:draft)
ngaihbaanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:charm/loveliness/attractiveness) (d:<ngaihbaang> lovely, attractive, with the noun suffix <na>: the charm of a woman) (s:ngaihban'na/ngaihbaan'na/melhoihna) (r:20.31.30) (q:draft)
ngaihban = (t:see) <ngaihban'na>
ngaihban'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:charm/attractiveness/loveliness) (d:<ngaihbaang>, lovely, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:ngaihbaanna/ngaihbaan'na/melhoihna) (q:draft)
ngaihbangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as one beloved/as a lovely one) (d:probably <ngaih> lovely or beloved with <bangin> as, like) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:lovely/charming/desirable/handsome) (d:<ngaih>, love or long for, with <huai>, deserving of: lovely, pleasing to look at, said of men and women) (s:ngaihbaang/etlawm/melhoih) (a:melsia) (q:draft)
ngaihhuai = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:worth listening to/worth heeding) (d:<ngaih>, listen, with <huai>, deserving of: worth listening to; with <zaw> it means more worth heeding) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:heeding/listening to) (d:<ngaih> with <in>; {ngaihin nei} is give heed to, hold dear) (b:ngaih) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:love/adore) (d:be fond of, long for; with <tuahpha>, it is right to love) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihlua = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very loud/too loud) (d:of a sound, loud, with <lua> very or too much) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihmuang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:secure/at ease/carefree) (d:without fear or worry; {ngaihmuang takin} is securely, in peace) (s:lungmuang) (a:patau) (q:draft)
ngaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:longing/affection) (d:<ngaih>, long for, with the noun suffix <na>: the missing of a person who is dear, longing) (s:lunggulhna) (b:ngaih) (q:draft)
ngaihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:listening/heeding/obedience) (d:<ngaih>, listen, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of listening to what is said; {thu ngaihna} is obedience) (s:thungaihna) (b:ngaih) (q:draft)
ngaihngaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep listening/listen again and again) (d:<ngaih>, listen, doubled for a continued action) (s:ngaingai) (q:draft)
ngaihno = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beloved/darling/sweetheart) (d:<ngaih>, long for, with the endearing <no>: the one a person loves, said by lovers of each other) (s:itluat/lungtup) (b:ngaih) (r:22.2.13) (q:draft)
Ngaihno = (i:1) (t:n) (w:beloved/darling) (d:<ngaihno> written with a capital at the start of a line, used to address a lover: {Ngaihno aw}, my beloved) (s:itluat/lungtup) (b:ngaihno) (q:draft)
ngaihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to listen/be willing to hear) (d:<ngaih>, listen, with <nop>, want; {mi’ ngaihnop dingin pau} is speak so that people like to listen, and {ngaihnop-huai} is pleasant to listen to) (s:ngainuam) (q:draft)
ngaihpente = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:loveliest/most beloved) (d:<ngaih>, dear or lovely, with <pen>, most, and plural <te>: the loveliest; {la ngaihpente} is the loveliest of songs, the Song of Songs) (q:draft)
ngaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:listen attentively/listen to/pay attention to) (d:<ngaih>, a form of <ngai>, listen, with <sak>: listen carefully to what someone says) (b:ngaih) (q:draft)
ngaihsuna = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thinking of/considering) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with the linking <a>: while thinking about something, or with someone in mind) (b:ngaihsun) (q:draft)
ngaihsunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:thinking/considering/meaning/having in mind) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with the linking suffix <in>: having something in mind while doing the next action, or meaning something by what is said) (b:ngaihsun) (q:draft)
ngaihsunkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:think at the same time/hope meanwhile) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with <kawm>, while: think or hope something at the same time as doing something else) (q:draft)
ngaihsunkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suppose/imagine/think) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with <kha>: come to think that something is so, often of a mistaken idea; {ngaihsunkha kei un} is do not suppose) (s:upmawh) (q:draft)
ngaihsunkhial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:think wrongly/be mistaken/be in error) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with <khial>, wrongly: have a mistaken idea) (q:draft)
ngaihsunsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let think/make think) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with the causative <sak>: let or make someone think; {bangmah ngaihsunsak thei lo} is leave one unable to perceive anything) (b:ngaihsun) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihsunsun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/keep thinking about) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with the last part doubled for thinking again and again: meditate on, ponder) (s:lungngaingai/lungngaihngaih) (q:draft)
ngaihsunsunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pondering/thinking over and over) (d:<ngaihsunsun>, keep thinking about, with <in>, linking to the next verb) (b:ngaihsunsun) (q:draft)
ngaihsunte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who think/those who plan/those who consider) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, with plural <te>: the people who think, plan or consider something; {thusia ngaihsunte} are those who plot evil) (b:ngaihsun) (q:draft)
ngaihsut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:think/consider/think about) (d:form of <ngaihsun>, think, used before <ciangin>, <ding>, <na>, <theihna> and in dependent clauses) (r:26.38.10) (q:draft)
ngaihsutin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:think about/consider/take to heart/pay attention to) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with the linking ending <in>; {ngaihsutin nei} is set the mind on something, take it to heart) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft)
ngaihsutkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:regard/think of/happen to think) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <kha>, happen to: come to regard something in a certain way; {neu ngaihsutkha} is think little of, show contempt for) (q:draft)
ngaihsutkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:think/suppose/have in mind) (d:form of <ngaihsutkha>, happen to think, come to think, used in dependent clauses) (b:ngaihsutkha) (q:draft)
ngaihsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:idea/thought) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with the noun suffix <na>: what a person thinks, a thought or idea) (s:thungaihsutna) (b:ngaihsut)
ngaihsutna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:plan/purpose/counsel) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with the noun suffix <na>: what has been thought out, a plan or purpose; also the advice that one gives) (s:geelna/ngimna/vaihawmna) (b:ngaihsut)
ngaihsutnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thoughts/plans) (d:plural of <ngaihsutna>: thoughts or plans, of God or of people) (s:geelnate/ngimnate) (b:ngaihsutna) (q:draft)
ngaihsutpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:goal/chief concern/main aim) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <pi>, great or main: the main thought or aim; {ngaihsutpi-in nei} is set the heart on something, make it the chief concern) (s:tupna) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft)
ngaihsutsa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plan/purpose/decision) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <sa>, already done: what has already been thought out or decided, a plan or decision) (b:ngaihsut) (r:27.2.8) (q:draft)
ngaihsutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consider on behalf of/regard as) (d:<ngaihsut>, consider, with <sak>: think of something on behalf of another, or regard something in a certain way) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft)
ngaihsutsiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:discerning/thoughtful/capable) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <siam>, skilled: good at thinking, discerning; {thu ngaihsutsiam mi} is a capable, sensible man) (q:draft)
ngaihsuttawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:self-devised/made up/of his own invention) (d:<ngaihsut> think, with <tawm>, by oneself: thought up on his own; {ngaihsuttawm thu} is what someone says on his own authority, not what he was given to say) (q:draft)
ngaihsutte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who regard/those who consider) (d:those who think of or regard something in a certain way; {a thupi ngaihsutte}, those who regard something as important) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft)
ngaihsutte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:thoughts/what people think) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with plural <te>: the things that people think, plan or take to be so) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft)
ngaihsutzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consider more/regard more highly) (d:<ngaihsut>, consider, with <zaw>, more; {thupi ngaihsutzaw} is consider more important, value above another) (b:ngaihsut) (q:draft)
ngaihsutzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fathom/comprehend) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <zawh>, form of <zo>, be able: be able to think through; with {ding hi lo}, beyond understanding) (q:draft)
ngaihsutzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of thinking/philosophy) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <zia>, manner) (q:draft)
ngaihtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:loudly/aloud) (d:<ngaih>, loud, with <takin>, which makes an adverb: loudly; said of singing or shouting for joy) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lovers/beloved ones) (d:<ngaih>, dear or beloved, with plural <te>; used after <lawm>, friend, as {lawm ngaihte}: lovers, and as a figure for allies) (b:ngaih) (q:draft)
ngaihzawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:listen rather/heed) (d:<ngaih>, listen, with <zawk>, rather or more: listen to or heed instead; said of what should have been heeded) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:listen again/hear again) (d:<ngai>, listen, with <kik>, again) (s:zakik) (b:ngai) (q:draft)
ngailai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep listening/bear with longer) (d:<ngai>, listen, with <lai>, still: go on listening, bear with someone a little longer) (q:draft)
ngailua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:love too much/be obsessed with) (d:<ngai>, long for or love, with <lua>, too much: be so in love as to be obsessed) (q:draft)
ngaingai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep listening/listen on) (d:<ngai>, listen, said twice for continued action: keep on listening) (s:ngaihngaih) (q:draft)
ngainuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to listen/be willing to listen) (d:<ngai>, listen, with <nuam>, want) (q:draft)
ngaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make obey/make listen) (d:<ngai>, listen or heed, with the causative <sak>: make someone or something obey) (s:thumangsak) (b:ngai) (q:draft)
ngaisim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:listen secretly/overhear) (d:<ngai>, listen, with <sim>, secretly: listen in on what others are saying) (s:zasim) (q:draft)
ngaisun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:think/consider) (d:another spelling of <ngaihsun>, think; {bangci na ngaisun hiam} is what do you think) (s:ngaihsun) (q:draft)
ngaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who listen/those who heed/those who welcome) (d:<ngai>, listen or heed, with plural <te>: the ones who listen to someone; also of those who welcome a person) (b:ngai) (q:draft)
ngaizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey/heed) (d:<ngai>, listen, with <zo>, carry through: do what one was told; {thu ngaizo} is obey a word) (s:mangzo) (b:ngai) (q:draft)
ngakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:waiting/waiting for) (d:<ngak>, wait, with the linking suffix <in>: waiting, while waiting; often followed by <om>, be) (b:ngak) (q:draft)
ngakkawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:while waiting) (d:<ngak>, wait, with <kawm>, while, and the linking suffix <in>: while waiting for something) (q:draft)
ngakkawmun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:while waiting) (d:<ngak>, wait, with <kawm>, while, and <un>, the linking suffix for more than one person: while you wait) (q:draft)
ngakkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep watch with/wait together) (d:<ngak>, wait or watch, with <khawm>, together) (b:ngak) (r:40.26.40) (q:draft)
ngakkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have laid on) (d:<ngak>, lay or rest upon, with <khit>, finish: have laid on, said of laying hands on someone; {ngakkhit ciangin} is after laying on) (q:draft)
ngaklah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:long for/wait eagerly/be eager) (d:wait for or want something with impatience, be eager for it; {an ngaklah} is be greedy for food) (s:lunggulh) (q:draft)
ngaklahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:longing/yearning) (d:<ngaklah>, long for, with the linking suffix <in>: longing, while longing) (b:ngaklah) (q:draft)
ngaklai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still wait/wait longer/go on waiting) (d:<ngak> wait, with <lai> still, any longer) (q:draft)
ngakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stand/rest/base) (d:<ngak>, rest or lay upon, with the noun suffix <na>: the thing on which something rests, as the stand of a basin; {khe ngakna} is a footstool) (s:kingakna) (r:2.31.9) (q:draft)
ngaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stands/rests/supports) (d:plural of <ngakna>: things on which something rests; {ban ngaknate} are armrests, and the {ngaknate} of a basin are its stand) (s:kingaknate) (b:ngakna) (q:draft)
ngaknate = (i:2) (t:n) (w:waiting/perseverance) (d:plural of <ngakna> in the sense of waiting: the times one waits patiently, perseverance) (b:ngakna) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngakngak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep waiting for/wait and wait) (d:<ngak>, wait, doubled to show that the waiting goes on) (q:draft)
ngakngakna = (t:see) <ngakngakna-in>
ngakngakna-in = (i:1) (t:n) (w:long waiting/longing) (d:<ngak> wait, said twice for continued action, with the noun suffix <na> and <in> marking the cause: because of waiting and waiting) (q:draft)
ngaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lay on/place on) (d:<ngak>, rest upon, with the causative <sak>: lay or place on; {khut ngaksak} is lay a hand on a person) (s:ngasak) (q:draft)
ngaksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:laying on/casting upon) (d:<ngaksak>, lay on, with the linking suffix <in>; {lupna ngaksakin} is laying someone on a bed) (b:ngaksak) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those laid upon) (d:those on whom something has been laid, here the hands, from <ngak> lay upon, <sa> already and plural <te>) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who wait/those who hope) (d:<ngak>, wait, with plural <te>: people who wait for someone or put their hope in him) (s:lamente) (b:ngak) (q:draft)
ngakzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wait rather/wait instead) (d:<ngak>, wait, with <zaw>, rather: wait instead of doing something else) (b:ngak) (q:draft)
ngakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to wait/manage to wait/wait through) (d:<ngak> wait, keep watch, with <zo>, be able, manage to) (b:ngak) (q:draft)
ngal = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild boar/boar) (d:a wild pig that lives in the forest) (q:draft)
ngal = (i:2) (t:part) (d:placed after <kei>, not, and before <leh>, if, to stress the condition: {kei ngal leh} is unless, if indeed not) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ngal = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild boar/boar) (d:a wild pig that lives in the forest; the same word as <ngal>, written with a capital in one text) (b:ngal) (q:draft)
ngaltak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:jointed leg/hind leg) (d:the jointed upper leg above the foot that an insect such as a locust uses for hopping) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaltuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:greaves) (d:armour worn on the lower legs, in the verse made of bronze) (q:draft)
Ngalvangte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:hyraxes/conies) (d:plural with <te>: small animals of little strength that make their home among the rocks) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dare) (d:have the courage to do something; placed after the main verb, and very often used with <kei> or <lo>, not dare) (s:ngap) (a:ngamlah) (q:draft)
ngamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:daring/risking) (d:<ngam>, dare, with the linking suffix <in>; follows the verb that names what is dared, as in {nuntakna pia ngamin}, risking life) (b:ngam) (q:draft)
