ngamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boldness/daring/courage) (d:<ngam>, dare, with the noun suffix <na>: being bold enough to do something; placed after the verb, as in {gen ngamna}, daring to speak) (s:hanna) (a:launa) (b:ngam) (q:draft)
ngamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:acts of daring/boldness) (d:<ngamna>, daring, with plural <te>; {mawh gamtat ngamnate} is their daring to act sinfully) (b:ngamna) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who dares) (d:<ngam>, dare, with <pa>, the male one: the one who dares to do something) (b:ngam) (q:draft)
ngamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who dare/those who risk) (d:<ngam>, dare, with plural <te>: the ones who dared to do something; {ngawng a dawh ngamte} are those who risked their necks) (b:ngam) (q:draft)
ngamzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:would rather dare/be more willing) (d:<ngam>, dare, with <zaw>, more or rather; {sum ngamzaw} is be willing rather to lose) (b:ngam) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngana = (i:1) (t:num) (w:fifth) (d:<nga>, five, with <na>, which makes an ordinal number: fifth; {sawm-le-ngana} is fifteenth) (b:nga)
nganeu = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:small fish) (d:<nga>, fish, with <neu>, small) (q:draft)
ngangngang = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:throbbing) (d:placed after a verb of pain, describing a continual throbbing ache; {tum ngangngang} is ache without stopping) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dare/be up to/venture) (d:have the courage or the strength to do something; {na ngap nak leh} is if you dare, {ka ngap kei} is I am not up to it) (s:ngam) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngap = (i:2) (t:v) (w:ford/wade across/cross) (d:cross water on foot, as at a ford; {ka ngap zo kei hi}, I could not get across) (s:ngaptan) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngapi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:great fish/huge fish/whale) (d:<nga>, fish, with <pi>, big: the great fish that swallowed Jonah) (b:nga) (q:draft)
ngaptan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wade through/ford/cross on foot) (d:<ngap> ford, with <tan>, cut across: go through water on foot; with <sak>, lead someone through) (s:ngap) (q:draft)
ngaptansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead through water/make wade through) (d:<ngaptan> wade through, with <sak>, cause to: take someone across water on foot) (b:ngaptan) (q:draft)
ngapzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to wade across/be able to ford) (d:<ngap>, wade across, with <zo>, be able) (b:ngap) (q:draft)
