ngasiahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fishing/angling) (d:catching fish with a hook; {ngasiahna sikkawi} is a fish hook) (q:draft)
ngasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lower/let down/set down) (d:put a carried thing down, with <suk>, downward: lower a jar or a sack to the ground) (s:koihsuk) (q:draft)
ngat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn toward/incline/face) (d:turn a part of the body toward something; {bil ngat} is incline the ear, pay attention, {mai ngat} is set the face toward, and {nung ngat} is turn the back on) (s:maingat) (a:thuang) (r:14.6.40) (q:draft)
ngate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fish) (b:nga) plural form of <nga>
