phatlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil/what is not good) (d:apparently <pha> good with <loh> not and the noun suffix <na>; here of evil done with the tongue) (s:hoihlohna/gilohna) (a:phatna/gitna) (q:draft, low confidence)
phatmawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:what is necessary/necessity) (d:apparently <phamawh> necessary with the noun suffix <na>; {phatmawhna khempeuh}, everything that has to be done) (q:draft, low confidence)
phatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:praise) (d:<phat>, praise, with the noun suffix <na>: words or song that praise; <phatna la> is a song of praise) (s:minphatna/pahtakna) (a:gensiatna) (b:phat) (q:draft)
phatna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:goodness/good) (d:noun of <pha>, good: what is good, doing good; {phatna bawl} is do good and {phatna thaman} the reward of doing good) (s:gitna/migitna) (a:siatna/phatlohna) (q:draft, low confidence)
Phatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:praise) (d:<phatna> written with a capital: at the start of a sentence, and as the name given to the gates of the city) (b:phatna) (q:draft)
phatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:praises) (d:<phatna>, praise, with the plural <te>: praises, mostly sung) (b:phatna) (r:19.9.14) (q:draft)
