phatphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep praising/praise again and again) (d:<phat>, praise, doubled to show that the praising goes on) (r:19.145.1) (q:draft)
phatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let praise/cause to praise) (d:<phat> praise with <sak>, cause or let: used in wishes, let them praise) (b:phat) (q:draft)
phattaak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:praiseworthy/worthy of praise) (d:<phat> praise, with <taak>, worthy of) (s:phathuai/minphathuai/pahtakhuai) (q:draft)
phattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to praise/may glorify) (d:<phat> praise with <theih>, form of <thei> can, used before <nading>) (b:phat) (q:draft)
phattheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:praise/being able to praise) (d:<phattheih>, be able to praise, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:phatna) (b:phattheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
phattuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:benefit/profit/be edified) (d:gain good from something; mostly in <phattuam nading>, for the good or welfare of) (s:phatuam/hamphat) (r:50.2.20) (q:draft)
