phukha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:press against/crowd/jostle/strike against/run into) (d:push or knock up against someone or something, as a crowd presses on a person or a ship strikes a sandbar; also meet with danger or hardship) (q:draft)
phukham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burst/break open/break through) (d:break something by force or pressure, as a door, a wineskin or an enemy line; of a rash, break out on the skin) (q:draft)
phukhamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break out/burst) (d:<phukham> break out, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb; of a disease breaking out over the skin) (b:phukham) (q:draft)
phukhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break out/break through/erupt) (d:<phu>, push against, with <khia>, out: force a way out or through; of a skin disease, break out on the skin) (b:phu) (q:draft)
phukhong = (i:1) (t:n) (d:found with <vei>, suffer from, in {phukhong vei}, be famished, faint with hunger and tiredness) (q:draft, low confidence)
phukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cutting down/felling) (d:<phuk> with the linking suffix {-in}; the action is followed by another verb) (b:phuk) (q:draft)
phukmai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut down/chop down) (d:<phuk> cut down, with <mai>, apparently clear away; of felling a forest) (q:draft, low confidence)
phukmaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut down/chop down) (d:<phukmai> cut down and clear, with <sak>; of felling the trees of another) (b:phukmai) (q:draft, low confidence)
phukmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut down/fell/clear away) (d:<phuk> cut down with <mang>, away or gone: cut trees down and clear them away) (q:draft)
phukpai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut down/hew down/fell) (d:<phuk> fell with <pai> away, said of idols and sacred poles) (q:draft)
phuksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut down/fell) (d:<phuk> cut down, with <sak>: cut down trees or timber, or have them cut down) (b:phuk) (q:draft)
phuksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cutting down/felling) (d:<phuksak>, cut down, with the linking ending <in>) (b:phuksak) (q:draft)
phuktan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut down/fell) (d:<phuk> cut down with <tan> cut off: cut a tree right down) (s:sattan) (q:draft)
phukte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cutters/woodcutters/fellers) (d:<phuk> cut down with the plural <te>: those who cut down; {sing a phukte}, those who fell timber) (s:singsuite) (b:phuk) (q:draft)
phul = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gush out/pour out/flow out/spring up) (d:of water, come out from a spring, well or rock; {phul khia}, gush out) (s:luangkhia) (q:draft)
Phul = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spring up/gush out) (d:of water, come up from a well or spring) (b:phul) (q:draft)
phula = (i:1) (t:v) (w:avenge/take vengeance/take revenge) (d:<phu> vengeance with <la> take, written here as one word) (s:thuhkik/thukkik) (a:maisak) (q:draft)
phulak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:avenge/take vengeance) (d:pay back a wrong done; {phulak ni} is the day of vengeance) (s:thuhkik/thukkik) (a:maisak) (b:phula) (q:draft)
phulakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vengeance/revenge) (d:the act of taking revenge or avenging) (s:thukkikna/thuhkikna) (a:maisakna) (b:phulak) (q:draft)
phulapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:avenger/avenger of blood) (d:the man who takes revenge, in the law the relative who avenges a killing; {-pa} marks a man) (s:thukpa) (q:draft)
phulet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break through/breach) (d:break right through a wall or barrier) (q:draft)
phulin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break through/burst through) (d:<phul> break or burst through, with the linking ending <in>) (b:phul) (r:13.11.18) (q:draft)
phulkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break out against/burst upon) (d:break through and overwhelm, as a flood breaks out) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulkhap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break out/burst through) (d:said of flood water that bursts through what holds it back) (r:13.14.11) (q:draft)
phulkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gush out/burst forth/spring out) (d:of water, come out with force from rock or ground) (s:luangkhia) (b:phul) (q:draft)
phulkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make gush out/bring forth) (d:<phulkhia> burst out, with the causative <sak>: make water or springs burst out) (s:phulsak) (b:phulkhia) (q:draft)
phulsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make gush out/open up/bring forth) (d:<phul> burst out, with the causative <sak>: make water or a spring break out) (s:phulkhiasak) (a:kangsak) (b:phul) (q:draft)
phum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bury/hide in the ground) (d:put a dead person or a thing under the ground; {sum phum} is buried treasure) (s:vui) (a:tokhia) (q:draft)
phum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:baptize/immerse) (d:with <tui>, water: dip in water, baptize) (s:tuiphum/baptaiz) (q:draft)
phumcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bury/submerge/swallow up) (d:put completely under earth or water; <phum> with <cip>, tightly, completely) (s:vukcip) (b:phum) (q:draft)
phumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:baptize/immerse) (d:<phum> baptize, with the linking ending <in>; {tui phumin}, baptizing in water) (b:phum) (q:draft)
phumin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:bury/bow down) (d:<phum> bury, with the linking ending <in>; {ka lu phumin}, with my head buried in my bosom, of a person bowed in prayer) (b:phum) (q:draft, low confidence)
phumlam = (i:1) (t:n) (d:the burying or the way of burying; <phum> bury, with <lam>, the manner or fact of doing) (q:draft, low confidence)
phumte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:buried things/buried ones) (d:<phum> bury with the plural <te>: the things that have been buried; {ka suang phumte}, the stones I have buried) (b:phum) (q:draft)
phumtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can immerse/can baptize) (d:<phum> immerse, with <theih> can, the form used before <nading>; {tui phum} is baptize) (b:phum) (q:draft)
phun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grumble/murmur/complain) (d:speak out one’s discontent, grumble or complain; with <tungah>, against someone) (a:lungkim) (q:draft)
phung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wall/earthwork/ramp) (d:a wall or bank of earth or stone, as around a field or raised against a city) (s:kulh) (q:draft)
phungah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:at the foot of/at the base of/at the root of) (d:<phung> with the place marker <ah>; {khe phungah}, at the feet of) (b:phung) (q:draft)
phungah = (i:2) (t:prep) (w:around/beside) (d:of people sitting by a pot to eat or drink: {sabeel phungah}, around the pot of meat; {zu phungah}, at the wine) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungcian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build up a wall/wall up) (d:<phung> wall with <cian> pile up: build a wall of piled stones; {a phungcian suangte}, the stones of its built wall) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ramp/earthwork/siege ramp) (d:<phung> earthwork with the ending <in>, as: {phungin ciang}, pile up as a ramp against a city) (b:phung) (q:draft)
phungmai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wall/rampart) (d:the wall or rampart of a city or building; hyssop is said to grow on it) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seat of honour) (d:<phung> with <pi> great; in {pahtawi ngahna phungpi}, where the English has a seat of honour for the house of his father; the exact sense of {phungpi} itself is not clear from the verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungsung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stock/stump/family line) (d:<phung> clan or lineage with <sung> inside; the single verse has it for the stump of Jesse) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ramps/earthworks/siege mounds) (d:<phung> wall or bank of earth, with the plural <te>) (b:phung) (q:draft)
phungte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:relatives/kindred/clan) (d:<phung> clan or family line, with the plural <te>; {na beh na phungte} is your own people) (s:behte/tanaute) (b:phung) (q:draft)
phunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grumbling/complaining/murmuring) (d:<phun>, grumble, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:phun) (q:draft)
phunkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grumble/complain/criticize) (d:<phun> grumble, with <khak> happen to, the form used before <loh>: so that no one may come to complain) (q:draft)
phunna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:<phun>, grumble, with the noun suffix <na>: grumbling or a complaint) (b:phun) (q:draft)
phunnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grumblings/complaints/murmurings) (d:<phunna>, grumbling, with the plural <te>) (b:phunna) (q:draft)
phunphun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:complain/grumble/murmur) (d:<phun> doubled: keep on complaining or muttering; {zi phunphun} is a nagging wife) (q:draft)
phunpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint) (d:<phun> grumble, with <pih> about or together and the noun suffix <na>) (q:draft)
phunsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grumble against/murmur against/complain against) (d:<phun> grumble with <san> directed at someone) (b:phun) (q:draft)
phunsanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:grumbling against someone) (b:phunsan) (q:draft)
phunsansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make grumble against) (d:<phunsan> grumble against, with <sak> cause) (b:phunsan) (q:draft)
phunsante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grumblers/those who grumble against) (d:<phunsan> grumble against, with the plural <te>: those who have grumbled against someone) (b:phunsan) (q:draft)
phusak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drive toward/make head for) (d:<phu> head into or push against, with <sak> cause; of steering a ship toward the shore) (b:phu) (q:draft, low confidence)
phusuakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:heading straight on/blundering on) (d:apparently <phu> head into with <suak> through and the ending <in>: going straight on into danger without turning aside) (r:20.22.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
phut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set up/erect/establish/plant) (d:set something firmly in place, as a pillar, a foundation or a people) (s:dingsak) (r:19.104.5) (q:draft)
phutin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set up/erect/establish) (d:<phut> with {-in}, linking it to the next verb: setting up, having erected) (b:phut) (q:draft)
phutkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:encounter/come upon/meet) (d:come up against someone or something on the way) (q:draft)
phutkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have established/have set up) (d:<phut> set up, with <khin> already done) (b:phut) (q:draft)
phutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:press/onset) (d:<phut> with the noun suffix <na>; {gal in a phutna}, the place where battle presses hard, where the English has the heat of battle) (q:draft, low confidence)
phutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have set up/cause to be erected) (d:<phut> set up, with the causative <sak>: have someone set a thing up) (b:phut) (q:draft)
phutthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can lay/can set up) (d:<phut> set up, with <thei> can) (b:phut) (q:draft)
pi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foot) (d:unit of length, a foot; where the English Bible has cubits the number is converted, one cubit counted as a foot and a half) (r:1.6.15) (q:draft)
pi = (i:3) (t:part) (d:suffix added to a noun or adjective, big, great or chief) (q:draft, low confidence)
Pia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give) (d:<pia>, give, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; {pia khia} is give up or hand over) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:inflict harshly) (d:<pia> give, with <gawp> roughly or severely; {gim piagawp} is punish severely) (b:pia) (q:draft, low confidence)
piak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gave/give/given) (d:form of <pia>, give, used in dependent clauses and before endings and words such as <ding>, <ciangin> and <bangin>) (b:pia)
Piak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give) (d:<piak>, form of <pia> give used before a noun; {Gim Piak Ni}, the day suffering is given, is the day of punishment) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piakha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:may give/happen to give) (d:<pia> give, with <kha> perhaps or happen to) (q:draft)
piakhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give together/offer along with) (d:<pia> give with <khawm> together: give or offer one thing with another) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give out/give away/give up/hand over) (d:<pia> give with <khia> out) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have given/have granted) (d:<pia> with <khin>, already: the giving is done) (s:piazo) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piakhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:command beforehand/give in advance) (d:<pia> give with <khol> beforehand; {thu piakhol}, give an order or a word ahead of time) (q:draft)
piakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give back/return/restore) (d:<pia> give with <kik> back, again) (a:lakik) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piakkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing together with another, of the grain offering that goes with an animal offering; <piak>, give, with <khawm>, together) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give out/give up/lay down) (d:give away from oneself; {nuntakna piakkhiat} is lay down the life) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piakkhiatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:givings/things given out) (d:<piakkhiat> give out, with the noun suffix <na> and plural <te>; paired with <ngahna>, receiving) (b:piakkhiat) (q:draft)
piakkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:<piak> give, with <khit> finish; with <ciangin>, after having given or offered) (q:draft)
piakkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:command beforehand/tell in advance) (d:<piak> give with <kholh> beforehand; the form of <piakhol> used before <bangin>: {thu a piakkholh bangin}, just as he said beforehand) (s:piakhol) (q:draft)
piakkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:word given beforehand/promise) (d:<piakkholh>, give beforehand, with the noun suffix <na>; {thu piakkholhna} is a word spoken or given in advance, such as a promise or an oath) (b:piakkholh) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakkhong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gift/free gift) (d:something given freely, a free gift, mostly of what God gives; also placed before <letsong> or <na>: a freely given gift or thing) (s:letsong) (q:draft)
piakkhongin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as a gift/as a free gift) (d:<piakkhong> free gift, with the suffix <in>) (s:letsongin) (b:piakkhong) (q:draft)
piakkhongna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:giving/gift/bestowal) (d:<piakkhong>, give freely, with the noun suffix <na>: the giving of something as a free gift, as of grace or of the Holy Spirit) (b:piakkhong) (q:draft)
piakkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing along with another; another form of <piakkhawm>) (s:piakkhawm/piakhawm) (r:26.46.5) (q:draft)
piakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give back/restore/give again) (d:<piak>, give, with <kik>, again or back: give something back to its owner, give again or restore; {thu piakkik} is give a further order) (s:piakik) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piakma = (i:1) (t:v) (w:before giving) (d:<piak> give, with <ma> before: before he gives) (q:draft)
piakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:offering) (d:<piak>, give, with the noun suffix <na>: something given to God, an offering) (s:biakpiakna/letsong) (b:piak)
piakna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:contribution/donation) (d:a gift of money or goods given freely for a purpose; {ut thu-a piakna} is a freewill offering) (b:piak)
piaknasa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:<piak> give, with <na> and <sa>, already done: what has been given, or the place where one has given) (b:piak) (q:draft, low confidence)
piaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:offerings/sacrifices/gifts) (d:plural of <piakna>: the offerings, sacrifices or gifts that are given to God) (s:biakpiaknate/biaknate) (b:piakna) (q:draft)
piaknop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to give/be willing to give) (d:<piak>, give, with <nop>, want; {ama piaknop zahzah} is as much as he wants to give) (s:pianuam) (q:draft)
piaknopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:willingness to give/willingness/generosity) (d:<piaknop> want to give, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:utna/citna) (b:piaknop) (r:47.8.12) (q:draft)
piakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one given to) (d:the man to whom something is given; <piak>, give, with <pa> marking a male person. {Topa thupha piakpa} is the one blessed by the Lord) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give at once/give immediately) (d:<piak> give, with <pah> at once) (q:draft)
piaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:given) (d:already given, <piak> with the completive suffix <sa>; {thu piaksa} is what was commanded) (s:kipiaksa) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:offer for/give on behalf of) (d:<piak>, give, with <sak>: give or offer something for another person, as a priest offers a sacrifice for someone) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piaksak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:make give/have given) (d:<piak>, give, with causative <sak>: cause something to be given or handed over) (b:piak) (q:draft, low confidence)
piaksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things given/those given) (d:what has been given, also of orders given and loans made) (b:piaksa) (q:draft)
piaktawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give of own accord/give voluntarily) (d:<piak> give, with <tawm> showing that the subject acts on his own) (q:draft)
piakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:offerings/gifts/things given) (d:the things that someone gives or has given) (s:piaknate) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piaktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can give/be able to give) (d:<piak> give with <theih> can; with <nading>, so that one may give or hand over) (s:piathei/piakzawh) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piaktheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ability to give/means of handing over) (d:being able to give or hand over; <piaktheih> can give, with the noun suffix <na>; with <dingzia>, the way in which one might hand over) (b:piaktheih) (q:draft)
piaktuak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:fit to be given to) (d:<piak> give with <tuak> fitting; {piaktuak sa} is consider it right to give to) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:amount given/as much as given) (d:<piak>, give, with <zah>, amount: the amount that was given; {a piakzah mah}, the same amount as was given) (s:kipiazah) (q:draft)
piakzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give more) (d:<piak> give with <zaw> more: give more than before or more than to others) (s:piazaw/piathuah) (b:piak) (q:draft)
piakzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to give/afford) (d:form of {pia zo}, can give, used before <bangbang>, <ding> and {kei leh}) (s:piaktheih/piathei) (q:draft)
piakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of giving/manner of giving) (d:<piak> give, with <zia> manner; {gim piakzia} is the way punishment is dealt out) (q:draft)
pial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn aside/stray/deviate) (d:leave the path or the right way, often as {lam pial}; with <panin>, turn away from a way, a teaching or a command) (s:lampial/pialkhia) (a:zui) (q:draft)
pialin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turning aside/straying/departing) (d:<pial>, turn aside, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (s:lampialin) (b:pial) (q:draft)
pialkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stray/turn aside/go astray) (d:<pial>, turn aside, with <kha>, happen to: leave the right way, often with <kei> in a warning) (s:pial/lampial) (q:draft)
pialkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away/stray/depart from) (d:<pial>, turn aside, with <khia>, out or away: turn aside and leave a path, a command or a way of acting) (s:pial/lampial) (a:zui) (b:pial) (q:draft)
pialkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn away/desert/depart from) (d:form of <pialkhia> used before <zawh> and endings) (b:pialkhia) (q:draft)
pialkhiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who stray/strays) (d:<pialkhia> turn away with the plural <te>: those who turn away from a path or a rule) (s:pialte/lampialte) (b:pialkhia) (q:draft)
pialkhiatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead astray/turn away with) (d:<pialkhiat> turn away, with <pih> together with: draw someone away) (b:pialkhiat) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have turned away/have departed) (d:<pial> turn aside, with <khin> already done) (b:pial) (q:draft)
pialna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:straying/turning aside/error) (d:<pial>, turn aside, with the noun suffix <na>; {lam pialna}, leaving the right way) (s:lampialna) (b:pial) (q:draft)
pialpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead astray/mislead) (d:<pial> turn aside, with <pih>, take along: make someone leave the right way, as {lam pialpih}) (s:pialsak/lampialsak) (b:pial) (q:draft)
pialpual = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:expressive word placed after <satsak>, make hot: heated through, inflamed; said of people heated by wine) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead astray/cause to stray/mislead) (d:<pial> turn aside with <sak> cause; {lam pialsak}, lead off the right way) (s:pialpih/lampialsak/khialsak) (b:pial) (q:draft)
pialsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leading astray/causing to stray) (d:<pialsak> cause to stray, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:pialsak) (q:draft)
pialte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:strays/those who stray) (d:<pial> stray with the plural <te>; {a lam pialte}, those that have left the way) (s:lampialte/pialkhiate) (b:pial) (q:draft)
pian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be born/come into being/come about) (d:often written {pian’}; form of <piang> used before endings and in compounds: {pian’na}, birth or origin; {pian’sak}, create or cause) (s:suah) (a:sih) (r:59.1.18) (q:draft)
pian = (i:2) (t:n) (w:likeness/form/appearance) (d:something that looks like another thing; {a kibang pian khat}, a figure like, what looked like) (s:lim/pianzia) (r:26.10.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
pian'napa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ancestor/forefather/father) (d:<pian> be born, come into being, with the noun suffix <na>, origin, and <pa> for a man: the man from whom a people descends) (s:pupi/pusawn) (q:draft)
pian'saksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creatures/created things) (d:<piansaksa> what has been created, with plural <te>; written with an apostrophe in this text) (s:piansaksate/piansakte) (q:draft)
piancil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creation/beginning) (d:the time when something first came into being; {lei piancil}, the creation of the world) (s:piancilna/kipatcil) (a:tawpna) (q:draft)
piancilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:origin/beginning/creation) (d:<piancil> with the noun suffix <na>: the first coming into being of something; {piancilna mun}, the place a people came from) (s:piancil/piankhiatna) (b:piancil) (q:draft)
piang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become/come into being/happen) (d:come into being: be born, be produced, come about or happen; with a noun before it, become that thing) (s:suak) begin to be
piangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:coming into being/arising/springing up) (d:<piang> be born or come about, with the linking ending <in>) (b:piang) (q:draft)
piangkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:may be produced/may come about) (d:<piang> come into being, with <kha> perhaps or happen to) (q:draft)
piangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come forth/arise/be born/break out) (d:<piang>, come into being, with <khia>, out: spring out of, originate from) (s:suakkhia) (b:piang) (r:23.48.1) (q:draft)
piangkhiasak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:bring forth/produce) (d:<piangkhia>, come forth, with the causative <sak>: cause to come out, said of the earth that brings forth plants) (b:piangkhia) (q:?)
piangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be produced again/come forth again/arise afterward) (d:<piang>, come into being, with <kik>, again or in turn: of crops, grow again; of a law or a generation, come later) (b:piang) (q:draft)
piangsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:happened/past) (d:<piang> happen with <sa> already; {a piangsa thu}, what has happened) (s:tungsa) (b:piang) (q:draft)
piangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:produce/create/bring about) (d:<piang>, come into being, with the causative <sak>: make something come into being, said of land that yields crops, of God who creates, and of whatever causes a result) (s:piansak) (b:piang)
Piangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:create/make/bring into being) (d:<piangsak>, cause to come into being, written with a capital when said of God: {a Piangsak pa}, the Creator, the Maker) (s:Bawl) (b:piangsak) (q:draft)
piangsaka = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause/produce/raise) (d:<piangsak> cause to be, with the linking <a>, and) (b:piangsak) (q:draft)
piangsakin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:creating/making/forming) (d:<piangsak>, create or cause to be, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:piangsak) (q:?)
piangsakkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause/bring about) (d:<piangsak> cause with <kha>, happen to: bring something about, often without meaning to) (q:draft)
piangsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to happen again/bring about again) (d:<piangsak> cause to be, with <kik> again) (b:piangsak) (q:draft)
piangsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creator/maker/author) (d:he who brings something into being; {-pa} marks a male) (s:bawlpa) (b:piangsak) (r:40.19.4) (q:draft)
Piangsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Creator/Maker) (d:<piangsak>, cause to come into being, with {-pa} marking a male person: the one who made, written with a capital as a title of God) (s:Bawlpa) (b:piangsakpa) (q:draft)
piangsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who cause/those who stir up) (d:<piangsak> cause or produce, with <te>, those who) (b:piangsak) (q:draft)
piangsakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can produce/can give rise to) (d:<piangsak> cause to be, with <thei> can) (b:piangsak) (q:draft)
piangsakzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause rather/produce more) (d:<piangsak> cause to be, with <zaw> more, used with <sangin> than) (b:piangsak) (q:draft)
piangsakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to bring about/manage to cause) (d:<piangsak> cause to be, with <zo> be able to) (b:piangsak) (q:draft)
piangsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:produce/things produced) (d:<piangsa> already come into being, with plural <te>; {lo pan-a piangsate} is what has grown from the field) (s:piangte) (b:piangsa) (q:draft)
piangtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:arise of itself/spring up by itself) (d:<piang> come into being with <tawm>, of oneself: come about on its own, without another cause) (s:pokhiatawm) (q:draft)
piangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crops/produce/fruit) (d:the things that are produced or come into being, plural noun use of <piang>) (s:gahte/ante) (b:piang) (r:5.7.13) (q:draft)
piangthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can come about/be able to arise/can happen) (d:<piang>, come into being, with <thei>, be able) (s:piangzo) (b:piang) (q:draft)
piangthuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be born in addition) (d:<piang> be born, with <thuah> in addition, more) (q:draft)
piangvat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen suddenly/come about quickly) (d:<piang> happen with <vat>, suddenly) (q:draft)
piangzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:arise instead/happen rather) (d:<piang> happen, with <zaw> rather or more) (b:piang) (q:draft)
piangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can happen/come to pass) (d:<piang> happen, with <zo> be able to) (s:piangthei) (b:piang) (q:draft)
pianin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:by birth/at birth) (d:<pian> be born, come into being, with the ending <in>: at or by the birth of a person, or when a thing came to be) (s:pianpihin) (b:pian) (q:draft)
piankhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen/take place) (d:<pian> happen, with <khak> happen to, the form used before <loh>: so that it may not happen) (q:draft)
piankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come into being/spring forth) (d:<pian> come into being, with <khiat> out) (b:pian) (q:draft)
piankhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:origin/source/place of origin) (d:where a person or thing comes from) (s:piancilna) (b:piankhiat) (q:draft)
piankhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have happened) (d:<pian> happen, with <khit> finish; with <ciangin>, after it had happened) (q:draft)
pianlim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shape/form/likeness) (d:the outward form of a thing; of the Son, the exact likeness of God) (s:pianzia/lim) (q:draft)
pianlui = (i:1) (t:n) (w:old self/old nature) (d:<pian> nature or form one is born with, with <lui> old) (a:mithak) (q:draft)
pianma = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:before the birth of/before the creation of/before it happens) (d:<pian>, form of <piang>, be born or come about, with <ma>, before: before something was born, made or took place; {leitung pianma} is before the world was made) (q:draft)
pianna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:formation/origin) (d:<pian>, come into being, with the noun suffix <na>: the way or the cause by which something comes to be) (s:piansakna)
pianna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:generation/birth/descent) (d:the birth or descent of a person or a people: {pianna khua} is the hometown, {pianna gam} the native land, and {pianna pupi} the ancestor from whom a people comes) (s:suahna)
pianngei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nature/natural state) (d:<pian> be born with <ngei>, the usual or original way: what a person or thing is by birth, by nature) (s:pianzia) (q:draft)
pianpih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:inborn/natural/from birth) (d:what one is born with; {a pianpih mittaw}, blind from birth, {pianpih lungsim}, the natural mind or instinct) (s:suahpih) (b:pian) (q:draft)
pianpihin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:from birth/by birth) (d:<pianpih> inborn, with the suffix <in>) (s:pianin) (b:pianpih) (q:draft)
piansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause/produce/create) (d:<pian>, come into being, with the causative <sak>: cause something to be, produce or create it) (s:piangsak) (q:?)
piansakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:create) (d:<piansak>, create, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:piansak)
piansakkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause/bring about) (d:<piansak> cause to be, with <khak> happen to, the form used before <loh>: so as not to cause) (q:draft)
piansakma = (i:1) (t:v) (w:before creating) (d:<piansak> create, with <ma> before) (q:draft)
piansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:formation) (d:<piansak>, cause to be, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of forming or creating something) (s:pianna)
piansaksa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creation) (d:<piansak>, create, with <sa>, already done: what someone has created) (s:bawlsa) (b:piansak)
piansaksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creatures/created things) (d:<piansaksa> what has been created, with plural <te>) (s:piansakte/pian'saksate) (b:piansaksa) (q:draft)
piansaktawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:introduce/originate) (d:<piansak> cause to be, with <tawm> showing that the subject acts on his own: bring in of own making) (q:draft)
piansakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creatures/creation/things created) (d:<piansak> create, cause to be, with the plural <te>: the things that someone has made) (s:piansaksate) (b:piansak) (q:draft)
piantheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can happen/be possible/can come about) (d:<pian> come into being, with <theih>, be able) (s:hithei) (b:pian) (q:draft)
pianuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to give/be willing to give) (d:<pia>, give, with <nuam>, want) (s:piaknop) (q:draft)
pianuamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those willing to give) (d:<pianuam>, be willing to give, with the plural <te>: people who would gladly give something) (b:pianuam) (q:draft)
pianzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have come into being/have happened/since) (d:<pian>, come into being or happen, with <zawh>, finished: used for the time since something began or happened, as in {mihing a pianzawh}, since mankind came to be) (s:piankhit) (q:draft, low confidence)
pianzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nature/appearance/form/character) (d:the way a person or thing is made: its outward form or appearance, and the inner nature or character that shows in what it does) (s:pianlim/pianngei) (q:draft)
pianzia = (i:2) (t:n) (w:glory/divine nature) (d:in the phrase {Pasian’ pianzia}, the nature of God that is seen as his glory; in John it stands where English has glory and glorify) (s:minthanna) (q:draft, low confidence)
pianziate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:appearances/natures/characteristics) (d:plural of <pianzia>: the outward looks of people, or the qualities of a nature, as in {Pasian’ pianziate}, the divine nature) (b:pianzia) (q:draft)
piapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:giver/one who gives) (d:<pia>, give, with <pa>, the man who gives; {an piapa}, the man who serves food and drink to the king, is the cupbearer) (a:ngahpa) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piapi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chief cupbearer/chief server) (d:in {an piapi pa}, the chief of those who serve food and drink to the king: <pia>, give, with <pi>, chief) (s:piapipa) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piapipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chief cupbearer/chief butler) (d:in {an piapipa}, the chief man who serves food and drink to the king; <pa> marks a man) (s:piapi) (b:piapi) (r:1.41.9) (q:draft)
piasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have someone give/let give/have given) (d:<pia>, give, with the causative <sak>: make or allow someone to give, or have a thing given to someone) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piasawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pass on/hand on/hand down) (d:<pia>, give, with <sawn>, onward: hand something on to those who come after, as land to one’s children) (q:draft)
piasim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give secretly) (d:<pia>, give, with <sim>, secretly; {kiciamna piasim} is swear an oath to someone in secret) (q:draft)
piasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give down/send down) (d:<pia>, give, with <suk>, downward: send something down from above, as fire from heaven) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piata = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have given/give over) (d:<pia>, give, with <ta>, marking that the act is now done; {khut sungah piata} is hand over into someone’s power) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:givers/those who give) (d:<pia>, give, with the plural <te>: the ones who give; {leitawi piate} are lenders, {an piate} those who serve food and drink, {biakna piate} those who offer sacrifices) (a:late) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piathei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to give/can give) (d:<pia>, give, with <thei>, be able: be able to give; {nuntakna a piathei} is life-giving) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piathuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give in addition/give more/give also) (d:<pia>, give, with <thuah>, add: give more on top of what someone already has) (r:20.3.16) (q:draft)
piau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bank/riverbank) (d:the side of a river; {a piau khempeuh}, all its banks, is said of a river in flood) (s:gunpang/gungei) (q:draft)
piazaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give instead/give all the more/give more) (d:<pia>, give, with <zaw>, more or rather: give to one instead of another, or give more; with {kan ding}, how much more will he give) (b:pia) (q:draft)
piazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have given/have granted) (d:<pia>, give, with <zo>, marking the action as completed: the thing has now been given) (s:piakhin) (b:pia) (q:draft)
Pibeseth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Bubastis) (d:city in the delta of Egypt, also called Bubastis, named in the prophecy of Ezekiel against Egypt) (r:26.30.17)
piciang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:measuring rod/measure) (d:a rod used for measuring length; {tehna piciang} is a measuring rod, and {piciang nam nih}, two kinds of measures, means dishonest measuring) (q:draft)
picing = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:mature/full-grown/grown up) (d:fully grown in body or in mind; {picing sak} is make mature) (s:cingtaak) (q:draft)
pih = (i:1) (t:part) (d:verb suffix meaning to do the action together with or for someone, written separately after a verb stem ending in an apostrophe, as in {ten’pih}, live with or marry, {pan’pih}, take the side of, and {tun’pih}, bring to) (r:20.16.29) (q:draft)
Piha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pilha) (d:one of the leaders of the people who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.24) (q:draft)
Pihahiroth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Pi Hahiroth) (d:place in Egypt between Migdol and the sea, facing Baal Zephon, where Israel camped before crossing the sea) (r:4.33.7/2.14.2)
pihin = (i:1) (t:part) (d:verb suffix <pih>, do together with or bring along, with the linking ending <in>; written after an apostrophe, as in {ten’pihin}, marrying, and {tun’pihin}, bringing) (b:pih) (q:draft)
pihkik = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<pih>, do together with someone, followed by <kik> back; {tun pihkik} is bring someone back to a place, normally written {tunpih kik}) (b:pih) (q:draft, low confidence)
pihna = (t:see) <ten'pihna>
pihpa = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the verb ending <pih>, together with or for someone, followed by <pa> for a man: the man who does the action with or for another; {kipawl pihpa}, ally, {paikhiat pihpa}, he who brings out) (b:pih) (q:draft)
pihsak = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the verb ending <pih>, together with or taking along, followed by <sak>, cause or let: {paikhiat pihsak}, let someone be brought out; {kiten’ pihsak}, have someone married) (b:pih) (q:draft, low confidence)
pihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:companions/fellows) (d:<pih> with the plural <te>: those who do something together with someone; it follows a verb or noun, as {kipawl pihte}, allies or friends, {innkuan pihte}, fellow citizens, and {teen’pihte}, those who marry someone) (b:pih) (q:draft)
piikpeek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:completely/fully/utterly) (d:placed after a verb or describing word to show that something is complete or full to the limit, as {kicing piikpeek}, fully supplied; also written <pikpek>) (s:pikpek/bikbek) (q:draft, low confidence)
pik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gore) (d:of a bull, strike or pierce with the horn; {ki tawh pik} is gore with its horns) (s:nawt) (q:draft)
pikhau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:measuring line/measuring cord) (d:<pi>, the measure of length, with <khau>, cord: a cord for measuring, named beside <piciang>, the measuring rod; the English has linen cord) (s:khauzang) (q:draft)
pikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead out/bring out) (d:<pi>, lead, with <khia>, out: lead people out of a place, as out of captivity) (s:paikhiatpih) (q:draft)
pikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lead back/bring back) (d:<pi>, lead, with <kik>, back: lead people back to where they came from) (s:tunpihkik/ciahpihkik) (q:draft)
piklup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gore to death) (d:of a bull, strike with the horns so that the victim falls dead) (q:draft)
pikpek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:completely/fully/utterly) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: to the full, altogether; also written <piikpeek>) (s:piikpeek/bikbek) (q:draft)
piksante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who purse the lips at) (d:with <neh>, lips: those who press their lips together at someone; apparently <pik> with <san>, directed at, and the plural <te>, parallel to <sitsante>, those who wink at) (q:draft, low confidence)
pil = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wise/learned/sensible) (d:having wisdom or good sense; also used as a verb, be or become wise, and {pil zaw} is wiser) (s:lungpil) (a:hai) (q:draft)
Pilat = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pilate) (d:Pontius Pilate, the Roman governor of Judea who tried Jesus and handed him over to be crucified) (r:43.19.8/42.23.13)
Pildash = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pildash) (d:son of Nahor, the brother of Abraham, and Milkah) (r:1.22.22)
pileser = (t:see) <Tiglath-pileser>
pilhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wise/prudent) (d:<pil>, wise, with <huai>, worthy of: wise or sensible to do; {pilhuai zaw} is the wiser course) (a:haihuai) (q:draft)
pilin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wise/sensible) (d:<pil> with the linking suffix <in>: being wise, or as wise; {a pilin kingaihsun} is think oneself wise, and {lungsim pilin} is in his right mind) (b:pil) (q:draft)
pilkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:return to one’s right mind/recovery of one’s senses) (d:<pil>, wise or sensible, with <kik>, again, and the noun suffix <na>: the state of being in one’s right mind again) (q:draft)
pillawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gain wisdom/become wise) (d:<pil>, wise, with <lawh>, get as a result: become wise through what happens to another) (q:draft)
pillohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:folly/foolishness) (d:<pil>, wise, with <loh>, not, and the noun suffix <na>: lack of wisdom, folly) (s:haina) (a:pilna) (q:draft)
pillote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fools/the simple/unwise people) (d:<pil>, wise, with <lo>, not, and plural <te>: those who are not wise) (s:mihaite/pilote) (a:mipilte/pilte) (q:draft)
pilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wisdom/knowledge/understanding) (d:<pil>, wise, with the noun suffix <na>: wisdom, and also knowledge and good understanding) (s:lungpilna/ciimna) (a:haina) (b:pil) (r:20.3.13) (q:draft)
Pilna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wisdom/understanding) (d:<pilna> written with a capital at the start of a sentence or line, and in Proverbs of Wisdom speaking as a person) (s:lungpilna/ciimna) (a:haina) (b:pilna) (r:42.11.49) (q:draft)
pilnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wisdom/knowledge) (d:<pilna> with the plural <te>: the things one knows, kinds of wisdom) (b:pilna) (q:draft)
pilneser = (t:see) <Tilgath-pilneser>
pilote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fools/foolish people) (d:<pil> wise, <lo> not and plural <te> written as one word: those who are not wise) (s:mihaite/pillote) (a:mipilte/pilte) (q:draft)
pilpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wisest/most wise) (d:<pil>, wise, with <pen>, most: the wisest of a group; {a pilpen pen} is extremely wise) (b:pil) (q:draft)
pilpennu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wisest woman) (d:<pilpen> wisest, with <nu> marking a woman) (b:pilpen) (q:draft)
pilsak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wise/make wise) (d:<pil>, wise, with the causative <sak>: make someone wise) (b:pil) (r:1.3.6)
pilsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the wise/those already wise) (d:<pil>, wise, with <sa>, already, and the plural <te>: people who are already wise) (s:mipilte/mipilsate/ciimsate) (a:mihaite) (q:draft)
Piltai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Piltai) (d:priest, head of the family of Moadiah in the days of the high priest Joiakim) (r:16.12.17)
pilte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the wise/wise ones) (d:<pil>, wise, with the plural <te>: the wise ones; after a noun it means wise, as {numei pilte}, wise women, and {mi pilte}, wise men) (s:mipilte/lungpilte) (a:haite/mihaite) (b:pil) (q:draft)
pilvan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wake up/sober up) (d:form of <pilvang> written with a final apostrophe before <ciangin>: of a drunk man, wake and be clear-headed again) (q:draft)
pilvang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be alert/keep watch/be sober/be shrewd) (d:stay awake, watchful and ready; of a drunk man, become sober again) (s:khuaphawk) (q:draft)
pilvangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:watchfully/alertly/soberly) (d:<pilvang>, be alert, with the ending <in>: staying watchful while doing the next action) (b:pilvang) (q:draft)
pilzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wiser) (d:<pil>, wise, with <zaw>, more: wiser, used with <sangin>, than) (b:pil) (q:draft)
pilzawk = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wiser) (d:form of <pilzaw> used before <manin>, because: being wiser) (b:pilzaw) (q:draft)
pingaihsut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have regard for/look on with favour/give heed to) (d:think of a person or thing with care or favour; built on <ngaihsut>, think) (q:draft)
pingpei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whirlwind/windstorm) (d:a wind that spins round, a whirlwind or violent windstorm; {pingpei bangin} is like a whirlwind) (s:huihpi) (q:draft)
pingpeipei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:whirl round/roll round and round) (d:turn something round and round, as in rolling it into a ball before throwing) (q:draft, low confidence)
Pingpeite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whirlwinds) (d:<pingpei> whirlwind with plural <te>) (q:draft)
Pinon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pinon) (d:one of the chiefs of Edom descended from Esau) (r:1.36.41/13.1.52)
pipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chief/head/leader) (d:<pi>, chief, with <pa> for a man, placed after a title: {tuucing pipa}, chief shepherd, {anhuan pipa}, chief baker) (q:draft)
pipa = (i:2) (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:in {zi pipa}, the man who takes a wife) (s:zipipa/mopipa/zineipa) (a:mo) (q:draft, low confidence)
pipi = (i:1) (t:part) (w:very/huge) (d:intensifier placed after a describing word, often of several things: {gol pipi}, very large, {lamdang pipi}, very wonderful) (q:draft)
pipi = (i:2) (t:part) (d:placed after a verb or state word, often with <in>: while in that state, with that feeling; {lunghimawh pipi-in}, while doubting, {ut lo pipi}, unwillingly, {dah pipi-in}, with grief) (q:draft)
Piram = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Piram) (d:Amorite king of Jarmuth, one of the five kings who attacked Gibeon and were defeated by Joshua) (r:6.10.3)
Pirathon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Pirathon) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim, home of the judge Abdon and of Benaiah, one of the mighty men of David) (r:7.12.15/10.23.30)
Pirras = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pyrrhus) (d:father of Sopater of Berea, a companion of Paul) (r:44.20.4)
Pisgah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Pisgah) (d:mountain ridge in Moab east of the Jordan, from whose top near Mount Nebo Moses saw the promised land) (r:4.21.20/6.13.20)
Pisgal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Pisgah) (d:another spelling of Pisgah, the mountain ridge in Moab east of the Jordan) (r:5.4.47)
Pishon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Pishon) (d:the first of the four rivers flowing out of Eden, which winds through the land of Havilah) (r:1.2.11)
Pisidia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Pisidia) (d:mountainous region in the south of Asia Minor, north of Pamphylia, through which Paul and Barnabas travelled) (r:44.14.24/44.13.14)
Pispa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pispah) (d:son of Jether in the genealogy of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.38)
pistakhio = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:pistachio) (d:loan word; {pistakhio gah}, pistachio nuts) (q:draft)
pite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grandmothers/grandparents) (d:<pi> grandmother with the plural <te>; {a pu a pite}, grandfathers and grandmothers, grandparents) (b:pi) (q:draft)
piteek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:old woman) (d:<pi> grandmother or woman, with <teek> old; paired with <puteek>, old man) (s:pitek) (a:puteek) (q:draft)
pitek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:old woman) (d:<pi> grandmother or woman, with <tek> old; paired with <putek>, old man; the 1977 text spells it <piteek>) (s:piteek) (a:puteek) (q:draft)
Piter = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Peter) (d:the apostle Simon Peter, a fisherman of Galilee and brother of Andrew, one of the twelve disciples of Jesus) (r:44.11.4/43.6.8)
Pithom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Pithom) (d:store city in Egypt built for Pharaoh by the Israelites during their slavery) (r:2.1.11)
Pithon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pithon) (d:son of Micah, a descendant of King Saul through Jonathan, of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.35/13.9.41)
po = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sprout/grow/come up) (d:of a seed or plant, come up out of the ground and grow) (s:sel)
poding = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:broom bush/broom tree/juniper) (d:desert shrub; {poding kung} is the bush, {poding zung} its root) (q:draft)
poi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:matter/be a loss) (d:be a matter of regret or loss; {a poi sa} is feel it as a loss, here of living with a hand or foot missing) (q:draft, low confidence)
poin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sprout/grow up) (d:<po> sprout, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:po) (q:draft)
poina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defect/blemish/flaw) (d:noun from <poi>, be hurt or damaged: a bodily defect or injury in a person or an animal, which bars a priest from serving and an animal from being offered) (s:sitbaanna) (b:poi) (q:draft)
poisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:injure/hurt/harm) (d:<poi>, be hurt or damaged, with the causative <sak>: cause bodily injury to someone) (s:liamsak) (b:poi) (q:draft)
Pokereth = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Pokereth) (d:first part of the name Pokereth-Hazzebaim, head of a family of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.57)
Pokereth-hazzebaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pokereth-Hazzebaim) (d:head of a family among the descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (q:draft)
pokhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grow together/grow up with) (d:<po>, sprout, with <khawm>, together: come up and grow together with other plants) (s:khangkhawm) (b:po) (q:draft)
Pokhereth = (t:see) <Pokhereth-hazzebaim>
Pokhereth-hazzebaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pokereth-Hazzebaim) (d:head of a family among the descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:16.7.59) (q:draft)
Pokherethhazzebaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pokereth-Hazzebaim) (d:a servant of Solomon whose descendants returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.57/16.7.59)
pokhia = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sprung) (d:of plants, having come up out of the ground; <po>, sprout, with <khia>, out) (b:po)
pokhia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:grow/spring up/sprout/come up) (d:<po>, sprout, with <khia>, out: of plants, come up out of the ground or the water; also of trouble or righteousness that springs up) (s:selkhia/khangkhia) (b:po)
pokhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring forth/produce/make grow) (d:<pokhia>, sprout forth, with the causative <sak>: make plants come up, said of the ground) (s:posak) (b:pokhia)
pokhiasak = (i:2) (t:n) (w:growth)
pokhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spring up/sprout forth) (d:form of <pokhia> used before <theih> and endings) (b:pokhia) (q:draft)
pokhiatawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sprout of itself/spring up by itself) (d:<pokhia>, sprout forth, with <tawm>, of its own accord: come up by itself, without a cause) (s:piangtawm) (q:draft)
pokhiato = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spring up/sprout up) (d:<pokhia>, sprout forth, with <to>, upward: spring up; with <sak>, make spring up) (s:poto) (b:pokhia) (q:draft)
pom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:embrace/hold fast/clasp/cling to) (d:take or hold in the arms; also hold on to a teaching, a god or a person) (s:kawi/lenkip) (a:nusia) (r:1.33.4) (q:draft)
pomcipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:embrace tightly/hug) (d:<pom> embrace, with <cip> tight and the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft)
pomin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take in the arms/embrace/hold) (d:<pom> embrace, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:pom) (q:draft)
pomlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:still cling to/keep holding) (d:<pom> hold fast, with <lai> still) (q:draft)
pona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:growing place/growth) (d:noun of <po>, sprout or grow; with <mun>, the place where a plant grows, as {lingkung pona mun}, a place overgrown with thorn bushes) (b:po) (q:draft)
pongkhaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scales/balance) (d:instrument for weighing; the second part is <khai>, hang or weigh, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:tawikhaina/khaina) (q:draft)
Pontas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Pontus) (d:Roman province on the south coast of the Black Sea, in the north of Asia Minor) (r:44.2.9)
Pontias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pontius) (d:family name of Pilate, the Roman governor of Judea who tried Jesus) (r:44.4.27/42.3.1)
Ponun = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Punon) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Zalmonah and Oboth) (r:4.33.43)
popah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spring up at once/sprout quickly) (d:<po>, sprout, with <pah>, at once: come up quickly, said of seed sown in shallow soil) (q:draft)
poplar = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:poplar) (d:the English tree name, used with <kung>, tree) (s:gialheek/gialhek) (q:draft)
Poratha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Poratha) (d:one of the ten sons of Haman, killed by the Jews in Susa) (r:17.9.7)
Porsias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Porcius) (d:family name of Festus, who followed Felix as Roman governor of Judea) (r:44.24.27)
posak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be sprout/make grow/cause to sprout) (d:<po>, sprout, with the causative <sak>: make grass, trees or hair grow) (s:khangsak/pokhiasak) (b:po)
posakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who makes grow) (d:<posak> make grow, with <pa> marking a male doer) (s:khangsakpa) (b:posak) (q:draft)
pote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:what grows/growth/crops) (d:<po> grow with the plural <te>: the things that grow; {a li pote}, what grows of itself without sowing) (b:po) (q:draft)
Potifar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Potiphar) (d:Egyptian officer of Pharaoh, captain of the guard, who bought Joseph as a slave) (r:1.37.36/1.39.1)
Potifera = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Potiphera) (d:priest of On in Egypt, father of Asenath the wife of Joseph) (r:1.41.50/1.46.20)
poto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grow up/sprout up/spring up) (d:<po> sprout with <to> upward) (s:pokhiato/khangto) (b:po) (q:draft)
pound = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pound) (d:unit of weight, the English word) (q:draft)
pozo = (t:see) <pozo-in>
pozo-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overgrow/grow all over) (d:<po> sprout or grow with <zo> and the linking ending <in>: of thorns growing over a whole land) (q:draft, low confidence)
Prisilla = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Priscilla) (d:wife of Aquila and fellow worker of Paul) (r:44.18.2/45.16.3)
Prokhoras = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Procorus) (d:one of the seven men chosen to serve the church in Jerusalem) (r:44.6.5)
psap = (t:todo) (q:draft, stands before the first word of the verse and has no meaning in it, probably a stray formatting marker in the text and not a word)
pua = (i:1) (t:n) (w:outside) (d:the outer side, mostly as {pua lam} or {pua lamah} outside of) (s:pualam) (a:sunglam) (q:draft)
puah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repair/mend/restore) (d:put right something damaged, such as a wall, a door or a house; in Nehemiah, repair a section of the city wall) (s:bawlpha/bawlkik) (a:susia) (r:12.12.14) (q:draft)
Puah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Puah) (d:name of a Hebrew midwife in Egypt, and of two men of the tribe of Issachar) (r:2.1.15)
puahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:mending/repairing/preparing) (d:<puah> mend with the linking ending <in>; of fishermen putting their nets in order) (b:puah) (q:draft)
puahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:renovate/repair/restore) (d:<puah>, repair, with <kik>, again: put a ruined place back in good order) (s:bawlkik/lamkik)
puahkik = (i:2) (t:v) (w:remodel/revamp/rebuild/renew) (d:rebuild or renew ruined towns and walls)
puahkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repair/rebuild/restore) (d:<puahkik> repair again, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:puahkik) (q:draft)
puahkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:repair/restoration/renovation) (d:<puahkik> repair again, with the noun suffix <na>; {puahkikna nasepna}, the work of repair) (s:puahna/lamkikna) (b:puahkik) (q:draft)
puahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:repair/repairing/restoring) (d:<puah> repair, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:puahkikna/puahphatna) (a:suksiatna) (b:puah) (q:draft)
puahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:smoother/finisher) (d:<puah> put in good order with <pa> for a man: here the workman who smooths an idol with a hammer) (b:puah) (q:draft, low confidence)
puahpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore/repair/put in order) (d:<puah> repair with <pha> good: mend something so that it is good again) (s:bawlpha/puah) (q:draft)
puahphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repair/put in order/set right) (d:form of <puahpha> used before <ding>, <nading> and <hun>: mend something so that it is good again) (s:bawlphat) (b:puahpha) (q:draft)
puahphatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rebuild/restore/repair again) (d:<puahphat> set right with <kik> again) (b:puahphat) (q:draft)
puahphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:repair/reform/improvement) (d:<puahphat> repair, set right, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:puahna) (b:puahphat) (q:draft)
puahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repair/restore/set right) (d:<puah>, repair, with <sak>: have something repaired, or repair it for someone) (b:puah) (q:draft)
puahsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:restore/rebuild/repair again) (d:<puahsak> repair, with <kik> again, back) (b:puahsak) (r:26.36.34) (q:draft)
puahsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cleanse/purify) (d:put in order and make clean, said of the temple and its articles) (s:siangsak/siansuah) (a:ninsak) (b:puah) (q:draft)
puahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dressers/tenders/keepers) (d:<puah> repair or tend, with <te>, those who; {leenggui puahte} are vinedressers) (b:puah) (q:draft)
puahtheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who can correct) (d:<puah> mend or set right with <thei> can and plural <te>: people able to correct the faults of others) (q:draft, low confidence)
puak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry/bear) (d:form of <pua> used before <nading>, <ciangin> and other endings; {van puak} is a load to carry) (b:pua) (r:7.3.18) (q:draft)
puakbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tent) (d:<buk> is tent or shelter; the part <puak> is not explained by the verse) (s:puanbuk) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be cracked/burst/split) (d:<puak> burst or crack with <gawp> badly, said of old wineskins; not the verb <puak> carry) (q:draft)
puakha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry/happen to carry) (d:<pua> carry with <kha>, which shows that the action happens or comes about) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear together/carry together/share) (d:<pua> carry with <khawm> together) (b:pua) (q:draft)
puakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry out/carry away/carry off) (d:<pua>, carry, with <khia>, out: carry something or someone out of a place, or carry it off) (s:puakkhia) (b:pua) (q:draft)
puakhiamang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry off/carry away) (d:<pua> carry with <khia> out and <mang> away, gone: take everything away as plunder) (q:draft)
puakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry back/bring back/take back) (d:<pua> carry with <kik> back) (s:puakkik) (b:pua) (q:draft)
puakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send/bring) (d:<puak> with the linking ending <in>: sending, and then; {thu puakin}, sending word) (b:puak) (r:11.21.14) (q:draft)
puakkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry/may carry) (d:<puak> carry or bring with <kha>, which shows that the action may happen: of a bird carrying a person's words to others) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burst/break out) (d:burst open, as a wineskin; of boils, break out on the skin) (s:phukham) (q:draft)
puakkhamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:burst open/burst forth) (d:<puakkham> burst, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:puakkham) (q:draft)
puakkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring along with/carry together) (d:<puak>, carry or bring, with <khawm>, together: bring one thing along with another, used with <tawh>) (b:puak) (q:draft)
puakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send away/carry away/deport) (d:<puak>, carry or send, with <khia>, out: take or send something or someone away from a place) (s:puakhia) (b:puak) (q:draft)
puakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry out/send away/send into exile) (d:form of <puakkhia> used before a noun, <uh> or <lai>; of a body carried out for burial and of people sent away as captives) (b:puakkhia) (q:draft)
puakkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:carrying away/deportation/exile) (d:<puakkhiat> carry away with the noun suffix <na>; {na puakkhiatna uh mun}, the place of those who were carried away) (b:puakkhiat) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakkhiatpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one carried away/exile/captive) (d:<puakkhiat> carry away with <pa> for a man: the man who was carried off as a captive) (b:puakkhiat) (q:draft)
puakkhop = (i:1) (t:n) (w:load) (d:<puak> carry with <khop> enough: as much as can be carried; {la-sakol nih puakkhop} is as much as two mules can carry) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send back/bring back/return) (d:<puak> carry, send, with <kik> back, again) (s:puakik) (b:puak) (r:24.38.26) (q:draft)
puakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:carrying/bearing) (d:the act of carrying or bearing something; {puakna ngah} is be carried up) (b:puak) (q:draft)
puakna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:sending) (d:the sending of a message or thing to someone) (s:sawlna) (b:puak) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bringer/bearer/messenger) (d:<puak> bring with <pa> for a man: the man who brings; {thu hong puakpa}, the one who brought the news) (s:puapa) (b:puak) (q:draft)
puakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send at once/send immediately) (d:<puak> send with <pah> at once) (s:sawlpah) (q:draft)
puakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:help carry/share a burden) (d:<puak> carry with <pih>, together with someone) (b:puak) (q:draft)
