Rehboth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:well) (w:Rehoboth) (d:well dug by Isaac, over which no one quarrelled) (r:1.26.22)
Rehob = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Rehob) (d:town in the territory of Asher, given to the Levites; also a place in the far north reached by the spies) (r:6.19.28) (q:draft)
Rehob = (i:2) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Rehob) (d:Levite who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (q:draft)
Rehoboam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Rehoboam) (d:son of Solomon, first king of Judah after the kingdom was divided) (r:40.1.7/11.14.30)
Rehoboth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Rehoboth-Ir/Rehoboth) (d:town on the river, home of Shaul king of Edom; also the first part of the name Rehoboth-Ir) (r:1.10.11)
Rehoboth-Ir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Rehoboth Ir) (d:city in Assyria built by Nimrod) (r:1.10.11) (q:draft)
Rehum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Rehum) (d:name of several men, among them a Persian commanding officer who wrote against Jerusalem) (r:16.12.3/15.4.8)
Rekah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Rekah) (d:place in Judah whose men were descendants of Eshton) (r:13.4.12) (q:draft)
Reke = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Rekem) (d:Rekem, one of the five chiefs of Midian defeated by Moses; this text spells the name {Reke}) (q:draft)
Rekem = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male/city) (w:Rekem) (d:name of a king of Midian, of a son of Hebron of Judah, and of a town in Benjamin) (r:13.2.43/6.18.27)
Rekhab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Rekab) (d:name of several men, among them the ancestor of the Rekabites and one of the murderers of Ish-Bosheth) (r:10.4.2)
Remaliah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Remaliah) (d:father of Pekah king of Israel) (r:12.15.37/23.7.5)
