sangtozaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be higher/rise higher) (d:<sangto> rise high with <zaw> more) (b:sangto) (q:draft)
sangun = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:than) (d:<sang>, than, in a comparison, with <un> marking a plural subject; the same as <sangin>) (q:draft)
sangzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:higher/taller) (d:<sang>, high, with <zaw>, more: higher or taller, used with <sangin> or <sanga>, than) (a:niamzaw) (b:sang) (q:draft)
sangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to accept/be able to receive) (d:<sang> receive or accept, with <zo> be able; with <kei>, could not accept; {hu sangzo} is be able to draw breath) (s:sangthei/santheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
sangzo = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be able to grow tall/reach high) (d:<sang> high, with <zo> be able) (b:sang) (q:draft, low confidence)
sanhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:acceptable/pleasing/reasonable) (d:<san>, accept, with <huai>, worthy of: fit to be accepted, pleasing to the one who receives it; of words, reasonable) (s:santheih/lungkimhuai) (q:draft)
Sani = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Saturday) (d:{Sani nitak} is Saturday evening, the evening that begins the first day of the week) (b:sani) (q:draft)
sanim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be bruised/be crushed) (d:of flesh, be bruised or crushed; {sanim gawpnate}, bruises) (q:draft)
sanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:exert/strain/rally) (d:form of <san> with the linking suffix <in>, used with <tha> or <thatang>, strength, for gathering or straining one's strength) (q:draft, low confidence)
sanin = (i:2) (t:v) (d:form of <san> with the linking suffix <in>, placed after a verb of gesture to show that it is done at or against someone, as gnashing the teeth at a person) (q:draft, low confidence)
sanin = (i:3) (t:adv) (w:red) (d:<san>, red, with the suffix <in>: red, looking red, as in {a sanin mu}, see something as red, and {van sanin}, the sky being red) (b:san) (q:draft)
sankang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:reddish-white) (d:<san>, red, with <kang>, white: reddish-white, said of a spot or sore on the skin) (q:draft)
sankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:breathe out/send forth) (d:<san>, form of <sang> breathe, with <khiat> out; said of God sending out his breath or Spirit) (q:draft, low confidence)
sankhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have received/have taken) (d:<san>, form of <sang> receive, with <khit> finished; {a sankhit ciangin} is after he had taken) (s:lakkhit/ngahkhit) (q:draft)
sankhitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:having accepted) (d:<sankhit> have received with the noun suffix <na>: the fact that someone has accepted) (b:sankhit) (q:draft)
sanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:height) (d:<sang>, high, with the noun suffix <na>: height, how high or tall something is; {a sanna munte} are the heights) (s:sangna)
sannath = (t:see) <Kiriath-sannath>
sansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:received/accepted) (d:<san>, form of <sang>, receive or accept, with the completive suffix <sa>: already received) (s:ngahsa) (b:san) (q:draft)
sansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make red/redden) (d:<san>, red, with the causative <sak>: make red, as with blood, or make red-hot in the fire) (b:san) (q:draft)
sansak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:raise/hold up/lift) (d:make high; apparently a spelling of <sangsak>) (s:sangsak) (a:niamsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
sansan = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:after a verb of speaking, apparently again and again or at length; {genpha sansan nawn kei ni} seems to be let us not go on speaking of these again) (q:draft, low confidence)
