santheih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:acceptable/pleasing) (d:<san>, accept, with <theih>, able: that can be accepted, pleasing; {Pasian’ santheih} is acceptable to God) (s:sanhuai/lungkimhuai) (q:draft)
santheih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be able to accept/accept/receive) (d:<san>, accept, with <theih>, able: be able to take or receive something as good or true) (s:sangthei/sangzo) (q:draft)
sanzawk = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:higher) (d:form of <sangzaw>, <sang> high with <zaw> more, used before {mah bangin}) (a:niamzaw) (q:draft)
sap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:call/summon/invite) (d:form of <sam>, call, used before a suffix or another word: call, summon or invite a person; also call on God) (r:46.7.20) (q:draft)
sapa = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<sa>, feel or regard as, with <pa>, the man or the one who, {nuam a sapa} is the one who delights) (q:draft, low confidence)
sapfaia = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:sapphire/lapis lazuli) (d:a blue precious stone; the word is the English sapphire) (s:sapfeiros/sapfira) (q:draft)
sapfeiros = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:sapphire/lapis lazuli) (d:a blue precious stone; the word follows the Greek name of the sapphire, and the NIV often has lapis lazuli) (s:sapfaia/sapfira) (q:draft)
sapfira = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:sapphire) (d:a blue precious stone, the second foundation stone of the new Jerusalem) (s:sapfaia/sapfeiros) (q:draft)
Sapfira = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Sapphira) (d:wife of Ananias, who died after lying with him about the price of the property they sold) (r:44.5.1)
