sepzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of working/manner of work) (d:<sep>, work, with <zia>, manner) (q:draft)
serafim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seraphim/seraph) (d:heavenly beings with six wings seen by Isaiah; in the text followed by <vanmite>, heavenly beings) (q:draft)
Serah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Serah) (d:daughter of Asher, sister of Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi and Beriah) (r:4.26.46/13.7.30)
Seraiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seraiah) (d:name of several men, among them the secretary of David and the chief priest when Jerusalem fell to Babylon, father of Jehozadak) (r:13.6.14/10.8.17)
Sered = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sered) (d:son of Zebulun, ancestor of the Seredite clan) (r:1.46.14/4.26.26)
Sergius = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sergius) (d:Sergius Paulus, the Roman proconsul of Cyprus who sent for Barnabas and Saul to hear the word of God) (r:44.13.7)
Serug = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Serug) (d:son of Reu and father of Nahor, an ancestor of Abraham) (r:1.11.22)
sese = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:ever/at all) (d:adds force to a question with {bang hangin}, why: why ever, why of all things; with <loin>, without any at all) (q:draft, low confidence)
sesing = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cypress/broom tree) (d:a kind of tree; the verses use it for the cypress of Isaiah 44:14 and for the broom bush whose wood makes hot coals in Psalm 120:4) (q:draft, low confidence)
Seth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seth) (d:third son of Adam and Eve, father of Enosh) (r:1.5.6)
Sethur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sethur) (d:son of Michael, the man from the tribe of Asher sent to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.13)
sette = (i:1) (t:n) (w:machines/engines/devices) (d:plural of <set>, machine, here war machines for shooting arrows and hurling stones) (q:draft)
seu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ephah) (d:a dry measure for grain and flour, used for the Hebrew ephah; tenths of it are counted with {sehsawm suah}) (r:28.3.2) (q:draft)
seuhseuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:describes a quick repeated movement: of wine, bubbling up in the cup; of arrows, being shaken to and fro) (q:draft, low confidence)
seuhseuhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:<seuhseuh> with the suffix <in>: with a quick shaking movement, here of arrows shaken to cast lots) (b:seuhseuh) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sha = (t:see) <Sha-araim>
Sha-af = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaaph) (d:name of two men in the family of Caleb: a son of Jahdai, and a son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah, the father of Madmannah) (r:13.2.47/13.2.49) (q:draft)
Sha-alabbin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalabbin) (d:town in the territory of the tribe of Dan, also called Shaalbim) (q:draft)
Sha-albim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbim) (d:town in the territory of Dan where the Amorites held out against Israel) (r:7.1.35) (q:draft)
Sha-albon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbon) (d:home town of Eliahba, one of the mighty warriors of David; {Sha-albon khuami} is a man of Shaalbon, the Shaalbonite) (r:13.11.33/10.23.32) (q:draft)
Sha-alim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaalim) (d:district through which Saul passed when he searched for the lost donkeys of his father) (q:draft)
Sha-araim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaaraim) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah; the Philistines fled along the road from it to Gath and Ekron after Goliath was killed) (r:6.15.36/9.17.52) (q:draft)
Sha-ariam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaaraim) (d:town of the tribe of Simeon; the text spells the name {Sha-ariam}) (r:13.4.31) (q:draft)
Sha-ashgaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaashgaz) (d:eunuch of King Xerxes who had charge of the concubines) (q:draft)
Shaaf = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaaph) (d:name of two men in the family of Caleb: a son of Jahdai, and a son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah, the father of Madmannah) (r:13.2.47/13.2.49)
Shaalbim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbim) (d:town in the territory of Dan where the Amorites held out against Israel, later in one of the districts of Solomon) (r:11.4.9)
Shaalbon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbon) (d:home town of Eliahba, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.32/13.11.33)
Shaalim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaalim) (d:district through which Saul passed when he searched for the lost donkeys of his father) (r:9.9.4)
Shaaraim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaaraim) (d:name of two towns, one in the western foothills of Judah and one of the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.15.36/13.4.31)
Shaarim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shaaraim) (d:spelling of Shaaraim, the town in Judah from which the Philistines fled to Gath and Ekron after Goliath was killed) (r:9.17.52)
Shaashgaz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaashgaz) (d:eunuch of King Xerxes who had charge of the concubines) (r:17.2.14)
Shabbethai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shabbethai) (d:Levite in the time of Ezra and Nehemiah who helped explain the Law and had charge of the outside work of the house of God) (r:15.10.15/16.11.16)
Shadrak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shadrach) (d:Babylonian name of Hananiah, one of the three friends of Daniel who were thrown into the blazing furnace) (r:27.3.30/27.3.16)
Shafam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shapham) (d:a chief of the tribe of Gad in Bashan, second after Joel) (r:13.5.12)
Shafan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaphan) (d:secretary of King Josiah, son of Azaliah, who read the Book of the Law to the king; father of Ahikam and Gemariah) (r:24.26.24/12.22.3)
Shafat = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaphat) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Hori sent from the tribe of Simeon to explore Canaan and the father of the prophet Elisha) (r:4.13.5)
Shafir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaphir) (d:town named in the prophecy of Micah) (r:33.1.11)
Shagee = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shagee) (d:the Hararite, father of Jonathan, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.11.34)
shah = (t:see) <Hada-shah>
shahar = (t:see) <Zereth-shahar>
Shaharaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaharaim) (d:man of the tribe of Benjamin who had sons in Moab after he divorced his wives Hushim and Baara) (r:13.8.8)
Shahazumah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shahazumah) (d:town on the border of the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.22)
Shalisha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shalisha) (d:district near the hill country of Ephraim through which Saul passed when he searched for the lost donkeys) (r:9.9.4)
Shallekheth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shalleketh) (d:gate on the west side of the temple in Jerusalem, on the upper road) (r:13.26.16)
Shallum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shallum) (d:name of many men, among them the son of Jabesh who was king of Israel for one month and a high priest, son of Zadok) (r:13.6.12/12.15.14)
Shalma = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Salma) (d:descendant of Caleb, called the father of Bethlehem; the NIV spells the name Salma) (q:draft)
Shalmai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalmai) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:16.7.48)
Shalman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalman) (d:king who destroyed Beth Arbel in battle, named by the prophet Hosea) (r:28.10.14) (q:draft)
Shalmaneser = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalmaneser) (d:king of Assyria who attacked King Hoshea of Israel and besieged Samaria) (r:12.17.3/12.18.9)
Shalum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shallum) (d:spelling of Shallum, the name of many men, among them the father of Jehizkiah of Ephraim and a high priest, son of Zadok) (r:14.28.12/13.6.12)
Shama = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shama) (d:son of Hotham the Aroerite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.11.44) (q:draft)
Shamah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammah) (d:son of Reuel and grandson of Esau, a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.17)
Shamai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamai/Shalmai) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile; the NIV spells the name Shalmai) (r:16.7.48)
Shamaneser = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalmaneser) (d:spelling of Shalmaneser, the king of Assyria who attacked King Hoshea of Israel) (r:12.17.3)
Shamgar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamgar) (d:son of Anath, a judge of Israel who killed six hundred Philistines with an oxgoad) (r:7.3.31/7.5.6)
Shamhuth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamhuth) (d:the Izrahite, commander of the army division for the fifth month under David) (r:13.27.8)
Shamir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shamir) (d:name of a town in the hill country of Judah, of the town in Ephraim where the judge Tola was buried, and of a Levite, son of Micah) (r:6.15.48)
Shamlai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamlai/Shalmai) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile; the NIV spells the name Shalmai) (r:15.2.46)
Shamma = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamma) (d:son of Zophah in the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37) (q:draft)
Shammah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Reuel and grandson of Esau, and some of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.1.37/10.23.25)
Shammai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammai) (d:name of several men in the tribe of Judah, among them a son of Onam and a son of Rekem) (r:13.2.28/13.2.44)
Shammoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammoth) (d:the Harorite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.11.27)
Shammua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammua) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Zakkur sent from the tribe of Reuben to explore Canaan and a son of David born in Jerusalem) (r:4.13.4/13.14.4)
Shamsherai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamsherai) (d:son of Jeroham in the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.26)
Shamua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammua) (d:son of Zakkur, the man from the tribe of Reuben sent to explore Canaan; the NIV spells the name Shammua) (r:4.13.4)
shar = (t:see) <Ja-shar>
Sharai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sharai) (d:one of the men who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.40)
Sharar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sharar) (d:a Hararite, father of Ahiam, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.33)
Sharezer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sharezer) (d:son of Sennacherib king of Assyria who with his brother Adrammelek killed his father; also a man sent from Bethel to ask the priests about fasting) (r:12.19.37/23.37.38)
Sharom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Sharon) (d:spelling of Sharon, the plain where the herds of King David grazed) (r:13.27.29)
Sharon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Sharon) (d:fertile coastal plain and pasture land in Israel, known for its flowers and its herds; {Sharon gam} is the land of Sharon) (r:23.65.10) (q:draft)
Sharuhen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sharuhen) (d:town in the south of Judah given to the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.19.6)
Shashai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shashai) (d:one of the men who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.40)
Shashak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shashak) (d:a Benjamite, son of Beriah, whose sons were heads of families) (r:13.8.14/13.8.25)
Shaul = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaul) (d:name of several men, among them a king of Edom from Rehoboth on the river and a son of Simeon) (r:1.36.37/1.36.38)
Shaveh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Shaveh) (d:valley near Salem, also called the Valley of the King, where the king of Sodom met Abram; in the text {Shaveh Kuam}, the Valley of Shaveh) (r:1.14.17) (q:draft)
Shavehkiriathaim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaveh-kiriathaim/Shaveh Kiriathaim) (d:place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Emites) (r:1.14.5)
Shavehkiriathain = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaveh Kiriathaim) (d:spelling of Shaveh Kiriathaim, the place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Emites) (r:1.14.5)
Shavsha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shavsha) (d:secretary of King David) (r:13.18.16)
Shawl = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaul) (d:spelling of Shaul: a son of Simeon, ancestor of the Shaulite clan, and a king of Edom) (r:1.46.10/13.4.25)
She = (t:see) <She-erah>
She-erah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Sheerah) (d:woman of the tribe of Ephraim who built Lower and Upper Beth Horon and Uzzen Sheerah) (q:draft)
Sheal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheal) (d:descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.29) (q:draft)
Shealtiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shealtiel) (d:son of King Jehoiachin, also called Jeconiah, and father of Zerubbabel, in the family line of Jesus) (r:13.3.17/40.1.12)
Sheariah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheariah) (d:one of the six sons of Azel, a Benjamite descendant of King Saul) (r:13.8.38/13.9.44)
Shearjashub = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shear-Jashub) (d:son of the prophet Isaiah, who went with him to meet King Ahaz; the name means a remnant will return) (r:23.7.3)
Sheatiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shealtiel) (d:spelling of Shealtiel, the father of Zerubbabel) (r:37.1.12)
Sheba = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheba) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Joktan and a son of Raamah; also the land whose queen visited Solomon) (r:1.10.28/1.10.7)
Shebaniah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shebaniah) (d:name of several priests and Levites, among them men who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.4/16.10.12)
Shebarim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shebarim) (d:place near Ai as far as which the men of Ai chased the Israelites; the NIV translates it as the stone quarries) (r:6.7.5)
Shebat = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Shebat) (d:the eleventh month of the Hebrew calendar, about January to February) (r:38.1.7)
Sheber = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheber) (d:son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah) (r:13.2.48)
Shebna = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shebna) (d:high official of King Hezekiah, palace administrator and later secretary, rebuked by the prophet Isaiah) (r:12.19.2) (q:draft)
Shebnah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shebna) (d:spelling of Shebna, the secretary of King Hezekiah) (r:12.18.18)
Shebuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shubael) (d:name of two Levites: a descendant of Gershom son of Moses in charge of the treasuries, and a son of Heman the musician) (r:13.23.16/13.26.24)
Shedeur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shedeur) (d:father of Elizur, the leader of the tribe of Reuben in the wilderness) (r:4.1.5/4.7.30)
Sheerah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Sheerah) (d:woman of the tribe of Ephraim who built Lower and Upper Beth Horon and Uzzen Sheerah) (r:13.7.24)
Shefam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shepham) (d:place on the eastern boundary of the promised land, between Hazar Enan and Riblah) (r:4.34.10/4.34.11)
Shefatiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shephatiah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of David and Abital born in Hebron and a son of King Jehoshaphat) (r:10.3.4/14.21.2)
Shefelab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shefelab/western foothills) (d:spelling of <Shefelah>, the western foothills of Judah, where olive and sycamore-fig trees grew) (r:13.27.28)
Shefelah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shefelah/foothills) (d:the low hill country between the coastal plain and the hills of Judah, known for its many sycamore-fig trees) (r:14.28.18/11.10.27)
Shefer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Shepher) (d:mountain where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Kehelathah and Haradah) (r:4.33.23/4.33.24)
Shefi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shepho) (d:son of Shobal, a descendant of Seir the Horite; spelled <Shefo> in Genesis) (r:13.1.40)
Shefo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shepho) (d:son of Shobal, a descendant of Seir the Horite) (r:1.36.23)
Shefufam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shupham) (d:descendant of Benjamin, ancestor of the Shuphamite clan) (r:4.26.39)
Shefufan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shephuphan) (d:son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin) (r:13.8.5)
Shehariah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shehariah) (d:a Benjamite, son of Jeroham, head of a family living in Jerusalem) (r:13.8.26)
Sheir = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Seir) (d:spelling of Seir, the hill country of Edom, in the prophecy of Balaam) (r:4.24.18)
Shekaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shekaniah) (d:spelling of Shekaniah, the priest to whom the tenth lot fell in the time of David) (r:13.24.11)
Shekaniah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shecaniah/Shekaniah) (d:name of several men, among them a priest who returned from exile with Zerubbabel and a descendant of David) (r:13.3.21/16.12.3)
Shekaniahte = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Shekaniah) (d:the name <Shekaniah> with the plural <te>, Shekaniah and those named with him: a priest who helped distribute the offerings in the time of Hezekiah) (b:Shekaniah) (r:14.31.15)
shekel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shekel) (d:unit of weight of about eleven grams, used for weighing silver and gold and so also a unit of money; {ngun shekel} is a shekel of silver and {biakinn shekel} is the sanctuary shekel) (r:9.17.5) (q:draft)
Shekhem = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shechem) (d:son of Hamor the Hivite, who wanted to marry Dinah daughter of Jacob; also a descendant of Manasseh, son of Shemida) (r:1.34.6)
Shelah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelah) (d:son of Arphaxad and father of Eber, a descendant of Shem; also the third son of Judah) (r:13.1.18)
Shelef = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheleph) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.26)
Shelemiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelemiah) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Jehukal, a Levite gatekeeper of the East Gate, and men who had married foreign wives in the time of Ezra) (r:13.26.14) (q:draft)
Shelesh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelesh) (d:a descendant of Asher, one of four brothers named in the family list of the tribe) (r:13.7.35)
sheli = (t:see) <Eglath-sheli-shiah>
shelishiah = (t:see) <Eglath-shelishiah>
Shelom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelomi) (d:father of Ahihud, the leader of the tribe of Asher; a spelling of Shelomi) (q:draft)
Shelomi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelomi) (d:father of Ahihud, the leader of the tribe of Asher who helped divide the land of Canaan) (q:draft)
Shelomith = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Shelomith) (d:name of several people, among them the mother of a man who blasphemed in the wilderness, a daughter of Zerubbabel, and a child of King Rehoboam) (r:3.24.11/15.8.10)
Shelomoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelomoth) (d:name of several Levites, among them a son of Shimei and the chief of the descendants of Izhar) (r:13.23.9/13.24.22)
Shelumiel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelumiel) (d:son of Zurishaddai, the leader of the tribe of Simeon in the wilderness) (r:4.1.6/4.10.19)
Shem = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shem) (d:one of the three sons of Noah, ancestor of Abraham and of the Semitic peoples) (r:1.6.10)
Shema = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shema) (d:town in the south of Judah; also the name of several men, among them a son of Hebron and a Benjamite family head of Aijalon) (r:6.15.26)
Shemaah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaah) (d:a man of Gibeah, father of Ahiezer and Joash, warriors who joined David) (r:13.12.3)
Shemai = (t:see) <Shemai-ah>
Shemai-ah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaiah) (d:Shemaiah the Nehelamite, a false prophet among the exiles in Babylon in the time of Jeremiah) (r:24.29.31) (q:draft)
Shemaiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaiah) (d:name of many men, among them a son of Joel of the tribe of Reuben and priests and Levites after the exile) (r:16.12.6/16.12.34)
Shemakhiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Semakiah) (d:a Levite gatekeeper, an able man of the family of Obed-Edom) (r:13.26.7)
Shemariah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemariah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of King Rehoboam and men who had married foreign wives in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.41/15.10.32)
Shemeber = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shemeber) (d:king of Zeboyim, one of the five kings attacked by Kedorlaomer and his allies in the time of Abram) (r:1.14.2)
Shemed = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemed) (d:a Benjamite, son of Elpaal, who built Ono and Lod) (r:13.8.12)
Shemer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemer) (d:owner of the hill of Samaria, which King Omri bought and named after him; also a Levite ancestor in the family of Merari) (r:11.16.24/13.6.46)
Shemiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaiah) (d:spelling of Shemaiah, the father of Delaiah, an official of King Jehoiakim) (r:24.36.12)
Shemida = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemida) (d:descendant of Manasseh, ancestor of the Shemidaite clan) (r:13.7.19/4.26.32)
Shemirahmoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemiramoth) (d:spelling of Shemiramoth, a Levite sent by King Jehoshaphat to teach in the towns of Judah) (r:14.17.8)
Shemiramoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemiramoth) (d:Levite musician who played the lyre when David brought the ark to Jerusalem) (r:13.15.20/13.15.18)
Shemuel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemuel) (d:son of Ammihud, the leader of the tribe of Simeon who helped divide the land of Canaan; also a son of Tola of the tribe of Issachar) (r:4.34.20/13.7.2)
Shenazzar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shenazzar) (d:son of King Jehoiachin, also called Jeconiah) (r:13.3.18)
Sheol = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Sheol/realm of the dead) (d:the realm of the dead, the grave; in the text {Sihna gam Sheol}, Sheol the land of death) (r:32.2.2)
Sheraiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheariah) (d:spelling of Sheariah, one of the six sons of Azel, a Benjamite) (r:13.9.44)
Sherebiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sherebiah) (d:name of Levites, among them a leader who came with Ezra and one who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:15.8.24/16.10.12)
Sheresh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheresh) (d:son of Makir and Maakah, grandson of Manasseh) (r:13.7.16)
Sheshai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheshai) (d:one of the three descendants of Anak living in Hebron, driven out by Caleb) (r:6.15.14)
Sheshan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheshan) (d:descendant of Jerahmeel of Judah who had no sons and gave his daughter in marriage to his Egyptian servant Jarha) (r:13.2.31/13.2.35)
Sheshbazzar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheshbazzar) (d:prince of Judah to whom Cyrus gave the temple articles, who laid the foundations of the temple in Jerusalem) (r:15.1.8/15.5.16)
Sheth = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Sheth) (d:in the prophecy of Balaam, {Sheth suante} is the descendants or people of Sheth, named together with Moab) (r:4.24.17) (q:draft)
Shethar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shethar) (d:one of the seven nobles of Persia and Media closest to King Xerxes) (r:17.1.14) (q:draft)
Shetharbozenai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shethar-Bozenai) (d:Persian official west of the Euphrates who with Tattenai wrote to King Darius about the rebuilding of the temple) (r:15.5.6/15.6.13)
Shethelah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuthelah) (d:spelling of Shuthelah, son of Ephraim) (r:13.7.20)
Shethur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sethur) (d:son of Michael, the man from the tribe of Asher sent to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.4)
Sheva = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheva) (d:secretary of King David; also a son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah, founder of Makbenah and Gibea) (r:13.2.49/10.20.25)
shiah = (t:see) <Eglath-sheli-shiah>
Shibab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobab) (d:spelling of Shobab, a son of David and Bathsheba born in Jerusalem) (r:13.3.5)
Shibah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:well) (w:Shibah) (d:well dug by the servants of Isaac, after which the town of Beersheba was named) (r:1.26.33) We have found water.
Shibboleth = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Shibboleth) (d:word that the men of Gilead made the fleeing Ephraimites say at the fords of the Jordan; those who said Sibboleth were killed) (r:7.12.6)
Shifeam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimeam) (d:spelling of Shimeam, son of Mikloth, a Benjamite living in Jerusalem) (r:13.9.38)
Shifi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shiphi) (d:a Simeonite, father of Ziza) (r:13.4.37)
Shifmoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shifmoth) (d:home of Zabdi, who was in charge of the produce of the vineyards of King David; the NIV calls him the Shiphmite) (r:13.27.27)
Shifrah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shiphrah) (d:one of the two Hebrew midwives in Egypt, named with Puah) (r:2.1.15)
Shiftan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shiphtan) (d:father of Kemuel, the leader of the tribe of Ephraim who helped divide the land of Canaan) (r:4.34.24)
Shihor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Shihor) (d:river on the eastern border of Egypt, named as the southern limit of the land of Israel) (r:13.13.5/6.13.3)
Shihorlibnath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shihor Libnath) (d:place on the western boundary of the territory of Asher, near Carmel) (r:6.19.26)
Shikkeron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shikkeron) (d:town on the northern boundary of Judah, between Ekron and Mount Baalah) (r:6.15.11)
Shilhi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shilhi) (d:the father of Azubah, the mother of King Jehoshaphat) (r:14.20.31) (q:draft)
Shilhim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shilhim) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.32)
Shillem = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shillem) (d:son of Naphtali, ancestor of the Shillemite clan) (r:1.46.24/4.26.49)
Shiloah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shiloah) (d:gently flowing stream in Jerusalem, also called Siloam) (r:23.8.6)
Shiloh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shiloh) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim where the tabernacle stood in the days of Joshua, the judges and Samuel) (r:9.4.12) (q:draft)
Shiloni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Shilonite) (d:person from Shiloh, said of the prophet Ahijah; {Shiloni mi} is the Shilonite) (r:11.15.29/11.12.15)
Shilshah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shilshah) (d:son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37)
Shimea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimea) (d:name of several men, among them the third son of Jesse and brother of David, and a Levite of the family of Merari) (r:13.2.13/13.20.7) (q:draft)
Shimeah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimeah) (d:name of two men: a brother of David and father of Jonadab, and a Benjaminite, son of Mikloth) (r:10.13.3/13.8.32)
Shimeath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shimeath) (d:Ammonite woman, mother of one of the officials who killed King Joash; {Shimeath mite} are the Shimeathites, a clan of scribes) (r:12.12.21)
Shimei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimei) (d:name of many men, among them the son of Gera who cursed David, and a governor of Solomon in Benjamin) (r:11.4.18)
Shimeon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimeon) (d:descendant of Harim who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.31)
Shimon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimon) (d:man of the tribe of Judah, father of Amnon, Rinnah, Ben-Hanan and Tilon) (r:13.4.20) (q:draft)
Shimrath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimrath) (d:Benjaminite, son of Shimei) (r:13.8.21)
Shimri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimri) (d:name of several men, among them a Simeonite, the father of one of David’s warriors, and a Levite in the time of Hezekiah) (r:13.4.37/13.11.45)
Shimrith = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shimrith) (d:Moabite woman, mother of Jehozabad, one of the men who killed King Joash) (r:14.24.26)
Shimron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimron) (d:son of Issachar, ancestor of the Shimronite clan; also a town in the territory of Zebulun) (r:1.46.13/13.7.1)
Shimronmeron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shimron Meron) (d:Canaanite royal city whose king was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.12.20)
Shimshai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimshai) (d:secretary who wrote with Rehum to King Artaxerxes against the rebuilding of Jerusalem) (r:15.4.8/15.4.9)
Shinab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shinab) (d:king of Admah in the time of Abraham) (r:1.14.2)
Shinar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shinar) (d:the land of Babylonia, the plain where Babylon, Uruk and Akkad lay) (r:1.11.2/1.10.10)
Shion = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shion) (d:town in the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.19)
Shisha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shisha) (d:father of Elihoreph and Ahijah, the secretaries of King Solomon) (r:11.4.3)
Shishak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shishak) (d:king of Egypt who sheltered Jeroboam and attacked Jerusalem in the time of Rehoboam) (r:11.11.40/11.14.25)
Shitrai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shitrai) (d:man of Sharon in charge of the herds of King David grazing in Sharon) (r:13.27.29)
Shitthim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Shittim) (d:valley of the acacia trees, watered by the stream from the house of the Lord in Joel 3:18) (r:29.3.18)
Shittim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shittim) (d:place in the plains of Moab east of the Jordan, the last camp of Israel before crossing the river) (r:4.25.1/6.3.1)
Shiza = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shiza) (d:Reubenite, father of Adina, one of David’s warriors) (r:13.11.42)
Shoa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Shoa) (d:people named with Pekod and Koa among the allies of Babylon) (r:26.23.23)
Shobab = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobab) (d:name of two men: a son of David born in Jerusalem, and a son of Caleb son of Hezron) (r:13.2.18/10.5.14)
Shobai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobai) (d:head of a family of temple gatekeepers who returned from exile) (r:15.2.42/16.7.45)
Shobak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobak) (d:commander of the army of Hadadezer king of Zobah, killed in battle against David; called Shophak in 1 Chronicles) (r:10.10.16/10.10.18)
Shobal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobal) (d:name of two men: a son of Seir the Horite and chief in Edom, and a descendant of Judah) (r:1.36.20/13.4.1)
Shobek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobek) (d:one of the leaders who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.24)
Shobi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobi) (d:son of Nahash, from Rabbah of the Ammonites, who brought supplies to David at Mahanaim) (r:10.17.27)
Shofak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shophak) (d:commander of the army of Hadadezer, killed in battle against David; called Shobak in 2 Samuel) (r:13.19.18/13.19.16)
shofan = (t:see) <Atoroth-shofan>
Shoham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shoham) (d:Levite of the family of Merari, son of Jaaziah) (r:13.24.27)
Shomer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shomer) (d:name of two men: a son of Heber of the tribe of Asher, and the parent of Jehozabad who killed King Joash) (r:13.7.32/13.7.34)
Shua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shua) (d:a Canaanite man, father of the wife of Judah) (r:1.38.12) (q:draft)
Shua = (i:2) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shua) (d:daughter of Heber, sister of Japhlet, Shomer and Hotham) (r:13.7.32) (q:draft)
Shuah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuah) (d:son of Abraham and Keturah; {Shuah gammi} is the Shuhite, said of Bildad the friend of Job) (r:1.25.2)
Shual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shual) (d:a descendant of Asher, in the list of the sons of Zophah) (q:draft)
Shual = (i:2) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shual) (d:{Shual gam}, the district of Shual near Ophrah) (q:draft)
Shubael = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shubael) (d:name of two Levites: a descendant of Amram, and a son of Heman who was a temple musician) (r:13.24.20)
Shuhah = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Shuhah) (d:relative of Kelub in the genealogy of Judah) (r:13.4.11)
Shuham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuham) (d:son of Dan, ancestor of the Shuhamite clan) (r:4.26.42)
Shulam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shulam/Shulammite) (d:home of the young woman of the Song of Songs; {Shulam numei} is the Shulammite) (r:22.6.13)
Shullam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shallum) (d:uncle of Jeremiah; the text spells the name {Shullam}) (q:draft)
Shumath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Shumathite) (d:one of the clans of Kiriath Jearim, descended from Caleb) (r:13.2.53)
Shunem = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shunem) (d:town in the territory of Issachar, where the Philistines camped before the battle of Gilboa; home of Abishag) (r:6.19.18/11.2.21)
Shuni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuni) (d:son of Gad, ancestor of the Shunite clan) (r:1.46.16/4.26.15)
Shuppim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuppim) (d:name of a Benjaminite and of a Levite gatekeeper in the time of David) (r:13.26.16)
Shur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shur) (d:desert region on the north-eastern border of Egypt) (r:9.15.7) (q:draft)
Shuthelah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuthelah) (d:son of Ephraim, ancestor of the Shuthelahite clan) (r:13.7.20/4.26.35)
si = (i:2) (t:n) (w:blood) (d:blood, a short form of <sisan>, used mostly of the blood of a sacrifice) (s:sisan)
Si = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:dead) (d:<si>, dead, written with a capital in the name {Si Tuipi}, the Dead Sea) (b:si) (q:draft)
sia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sir) (d:respectful word used in speaking to a man, as in {sia aw})
sia = (i:3) (t:n) (w:evil) (d:what is bad or wrong, the opposite of <pha>, good; {a sia gamta} is do evil) (s:siatna) (a:phatna)
sia = (i:4) (t:n) (w:damage) (d:harm done to a thing so that it is spoiled or worn out; {sia lo} is undamaged) (s:kisia)
sia = (i:5) (t:n) (w:ruin) (d:the state of being destroyed, said of cities, houses and peoples) (s:siatna)
Sia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Teacher/teacher) (d:<sia>, teacher, written with a capital as a title or a form of address; {Sia aw} is Teacher, said to the person spoken to) (s:Siapa/Rabbi) (b:sia) (q:draft)
Sia = (i:2) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sia) (d:head of a family of temple servants who returned from exile, called Siaha in Ezra 2:44) (q:draft)
sia-hil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sign/portent/wonder) (d:a person or thing that others look on with wonder or as a warning) (s:siahil) (q:draft, low confidence)
siacimit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish/be destroyed/come to an end) (d:be ruined so as to be no more) (s:siamang) (q:draft, low confidence)
siacimitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:ruin utterly/destroy completely) (d:<siacimit>, be utterly ruined, with the causative <sak>: bring to complete ruin) (s:susiamang/siasakmang) (b:siacimit) (q:draft)
siacip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ruined/perish/be destroyed completely) (d:<sia>, be ruined, with <cip>, completely; also cried out as a ruin, a ruin) (s:siamang/siagawp) (b:sia) (r:26.21.27) (q:draft)
siacipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lie in ruins/be desolate) (d:<siacip>, be utterly ruined, with the linking ending <in>; {a siacipin om} is lie in ruins) (b:siacip) (q:draft)
siagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ruined/lie in ruins/be spoiled) (d:<sia>, be spoiled, with <gawp>, severely: be badly damaged or brought to ruin) (s:siacip) (b:sia) (q:draft)
siagawppah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:collapse at once/be ruined immediately) (d:<siagawp>, be ruined, with <pah>, at once) (b:siagawp) (q:draft)
siah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tribute/tax) (d:payment required by a ruler; {siah pia} is pay tax and {siah puak} is bring tribute) (s:mangmu) (q:draft)
siah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:set a trap/lay a snare/ensnare) (d:set a trap or net for someone, mostly with <thang>, trap, as in {thang siah}) (s:thangsiah) (q:draft, low confidence)
Siaha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Siaha) (d:head of a family of temple servants who returned from exile, called Sia in Nehemiah 7:47) (r:15.2.44) (q:draft)
siahah = (t:todo) (q:draft, in {tua ban siahah}, Numbers 32.19, apparently on the far side or beyond, NIV on the other side of the Jordan; the word <siah> here is not clear)
siahdon = (t:see) <siahdon'na>
siahdon'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tax collection/collecting of taxes) (d:<siah>, tax, with <don>, collect, and the noun suffix <na>; {siahdonna buk} is the booth where taxes are collected) (s:siahdonna) (q:draft)
siahdong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tax collector/publican) (d:<siah>, tax, with <dong>, ask or demand: one who collects taxes) (s:siahdongpa) (q:draft)
siahdongpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tax collector/publican) (d:<siahdong>, tax collector, with <pa>, marking a man: a man who collects taxes) (s:siahdong) (b:siahdong) (q:draft)
siahdongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tax collectors/publicans) (d:<siahdong>, tax collector, with the plural <te>) (s:siahkhawmte) (b:siahdong) (r:42.19.2) (q:draft)
siahdonna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tax collecting/collection of taxes) (d:<siah>, tax, and <don>, collect, with the noun suffix <na>; {siahdonna zum} is the tax office) (s:siahdon'na) (q:draft)
siahil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:portent/omen/warning sign) (d:something that serves as a sign or warning to others, used beside <lim>, sign) (s:sia-hil) (q:draft)
siahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:setting a trap/ensnaring) (d:<siah>, set a trap, with the linking ending <in>; {thang siahin}, laying a snare) (s:thangsiahin) (b:siah) (q:draft)
siahin = (i:2) (t:n) (w:as tax/as tribute) (d:<siah>, tax, with the marker <in>, as; {siahin pia}, pay as tax) (b:siah) (q:draft)
siahkhawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tax collectors/revenue collectors) (d:<siah>, tax or tribute, with <khawm>, gather, and plural <te>: those who collect the tribute) (s:siahdongte) (q:draft)
siahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trapping/trap/snare) (d:<siah>, set a trap, with the noun suffix <na>: trapping or the thing used to trap; {ngasa siahna sikkawi} is a fishhook) (s:thangsiahna) (b:siah) (q:draft)
siahsim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set a trap secretly/lay a hidden snare) (d:<siah>, set a trap, with <sim>, secretly) (q:draft)
siahsimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hidden trap/hidden snare) (d:<siahsim>, set a trap secretly, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:siahsim) (q:draft)
siahsun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:present tribute/offer tribute) (d:<siah>, tribute, with <sun>: hand over the tribute to a ruler) (q:draft, low confidence)
siahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:taxes/revenues/tribute) (d:<siah>, tax, with plural <te>) (b:siah) (q:draft)
siahuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wicked/vile/heinous/terrible) (d:<sia>, bad, with <huai>, worthy of: very bad, mostly of conduct or of a person; {siahuai zaw} is worse) (s:gilo) (a:hoih) (q:draft)
siahuaite = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wicked/evil) (d:<siahuai>, wicked, with the plural <te>; {mi siahuaite} is evildoers, wicked people) (s:gilote) (a:hoihte) (b:siahuai) (q:draft)
siahuaizaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:worse/more terrible/more evil) (d:<siahuai>, wicked or terrible, with the comparative <zaw>; the thing compared takes <sangin>, than) (s:siazaw) (a:hoihzaw/phazaw) (b:siahuai) (q:draft)
siakhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish together/be ruined together) (d:<sia>, be ruined, with <khawm>, together) (s:beikhawm) (b:sia) (q:draft)
siakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spit out) (d:put out of the mouth, with <khia>, out) (s:luakhia) (a:valh) (q:draft)
siakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be corrupted/be already spoiled) (d:<sia>, be bad or spoiled, with <khin>, already) (q:draft)
siakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wipe out/destroy/root out) (d:remove completely from a place, with <khia>, out) (s:susiamang) (q:draft)
siakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wipe out/destroy) (d:form of <siakkhia> used before <dongin> and other linking words; {a siakkhiat dongin}, until he had wiped them out) (b:siakkhia) (q:draft)
siakmit = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ankle) (q:draft)
siakmitte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ankles) (d:<siakmit>, ankle, with the plural <te>: the ankles) (b:siakmit) (q:draft)
siaksiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:wipe out/destroy completely) (d:<siak> as in <siakkhia>, wipe out, with <siang>, clean: clear away people and animals so that none is left) (s:susiamang) (q:draft, low confidence)
sial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prepare/make ready/clear) (d:clear or make ready a road for someone who is coming; {Topa paina lam sial} is prepare the way for the Lord) (r:40.3.3) (q:draft)
sial = (i:2) (t:v) (w:lay/lay down/place) (d:lay a person or a body down on a bed, in a manger or in a tomb) (s:lumsak) (q:draft)
sial = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:raw/uncooked) (d:of meat, grain or dough, not cooked; {sa sial} is raw meat and {annel sial} is unbaked dough) (a:minsa/huansa) (r:2.12.9) (q:draft)
sialam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil/the bad side) (d:<sia>, bad, with <lam>, side or direction: what is bad; {a sialam bekbek ngaihsutna}, thinking only evil, is malice) (q:draft)
sialamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:badly/evilly/unfavourably) (d:<sialam>, the bad side, with <in>: in a bad way, as think evil or give a bad report) (a:hoihlamin) (b:sialam) (q:draft)
sialh = (t:see) <kima-sialh>
sialin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:every/whenever/each time) (d:placed after a time word or a verb: {zan sialin}, every night, all night; {ka sap sialin}, every time I call) (s:hunhunin) (b:sial) (q:draft)
sialin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:laying/placing/putting) (d:<sial>, lay down, with the linking ending <in>, joining it to the next verb) (b:sial) (q:draft)
sialo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:not bad/not evil) (d:<sia>, bad, with the negative <lo>; {a gamtat a sialo}, one whose conduct is not bad) (b:sia) (q:draft)
sialo = (i:2) (t:v) (w:not wear out/not be spoiled) (d:<sia>, be ruined, with the negative <lo>, said of clothes) (b:sia) (q:draft)
sialomtangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:heap of ruins/ruins) (d:things that lie ruined in heaps; with the plural <te>) (q:draft, low confidence)
sialpai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lay down/lay low) (d:<sial>, lay down, with <pai>: lay someone down in the dust) (q:draft, low confidence)
sialsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prepare a way for/clear for) (d:<sial>, clear or make ready a road, with <sak>: make a path for someone or something) (b:sial) (q:draft)
sialsial = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:placed after <luang>, flow, it describes water running in a steady stream) (q:draft, low confidence)
sialtalling = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:thistle/thornbush) (d:a thorny wild plant) (s:thangling/kiak) (q:draft)
sialun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:whenever/every time) (d:placed after a verb, with the plural <un>: each time that they do something) (s:simun) (q:draft)
siam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:skilled/expert/skillful) (d:good at something, placed after the skill or action named) (s:khutsiam) (q:draft)
siam = (i:2) (t:v) (w:grant/bless) (d:of God, grant or enable someone to do or see something) (q:draft, low confidence)
siamaimang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish utterly/be completely destroyed) (d:<sia>, be ruined, with <maimang>, vanish completely) (s:siamang/kisusiamang) (q:draft)
siamang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish/be destroyed/be ruined) (d:come to complete ruin and be no more) (s:mangthang/maimang/beimang) (q:draft)
siamangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy/annihilate) (d:<siamang>, perish, with the causative <sak>) (s:susiamang/beimangsak/maimangsak) (b:siamang) (q:draft)
siambu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:loom) (d:the frame on which cloth is woven) (q:draft)
siamgante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weaver/weavers) (d:one who weaves cloth, from {siam gan} weave, with <te> for the people who do it) (s:gante) (q:draft)
siamgat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weaving) (d:the weaving of cloth; {siamgat siamte}, skilled weavers) (s:gatna) (q:draft)
siamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:skillfully/well/ably) (d:<siam> with <in>; {thugen siamin} is being good at speaking) (b:siam) (q:draft)
siamin = (i:2) (t:n) (w:web/loom) (d:<siam> the weaving on a loom, with <in>: into the web, with the loom) (q:draft, low confidence)
siamkhau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:loom threads/web) (d:the threads stretched on a loom for weaving, from <siam>, loom or weaving, and <khau>, cord) (q:draft, low confidence)
siamlawngpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:weaver's beam/weaver's rod) (d:the large beam of a loom, used as a picture of a very thick spear shaft) (q:draft)
siamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:skill/ability/understanding) (d:<siam>, skilled, with the noun suffix <na>: the skill or ability to do something well; {ngaihsut siamna} is understanding and {sumbawl siamna} is skill in trading) (s:khutsiamna) (b:siam) (r:2.35.10) (q:draft)
siamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:skills/abilities/gifts/arts) (d:plural of <siamna>; with {Kha Siangtho}, gifts of the Spirit; with <mitphial> or <aisan>, magic arts) (b:siamna) (q:draft)
siamneelte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:craftsmen/skilled workers/artisans) (d:<siam>, skilled, with <neel> and plural <te>) (s:khutsiamte) (q:draft)
siampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:skilled man/expert) (d:after a verb or noun, a man who is skilled at it, <pa> marks a man; {thugen siampa}, the Teacher or Preacher; {lasakna a tum siampa}, the harpist) (s:misiam) (b:siam) (q:draft)
Siampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Teacher/Preacher) (d:<siampa>, a skilled man, written with a capital in {Thugen Siampa}, the Teacher or Preacher of Ecclesiastes) (b:siampa) (q:draft)
siampi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophet)
siampi = (i:2) (t:n) (w:priest) (d:a person set apart to offer sacrifices and serve God on behalf of the people; {siampi liante} are the chief priests and {siampi ukpa} is the high priest) (s:siampipa)
Siampi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Priest/priest) (d:<siampi> written with a capital as a title before a name or in {Siampi Ukpa}, the High Priest) (b:siampi) (r:11.1.26) (q:draft)
siampipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:priest) (d:<siampi>, priest, with <pa> marking a man: the priest who carries out a duty) (s:siampi/tulpipa) (b:siampi) (q:draft)
Siampipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:priest) (d:<siampi> priest with <pa> marking a man, written with a capital in {a tawntung Siampipa}, a priest forever) (b:siampipa) (r:58.7.17) (q:draft)
siampipih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fellow priest/associate) (d:<siampi>, priest, with <pih>, fellow or companion) (b:siampi) (q:draft)
siampipihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fellow priests) (d:<siampipih>, fellow priest, with plural <te>) (b:siampipih) (q:draft)
siampipuan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ephod) (d:the sacred garment of the priest, from <siampi>, priest, and <puan>, cloth) (q:draft)
siampipuante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ephod) (d:<siampipuan>, ephod, with <te>; in the verse {siampipuante’ puankhau} is the waistband of the ephod) (b:siampipuan) (q:draft, low confidence)
siampite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophets) (b:siampi) plural form of <siampi>
siampte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:priests) (d:apparently a misprint of <siampite>, priests) (q:draft, low confidence)
siamsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:trained/already skilled) (d:<siam>, skilled, with <sa>, already: having become skilled through learning) (b:siam) (q:draft)
siamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:experts/skilled ones) (d:those skilled in something, <siam> with plural <te>; {mitphial siamte} are magicians, {aksi et siamte} are readers of the stars) (b:siam) (q:draft)
siamzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more skilled/more able) (d:<siam>, skilled, with the comparative <zaw>) (b:siam) (q:draft)
siamzawk = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more skilled/better) (d:form of <siamzaw>, more skilled, used before <lam> and <na>) (b:siamzaw) (q:draft)
siamzawklam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being more skilled/superiority in skill) (d:<siamzawk>, more skilled, with <lam>: the fact or extent of being more skilled) (q:draft)
sian = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be clean/be pure) (d:form of <siang> clean, written {sian’} before <nading> and in {sian’suah} and {sian’sak}, which mean purify or cleanse) (r:16.12.30) (q:draft)
sian'thona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holiness/purity/sanctification) (d:shortened spelling of <siangthona>, the state of being holy or pure) (s:siangthona/sianthona) (a:kihhuaina) (q:draft)
sian'thosakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sanctification/making holy) (d:{sian'tho}, a short form of <siangtho>, holy, with the causative <sak> and the noun suffix <na>) (s:sianthosakna) (q:draft)
sian'thosaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:consecrated/made holy) (d:spelling of <siangthosak>, make holy, with <sa>, already) (s:sianthosaksa) (q:draft)
siangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:clean/cleanly/clearly) (d:<siang>, clean, with the ending {-in}; after a verb it gives the result, as {kiphiat siangin}, swept clean, and {hah siangin}, clearing away) (a:ninin) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purge/cleanse away/remove) (d:<siang>, clean, with <khia>, out, and the causative <sak>: clear something evil out from among people) (q:draft)
siangkhiasakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:driving out/clearing away) (d:<siang>, clean, with <khia>, out, the causative <sak> and the linking suffix <in>: clear a people out of a land) (q:draft)
siangkhin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:clean/cleansed) (d:<siang>, clean, with <khin>, already or completely: already made clean) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become clean again/be clean again) (d:<siang>, clean, with <kik>, again) (s:siankik) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cleansing/cleanness) (d:<siang>, clean, with the noun suffix <na>; {sawp siangna}, washing clean; {bei siangna}, a complete end) (s:siansakna) (a:nitna/ninna) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:purest/most pure) (d:<siang>, pure, with the superlative <pen>; {kham siangpen} is pure or solid gold) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangpente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:most sacred things/most holy things) (d:<siangpen>, most clean or sacred, with plural <te>; {biakna an siangpente} is the most sacred food of the offerings) (s:siangthopente) (b:siangpen) (q:draft)
siangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cleanse/purify/make clean/purge) (d:<siang>, clean, with the causative <sak>: make a person, a place or a thing clean, from dirt, from ritual uncleanness or from sin) (s:siansak/siansuah) (a:ninsak/nitsak) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cleansing/purifying/making clean) (d:<siangsak> with the linking suffix <in>: cleansing, and then) (s:siansuahin) (b:siangsak) (q:draft)
siangsakkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making clean again/making fresh) (d:<siangsak>, make clean, with <kik>, again, and the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft)
siangsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:purifier/refiner) (d:<siangsak>, purify, with <pa> marking a man: one who purifies) (b:siangsak) (q:draft)
siangsakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to cleanse/can take away) (d:<siangsak>, cleanse, with <zo>, be able) (b:siangsak) (q:draft)
siangtak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:pure/sincere/wholesome) (d:<siang>, pure, with <tak>, truly) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:clearly/plainly/openly) (d:<siang>, clean or clear, with <takin>, which makes an adverb) (s:teltakin/kiteltakin) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:clean/pure) (d:<siang> with plural <te>: those that are clean or pure, of animals that may be eaten, people who are ritually clean, and pure gold) (b:siang) (q:draft)
siangtho = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:holy/sacred) (d:set apart for God and belonging to him; said of God himself, his Spirit, his people, and of places, days and things) (a:mawkmawk)
siangtho = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:clean/pure) (d:free from dirt or from ritual uncleanness, said of animals that may be eaten or offered, of places and of people) (s:siang) (a:nin)
Siangtho = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:holy) (d:written with a capital in {Kha Siangtho} the Holy Spirit and {Lai Siangtho} the Holy Scripture) (b:siangtho) (r:45.3.10) (q:draft)
siangthoin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:holily/in holiness/purely) (d:<siangtho> holy or clean, with <in>: in a holy or pure way, as holy) (b:siangtho) (q:draft)
siangthona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holiness/sanctification) (d:<siangtho>, holy, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being holy, or of having been made holy) (s:sianthona/sian'thona) (b:siangtho) (r:19.93.5) (q:draft)
Siangthona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holiness) (d:{Siangthona Mun}, the place of holiness, is the Most Holy Place) (b:siangthona) (q:draft)
siangthonate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holiness) (d:<siangthona> holiness, with the plural <te>) (b:siangthona) (q:draft)
siangthopa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holy one/holy man) (d:<siangtho> holy, with <pa>, a male person) (s:misiangtho) (b:siangtho) (q:draft)
siangthopen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:most holy/holiest) (d:<siangtho>, holy, with superlative <pen>) (b:siangtho) (r:3.7.1) (q:draft)
Siangthopen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:Most Holy/holiest) (d:<siangthopen> written with a capital in {Siangthopen Mun}, the Most Holy Place of the temple) (b:siangthopen) (q:draft)
siangthopente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:most holy things/most holy offerings) (d:<siangthopen>, most holy, with plural <te>) (s:siangpente) (b:siangthopen) (q:draft)
siangthosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make it holy/make holy/sanctify/consecrate) (d:<siangtho>, holy, with the causative <sak>: set a person, a day or a thing apart as holy to God) (s:sianthosak/siansuah) (a:daisak) (b:siangtho)
siangthosak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:make it clean/make clean/cleanse/purify) (d:<siangtho>, clean, with the causative <sak>: make a person or a thing ritually clean) (s:siangsak/siansak) (a:ninsak) (b:siangtho)
siangthosakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sanctify/consecrate/make holy/purify) (d:<siangthosak> with the ending <in>, which links to the next verb or, at the end of a sentence, gives a command) (s:siansuahin) (b:siangthosak) (q:draft)
siangthosakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sanctifier/one who makes holy) (d:the one who makes holy, said of the Lord; <pa> marks a male person) (b:siangthosak) (r:3.21.15) (q:draft)
siangthota = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:clean) (d:<siangtho> clean, holy, with <ta> showing a state now reached; already clean) (b:siangtho) (q:draft)
siangthote = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:holy/sacred/clean) (d:plural form after a plural noun, as in {mi siangthote}, holy people or saints, and {ganhing siangthote}, clean animals) (b:siangtho) (q:draft)
siangthozaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:holier/more holy) (d:<siangtho> holy, with the comparative <zaw>) (b:siangtho) (q:draft)
siangthozo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be pure/be able to be holy) (d:<siangtho> pure, holy, with <zo> be able) (b:siangtho) (q:draft)
siankik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become clean again) (d:<sian> be clean, with <kik> again; be cleared of guilt) (s:siangkik) (b:sian) (q:draft)
siansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purify/cleanse/make clean) (d:<sian> be clean with <sak>, cause; in Deuteronomy 1.12 used of clearing up disputes) (s:siangsak/siansuah) (a:ninsak/nitsak) (b:sian) (r:58.1.3) (q:draft)
siansakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cleanse again/make clean again) (d:<siansak> make clean, with <kik> again) (b:siansak) (q:draft)
siansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cleansing/purification) (d:<siansak> make clean, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:siansuahna) (b:siansak) (q:draft)
siansuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purify/consecrate/make holy) (d:make a person, place or thing ritually clean and set apart for God) (s:siansak/siangsak/sianthosak) (a:ninsak) (r:14.29.17) (q:draft)
siansuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:purifying/cleansing) (d:<siansuah> make clean, with <in> linking to the following verb; purifying) (s:siangsakin) (b:siansuah) (q:draft)
siansuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:purification/cleansing/atonement) (d:act or rite of making something ritually clean or holy) (s:siansakna/kisiansuahna) (b:siansuah) (q:draft)
siantheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be cleared/can be settled) (d:<sian> be clean, with <theih> can; of a dispute, be able to be cleared up) (b:sian) (q:draft, low confidence)
siantho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be holy/be clean/be pure) (d:form of <siangtho>, holy or clean, used before <nading> and in <sianthosak>: become clean or pure) (q:draft)
sianthona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holiness/purity/cleanness) (d:<siantho>, a short form of <siangtho>, holy, with the noun suffix <na>: holiness, purity) (s:siangthona/sian'thona) (a:nitna/ninna) (b:siantho) (q:draft)
sianthosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make holy/sanctify/consecrate) (d:<siantho>, a short form of <siangtho>, holy, with the causative <sak>: make holy, set apart for God, or treat as holy) (s:siangthosak/siansuah) (a:ninsak/nitsak) (b:siantho) (q:draft)
sianthosakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sanctification/making holy/purification) (d:<sianthosak>, make holy, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:sian'thosakna/siansuahna) (a:nitsakna) (b:sianthosak) (q:draft)
sianthosaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:consecrated/sanctified) (d:<sianthosak> make holy, with <sa> already done) (s:sian'thosaksa/apsa) (b:sianthosak) (q:draft)
siapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teacher/master) (d:a male teacher, <pa> marks a man; {thukham siapa} is an expert in the law) (s:sia/thuhilhpa/hilhpa) (a:nungzui) (b:sia) (q:draft)
Siapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Teacher/Master) (d:<siapa>, teacher, capitalised as a title for Jesus) (s:Rabbi) (b:siapa) (q:draft)
siapi = (t:see) <siapi-in>
siapi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in ruins/in a ruined state) (d:<sia>, be ruined, with <pi-in>, while still in that state) (q:draft, low confidence)
siasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:ruined/destroyed) (d:<sia>, be ruined, with <sa>, already: ruined, lying in ruins; {a siasa-in om} is lie in ruins) (s:kisiasa/kisusiasa/suksiatsa) (q:draft)
siasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy/ruin/spoil) (d:<sia>, be ruined, with the causative <sak>: bring a person, a city or someone’s faith to ruin) (s:susia/siatsak/suksiat) (a:puah/puahkik/lamkik) (b:sia) (r:20.29.4) (q:draft)
siasakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy/ruin/bring down) (d:<siasak>, destroy, with the linking ending <in>: destroying, used when another action follows) (b:siasak) (q:draft)
siasakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy completely/ruin utterly) (d:<siasak> destroy, with <mang> away, completely) (s:susiamang/suksiatmang) (q:draft)
siasakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who foils/one who ruins) (d:<siasak> destroy, spoil, with <pa> marking a male doer) (b:siasak) (q:draft)
siasakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:destroyers/those who lay waste) (d:<siasak>, destroy, with plural <te>: those who destroy) (s:susiate/suksiatsakte) (a:lamte) (b:siasak) (q:draft)
siasate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ruins/ruined places) (d:<siasa>, ruined, with plural <te>) (s:kisiamaisate) (b:siasa) (q:draft)
siat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be ruined/perish) (d:form of <sia> used before a suffix or another word, {siat nading} is the ruin or harm of someone) (s:siamang/siacip) (b:sia) (r:9.24.9) (q:draft)
siat = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:evil/bad/wrong) (d:form of <sia>, in {gamtat siat} or {siat gamtat}, do evil or act wrongly) (a:hoih/pha) (b:sia) (r:26.18.8) (q:draft)
siat = (i:3) (t:v) (w:thrust/put into/sheathe) (d:push a blade or point into something, as arrows into the heart or a sword into its sheath; {siat kik} is put a sword back) (q:draft, low confidence)
siatbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:treat badly/mistreat/harm) (d:<siat>, bad, with <bawl>, do or treat) (s:bawlsia) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teachers) (d:<sia>, teacher, with plural <te>; {Thukham siate} or {Thukham hilh siate} are the teachers of the law) (s:thuhilhte/hilhte) (a:nungzuite) (b:sia) (q:draft)
siate = (i:2) (t:n) (w:ruins/broken parts) (d:<sia>, ruined or spoiled, with plural <te>: ruined things or places; {khuapi siate} are ruined cities) (s:siasate/kisiamaisate) (b:sia) (q:draft)
siate = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:evil/bad) (d:<sia> bad or evil with the plural marker <te>, placed after the noun, as in {gamtat siate} evil ways; {a siate} is the evil things) (s:gilote) (a:hoihte) (b:sia) (q:draft)
Siate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teachers) (d:<sia> teacher with plural <te>) (s:thuhilhte/hilhte) (b:siate) (q:draft)
siateng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the evil things/every evil) (d:<sia> bad, evil, with <teng> all) (q:draft, low confidence)
siatgamtatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:act corruptly/do evil) (d:<siat> bad, with <gamtat> behave and <in>; behaving corruptly) (q:draft)
siatgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be utterly ruined/be laid waste/be destroyed) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with <gawp>, completely) (s:siamang/siacip) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siatgawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:devastation/ruin) (d:<siatgawp> be badly ruined, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kisiatna/siatna) (b:siatgawp) (q:draft)
siathei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:perishable/corruptible) (d:<sia>, spoil or go bad, with <thei>, able; {a siathei lo} is imperishable. {A siathei tawpin} is as badly as they can) (s:muatthei/kisiathei/sithei) (b:sia) (q:draft)
siatkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come to ruin/be harmed/be corrupted) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with <khak>, happen to: fall into ruin or harm, mostly of something feared) (q:draft)
siatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sheathe/put back) (d:<siat>, thrust in, with <kik>, back: put a sword back into its sheath) (a:dok) (q:draft)
siatlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ruined by/come to ruin through) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with <lawh>: suffer ruin as the outcome of something, like <sihlawh>, die as the outcome) (q:draft)
siatlawhkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be destroyed/come to ruin) (d:<siat> be ruined, with <lawh> as a result and <khak> happen to; end up destroyed by it) (q:draft)
siatloh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not be ruined/not decay/not be bad) (d:<siat>, form of <sia> be bad or ruined, with the negative <loh>; {a siatloh nadingin} is so that it will not be ruined) (q:draft)
siatmai = (t:see) <siatmai-na>
siatmai-na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ruin/devastation) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with <mai>, wholly, and the noun suffix <na>: complete ruin, devastation) (s:siatmaina/suksiatna/kisiatna) (q:draft)
siatmaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ruin/devastation) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with <mai>, wholly, and the noun suffix <na>: complete ruin, devastation) (s:siatmai-na/suksiatna/kisiatna) (q:draft)
siatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil/wickedness) (d:<siat>, bad, with the noun suffix <na>: evil, wrongdoing; {siatna bawl} is do evil) (s:gitlohna/hoihlohna/gilohna) (a:phatna) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siatna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:disaster/harm/ruin/destruction) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with the noun suffix <na>: ruin or disaster that comes on someone; {siatna tung} is disaster comes) (s:tuahsiatna/kisiatna/suksiatna) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siatnasate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil deeds/evils done) (d:<siatna>, evil, with <sa>, already done, and plural <te>; {na gamtat siatnasate uh}, the evil things you have done) (s:siatnate/gamtatsiatnate) (q:draft)
siatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disasters/calamities/evils) (d:<siatna>, disaster, with plural <te>: the bad things that come on people) (s:tuahsiatnate) (b:siatna) (q:draft)
siatnate = (i:2) (t:n) (w:evil deeds/wickedness) (d:<siatna>, evil, with plural <te>: evil deeds; often after <gamtat>, conduct, as in {gamtat siatnate}, evil doings) (s:gamtatsiatnate/tatsiatnate/siatnasate) (b:siatna) (r:30.8.7) (q:draft)
siatnateng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the wickedness) (d:<siatna> evil, wickedness, with <teng> all) (b:siatna) (q:draft)
siatni = (i:1) (t:n) (w:day of ruin/day of doom) (d:<siat> be ruined, with <ni> day) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:destroy/ruin/harm) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with the causative <sak>: destroy or ruin something, or do harm to someone) (s:susia/siasak/suksiat) (a:puah/puahkik/lamkik) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:defilement/ruining) (d:<siatsak> ruin, defile, with the noun suffix <na>; the act of defiling) (s:nitsakna) (b:siatsak) (q:draft)
siatsakzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can break/be able to destroy) (d:<siatsak> destroy, break, with <zawh> be able) (s:susiazo) (q:draft)
siatsuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spoil/ruin) (d:bring to ruin; the NIV has blemishes at your love feasts) (q:draft, low confidence)
siatsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plunge in/thrust down into) (d:<siat>, thrust, with <suk>, downward) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siattat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do harm/do evil/act violently) (d:keep doing what is bad or destructive; {siattat semsem}, go from bad to worse) (s:gamtatsiat) (q:draft, low confidence)
siattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be ruined/can ruin) (d:<siat>, be ruined, with <theih>, can, the form used before <nading>; {siattheih nading}, so as to be able to ruin or be ruined) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siattheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wickedness/offensive way) (d:<siat> bad, with <theih> can and the noun suffix <na>; something that can be evil) (b:siattheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
siatzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:worse/more wicked) (d:<siat> bad, evil, with the comparative <zaw>) (s:siazaw) (a:hoihzaw/phazaw) (b:siat) (q:draft)
siavuan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doctor/physician) (d:a doctor, one who treats the sick) (s:zato/siavuanpa) (q:draft)
