siavuante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:doctors/physicians) (d:<siavuan>, doctor, with plural <te>) (s:zatote) (b:siavuan) (q:draft)
siazaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:worse/more evil) (d:<sia> bad with the comparative <zaw>; what it is compared with takes <sangin>) (s:siatzaw/siahuaizaw) (a:hoihzaw/phazaw) (q:draft)
Sibbekai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sibbekai) (d:Sibbekai the Hushathite, one of David’s mighty warriors, who killed a Philistine giant and commanded the army division of the eighth month) (r:13.11.29/13.27.11)
Sibboleth = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Sibboleth) (d:the way the men of Ephraim said Shibboleth, by which the men of Gilead knew them at the fords of the Jordan) (r:7.12.6)
Sibmah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sibmah) (d:town east of the Jordan in the territory of Reuben, known for its vines) (r:4.32.38/6.13.19)
Sibon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sidon) (d:spelling of Sidon in 1 Chronicles 22:4, the Phoenician port city whose people brought cedar logs to David) (r:13.22.4)
Sibraim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sibraim) (d:place on the northern border of the land in Ezekiel’s vision, between Damascus and Hamath) (r:26.47.16)
sibup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:faint/swoon/lose consciousness) (d:become like dead from hunger or fear; {sibup natna} is an illness with seizures) (r:40.17.15) (q:draft)
