sicip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die) (d:<si> die, with <cip>, apparently all without exception or for good) (b:si) (q:draft, low confidence)
sidaangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make pale/terrify) (d:of fear, make someone turn pale; the NIV has makes me tremble) (q:draft, low confidence)
sidar = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cedar) (d:the cedar tree, a loan from English cedar) (s:taamtak/taamtaak) (q:draft)
Siddim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Siddim) (d:valley by the Dead Sea, full of tar pits, where the kings of Sodom and Gomorrah fought the four kings) (r:1.14.3/1.14.8)
sidek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be about to die/be dying) (d:<si>, die, with <dek>, almost: on the point of death; {sidek tak}, deathly) (s:sihkuan) (q:draft)
Sidon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sidon) (d:firstborn son of Canaan; also the Phoenician port city north of Tyre that bears his name) (r:1.10.15/13.1.13)
Sidonte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Sidonians) (d:the people of the Phoenician city of Sidon) (b:Sidon) (r:7.18.7)
Siene = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aswan) (d:town on the southern border of Egypt next to Cush, also called Syene, the modern Aswan) (r:26.29.10/26.30.6)
Sifas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cephas) (d:Aramaic name meaning rock that Jesus gave to Simon Peter; the same man as Peter) (r:43.1.42)
Sifmoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Siphmoth) (d:town in the south of Judah to which David sent a share of the plunder) (r:9.30.28)
sigalna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mourning/funeral) (d:mourning for the dead, set against feasting; the NIV has house of mourning) (q:draft, low confidence)
sigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die in great numbers/perish) (d:<si> die, with <gawp> heavily, in a mass) (b:si) (q:draft)
sih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die) (d:form of <si> used before linking words and endings such as <khit>, <ciangin>, <na> and <ding>; {a sih khit ciangin} means after his death) (b:si) (q:draft)
sihbup = (i:1) (t:n) (w:epilepsy/seizure) (d:used with <natna> illness for the falling sickness) (q:draft)
sihdaan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:death sentence/death penalty) (d:<sih>, die, and <daan>, punishment; {sihdaan pia}, sentence to death) (q:draft)
sihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die/when one dies/at death) (d:<sih>, form of <si>, die, with the ending <in>: at the time of dying, or dying in a certain state; {a sihin kum za} is he was a hundred years old when he died) (b:sih) (q:draft)
sihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die) (d:<sih> die, with <khak> happen to; might die) (q:draft)
sihkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die together/die with) (d:<sih>, die, with <khawm>, together) (s:sikhawm) (a:hingkhawm) (b:sih) (q:draft)
sihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have died/be dead) (d:<sih>, die, with <khit>, completion; {a sihkhit ma-in}, before they have died) (s:sikhin) (q:draft)
sihkhitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:having died/death) (d:<sihkhit>, have died, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact that someone has already died) (b:sihkhit) (q:draft)
sihkuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be about to die/be dying) (d:<sih>, die, with <kuan>, be about to: be at the point of death) (s:sidek) (q:draft)
sihlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die because of/perish because of/bring death on oneself) (d:meet death as the result of something; <sih> die with <lawh> get as a consequence) (s:sihpih) (r:18.5.2) (q:draft)
sihlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<sih> die, with <loh> not and the noun suffix <na>; {a sihlohna inn} is a house where no one has died) (q:draft)
sihmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:perish/die out) (d:<sih>, die, with <mang>, away or lost: die and be gone) (q:draft)
sihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:death) (d:<sih>, die, with the noun suffix <na>: death; also the state of the dead, as in {sihna pan thokik}, rise from the dead) (a:nuntakna/hinna) (b:sih) (r:44.10.40) (q:draft)
Sihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Death/Hades) (d:<sihna>, death, written with a capital when death is spoken of as a person or power; {Sihna Gam}, Hades, the land of the dead) (b:sihna) (q:draft)
sihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deaths) (d:<sihna> death, with the plural <te>; the NIV has sword) (b:sihna) (q:draft)
Sihon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sihon) (d:king of the Amorites who ruled in Heshbon and was defeated by Israel under Moses) (r:4.21.21/19.135.11)
sihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die at once/wither at once) (d:<sih> die, with <pah> immediately) (s:sipah) (q:draft)
sihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die for/die because of) (d:die on account of something, as one's own folly or another's sin, also die for the sake of another, as a shepherd for his sheep) (s:sihlawh) (b:sih) (q:draft)
sihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:kill/put to death/cause to die) (d:<sih>, die, with the causative <sak>: kill, put to death; {teek sihsak} is let someone die in old age) (s:that/sisak/thatlum) (a:hingsak/nungtasak/nuntaksak) (b:sih) (q:draft)
sihsan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die leaving/leave behind by dying) (d:die and leave someone behind; the one who dies is the subject and the one bereaved is the object) (b:sih) (q:draft)
