sihsuahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the bereaved) (d:those who have lost someone by death, with the plural <te>) (b:sihsuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
sihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dead ones/those that died) (d:<sih>, die, with plural <te>; {a mawk sihte}, animals that died of themselves) (b:sih) (q:draft)
sihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to die/may die) (d:<sih>, die, with <theih>, can; {a sihtheih nadingin} is so that he may die) (b:sih) (q:draft)
sihtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deadliness) (d:<sih> die, with <theih> can and the noun suffix <na>; {sihtheihna gu} is deadly poison) (b:sihtheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
sihzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:after dying/after death) (d:<sih>, die, with <zawh>, after or finished: after someone has died; {a sihzawh a sawtpi} is long after his death) (q:draft)
sii = (i:1) (t:v) (w:butt/charge at) (d:of a horned animal, run at something and strike it with the horns) (q:draft, low confidence)
siik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:exact/demand payment/collect a debt) (d:require a debtor to pay back what he owes; {leiba siik} is demand payment of a debt) (s:dok) (a:maisak) (q:draft)
siik = (i:2) (t:n) (w:side/corner) (d:side or corner of a shape; {a siik kikim} is with equal sides, squared, said of doorposts, and {siik li nei} is having four corners) (q:draft, low confidence)
siim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:attend/come to/join in) (d:go to a feast or a show as a guest or onlooker; {pawi siim} is attend a feast and {mopawi siim} is attend a wedding) (q:draft)
siimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:attending/attendance) (d:<siim>, attend a feast, with the noun suffix <na>; {mo pawi siimna puan} is clothes for attending a wedding feast) (b:siim) (q:draft)
siin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lid/cover) (d:the lid or cover that closes a chest, a basket or a pit) (s:khuhna) (q:draft)
siin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cover/put a lid on) (d:close something with a lid or cover, as a pit or a basket) (s:khuh) (a:hon) (q:draft)
siinkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cover again/put the lid back on) (d:<siin>, cover with a lid, with <kik>, again or back: put the lid back on) (s:khuhkik) (b:siin) (q:draft)
siipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make smart/sting/irritate) (d:make the eyes smart, said of smoke) (q:draft, low confidence)
siit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spare/leave over/leave remaining) (d:keep back from destruction or from use: spare a person, or leave something over; with <lo> or <kei>, leave nothing) (q:draft)
siitsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:leave for/spare for) (d:<siit>, spare or leave over, with <sak>: leave something remaining for someone) (b:siit) (q:draft)
sik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:iron) (d:the metal iron; also the first part of words for things made of iron or metal, such as <sikkhau>, chain, and <siklukhu>, helmet) (r:4.31.22) (q:draft)
sik = (i:2) (t:v) (w:step on/tread/set foot on) (d:set the foot on something) (r:19.36.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
sikbawk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plummet/plumb weight) (d:the iron weight of a plumb line; {khaukhai sikbawk} is a plumb line) (q:draft)
sikbeel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pan/iron pot) (d:<sik>, iron, with <beel>, pot: an iron cooking vessel; {sikbeel dai} is a flat pan or griddle) (q:draft)
sikbeeldai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pan) (d:iron cooking pan) (q:draft)
sikbel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pan/iron pan/frying pan) (d:<sik>, iron, with <bel>, pot; in both verses as {sikbel dai}) (q:draft)
