sikcipsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trample down/stamp down) (d:<sikcip>, trample, with <suk>, downward) (s:tuancilgawp) (b:sikcip) (q:draft)
sikgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trample/tread down) (d:<sik>, tread, with <gawp>, roughly or thoroughly: trample underfoot) (s:sikcip/tuancil/tuatcil) (b:sik) (q:draft)
sikh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:provide/supply) (d:provide what is needed, as food or offerings) (q:draft, low confidence)
sikha = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ghost/spirit of a dead person) (d:the spirit of a dead person; {sikha sa} is think that one sees a ghost) (q:draft)
sikhate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spirits of the dead/ghosts) (d:<sikha>, spirit of a dead person, with the plural <te>; {sikhate tawh kiho} is consult the dead) (b:sikha) (q:draft)
sikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:die together/die with) (d:<si>, die, with <khawm>, together: die at the same time as others or along with someone) (b:si) (r:9.31.6) (q:draft)
sikhawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dying together/dying with) (d:<sikhawm>, die together, with the linking ending <in>: being joined with someone in death) (b:sikhawm) (q:draft)
sikhiau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spring) (d:season of the year; the NIV has every spring) (q:draft, low confidence)
sikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dead/have died) (d:<si>, die, with <khin>, already: have died, be dead; also of being dead to the law or dead in spirit) (s:sita) (a:nungta) (b:si) (q:draft)
sikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:treading/trampling/stepping on) (d:<sik>, tread, with the linking ending <in>: stepping on something and then going on to the next action) (b:sik) (q:draft)
sikkate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:meat forks/forks) (d:meat forks, with the plural <te>; named in the lists of the bronze utensils of the altar) (s:sikkeute/sikkeukate) (r:2.27.3) (q:draft)
sikkawi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hook/fishhook) (d:<sik>, iron, with <kawi>, bent: a metal hook, especially a hook for catching fish) (q:draft)
sikkawi = (i:2) (t:n) (w:anchor) (d:the iron hook that holds a ship in place, in full {teembaw khawlna sikkawi}) (s:sikkawipi/siklum) (r:44.27.40) (q:draft)
