sikkeukate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:meat forks/forks) (d:<sikkeuka> with plural <te>: metal forks used for the meat of the offerings) (s:sikkeute/sikkate) (b:sikkeuka) (q:draft)
sikkeute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:forks/meat forks) (d:<sikkeu>, meat fork, with the plural <te>: the forks among the utensils of the altar and the temple) (s:sikkate/sikkeukate) (b:sikkeu) (q:draft)
sikkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stepping on unawares) (d:<sik> step on, with <khak> happen to and the noun suffix <na>; {a va sikkhakna munte} are places walked over by accident) (q:draft)
sikkhap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush underfoot/trample) (d:tread on a thing so that it breaks) (q:draft)
sikkhau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chain) (d:<sik>, iron, with <khau>, rope: an iron chain, used for binding a prisoner) (q:draft)
sikkhaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chains/shackles) (d:<sikkhau>, iron chain, with the plural <te>: the chains that bind a prisoner) (s:kolte) (b:sikkhau) (q:draft)
sikkhetna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nailing/nail piercing) (d:<sik>, iron, with <khet>, drive in, and the noun suffix <na>; {sikkhetna pawn} is the scar left by the nails) (q:draft)
sikkhu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:iron tool/iron chisel/iron pen) (d:an iron tool for cutting letters into stone) (q:draft)
sikkhuampi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:iron pillar) (d:<sik> iron, with <khuampi> pillar) (q:draft)
sikkol = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shackles/fetters/chains/irons) (d:iron bonds put on the feet or neck of a prisoner) (s:kol/kolbulh) (q:draft)
