Sinim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Aswan/Sinim) (d:distant land in the south from which the scattered people of God will return, called Sinim in older versions and Aswan in the NIV) (r:23.49.12)
sinin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:learning/studying) (d:<sin>, learn, with <in> linking to the next verb: learning or having learned) (b:sin) (q:draft)
sinin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:testing/examining) (d:<sin>, test, with <in> linking to the next verb: testing or examining) (b:sin) (q:draft)
