Solomon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Solomon) (d:son of David and Bathsheba, king of Israel after David, known for his wisdom and as builder of the temple in Jerusalem) (r:10.12.24/11.1.46)
Somathroasia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Samothrace) (d:island in the northern Aegean Sea where the ship of Paul called on the way from Troas to Neapolis) (r:44.16.11)
sona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fury/burning/heat) (d:<so>, burn, with the noun suffix <na>: burning; {sin sona}, burning of the liver, is fierce anger or fury) (s:sinsona/hehna/thangpaihna/hehluatna) (b:so) (q:draft)
song = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillar/post/sacred stone) (d:an upright pillar; {biakna song} is a pillar or standing stone set up for worship) (s:khuam) (q:draft)
songpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillar/sacred stone/standing stone) (d:<song>, pillar, with <pi>, great: a large pillar or standing stone) (s:khuampi) (b:song) (q:draft)
songte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:pillars/posts/poles) (d:plural of <song>; {biakna songte} are the sacred stones or poles set up for worship) (s:khuamte) (b:song) (q:draft)
sop = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after <zaw>, rather, at the end of a clause, to stress that the opposite of what is right or expected is done) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sopater = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sopater) (d:son of Pyrrhus from Berea, one of the companions of Paul on his journey to Asia) (r:44.20.4)
sopin = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<sop> with the linking <in>, after <zaw>, rather: doing instead the opposite of what is expected) (b:sop) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sorek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Sorek) (d:valley between the hill country of Judah and the Philistine plain, where Delilah lived) (r:7.16.4)
Sorekkuam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Valley of Sorek) (d:the Valley of Sorek, where Delilah lived; <Sorek> with <kuam>, valley) (r:7.16.4)
sosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:boil/bring to a boil/heat) (d:<so>, be hot or boil, with the causative <sak>: make water boil, cook by boiling) (a:votsak) (b:so) (q:draft)
sosak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:kindle/inflame) (d:figurative, of anger: {hehna sosak} is to let anger burn hot or stir it up) (s:kuangsak) (a:daisak) (b:so) (q:draft)
Sosipater = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sosipater) (d:companion of Paul and fellow Jew who sends greetings in the letter to the Romans) (r:45.16.21)
Sosthenes = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sosthenes) (d:name of the synagogue leader at Corinth who was beaten before Gallio, and of the brother named with Paul at the opening of 1 Corinthians) (r:46.1.1/44.18.17)
sosuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stir up/incite/fan into flame) (d:rouse people against someone; also make a gift burn brightly again, fan into flame) (s:hanthawn/hansuah) (q:draft)
sosuahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stirring up/inciting) (d:<sosuah> stir up, with the linking <in>) (s:hanthawnin) (b:sosuah) (q:draft)
sosuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pour down on/break out upon) (d:<so>, boil or be hot, with <suk>, downward: boil over and pour down, said of disaster) (b:so) (q:draft, low confidence)
sot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:extend/prolong/lengthen) (d:make a time or a course go on longer; {hun sot} is to give more time) (s:sotto/sausak) (a:tomsak/khiapsak) (q:draft)
Sotai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sotai) (d:head of a family of the servants of Solomon whose descendants returned from the exile) (r:15.2.55/16.7.57)
sotsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:extend/enlarge/prolong) (d:<sot>, extend, with <sak>, cause: make a border wider or let a plan go further) (s:keeksak) (a:tomsak) (b:sot) (q:draft)
sotto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lengthen/extend/prolong) (d:make longer in time, add to; {hun sotto} is to put off or delay; also go on further) (s:sot/sausak) (a:tomsak) (b:sot) (q:draft)
Spain = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Spain) (d:land at the western end of the Mediterranean Sea that Paul planned to visit after Rome) (r:45.15.28/45.15.24)
Stakhus = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Stachys) (d:Christian in Rome whom Paul greets as his dear friend) (r:45.16.9)
stakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stacte/gum resin) (d:a fragrant gum resin, one of the spices of the holy incense) (q:draft)
Stefanas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Stephanas) (d:Christian of Corinth whose household, baptized by Paul, were the first converts in Achaia) (r:46.1.16/46.16.15)
Stefen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Stephen) (d:one of the seven chosen to serve in the church at Jerusalem, a man full of grace and power, stoned to death as the first Christian martyr) (r:44.6.5/44.8.2)
Stoik = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Stoic) (d:school of Greek philosophers, some of whom debated with Paul in Athens) (r:44.17.18)
su = (i:1) (t:v) (w:touch/lay a hand on/harm) (d:touch, lay a hand on, and so harm; often in the compound {su-kha}, touch) (s:lawng/sukha) (q:draft)
su = (i:2) (t:v) (w:attack/strike/seize) (d:also the first part of compounds of forceful action such as {su-tat} cut off) (s:sim) (r:18.18.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
su = (i:3) (t:v) (w:pound/crush/knead) (d:pound grain in a mortar, also work dough) (q:draft, low confidence)
suah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be born/give birth) (d:form of <suak> used before <ciangin>, <hun> and other dependent endings) (s:pian) (a:sih) (r:42.1.57) (q:draft)
suah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:become) (d:form of <suak> used before <ciangin>, <nadingin> and other dependent endings) (r:58.2.17) (q:draft)
suah = (i:3) (t:v) (w:shed/bring out) (d:cause to come out; {sisan suah} is to shed blood) (s:luangsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
suah = (i:4) (t:part) (d:used in fractions between the number of parts and the part taken, as in {seh-sawm-suah-seh-khat} one tenth) (q:draft, low confidence)
suahhun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:time of birth/time to give birth) (d:<suah> be born or give birth, with <hun> time) (q:draft)
suahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making into/dividing into) (d:<suah> with <in>, after a number of parts or groups, turning something into that many) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:taking off/removing) (d:of clothing, taking it off before the next action) (a:silhin) (q:draft)
suahkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn out to be/happen to become/prove) (d:<suak> become with <kha>, happen to: become something that was not intended; mostly in {a suahkhak loh nadingin}, so that it may not turn out to be) (s:suakkha) (q:draft)
suahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take off/strip off/remove) (d:take off clothes, sandals or ornaments) (a:silh) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:bring out/take out/bring to light) (d:bring something out from where it was kept or hidden; also pour out what is in the heart) (s:paikhiatpih/pusuaksak) (a:seel) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahkhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who takes off) (d:<suahkhia> take off, with {-pa} for a man: the man who takes off his armour) (b:suahkhia) (q:draft)
suahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come out/be born/come forth) (d:<suah> with <khiat> out: come out, as a child from the womb; form of <suahkhia> used before <ciangin>, <sak> and similar words) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahkhiat = (i:2) (t:v) (w:turn out/result) (d:of a matter, how it ends) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:coming out/coming forth) (d:<suahkhiat> come out, with the noun suffix <na>; {suahkhiatna mun} is the place something comes out from) (b:suahkhiat) (q:draft)
suahkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take off/strip/remove) (d:<suahkhiat> take off, with <sak>, do to or for another, take the clothes off someone) (a:silhsak) (b:suahkhiat) (q:draft)
suahkhiatsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking off/stripping) (d:<suahkhiatsak> take the clothes off someone, with the linking <in>) (b:suahkhiatsak) (q:draft)
suahkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become) (d:<suah>, become, with <khit>, finished; before <ciangin>: once one has become) (q:draft)
suahkhit = (i:2) (t:v) (w:give birth/be born) (d:<suah>, give birth, with <khit>, finished; before <ciangin>: once the child has been born) (q:draft)
suahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be born again) (d:<suah>, be born, with <kik>, again: be born a second time) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahkik = (i:2) (t:v) (w:reappear/break out again) (d:<suah>, come out, with <kik>, again: said of a disease or mold that breaks out again) (s:kilangkik/kilatkik) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahloh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not become) (d:<suah> become with <loh>, not; {a mawh suahloh nading}, so as not to become guilty) (q:draft)
suahlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:not becoming) (d:<suahloh> not become, with the noun suffix <na>; {a mawkna a suahlohna}, the fact that it did not turn out in vain) (b:suahloh) (q:draft)
suahma = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be born/become) (d:<suah>, be born or become, with <ma>, before: before one was born, before one became; {ka suahma pekin}, even before I was born) (q:draft)
suahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:birth/birthplace/native) (d:<suah>, be born, with the noun suffix <na>: birth or place of birth; {suahna gam} is the land of birth, the native land) (s:pianna) (a:sihna) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:rising/sunrise/east) (d:the rising of the sun; {ni a suahna lam} is the east) (s:nisuahna) (a:tumna/nitumna) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahna = (i:3) (t:n) (w:flow/issue) (d:a coming out, as in {si suahna} flow of blood) (s:luanna) (b:suah) (q:draft, low confidence)
suahnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to become/want to be) (d:<suah>, become, with <nop>, want to) (s:suaknuam) (r:41.8.34) (q:draft)
suahpih = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:from birth/born with) (d:<suah>, be born, with <pih>, together with: had since birth, as {a suahpih mittaw}, blind from birth) (s:pianpih) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahsa = (t:see) <man'suahsa>
suahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring out/send out/produce) (d:cause to come out; <suah> with <sak>, cause) (s:pusuaksak) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:turn into/make into/change to) (d:<suah> with the causative <sak>: make one thing or person become another) (s:suaksak) (b:suah) (r:19.46.8) (q:draft)
suahsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking off/removing) (d:<suahsak> with the linking <in>; here take a garment off someone) (b:suahsak) (q:draft)
suahsakkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to make/let become) (d:<suahsak> make into, with <khak>, happen to; with <loh>, so as not to let something become so) (q:draft)
suahsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:making/turning into/causing) (d:the act or place of making something become or come out; {sal suahsakna} is sending into exile) (b:suahsak) (q:draft)
suahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:escape/be saved/go free) (d:stem two form of <suakta>; {suahtak theih nading} is a way of escape) (q:draft)
suahtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:freedom/liberty/deliverance/release) (d:<suahtak>, escape or go free, with the noun suffix <na>: freedom, release from slavery, prison or danger) (s:khahkhiatna/hotkhiatna) (a:salsuahna/koltanna/saltanna) (b:suahtak) (r:59.2.12/42.4.18) (q:draft)
Suahtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:escape/deliverance) (d:{Suahtakna Suangpi}, Rock of Escape, renders the place name Sela Hammahlekoth) (b:suahtakna) (q:draft)
suahtaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:set free/save/spare/deliver) (d:causative of <suahtak>, cause someone to escape or go free) (s:suaktasak/honkhia/khah) (b:suahtak) (q:draft)
suahtaksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:release/deliverance/setting free) (d:the act of setting someone free or sparing a life; {suahtaksakna hun}, the set time of release) (s:khahkhiatna/suahtakna) (b:suahtaksak) (q:draft)
suahtakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to escape/be able to save) (d:<suahtak> escape, be saved, with <zo>, be able, manage to) (s:pelhthei) (b:suahtak) (q:draft)
suahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who give out/those who serve) (d:<suah> bring out with <te>, those who; of one who gives a cup of water) (b:suah) (q:draft, low confidence)
suahthei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can make/can turn into) (d:<suah> with <thei>, be able; {a sia suahthei}, can make bad, corrupt) (s:suahzo/suaksakzo) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to become/can become) (d:<suah> become with <theih> can, the form used before <nading>; {a suahtheih nadingin} means so that one may become) (s:suakthei) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suahtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being able to become/becoming) (d:<suahtheih>, can become, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:suahtheih) (q:draft)
suahtung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:birth/rising) (d:the moment of coming out: the birth of a person or the rising of the sun; {a suahtung a kipan}, from birth) (q:draft)
suahzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have become/since becoming) (d:<suah> become with <zawh> after finishing; {kumpi a suahzawh} counts the years from the time someone became king, where English says in the year of his reign; also counts days from a birth, {ka suahzawh a ni giat ni-in}, on the eighth day after I was born) (q:draft)
suahzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to make/can make into) (d:<suah> with <zo>, be able; {mi cingtaak suahzo}, able to make people perfect) (s:suahthei/suaksakzo) (b:suah) (q:draft)
suak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:through/on/continuously) (d:placed after a verb: the action goes right through or carries on without stopping, as in {zui suak}, go on following, and {om suak}, stay on)
suak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:become/turn into) (d:come to be something; the thing or state one becomes stands before the verb) (s:piang)
suakah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:along/throughout) (d:<suak> through with <ah>; {paiphei suakah}, all along the length) (b:suak) (q:draft, low confidence)
suakcilte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:newborn/newly born) (d:<suak> be born with <cil>, just begun, and plural <te>) (q:draft)
suakgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become utterly/be reduced to) (d:<suak> become with <gawp>, utterly, badly) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:becoming/turning into) (d:<suak> with the linking ending <in>: become, and then) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suakin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:rising/coming out) (d:of the sun, rising) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suakkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become/turn out to be/end up as) (d:<suak>, become, with <kha>, happen to: come to be something without meaning to) (s:suahkhak/hikha) (q:draft)
suakkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become together/become one) (d:<suak> become with <khawm>, together) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come out/come forth/break out/be born) (d:<suak> with <khia>, out: said of a child at birth, of flames, of a disease on the skin, of light rising) (s:piangkhia/pusuak) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suakkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring forth/bring out/issue) (d:cause to come out: give birth to young, or issue an order) (s:pusuaksak) (b:suakkhia) (q:draft)
suakkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have become/become wholly) (d:<suak>, become, with <khin>, already or completely) (s:hikhin) (b:suak) (r:23.63.19) (q:draft)
suakkhin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:have been born/be already born) (d:<suak>, be born, with <khin>, already) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:reform/turn back into/return to) (d:<suak>, become, with <kik>, again: become again what one was before) (b:suak) return into previous status
suaklua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be very sleepy/be overcome) (d:with <lua>, too much; {ihmut suaklua}, sleepiness coming on too strongly) (b:suak) (q:draft, low confidence)
suakmangkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become completely/turn wholly into) (d:<suak>, become, with <mang>, away or utterly, and <khin>, completely) (q:draft)
suakmasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:firstborn/born first) (d:<suak> be born with <masa> first) (s:tacil/naucil) (a:nautum) (q:draft)
suakmawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn out to be/become) (d:<suak>, become, with <mawk>, which marks something unexpected or regrettable: turn out to be, become after all) (q:draft)
suakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:continuing/lasting) (d:<suak>, right through, with the noun suffix <na>: a going on without end; {piak suakna} is giving that continues forever) (b:suak) (q:draft, low confidence)
suaknuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to become/wish to be) (d:<suak>, become, with <nuam>, want: wish to become something, such as a teacher) (q:draft)
suakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:man who becomes/one who has become) (d:<suak>, become, with <pa> for a man: the man who becomes something; {mi nin a suakpa} is the man who becomes unclean) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become at once/become immediately) (d:<suak>, become, with <pah>, at once: become something immediately) (q:draft)
suakpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:become quickly/soon become) (d:<suak>, become, with <pak>, quickly: become something in a short time) (q:draft)
suaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:having become/become) (d:<suak>, become, with <sa>, already: having become; {sal a suaksa} are those who had become captives, the exiles, and {a khu suaksa} is smoldering) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make/cause to become/turn into) (d:<suak>, become, with the causative <sak>: make someone or something become what is named, as make a man king or turn a land into a waste) (s:hisak) (b:suak) (q:draft)
suaksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making/turning into/causing to become) (d:<suaksak>, cause to become, with the linking suffix <in>: making something become, and then) (b:suaksak) (r:26.32.15) (q:draft)
suaksakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:turn back into/make become again) (d:<suaksak>, cause to become, with <kik>, again or back: turn something back into what it was) (b:suaksak) (q:draft)
suaksakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who makes/one who turns into) (d:<suaksak>, cause to become or bring out, with <pa> for a man: he who makes something become, or who brings out) (b:suaksak) (q:draft)
suaksakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who made/those who turned into) (d:<suaksak>, cause to become, with <te>, those who: the ones who made something become) (b:suaksak) (q:draft)
suaksakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to make/can turn into) (d:<suaksak>, cause to become, with <zo>, be able: be able to make someone become something) (b:suaksak) (q:draft)
suaksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who made/those who have become) (d:<suaksa> with <te>, those who; in the verse those who turned the city into a place for wild animals) (b:suaksa) (q:draft, low confidence)
suaksuak = (t:see) <suaksuak-in>
suaksuak-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:right through/on and on) (d:<suak> through, doubled, with <in>; {pai suaksuak}, keep passing through) (q:draft)
suakta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:alive/survive/stay alive) (d:come through danger alive, be spared from death) (a:si)
suakta = (i:2) (t:v) (w:escape/e emancipated/be liberated/be freed) (d:be set free or released from a bond, an oath, guilt or a master) (r:27.11.42)
suakta = (i:3) (t:v) (w:escape) (d:get away safely from an enemy, a danger or a trap) (s:peng/taikhia) (a:kiman)
suakta = (i:4) (t:v) (w:free/be free) (d:be free, not a slave; {suakta-in paikhia} is go out free, and {a suakta mi} is a free person)
suakta = (i:5) (t:v) (w:get away/get out/run away/run off/break out/break free) (d:get away from a place or from someone who holds or pursues) (s:taimang/taikhia)
Suakta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be freed/free) (d:<suakta> written with a capital in {Sal Suakta}, the Freedmen, slaves who were set free) (b:suakta) (q:draft)
suaktak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be free/go free/escape) (d:form of <suakta> used before <nading> and <zo>; {suaktak nading} is freedom or release) (b:suakta) (q:draft)
suaktakha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:happen to escape/survive) (d:<suakta>, escape, with <kha>, happen to: happen to escape; {a suaktakha} are those who have survived) (q:draft)
suaktakik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go free again/be released) (d:<suakta>, be freed, with <kik>, back or again: go free again, said of a vowed person redeemed by payment) (b:suakta) (q:draft)
suaktalai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:survive/remain/be left) (d:<suakta>, escape or stay alive, with <lai>, still: be still left alive; {a suaktalai} is the remnant) (s:nungtalai) (q:draft)
