sucip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush/oppress/press down) (d:<su>, strike, with <cip>, tight: press down hard, crush or oppress) (s:sukcip/nengniam) (b:su) (q:draft)
sucipgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush completely/crush) (d:<sucip> crush with <gawp>, which shows that the action is done thoroughly or violently) (b:sucip) (q:draft)
sucipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crushing/oppressing) (d:<sucip> crush with <in>, which links it to the following verb) (b:sucip) (q:draft)
sucipsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush down/press down) (d:<sucip>, crush, with <suk>, downward: press or crush down) (b:sucip) (q:draft, low confidence)
Suf = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Suph) (d:place east of the Jordan near the Arabah, named where Moses spoke to Israel) (r:5.1.1) (q:draft)
Sufa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Suphah) (d:region near the Arnon in Moab, named in the Book of the Wars of the Lord) (r:4.21.14)
Sufah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Suphah) (d:spelling of <Sufa>, a region near the Arnon in Moab named in the Book of the Wars of the Lord) (r:4.21.14)
sugawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush/destroy/break to pieces) (d:<su>, strike, with <gawp>, thoroughly or violently: crush or destroy an enemy) (s:sukgawp/zogawp) (b:su) (r:19.89.10) (q:draft)
sugawpin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crushing/shattering/attacking) (d:<sugawp> with the linking suffix {-in}, crushing and then doing the next action) (b:sugawp) (r:28.13.8) (q:draft)
sugawppa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the one who struck down/crusher/destroyer) (d:<sugawp> crush with <pa>, the man who does it) (s:susiapa) (b:sugawp) (q:draft)
sugawpte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who crush/destroyers) (d:<sugawp> crush with the plural <te>, those who do it) (s:susiate) (b:sugawp) (q:draft, low confidence)
sugawpzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to crush/crush) (d:<sugawp>, crush, with <zo>, be able or succeed) (b:sugawp) (q:draft)
suh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take by force/seize/plunder/rob) (d:take away what belongs to another by force) (s:sut/laksak) (q:draft)
suhgawpnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:robberies/plunder/stolen goods) (d:<suh> take by force with <gawp> violently, the noun suffix <na> and the plural <te>) (q:draft)
suhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:robbery/plunder/extortion) (d:<suh>, take by force, with the noun suffix <na>: taking the goods of another person by force or unjustly) (s:kisuhna) (b:suh) (q:draft)
suhsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seized/taken by force) (d:<suh> take by force with <sa>, already done; placed before the thing seized) (b:suh) (q:draft)
suhsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things seized/things taken by force) (d:what someone has taken by force from another, with the plural <te>) (q:draft, low confidence)
suhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plunder/things taken by force) (d:<suh>, take by force, with plural <te>: the things one has seized or robbed) (s:lakte/kisutte) (b:suh) (q:draft)
