sui = (i:2) (t:v) (w:stumble/trip/strike against) (d:hit the foot against something; {sui kha} is stumble over, and {sui-a kipuk} is stumble and fall) (q:draft)
suih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carve/hew/cut) (d:form of <sui> used before <siam>, <zia> and other following words, also as a noun for carved work; {sing suih} is cutting or working wood) (b:sui) (q:draft)
suih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:stumble/trip) (d:in {suih khak nading}, a thing to strike the foot against, a stumbling block) (q:draft)
suihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strike against/stumble on/dash against) (d:hit the foot against something; form of {sui kha} used before <loh> and <na>) (s:kitahkhak) (q:draft)
suihkhakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things stumbled on/stumbling blocks) (d:<suihkhak> strike the foot against with the plural <te>, the things that someone stumbles on) (b:suihkhak) (q:draft)
suikha = (t:see) <suikha-in>
