sumleite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:buyers) (d:<sumlei> buy with the plural <te>, those who buy) (s:leite/vanleite) (a:sumzuakte) (b:sumlei) (q:draft)
sumlepai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:money/wealth/money and goods) (d:{sum le pai}, money and goods: money, wealth or payment; {sumlepai vai} is money matters) (s:sum/neihsa) (q:draft)
sumlepaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:possessions/money and goods) (d:<sumlepai>, money and goods, with the plural <te>: the things a person owns) (s:neihsate) (b:sumlepai) (q:draft)
summeet = (i:1) (t:n) (w:profit/gain/trade) (d:<sum>, money, with <meet>, profit: money made by trading or by a business; {summeet ngah} is make money and {summeet bawlte} are traders) (s:summet/meet/met) (q:draft)
summet = (i:1) (t:n) (w:profit/gain) (d:<sum> money with <met> profit; {summet bawl} is trade with money to make a profit) (s:summeet/met/meet) (q:draft)
summgo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bronze) (d:probably a misprint of <sumngo> bronze, which follows in the same verse) (s:sumngo) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumnei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wealthy/having money) (d:<sum> money with <nei> have; {sumnei pa} is a man of means, the owner of a house and its store) (s:sumhau/hau) (a:zawng) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumneite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:creditors/lenders) (d:<sumnei> having money with the plural <te>; set against <leibate>, debtors) (a:leibate) (b:sumnei) (q:draft)
sumnen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small coin/coin) (d:a coin of little value; {sumnen tang nih}, two small coins) (s:sumtang) (q:draft)
sumngah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make money/earn money/get money) (d:<sum>, money, with <ngah>, get: earn or make money; {sumngah nading} is a way of making money) (q:draft)
sumngo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bronze) (d:a hard reddish-brown metal, bronze or copper, used for tools, vessels and weapons) (s:sumsan)
