sungnungah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the inner part/into the inner part/in the inner room) (d:<sungnung> inner, inner room, with the place marker <ah>: in or into the inner part; {tual sungnungah} is into the inner court, {biakinn sungnungah} in the inner sanctuary) (b:sungnung) (q:draft)
sungnungte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inner rooms/inner parts) (d:<sungnung> inner with the plural <te>: the innermost parts of a building; {a dei sungnungte}, its inner rooms, {kawm sungnungte}, the inner walls) (b:sungnung) (q:draft)
sungnungteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the whole inner part) (d:<sungnung> inner with <teng> all; {biakinn tual sungnungteng} is the whole inner court of the temple) (b:sungnung) (q:draft)
sungpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:father-in-law) (d:the father of a man’s wife) (r:7.19.7) (q:draft)
sungpan = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:out of/from within) (d:<sung> inside with <pan> from; {kam sungpan} is out of the mouth) (s:lakpan) (q:draft)
