sungpate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:father-in-law's family/in-laws) (d:<sungpa> father-in-law with the plural <te>; the family of a man's wife) (b:sungpa) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have cast/cast) (d:<sung> cast metal in a mould with <sak>, cause: have metal objects cast) (q:draft)
sungsilhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:undergarments/inner garments) (d:<sung> inside with <silh> wear and the plural <te>, clothes worn underneath) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pour out/pour down) (d:<sung>, pour, with <suk>, downward: pour something down on a person or thing, as perfume on the head or anger on a people) (s:sungkhia) (q:draft)
sungtang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come in to/come in) (d:come in to where a person is; in Genesis 39 of a man coming in to a woman in the house) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungtawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inmost part/innermost being/heart) (d:the innermost part, of a person the inner being, of a building the inner rooms) (q:draft)
sungte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:insides/interiors/rooms) (d:<sung>, inside, with plural <te>: the inner parts of several things, {inn sungte} the rooms of a house; with <ah> or <panin>, into or from inside them) (b:sung) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungteng = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:within/throughout/during all) (d:<sung>, during, with <teng>, all: through the whole of a time; {khan sungteng} is the whole length of a life) (r:1.5.5)
sungtengah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:throughout/within) (d:<sungteng> with <ah>, in the whole of an area) (b:sungteng) (q:draft)
sungtengin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:during/throughout/all the while) (d:<sungteng>, within the whole of, with the ending <in>; {tua sungtengin}, all that while) (b:sungteng) (q:draft)
sungtengun = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:throughout/during all) (d:<sungteng> within with <un>; {na tun ma sungtengun} is all the time before you arrived) (b:sungteng) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungthu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inner matter/private matter) (d:<sung> inside with <thu> matter; {lungsim sungthu} is what is in the heart) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungtum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come in/go in/enter) (d:go inside, the opposite of <pusuah> or <paikhiat>, go out) (s:lut) (a:pusuak/pusuah/paikhiat) (q:draft)
sungtumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:going in/entering) (d:<sungtum> go inside with the linking suffix {-in}: having gone in) (a:pusuakin) (b:sungtum) (q:draft)
sungtumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:coming in/going in/entering) (d:the act of going inside; paired with <pusuahna> going out for all one's comings and goings) (s:lutna) (a:pusuahna) (b:sungtum) (q:draft)
sungun = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:during/while) (d:<sung> with the plural ending {-un}, used after a clause whose subject is plural: while they were, during their time) (b:sung) (q:draft)
sungvan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:furnishings/furniture) (d:<sung> inside with <van> goods; {inn sungvan} is the things kept inside a house) (q:draft)
sungvumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:heaping up/piling up) (d:{lei sungvum} is heap up earth into a mound or ramp; with <in>, which links it to the next verb) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungzah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for as long as) (d:<sung> during with <zah> amount; {hun tanvei sungzah} is for the same length of time as) (q:draft, low confidence)
suniam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring down/bring low) (d:<su>, strike, with <niam>, low: bring someone down or make them low) (s:niamsak) (q:draft)
sunim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bruise/crush) (d:strike so as to bruise or crush)
sunin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:likeness)
