taansa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lost) (d:<taan> lose with <sa>, already done; placed before the thing lost) (b:taan) (q:draft)
taansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take away/cause to lose/deprive of) (d:<taan>, lose, with the causative <sak>) (b:taan) (q:draft)
taanzaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flash/light up) (d:of lightning, flash across the sky) (s:taangzaih) (q:draft)
taanzaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:light up/make flash) (d:<taanzaih>, flash, with the causative <sak>: of lightning lighting the sky from end to end) (b:taanzaih) (q:draft)
taanzausak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:open wide/widen) (d:of the heart, {lungsim taanzausak} is open the heart wide; ends in the causative <sak>) (q:draft, low confidence)
taanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shine on/shine over) (d:<taan>, shine, with <zo>: of light or glory, come to shine on someone) (b:taan) (q:draft)
taat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sharpen/whet) (d:make the edge of a blade sharp; also used of the tongue) (s:hiamsak) (q:draft)
taatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sharpening/whetting) (d:<taat> sharpen with <in>, which links it to the following clause) (b:taat) (q:draft)
taatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who sharpen) (d:<taat>, sharpen, with the plural <te>) (b:taat) (q:draft)
taaubeelin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in a bronze pot) (d:{taaubeel}, a bronze pot, with the marker <in>) (q:draft)
taaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bracelets) (d:ornaments worn on the wrist or arm, with plural <te>) (q:draft)
Tabbaoth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tabbaoth) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.43/16.7.46)
Tabbath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tabbath) (d:place near Abel Meholah, toward which the Midianites fled from Gideon) (r:7.7.22)
Tabe = (t:see) <Tabe-el>
