taikhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drive out/make flee) (d:<taikhia>, flee, with the causative <sak>) (s:taisak/taimangsak) (b:taikhia) (q:draft, low confidence)
taikhiasim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee secretly/slip away/run away) (d:<taikhia> run away with <sim>, secretly) (s:taisim) (q:draft)
taikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee/run away/leave/escape) (d:form of <taikhia> used before <manin>, <ni>, <nading> and <zawh>) (b:taikhia) (q:draft)
taikhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flight/fleeing/running away) (d:<taikhiat>, flee, with the noun ending <na>: the act of fleeing, or the place one fled from) (s:taina/taisimna) (b:taikhiat) (q:draft)
taikhiatzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to escape) (d:<tai>, flee, with <khiat>, out, and <zawh>, be able; {taikhiatzawh hetlohna} is a place from which there is no escape) (q:draft)
taikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee back/run back) (d:<tai> run with <kik>, back again) (s:lehtai) (b:tai) (q:draft)
tailahpi = (t:see) <tailahpi-in>
tailahpi-in = (t:todo) (q:draft, describes how a hunted deer runs on before the hunters, perhaps exhausted or in panic; the verse does not fix the meaning)
tailam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flight/way of escape) (d:<tai>, flee, with <lam>, way or direction: the fact or direction of someone fleeing) (q:draft, low confidence)
taimang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee/run away/escape) (d:<tai>, flee, with <mang>, away out of sight: run off and be gone) (s:taikhia/taikeek/taisim) (q:draft)
taimangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fleeing/running away) (d:<taimang> flee with <in>, which links it to the following verb) (b:taimang) (q:draft)
taimangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:chase away/put to flight/make flee) (d:<taimang> flee with <sak>, cause) (s:taisak/taikeeksak/delhmang) (b:taimang) (q:draft)
taimangta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have fled/be gone) (d:<taimang>, flee away, with <ta>, marking that the change has taken place) (b:taimang) (q:draft)
taina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flight/fleeing) (d:<tai> flee with the ending {-na}; also the place someone flees to, and {a taina-ah}, while he flees) (s:taikhiatna/galtaina/taisimna) (b:tai) (q:draft)
taina = (i:2) (t:n) (w:rebuke/reproof) (d:from <tai> in the sense of scold or discipline) (s:taiina/taaina) (a:phatna) (q:draft)
tainate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rebukes/reproofs) (d:<taina> rebuke, with the plural <te>) (b:taina) (q:draft)
taipah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:run at once/hurry off) (d:<tai>, run, with <pah>, immediately) (q:draft)
taipak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hurry/run quickly) (d:<tai> run with <pak>, quickly or for a short while) (q:draft)
taipih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee with/escape with/run away taking) (d:<tai> with <pih>: flee taking someone or something along) (b:tai) (q:draft)
taisa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fled) (d:<tai> flee with <sa>, already done; {a taisa mipa} is the man who has fled) (b:tai) (q:draft)
taisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put to flight/rout/drive out) (d:make someone run away: <tai> run or flee with the causative <sak>) (s:taimangsak/taikeeksak/delhmang) (b:tai) (q:draft)
taisak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:let flee/allow to run) (d:<tai> with <sak> in the sense of allowing; {hong taisak un} is let me flee) (b:tai) (q:draft)
taisakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:putting to flight/driving away) (d:<taisak>, make flee, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:taisak) (q:draft)
taisakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to put to flight) (d:<taisak>, make flee, with <zo>, be able) (b:taisak) (q:draft)
taisan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forsake/desert/abandon/flee from) (d:<tai>, run, with <san>, away from: run away from someone and leave him, and so desert or forsake a person or God) (s:nusia/nusiat/taisanmang) (a:zui) (b:tai) (r:40.26.56) (q:draft)
taisanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forsaking/deserting/leaving) (d:<taisan> with <in> linking to the next verb) (s:paisanin) (b:taisan) (q:draft)
taisanmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:desert/abandon/forsake) (d:<taisan> forsake with <mang>, away completely) (s:taisan/nusiat) (q:draft)
taisansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:alienate/make forsake) (d:<taisan>, forsake, with the causative <sak>: cause people to leave someone) (b:taisan) (q:draft)
taisanta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forsake/leave) (d:<taisan>, forsake, with <ta>, marking a change that takes place) (b:taisan) (q:draft)
taisante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deserters/renegades/fugitives) (d:<taisan>, desert, with the plural <te>: those who have deserted) (s:galtaite) (b:taisan) (q:draft)
taisanzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:run away from instead/rather flee from) (d:<taisan>, flee from, with <zaw>, rather) (b:taisan) (q:draft)
taisanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have forsaken/have abandoned) (d:<taisan>, forsake, with <zo>, showing the act as done) (s:nusiazo) (b:taisan) (q:draft)
taisatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desertion/shunning/forsaking) (d:the form of <taisan> forsake used before the noun suffix <na>) (s:nusiatna) (q:draft)
taisim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee/run away/escape/desert) (d:<tai>, run, with <sim>, secretly: slip away from danger or from a person) (s:taikhia/taimang/taikhiasim) (q:draft)
taisimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fleeing/flight) (d:<taisim>, flee, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of running away) (s:taina/taikhiatna) (b:taisim) (q:draft)
taisuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let escape/let get away) (d:of one guarding a captive, let him run off; compare <taisuak>, escape) (q:draft, low confidence)
taisuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee/escape/run out) (d:<tai> run with <suak> come out: get away from a place or from people) (s:taikhia/suakta) (q:draft)
taisuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:running on/running out) (d:<taisuak>, run out or get away, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:taisuak) (q:draft)
taisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:run down/rush down) (d:<tai> run with <suk> downward) (s:suktai) (a:taito/totai) (b:tai) (q:draft)
taisukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rushing down/running down) (d:<taisuk>, run down, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:taisuk) (q:draft)
taitai = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:follows <kawi> in Jeremiah 49.3, where the sense is rush or wander here and there) (q:draft, low confidence)
taiteh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:tongs) (d:tool for picking up a live coal) (q:draft)
taitehte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wick trimmers/snuffers/tongs) (d:tools for trimming the lamps of the lampstand) (s:meitehte) (b:taiteh) (r:12.25.14) (q:draft)
taito = (i:1) (t:v) (w:flee up/run up) (d:<tai>, run or flee, with <to>, upward) (s:totai) (a:taisuk) (b:tai) (q:draft)
taizia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of running/manner of running) (d:<tai>, run, with <zia>, manner) (q:draft)
taizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:manage to flee/escape) (d:<tai>, flee, with <zo>, be able: succeed in getting away) (b:tai) (q:draft)
tak = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after an adjective or adverb to strengthen it or to make an adverb of manner, usually as {tak-a} or <takin>, as in {tampi tak} very many and {nakpi tak-a} greatly; {lai tak} means at that very time) (q:draft)
tak = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:right) (d:the right hand or right side, as in {tak lam}) (a:vei) (q:draft)
tak = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:true/real/genuine) (d:true or sincere; doubled as <taktak> or {a tak takin} it means truly) (s:mantak) (q:draft, low confidence)
taka = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:makes the word before it an adverb of manner, like <takin>, used before a describing clause, as in {a tel taka} clearly and {nakpi taka} greatly) (s:takin) (b:tak) (q:draft)
taka = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:at the time/at the very time) (d:after <lai>, at the very time of something, as in {tu lai taka} now, at present) (s:laitaka) (b:tak) (q:draft, low confidence)
takah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:right at/exactly at) (d:<tak> exact with the locative marker <ah>, used after <lai> or <san> to point to an exact spot, {hih lai takah} right here, {tua san takah} right there) (s:laitakah) (b:tak) (q:draft)
takei = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the negative <kei> after <ta>, used in the pair {nei taleh nei takei leh}, whether he has or has not) (q:draft, low confidence)
takhawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:twin) (d:of two young animals born together; apparently <ta>, young, with <khawm>, together) (q:draft, low confidence)
takhial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:commit/do wrong) (d:in {mawhna bang takhial}, what wrong has he done; <khial> is err) (q:draft, low confidence)
takhialsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let go astray/let run wild) (d:cause or allow people to behave wrongly; with <sak>, cause or let) (q:draft, low confidence)
takin = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:while/when) (d:after <lai>, at the very time that) (s:laitakin/kawmin) (b:tak)
takin = (i:2) (t:adv) (d:placed after a descriptive word to make an adverb of manner, like English -ly, as in {nakpi takin} greatly and {lim takin} well, thoroughly) (s:taka) (b:tak)
taklam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:right/right side/right hand) (d:the right as opposed to <veilam>, the left; {taklam khut}, right hand) (s:ziatlam/ziat) (a:veilam) (q:draft)
taklama = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at the right/on the right side) (d:<taklam>, right side, with the place ending <a>) (a:veilama) (b:taklam) (q:draft)
taklamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:at the right/on the right side/in the right hand) (d:<taklam>, right side, with the place ending {-ah}) (a:veilamah) (b:taklam) (q:draft)
taklamin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:with the right/by the right) (d:<taklam> right with <in>; {khut taklamin} is with or by the right hand) (a:veilamin) (b:taklam) (q:draft)
takna = (t:see) <kisuan'takna>
takpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truly/surely/indeed/really) (d:also as {takpi-in}; {aman takpi kong cih-inah} means truly I tell you) (s:taktak/mantakin/hamtang) (b:tak) (q:draft)
takpina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sincerity/genuineness) (d:<takpi>, truly, with the noun suffix <na>; {it takpina} is sincere love) (s:taktakna/cihtakna/lungsimtak) (b:takpi) (q:draft)
taksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:plump/full/well filled) (d:of grain, having a full kernel, not empty; {gah taksa} is the full grain) (a:hawm) (q:draft, low confidence)
taksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make thirsty/let go dry) (d:of the throat, <dang>, let it become dry; {dang tak} is be thirsty, with the causative <sak>) (q:draft, low confidence)
taksang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:believe/be convinced/accept as true) (d:<tak> true with <sang> receive; in the verses negated, not believe) (s:um) (q:draft)
taksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good grain/wheat) (d:<taksa>, full of kernel, with the plural <te>: the full grains as against <ansite>, the chaff) (s:taangte) (a:ansite) (b:taksa) (q:draft)
taksing = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:juniper/fir/pine) (d:an evergreen timber tree of Lebanon, named together with <taamtak>, the cedar; {taksing kung} is a juniper tree) (s:taaksing/taaksan) (r:23.14.8) (q:draft)
taksingte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:junipers/firs/pines) (d:plural of <taksing>, an evergreen timber tree) (s:taaksingte/taaksante) (b:taksing) (q:draft)
taksuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come true/be carried out) (d:<tak>, real, with <suak>, become: come to be real; {taksuak sak} is make it happen, carry it out) (q:draft, low confidence)
taktak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truly/surely/certainly/really) (d:placed after a verb to stress that something really is so or will surely happen; after a noun it means real or true, as in {Israel mi taktak}, a true Israelite) (s:takpi/taktakin/petmah) (r:1.2.17)
taktakah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the very/truly in) (d:<taktak>, truly, with the place marker <ah>; {lungsim tawng taktakah} is in the very depth of the heart) (b:taktak) (q:draft)
taktakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truly/really/indeed/in fact) (d:<taktak>, truly, with the adverb ending <in>; mostly as {a taktakin}, truly or indeed, at the opening of a statement) (s:taktak/takpi/mantak) (b:taktak) (q:draft)
taktakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:genuineness/sincerity/reality) (d:<taktak>, truly, with <na>, placed after a verb or adjective to make a noun: the fact of truly doing or being so, as in {it taktakna}, true love, and {lungkim taktakna}, full conviction) (s:takpina) (b:taktak) (q:draft, low confidence)
taktakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the true one/the real one) (d:<taktak>, truly, with <pa>, the man who: after a verb, the one who truly does it, as {a nei taktakpa}, the true owner) (b:taktak) (q:draft)
taktakta = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truly now/really) (d:<taktak>, truly, with <ta>, marking that a new state has come) (b:taktak) (q:draft)
taktakte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:true/real/genuine) (d:<taktak> with the plural suffix <te>, the true or real ones, after a verb those who truly do it, as in {a bia taktakte}, the true worshipers) (b:taktak) (q:draft)
takte = (i:1) (t:part) (d:the strengthening particle <tak> followed by the plural <te>, which makes the phrase before it mean those who or the things that, as in {a taisuak dek takte}, those who are just escaping) (b:tak) (q:draft, low confidence)
takteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good grain/sound grain) (d:the full grain, all of it, as against {a siteng}, the chaff; ends in <teng>, all) (a:siteng) (q:draft, low confidence)
takun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:while/when) (d:<tak> with the plural ending <un>, in {lai takun}, at the very time when they) (s:laitakun) (b:tak) (r:44.8.36) (q:draft)
tal = (i:1) (t:n) (w:carrying frame/frame) (d:frame on which a load is laid to be carried) (r:4.4.12) (q:draft)
tal = (i:2) (t:n) (w:forehead) (d:the forehead, {tal kolh} is a bald forehead) (s:taltang) (q:draft)
tal = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:male) (d:male of an animal, written after the animal name, as in {la-tal}, a male donkey, and {bawng-tal}, a bull) (q:draft)
talap = (i:1) (t:n) (w:colonnade/porch) (d:a roofed walk or porch with pillars, as the five that stood round the pool in Jerusalem) (s:innliim/innlim) (q:draft)
