talapte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:porches/colonnades) (d:<talap>, covered porch, with the plural <te>: the five roofed colonnades beside the pool of Bethesda, where the sick lay) (q:draft, low confidence)
talecin = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:even if/though) (d:follows a verb and is followed by <zong>: even if one does so) (s:taleng/taleh) (q:draft, low confidence)
taleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:whether/or/even if/though) (d:follows a verb, most often <hi>; repeated, as {hi taleh, hi taleh}, it means whether this or that; used once it means even if, although) (s:taleng/talecin) (r:45.5.7) (q:draft)
talen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:talent) (d:a large unit of weight used for gold, silver and bronze, about thirty-four kilograms) (q:draft)
taleng = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:even if/even though/although) (d:placed after the verb and often followed by <zong>: even if, though it be so; alone it can also express a wish, if only) (s:taleh/talecin) (q:draft)
talin = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:placed after <kai>, drag: dragged along the ground) (q:draft, low confidence)
Talitha = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Talitha) (d:Aramaic word for little girl, in the words {Talitha kumi}, little girl, get up, which Jesus spoke to the daughter of Jairus) (r:41.5.41)
talkaihgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drag away/carry off) (d:carry off by force as a lion does its prey; contains <kaih>, pull, and <gawp>, violently) (q:draft, low confidence)
talkolh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bald forehead) (d:baldness at the front of the head, named beside <lutol>, bald head; also said of the person who has it) (q:draft)
