tam = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:a lot of) (d:great in amount, said of goods, plunder or a catch) (a:tawm)
tamah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in much) (d:<tam> many or much with <ah>, in; {a tamah} is in what is much, set against {a tawmno-ah}, in what is very little) (b:tam) (q:draft)
Tamar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Tamar) (d:name of three women: the daughter-in-law of Judah and mother of Perez and Zerah, a daughter of David and sister of Absalom, and a daughter of Absalom) (r:10.13.7) (q:draft)
Tamar = (i:2) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tamar/Tadmor) (d:town in the desert on the southern border of the land; the NIV has Tadmor for the town Solomon built) (r:26.47.19) (q:draft)
tamasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fail/forsake/abandon) (d:fail someone by leaving him without help; in the verses always negated and often paired with <nusia>, leave) (s:nusia/taisan) (q:draft)
tamasak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:run out/run dry) (d:of a supply such as oil, give out or come to an end; in the verses always negated) (s:bei) (q:draft, low confidence)
tambong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:measure/liquid measure) (d:a measure for liquids such as water, wine and oil; the numbers in the verses are twice those of the baths in the English Bible, so one {tambong} is about half a bath) (q:draft)
tamin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:child name) see <ta> and <min>
tamkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be broken/be shattered/be downcast) (d:break in pieces; of the heart or mind, be crushed, downcast) (s:kitamkham) (q:draft, low confidence)
