tamzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:manage many/be able to do much) (d:<tam>, many, with <zo>, be able; {thah tamzo} is manage to kill many) (b:tam) (q:draft, low confidence)
tan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fast/abstain) (d:abstain from, in {an tan}, go without food, usually written with a final apostrophe) (s:antan) (q:draft)
tan = (i:2) (t:prep) (w:as far as/up to/as much as) (d:marks a measure of extent in time or distance: {bang tan} is how much or how long, and {suang lot khat tan} is about a stone’s throw) (q:draft)
tan = (i:4) (t:v) (w:redeem/ransom/rescue) (d:buy back or bring out of the power of another, also as {tan khia}) (s:tankhia/honkhia/tanh) (q:draft)
Tan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:redeem) (d:<tan> redeem, written with a capital in titles of God: {hong Tan} the one who redeems you, {Tan pa} the Redeemer) (b:tan) (q:draft)
tanaupa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:kinsman/male relative) (d:<tanau> relative with <pa> marking a man; in Ruth the kinsman who has the right to redeem) (s:behpa) (b:tanau) (q:draft)
tanaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:relatives/kinsmen/clan) (d:<tanau>, relative, with the plural <te>; used also of one relative together with his family) (s:behte) (b:tanau) (q:draft)
taneu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:younger child/younger son) (d:<ta> child with <neu> small; in the verses the younger of two sons) (s:nauzawpa) (q:draft)
taneute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:little ones/little children/infants) (d:plural of <taneu>, small child; also used as a tender way of addressing people) (s:tanote/naupangnote/naungekte) (b:taneu) (q:draft)
tang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seed) (d:the seed or grain of a plant; {nannan tang} is coriander seed) (s:khaici/taangci)
Tang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:straight) (d:written with a capital as the name of a street in Damascus, Straight Street) (q:draft)
tang-awl = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bereaved/alone) (d:left without husband or children; compare <tanggawl>, unmarried) (q:draft, low confidence)
tang-awlin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bereaved/alone) (d:<tang-awl> with the suffix <in>; {tang-awlin om} is live left alone, without husband or children) (q:draft, low confidence)
tanga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:in place of/instead of) (d:<tang>, place or stead, with the linking <a>, as in {a pa tanga}, in the place of his father) (s:tangin/taangin) (q:draft, low confidence)
tanga = (i:2) (t:part) (d:<tang> after <guak>, bare, or <hing>, alive, names the state someone is in, with the linking <a>, as in {guak tanga} naked and {a hing tanga} while alive) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:on the head/on/upon) (d:<tang> with the place marker <ah>: on the top or surface of something; mostly in {lu tangah}, on the head, and also in {lei keu tangah}, on the dry ground) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangban = (i:1) (t:n) (w:parapet/railing) (d:a low wall or railing put round the edge of a flat roof so that no one falls off) (q:draft)
tangciak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be stuck/be trapped/be hemmed in) (d:be caught in a place with no way out, said of people shut in by the desert and of a narrow well) (s:awkcip) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangding = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for/in exchange for/in place of) (d:placed between two nouns, the first given or counted in place of the second, as {mit tangding mit} eye for eye; also written {tang ding}) (s:tangdingin/tangin) (q:draft)
tangdinga = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:for/in place of) (d:<tangding>, in place of, with the linking <a>) (s:tangdingin) (b:tangding) (q:draft)
tangdingin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:in place of/instead of/for/on behalf of) (d:placed after the person or thing that is replaced or represented) (s:tangin/taangin/tangding) (b:tangding) (q:draft)
tangdinzo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:independent/able to stand alone) (d:contains <din> stand and <zo> be able; in the verse with <lo>, not independent of the other) (q:draft)
tangeekte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:little ones/infants/young of the flock) (d:the very young, said of small children and of the young of a flock) (s:naungekte/naungeekte/taneute) (q:draft)
tanggawl = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:unmarried/single) (d:living without a husband or wife; {tanggawl om} is stay unmarried) (q:draft)
tangguak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:naked/bare/stripped) (d:without clothes; {tangguak leh kheguak} is naked and barefoot, and {tangguak-a om mi} is a person who is naked) (s:guaktang) (q:draft)
tangguakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:naked/without clothes) (d:<tangguak>, naked, with the adverb ending <in>: in a naked state) (s:pumguakin) (b:tangguak) (q:draft)
tangguakun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:naked/stripped) (d:<tangguak> naked with the ending <un>, the adverb ending used when several people are spoken to) (b:tangguak) (q:draft)
tanghial = (t:todo) (q:draft, follows <ne> eat in one verse where mothers eat their own children; perhaps an intensifier such as even or outright, but one verse does not show it)
tangho = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dough/cake/bread) (d:dough or cake made of flour; {tangho su} is knead the dough) (s:anlum/moh) (q:draft)
tangin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:instead of/in place of/on behalf of) (d:placed after a noun or pronoun: in the place of, or speaking and acting for someone; {ama tangin uk} is reign in his place, succeed him) (s:taangin) (q:draft)
tangin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:fast/abstain/keep/observe) (d:<tang> with the linking ending <in>: keeping from something or keeping a day, as in {an tangin}, fasting, and {sabbath tangin}, keeping the Sabbath) (s:antangin) (r:16.1.4/3.26.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangkai = (t:todo) (q:draft, {kei tangkai ka hih manin} stands where the NIV has I sat alone because your hand was on me; the meaning of the word is not clear from the verse)
tangkhai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:crop) (d:the crop of a bird, the pouch in its throat, taken out with the feathers when a bird is offered) (q:draft)
tangkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stretch out/raise) (d:of the hand, put it out against someone; ends in the causative <sak>) (q:draft)
tangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:possess again/take back) (d:take possession of a land again; <kik> is again) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangko = (i:1) (t:v) (w:proclaim/announce/declare) (d:make known publicly, announce a message aloud for all to hear) (s:taangko/pulak/genkhia) (a:seel) (q:draft)
tangkoko = (i:1) (t:v) (w:proclaim/expose/make known) (d:<tangko>, proclaim, with <ko> said twice: keep making something known to all) (s:pulak) (q:draft)
tangkona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:proclamation/announcement) (d:<tangko>, proclaim, with the noun suffix <na>: a public announcement; {tangkona bawl} is make a proclamation) (s:taangkona/zaksakna/pulakna) (b:tangko) (q:draft)
tanglai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ancient times/long ago/old times) (d:the distant past; before a noun it means ancient, as in {tanglai mite}, the people of old) (s:taanglai/tangtawng/hunlui/khanglui/nidang) (q:draft)
tangmai = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cucumber) (d:a cucumber plant or its fruit; {tangmai lo} and {tangmai huan} are a cucumber field) (q:draft)
tangmaite = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cucumbers) (d:<tangmai>, cucumber, with the plural <te>) (b:tangmai) (q:draft)
tangmi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:envoy/messenger/ambassador) (d:a person sent to speak for a ruler or people) (s:taangmi/kamtai/palai) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangmite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:envoys/ambassadors/messengers) (d:<tangmi>, envoy, with the plural <te>; also written <taangmite>) (s:taangmite/kamtaite) (b:tangmi) (q:draft)
tangngol = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:grasshopper/young locust/caterpillar) (d:an insect that eats crops, named beside <kauphe>, locust) (q:draft)
tangngolte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:grasshoppers/young locusts) (d:<tangngol>, grasshopper, with the plural <te>) (b:tangngol) (q:draft)
tangpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:right before/in full view/in broad daylight) (d:strengthens a word of seeing or time: {muh tangpi} is right before the eyes, {sun tangpi} is in broad daylight, at midday) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make straight/make level/straighten) (d:make a road or path straight and level, as in {lampi tangsak}) (s:mamsak/neelsak) (q:draft)
tangsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:make shine/let shine/give light to) (d:cause light to shine on someone or something; <taang>, shine, here written <tang>, with the causative <sak>) (s:taangsak/vaaksak) (q:draft)
tangsapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:need/lack/want) (d:what someone lacks or requires; {bangmah tangsapna nei lo} is lack nothing) (s:kisapna/kitangsapna) (a:hauhna) (q:draft)
tangtakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:straight/directly/truthfully) (d:straight ahead without turning aside; of teaching, truly and without partiality) (q:draft)
tangtakpi = (t:see) <tangtakpi-in>
tangtakpi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:plainly/clearly/openly) (d:of speaking: plainly, without holding anything back) (s:teltakin) (q:draft)
tangtang = (i:1) (t:v) (d:<tang> said twice, apparently for an action that keeps going on; in {gam tangtang}, keep moving past, and in {an tangtang}, keep on fasting) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangtanglai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep fasting/go on fasting) (d:{an tang}, abstain from food, with <tang> repeated and <lai>, still) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangtawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ancient times/long ago/of old) (d:the far past; before a noun, ancient: {tangtawng mualtung gamte}, the ancient heights) (s:tanglai/taangtawng/hunlui) (q:draft)
tangtawnga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:long ago/of old/in ancient times) (d:<tangtawng>, ancient times, with the linking ending <a>, used before a verb or noun) (s:sawtpekin) (b:tangtawng) (q:draft)
tangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bones/joints) (d:in the pair {guh le tangte} or {guh leh tangte}, the bones and frame of the body) (s:guhte) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:exiles/captives) (d:in {sal tangte}, those who have been taken away as captives) (s:saltangte/salte) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangten = (i:1) (t:v) (w:live alone/live apart/dwell alone) (d:live alone or apart from others; written with a final apostrophe before the next word) (q:draft)
tangteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:share/portion due) (d:in {ngah ding tangteng}, the part that someone is to receive, as a share of an estate or of a harvest) (s:tanh) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangteuh = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizard) (d:a kind of lizard among the unclean creeping things, where the NIV has wall lizard; {sehnel gam tangteuh}, lizard of the sand country, stands for the skink) (q:draft)
tangthu = (i:2) (t:n) (w:tale/myth) (d:a made-up story that is not true; {tangthu phuahtawm} is a myth)
tangthu = (i:3) (t:n) (w:history/annals/record) (d:a written record of past events; {khang tangthu} is the annals of a reign or a line)
tangthu = (i:4) (t:n) (w:generation/family line/genealogy) (d:the account of a family line, the descendants of a man told in order)
Tangthu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:annals/chronicles/history) (d:capitalised in the title {Khang Tangthu Laibu}, book of the annals) (b:tangthu) (r:12.15.26/12.15.21/12.23.28) (q:draft)
tangthute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:stories/tales/myths/accounts) (d:<tangthu>, story, with the plural <te>; {phuahtawm tangthute} are myths) (s:tuanthute) (b:tangthu) (q:draft)
tangtun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:achieve/accomplish/fulfil/carry out) (d:bring a plan, wish or promise to completion) (s:semkhia) (q:draft)
tangtung = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be fulfilled/come true/succeed/come to pass) (d:of a plan, word or promise, be carried through to its end) (a:maimawk) (r:42.4.21) (q:draft)
tangtungsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fulfil/bring to pass/grant/make succeed) (d:<tangtung>, come to fulfilment, with the causative <sak>: make a word, wish or plan come true) (s:tangtunsak/cingsak) (b:tangtung) (q:draft)
tangtungzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to succeed/succeed) (d:<tangtung>, be fulfilled, with <zo>, be able) (b:tangtung) (q:draft)
tangtunna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fulfilment/accomplishment) (d:<tangtun>, fulfil, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:tangtun) (q:draft)
tangtunsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fulfil/accomplish/carry out) (d:<tangtun> with the causative <sak>: bring a word, plan or promise to completion) (s:tangtungsak/cingsak) (b:tangtun) (q:draft)
tangtut = (i:1) (t:v) (w:complete/finish/accomplish) (d:carry a task through to its end; apparently the form of <tangtun> used before words such as <zawh> and <ding>) (q:draft)
tangun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:alive/while still living) (d:in {a hing tangun}, still alive, with <un> for a plural subject) (s:hingtangun) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangun = (i:2) (t:prep) (w:by/according to) (d:in {a beh tangun}, by their clans, clan by clan) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangval = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:good boy)
tangval = (i:3) (t:n) (w:gentleman/young man) (a:nungak)
Tangval = (i:1) (t:n) (w:young man) (d:<tangval> written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the speaker headings of the Song of Songs, where it is the young man who is the lover) (b:tangval) (r:22.6.3) (q:draft)
tangvalnopa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:young man) (d:<tangval>, young man, with <no>, young, and <pa>, marking a male: the young man) (s:tangvalpa) (q:draft)
tangvalnote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:young men/youths) (d:<tangval>, young man, with <no>, young, and the plural <te>) (s:khangnote/tangvalte) (q:draft)
tangvalpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:boy/lad/young man) (d:<tangval>, young man, with <pa> marking a male: the boy, the young man) (s:naupangpa) (b:tangval) of unmarried adult man
tangvalte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gentleman/young men/youths) (d:<tangval> with the plural <te>: young men) (a:nungakte) (b:tangval)
tangvalteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the young men/young men) (d:<tangval>, young man, with <teng>, all) (b:tangval) (q:draft)
tangzaizaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:wider/more extensive) (d:of work or its reach, more widely spread; ends in the comparative <zaw>) (s:zaizaw) (q:draft)
tangzang = (t:todo) (q:draft, occurs in {lum tangzang}, the shields of warriors hung on a tower, and inside <teitangzang>, javelin; its own meaning is not clear)
tangzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:brighter) (d:<taang>, shine, here written <tang>, with the comparative <zaw>) (s:taangzaw) (q:draft)
tanh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:portion/share/allotment) (d:the part that falls to someone: a share of food, of land or of an inheritance) (s:seh/kaih) (q:draft)
tanh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:redeem/buy back) (d:buy back or set free by paying a price, said of land, of a firstborn and of a people) (s:tat/tankhia) (a:zuak) (r:3.25.26) (q:draft)
tanhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:redeem/buy back) (d:<tanh>, redeem, with <kik>, back again) (s:tatkik/leikik) (a:zuak) (b:tanh) (q:draft)
tanhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:portions/shares) (d:<tanh> portion with the plural <te>; in the verse the portions of meat from offerings) (b:tanh) (q:draft)
Tanhumeth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tanhumeth) (d:Netophathite, father of Seraiah, an army officer who came to Gedaliah at Mizpah) (r:24.40.8/12.25.23)
tanhzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to redeem) (d:<tanh>, redeem, with <zo>, be able) (s:tankhiazo/tatkikzawh) (b:tanh) (q:draft)
tanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crossing/cutting through) (d:<tan>, cut across, with <in> linking to the next verb; {kan tanin} is going across or through) (b:tan) (q:draft, low confidence)
tanin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:breaking off/severing) (d:after a verb of striking, so that the thing is broken through: {deng tanin} is striking and breaking) (b:tan) (q:draft, low confidence)
tankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:redeem/ransom/deliver/set free) (d:set free by paying a price or by power, said above all of God saving his people) (s:tanh/tat/honkhia) (q:draft)
Tankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:redeem) (d:<tankhia> written with a capital of God as Redeemer: {hong Tankhia Topa}, the Lord who redeems you; {hong Tankhia-pa}, your Redeemer) (b:tankhia) (q:draft)
tankhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:redeemer/deliverer) (d:<tankhia>, redeem, with <pa>, the man who: the one who redeems, said of God) (s:honkhiapa/gumkhiapa) (b:tankhia) (q:draft)
Tankhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Redeemer) (d:the one who redeems, <tankhia> with <pa>; capitalised as a title of God) (s:Tanpa/Honpa) (b:tankhiapa) (q:draft)
tankhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let cut off/cut off) (d:<tan>, cut, with <khia>, off, and <sak>, here of letting someone do it; {lu tankhiasak} is let cut off the head) (s:sattan/attan/satkhia) (q:draft)
tankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut off/behead) (d:<tan>, cut, with <khiat>, off; {lutang tankhiat} is cut off the head) (s:sattan/attan/satkhia) (b:tan) (q:draft)
tankhiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to ransom/be able to redeem) (d:<tankhia>, redeem, with <zo>, be able) (s:tanhzo/tatkikzawh) (b:tankhia) (q:draft)
tanlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fasting) (d:<tan>, abstain, with <lam>, the fact that: {an tanlam}, the fact that one is fasting) (s:antanna) (q:draft)
tanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cutting/cutting off) (d:<tan>, cut, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of cutting off; {sam at tanna} is cutting off the hair, {phuk tanna} is being cut down) (b:tan) (q:draft)
tanna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:sentence/judgment/punishment) (d:in {thu tanna}: the deciding of a case and the punishment given; {thu tanna thuak} is be judged or be under sentence) (s:thukhenna/thutanna) (q:draft)
tanote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:children/little children/young) (d:plural: the young of people or animals; {ka tanote aw} is a fond address, my little children) (s:taneute/naupangnote) (q:draft)
Tanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Redeemer) (d:<tan>, redeem, with <pa>, the one who redeems; capitalised as a title of God) (s:Tankhiapa/Honpa) (b:Tan) (r:23.47.4) (q:draft)
tansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:priced/valued) (d:with <man>, price: {a man a tansa}, whose price has been set; <tan>, set or fix, with <sa>, already done) (q:draft, low confidence)
tansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut off/have cut off/behead) (d:<tan>, cut off, with the causative <sak>: have something cut off; with <lutang>, head, or <ngawng>, neck, behead) (s:sattan/attan) (b:tan) (q:draft)
tantan = (t:todo) (q:draft, follows <hanciam> strive in one verse about someone trying hard to escape; perhaps with all his might or again and again, not clear)
Tanu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:daughter) (d:<tanu> written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in names for a city and its people, such as {Zion Tanu}, Daughter Zion) (b:tanu) (q:draft)
tanungak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:virgin daughter/maiden daughter) (d:<tanu>, daughter, with <nungak>, virgin or young woman; said of the city of Zion) (q:draft)
tanute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:daughters) (d:<tanu>, daughter, with the plural <te>) (a:tapate) (b:tanu) plural form of <tanu>
tanvei = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:how long) (d:a length of time, found in the question {bang tanvei}, how long) (q:draft)
tanzau = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:spacious/broad/wide/roomy) (d:of a place, wide and open; {mun tanzau}, a spacious place) (s:zai) (a:kawciik/kawcik) (q:draft)
tanzauna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spaciousness/abundance/wideness) (d:<tanzau>, spacious, with the noun suffix <na>; {a tanzauna mun} is a spacious place, a place of abundance) (b:tanzau) (q:draft)
tanzumte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hips/hip joints) (d:a part of the body named with <phei> thigh, where the NIV has legs and the KJV joints of thy thighs; with the plural <te>) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tapa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Son) (d:the Son, written with a capital in titles of Jesus such as {Mihing Tapa} Son of Man and {David’ Tapa} Son of David) (b:tapa) (q:draft)
tapate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sons) (d:<tapa>, son, with the plural <te>) (a:tanute) (b:tapa) (r:1.6.2) plural form of <tapa>
tapeeng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:twins) (d:two children born at one birth) (q:draft)
tapeuh = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after a verb and before <hen> in a wish: may it indeed be so; apparently <ta> with <peuh>) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tapil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wise son/wise child) (d:<ta>, child, with <pil>, wise, written as one word at the start of a proverb; set against <tahai>, foolish child) (a:tahai) (q:draft)
tapkhap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:break/be crushed) (d:said of the heart, <lungsim>: be broken by grief) (q:draft, low confidence)
tapkual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hearth/fireside) (d:in the expression <tapkual han>, bold only at one's own fireside, said of a person who is bold when away and timid face to face; the meaning of the word alone is not shown by the verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
