thahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:killing/murder/bloodshed/slaughter) (d:<thah>, form of <that>, kill, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of killing; {mi thahna} is murder or bloodshed) (s:thatna/mithahna) (b:thah) (q:draft)
Thahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:killing/bloodshed) (d:<thahna>, killing, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the place name {Mi Thahna Lo}, the field of killing people, Field of Blood in the NIV) (b:thahna) (r:44.1.19) (q:draft)
thahnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:murders/killings) (d:<thahna>, killing, with the plural <te>: acts of murder) (b:thahna) (q:draft)
