thawhkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise from the dead/raise again) (d:<thawhkik>, rise again, with the causative <sak>: make someone rise again from death) (s:thawhsakkik/hingsakkik/thosakkik) (b:thawhkik) (q:draft)
thawhkiksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:raising to life/resurrection) (d:<thawhkiksak>, raise again, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact of having raised someone from death) (s:thawhsakkikna/hinkiksakna) (b:thawhkiksak) (q:draft)
thawhkiksakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one raised to life) (d:<thawhkiksak>, raise again, with <pa> marking a man: in the verse, the man whom Jesus raised from the dead) (b:thawhkiksak) (q:draft)
thawhlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rising/getting up) (d:<thawh>, rise, with <lam>: the fact or moment of getting up, paired with <luplam>, lying down) (a:luplam) (r:1.19.35) (q:draft)
thawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise/raise up) (d:<thawh>, rise, with the causative <sak>: make someone rise, especially from death) (s:thosak/hingkiksak) (b:thawh) (q:draft)
thawhsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raise again/raise up/bring back to life) (d:<thawhsak>, make rise, with <kik>, again: raise someone from death) (s:thawhkiksak/thokiksak/hingkiksak) (b:thawhsak) (q:draft)
thawhsakkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:resurrection/raising again) (d:<thawhsakkik>, raise again, with the noun suffix <na>: the raising of someone from death) (s:thawhkiksakna/hinkiksakna) (b:thawhsakkik) (q:draft)
thawhtoh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come up/rise up/go up) (d:<thawh>, rise, with <toh>, upward: come up, as out of the water; the form used before {lai takin}) (a:kumsuk) (b:thawh) (q:draft)
thawhtohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rising up/arising) (d:<thawhtoh>, rise up, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of rising up) (b:thawhtoh) (q:draft)
thawhzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to get up/recover) (d:<thawh>, rise, with <zawh>, a form of <zo>, be able: be able to get up again after an injury) (s:thozo/damkik) (q:draft)
thawi = (i:1) (t:v) (w:search/rummage through/ransack) (d:go through a house or belongings looking for something) (q:draft)
thawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bottle/jar/flask/skin) (d:container for liquids such as water, oil or wine; {savun thawl} is a wineskin, and {thawl khat} also renders the liquid measure hin) (q:draft)
thawlkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one jar/a bottle) (d:<thawl>, bottle or jar, with <khat>, one, written as one word) (q:draft)
thawlpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:large jar/measure) (d:<thawl>, jar, with <pi>, big: a large jar; in Haggai a measure of wine) (b:thawl) (q:draft)
thawlsan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:flask/jar) (d:a container of the <thawl> kind, here one filled with perfume; the part <san> is not explained by the verse) (b:thawl) (q:draft, low confidence)
thawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shake/quake/resound) (d:shake or ring with a loud noise, said of the ground or the shore) (s:liing) (q:draft)
thawn = (i:2) (t:v) (w:thunder against/startle) (d:strike with a loud noise so as to throw into panic) (q:draft, low confidence)
thawnkham = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shake/resound) (d:<thawn>, shake, written as one word with <kham>: of the ground, shake and ring with the noise of a crowd) (s:thawn/liing) (q:draft)
thazaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be weak/grow weak/fail/lose heart) (d:<tha>, strength, with <zaw>, weak: have no strength left, said of eyes, hands and courage; {thazaw sak} is weaken or discourage) (b:tha) (q:draft)
thazawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:faint/weak) (d:<tha>, strength, with <zawm>, weak: faint and worn out, as with hunger) (s:thazawng/thanem/zawngkhal) (a:thahat/hat) (q:draft)
thazawng = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:weak/debilitated/feeble) (d:having little strength, weak; said of the body and of people) (s:thanem/thaneem/zawngkhal) (a:thahat/hat) (r:40.26.41)
thazawngkhal = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:powerless/feeble/weak) (d:<tha>, strength, with <zawngkhal>, weak, written as one word: without strength, powerless) (s:thazawng/zawngkhal/thanem) (a:thahat) (q:draft)
thazawngte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:weak/debilitated) (d:<thazawng>, weak, with the plural <te>: the weak, people who are weak) (b:thazawng)
thazawsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:weaken/discourage/let hang limp) (d:<thazaw>, be weak, with the causative <sak>: take away strength or courage; of hands, let them hang limp) (s:thanemsak/thakiamsak/lungkiasak) (a:thahatsak/thakhauhsak) (b:thazaw) (q:draft)
thazung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:root) (d:said of the root of the olive tree whose sap feeds the branches; {thazung tui} is its sap) (s:zung) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thebes = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Thebes) (d:chief city of Upper Egypt on the Nile, against which the prophets announced judgment) (r:26.30.14/26.30.15/34.3.8)
Thebez = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Thebez) (d:town near Shechem where Abimelek son of Gideon was killed by a millstone a woman dropped on him) (r:7.9.50/10.11.21)
theem = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:thin/shrivelled/withered) (d:said of heads of grain that are poor and empty; which of the three English words it answers to is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
theemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scorch/blast/wither) (d:<theem>, thin, with the causative <sak>: of the east wind, make ears of grain thin and dried up) (s:keusak) (b:theem) (q:draft)
theemsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scorching/withering) (d:<theemsak> cause to shrivel with the connective <in>; said of the east wind blasting ears of grain) (s:keusakin) (b:theemsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
theh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sprinkle/splash) (d:throw a liquid in drops over something, as blood on the altar or oil before the Lord) (q:draft)
thehin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sprinkling/splashing/scattering) (d:<theh>, sprinkle, with the linking ending <in>: sprinkling, before the next action in the sentence) (b:theh) (q:draft)
thehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sprinkling/splashing) (d:<theh> sprinkle with the noun suffix <na>: the act of sprinkling blood) (b:theh) (q:draft)
thehthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scatter/disperse) (d:throw or drive apart in all directions: scatter a people among the nations, or scatter things such as frost and arrows) (s:khenthang) (a:kaikhawm/khawm) (q:draft)
thehthangin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scattering/dispersing) (d:<thehthang>, scatter, with the linking ending <in>: scattering, before the next action in the sentence) (a:khawmin) (b:thehthang) (q:draft)
thehthangna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scattering/dispersion) (d:noun of <thehthang>, scatter; before <gam> or with <panin> it names the place to which people were scattered, as {note kong thehthangna gamte}, the lands where I scattered you) (b:thehthang) (q:draft)
thehthangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who scattered) (d:<thehthang> scatter with <pa> marking a male person: he who scattered them) (b:thehthang) (q:draft)
thehthangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have scattered) (d:<thehthang> scatter with <zo> marking that the act is completed) (b:thehthang) (q:draft)
thei = (i:3) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:fig) (d:the fig; {thei gah} is the fruit, {thei kung} the tree and {thei moh} a cake of pressed figs) (s:theigah)
Thei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:know/see/look) (d:<thei>, know, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or of quoted speech; {thei in} is the command know, often translated see or look) (b:thei) (q:draft, low confidence)
theiba = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:sycamore-fig/sycamore) (d:the sycamore-fig tree, common in the foothills; said as {theiba sing} or {theiba kung}) (s:theithek/theitheek) (q:draft)
theigah = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:fig) (d:the fruit of the fig tree) (s:thei/theipum) (q:draft)
theigahte = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:figs) (d:<theigah>, fig, with the plural <te>; in a list of crops it also stands for the fig trees) (b:theigah) (q:draft)
theih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be know/know/be able) (d:form of <thei>, know or be able, used before words such as <ni>, <ma-in>, <loh>, <ding> and <nading>; <theih nadingin> is so that one may) (b:thei) (r:40.24.50)
theihhak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:hard to understand/obscure) (d:<theih>, know, with <hak>, hard: difficult to know or understand, said of a saying or riddle) (s:telhak/theihtelhak) (q:draft)
theihin = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:before/in the presence of/with the knowledge of) (d:<theih>, know, with the ending <in>, placed after a possessive: with that person knowing, in the hearing or sight of; {mite’ theihin} is before people, openly) (s:muhin) (b:theih) (q:draft)
theihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come to know/learn/get to know) (d:<theih>, know, with <khak>, happen to: come to know or learn something) (q:draft)
theihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:find out/discover/fathom) (d:<theih>, know, with <khiat>, out: come to know by searching; the form used before a noun or <zawh>) (s:phawkkhiat/kankhiat) (b:theih) (q:draft)
theihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have come to know/know fully/finish learning) (d:<theih>, know, with <khit>, finished: {theihkhit ciangin} is after one has come to know, {theihkhit phetin} as soon as one knows) (s:theikhin) (q:draft)
theihkhitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knowing already/full knowledge) (d:<theihkhit> have come to know, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact of already knowing) (b:theihkhit) (q:draft)
theihkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:foreknow/know beforehand) (d:<theih>, know, with <khol>, beforehand: know in advance) (q:draft)
theihkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:know beforehand/find out in advance/foresee) (d:<theih>, know, with <kholh>, beforehand; {theihkholh lohin}, without knowing beforehand, means unexpectedly, suddenly) (s:mukhol) (b:theihkhol) (q:draft)
theihkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foreknowledge) (d:<theihkholh> know beforehand with the noun suffix <na>) (b:theihkholh) (q:draft)
theihkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being able again) (d:<theih> able with <kik> again and the noun suffix <na>; {khua muh theihkikna} is the regaining of sight) (q:draft)
theihkim = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:well-known/known to all/commonly known) (d:<theih>, know, with <kim>, all: known to everyone, well known or in common use) (s:minthang) (q:draft)
theihkim = (i:2) (t:v) (w:come to know/know fully) (d:<theih>, know, with <kim>, all: of everyone, come to know; also be known by all) (q:draft, low confidence)
theihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ability to know/way of knowing) (d:<theih> know or able with <lam> way, manner; in the verse, that someone is able to know all mysteries) (q:draft, low confidence)
theihlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:unintentionally/ignorance/lack of understanding) (d:<theih>, know, with <loh>, not, and the noun suffix <na>: not knowing, ignorance; {theihlohna hangin} is through ignorance, unintentionally) (s:mawlna) (a:theihna)
theihma = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:before being able) (d:<theih> able with <ma> before, placed after a verb: before one could do it) (q:draft)
theihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knowledge) (d:<theih>, know, with the noun suffix <na>: what one knows, knowledge) (s:pilna/thutheihna) (a:theihlohna/mawlna) (b:theih)
theihna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:understanding) (d:the power to think and understand; {thu ngaihsut theihna} is good sense or discretion) (s:thutelna/theihtelna) (a:haina) (b:theih) (r:18.28.28)
theihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knowledge/understanding) (d:plural of <theihna>, the things one knows; also the way one came to know something) (s:pilnate) (b:theihna) (r:42.24.35) (q:draft)
theihngei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have ever known) (d:<theih> know with <ngei> ever; with {nai lo}, have never yet known) (q:draft)
theihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to know/wish to know) (d:<theih> know, with <nop> want; the form used before a noun, as in {theihnop thu}, a thing someone wants to know) (q:draft)
theihnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:desire to know/wish to know) (d:<theihnop> want to know with the noun suffix <na>) (b:theihnop) (q:draft)
theihnopte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things one wants to know) (d:<theihnop> want to know with the plural <te>; {thu theihnopte} are the matters people want to learn by inquiring) (b:theihnop) (q:draft)
theihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able at once) (d:<theih> able with <pah> at once, placed after a verb: can do it right away) (q:draft, low confidence)
theihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:witness/be witness to) (d:know about a matter together with someone, so as to be a witness to it; {a theihpih mite} are the witnesses, and {theihpih lohin} is without the knowledge of) (b:theih) (r:24.32.44) (q:draft)
theihpih = (i:2) (t:v) (w:boast in/take pride in) (d:in the phrase {kisak theihpih}: be proud of something, boast in it) (s:kisaktheihpih/kisialhpih/kiphatsakpih) (q:draft, low confidence)
theihsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:known/already known) (d:<theih>, know, with <sa>, which marks something already done: what one already knows or has come to know) (b:theih) (r:5.7.15) (q:draft)
theihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make known/inform/reveal/warn) (d:<theih>, know, with the causative <sak>: cause someone to know, make known, reveal or warn) (s:zasak/pulak/kilangsak) (a:seel/im) (b:theih) (q:draft)
theihsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:signal/alarm/sign/notice) (d:<theihsak>, make known, with <na>: something that gives notice, such as a trumpet blast or a smoke signal; {theihsakna lim} is a sign) (b:theihsak) (q:draft)
theihsaknop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to make known/choose to reveal) (d:<theihsak>, make known, with <nop>, want: wish to make something known to someone; the form used before a noun) (r:42.10.22) (q:draft)
theihsiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good judgment/discernment/understanding) (d:<theih>, know, with <siam>, skilled, and the noun suffix <na>: the skill of knowing well, good judgment) (s:theihtelna/thutelna) (q:draft)
theihtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:know by oneself/find out on one's own) (d:<theih>, know, with <tawm>, by oneself: come to know something by one’s own effort, without being told) (q:draft)
theihtawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:own understanding/own knowledge) (d:<theihtawm> know by oneself, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:theihtawm) (q:draft)
theihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things that can be) (d:<theih> with plural <te> after a verb: the things that can be so used; {tum theihte} instruments that are played, {nek theihte} things that can be eaten) (b:theih) (q:draft)
theihte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:acquaintances) (d:in {mel theihte}, those known by face) (s:meltheihte/meeltheihte/theisate) (b:theih) (q:draft)
theihtel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:understand/comprehend/know fully) (d:<theih>, know, with <tel>, clearly: know thoroughly; also used as a noun, full knowledge) (s:teltheih/tel) (q:draft)
theihtelhak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:hard to understand) (d:<theihtel> understand with <hak> hard) (s:telhak/theihhak) (q:draft)
theihtelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:understanding/discernment/knowledge) (d:clear and full knowing of a matter) (s:thutelna/pilna/lungpilna/theihna) (a:mawlna/haina) (b:theihtel) (q:draft)
theihtelnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:understandings/understanding) (d:plural of <theihtelna>) (b:theihtelna) (q:draft)
theihtelnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to understand/long to understand) (d:<theihtel> understand with <nop> want) (q:draft)
theihteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all that one knows) (d:<theih> know with <teng> all, the whole of) (b:theih) (q:draft)
theihthang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:scatter) (d:in the verse the horns that scattered Judah; probably a misprint of <thehthang> scatter) (q:draft, low confidence)
theihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to understand/can know) (d:<theih>, know, with <theih>, be able) (s:teltheih/telthei/telzawh) (b:theih) (q:draft)
theihtheih = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:as much as possible) (d:after a descriptive word: as much as possible; {hunsau theihtheih} is as long a time as possible) (q:draft, low confidence)
theihtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knowledge/understanding) (d:the ability to know) (s:theihna) (b:theihtheih) (q:draft)
theihtheihna = (i:2) (t:n) (d:after a descriptive word, a way of being so as far as possible; {hun sau theihtheihna}, a means of making the time as long as can be) (b:theihtheih) (q:draft, low confidence)
theihtheihsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:already known/already understood) (d:<theihtheih> with <sa> already done: what one has come to know) (s:theihsa) (b:theihtheih) (q:draft)
theihzah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as much as one can) (d:<theih> able with <zah> amount, placed after a verb: to the extent one is able) (q:draft)
theihzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:understand/comprehend/find out) (d:be able to know or grasp; after a possessive, what someone is able to understand) (s:teltheih/telzawh) (q:draft)
theihzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ability to know fully/ability to fathom) (d:<theihzawh> be able to know, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:theihzawh) (q:draft)
theihzawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:know more/know better) (d:<theih> know with <zawk> more, used with <sangin> than) (q:draft)
theihzel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be apt to/be used to) (d:<theih> able with <zel> habitually, placed after a verb: something one tends to do again and again) (q:draft, low confidence)
theikha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:experience/come to know/know) (d:get to know or taste something for oneself; with {ngei lo} or {nai lo}, never having experienced) (q:draft)
theikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:know together/understand together) (d:<thei> know with <khawm> together) (b:thei) (q:draft)
theikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:find out/discover/come to know) (d:<thei>, know, with <khia>, out: come to know something by searching or thinking it through) (s:mukhia/phawkkhia/kankhia) (b:thei) (q:draft)
theikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:already know/know fully) (d:<thei> know, with <khin>, already, completely) (s:theihkhit) (b:thei) (q:draft)
theikhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:know beforehand/know in advance/foreknow) (d:<thei>, know, with <khol>, ahead of time) (q:draft)
