thuah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in addition/additionally/as well) (d:placed after a verb: do something in addition to what is already done, given or worn, as in {ci thuah}, say further, and {silh thuah}, wear an extra layer) (q:draft)
thuahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in addition/on top/besides/more) (d:<thuah> with the ending <in>, after a verb: doing it over or on top of what is there already, adding a further layer or more of the same) (b:thuah) (q:draft)
thuahkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:combine with/do along with) (d:<thuah> in addition with <khawm> together: take on one work together with another, be involved in it as well) (b:thuah) (q:draft)
thuahpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow at once with/add straight after) (d:<thuah> add on with <pah> at once: do a second thing right after the first) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:additional gifts/special gifts) (d:<thuah> in addition with the plural <te>, in {piak thuahte}: the things given on top of the tithe) (b:thuah) (r:5.12.11) (q:draft)
thuahthuah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:one after another/again and again/more and more) (d:<thuah> said twice: one thing added on another, repeatedly) (s:kikkik/zelzel) (q:draft)
thuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear/suffer/undergo) of punishment, suffering
thuak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:endure) (d:hold out under something hard without giving way; {thuak zo} and {thuak thei} are be able to endure)
thuakhak = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cruel/harsh/hard to bear) (d:<thuak>, bear, with <hak>, hard: hard to endure, said of a harsh master) (q:draft)
thuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffering/enduring/bearing) (d:<thuak>, suffer or bear, with the linking suffix <in>, used when another action follows; {lungduai takin thuakin} is enduring patiently) (b:thuak) (r:58.6.15) (q:draft)
thuakkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer/undergo/incur) (d:<thuak>, suffer, with <kha>, happen to: come to experience something bad) (s:thuaklawh) (q:draft)
thuakkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer/undergo/incur) (d:form of <thuakkha> used before <ding> and {loh nading}: come to suffer something bad) (s:thuaklawh) (b:thuakkha) (q:draft)
thuakkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer together/suffer with/share in) (d:<thuak>, bear or suffer, with <khawm>, together: undergo something along with another) (s:thuakpih) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuakkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have suffered/have undergone) (d:<thuak>, suffer or bear, with <khin> marking a completed action: have already undergone) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer in return/bear in turn/undergo again) (d:<thuak>, bear or undergo, with <kik>, back or again: have something come back on oneself, or undergo it again) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuaklahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being unable to resist/being enslaved by) (d:<thuak> bear with <lah> and the linking suffix <in>; in the verse, being overcome by desires) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuaklawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer/incur/bring upon oneself) (d:have to bear something, such as harm or suffering, as the result of what one does) (s:thuakkha) (r:52.1.6) (q:draft)
thuakma = (t:see) <thuakma-in>
thuakma-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:before suffering) (d:<thuak>, suffer, with <ma>, before, and the suffix <in>: before suffering something) (q:draft)
thuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:suffering/affliction/endurance) (d:<thuak>, suffer or bear, with the noun suffix <na>: what a person suffers, and also the patient bearing of it) (s:gimna/gimthuakna/gentheihna) (a:nopna) (b:thuak) (r:47.6.4) (q:draft)
thuaknasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:past suffering) (d:<thuakna> suffering with <sa> already: what someone has already suffered) (b:thuakna) (q:draft)
thuaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sufferings/afflictions) (d:<thuakna>, suffering, with the plural <te>) (s:gimnate) (b:thuakna) (q:draft)
thuakngap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear/dare to endure) (d:<thuak>, bear, with <ngap>, dare; with <lo> it is could not bear) (q:draft)
thuaknuam = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:willing to suffer) (d:<thuak> suffer with <nuam> willing, wanting) (q:draft)
thuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who bears/sufferer) (d:<thuak> bear, suffer with <pa> marking a man: the man who undergoes something) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer at once/undergo immediately) (d:<thuak> bear, undergo with <pah> at once) (q:draft)
thuakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bear with/put up with/suffer with) (d:<thuak>, bear, with <pih>, together with: share in another person’s trouble, or be patient with his weakness) (s:thuakkhawm) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make suffer/inflict/afflict) (d:<thuak>, suffer, with the causative <sak>: make someone undergo something, bring suffering on someone) (s:gimsak/tuaksak) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuaksakgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make suffer severely/pour out on) (d:<thuaksak> make suffer with <gawp> thoroughly, violently; of anger, pour it out on someone) (b:thuaksak) (q:draft)
thuaksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:making suffer/making bear) (d:<thuaksak> make suffer with the linking suffix <in>) (b:thuaksak) (q:draft)
thuakta = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer/bear/undergo) (d:<thuak>, bear, with <ta> marking that the state has now come: now suffer, come to bear) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who suffer/the afflicted/the oppressed) (d:<thuak>, suffer or bear, with the plural <te>: people who undergo hardship or oppression, often in {gimna thuakte}, the afflicted) (s:gentheite/kinengniamte) (b:thuak) (r:19.9.9) (q:draft)
thuakthuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep suffering/suffer again and again/face repeatedly) (d:<thuak>, bear or suffer, doubled for repeated action: suffer something again and again, as in {sihna a thuakthuak}, one who faces death daily) (q:draft)
thuakzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:suffer more/bear more) (d:<thuak>, suffer, with <zaw>, more: suffer more than another; also rather suffer, as in {thuakzaw mai lo}, why not rather be wronged) (b:thuak) (q:draft)
thuakzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:endure/bear/persevere) (d:be able to bear, endure; the form of <thuakzo> used before <nading> and in noun phrases, where English often has endurance or perseverance) (s:thuakzo) (a:lungkiat) (q:draft)
thuakzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:perseverance/endurance/patience) (d:<thuakzawh>, be able to bear, with the noun suffix <na>: the strength to endure hardship without giving up) (s:lungduaina/kithuakzawhna) (a:lungtomna) (b:thuakzawh) (r:45.5.4) (q:draft)
thuakzawhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:endurance/perseverance) (d:plural of <thuakzawhna>) (b:thuakzawhna) (q:draft)
thuakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:endure/withstand/be able to bear) (d:<thuak>, bear, with <zo>, be able: be able to bear something, hold out to the end) (s:thuakzawh/nangzo) (a:lungkia) (b:thuak) (r:40.20.22) (q:draft)
thuakzote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who endure/those who stand firm) (d:<thuakzo>, endure, with the plural <te>: the people who hold out) (s:kipte) (b:thuakzo) (q:draft)
thuambuak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (w:rue) (d:rue, a strong-smelling garden herb; named after <lengmasel>, mint, in the list of herbs on which the Pharisees paid a tenth) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuap = (i:1) (t:v) (w:patch/add on top/overlay/layer) (d:put one thing on or over another as a further layer: patch cloth, panel a wall with boards; {koih thuap} is add one thing on top of another) (s:phop) (q:draft)
thuap = (i:2) (t:n) (w:layer/fold/course/storey) (d:one thickness of something folded, laid or built one on another; {thuap nih} is two layers or folded double, {suang thuap thum} three courses of stone, {inn thuap thum} the third storey of a house) (q:draft)
thuapna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:patch/patching) (d:<thuap> put on as a further layer, with the noun suffix <na>: the piece put on, or the act of patching; {thuapna puan} is the patch) (b:thuap) (q:draft)
thuapthuapin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:doubly/layer upon layer) (d:<thuap> layer, doubled, with the suffix <in>; in the verse of sin heaped on sin) (q:draft, low confidence)
thubul = (i:1) (t:n) (w:theme) (d:the main subject of a speech, song or piece of writing)
thubul = (i:2) (t:n) (w:subject/topic)
thubul = (i:3) (t:n) (w:subject matter)
Thubul = (i:1) (t:n) (w:theme/subject) (d:<thubul> written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (b:thubul) (q:draft)
thubulpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sum/essence/main substance) (d:<thubul> subject with <pi> great: the main substance of what is said, here of the word of God) (b:thubul) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuciam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promise/vow/covenant/oath) (d:a solemn promise: a vow made to God, a promise given by God, or a covenant between two parties) (s:thuciamna/kiciamna/kamciam/kamciamna) (q:draft)
thuciam = (i:2) (t:v) (w:promise/vow/swear) (d:make a solemn promise or vow; {thuciam khin} is has promised) (s:kiciam/ciam/kamciam) (q:draft)
Thuciam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:covenant/testament) (d:<thuciam> written with a capital in titles: {Thuciam Lui}, the old covenant or Old Testament; {Thuciam Gam}, the land of the covenant, Beautiful Land in the NIV) (s:Thuciamna) (b:thuciam) (q:draft)
thuciamin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:promising/vowing) (d:<thuciam> promise with the linking ending <in>: making a promise, having promised) (b:thuciam) (q:draft)
thuciammna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:covenant/promise) (d:the covenant terms given at the exodus; probably a misprint of <thuciamna>) (s:thuciamna) (q:draft)
thuciamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:covenant) (d:a solemn binding agreement, above all the covenant between God and his people; {thuciamna bawl} is make a covenant) (s:thuciam/thukimna) (b:thuciam) (r:1.6.18)
thuciamna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:deal) (d:an agreement or treaty that people make with one another) (s:thukimna) (b:thuciam)
Thuciamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:covenant/promise) (d:capitalised in titles such as {Thuciamna Singkuang}, the ark of the covenant, {Thuciamna thak}, the new covenant, and {Thuciamna Gam}, the promised land) (s:Thuciam) (b:thuciamna) (r:58.8.8) (q:draft)
thuciamnasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vow made/promise made/covenant made) (d:<thuciamna>, promise or covenant, with <sa>, already done: the vow, promise or covenant that has been made) (s:thuciamsa) (b:thuciamna) (q:draft)
thuciamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promises/vows) (d:plural of <thuciamna>; God's promises or the vows a person has made) (s:thuciamte/kiciamnate/kamciamnate) (b:thuciamna) (q:draft)
thuciampih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:covenant partner) (d:<thuciam> covenant with <pih> together with: one who is in covenant with someone) (s:thuciampihpa) (b:thuciam) (q:draft)
thuciampihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:covenant partner) (d:<thuciampih> with <pa> marking a man: the man in covenant with someone) (s:thuciampih) (b:thuciampih) (q:draft)
thuciamsa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promise made/vow made/what was promised) (d:<thuciam>, promise, with <sa> marking a completed action: what has been promised or vowed) (s:thuciamnasa) (b:thuciam) (q:draft)
thuciamsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vows/promises made) (d:<thuciamsa> what has been vowed, with the plural <te>) (s:thuciamnate/thuciamte) (b:thuciamsa) (q:draft)
thuciamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promises/covenants/vows) (d:<thuciam>, promise or covenant, with the plural <te>) (s:thuciamnate/kiciamnate/kamciamnate) (b:thuciam) (q:draft)
thuciamteh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:recorder) (d:<thu>, matter, with <ciamteh>, record; in the verses always followed by <pa>: {thuciamteh pa}, the official who keeps the king's records) (s:thuciamtehpa) (q:draft)
thuciamtehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:record/records) (d:the writing down of matters, <thuciamteh> note down a matter with the noun suffix <na>; {thuciamtehna laibu} is a book of records, an archive) (s:ciamtehna/kiciamtehna) (b:thuciamteh) (q:draft)
thuciamtehpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:recorder/chronicler) (d:<thuciamteh> with <pa>, the man: the court official who keeps the records) (s:thuciamteh) (b:thuciamteh) (q:draft)
thudam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gentleness/peaceable manner) (d:<thu>, word or manner, with <dam>, gentle: a gentle, peaceable way; {thudam tawh} is gently, without force) (s:lungnemna/thunem/nemna) (a:ngongbawlna) (q:draft)
thudamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:peaceably/peacefully) (d:<thudam> with the adverb suffix <in>: without a quarrel) (b:thudam) (q:draft)
thudang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:another thing/another matter/anything else) (d:<thu>, matter, with <dang>, other) (s:nadang) (r:46.2.2) (q:draft)
thudangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:other matters/other things) (d:<thudang> other matter with the plural <te>) (s:nadangte) (b:thudang) (q:draft)
Thudas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Theudas) (d:man who claimed to be somebody and gathered about four hundred followers before he was killed, cited by Gamaliel) (r:44.5.36)
thudawnna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:answer/reply) (d:<thu>, word, with <dawnna>, answering: the answer given to a question) (s:dawnkikna) (a:thudotna/dotna) (q:draft)
thudik = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:upright/just/fair/trustworthy) (d:<thu>, matter, with <dik>, right: dealing rightly and fairly with others, worthy of trust) (s:dik/thutang/diktat) (a:gilo/gitloh) (q:draft)
thudikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness/uprightness) (d:<thudik>, upright, with the noun suffix <na>: what is right and just) (s:dikna/diktatna/thumanna) (a:gitlohna/gilohna) (b:thudik) (q:draft)
thudon = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pay attention/heed/take note/consider) (d:give heed to what is said or seen, take it to heart; {thudon lo} and {thudon kei} are pay no attention) (s:don/ngai) (a:mawhbawl) (q:draft)
thudong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:inquire/ask/consult) (d:<thu>, matter, with <dong>, ask: seek an answer from God or from a person) (s:dong/thudot/thukan) (a:dawng) (q:draft)
thudonin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:heeding/paying attention) (d:<thudon> pay attention, with the linking ending <in>; {thudonin nei} is take to heart, pay heed to) (b:thudon) (q:draft)
thudot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:question/ask/inquire) (d:<thu>, matter, and <dot>, ask: put questions to someone) (s:dong/dot/thudong/thukan) (a:dawng) (q:draft)
thudot = (i:2) (t:n) (w:counsel/advice/consultation) (d:asking for advice; found in {thudot mite}, the men a king asks for advice: his counsellors or wise men) (q:draft)
thudotin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as one to consult/as an oracle) (d:<thudot>, one who is asked for advice or for a word from a god, with the marker <in>; {thudotin nei} is consult, {thudotin om} is be consulted) (b:thudot) (q:draft, low confidence)
thudotna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:question/inquiry/questioning) (d:<thudot>, ask about a matter, with the noun suffix <na>: a question or the act of questioning; {thudotna thuak} is be questioned, give account) (s:dotna/thukanna) (a:thudawnna/dawnkikna) (b:thudot) (q:draft)
thudotnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:questions) (d:plural of <thudotna>) (s:dotnate) (b:thudotna) (q:draft)
thudotte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:advisers/counsellors/wise men) (d:<thudot>, counsel, with the plural <te>: those whom a king asks for advice) (s:lamlakte/thulamlakte/thukuppihte) (b:thudot) (r:27.3.24) (q:draft)
Thugen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speak/preach) (d:<thugen>, speak or preach, capitalised in titles, {Thugen Siampa} the Teacher of Ecclesiastes, {Thugen Kholhna} the Prophecy of Ahijah) (b:thugen) (r:14.9.29) (q:draft)
thugenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:speaking/saying) (d:<thugen> speak, with the linking ending <in>: speaking, or as what one speaks) (b:thugen) (q:draft)
thugenkholh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophecy/prediction) (d:<thu>, word, with <genkholh>, tell beforehand: what is spoken beforehand, foretelling) (s:genkholhna/thugenkholhna) (q:draft)
thugenkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prophecy/prediction) (d:<thugenkholh> speak of a thing beforehand, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:genkholhna/thugenkholh) (b:thugenkholh) (q:draft)
thugenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:speech/words/saying) (d:<thugen>, speak, with the noun suffix <na>: what someone says, or the act and manner of speaking) (s:kampau/kampauna/pauna/genna) (b:thugen) (r:54.4.12) (q:draft)
thugennate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/sayings/speeches) (d:plural of <thugenna>: the things someone says) (s:thugente/kammalte) (b:thugenna) (q:draft)
thugennna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:word/saying) (d:what someone has spoken; probably a misprint of <thugenna>) (s:thugenna) (q:draft)
thugenpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:speaker/the one who speaks) (d:<thugen> speak with <pa> marking a man: the man who is speaking or who spoke) (s:genpa) (b:thugen) (q:draft)
thugenpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:chief speaker/main speaker) (d:<thugen> speak with <pi> great, chief) (b:thugen) (q:draft)
thugente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/sayings) (d:<thugen>, speak, with the plural <te>: the things that someone says) (s:thugennate/kammalte/gente) (b:thugen) (r:20.1.6) (q:draft)
thugentehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:parable/story/illustration) (d:a story or comparison told to teach a truth; from <thu>, word, and <genteh>, compare, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:thungentehna) (r:42.15.3) (q:draft)
Thugentehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:parable) (d:<thugentehna>, parable, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the title of a parable) (b:thugentehna) (q:draft)
thugentehnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:parables) (d:plural of <thugentehna>) (b:thugentehna) (q:draft)
thugenzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of speaking/statement/testimony) (d:<thugen> speak with <zia> manner: how someone speaks or what he states) (q:draft)
thugetna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prayer/plea) (d:in the verse a prayer from lips without deceit; probably a misprint of <thungetna>) (s:thungetna) (q:draft, low confidence)
thugik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grave message/heavy news/bad news) (d:<thu> word with <gik> heavy: a weighty or hard message) (s:thusiate) (a:thuhoih) (q:draft)
thuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seal/stamp) (d:press a seal or signet on a document) (q:draft)
thuh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:repay/avenge) (d:in {thuh kikna}, repayment or vengeance; the same as <thuhkik> pay back a wrong) (s:thuhkik/thukkik) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuhaksa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:riddle/hard question/difficult matter) (d:<thu> matter with <haksa> hard: something hard to understand or answer) (q:draft)
thuhaksa = (i:2) (t:n) (w:trial/hardship/difficulty) (d:a hard thing that one has to go through) (s:haksatna/gentheihna) (q:draft)
thuhaksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:difficult cases/hard matters) (d:plural of <thuhaksa>; also of hard burdens laid on people) (b:thuhaksa) (q:draft)
thuhelhhawt = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:ruthless/violent) (d:describes men who seek to kill; the same word is written <thu-helhawt> in the other text) (s:thu-helhawt) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuhilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teach/preach/instruct) (d:<thu>, word, with <hilh>, teach: teach, preach or give instruction to people) (s:hilh/sinsak/hilhsak) (q:draft)
thuhilh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:discipline/rebuke/chastise) (d:correct someone by rebuke or punishment) (s:taii/taai/khal) (r:19.38.1) (q:draft)
Thuhilh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:preach/proclaim/teach) (d:<thuhilh>, teach or preach, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in {Lungdamna Thuhilh}, preaching the gospel) (b:thuhilh) (q:draft)
thuhilhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:teaching/instructing/disciplining) (d:<thuhilh>, teach, with the linking ending <in>: teaching, giving instructions to, or disciplining someone while doing something else) (b:thuhilh) (r:20.13.24) (q:draft)
thuhilhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:punish again/discipline further) (d:<thuhilh> discipline with <kik> again) (b:thuhilh) (q:draft)
thuhilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teaching/doctrine/instruction) (d:<thuhilh>, teach, with the noun suffix <na>: what is taught, or the act of teaching) (s:hilhna/kihilhna) (b:thuhilh) (r:20.19.27) (q:draft)
thuhilhna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:discipline/rebuke/correction) (d:correction by rebuke or punishment) (s:taiina/khalna) (b:thuhilh) (q:draft)
thuhilhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teachings/precepts/statutes) (d:plural of <thuhilhna>: the things God or a teacher teaches) (s:thuhilhte/hilhnate) (b:thuhilhna) (q:draft)
thuhilhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:teacher/preacher/overseer) (d:<thuhilh>, teach, with <pa> for a man: the man who teaches, preaches or corrects; in 1 Timothy 3 the office of overseer) (s:hilhpa/siapa) (b:thuhilh) (q:draft)
thuhilhsia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evangelist/preacher) (d:<thuhilh> preach, teach with <sia> teacher) (q:draft)
thuhilhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:precepts/teachings/instructions) (d:<thuhilh>, teach, with the plural <te>: the things that are taught) (s:thuhilhnate/hilhnate) (b:thuhilh) (r:20.3.2) (q:draft)
thuhilhte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:teachers) (d:<thuhilh>, teach, with the plural <te>: those who teach) (s:siate/laihilhte) (b:thuhilh) (q:draft)
thuhkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have sealed/have signed) (d:<thuh> seal, stamp with <khit> finished; <letmat thuh> is put a signature to an agreement) (q:draft)
thuhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:avenge/take vengeance/repay) (d:<thuh>, repay, with <kik>, back: pay back a wrong, take vengeance) (s:thukkik/phulak) (a:maisak) (q:draft)
thuhkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vengeance/revenge/retaliation) (d:<thuhkik>, pay back a wrong, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:phulakna/thukkikna) (a:mawhmaisakna) (b:thuhkik) (r:24.51.11) (q:draft)
thuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sealing/stamping) (d:<thuh> press a seal on, with the noun suffix <na>; {min thuhna zungbuh} is a signet ring, the ring that stamps the name) (b:thuh) (q:draft)
thuhna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:reward/repayment/recompense) (d:what is given back in return for something done) (s:thaman) (b:thuh) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good news/good word/good) (d:<thu>, word or matter, with <hoih>, good: good news or a good report, also what is good as opposed to <thusia>) (a:thusia/thugik) (r:10.18.25) (q:draft)
Thuhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good news/good) (d:<thuhoih>, good word or good thing, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in {Lungdamna Thuhoih}, the good news) (b:thuhoih) (q:draft)
thuhoihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good thing/good to come) (d:<thuhoih> good news, good with the noun suffix <na>; {mailam thuhoihna} is good things to come) (b:thuhoih) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuhoihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good things/good) (d:<thuhoih> with the plural <te>: good things, good deeds or good teaching) (s:hoihnate/nahoih) (a:thusiate) (b:thuhoih) (r:58.10.1) (q:draft)
thuin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:of one's own accord/by oneself) (d:<thu> with the suffix <in> after a possessive: {ama thuin} is of its own accord, by itself) (b:thu) (q:draft)
thuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:revenge/avenge/repay/pay back) (d:pay someone back for what he has done, usually a wrong) (s:thukkik/thuhkik/phulak) (a:maisak)
thuk = (i:2) (t:n) (w:payback) (s:loh) of loan, debt
thuk = (i:3) (t:v) (w:respond/reply/answer) (d:give an answer to a message, a letter or a question) (s:dawng/dawngkik)
thukan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spy/scout) (d:one who secretly searches out information about a land or an enemy, from <thu>, matter, and <kan>, search) (q:draft)
thukan = (i:2) (t:v) (w:inquire/investigate/ask) (d:look into a matter or ask for guidance, from <thu>, matter, and <kan>, search; {Topa kiangah thukan} is to inquire of the Lord) (s:thudot) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as spies/as a spy/to spy) (d:<thukan>, spy, with the marker <in>: as spies, in order to spy) (b:thukan) (q:draft)
thukanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:inquiry/investigation) (d:<thukan> inquire with the noun suffix <na>; in the verse the NIV has due punishment) (s:kanna) (b:thukan) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukansim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spy out/explore) (d:<thu> matter with <kansim> search out in secret: spy out a land) (s:kansim/ensim) (q:draft)
thukante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:spies/scouts) (d:plural of <thukan>: spies or scouts sent out to gather information) (s:kansimte/kante) (b:thukan) (q:draft)
thukawi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:devious/crooked/perverse) (d:not straight in word or conduct, from <thu> matter and <kawi> crooked; also as a noun, a crooked word) (s:kawi/lampial) (a:thutang/thudik) (q:draft)
thukham = (i:1) (t:n) (w:law/commandment) (d:a law or commandment, or the whole body of commandments given by God or by a ruler; {thukham zui} is to keep the law) (s:upadi/thukhamna) (r:40.22.38)
Thukham = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Law) (d:<thukham> written with a capital, the Law of God given through Moses) (s:Thukhamna) (b:thukham) (r:45.2.17) (q:draft)
thukhamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as a decree/as a law) (d:<thukham>, law, with the suffix <in>: as a law or decree) (b:thukham) (q:draft)
thukhamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:law/commandment) (d:<thukham>, law, with the noun suffix <na>: a law or a single commandment) (s:thukham/thupiakna/upadi) (b:thukham) (q:draft)
Thukhamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Law/law) (d:the Law of Moses, the first part of the Scriptures; {Thukhamna lai} is the book of the Law) (s:Thukham) (b:Thukham) (r:43.7.51) (q:draft)
thukhamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:laws/statutes/decrees) (d:<thukhamna> law with the plural <te>; paired with <thupiaknate>, commands) (s:thukhamte) (b:thukhamna) (q:draft)
Thukhamnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:laws/commandments) (d:<Thukhamna>, law, with the plural <te>; the commandments of the Law taken together) (s:Thukhamte) (b:Thukhamna) (q:draft)
thukhamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:decrees/laws/statutes/commands) (d:plural of <thukham>: the decrees, laws or statutes that are to be kept, often paired with <thupiaknate>, commands) (s:thukhamnate/ngeinate) (b:thukham) (q:draft)
Thukhamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Law/laws) (d:<Thukham>, the Law, with the plural <te>: {Moses Thukhamte}, the laws of Moses, the Law of Moses) (s:Thukhamnate) (b:Thukham) (q:draft)
thukhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one rule/one law/precept) (d:<thu>, word or law, with <khat>, one) (r:23.28.13) (q:draft)
thukhauh = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:harsh/severe/fierce) (d:<thu> word, matter with <khauh> hard: stern in what one says or orders; {thukhauh pa} is a harsh man, a tyrant; in Daniel 2:15 a harsh decree) (q:draft)
thukhen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:judge/pass judgment) (d:hear and decide a case, or rule a people as judge, from <thu>, matter, and <khen>, divide; {thukhen mangpa} is a judge) (s:thusit/khensak) (r:42.18.6) (q:draft)
Thukhen = (i:1) (t:n) (w:judgment) (d:<thukhen> written with a capital in fixed terms: {Thukhen Ni} is the Day of Judgment, {Thukhen zum} is the court of law) (s:Thukhenna) (b:thukhen) (q:draft)
Thukhen = (i:2) (t:n) (w:Judge) (d:in {Thukhen pa}, the Judge, as a title of God; also {thukhen mangpa}, judge, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (s:Thukhenpa) (b:thukhen) (q:draft)
thukhenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:judging/judge/as judge) (d:<thukhen> with the linking ending <in>, judging; also in the role of judge) (b:thukhen) (q:draft)
thukhenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:judgment/verdict/sentence/condemnation) (d:<thukhen>, judge, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of judging, or the verdict or sentence given; {thukhenna thuak} is to come under judgment) (s:thutanna/khenna) (b:thukhen) (r:43.16.11) (q:draft)
Thukhenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:judgment/justice) (d:<thukhenna> capitalised in a name: {Thukhenna Ni}, the Day of Judgment; {Thukhenna Innpi}, the Hall of Justice) (s:Thukhen) (b:thukhenna) (q:draft)
thukhennasa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:decree/decision) (d:what has already been decided or decreed, <thukhenna> judgment with <sa> already done) (s:thukhensatna) (b:thukhenna) (q:draft)
thukhennate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:judgments/decisions/rulings) (d:plural of <thukhenna>; in Psalm 119 God's judgments in the sense of his laws) (s:thukhensatnate/thutannate/khennate) (b:thukhenna) (r:5.17.11) (q:draft)
thukhenpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:judge) (d:<thukhen>, judge, with <pa> marking a man: one who hears and decides cases) (s:khenpa) (b:thukhen)
Thukhenpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Judge) (d:<thukhenpa>, judge, capitalised as a title of God) (s:Thukhen) (b:thukhenpa) (q:draft)
thukhensak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:judge for/give judgment for) (d:<thukhen> judge with <sak>, do for another) (s:khensak) (b:thukhen) (q:draft)
thukhensatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:decision/ruling/decree) (d:<thu> matter with <khensat> decide and the noun suffix <na>: the decision given in a case) (s:thukhentatna/khensatna/khenna) (q:draft)
thukhensatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:decisions/rulings) (d:plural of <thukhensatna>) (s:thukhennate) (b:thukhensatna) (q:draft)
thukhentatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:decision/resolution) (d:<thu> matter with <khentat> decide and the noun suffix <na>) (s:thukhensatna/khensatna) (q:draft)
thukhente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:judges) (d:plural of <thukhen> in the sense of judge: those who hear and decide cases) (b:thukhen) (r:5.19.17) (q:draft)
thukhialhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wrong/injustice) (d:<thu> matter with <khialhna> error: something that is not right) (s:diklohna/manlohna) (q:draft)
thukhual = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have regard/be considerate/show mercy) (d:care about what is right and about other people; in the verses only negated, {thukhual lo}, ruthless) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukhualna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:consideration/respect/mercy) (d:regard for other people; {thukhualna nei lo} is ruthless, without respect) (s:khualna/hehpihna) (b:thukhual) (q:draft)
thukhupna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:closing/conclusion) (d:apparently <thu> with <khup> close and the noun suffix <na>; {a thukhupna kikhopna} is the closing assembly of a festival) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukiciamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:promise/what was promised) (d:<thu> word with <kiciam> be promised and the noun suffix <na>) (s:thuciam/kiciamna) (q:draft)
thukidotna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:questioning/debate) (d:<thu> matter with <kidot> ask one another and the noun suffix <na>) (s:kidotna/thudotna) (q:draft)
thukihilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:discipline/correction/instruction) (d:being taught or corrected, from <thuhilh> teach, discipline, with <ki> and the noun suffix <na>) (s:kithuhilhna/thuhilhna/taiina/khalna) (q:draft)
thukimin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:agreeing/in agreement) (d:<thukim> agree with the linking suffix <in>; with <tawh>, with the consent of someone) (b:thukim) (q:draft)
thukimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:agreement/consent/covenant) (d:<thukim>, agree, with the noun suffix <na>: the state of being agreed, or the agreement or pact that is made) (s:kithukimna/thuciamna) (b:thukim) (q:draft)
thukimnasate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:agreements) (d:<thukimna> agreement with <sa> already and plural <te>: the things that have been agreed; the NIV wording of the verse differs) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukimpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:agree with/approve/consent to/permit) (d:be of one mind with someone about a matter, approve what is done or grant a request; {Topa in hong thukimpih nakleh} is if the Lord permits) (s:lungkimpih/phal) (b:thukim) (q:draft)
thukimpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:agreeing with/approving/consenting to) (d:<thukimpih> agree with, approve, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:thukimpih) (q:draft)
thukimpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:approval/agreement) (d:<thukimpih> agree with, with the noun suffix <na>; in the verse a sign of God's approval) (b:thukimpih) (q:draft)
thukimsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have agreed/agreed) (d:<thukim> agree with <sa> already done) (b:thukim) (q:draft)
thukin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deep) (d:<thuk> deep with the linking ending <in>, being deep; after a measure, to that depth) (q:draft)
thukin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:serve/dish out) (d:in {an thukin}, serving out food to people at a meal) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukip = (i:1) (t:n) (w:firm word/sure word/decree) (d:<thu> word with <kip> firm: a word or ruling that stands and is not changed) (q:draft)
thukipin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:firmly/with sure counsel) (d:<thukip> firm word with the suffix <in>; the verse says counsel and understanding are God's) (b:thukip) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:serve out/dish out/ladle out) (d:take cooked food out of the pot and serve it for people to eat) (q:draft)
thukkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repay/pay back/avenge/requite) (d:<thuk>, pay back, with <kik>, again: return to someone what his deeds deserve, whether punishment or reward; {a thukkik Pasian} is the God who avenges) (s:thuhkik/lohkik/phulak) (a:maisak) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thukkikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:answering back/replying/refuting) (d:<thukkik>, pay back or answer back, with the linking ending <in>; here of answering the arguments of others) (b:thukkik) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vengeance/repayment/recompense/reward) (d:<thukkik>, pay back, with the noun suffix <na>: paying back, whether vengeance for evil or reward for service) (s:phulakna/thuhkikna/thukna) (a:maisakna) (b:thukkik) (q:draft)
thuklua = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:too deep/very deep) (d:<thuk> deep with <lua> too much, said of water) (q:draft)
thukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:depth/the deep/depths) (d:a deep place, of the sea or a pit, from <thuk> deep) (s:thukpi/tuithuk) (a:sangna) (r:19.88.6) (q:draft)
thukna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:revenge/vengeance/repayment) (d:the act of paying back, a wrong with revenge or a gift or kindness with something in return; {heh thukna} is vengeance in anger) (s:phulakna/thukkikna/thuhkikna) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thuknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:depths/deeps/deep places) (d:<thukna> depth with the plural <te>; {lei thuknate} is the depths of the earth) (s:thukpite) (b:thukna) (q:draft)
thuko = (i:1) (t:v) (w:report/bring word/inform) (d:{thuko mi} is a person who comes with word from someone, a messenger) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who repays/avenger) (d:<thuk> repay, take revenge, with <pa> marking a man: he who pays back what was done) (s:thukpahpa/phulapa) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thukpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:repay/pay back) (d:form of <thuk>, repay, used before <pa>: {a thukpah pa} is the one who repays) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukpahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who repays) (d:<thukpah> repay with <pa> marking a man: he who pays back) (s:thukpa) (b:thukpah) (q:draft)
thukpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deepest) (d:<thuk> deep with the superlative <pen>; in 2 Kings 19:23 of the innermost part of a forest) (a:sangpen) (q:draft)
thukpenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deepest part/depths) (d:<thuk>, deep, with <pen>, most, and <na>; usually {a thukpenna mun}, the deepest place) (s:thuktawng) (b:thukpen) (q:draft)
thukpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deep/very deep) (d:<thuk>, deep, with the intensive <pi>: very deep, said of water, a pit, the earth or darkness; {tui thukpi} is the deep) (s:nakthuk) (b:thuk) (r:23.44.27) (q:draft)
thukpi = (i:2) (t:n) (w:depths/the deep) (d:a deep place, the depths, in {a thukpi}, used without a noun before it) (s:thukna/tuithuk) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thukpi = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:mysterious/hidden/secret) (d:of a matter, deep and hidden; {thu thukpi} is a mystery) (s:simtham) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thukpipi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:very deep/lofty) (d:<thukpi> deep with a second <pi> for emphasis; {kam thukpipi} is deep or lofty words, eloquence) (b:thukpi) (q:draft)
thukpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deeps/depths/deep things) (d:<thukpi> with plural <te>; {tui thukpite} the deep waters, {thu thukpite} deep matters) (s:thuknate/thuthukte) (b:thukpi) (q:draft)
thuksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:avenge/repay/reward) (d:pay back on behalf of someone; of God, avenge a person on his enemies or repay each one according to his deeds) (s:phulak/phula) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thuksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:avenging/upholding the cause of) (d:<thuksak> avenge with the linking suffix <in>) (b:thuksak) (q:draft)
thuktawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deepest part/utmost depth) (d:<thuk> deep with <tawng>, the inmost part or bottom; {khuamial thuktawng} is the deepest darkness) (s:thukpenna) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukte = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deep) (d:<thuk>, deep, with plural <te>, after a noun: {tui thukte}, the deep waters, the deeps; {pilna thukte}, deep learning) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thukte = (i:2) (t:n) (w:those who repay) (d:<thuk>, pay back, with plural <te>: the ones who return good or evil for what was done) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thuktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to take revenge/can avenge) (d:<thuk>, take revenge, with <theih>, be able; used before <nadingin>) (b:thuk) (q:draft)
thuktum = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deep/deep-seated/deep-rooted) (d:going deep in, as a sore deeper than the skin or a word taking root in a person) (q:draft)
thukuppihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:advisers/counsellors) (d:{thukup} take counsel with <pih> together with and plural <te>: those with whom the king takes counsel) (s:thulamlakte/thudotte/lamlakte) (q:draft)
thukzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deeper) (d:<thuk>, deep, with <zaw>, more: {a vun sangin thukzaw} means deeper than the skin) (q:draft)
thukzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:finish avenging/avenge fully) (d:<thuk>, take revenge, with <zawh>, finish or be able; used before <matengin>, until) (q:draft)
thukzawk = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deeper) (d:form of <thukzaw>, deeper, used before <kei> and <leh>; {a vun sangin a thukzawk leh} means if it is deeper than the skin) (b:thukzaw) (r:3.13.26) (q:draft)
thulah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:counsel) (d:give counsel or guidance, show someone what to do) (s:lamlak/lamlah)
thulah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:advice/guidance/direction/instruction/information/enlightenment)
thulahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:counsel/guidance/advice) (d:<thulah>, counsel, with the noun suffix <na>: the advice or guidance that is given) (s:lamlahna) (b:thulah)
Thulahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:counsel/guidance) (d:<thulahna>, counsel, at the start of a sentence) (s:lamlahna) (b:thulahna) (q:draft)
Thulak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:counselor) (d:one who gives counsel, with <pa> for a male person in the title {Lamdang Thulak pa}, Wonderful Counselor) (s:lamlakpa/thulamlakpa) (q:draft)
Thulakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:counselor) (d:<Thulak>, counselor, with <pa> marking a male person; a title of the promised child) (s:lamlakpa/thulamlakpa) (b:Thulak) (q:draft)
thulamlak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:counselor/adviser/guidance) (d:<thu>, matter, with <lamlak>, show the way: one who gives counsel, or the counsel given) (s:lamlakpa/vaihawmpa) (q:draft)
thulamlakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:counselor/adviser) (d:<thulamlak> counsel with <pa> marking a man) (s:lamlakpa/Thulakpa) (b:thulamlak) (q:draft)
thulamlakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:advisers/counselors) (d:plural of <thulamlak>: the advisers or counselors of a king or ruler) (s:lamlakte/thukuppihte/thudotte) (b:thulamlak) (q:draft)
thulang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:open matter/thing made known) (d:a matter that is in the open and known, the opposite of <thusim> a secret; {thulang suak} is be disclosed) (a:thuthuk) (r:40.10.26) (q:draft)
thulhilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:discipline/instruction/teaching) (d:probably a misprint of <thuhilhna>, which stands earlier in the same verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
thulian = (i:1) (t:n) (w:great matter/great thing) (d:<thu> matter with <lian> great; {a thulian} is said of what is great or weighty) (a:thuneu) (q:draft)
thum = (i:1) (t:num) (w:three) (d:the number three; {a ni thum ni} is the third day, {thum vei} is three times) (r:42.2.46/9.20.19)
thum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:beg/ask/plead) (d:ask earnestly; {kong thum hi} and {hong thum ing} are said with a request, I beg you, please) (s:thuum)
Thum = (i:1) (t:num) (w:three) (d:<thum>, three, written with a capital in the place name {Mangbuk Thum}, Three Taverns, and at the start of a sentence, as in {Thum vei}, three times) (b:thum) (q:draft)
thumaan = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:right/true/faithful) (d:another spelling of <thuman>) (s:thuman/maan) (q:draft)
thumaanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness/uprightness) (d:<thumaan> right, true, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:thumanna/dikna) (a:diklohna) (b:thumaan) (q:draft)
thumah = (i:1) (t:num) (w:three) (d:<thum> three with the marker <ah>: {pawta thumah} is for three measures) (b:thum) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuman = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:righteous/upright/true) (d:right and true: of a person righteous and upright, of words true; <thuman thutak> is the truth and {thuman lampi} the way of righteousness) (s:dik/thutang) (a:thumanlo/gilo) (r:1.6.9)
Thuman = (i:1) (t:n) (w:truth/what is right/justice) (d:<thuman> written with a capital: the Truth as a title of Christ, and at the start of a sentence truth or what is right) (s:thutak/thumanna) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
Thuman = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:True/righteous) (d:<thuman> written with a capital: the name True of the rider called Faithful and True, and at the start of a sentence righteous or true, as in {Thuman mi}, a righteous person) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
thumanah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the truth) (d:<thuman>, what is right and true, with the place marker <ah>) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
thumang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey/be obedient) (d:<thu>, word, with <mang>, obey: do what one is told; {thumang lo} is disobedient, rebellious) (s:thungai/mang) (a:lehdo) (r:56.1.6) (q:draft)
Thumang = (t:see) <Thumang-in>
Thumang-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:obediently/in obedience) (d:<thumang>, obey, with the ending <in>, written with a capital and a hyphen in Philippians 2:8: obediently) (s:thumangin) (q:draft)
thumangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:obediently/in obedience) (d:<thumang>, obey, with the linking ending <in>; {thumangin om} is live in obedience) (s:Thumang-in) (b:thumang) (q:draft)
thumangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make obey/cause to obey) (d:<thumang>, obey, with the causative <sak>: make someone obey) (b:thumang) (q:draft)
thumanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:righteously/uprightly/faithfully/justly) (d:<thuman>, right and true, with the adverb ending <in>: in a right, upright or faithful way; {thumanin gamta} and {thumanin om} are act rightly) (s:diktakin/thutangin/citakin) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
thumanlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:unrighteous/unjust) (d:<thuman>, righteous, with <lo>, not: unrighteous, unjust; {thumanlo pi-a} is by unrighteousness and {thumanlo-pa} an unjust one) (a:thuman/dik) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
Thumanlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:injustice/unrighteousness) (d:<thuman>, truth or right, with <loh>, not, and the noun suffix <na>; in the text it is part of a section heading, {Leitungah Thumanlohna}, that follows the verse) (s:diklohna) (a:thumanna) (r:21.3.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
thumanlote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the unjust/the unrighteous) (d:<thumanlo>, unrighteous, with the plural <te>: unjust people) (s:diklote) (a:thumante/midikte) (b:thumanlo) (q:draft)
thumanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteousness/faithfulness/truth) (d:<thuman>, right and true, with the noun suffix <na>: righteousness, faithfulness or truth, said of God and of people) (s:dikna/cihtakna/thutakna) (a:diklohna/gitlohna) (b:thuman) (r:11.17.24) (q:draft)
thumannate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:faithfulness/faithful acts) (d:<thumanna>, faithfulness, with the plural <te>: the faithful dealings of God toward a person) (b:thumanna) (q:draft)
thumanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:righteous man/faithful one/honest man) (d:<thuman>, righteous and true, with <pa> marking a man: one who is righteous or true to his word) (s:dikpa/midikpa) (a:migilopa) (b:thuman) (r:43.8.26) (q:draft)
thumanpha = (i:1) (t:n) (w:valuable word/good advice/worthy thing) (d:<thu>, word, with <manpha>, precious: something worth hearing, good advice) (q:draft)
thumantak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:honesty/integrity/good faith) (d:<thuman>, right and true, with <tak>, real: true uprightness; {lungsimtak le thumantak tawh} is sincerely and in good faith) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
thumante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the righteous/the upright) (d:<thuman>, righteous, with the plural <te>: righteous people, often after <mi> and set against <migilote>, the wicked) (s:midikte/thutangte) (a:migilote/thumanlote) (b:thuman) (r:19.34.15) (q:draft)
thumanzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:more righteous) (d:<thuman>, righteous, with <zaw>, more; the one compared takes <sangin>, than) (s:dikzaw) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
thumanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:can be righteous/be able to be righteous) (d:<thuman>, righteous, with <zo>, be able) (b:thuman) (q:draft)
thumawkna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:vanity/delusion/empty thing) (d:<thu>, matter, with <mawk>, vain or for nothing, and the noun suffix <na>: an empty thing, a delusion) (s:mawkna) (q:draft)
thumin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in three/into three) (d:<thum>, three, with the marker <in>; {pawl thumin khen}, divide into three groups; {a thumin}, all three) (b:thum) (q:draft)
thumin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:groan/moan/wail) (d:<thum>, groan or plead, with the linking suffix <in>: groaning; {thumin kap} is wail and {thumin tau} is groan) (s:thuumin) (b:thum) (r:2.2.23) (q:draft)
thumletau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:moaning and groaning/woe) (d:apparently <thum> moan and <tau> groan joined by <le>, and; {thumletau thute} are words of woe) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thummim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Thummim) (d:one of the two sacred lots, the Urim and Thummim, kept in the breastpiece of the high priest and used to seek a decision from God) (r:3.8.8)
Thummin = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Thummim) (d:spelling of <Thummim> in Ezra 2:63: the sacred lot used with the Urim by a priest to seek a decision from God) (q:draft)
thumna = (i:1) (t:num) (w:third) (d:<thum>, three, with the ordinal suffix <na>: the third in a series) (b:thum)
Thumna = (i:1) (t:num) (w:third) (d:<thumna>, third, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the place name {Ansai Thumna}, given in the NIV as Three Taverns) (b:thumna) (q:draft)
thumnate = (i:1) (t:num) (w:third) (b:thumna) plural form of <thumna>
thumnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to plead/wish to beg) (d:<thum>, beg, with <nop>, want; {kong thumnop thu} is the thing I wish to plead for, my petition) (q:draft)
thumong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:fate/destiny/lot/end) (d:<thu>, matter, with <mong>, end: what a person comes to in the end, the outcome of a life) (r:21.9.2) (q:draft)
thumongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:outcomes/end/consequences) (d:<thumong>, the end a matter comes to, with the plural <te>) (b:thumong) (q:draft)
thumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:intercede/pray for/plead for) (d:<thum>, beg, with <sak>, do for another: ask or pray on behalf of someone) (s:ngetsak/thuumsak/thungetsak) (b:thum) (q:draft)
thumsuah = (i:1) (t:num) (w:three parts) (d:<thum> three with <suah>: divided into three; {seh thumsuah seh khat} is one part out of three, a third) (q:draft, low confidence)
thumte = (i:1) (t:num) (w:three/the three) (d:<thum>, three, with the plural marker <te>: a group of three already known) (b:thum) (q:draft)
thumthum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plead/beg earnestly/keep asking) (d:<thum>, beg, doubled to show that the asking is repeated or urgent) (q:draft)
thumthum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:moan/coo) (d:of doves, make a low mournful sound) (q:draft, low confidence)
thumu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seer/one with insight) (d:one who sees or understands matters, usually with <pa> as {thumu pa}, a seer) (s:mupa) (q:draft)
Thumu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seer) (d:<thumu>, seer, capitalised as a title with <pa> before a name: {Thumu pa Iddo}, Iddo the seer) (b:thumu) (r:14.12.15) (q:draft)
thumuh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:insight/understanding) (d:<thu>, matter, with <muh>, see: seeing into matters, insight; used before <nading>) (q:draft)
thumuhkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:foresight) (d:<thu> matter, <muh> see, <kholh> beforehand, with the noun suffix <na>: seeing matters ahead of time) (q:draft)
thumuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:insight/understanding) (d:<thumuh>, seeing into matters, with the noun suffix <na>: insight, understanding) (s:thutelna/theihtelna) (b:thumuh) (q:draft)
thumuhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:insights/visions) (d:<thumuhna>, what one sees or perceives of a matter, with plural <te>; of a prophet, the things seen in a vision) (b:thumuhna) (q:draft)
thumun = (i:1) (t:num) (w:the three/all three) (d:<thum> three with <un>, the plural ending on those who act: the three of them) (b:thum) (q:draft)
thumute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seers) (d:<thumu>, seer, with the plural <te>) (s:mutheite) (b:thumu) (q:draft)
Thumute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seers) (d:<Thumu>, seer, with the plural <te>; in the title of a book of records of the seers) (b:Thumu) (q:draft)
thumvei = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:three times/thrice) (d:<thum>, three, with <vei>, time; also the third time) (q:draft)
thumveina = (i:1) (t:num) (w:third time) (d:<thumvei>, three times, with the ordinal suffix <na>: the third time, for the third time) (b:thumvei) (q:draft)
thumveita = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:three times) (d:<thumvei>, three times, with <ta>; {nisimin thumveita} is three times every day) (b:thumvei) (q:draft)
thun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put into/pour into/fill) (d:put a liquid or other thing into a container such as a skin, a jar or a horn; used with <sungah>, into) (s:guang) (q:draft)
Thunei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dispute/case) (d:a matter that someone has against another, brought to be judged; <thu>, matter, with <nei>, have) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuneih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have authority/have power) (d:<thu>, word, with <neih>, have; {thuneih theihna} is power or authority) (q:draft)
thuneihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:authority/right/power) (d:<thuneih>, have authority, with the noun suffix <na>: the right or authority to command or decide; {thuneihna tawh} is by the authority of) (s:aana) (b:thuneih) (q:draft)
thuneihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have a dispute with/be at law with) (d:<thuneih>, have a case, with <pih>, together with; {na thuneihpih} is the one you have a dispute with) (b:thuneih) (q:draft)
thuneite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:authorities/rulers/those in authority) (d:those who hold authority, from <thu> matter and <nei> have, with <te> plural; {ukna thuneite}, the governing authorities) (q:draft)
thuneite = (i:2) (t:n) (w:parties/those involved) (d:those who have a matter or case, such as the two sides of a dispute) (r:46.6.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
thunem = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gentle word/gentleness) (d:<thu>, word, with <nem>, soft; {thunem tawh} and {thunem zangin} are gently) (s:thudam/lungnemna) (q:draft)
thunemin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:gently/with gentleness) (d:<thunem>, gentleness, with the linking ending <in>: gently) (s:damtakin) (b:thunem) (q:draft)
thuneu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small matter/trifle/easy thing) (d:<thu>, matter, with <neu>, small: something of little weight or difficulty; {thuneu sa} is think it a small thing) (a:thulian) (q:draft)
thuneute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small matters/little things/trivial cases) (d:<thuneu>, small matter, with the plural <te>) (a:thuhaksate) (b:thuneu) (q:draft)
thung = (t:see) <thung-ip>
thung-ip = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bag/pouch/satchel) (d:a bag carried on a journey or by a shepherd, named beside {dangka-ip}, the money bag) (s:thungip/ip) (q:draft)
thungai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey/be obedient/heed) (d:<thu>, word, with <ngai>, listen: listen to what is said and do it; {thungai lo} is disobedient) (s:thumang/mang) (a:lehdo) (q:draft)
thungaih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:obey/heed/listen) (d:form of <thungai>, obey or listen, used before <ding>, <nading> and <lohna>; {thungaih lohna} is disobedience) (b:thungai) (q:draft)
thungaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:obedience) (d:<thungaih>, obey or listen, with the noun suffix <na>: obedience; {thungaihna ngah} is be heard) (b:thungaih) (r:60.1.1) (q:draft)
thungaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:consider/reflect/discern) (d:think matters over; {thungaihsun theite}, those able to think things through, are the discerning) (r:20.14.33) (q:draft)
thungaihsut = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thinking/reasoning/consideration) (d:thought given to a matter; {thungaihsut theihna}, the ability to think a matter through, is good judgment, discretion or understanding) (r:20.13.15) (q:draft)
thungaihsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plan/thought/planning) (d:<thungaihsut>, think a matter over, with the noun suffix <na>: a plan or purpose, planning) (s:ngaihsutna/geelna) (b:thungaihsut) (q:draft)
thungaite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hearers/listeners) (d:<thungai>, listen to what is said, with the plural <te>: those who listen to the word) (b:thungai) (q:draft)
thungeek = (i:1) (t:n) (w:elementary principles/rudiments/elemental things) (d:<thu> matter with <ngeek> infant, tender: the first and basic things; {leitung thungeek} is the elemental things of the world) (q:draft)
thungen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pray) (d:<thu>, word, with <ngen>, ask: speak to God in prayer; {thungen ding} is to pray) (r:23.38.2)
thungenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:praying/pray) (d:<thungen>, pray, with the linking suffix <in>: praying, or prayed and then) (b:thungen) (r:23.37.15) (q:draft)
thungennate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/sayings) (d:the things said, here by the seers; apparently <thu> word and <gen> speak with <nate>, written as one word) (q:draft, low confidence)
thungent = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prayer) (s:thungetna)
thungente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who pray/those who call on) (d:<thungen> pray with the plural <te>; {tua min tawh thungente} is those who pray in that name) (b:thungen) (q:draft)
thungentehna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:parable) (d:<thu> word, <gen> speak, <teh> compare, with the noun suffix <na>: a saying told as a comparison) (s:thugentehna) (q:draft)
thungentna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prayer) (s:thungetna)
thunget = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pray) (d:form of <thungen>, pray, used in dependent clauses and before endings; also as a noun, praying) (q:draft)
thungetna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prayer/plea) (d:<thunget>, pray, with the noun suffix <na>: a prayer, what is asked of God) (s:thuumna/kutna) (q:draft)
thungetnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prayers/pleas) (d:<thungetna>, prayer, with the plural <te>) (s:thuumnate/ngetnate) (b:thungetna) (q:draft)
thungetsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pray for/intercede for) (d:<thunget>, pray, with <sak>, do for another person: pray for someone) (s:ngetsak/thumsak/thuumsak) (b:thunget) (q:draft)
thungetsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:praying for) (d:<thungetsak>, pray for someone, with the linking ending <in>) (b:thungetsak) (q:draft)
thungetsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prayer for someone/intercession) (d:<thungetsak>, pray for someone, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:ngetsakna) (b:thungetsak) (q:draft)
thungette = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prayers) (d:<thunget> praying with the plural <te>: the things prayed; the NIV has what you are saying) (b:thunget) (q:draft, low confidence)
thungetzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way of praying/how to pray) (d:<thunget>, pray, with <zia>, manner: the way to pray) (q:draft)
thungip = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bag/pouch) (d:a bag carried on a journey or by a shepherd) (s:thung-ip/ip) (q:draft)
thunin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:putting in/filling) (d:<thun>, put into a container, with the linking ending <in>; {a dimtakin thunin} is having filled it full) (b:thun) (q:draft)
thunthuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put in/pour in/add into) (d:<thun> put into with <thuah>, add: fill a vessel with something, here oil into a lamp) (q:draft)
thunuam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:peace/fellowship/goodwill) (d:peace or good terms between people or with God; {thunuam gen} is proclaim peace and {thunuam-a biakna} is the fellowship or peace offering) (s:kilemna) (q:draft)
thunuam = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be good to/be kind to/be favourable to/be gracious to) (d:used with <tungah> for the person who is treated kindly) (q:draft)
thunuama = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:of fellowship/of peace) (d:<thunuam> with the linking suffix <a>, describing the next noun; {thunuama biakna} is the fellowship or peace offering) (b:thunuam) (r:3.7.33) (q:draft)
thunuamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the diligent/the willing) (d:{mi thunuamte} stands where the NIV has diligent hands, set against {a thadahte}, the lazy) (s:thanuamte) (a:thadahte) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thupalsat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:transgress/break the law) (d:<thu>, word or law, with <palsat>, transgress; {thupalsat mite} are transgressors) (q:draft)
thupalsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:transgression/rebellion/offence/wrongdoing) (d:<thu>, word or law, with <palsat>, transgress, and the noun suffix <na>: the breaking of a law or command) (s:palsatna/mawhna/khialhna) (q:draft)
thupalsatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:transgressions/offenses) (d:<thupalsatna>, transgression, with the plural <te>) (s:palsatnate/mawhnate) (b:thupalsatna) (r:23.43.25) (q:draft)
thupalsatte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:transgressors) (d:<thu>, word or law, with <palsat>, transgress, and the plural <te>: those who break the law) (s:palsatte/mimawhte) (q:draft)
thupang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plead a case/contend) (d:take part in a case at court; the verse has the Lord taking his place to do so) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupeelin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:shrewdly/craftily) (d:how God deals with the devious, {thukawi mi}; the base {thupeel} is not otherwise attested) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bless) (d:<thu>, word, with <pha>, good: a blessing; <thupha pia> is bless and {thupha ngah} is be blessed) (a:phuisam/hamsiat) (r:1.1.22)
thupha = (i:2) (t:v) (w:good news) (s:thuhoih)
Thupha = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blessing/blessed) (d:<thupha>, blessing, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or as a title: {Thupha a ngah} is receive blessing or be blessed, and {Thupha a nei} is the Blessed One) (a:samsiatna) (b:thupha) (r:41.14.61) (q:draft)
thuphate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:blessings) (d:<thupha>, blessing, with the plural <te>; {Kha Siangtho piak thuphate} are the blessings the Holy Spirit gives, the spiritual gifts) (s:daupainate) (a:samsiatnate) (b:thupha) (r:46.14.1) (q:draft)
thuphawk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take heed/be aware/pay attention) (d:<thu>, matter, with <phawk>, notice: be aware of how things stand and take them to heart; {thuphawk loin} is heedlessly or complacently, and {thuphawk theih lohna} is a heart that cannot take things in) (s:phawk) (q:draft)
thuphawkna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:warning/awareness/heed) (d:<thuphawk>, take heed, with the noun suffix <na>: a warning that makes one aware; {thuphawkna ngah} is be warned) (s:hilhkholhna) (b:thuphawk) (q:draft)
thuphawksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:experienced/discerning/respected) (d:<thuphawk>, be aware of matters, with <sa>, already: experienced, having come to know how things are; said of men fit to lead) (s:phawksa) (b:thuphawk) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:important/great/special/solemn) (d:<thu>, matter, with <pi>, great: of great weight or worth; {a thupi lo} is unimportant, {thupi takin} is solemnly, and {thupi ngaihsut} is count as important) (s:lian/phamawh) (b:thu) (r:1.43.3) (q:draft)
thupia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give an order/command/issue an order) (d:<thu>, word, with <pia>, give: give an order or command; the form used before another word is <thupiak>) (s:sawl/vaikhak) (r:1.12.20) (q:draft)
thupiak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:command/order) (d:form of <thupia>, give an order, used before another word; {a thupiak bangin} is just as he commanded) (s:sawl/vaikhak) (b:thupia) (r:1.7.5)
thupiakkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:warning/advance instruction/revelation) (d:<thupiak>, command, with <kholh>, beforehand, and the noun suffix <na>: a word given in advance about what is to come, a warning or revelation) (s:hilhkholhna) (q:draft)
thupiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:command/commandment/order) (d:<thupiak>, command, with the noun suffix <na>: a command or order; {thupiakna zui} or <mang> is keep a command) (s:sawlna/vaikhakna) (b:thupiak) (r:5.4.13) (q:draft)
thupiaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:commands/commandments/orders) (d:<thupiakna>, command, with the plural <te>) (s:thupiakte/sawlnate/thukhamte) (b:thupiakna) (q:draft)
thupiaksa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:commanded) (d:<thupiak>, command, with <sa>, already: what has been commanded; {a thupiaksa bangin} is just as he had commanded) (s:sawlsa) (b:thupiak) (q:draft)
thupiaksate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:commands/things commanded/instructions) (d:<thupiaksa>, what has been commanded, with the plural <te>) (s:thupiakte/thupiaknate) (b:thupiaksa) (q:draft)
thupiakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:commands/commandments/orders) (d:<thupiak>, command, with the plural <te>) (s:thupiaknate/sawlnate/thukhamte) (b:thupiak) (q:draft)
thupiang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:event/happening/occurrence) (d:<thu>, matter, with <piang>, happen: what has happened or will happen; {thupiang khempeuh} is everything that happened) (q:draft)
thupiangsate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things that have happened/past events) (d:<thupiang>, what happens, with <sa>, already, and the plural <te>: the things that have happened) (q:draft)
thupiangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:events/happenings/things that happened) (d:<thupiang>, event, with the plural <te>: the things that happen or have happened) (b:thupiang) (q:draft)
thupiangteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all that happened/the whole matter) (d:<thupiang>, event, with <teng>, all: everything that has happened, the whole matter) (b:thupiang) (q:draft)
thupilak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take seriously/regard as important/honor) (d:<thupi>, important, with <lak>, take: take seriously, treat as important; the same verse also writes it as {thupi takin lak}) (s:thupisak/thupisan/thupisim) (a:simmawh) (q:draft)
thupina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:dignity/splendor/honor/greatness) (d:<thupi>, great or honorable, with the noun suffix <na>: dignity or splendor; {lungsim thupina} is integrity of heart) (s:thupitna/minthanna) (b:thupi) (q:draft)
thupinate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:glories/splendors/great things) (d:<thupina>, greatness, with the plural <te>: the splendors or precious things someone once had, where the NIV has treasures) (s:thupitnate/minthannate) (b:thupina) (q:draft)
thupipen = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:greatest/most important) (d:<thupi>, great, with <pen>, most: the greatest or most important) (s:lianpen/lianbel) (b:thupi) (q:draft)
thupisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:value highly/regard as important) (d:<thupi>, important, with <sak>, hold to be: value highly, set great store by something) (s:thupilak/thupisan) (b:thupi) (q:draft)
thupisan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:respect/take seriously/regard as important) (d:<thupi>, important, with <san>, take as: take seriously, not make light of; the NIV turns it round as do not despise) (s:thupilak/thupisak) (a:simmawh) (b:thupi) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupisim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:regard/heed/take seriously/pay attention to) (d:count as important, pay heed to; with <kei> or <lo> it means disregard or not listen to) (s:thupilak/thupisan) (a:simmawh) (q:draft)
thupite = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:important/great/chief) (d:plural of <thupi>, said of persons or things of high rank or importance; {mi thupite} is the great, the mighty) (b:thupi) (q:draft)
thupiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:important things/valuables) (d:<thupi> important with <teng> all of: the things that matter most, the valuable things) (b:thupi) (q:draft)
thupitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:majesty/greatness/glory) (d:<thupi>, great, with the noun suffix <na>: majesty, greatness) (s:thupina/minliatna/vangliatna) (q:draft)
thupitnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:glories/splendors/great things) (d:<thupitna>, greatness, with the plural <te>: the splendors or precious things someone once had, where the NIV has treasures) (s:thupinate/minthannate) (b:thupitna) (q:draft)
thupizaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:greater/more important/better) (d:<thupi>, great or important, with the comparative <zaw>: greater, worth more; the thing compared is marked by <sangin>, than) (s:lianzaw) (a:neuzaw) (b:thupi) (q:draft)
thupuak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:message/news/report) (d:<thu>, word, with <puak>, carry or send: a message or news brought to someone, also an order sent; {thupuak pa} is a messenger) (s:thuzak/thuthak) (q:draft)
thupuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:messengers/bearers of the word) (d:<thupuak>, word that is carried, with the plural <te>: those who bring the message) (s:kamtaite) (b:thupuak) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuseel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:quarrel/argue/dispute) (d:<thu>, matter, with <seel>, argue: quarrel or dispute; {thuseel lo} stands where the NIV has will not quarrel; also written <thusel>) (s:thusel/kisel) (q:draft, low confidence)
thusel = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dispute/debate/argue) (d:argue a matter against someone; {thusel a siamte} are skilled debaters, {thusel zo lo} is unable to out-argue) (s:thuseel/kisel/kinial) (q:draft)
thusia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:evil/mischief/wicked scheme) (d:<thu>, matter, with <sia>, bad: evil that is planned, spoken or done; {thusia bawl} is do evil and {thusia geel} is plot evil) (s:gilohna/hoihlohna) (a:thuhoih) (r:19.64.2) (q:draft)
thusia = (i:2) (t:n) (w:disaster/harm/trouble/calamity) (d:something bad that happens to someone, misfortune) (s:tuahsiatna/siatna) (r:21.11.2) (q:draft)
thusiapi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:grievous thing/bitter thing/great evil) (d:<thusia>, evil matter, with <pi>, great: a grievous or bitter thing; here the bitter things sought against someone) (b:thusia) (q:draft)
thusiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bad news/distressing words) (d:<thusia>, bad matter, with the plural <te>: bad news, words that bring distress) (b:thusia) (q:draft)
thusim = (i:1) (t:v) (w:attentive/mindful/be careful/regard/respect) (d:<thu>, matter, with <sim>, count: pay regard to a person or thing, look on with favor; {thusim lo} is disregard or show contempt for) (s:thupisim) (a:simmawh)
thusim nei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hypocrite) (d:<thusim>, secret, with <nei>, have: one who keeps hidden motives, a hypocrite) (s:simtatpa/thusimnei/thusimneimi)
thusim neite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hypocrites) (d:<thusim nei>, hypocrite, with the plural <te>) (s:simtatte/misimtatte/kineihkhemte) (b:thusim nei)
thusimin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:secretly/in secret) (d:<thusim>, secret, with the adverb ending <in>: secretly; {thusimin a kikoih} is what is kept hidden) (s:simthamin) (a:kilangin/langtangin) (r:42.8.17) (q:draft)
thusimlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:contempt/scorn/mockery) (d:<thusim>, regard, with <loh>, not, and the noun suffix <na>: contempt, treating someone with no respect) (s:simmawhna/zahkona) (a:thusimna/zahtakna) (q:draft)
thusimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:respect/esteem/regard) (d:<thusim>, pay regard to, with the noun suffix <na>: the respect or esteem shown to someone) (s:zahtakna) (a:thusimlohna/simmawhna) (b:thusim) (q:draft)
thusimnei = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hypocrite) (d:<thusim>, secret, with <nei>, have: one who hides his real motives, a hypocrite; also written <thusim nei>) (s:simtatpa/thusim nei/thusimneimi)
thusimneimi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hypocrite) (d:<thusim nei>, having hidden motives, with <mi>, person: a hypocrite) (s:simtatpa/thusim nei/thusimnei)
thusimte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:secrets/mysteries/hidden things) (d:<thusim>, secret, with the plural <te>: things kept secret or not yet made known) (s:thuthukte/kiseelte) (b:thusim) (q:draft)
thusimteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:whole secret/mystery) (d:<thusim>, hidden matter, with <teng>, all of) (s:thuthuk) (q:draft, low confidence)
thusit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:try/judge/put on trial) (d:<thu>, matter, with <sit>, examine: examine a case in court, put someone on trial) (s:thukhen) (q:draft)
thusitin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:trying a case/sitting in judgment) (d:<thusit>, examine a case in court, with the linking ending <in>) (b:thusit) (q:draft)
thusitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trial/examination/account) (d:<thusit>, try a case, with the noun suffix <na>: the examining of a case or of a person’s conduct; {thusitna thuak} is stand trial or give account) (s:sittelna/thusuahna) (b:thusit) (r:44.25.9) (q:draft)
thusuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:account/giving account) (d:<thu> matter with <suah>, bring out, and the noun suffix <na>: having to state one's case before a judge) (s:thusitna) (q:draft, low confidence)
thutak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:truth) (d:<thu>, word, with <tak>, true: truth, what is true; most often paired with <thuman> as <thuman thutak>) (s:thumanna) (a:thuzuau/zuauthu) (b:thu) (r:19.119.138) (q:draft)
thutakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:truthfully/faithfully/justly) (d:<thutak>, truth, with the adverb ending <in>; often paired with <thuman>) (s:thumanin/citakin/mantakin) (b:thutak) (q:draft)
thutakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:faithfulness/truthfulness) (d:<thutak>, truth, with the noun suffix <na>: faithfulness, being true to one’s word; often paired with {itna kip}, steadfast love) (s:thumanna/cihtakna) (b:thutak) (q:draft)
thutakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the true one) (d:<thutak> truth with <pa> marking a man: he who is true; paired as {thuman thutakpa}) (s:taktakpa) (b:thutak) (q:draft)
thutakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:truths/true things) (d:<thutak> truth with the plural <te>, often in the pair {thuman thutakte}) (b:thutak) (q:draft)
thutan = (t:see) <thutan'na>
thutan'na = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justice/uprightness/fair judgment) (d:the quality of judging and acting rightly; from <thutang> just, upright, with <na>) (s:thutang/diktatna) (a:diklohna) (r:2.23.6) (q:draft)
thutan'nate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justice/judgments) (d:<thutan'na>, justice, with the plural <te>; another spelling of <thutannate>) (s:thutannate) (q:draft)
thutang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justice/uprightness) (d:what is just and right, justice; often paired with <thuman>, righteousness, and used with <zang>, practise, or <heikhia>, pervert) (s:thutan'na/diktatna) (a:diklohna) (r:21.3.16) (q:draft)
thutang = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:upright/just) (d:just and upright in character; {lungsim thutang} is upright in heart) (s:dik/maan) (a:thukawi/thumanlo) (r:20.2.8) (q:draft)
thutangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:justly/with justice/uprightly) (d:<thutang>, just, with the adverb ending <in>: justly; often in the pair {thuman thutangin}, in righteousness and justice) (s:thumanin/diktakin/maanin) (b:thutang) (r:28.12.6) (q:draft)
thutangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the upright/upright people) (d:<thutang>, upright, with the plural <te>: those who are upright; most often {lungsim thutangte}, the upright in heart) (s:midikte/thumante/mihoihte) (a:migilote) (b:thutang) (r:19.73.1) (q:draft)
thutanna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:judgment/condemnation/verdict/sentence) (d:<thu>, case, with <tan>, decide, and the noun suffix <na>: the deciding of a case and the sentence given; {mawhna thutanna} is condemnation and {thutanna thuak} is suffer judgment; in some texts also a spelling of <thutan'na>, justice) (s:thukhenna) (q:draft)
thutannate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:justice/judgments) (d:<thutanna> judgment with the plural <te>) (s:thutan'nate) (b:thutanna) (q:draft)
thutawng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deep things/depths) (d:<thu> matter with <tawng>, the inmost part: the deepest part of a matter; {thutawng dongtakin} is right to the depths) (q:draft, low confidence)
thutawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:end/final outcome/destiny/fate) (d:<thu> matter with <tawpna> end: how things end for someone) (s:thumong/beina) (q:draft)
thute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:words/things/matters) (d:<thu>, word or matter, with the plural <te>: words, things, matters; {hih thute} is these words or these things) (s:thugente/kammalte) (b:thu) (q:draft)
Thute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:things/words) (d:<thute>, words or matters, capitalised for the message that was preached) (b:thute) (q:draft)
thutelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:understanding/discernment/insight) (d:<thu>, matter, with <tel>, understand, and the noun suffix <na>: understanding, insight into matters) (s:theihtelna/thutheihna/pilna) (q:draft)
thuteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:all the words/all the things/matters) (d:<thu> word or matter with <teng> all; {hih thuteng} is all this, all these things) (b:thu) (q:draft)
Thuthak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:news/tidings) (d:<thuthak>, news, capitalised in {Lungdamna Thuthak}, the Good News, the gospel) (b:thuthak) (q:draft)
thuthakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:new teachings/new things/news) (d:<thuthak>, new word or matter, with the plural <te>) (b:thuthak) (q:draft)
thuthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:knowledgeable/learned/understanding/prudent) (d:knowing or understanding matters, from <thu> and <thei> know; {thuthei mi} is a man of learning or insight, {thuthei lopi-in} is without knowledge) (s:pil/pilhuai) (a:hai) (b:thu) (q:draft)
thutheih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knowledge) (d:<thu> matter with <theih> know; {thutheih siamna} is the gift of knowledge) (s:thutheihna) (b:thuthei) (q:draft)
thutheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knowledge/understanding) (d:<thu>, matter, <theih>, know, with <na>: knowing and understanding of things) (s:theihna/thutelna/pilna/theihtelna) (b:thutheih) (q:draft)
thutheihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:knowledge/things known/learning) (d:<thu> matter with <theih> know and the plural <te>: the things one knows) (b:thutheih) (q:draft)
thutheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:experts/those who know) (d:<thuthei>, knowing matters, with the plural <te>) (s:siamte) (b:thuthei) (q:draft)
thuthu = (t:see) <thuthu-in>
thuthu-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:as one pleases/according to one's own will) (d:after a possessive: following only one's own mind, as in {ama thuthu-in}, as he pleases) (s:ututin/duhduhin) (q:draft)
thuthuin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:of oneself/by nature) (d:another spelling of <thuthu-in>, by one’s own will; {ama thuthuin} is of himself, as he is, where the NIV has physically) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuthuk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mystery/secret/deep matter) (d:<thu> matter with <thuk> deep: something hidden or hard to understand) (s:thuthukpi/thuthukna/thusimteng) (r:49.1.9) (q:draft)
thuthukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mystery/deep matter) (d:<thuthuk>, deep or hidden matter, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:thuthuk) (b:thuthuk) (q:draft)
thuthukpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mystery/deep mystery/profound matter) (d:<thuthuk> with <pi>, great: a great or deep mystery) (s:thuthuk/thuthukna) (b:thuthuk) (q:draft)
thuthukpite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deep things/mysteries) (d:<thuthukpi>, deep mystery, with the plural <te>) (s:thuthukte/thusimte) (b:thuthukpi) (q:draft)
thuthukte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mysteries/deep things/hidden things) (d:<thuthuk>, deep or hidden matter, with the plural <te>) (s:thuthukpite/thusimte/kiseelte) (b:thuthuk) (r:49.3.5) (q:draft)
thuum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plead/beseech/beg) (d:ask earnestly, plead or beg, often with <tungah>, to or before someone; {kong thuum hi} is I beg you, please) (s:thum/ngenngen) (r:44.25.3) (q:draft)
thuum = (i:2) (t:v) (w:mourn/lament/wail) (d:mourn or wail for the dead or over bad news, often with <hangin>, because of) (s:dah/mau) (a:kipak) (q:draft)
thuumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:groan/mourn/wail) (d:<thuum>, mourn, with the linking ending <in>: groaning or lamenting, used before another verb as in {thuumin tau} and {thuumin kap}) (b:thuum) (q:draft)
thuumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:supplication/plea/entreaty) (d:<thuum>, plead, with the noun suffix <na>: an earnest plea or supplication, often paired with <thungetna>, prayer) (s:thungetna/kutna) (b:thuum) (r:25.3.56) (q:draft)
thuumna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:mourning/lamentation/wailing) (d:<thuum>, mourn, with the noun suffix <na>: mourning or lamentation for the dead or in distress) (s:dahna/kahna/tamlawhna) (a:lungdamna/kipahna) (b:thuum) (q:draft)
thuumnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:supplications/pleas/cries for mercy) (d:<thuumna>, plea, with the plural <te>; often paired with <thungetna>, prayer) (s:thungetnate/ngetnate) (b:thuumna) (q:draft)
thuumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plead for/intercede/petition for) (d:<thuum>, plead, with <sak>: plead or pray on behalf of another) (s:ngetsak/thumsak/thungetsak) (b:thuum) (r:24.7.16) (q:draft)
thuumthuum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:moan/coo) (d:repeated form: make a low moaning sound again and again, as a dove does) (s:thumthum/tautau) (q:draft)
thuvaante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:officials/administrators) (d:another spelling of <thuvante>: holders of a court office, with the plural <te>) (s:thuvante) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvaihawm = (i:1) (t:n) (w:council) (d:<thu> matter with <vaihawm>, plan or deliberate: the body that deliberates; {ulian thuvaihawm} is the council of the leaders) (s:vaihawmte) (q:draft)
thuvaihawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plan/counsel) (d:<thuvaihawm>, deliberate on matters, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:vaihawmna/geelna) (b:thuvaihawm) (q:draft)
thuvan = (i:1) (t:n) (w:official/officer/secretary) (d:a court office; {thuvan pa} and {thuvan pipa} stand where the NIV has staff officer and secretary) (s:thuvanpa) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:staff officer/officer/official) (d:<thuvan>, a court office, with <pa> marking a man: an officer in the service of the king) (b:thuvan) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvanpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:secretary/scribe) (d:official who keeps the writings of the king; followed by <pa> for a man) (q:draft)
thuvanpipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:scribe/secretary) (d:an official who writes and keeps records for the king; <pa> marks a man) (b:thuvanpi) (q:draft)
thuvante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:officials/administrators) (d:<thuvan>, a court office, with the plural <te>) (b:thuvan) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvum = (i:1) (t:n) (w:hump) (d:the hump on the back of a camel) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuzak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:news/report/what is heard) (d:<thu>, word, with <zak>, hear: what one hears, a message, report or news) (s:thupuak) (q:draft)
thuzaksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:proclamation/announcement/report) (d:<thu>, word, with <zaksak>, cause to hear, and <na>: the making known of something) (s:zaksakna/taangkona) (q:draft)
thuzang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:trivial matter/light thing) (d:<thu>, matter, with <zang>, light: a small thing of little weight, here of sin that is treated as trivial) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overrule/prevail over/win over/gain control over) (d:get the better of someone by words, whether by command or by persuasion) (s:zolzawh) (q:draft)
thuzia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way/manner/nature) (d:<thu> matter with <zia> manner: how a thing is or works) (q:draft)
thuzol = (i:1) (t:n) (w:smooth words/flattery/pleasant things) (d:<thu> word with <zol> coax: words that please but are not true) (s:kamzol/mawkphatna) (q:draft)
thuzuau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood/false word) (d:untrue speech; {thuzuau gen} means tell a lie, {thuzuau teci} is false witness) (s:zuauthu) (a:thutak/thuman) (q:draft)
Thuzuau = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood) (d:<thuzuau>, lie, at the start of a clause; {thuzuau gen} is tell a lie) (b:thuzuau) (q:draft)
thuzuaupa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:liar) (d:<thuzuau> lie with <pa> marking a man) (s:zuaugen/Mizuau) (b:thuzuau) (q:draft)
Thuzuaute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lies/deceit) (d:<Thuzuau>, lie, with the plural <te>) (s:zuauthute) (b:Thuzuau) (q:draft)
thuzui = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disciple/follower) (d:<thu> word with <zui> follow: one who follows the teaching) (s:nungzui) (q:draft)
Tiberias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tiberias) (d:city on the western shore of the Sea of Galilee, after which the lake is also called the Sea of Tiberias) (r:43.6.23/43.6.1)
Tiberius = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiberius) (d:Roman emperor, Tiberius Caesar, in the fifteenth year of whose reign John the Baptist began to preach) (r:42.3.1)
Tibhath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tebah) (d:town of Hadadezer king of Zobah, from which David took a great quantity of bronze) (r:13.18.8)
Tibni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tibni) (d:son of Ginath, who was the rival of Omri for the throne of Israel) (r:11.16.22/11.16.21)
Tidal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Tidal) (d:king of Goyim, one of the four kings allied with Kedorlaomer in the time of Abram) (r:1.14.1)
Tidalte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tidal) (d:<Tidal>, king of Goyim, written with the ending <te> that closes a list of names) (b:Tidal) (r:1.14.1)
Tifsah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tiphsah) (d:town on the Euphrates that marked the far limit of the rule of Solomon) (r:11.4.24)
Tiglath = (t:see) <Tiglath-pileser>
Tiglath-pileser = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath-Pileser) (d:king of Assyria who took Gilead and Galilee from Israel in the time of Pekah and to whom Ahaz of Judah turned for help) (r:12.16.7) (q:draft)
Tiglathpileser = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath-Pileser) (d:king of Assyria who carried people of Israel into exile and to whom Ahaz of Judah turned for help) (r:14.28.20/13.5.6)
Tigris = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (w:Tigris) (d:great river of Mesopotamia, the third river of Eden, beside which Daniel saw a vision) (r:27.10.4/1.2.14)
Tikhikas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tychicus) (d:companion of Paul from the province of Asia, who carried his letters to the Ephesians and the Colossians) (r:51.4.7/55.4.12)
Tikoa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tekoa) (d:town in Judah south of Bethlehem, home of the prophet Amos) (r:24.6.1)
Tikvah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tikvah) (d:father of Shallum the husband of the prophet Huldah; also the father of Jahzeiah in the time of Ezra) (r:12.22.14/15.10.15)
Tilgath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath) (d:first part of <Tilgath-pilneser>, the spelling of the name of Tiglath-Pileser king of Assyria used in Chronicles) (r:13.5.6/14.28.20)
Tilgath-pilneser = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath-Pileser) (d:king of Assyria, the spelling of Tiglath-pileser used in Chronicles) (r:13.5.6) (q:draft)
Tilon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tilon) (d:son of Shimon in the genealogy of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.20)
Timeus = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timaeus) (d:father of the blind beggar Bartimaeus of Jericho) (r:41.10.46)
Timias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timaeus) (d:father of the blind beggar Bartimaeus of Jericho) (r:41.10.46)
Timna = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Timna) (d:sister of Lotan the Horite and concubine of Eliphaz son of Esau, mother of Amalek; also the name of a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.22)
Timnah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Timnah) (d:name of two towns: one in the hill country of Judah, and one on the border of Judah and Dan where Samson sought a Philistine wife) (r:1.38.12/6.15.57)
Timnathheres = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Timnath Heres) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim where Joshua was buried, also called Timnath Serah) (r:7.2.9)
Timnathserah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Timnath Serah) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim that was given to Joshua, where he lived and was buried) (r:6.19.50/6.24.30)
Timon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timon) (d:one of the seven men chosen in the church at Jerusalem to serve at the daily distribution of food) (r:44.6.5)
Timoti = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timothy) (d:fellow worker of Paul from Lystra, to whom two letters of the New Testament are addressed) (r:57.1.1/44.16.1)
Tirannas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tyrannus) (d:man of Ephesus in whose lecture hall Paul taught daily) (r:44.19.9)
Tiras = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiras) (d:son of Japheth and grandson of Noah) (r:1.10.2)
Tirath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (w:Tirathite) (d:the Tirathites, a clan of scribes who lived at Jabez, counted among the Kenites) (r:13.2.55)
Tirhakah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tirhakah) (d:king of Cush who marched out against Sennacherib of Assyria in the days of Hezekiah) (r:12.19.9/23.37.9)
Tirhanah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tirhanah) (d:son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah) (r:13.2.48)
Tiria = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiria) (d:son of Jehallelel in the genealogy of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.16)
Tirzah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Tirzah) (d:city that was the capital of the northern kingdom of Israel from Jeroboam to Omri; also the name of a daughter of Zelophehad) (r:11.15.21/11.16.6)
Tishbe = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tishbe) (d:town in Gilead, the home of the prophet Elijah) (r:11.17.1)
Titu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Titus) (d:Greek fellow worker of Paul, sent by him to Corinth, to whom the letter to Titus is addressed) (r:48.2.3) (q:draft)
Titus = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Titus) (d:Greek fellow worker of Paul, sent by him to Corinth, to whom the letter to Titus is addressed) (r:48.2.3/47.7.6)
Tiz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tiz) (d:home of Joha the Tizite, one of the mighty warriors of David; the place is not otherwise known) (r:13.11.45)
to = (i:1) (t:part) (w:up/upward) (d:placed after a verb to show upward movement, as in {en to}, look up, {la to}, take up, and {leeng to}, fly up) (a:suk) (q:draft)
to = (i:2) (t:v) (w:dig) (d:dig a hole, pit or well) (q:draft)
to = (i:3) (t:n) (w:lord/master) (d:lord or master, a person who has authority over others; {ka to kumpipa} is my lord the king) (s:topa) (a:sila) (q:draft)
To = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tou) (d:first part of the name of the king of Hamath who sent gifts to David after the defeat of Hadadezer, written {To-i} in 2 Samuel and {To-u} in 1 Chronicles) (r:13.18.9) (q:draft)
Toah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Toah) (d:Levite of the clan of Kohath, an ancestor of Samuel and of the singer Heman) (q:draft)
Tob = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Tob) (d:region east of the Jordan where Jephthah lived after he fled from his brothers) (r:7.11.3/7.11.5)
Tobadonijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tob-Adonijah) (d:Levite sent by King Jehoshaphat to teach in the towns of Judah) (r:14.17.8)
Tobiah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tobiah) (d:Ammonite official who with Sanballat opposed Nehemiah and the rebuilding of the wall of Jerusalem; also the head of a family of returned exiles) (r:16.6.18/16.2.10)
Tobijah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tobijah) (d:name of two men: a Levite sent by Jehoshaphat to teach in Judah, and an exile who came back from Babylon in the time of Zechariah) (r:14.17.8/38.6.10)
Tofel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tophel) (d:place in the wilderness east of the Jordan, named with Paran where Moses spoke to Israel) (r:5.1.1)
Tofeth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Topheth) (d:place in the Valley of Ben Hinnom outside Jerusalem where children were burned as sacrifices to Molek) (r:12.23.10/24.19.14)
togarmah = (t:see) <Beth-togarmah>
Togarmah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Togarmah) (d:son of Gomer and grandson of Japheth, ancestor of a people of the far north) (r:1.10.3)
toh = (i:1) (t:part) (w:up/upward) (d:placed after a verb for upward movement; a spelling of <to> used before a following word such as <ni>, <ciangin> or <ding>) (b:to) (q:draft)
tohkik = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:back up) (d:<toh> up with <kik> back, placed after a verb: bring up again, here the hand from the dish to the mouth) (b:toh) (q:draft, low confidence)
tohna = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<toh> up or upward with <na>, which makes a noun; placed after a verb it names the going up or rising that the verb tells of, or the place gone up to: {kah tohna} a climbing up, {sap tohna} a calling up, {khan’tohna} growth or progress, {san’tohna} a being raised high) (b:toh) (r:54.4.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
tohsak = (i:1) (t:part) (d:<toh> up with <sak>, cause or do for another, placed after a verb: {sap tohsak} is call up, bring up for someone) (b:toh) (q:draft, low confidence)
tohtoh = (i:1) (t:part) (d:placed after a verb for an action that goes on and on: {a gen tohtoh ciangin} is as he went on speaking) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tohu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tohu) (d:son of Zuph of Ephraim, an ancestor of Elkanah the father of Samuel) (r:9.1.1)
Toi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tou) (d:king of Hamath who sent his son with gifts to David after the defeat of Hadadezer) (r:10.8.9)
toin = (i:1) (t:part) (w:up/upward) (d:the particle <to> with the linking ending <in>; after a verb, doing it upward and then the next action follows) (a:sukin) (b:to) (q:draft)
tok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stir up/churn/trouble) (d:stir water so that it becomes rough or muddy) (q:draft)
tok = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be missing/fall out) (d:said of a tooth that is gone and leaves a gap) (q:draft, low confidence)
tokgawpin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stirring up/churning up) (d:<tok> stir with <gawp> violently and the linking suffix <in>: stirring water until it is rough or muddy) (q:draft)
Tokhath = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tokhath) (d:father of Shallum the husband of the prophet Huldah, called Tikvah in 2 Kings) (r:14.34.22)
Tokhen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Token) (d:village of the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.32)
tokhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dig out/dig up/quarry/mine) (d:<to> dig with <khia> out: take stone or metal out of the ground) (b:to) (q:draft)
tokhiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who quarry/those who dig out) (d:<tokhia> dig out with the plural <te>) (b:tokhia) (q:draft)
tokhom = (i:1) (t:n) (w:throne/seat) (d:seat of a king or person of rank, as in {kumpi tokhom} royal throne; {hehpihna tokhom} is the atonement cover of the ark) (s:kumpitokhom/tutna) (r:2.39.35) (q:draft)
Tokhom = (i:1) (t:n) (w:throne) (d:<tokhom>, throne, capitalised for the throne of God and in {Kumpi Tokhom Innpi}, the Throne Hall of Solomon) (b:tokhom) (q:draft)
tokhomah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:on the throne/to the throne) (d:<tokhom> throne with the place marker <ah>) (b:tokhom) (q:draft)
tokhomkip = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:throne be established) (d:<tokhom> throne and <kip>, firm or established, written as one word in this verse) (q:draft, low confidence)
tokhomte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:thrones/seats) (d:<tokhom>, throne, with the plural <te>; {kumpi tokhomte} are royal thrones) (s:tutnate) (b:tokhom) (r:66.4.4) (q:draft)
tokin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stirring/churning) (d:<tok> stir with the linking suffix <in>) (b:tok) (q:draft)
toklo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stir up/incite/arouse) (d:stir people up against someone; <lo> here does not seem to be the negative) (b:tok) (q:draft, low confidence)
toknawi = (t:see) <toknawi-in>
toknawi-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:troubling/throwing into confusion) (d:<tok> stir up with <nawi>, and the linking ending <in>: stir up and unsettle the mind) (s:buaisakin) (q:draft)
toksuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:incite/stir up) (d:<tok> stir with <suah>, bring out: move someone to act against another) (s:hansuah/hanthawn) (q:draft)
toksuahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who incites/inciter) (d:<toksuah> incite with <pa> marking a man) (b:toksuah) (q:draft)
toktok = (i:1) (t:v) (w:churn/keep stirring) (d:repeated form of <tok>, stir: stir again and again, as milk to make butter) (q:draft)
toktol = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:slug/snail) (d:a soft creature that leaves slime as it moves) (q:draft, low confidence)
tol = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:bald/bare) (d:of the head, without hair, whether from loss of hair or from shaving; {met tol}, shave bare) (s:kolh/lukolh) (q:draft)
Tola = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tola) (d:eldest son of Issachar and ancestor of the Tolaite clan; also a judge of Israel, the son of Puah) (r:1.46.13/13.7.1)
Tolad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tolad) (d:town of the tribe of Simeon in the south of Judah, also called Eltolad) (q:draft)
Tolef = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tophel) (d:spelling of <Tofel>, a place in the wilderness east of the Jordan named with Paran where Moses spoke to Israel) (r:5.1.1)
Tolemais = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ptolemais) (d:seaport on the coast north of Mount Carmel, the Old Testament Akko, where Paul stayed one day) (r:44.21.7)
Tolemias = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ptolemais) (d:seaport on the coast north of Mount Carmel, the Old Testament Akko, where Paul stayed one day) (r:44.21.7)
tolen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fly upward/fly up) (d:<to>, up, with <len>, fly: fly upward, as sparks from a fire) (s:leengto/lengto) (a:leengsuk/lengsuk) (q:draft)
tolh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:miscarry) (d:lose the young before the time of birth, said of animals and of a woman; mostly with <ta>, young, written {ta tolh} or {ta-tolh}) (s:tatolh/nausia) (q:draft)
tolh = (i:2) (t:v) (w:slip out/come out) (d:slip or come out of its place, said of the bowels; followed by <khia>, out) (q:draft, low confidence)
tolhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:slip off/drop off/come out) (d:<tolh> slip out with <khia> out: of bonds falling from the hands, of bowels coming out of the body) (b:tolh) (q:draft)
tolhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come out/slip out) (d:form of <tolhkhia> used before <dongin> and other following words; of bowels coming out of the body) (b:tolhkhia) (q:draft)
tolsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make bald/shave bald) (d:<tol>, bald, with the causative <sak>: shave the head bare as a sign of mourning) (s:kolhsak/mettol) (b:tol) (q:draft)
tom = (i:2) (t:v) (w:gather/pick up/collect) (d:gather firewood or sticks, as in {sing tom}; of a bird, {bu tom} is build a nest) (s:tawm) (q:draft)
tomin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:briefly/in short) (d:<tom>, short, with the ending <in>: {a tomin} is in short, in few words; also being short, said of time) (b:tom) (q:draft)
tomin = (i:2) (t:v) (w:gathering/building) (d:<tom>, gather, with the linking ending <in>: {sing tomin} is gathering wood and {bu tomin} is building a nest) (b:tom) (q:draft)
tomkha = (i:1) (t:n) (w:short while/little while/moment) (d:a short time, usually as {tomkha sung}, for a little while; also a short distance, as in {tomkha pai}, go a little farther) (s:tawmvei/Tomnokhat) (a:hunsau) (q:draft)
tomkhano = (i:1) (t:n) (w:brief moment/very short while) (d:<tomkha>, short while, with the diminutive <no>: a very short moment, used with <sung>, within) (s:Tomnokhat) (b:tomkha) (q:draft)
tomlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shortness/brevity) (d:<tom>, short, with <lam>: how short something is, said of the length of life) (s:tomna) (q:draft, low confidence)
tomluate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those that are too short/stunted ones) (d:<tom> short with <lua>, too much, and the plural <te>; of an animal with a limb too short) (q:draft)
tommet = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cut short/crop) (d:<tom> short with <met>, shave or clip: {a sam uh a tommet} is those who clip their hair short; the NIV text has who are in distant places) (s:mettom) (q:draft, low confidence)
tomna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shortness/brevity) (d:<tom> short with the noun suffix <na>: the fact of being short in time) (s:tomlam) (b:tom) (q:draft)
tomna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:nest building) (d:<tom> gather, in {bu tom} build a nest, with the noun suffix <na>; {bu a tomna ding} is that it should build its nest) (b:tom) (q:draft)
tomno = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:brief/short/momentary/few) (d:very short, mostly of time: {tomno sung} is a moment, a short while, {tomno sungin} is in a moment, soon, and {ni tomno} is a few days) (a:sawt) (b:tom) (r:19.73.19) (q:draft)
Tomnokhat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:moment/short time) (d:a very short time; {Tomnokhat sungin} is in a moment) (s:tomkha/tomkhano) (q:draft)
tomsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shorten/cut short) (d:<tom>, short, with the causative <sak>: make shorter, cut short, said of days or of a time of life) (s:khiapsak) (a:sausak) (b:tom) (q:draft)
tomsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:gathering for) (d:<tom> gather firewood with <sak>, do for someone, and the linking ending <in>: gathering wood for another) (b:tom) (q:draft, low confidence)
tomtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:being able to nest/place to nest) (d:<tom>, build a nest, with <theih>, be able, and the noun suffix <na>: {bu a tomtheihna} is that birds are able to nest, said of the branches of a tree) (q:draft, low confidence)
ton = (i:1) (t:v) (w:accompany/be with/go together with) (d:be in the company of someone, come or go along with; <tawh>, with, marks the companion) (s:kithuah/ompih/tonkhawm) (q:draft)
tonbucip = (t:see) <tonbucip-a>
tonbucip-a = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:cringing/crouching/bowed down) (d:<tonbucip>, crouch down small, with <a> linking it to the verb <om>, be) (q:draft, low confidence)
tonbucipin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:cringing/crouching/bowed down) (d:<tonbucip>, crouch down small, with the linking ending <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
toncip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:stick to/cling to/cleave) (d:hold fast against something, as the tongue sticking to the roof of the mouth or people pressing themselves against a rock) (q:draft)
tong = (i:1) (t:n) (w:cubit) (d:unit of length, from the elbow to the tip of the fingers; the number follows, as in {tong sawmnga}, fifty cubits) (q:draft)
tongguk = (i:1) (t:n) (w:six cubits) (d:<tong> cubit with <guk> six, written as one word) (q:draft)
tongkua = (i:1) (t:n) (w:nine cubits) (d:<tong> cubit with <kua> nine, written as one word) (q:draft)
tongli = (i:1) (t:n) (w:four cubits) (d:<tong> cubit with <li> four, written as one word) (q:draft)
tongte = (t:see) <le-tongte>
tonin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:folded/creased) (d:<ton>, draw together in folds, with the linking ending <in>; said of cloth) (q:draft, low confidence)
tonkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go together/accompany/come along with/travel together) (d:<ton>, go in company, with <khawm>, together: travel or walk along with someone; <tawh>, with, marks the companion) (s:kithuah/ton) (b:ton) (q:draft)
tonkhawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:companions) (d:<tonkhawm>, go together, with the plural <te>: those who travel along with someone) (s:tonpihte/lawmte) (b:tonkhawm) (q:draft)
tonna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wrinkle) (d:<ton>, draw together in folds, with the noun suffix <na>; {sa tonna} is a wrinkle of the skin) (q:draft)
tonpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take along/accompany/go with) (d:have someone with oneself on a journey, take along; the person taken is the object) (r:46.9.5) (q:draft)
tonpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:taking along/accompanied by) (d:<tonpih>, take along, with the linking ending <in>) (b:tonpih) (q:draft)
tonpihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:companion) (d:<tonpih>, go with, with <pa> marking a man: the man who is with someone) (s:lawmpa/kikhawlpa) (b:tonpih) (q:draft)
tonpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:companions/those who go with) (d:<tonpih> go with, with plural <te>: the people who are with one on the way) (s:tonkhawmte/lawmte) (b:tonpih) (q:draft)
tonsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:send along with/cause to accompany) (d:<ton>, accompany, with the causative <sak>: send someone along with others) (s:kithuahsak/zuisak) (b:ton) (q:draft)
tonsak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:draw back/bring back) (d:<ton>, draw in, with the causative <sak>; with <kik>, back, it is draw a stretched-out hand back to the body) (s:kaiton/lehkaih) (q:draft, low confidence)
tonsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw back/pull back) (d:<tonsak>, draw in, with <kik> back: bring a stretched-out hand back to the body) (s:kaiton/lehkaih) (a:zankhia) (b:tonsak) (q:draft)
tonu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:mistress/lady) (d:<to>, lord or master, with <nu> marking a woman: a woman who is head of a household or has servants; also a queen, and a polite word for a lady) (a:nasemnu) (b:to) (q:draft)
Tonu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lady/queen) (d:<tonu>, lady or mistress, written with a capital: the lady to whom 2 John is addressed, and Babylon speaking of herself as queen) (b:tonu) (q:draft)
top = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pick up/gather/glean) (d:pick up things left lying: of grain, glean; of food, gather up what is left over; {van top} is take plunder) (s:tawm) (q:draft)
Top = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Tob) (d:region east of the Jordan, also written <Tob>, whose men were hired by the Ammonites to fight against David) (q:draft)
topa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:master/lord) (d:a human master or owner, the husband or lord one serves; {topa aw} is a polite form of address, and <Topa> with a capital is the Lord) (s:to) (a:nasem/sila/nasempa) (b:to) (r:1.43.20) (q:draft)
Topa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:Lord) (d:the Lord, the name by which God is called throughout the Bible text, and the title of Jesus as Lord; written with a capital to set it apart from <topa>, a human master) (s:Pasian/mangpa) (r:5.2.17)
topate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lords/masters) (d:<topa> with the plural <te>; in the verses always in the title Lord of lords) (s:tote) (b:topa) (r:66.19.16) (q:draft)
topaz = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:topaz) (d:a precious stone, the English name; one of the stones of the breastpiece of the high priest, where the NIV has chrysolite) (q:draft)
Topaz = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (w:topaz) (d:<topaz>, a precious stone, capitalised in the text) (b:topaz) (q:draft)
topsa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:gleanings/what was gathered) (d:<top> glean with <sa>, already done: what has been gleaned) (b:top) (q:draft)
tosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strengthen/make firm) (d:make strong and firm, said of the bars of a city gate) (s:khauhsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
tosak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:send up/cause to go up) (d:<to> upward with the causative <sak>, after a verb of movement: {paikhia tosak} is make someone go up out of a place) (a:paisuksak) (b:to) (q:draft)
tosukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:digging down) (d:<to> dig with <suk>, downward, and the linking ending <in>) (q:draft)
tot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:walk/tread/travel along) (d:walk along a path or road, and so follow a way of life; the form of <tawn> used before a noun or <ding>, as in {tot lampi}, the path walked) (s:tawn) (q:draft)
totai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:run up) (d:<to> up with <tai> run; {a suktai a totai kawikawi} is running down and up, here and there) (s:taito) (a:suktai) (q:draft, low confidence)
totawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dig for oneself/dig) (d:<to>, dig, with <tawm>, by oneself or for oneself: {tuikhuk totawm} is dig cisterns of their own) (s:to) (q:draft, low confidence)
tote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:masters/lords/sirs) (d:plural of <to>, master or lord: the masters of slaves or servants; {ka tote aw} is the polite address my lords, sirs) (s:topate) (a:silate/nasemte) (r:44.16.30) (q:draft)
tote = (i:2) (t:n) (w:diggers/those who dig) (d:<to>, dig, with <te>, the people who dig) (b:to) (q:draft, low confidence)
totna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:treading/walking/stepping) (d:<tot>, walk along, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of treading or walking; {a totna mun} is the place where the foot treads, and {lampi totna} is walking in the ways of someone) (b:tot) (q:draft)
toto = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:more and more/continually/onward) (d:<to>, upward, said twice and placed after a verb to show that an action or state goes on and increases) (s:semsem) (b:to) (q:draft)
totsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:trodden/walked on) (d:<tot> with <sa>, already done: describes land or a path on which someone has walked) (b:tot) (q:draft)
totte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ways/paths walked) (d:<tot> walk along with the plural <te>: the paths one has walked, one's conduct) (b:tot) (q:draft, low confidence)
tovang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dig through/dig into) (d:<to> dig with <vang> hole: dig a hole through a wall) (s:tawhvang) (q:draft)
tovungin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:dig around/dig) (d:dig up the soil around a plant, with the connective ending <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
Trakhonis = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Traconitis) (d:region south of Damascus and east of Galilee, ruled by the tetrarch Philip) (r:42.3.1)
Trakhonitis = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Traconitis) (d:region south of Damascus and east of Galilee, ruled by the tetrarch Philip) (r:42.3.1)
Trifana = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Tryphena) (d:Christian woman in Rome whom Paul greets as a worker in the Lord, named together with Tryphosa) (r:45.16.12)
Trifosa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Tryphosa) (d:Christian woman in Rome whom Paul greets as a worker in the Lord, named together with Tryphena) (r:45.16.12)
Troas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Troas) (d:port city on the north-west coast of Asia Minor, where Paul saw the vision of the man of Macedonia) (r:44.16.8/44.20.5)
Trofimas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Trophimus) (d:Christian from Ephesus who travelled with Paul to Jerusalem and was later left sick at Miletus) (r:44.21.29/55.4.20)
Trofosa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Tryphosa) (d:Christian woman in Rome whom Paul greets as a worker in the Lord, named together with Tryphena) (r:45.16.12)
tu = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:this/present) (d:this, the present, said of time: {tu ni} is today, <tu-in> is now, and {tu-a kipan} is from now on)
tu takin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (w:at the moment/at present/just now/right now/at the present time)
Tua = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:that/those) (d:<tua>, that, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; it stands before a noun, or before <bang> and <ciangin>, as in {Tua bangin}, in that way, and {Tua ciangin}, then) (b:tua) (r:9.25.3) (q:draft)
tuaci = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:like/just as/so/like that) (d:in that way, as it is: {a tuaci bang} is such a thing, {a tuaci mah} is just like that, and {tuaci omsak} is leave someone or something as it is)
tuacih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:do so/do that/be so) (d:<tuaci>, in that way, in the form used as a verb: act in the way just spoken of, do so) (b:tuaci) (q:draft)
tuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:join/bring together) (d:bring two things together so that they touch or are joined: {khui tuah} is sew together, and {kimai tuah} is come face to face) (s:gawm)
tuah = (i:2) (t:v) (w:bring/meet with/encounter/come upon) (d:meet with or come upon something, most often trouble, an enemy or a fate; {haksatna tuah} is meet hardship and {gal tuah} is face war) (s:tuak/tuakkha)
tuahin = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:together) (d:<tuah>, join or meet, with the linking ending <in>, placed after a verb: {khui tuahin} is sewing together and {kimai tuahin} is face to face) (b:tuah)
tuahin = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:attach) (d:<tuah>, put against, with the linking ending <in>: putting one thing against another so that they touch)
tuahkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet/encounter/come upon/fall into) (d:<tuah>, meet, with <khak>, happen to: happen to meet a person or meet with an event; {a tuahkhak peuh} is whoever one happens to meet) (s:tuakkha) (q:draft)
tuahlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:incur/meet with/suffer) (d:<tuah>, meet with, with <lawh>, as a result: bring upon oneself, come to suffer) (s:tuaklawh/thuaklawh) (q:draft)
tuahmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry off/plunder) (d:<tuah> come upon, with <mang> away; followed by <sak>, let someone carry off, give as plunder) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahmangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give as plunder/let carry off) (d:<tuahmang> with the causative <sak>; let the enemy carry everything off) (s:tuahsakmang/sutsak) (b:tuahmang) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:encounter/experience) (d:<tuah>, meet with, with the noun suffix <na>: meeting with or going through something; {na tuahna mun peuh} is any place you happen upon) (b:tuah) (q:draft)
tuahpha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet with good/fare well) (d:<tuah> meet with and <pha> good: have good come to one, set against <tuahsiatna>, misfortune) (a:tuahsia) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahphasak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give success/make prosper) (d:<tuahpha> meet with good, with the causative <sak>) (s:daupaisak) (b:tuahpha) (q:draft)
tuahphat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prosper/fare well/meet with good) (d:form of <tuahpha> used before <ciangin>) (s:daupai/cithei) (a:tuahsiat) (b:tuahpha) (q:draft)
tuahsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:experienced/met with) (d:<tuah> meet with, with <sa> already done; {tuahsa thute} is the things one has gone through) (b:tuah) (q:draft)
tuahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let come upon/hand over) (d:<tuah> meet, come upon, with the causative <sak>; with <mang>, give away as plunder) (b:tuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsakmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:give as plunder/let carry off) (d:<tuah> come upon, with the causative <sak> and <mang> away) (s:tuahmangsak/sutsak) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsia = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:unfortunate/hapless/afflicted) (d:<tuah>, meet with, and <sia>, bad: meeting with misfortune; {mi tuahsia} or {tuahsia mi} is a victim, one struck by trouble) (s:kamsia) (a:hampha) (q:draft)
tuahsia = (i:2) (t:v) (w:meet disaster/suffer ruin) (d:be struck by calamity; {tuahsia-in}, in calamity) (a:tuahpha) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet with disaster/suffer misfortune) (d:form of <tuahsia> used before <ni>, <ciangin> and other following words; {a tuahsiat ni} is the day of their disaster) (a:tuahphat) (b:tuahsia) (q:draft)
tuahsiate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:victims/unfortunate ones) (d:<tuahsia> unfortunate with the plural <te>; {mi tuahsiate}, people struck by misfortune) (b:tuahsia) (q:draft)
tuahsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:misfortune/disaster/calamity/trouble) (d:<tuahsiat>, meet with disaster, with the noun suffix <na>: something bad that befalls a person; {tuahsiatna tuak} is meet with calamity) (s:kamsiatna/siatna/thusia) (b:tuahsiat) (q:draft)
tuahsiatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:disasters/calamities/misfortunes) (d:<tuahsiatna>, disaster, with the plural <te>) (s:kamsiatnate/siatnate) (b:tuahsiatna) (q:draft)
tuahsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go down/descend) (d:go down a slope toward a place, the opposite of <kahto>, go up) (s:paisuk/kumsuk/tuaksuk) (a:kahto/paito) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:slope/descent) (d:<tuahsuk>, go down, with the noun suffix <na>: the way down, a slope; {tuahsukna mun} is the place where the road goes down) (s:paisukna) (b:tuahsuk) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahtuah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come upon/find) (d:reduplicated <tuah>, meet: wherever one comes upon something; {a tuahtuah munah} is right on the spot where they found them) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahtuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<tuahtuah>, come upon, with the noun suffix <na>: the place where one comes upon something; {a tuahtuahna munah} is on the very spot) (b:tuahtuah) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:at that time/then/in those days) (d:<tua>, that, with <hun>, time: at that time; of the past it is followed by <lai-in> or <laitakin>, of the future by <ciangin>) (r:49.2.12) (q:draft)
tuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be lawful/be right/be proper/be fitting) (d:be right, fitting or allowed, placed after another verb: {piak tuak} is right to give, and with <lo> it is not allowed) (q:draft)
tuak = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:each/both) (d:each of them, both alike, placed after a noun, a number or a verb) (s:ciat/tek) (r:2.32.15) (q:draft)
tuak = (i:3) (t:v) (w:meet/meet with/come upon/experience) (d:come upon a person or thing, or meet with an experience such as trouble, fear or punishment) (s:tuakkha/kimu) (r:1.4.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuaka = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:each/both) (d:<tuak>, each, with the ending <a>, used after <pang>, side: {pang tuaka om} is being on each side or on both sides) (b:tuak) (q:draft)
tuakah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:on both sides/on each side/on either side) (d:<tuak>, each or both, with the place marker <ah>, used after <pang> or <lang>, side: on both sides, on each of the two) (s:langtuakah) (b:tuak) (q:draft)
tuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meeting/coming upon/finding) (d:<tuak>, meet, with the linking ending <in>: meeting a person, or meeting with death or trouble, and then the next action follows) (q:draft)
tuakin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:both/each) (d:<tuak>, each, with the ending <in>, mostly after a number: {a nih tuakin} is both of the two; {a tuam tuakin} is each one apart) (s:tegel) (b:tuak) (q:draft)
tuakin = (i:3) (t:v) (w:getting down/alighting/plunging) (d:<tuak> with the linking ending <in>: getting down from an animal or a chariot, or plunging down into something) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuakkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet with/come upon/happen to meet/find) (d:<tuak>, meet, with <kha>, happen to: come upon a person by chance, find someone doing something, or meet with trouble) (s:tuak) (q:draft)
tuakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:get off/disembark/get out) (d:<tuak>, get down, with <khia>, out: come out and down from a ship or boat) (s:kumkhia) (q:draft)
tuaklawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:incur/meet with/suffer) (d:<tuak>, meet with, and <lawh>, as a result: bring something bad upon oneself) (s:thuaklawh/thuakkha) (q:draft)
tuaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:not meet with/not suffer) (d:<tuak> meet with and <lo> not, written as one word) (b:tuak) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuaklo = (i:2) (t:v) (w:not be possible/not be proper) (d:<tuak> be fitting with <lo> not, placed after another verb) (b:tuak) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<tuak>, each or meet, with the noun suffix <na>; in the text it is part of a section heading, {A Kideih Tuakna}, apparently the desire of each for the other) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who meets) (d:<tuak> meet with <pa>, the man: the man who meets or runs into something) (b:tuak) (q:draft)
tuakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet at once/find right away) (d:<tuak> meet, with <pah> at once) (q:draft)
tuakpeuh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:retaliate) (d:<tuak>, meet, with <peuh>, any: {a tuakpeuh} in the verse is anyone who comes upon him)
tuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:inflict/make suffer/bring upon) (d:<tuak>, meet with, and <sak>, cause: make someone meet with or undergo something, usually trouble or punishment) (s:thuaksak) (b:tuak) (r:15.9.13) (q:draft)
tuaksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come down/go down/descend/jump down) (d:move downward from a higher place, also step, climb or jump down, the opposite of <kahto>, go up) (s:paisuk/kumsuk/tuahsuk) (a:kahto/paito) (q:draft)
tuaksukin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:come down/alight) (d:<tuaksuk> go down, with the connective ending <in>) (b:tuaksuk) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuaksuksuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go straight down/descend) (d:<tuaksuk> go down, with <suak> right through) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuaktuak = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:each/both alike) (d:reduplicated <tuak>, each; said of two who are equally so) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuakun = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:both/each) (d:<tuak>, each, with the plural ending <un>, after a number: {a nih tuakun} is both of them) (s:tegel) (b:tuak) (q:draft)
tuakzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:meet with more/encounter more) (d:<tuak> meet with, with <zaw> more) (b:tuak) (q:draft)
tual = (i:1) (t:n) (w:court/courtyard/open space) (d:open enclosed space around or in front of a building: {buk tual} is the courtyard of the tabernacle, {biakinn tual} the court of the temple) (s:huang/inntual) (r:26.40.47) (q:draft)
tual = (i:2) (t:adj) (w:native/native-born/local) (d:in {tual sung mi}, a native-born person as opposed to <peemta> or <khualmi>, a foreigner; also written as one word, <tualsung>) (s:tualsung) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuala = (i:1) (t:n) (w:of the court/in the court) (d:<tual> court, with the ending <a>, of or in) (b:tual) (q:draft, low confidence)
tualah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in the courtyard/into the court) (d:<tual> courtyard with the place marker <ah>) (b:tual) (q:draft)
tualno = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small court/small courtyard) (d:<tual> court with <no> small) (b:tual) (q:draft)
tualnote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:small courts/small courtyards) (d:plural of <tualno>) (b:tualno) (q:draft)
tualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:square/open square/public square) (d:large open space of a town where people gather, from <tual>, open space, with <pi>, large) (b:tual) (q:draft)
tualpi = (i:2) (t:n) (w:robe) (d:in {puan tualpi}, a long outer garment or robe, also written as one word <puantualpi>) (q:draft, low confidence)
tualsuak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:native-born/native) (d:a person born in the land, set against <peemta>, a foreigner living there) (s:gammi) (a:peemta/khualmi/gamdangmi) (q:draft)
tualsung = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:native-born/native/local) (d:belonging to the home community: {tualsung mi} is a native-born person as opposed to <peemta>, a foreigner living among them) (s:tual) (a:gamdang) (q:draft)
tualte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:courts/courtyards) (d:plural of <tual>: the courts of a building, mostly of the temple) (b:tual) (q:draft)
tualtengah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in all the courts) (d:<tual> court, with <teng> all and <ah> in) (q:draft)
tuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cover/wrap/cover up) (d:spread over something so that it is hidden, or wrap it round, as cloud covers a mountain or a cloth covers the face) (s:khuh) (a:guak) (r:26.1.23) (q:draft)
tuamah = (i:1) (t:pron) (w:that very/the same) (d:<tua> that with the emphatic <mah>; {tuamah bangin}, in the same way, likewise) (b:tua) (q:draft)
tuamah = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:in his own place) (d:apparently <tuam> separate with the place marker <ah>: in the separate place, his own place) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuamcip = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cover completely/envelop/surround) (d:<tuam>, cover, with <cip>, tightly: cover over completely or wrap all round, said of smoke, darkness, worms, shame or love) (s:khuhcip) (b:tuam) (q:draft)
tuamcipin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:covering completely) (d:<tuamcip> cover completely with the linking ending <in>) (b:tuamcip) (q:draft)
tuamcippa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who wraps up) (d:<tuamcip> wrap up completely, with <pa>, the male one who does it) (b:tuamcip) (q:draft)
tuamdang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:different/other/another) (d:of another kind, not the same as before or as the rest; placed after the noun) (s:dang/tuam) (a:kibang) (q:draft)
