Zefi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zepho) (d:son of Eliphaz and grandson of Esau, called Zepho in Genesis) (r:13.1.36)
Zefo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zepho) (d:son of Eliphaz and grandson of Esau, a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.11/1.36.15)
Zefon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zephon) (d:son of Gad, ancestor of the Zephonite clan) (q:draft)
zehphi = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:defiled/unclean) (d:ritually defiled or unclean; in 1 Corinthians 8:7 said of people of weak conscience who think of themselves as defiled after eating food offered to idols) (s:nin/kihhuai) (a:zehsiang/siang) (q:draft, low confidence)
zehphitna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:abomination/defilement) (d:a thing that defiles what is holy; {a lipkhaphuai zehphitna} is the abomination that causes desolation spoken of by Daniel) (s:kihhuaina/nitna) (r:40.24.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
zehsiang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:ceremonially clean/purified) (d:clean according to the ritual law and so fit to take part in worship; said of priests and Levites who had purified themselves) (s:siang) (a:zehphi/nin) (q:draft)
Zeisu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jesus) (d:Jesus of Nazareth, the Christ; a Tedim spelling of the name, also written <Jesuh>) (r:43.11.35/41.1.43)
ZEISU = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jesus) (d:<Zeisu>, Jesus, written in capital letters in the notice placed above him on the cross) (r:40.27.37) (q:draft)
zeizai = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:all over/spread about) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, describing many things lying, falling, hanging or shining spread out over a wide area: {paak zeizai} is strewn everywhere, {tuk zeizai} is fall dead all over a field) (q:draft, low confidence)
zeizaina = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<zeizai>, spread all over, with the noun suffix <na>: a place where many things hang or lie all about; in Song of Songs 4:4 the tower on which a thousand shields hang) (b:zeizai) (q:draft, low confidence)
zek = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:a little/slightly) (d:placed after a word of time, amount or distance: a little, a short while; {a den zek ciangin} is a little later, {kumkhat val zek} is a little over a year) (s:neukha/themcik) (q:draft, low confidence)
zekaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:delay/detain/hinder) (d:<zekai>, be late, with the causative <sak>: make someone late, hold someone back) (b:zekai) (q:draft)
Zekhariah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zechariah) (d:name of many men, among them the prophet Zechariah son of Berekiah and the priest who was the father of John the Baptist) (r:38.7.8/13.9.37)
Zekher = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zeker) (d:son of Jeiel of Gibeon, of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.31)
zekna = (t:see) <zekna-ah>
zekna-ah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in managing/in the handling of) (d:<zekna> management, handling of what is entrusted, with <ah> in) (r:40.25.23) (q:draft)
zeksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:put in charge of/entrust with) (d:cause to manage, with causative <sak>) (s:kepsak) (r:40.25.23) (q:draft)
zel = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:repeatedly/habitually/again and again) (d:placed after a verb for an action done time after time or by custom) (s:zelzel/zeel/kikkik) (r:44.9.28) (q:draft)
zel = (i:2) (t:v) (w:spread over/pervade) (d:of fame, news or praise: spread and reach throughout a land) (s:zeel/kizel) (r:45.10.18) (q:draft)
Zela = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zelah/Zela) (d:town of Benjamin where Saul and Jonathan were buried in the tomb of Kish) (r:6.18.28/10.21.14)
Zelek = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zelek) (d:an Ammonite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.37/13.11.39)
zelh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread over/reach) (d:form of <zel> spread over, used before <bangin>) (b:zel) (q:draft)
zelin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:throughout/all over) (d:<zel>, spread over, with the marker <in>: spreading through a whole area) (b:zel) (q:draft)
zelin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:again and again/repeatedly) (d:<zel>, repeatedly, with the linking marker <in> after a verb) (s:zelzelin/kikkik) (b:zel) (q:draft)
Zelofehad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zelophehad) (d:son of Hepher of the tribe of Manasseh, who had no sons and whose five daughters received his inheritance) (r:4.26.33/4.36.11)
zelpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:spread quickly) (d:<zel> spread through, with <pak> quickly, of news) (q:draft)
Zelzah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zelzah) (d:place on the border of Benjamin near the tomb of Rachel) (r:9.10.2)
zelzelin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:again and again/repeatedly/often) (d:<zelzel>, repeatedly, with the ending <in>, placed after a verb) (s:zelin/kikkik) (b:zelzel) (r:19.59.14) (q:draft)
zelzelna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:frequent occurrence/repeated doing) (d:<zelzel>, again and again, with the noun suffix <na>: the fact that something is done or happens many times; {na nat mun zelzelna} is your frequent illnesses) (b:zelzel) (q:draft)
zelzelte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who often/those who repeatedly) (d:<zelzel> again and again, with the plural <te>, after a verb: {a khialthei zelzelte}, those who err again and again) (b:zelzel) (q:draft)
zelzul = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:disorderly/confused) (d:in disorder, confused; in 1 Corinthians 14 said of what God did not call his people to be, set against {hoihtak nuamtakin}, in a good and peaceful way) (q:draft, low confidence)
zem = (i:1) (t:v) (w:decorate/adorn) (d:make something beautiful by adding ornament, as overlaying an idol with silver and gold, decorating a tomb or working cloth with coloured thread) (s:zep/zeem/etlawmsak)
Zemaraim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zemaraim) (d:town of Benjamin near Bethel; also a mountain in the hill country of Ephraim) (r:6.18.22)
