zep = (i:1) (t:v) (w:decorate/adorn/ornament) (d:make beautiful with ornament; {sing zep nasep} is ornamental work in wood, carving; in Titus 2 said of adorning the teaching by good conduct) (s:zem/zeem/etlawmsak/hoihbawl) (q:draft)
zepin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:folding) (d:fold the hands, with <in> linking it to the next verb; {khut zepin om} is sit with folded hands) (q:draft)
zepna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:setting/ornament/decoration) (d:something made to adorn or to hold a stone, as the gold settings on the priestly garments and carved decoration on a wall, from <zep> adorn) (s:kizepna) (b:zep) (q:draft)
zepna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:folding) (d:in {khut zepna}, folding of the hands to rest) (q:draft, low confidence)
zepnate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ornaments/decorations/overlays) (d:<zepna>, ornament, with the plural <te>; {khuamlu zepnate} are the decorated tops of the posts, overlaid with silver) (s:kizepnate) (b:zepna) (q:draft)
Zer = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zer) (d:one of the fortified towns of Naphtali) (q:draft)
