Zethar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zethar) (d:one of the seven eunuchs who served King Xerxes) (r:17.1.10)
Zeus = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Zeus) (d:chief god of the Greeks; the people of Lystra called Barnabas by this name) (r:44.14.12/44.14.13)
zeza = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:quite/very) (d:expressive word placed after a descriptive word to strengthen it; {mam zeza} is quite straight, {san zeza} is bright red) (q:draft, low confidence)
zia = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way/manner/conduct) (d:the way something is done, placed after a verb or verbal noun as in {hih zia}, way of doing) (s:omdan/paizia/lampi) (q:draft)
Zia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zia) (d:a man of the tribe of Gad, head of a family) (q:draft)
ziahziah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:freely/generously/liberally) (d:placed after a verb of giving or spending: without holding back) (s:zuahzuah) (q:draft)
zial = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roll up/roll) (d:roll up a scroll, a cloth, a sleeve or a bundle; {laidal zial} is a rolled scroll) (s:khep/hial) (a:phen) (q:draft)
zialetongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ways/manners) (d:<zia le tong>, manner and way of doing, written as one word with the plural <te>) (s:ziate/paiziate) (q:draft)
zialin = (i:1) (t:adv) (d:follows <dak>, look, in {tawlet-ah hong dak zialin}, looking in at the window; what <zial> adds here is not clear) (q:draft, low confidence)
zialkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roll away/roll off) (d:<zial> roll, with <khia> out, away) (b:zial) (q:draft)
zialkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:pack up/roll up beforehand) (d:<zial> roll up, with <khol> beforehand: roll up a bundle in readiness) (q:draft)
zialmang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:swallow up/make an end of) (d:<zial> roll up with <mang> away; NIV has devour, said of overcoming a people easily) (q:draft, low confidence)
zialto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:roll up) (d:<zial> roll, with <to> upward: roll up a sleeve) (b:zial) (q:draft)
zialzial = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:flashing/glittering) (d:after <tee> shine, describes light that flashes again and again like lightning) (s:zalzal) (q:draft, low confidence)
zialzial = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:freely/about) (d:after <pai> go, describes going about freely wherever one wishes) (s:kawikawi) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziat = (i:1) (t:n) (w:right/right side/right hand) (d:the right as opposed to <vei>, the left; {ziat lam} is the right-hand side) (s:taklam/ziatlam) (a:veilam/vei) (q:draft)
ziate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ways/manners/conduct) (d:<zia>, way or manner, with the plural <te>: the ways in which a person lives and acts) (s:paiziate/gamtatnate/omziate) (b:zia) (q:draft)
ziatlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:right/right side/right hand) (d:the right-hand side; the opposite is <veilam>, left) (s:taklam/ziat) (a:veilam) (q:draft)
ziatlamah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:on the right/at the right side) (d:<ziatlam> right side, with <ah> at) (a:veilamah) (b:ziatlam) (q:draft)
ziau = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:swiftly/easily/at once) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done quickly and lightly in one movement: {la ziau}, snatch away; {botsat ziau}, snap off; {paikhia ziau}, slip away) (s:pak) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziauziau = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:readily/lightly/easily) (d:placed after a verb: do something lightly and readily, as changing the mind again and again or bringing out whatever one pleases; exact force not confirmed) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziazua = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:all about/rattling) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, describing many things together making a rattling or crackling noise, lying or seen all over a place, or shining brightly: {ging ziazua} is rattle, {om ziazua} is lie all about, {tee ziazua} is shine all over) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziazuana = (i:1) (t:n) (w:splendour/majesty) (d:<ziazua>, expressive word, with the noun suffix <na>; {thupi ziazuana} is great splendour on display) (b:ziazua) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziazuate = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<ziazua>, expressive word for a rattling noise, with the plural <te>: {sakol leeng ging ziazuate}, the rattling chariots) (b:ziazua) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ziba = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ziba) (d:servant of the household of Saul, who managed the land of Mephibosheth for David) (r:10.9.9/10.9.12)
Zibeon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zibeon) (d:a Horite chief, son of Seir and father of Anah) (r:1.36.20/1.36.29)
Zibia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zibia) (d:a Benjamite, son of Shaharaim and his wife Hodesh) (q:draft)
