zidang = (i:1) (t:n) (w:other wife) (d:<zi> wife, with <dang> other: {a pa’ zidang} is a wife of his father other than his own mother) (q:draft)
zidangte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:other wives) (d:<zidang>, another wife, with the plural <te>: the other wives of a man, as a father’s wives other than one’s own mother) (b:zidang) (q:draft)
Ziddim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ziddim) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.35)
Zif = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ziph) (d:town in the hill country of Judah with a desert nearby where David hid from Saul, also a town in the south of Judah and a man of Judah; {Zif mite} are the Ziphites) (r:14.11.8) (q:draft)
Zifah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ziphah) (d:son of Jehallelel, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.16)
Zifion = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ziphion/Zephon) (d:son of Gad, called Zephon in the NIV) (r:1.46.16)
Zifron = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ziphron) (d:place on the northern border of the land of Canaan) (r:4.34.9)
Ziha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ziha) (d:head of a family of temple servants who returned from exile, and an overseer of the temple servants living on Ophel) (r:15.2.43/16.11.21)
ziik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build up/raise up) (d:build up a road by heaping up earth; a spelling of <zik> with a long vowel, in {lampi ziik sak}, have a road built up) (s:zik) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquake/earth tremor) (d:a shaking of the earth; used with <liing>, shake: {ziin liing} is the earth quakes) (s:zin/zinling/zinliing) (r:42.21.11) (q:draft)
ziing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:deep darkness/gloom) (d:paired with <khuamial>, darkness: {khuamial sung leh a ziing sung} is darkness and the deepest gloom; written with a long vowel, the same word as <zing>) (s:khuazing/khuamialpi) (a:khuavak) (q:draft)
ziing = (i:2) (t:v) (w:grow dark/be darkened) (d:become dark, in {khim ziing}, darkness falls over a place; written with a long vowel, the same word as <zing>) (s:khimzing) (a:vak) (q:draft)
ziingin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dark/be gloomy) (d:<ziing> grow dark, with the linking suffix <in>: {khua ziingin}, the day being dark) (s:zingin/mialin) (b:ziing) (q:draft)
ziingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:darken/make dark) (d:<ziing> grow dark, with causative <sak>) (s:zingsak/mialsak) (a:taangsak) (b:ziing) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziingtho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rise early/get up early) (d:<ziing>, a spelling of <zing>, morning, with <tho>, rise: get up early in the morning) (s:zingtho/thobaih) (q:draft)
ziinling = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:another spelling of <zinling>: <zin>, earthquake, and <ling>, shake) (s:zinling/zinliing/ziin) (q:draft)
zik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build up/raise up) (d:build up a road by heaping up earth) (s:ziik) (q:draft, low confidence)
zikik = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wife) (d:<zi> wife with <kik> again, perhaps a wife taken after an earlier one; NIV has simply wife) (s:zi) (b:zi) (q:draft, low confidence)
zikin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build up/raise up) (d:<zik> build up a road, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:zik) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ziklag = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ziklag) (d:town in the south of Judah, given to David by Achish king of Gath) (r:6.15.31/13.4.30)
Zikri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zikri) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Izhar the Levite and an Ephraimite warrior in the time of Ahaz) (r:2.6.21)
ziksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:build up/make into a road) (d:<zik> build up a road, with <sak>: cause a road to be built up) (b:zik) (q:draft, low confidence)
zilepasal = (i:1) (t:n) (w:husband and wife/spouse) (d:{zi le pasal}, wife and husband, written as one word; {zilepasal neisate} are married people) (q:draft)
zileta = (t:see) <zileta-in>
zileta-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:by marriage) (d:{zi le ta}, wife and child, with <in>: joined as wife and children, that is by marriage and family ties) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zillah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zillah) (d:one of the two wives of Lamech, mother of Tubal-Cain) (r:1.4.19/1.4.22)
Zillethai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zillethai) (d:name of two men, a Benjamite and a commander of Manasseh who joined David at Ziklag) (r:13.12.20/13.8.20)
Zilpah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Zilpah) (d:servant of Leah, given to Jacob as a wife, mother of Gad and Asher) (r:1.30.12)
Zilpahte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Zilpah) (d:<Zilpah>, servant of Leah and wife of Jacob, with <te> marking her together with Bilhah) (b:Zilpah) (r:1.37.2)
Zimmah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zimmah) (d:Levite of the clan of Gershon) (r:13.6.20/13.6.42)
zimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:band/binding/hem) (d:edging worked round the neck opening of a robe so that it does not tear) (q:draft)
Zimran = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zimran) (d:son of Abraham and Keturah) (r:1.25.2)
Zimri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zimri) (d:name of several men, among them the king of Israel who reigned seven days in Tirzah; also a land whose kings are named in Jeremiah) (r:13.2.6/24.25.25)
zin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:a shaking of the earth; {zin liing} or {zin ling} is the earth quakes) (s:ziin/zinling/zinliing) (q:draft)
zin = (i:3) (t:v) (w:travel/journey) (d:go on a journey or move from place to place; {khual zin} is travel away from home) (s:khualzin/lampai) (q:draft)
zin = (i:4) (t:v) (w:be overcast/grow dark) (d:of clouds, gather and darken the sky; written {zin’} before <ding>) (s:ziing/khimzing) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zin) (d:desert on the southern border of Canaan in which Kadesh lies, in the phrase {Zin gamlak}, the Desert of Zin) (r:6.15.1) (q:draft)
Zina = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ziza) (d:son of Shimei, a Levite of the clan of Gershon, called Ziza in the NIV) (r:13.23.10/13.23.11)
zindo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:show hospitality/entertain/receive as guest) (d:<zin>, guest, with <do>, receive: welcome and look after a guest; {zindo siam} is hospitable; also used as a noun, hospitality) (q:draft)
zindona = (i:1) (t:n) (w:reception/welcome/hospitality) (d:<zindo> receive as a guest, with the noun suffix <na>) (b:zindo) (q:draft)
zinei = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marry/take a wife) (d:of a man, have or take a wife, from <zi> wife and <nei> have; {zinei thak pa} is the bridegroom, {zinei pasalnei} is marrying and being given in marriage) (s:tenpih) (q:draft)
zineih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:marry/take a wife) (d:form of <zinei> used before <ding> and in dependent clauses; {zineih ding hun} is the time of the wedding) (b:zinei) (q:draft)
zineihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:<zineih> take a wife, with the noun suffix <na>; {zineihna pawi} is a wedding feast) (s:zipina/zipi/mopina/kitenna) (b:zineih) (q:draft)
zineipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:{zi nei}, take a wife, with {-pa} for a man) (s:zipipa/mopipa) (b:zinei) (q:draft)
zineite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:married men/those who have a wife) (d:<zinei> have a wife, with the plural <te>) (b:zinei) (q:draft)
zineu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:concubine) (d:<zi>, wife, with <neu>, small: a secondary wife of lower rank) (q:draft)
zineute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:concubines) (d:plural of <zineu>, a lesser wife, <zi> wife with <neu> small) (b:zineu) (q:draft)
zing = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:cloudy/overcast/dark) (d:of the sky or a day, clouded over and dark; {khim zing} is darkness falls over a place)
zing = (i:2) (t:n) (w:dwell) (d:of a cloud, settle and stay over a place)
zinga = (i:1) (t:n) (d:second part of {kong zing}, street, with <a>, at: {kong zinga}, in the streets) (q:draft, low confidence)
zingciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:tomorrow/the next day/the next morning) (d:<zingciang>, tomorrow, with the suffix <in>; {a zingciangin} is on the following day) (a:zani) (b:zingciang) (q:draft)
zinggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:grow utterly dark) (d:<zing> dark or cloudy, with <gawp> thoroughly: {khim zinggawp}, darkness falls completely) (b:zing) (q:draft)
zingin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be dark/be gloomy) (d:<zing> dark or cloudy, with the linking suffix <in>: {khua zingin}, the day being dark) (s:ziingin/mialin) (b:zing) (q:draft)
zingsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:darken/make dark) (d:<zing> dark, cloudy, with causative <sak>) (s:ziingsak/mialsak) (a:taangsak) (b:zing) (q:draft)
zingsanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the morning/of the morning) (d:<zingsang>, morning, with the suffix <a>, in or of; {zingsanga meihal biakna} is the morning burnt offering) (s:zingsangin) (a:nitakin) (b:zingsang) (q:draft)
zingsangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in the morning) (d:<zingsang>, morning, with the suffix <in>: in the morning; often followed by {tho baih}, get up early) (s:zingsanga) (a:nitakin) (b:zingsang) (q:draft)
zingsol = (i:1) (t:n) (c:star) (w:morning star) (d:the bright star seen before dawn, <zing>, morning, with {sol}) (q:draft)
Zingsol = (i:1) (t:n) (c:star) (w:Morning Star) (d:<zingsol>, the morning star, written with a capital as a title) (b:zingsol) (q:draft)
zingtho = (i:1) (t:v) (w:rise early/get up early) (d:<zing> morning, with <tho> rise: get up early in the morning) (s:ziingtho/thobaih) (q:draft)
zingtungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:early in the morning/at dawn) (d:<zingtung> early morning with the marker {-in}) (s:zingtuungin) (q:draft)
zingtuungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:early in the morning) (d:<zing> morning, with <tuung> and <in>) (s:zingtungin) (q:draft)
zinin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:travelling/journeying) (d:<zin>, travel, with the linking suffix <in>; {khual zinin} is travelling away from home) (s:khualzinin) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zinin = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:as a guest/as a stranger) (d:<zin>, guest or sojourner, with the suffix <in>; {zinin om} is stay as a guest or live as a foreigner) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zinkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go away on a journey/set out/leave home) (d:<zin>, travel, with <khia>, out) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zinkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:travel again/journey back) (d:<zin> travel, with <kik> again or back) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zinleleeng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guests/visitors/strangers) (d:<zin> and <leeng>, guests and visitors of every kind; {zinleleeng do} is show hospitality) (s:zinte) (q:draft)
zinliing = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:<zin> earthquake, with <liing> shake) (s:zinling/ziinling/ziin) (q:draft)
zinliingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquakes) (d:{zin liing} the earth quakes, with plural <te>) (b:zinliing) (q:draft)
zinlin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:<zinling>, earthquake, written without the final g and with an apostrophe before <ma>, before, and before the suffix <na>) (q:draft)
zinling = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquake/quake) (d:<zin>, earthquake, and <ling>, shake; also written apart as a clause, {zin hong ling} is the earth quaked) (s:zinliing/ziinling/ziin) (q:draft)
zinlinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:<zinlin> earthquake, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:zinling) (b:zinlin) (q:draft)
zinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:journey/travel/travelling) (d:<zin>, travel, with the noun suffix <na>; {ka zinna khempeuhah} is everywhere I travelled) (s:khualzinna/lampaina) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zinpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guest/visitor) (d:<zin> guest, with <pa> for a man: the male guest) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zinsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:travel down/go down) (d:<zin> travel, with <suk> downward; {a zinsuk a zintohna} is their travelling to and fro) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zinte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guests/strangers/visitors) (d:plural of <zin>; people who come from elsewhere, guests in a house or foreigners in a place) (s:khualmite/leenglate/zinleleeng) (b:zin) (q:draft)
zintohna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:travelling up/going up) (d:<zin> travel, with <toh> upward and the noun suffix <na>; {a zinsuk a zintohna} is their travelling to and fro) (q:draft)
zintun = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lodge/stay as a guest/put up) (d:<zin>, guest, with <tun>, arrive: arrive and stay somewhere as a traveller; {zintun inn} is an inn and {zintun nading mun} a place to lodge) (s:giak/taam) (q:draft)
zintunna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lodging/place of stay) (d:the place where a traveller stays as a guest; before <inn>, <mun> or <pa> it means the house, the place or the host where one is staying) (s:peemna) (b:zintun) (q:draft)
zinzin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:travel about/journey) (d:<zin> travel, doubled for going on and on or from place to place; used with <khual>, away from home) (s:khualzinzin) (q:draft)
zinzinna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:travels/journeying) (d:<zinzin> travel about, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:khualzinna) (b:zinzin) (q:draft)
Zion = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Zion) (d:the hill of Jerusalem with the fortress David captured, the City of David; also a name for Jerusalem and its people) (r:19.78.68) (q:draft)
Zior = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Zior) (d:town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.54)
Ziph = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ziph) (d:town and desert in the hill country of Judah, written <Zif> in the Tedim Bible)
zipi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:<zi>, wife: the taking of a wife; {zipi hun} is the time of the wedding and {zipi pa} the bridegroom) (s:zipina/zineihna/mopina) (b:zi) (q:draft)
zipih = (i:1) (t:n) (w:co-wife/rival wife) (d:<zi> wife with <pih> fellow: another wife of the same husband) (b:zi) (q:draft)
zipil = (i:1) (t:n) (w:prudent wife/wise wife) (d:<zi> wife, with <pil> wise) (q:draft)
zipina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:<zipi> wedding, with the noun suffix <na>; {zipina pawi} is a wedding feast) (s:zipi/zineihna/mopina/kitenna) (b:zipi) (q:draft)
zipipa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:the man who is taking a wife; {-pa} marks a male) (s:zineipa/mopipa) (b:zipi) (r:42.5.34) (q:draft)
Zippor = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zippor) (d:father of Balak king of Moab) (r:4.22.10) (q:draft)
Zipporah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zipporah) (d:daughter of Jethro the priest of Midian and wife of Moses) (r:2.4.25)
Zipporah = (i:2) (t:name) (c:female) (w:Zipporah) (d:daughter of Jethro the priest of Midian and wife of Moses) (r:2.2.21)
zite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wives) (b:zi) (r:51.3.19) plural form of <zi>
Ziv = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Ziv) (d:second month of the Hebrew year, in which Solomon began to build the temple) (r:11.6.1/11.6.37)
Ziz = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ziz) (d:place named in {Ziz kahtohna lampi}, the way going up at Ziz, the Pass of Ziz in the NIV) (q:draft)
Ziza = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ziza) (d:name of two men, a leader of the tribe of Simeon and a son of King Rehoboam and Maakah) (r:13.4.37/14.11.20)
zo = (i:1) (t:n) (w:zomi) the people of {zomi}
zo = (i:2) (t:v) (w:win/defeat/overcome) (d:get the better of an enemy or opponent; {gal zo} is win a battle) (s:gualzo) (a:lel/guallel)
zo = (i:3) (t:v) (w:gain) (d:after <ngah>, get: succeed in getting, gain)
Zoan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zoan) (d:ancient city in the Nile delta of Egypt, also called Tanis) (r:26.30.14/19.78.12)
Zoans = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zoan) (d:spelling of Zoan, the city in the Nile delta of Egypt, found in Isaiah 30:4) (r:23.30.4)
Zoar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Zoar) (d:small town near the Dead Sea, earlier called Bela, to which Lot fled from Sodom) (r:1.19.23)
Zobah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Zobah) (d:Aramean kingdom north of Damascus, ruled by Hadadezer and defeated by David) (r:13.18.9/10.23.36)
Zobebah = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Hazzobebah) (d:descendant of Judah, child of Koz) (r:13.4.8)
Zobehah = (i:1) (t:name) (w:Hazzobebah) (d:descendant of Judah, child of Koz; another spelling of the same name in 1 Chronicles 4:8) (r:13.4.8)
Zofah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zophah) (d:son of Helem, a chief of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.35/13.7.36)
Zofai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zophai) (d:Levite of the family of Kohath, son of Elkanah and ancestor of the prophet Samuel) (r:13.6.26)
Zofar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zophar) (d:Zophar the Naamathite, one of the three friends of Job) (r:18.2.11/18.11.1)
Zofim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zophim) (d:field on the top of Mount Pisgah in Moab, where Balak took Balaam to curse Israel) (r:4.23.14)
zogawp = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush/overpower/subdue) (d:<zo>, overcome, with <gawp>, thoroughly or violently: crush an enemy or bring a people completely under control) (s:sugawp) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zogawpin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overpowering/crushing/defeating completely) (d:<zogawp>, defeat utterly, with the linking suffix {-in}, followed by another verb: crush and then drive out, kill or destroy) (b:zogawp) (q:draft)
zogawpsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let conquer/cause to be conquered) (d:<zogawp>, crush or overpower, with the causative <sak>: let one people conquer another) (b:zogawp) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zohar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zohar) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Ephron the Hittite and a son of Simeon) (r:1.23.8/1.46.10)
Zoheth = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zoheth) (d:son of Ishi, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.20)
zoin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overcome/defeat/conquer/triumph over) (d:<zo> with the linking suffix {-in}, overcoming and then doing the next action; after another verb, being able to do it) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zokhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have overcome/have won/have finished) (d:<zo>, win, overcome or finish, with <khin>, already, showing a completed action) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zokik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:conquer again/overrun again) (d:<zo>, overcome, with <kik>, again: conquer a place once more) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zol = (i:1) (t:v) (w:persuade/entice/coax) (d:win someone over by words, whether to believe or do something good or to do wrong; the same word covers persuade, coax and entice) (s:umsak) (a:tawng) (q:draft)
zolbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (w:plead with/persuade) (d:<zol>, persuade, with <bawl>, do: work at persuading someone, plead with a person to change) (b:zol) (q:draft)
zolin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:persuading/enticing/seducing) (d:<zol>, persuade or entice, with the linking suffix {-in}, followed by another verb) (b:zol) (q:draft)
zolkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw away/entice away) (d:<zol>, persuade, with <khia>, out or away: draw people away from where they belong) (b:zol) (q:draft)
zolkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:draw away/entice away) (d:form of <zolkhia> used before a noun such as <hun>, time) (b:zolkhia) (q:draft)
zolkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:win back/allure) (d:<zol>, persuade or coax, with <kik>, back or again: win someone back with kind words) (b:zol) (q:draft)
zolna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:enticement/persuasion/temptation) (d:<zol>, persuade or entice, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of persuading, or an enticement to do wrong) (s:zolzolna) (b:zol) (r:48.5.8) (q:draft)
zolo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cannot/be unable to) (d:<zo>, be able, with the negative <lo>, written as one word after a verb: not able to do it) (a:hizo) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zolopa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who cannot/man who is unable) (d:<zolo>, be unable, with <pa> for a man: {a ki-uk zolopa} is the man who cannot control himself) (b:zolo) (q:draft)
zolsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make shine) (d:make something shine or glisten, with the causative <sak>; said of oil that makes the face shine) (q:draft)
zolsimna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:persuasion/enticement) (d:apparently <zol> persuade, with <sim> and the noun suffix <na>: the urging of others, which a person heeds) (s:zolna) (q:draft, low confidence)
zolua = (i:1) (t:v) (w:defeat utterly) (d:<zo> overcome, with <lua> very, exceedingly) (b:zo) (q:draft, low confidence)
zolzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:persuade/win over) (d:<zol>, persuade, with <zawh>, be able or succeed: succeed in persuading, win someone over) (s:umsak) (q:draft)
zolzolna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:persuasion/coaxing) (d:<zol>, persuade, said twice for continued action, with the noun suffix <na>: patient and repeated persuading) (s:zolna) (q:draft)
zom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:continue/go on/carry on) (d:carry on with what was being done, such as a journey or a speech; often as {zom lai}, still continue) (s:zomlai/zomsuak) (a:tawp) (q:draft)
zom = (i:2) (t:v) (w:join/attach/fasten) (d:join one thing to another, fasten the end of one thing onto another) (a:khen) (q:draft)
zom = (i:3) (t:n) (w:next/second) (d:the one that comes next in place, order or rank; {ama zom-ah} means next to him or after him) (r:9.23.17) (q:draft)
zomah = (i:1) (t:prep) (w:next to/after) (d:<zom>, next, with the place marker <ah>: next to or after a person or thing in a row or a list, with <a>, <ama> or <amaute> before it) (b:zom) (q:draft)
zomang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:crush completely/wipe out) (d:<zo>, overcome, with <mang>, gone: overcome so that nothing is left) (s:susiamang) (q:draft)
zomin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:joining on/continuing/adding to) (d:<zom>, join or continue, with the linking suffix {-in}: joining on to something already there, as in building upon a foundation, sharing in one loaf or keeping on in good conduct) (b:zom) (r:49.2.20) (q:draft)
zomkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:share together/join together in) (d:<zom>, join, with <khawm>, together: have a share in something together with others) (b:zom) (q:draft)
zomlai = (i:1) (t:v) (w:continue/go on/keep on) (d:carry on with what was being done or said; {a thugen zomlai}, he continued speaking) (s:zom/zomsuak) (a:tawp) (q:draft)
zomna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:continuing/continuation) (d:<zom> continue, with the noun suffix <na>; {nasep zomna} is going on with the work) (b:zom) (q:draft)
zompa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:the next man/one next to) (d:<zom> next, with <pa> marking a male: the man who comes next after someone) (b:zom) (q:draft)
zomsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let continue/make continue) (d:<zom>, continue, with the causative <sak>: let something go on) (s:zomzomsak) (b:zom) (q:draft)
zomsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:continue/keep on/carry through) (d:<zom>, continue, with <suak>, through: go on with something without stopping, carry it through to the end) (s:zom/zomlai) (a:tawp) (q:draft)
zomto = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry on/continue/keep up) (d:<zom>, continue, with <to>, onward: carry on what others began; {innkuan zomto} is carry on a family line) (s:zom) (b:zom) (q:draft)
zomzom = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go on and on/continue) (d:<zom>, continue, doubled for an action that keeps going on and on) (s:zomlai) (q:draft)
zomzomsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let go on/let continue) (d:<zomzom>, go on and on, with the causative <sak>: let something keep going) (s:zomsak) (b:zomzom) (q:draft)
zon = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek/search/look for) (d:form of <zong> used before a suffix or another word, usually written with a final apostrophe) (s:kan) (q:draft)
zong = (i:2) (t:adv) (w:in addition) (d:adds a further person or thing to those already mentioned)
zong = (i:3) (t:adv) (w:too) (d:shows that what was said of one person or thing is true of another)
zong = (i:4) (t:adv) (w:as well) (d:placed after the subject: this one does the same as another)
zong = (i:5) (t:v) (w:look/seek/look for/search for) (d:try to find someone or something; {Topa zong} is seek the Lord, and {thah dingin zong} is seek to kill) (s:kan) looking for something such as a job or an object
zonga = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek/look for) (d:<zong> seek, with the linking <a>: {i zonga}, we sought and; not the adverb <zong>, also) (q:draft)
zongkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:search out/track down/find) (d:<zong>, seek, with <khia>, out: search until the person or thing is found) (s:kankhia) (b:zong) (q:draft)
zongkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek again/look for again) (d:<zong> seek, with <kik> again) (s:kankik) (b:zong) (q:draft)
zongpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seeker/one who seeks/searcher) (d:<zong> seek with <pa>, the one who does it: he who seeks or searches) (b:zong) (q:draft)
zongpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek at once/begin to look for) (d:<zong> seek, with <pah> at once, straight away) (q:draft)
zongpahin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek at once/look for straight away) (d:<zongpah> seek at once, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:zongpah) (q:draft)
zongpak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:hurry to seek/seek quickly) (d:<zong> seek, with <pak> quickly) (q:draft)
zongsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:order a search/have someone search for/cause to seek) (d:<zong> seek with <sak> cause: have someone look for a person or thing; {mawhna zongsak}, have charges brought) (b:zong) (q:draft)
zongsang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be accustomed/be used to/make a habit of) (d:be practised in something or given to it through constant doing) (q:draft)
zongsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:habit/addiction/depravity) (d:something a person has grown used to and is mastered by; here of evil habits that bring ruin) (q:draft, low confidence)
zongtawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:forage/search for) (d:<zong> seek, with <tawm> by oneself: look for what one needs wherever it can be found) (q:draft, low confidence)
zongte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who seek/seekers) (d:<zong> seek with plural <te>; the people who look for or try to get someone or something) (q:draft)
zongun = (i:1) (t:conj) (w:even though/although/even if) (d:<zong> even, also, with <un> for a plural subject, closing a clause) (s:napi) (b:zong) (q:draft)
zongzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek rather/seek instead/seek all the more) (d:<zong>, seek, with <zaw>, rather or more) (b:zong) (q:draft)
zongzong = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep seeking/look for/search for) (d:<zong> seek said twice, for seeking that goes on or is done persistently) (s:kan) (q:draft)
zonkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:search out for/find for) (d:<zon> seek, with <khiat> out and <sak> for another: search out something for someone) (s:zonsak) (q:draft)
zonkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek again/return to seek) (d:<zon> seek, with <kik> again, back) (s:kankik) (b:zon) (q:draft)
zonna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seeking/search) (d:the act of seeking or looking for something; with <ding>, a means or purpose of seeking) (b:zon) (q:draft)
zonpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:help look for/seek together with) (d:<zon> seek, with <pih> together with) (b:zon) (q:draft)
zonsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek for/find for/provide) (d:<zon> seek with <sak>, here doing it for someone else: look for and get something on behalf of another) (s:zonkhiatsak) (b:zon) (q:draft)
zontheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to seek/can seek) (d:<zon>, seek, with <theih>, can, the form used before <nading>: so that one can seek or find) (b:zon) (q:draft)
zonzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:seek more/search for rather) (d:<zon> seek, with <zaw> more: seek one thing more than another) (b:zon) (q:draft)
zonzon = (i:1) (t:v) (w:keep searching/search and search/look for) (d:<zon>, form of <zong> seek, doubled to show continued or repeated searching) (s:kan) (r:19.37.36) (q:draft)
zop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:carry on/continue) (d:form of <zom> join or continue used before <ding>, <zawh> and <nading>; to carry on a name or go on with a work; {zop zawh} is be able to carry through, to finish) (q:draft)
zop = (i:2) (t:v) (w:share in/join in) (d:to be joined to something and so have a part in it) (q:draft, low confidence)
zopa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who is able/he who can) (d:<zo> be able with <pa>, the one who: follows a verb, as {honkhia zopa}, the one who is able to save) (s:theipa) (q:draft)
zopa = (i:2) (t:n) (w:conqueror/victor/one who subdues) (d:<zo> win or defeat with <pa>: the one who defeated or subdues) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zopna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sharing/partnership/fellowship) (d:<zop> join or share in, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:kizopna) (b:zop) (q:draft, low confidence)
zoppihte = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<zop> join, with <pih> together with and the plural <te>: those joined with one; {laigui zoppihte}, those of the same umbilical cord, are brothers born of the same mother) (q:draft, low confidence)
zoptheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to continue) (d:<zop> continue, with <theih> be able; used before <nading>) (b:zop) (q:draft)
Zorah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Zorah) (d:town in the lowland of Judah allotted to the tribe of Dan, the home of Manoah, father of Samson) (r:6.19.41/16.11.29)
zosak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:bring to completion/make complete) (d:<zo>, finish, with the causative <sak>: bring a work to its completion) (s:kicingsak) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zosak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:give victory over/make win) (d:<zo>, win, with the causative <sak>: make someone win, give victory over enemies) (s:gualzosak) (a:guallelhsak) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zosakhi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:antelope/ibex) (d:a clean wild animal of the deer or goat kind, named in a list beside <sakhi> deer; which animal is meant is not certain) (q:draft, low confidence)
zosiang = (i:1) (t:v) (w:finish/complete) (d:<zo> finish, with <siang> clean: bring a matter fully to an end) (s:mansiang/zawhkhit/mankhit) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zota = (i:1) (t:v) (d:<zo> be able, finish, with <ta> marking a change now complete, placed after another verb: has now come to pass, have now managed to) (b:zo) (q:draft, low confidence)
zote = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who are able/those who manage) (d:<zo> be able or succeed with plural {-te}, after a verb: those who manage to do it, as {a thuak zote}, those who endure) (b:zo) (r:40.10.22) (q:draft)
zothawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overpower/get the better of) (d:<zo> overcome, with <thawh> and the linking suffix <in>) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zozabad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jozabad) (d:a head of the Levites in Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah, in charge of the outside work of the house of God) (r:16.11.16)
zozaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:prevail/overcome/triumph) (d:<zo> win with <zaw> more: be the stronger, get the upper hand) (s:gualzo/zozo) (a:lel/guallel) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zozaw = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be more able/can all the more) (d:after a verb, <zo> be able with <zaw> more: be able to do it even more, how much more) (s:theizaw) (q:draft, low confidence)
zozo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overcome/prevail/tame) (d:reduplicated <zo>, win or be able; with a negative, cannot manage at all) (s:gualzo) (a:lel/guallel) (b:zo) (q:draft)
zu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wine/strong drink/beer) (d:fermented drink that can make a person drunk; {zu kham} is be drunk, and {kham theih zu} is strong drink) (s:khamtheihzu) (q:draft)
zu = (i:2) (t:v) (w:rain/fall) (d:of rain, fall; {guah zu}, it rains) (s:guahzu) (q:draft)
zuahzuah = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:freely/generously/lavishly) (d:placed after a verb of giving or distributing: give out widely without holding back) (s:ziahziah) (a:tawmkha) (q:draft)
zuahzuahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:freewill offerings/things freely given) (d:<zuahzuah> freely, with the plural <te>, after a verb of giving: the things given freely) (b:zuahzuah) (q:draft)
zuakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sell) (d:<zuak>, sell, with the linking ending <in>: sell something and then do the next action) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zuakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sell off/export) (d:<zuak>, sell, with <khia>, out: sell something off, or sell goods on to other countries) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zuakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sell off/sell/export) (d:<zuak>, sell, with <khiat>, out or away; the form of <zuakkhia> used before <ding> and similar words) (b:zuakkhia) (q:draft)
zuakkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have sold/finish selling) (d:<zuak> sell, with <khit> finished; {zuakkhit ciangin} is after selling) (q:draft)
zuakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sell back) (d:<zuak>, sell, with <kik>, back: sell someone back to her family, so that she is bought back) (a:leikik) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zuakma = (t:see) <zuakma-in>
zuakma-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:before selling) (d:<zuak> sell, with <ma> before and <in>: before it was sold) (q:draft)
zuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sale/selling) (d:the act of selling; {a zuakna mipa} is the man it was sold to, {zuakna mun} the place sold to) (s:sumzuakna) (a:leina) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:seller/merchant/trader) (d:<zuak>, sell, with <pa>, the man who sells; {sum zuakpa} is a merchant) (s:vanzuakpa/sumbawlpa) (a:leipa) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zuakpahte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who sell readily) (d:<zuak> sell, with <pah> at once and the plural <te>: those who sell without holding back) (q:draft)
zuaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:sold) (d:<zuak>, sell, with <sa>, already done; that which has been sold) (s:kizuaksa) (a:leisa) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zuaksawn = (i:1) (t:v) (w:sell on/resell) (d:<zuak>, sell, with <sawn>, pass on: sell on to another what one has bought) (q:draft)
zuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sellers/those who sell) (d:<zuak> sell with the plural <te>: the people who sell something) (s:sumzuakte) (a:leite) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zuaktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to sell) (d:<zuak> sell, with <theih> can; used before <nading>) (b:zuak) (q:draft)
zual = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:tame/tamed) (d:of an animal, used to people, broken in; {zual nai lo} is not yet tamed, wild) (a:gamsung/lee) (q:draft)
zualsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tame/subdue) (d:<zual>, tame, with the causative <sak>: make a wild animal tame) (b:zual) (q:draft)
zualsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:tame) (d:<zualsak>, tame, with the linking ending <in>: tame something and then do the next action) (b:zualsak) (q:draft)
zuan = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go to/head for/make for/turn to) (d:move toward a place or person; with <kiang>, go or come to a person, as in {Pasian kiang zuan}, draw near to God) (s:manawh) (r:22.2.8) (q:draft)
zuanin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:heading for/making for/going to) (d:<zuan>, head for, with the linking ending <in>: making for a place while another action follows) (b:zuan) (q:draft)
zuankik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:return to/go back to/turn back toward) (d:<zuan>, head for, with <kik>, back or again: go back to the place or person one came from) (s:ciahkik/paikik) (b:zuan) (q:draft)
zuanpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:head for at once/go straight to) (d:<zuan> go to, with <pah> at once) (q:draft)
zuansak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let go to/cause to go to/send to) (d:<zuan>, head for, with the causative <sak>: make or let someone go to a place or person) (b:zuan) (q:draft)
zuansuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go down to/head down to) (d:<zuan> go to, with <suk> downward) (s:paisuk) (b:zuan) (q:draft)
zuante = (i:1) (t:n) (w:those who come to/those who go to) (d:<zuan> go to, with the plural <te>) (b:zuan) (q:draft)
Zuar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zuar) (d:father of Nethanel, the leader of the tribe of Issachar in the wilderness) (r:4.7.18/4.10.15)
zuat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go to/head for/return to) (d:make one's way toward a place or person; the form used in dependent clauses and before <nading>) (s:manawh) (r:20.26.11) (q:draft)
zuatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:return to/go back to) (d:<zuat>, head for, with <kik>, back or again) (b:zuat) (q:draft)
zuatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:way to/going to) (d:the act of heading for a place; with <lampi> or <lam>, the road that leads to a place) (b:zuat) (q:draft)
zuau = (i:1) (t:v) (w:evil/lie/deceive/tell lies) (d:say what is not true; often with <gen>, speak, as {zuau gen}, tell a lie, and before a noun, as {zuau teci}, a false witness) (s:zuaugen/khem)
zuau-tatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be unfaithful/act falsely) (d:<zuau> lie, with <tat> act and the linking suffix <in>; the same word as <zuautat>) (q:draft)
zuaugen = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lie/tell lies/deceive) (d:<zuau>, false, with <gen>, speak: say what is not true; {zuaugen mi} is a liar) (s:zuau) (r:62.2.4) (q:draft)
zuaugen = (i:2) (t:n) (w:liar) (d:one who tells lies; also said as {zuaugen mi} and {zuaugen pa}) (s:Mizuau/thuzuaupa) (r:62.5.10) (q:draft)
zuaugenin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:lie/tell lies) (d:<zuaugen> tell lies, with the linking suffix <in>) (b:zuaugen) (q:draft)
zuaugenna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lying/lie/falsehood) (d:<zuaugen>, tell lies, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:zuauna/zuauthu/thuzuau) (b:zuaugen) (q:draft)
zuaugente = (i:1) (t:n) (w:liars) (d:<zuaugen> liar, with the plural <te>) (s:mizuaute/zuautheite) (b:zuaugen) (q:draft)
zuauna = (i:1) (t:v) (w:evil/lie/deceive) (b:zuau)
zuauna = (i:2) (t:n) (w:falsehood/lie/deceit) (d:<zuau>, lie, with the noun suffix <na>: what is false, lying or deceit) (s:zuauthu/thuzuau/zuaupi) (a:thutak/thumanna) (b:zuau)
zuaunate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:falsehoods) (d:<zuauna>, falsehood, with the plural <te>) (s:zuauthute) (b:zuauna)
Zuaunate = (i:1) (t:n) (w:falsehoods/lies) (d:<zuaunate> written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (s:zuauthute) (b:zuaunate) (q:draft)
zuauphuah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:intrigue/deceit/fabrication) (d:<zuau> lie with <phuah> make up: the making up of lies) (s:zuausiamna/khemsiamna) (q:draft)
zuaupi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood/great lie) (d:<zuau>, lie, with <pi>, great: something wholly false or empty) (s:zuauthu/thuzuau) (b:zuau) (q:draft)
zuaupiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lies/all the lies) (d:<zuaupi> lie, with <teng> all) (b:zuaupi) (q:draft)
zuausiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:intrigue/deceit/cunning) (d:<zuau> lie, with <siam> skilled and the noun suffix <na>: skill in lying) (s:zuauphuah/khemsiamna) (q:draft)
zuautat = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be unfaithful/act treacherously/deal falsely) (d:<zuau>, lie, with <tat>, act: break faith with God or with people, act disloyally) (q:draft)
zuautatin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being unfaithful/acting falsely) (d:<zuautat> be unfaithful, with <in> linking it to the next verb) (b:zuautat) (q:draft)
zuautatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:unfaithfulness/treachery/falsehood/deceit) (d:<zuautat>, be unfaithful, with the noun suffix <na>: acting falsely or disloyally) (s:cihtaklohna) (a:cihtakna) (b:zuautat) (q:draft)
zuautatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:cause to be unfaithful/lead astray) (d:<zuautat> be unfaithful, with causative <sak>) (b:zuautat) (q:draft)
zuaute = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:false/lying) (d:<zuau>, false, with the plural <te>, placed after a noun: {pasian zuaute} is false gods, {kamsang zuaute} is false prophets) (s:manlo) (b:zuau) (q:draft)
zuauthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:deceitful/deceiving/lying) (d:<zuau>, lie, with <thei>, able or given to; one that deceives) (a:citak) (b:zuau) (q:draft)
zuautheite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:liars/false ones) (d:<zuauthei>, liar, with plural <te>; after a noun it means false: {kamsang zuautheite} is false prophets) (s:zuaugente/mizuaute) (b:zuauthei) (q:draft)
zuauthu = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood/false word) (d:<zuau>, false, with <thu>, word: a lie, something said that is not true; {zuauthu gen} is tell lies) (s:thuzuau/zuauna/zuaupi) (a:thutak) (r:20.6.17) (q:draft)
zuauthute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:lies/false words/deceptive words) (d:<zuauthu>, lie, with the plural <te>) (s:zuaunate/Thuzuaute) (b:zuauthu) (q:draft)
zuazua = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:roaring/with a roar) (d:expressive word placed after a verb for a loud, continuous rushing or roaring, said of water, waves, flames and the noise of a crowd; {ging zuazua} is roar) (q:draft)
zuazuate = (i:1) (t:n) (d:<zuazua>, expressive word for a loud rushing sound or a continuous stream, with plural <te> making a noun of the phrase before it: {ging zuazuate}, things that rattle loudly; {a piak khiat zuazuate}, the things given freely one after another) (b:zuazua) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zubeel = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wine jar/wineskin) (d:<zu>, wine or beer, with <beel>, pot: a vessel for wine; written here with a capital at the start of a sentence) (q:draft)
Zuf = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zuph) (d:ancestor of Elkanah and Samuel, from the hill country of Ephraim; also the district of Zuph through which Saul passed) (r:9.1.1/13.6.35)
zuhai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drunkard) (d:<zu>, liquor: one given to heavy drinking; paired with <anhai>, glutton) (s:zukhampa/khampa) (r:42.7.34) (q:draft)
zui = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow/obey/keep) (d:go after or behind someone, as in {a nung zui}, follow him; also keep or obey a word, law or teaching) (s:nungzuih/mang) (a:palsat) (q:draft)
zuibup = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow completely/follow wholly) (d:<zui> follow, with <bup> whole) (q:draft)
zuih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow/obey/keep/observe) (d:form of <zui> used before <ding>, <nading>, <man> and in dependent clauses) (s:nungzuih) (a:palsat) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuihbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow/ensue/result) (d:<zuih>, follow, with <beh>, in addition: come after as a further consequence) (q:draft)
zuihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow/observe) (d:<zuih> follow or observe, with the linking suffix <in>: {zuihin nei}, hold to as a rule) (b:zuih) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall into following/come to follow) (d:<zuih> follow, with <khak> happen to: take up the ways of others) (q:draft)
zuihlah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be unable to follow/fail to keep) (d:<zuih> follow or keep, with <lah> fail, not manage) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihlahna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:failure to keep) (d:<zuihlah> fail to keep, with the noun suffix <na>: {Thukham zuihlahna}, not keeping the Law) (b:zuihlah) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (w:following) (d:<zuih> follow, with <lam>, the fact or manner of: {a zuihlam a muh ciangin}, when he saw them following) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:following/obeying/observance) (d:the act of following or obeying; {tuu zuihna} is tending sheep) (a:palsatna) (b:zuih) (q:draft)
zuihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to follow/want to obey) (d:<zuih>, the form of <zui>, follow or obey, with <nop>, want to) (q:draft)
zuihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow at once/go with readily) (d:<zuih> follow, with <pah> at once; used before <nading>) (q:draft)
zuihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow along with/go along with) (d:<zuih>, follow, with <pih>, together with: follow a practice along with others, or go with someone along a path) (s:zuikhawm) (b:zuih) (q:draft)
zuihpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go along with/lead along) (d:<zuihpih> follow along with, with the linking suffix <in>: go with someone along a path) (b:zuihpih) (q:draft)
zuihsa = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have followed/have kept) (d:<zuih>, follow or keep, with <sa>, already done: what one has already followed or kept) (s:zuikhin) (b:zuih) (q:draft)
zuihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let go with/send along) (d:<zuih> follow, with causative <sak>: let someone accompany) (s:paikhawmsak) (b:zuih) (q:draft)
zuihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to obey) (d:<zuih> follow or obey with <theih> can; the form used before <nading>, so that one may follow or obey) (s:zuihzawh) (b:zuih) (q:draft)
zuihzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to keep) (d:<zuih> follow, obey, with <zawh> be able; used before <ding> and <nading>) (s:zuihtheih) (q:draft)
zuihzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:keeping/observance) (d:<zuihzawh> be able to keep, with the noun suffix <na>; {Thukham zuihzawhna} is keeping the Law) (b:zuihzawh) (q:draft)
zuikha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow/be led to follow) (d:<zui> follow with <kha> happen to: follow by mistake or be drawn into following, often in warnings) (q:draft)
zuikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow together/go along with) (d:<zui> follow, with <khawm> together) (s:zuihpih) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:have kept/have fulfilled/keep fully) (d:<zui>, follow or keep, with <khin>, completely or already) (s:zuihsa) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuikik = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go back with/follow back) (d:<zui>, follow, with <kik>, back or again: go back with someone; in Daniel 11:20 follow after in turn, succeed) (s:lehzuihkik) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuinuam = (i:1) (t:v) (w:want to follow/be willing to keep) (d:<zui> follow or keep, with <nuam> want to) (q:draft)
zuipah = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow at once/follow immediately) (d:<zui> follow with <pah>, at once, without delay) (q:draft)
zuisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:let follow/make follow/send along with) (d:<zui>, follow, with the causative <sak>: let or make someone follow or go along; also make someone keep a covenant) (s:tonsak) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuisakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:one who makes follow/one who subjects) (d:<zuisak> make follow with <pa> marking a male person: the one who made the creation subject, whose will it follows) (b:zuisak) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuisuak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:go on with/keep following/continue in) (d:<zui>, follow, with <suak>, through or onward: go along with someone all the way, keep on following) (q:draft)
zuisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow down/go down along/descend with) (d:<zui>, follow, with <suk> for movement downward) (a:zuito) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuite = (i:1) (t:n) (w:followers/those who follow/those who keep/those who obey) (d:<zui>, follow or keep, with the plural <te>, used after <a>: the people who follow someone or keep a law) (s:nungzuite) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuito = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow upward/climb after) (d:<zui>, follow, with <to>, upward: follow someone up, or go up along a path or border) (a:zuisuk) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (w:follow rather/follow instead) (d:<zui> follow with <zaw> rather, more: follow one way in preference to another) (b:zui) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuizo = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to keep/manage to obey) (d:<zui> follow or obey with <zo> be able) (s:mangzo) (b:zui) (q:draft)
zuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall/rain) (d:of rain; the form of <zu> used before <loh>, <nading>, <mateng> and similar words) (b:zu) (r:59.5.7) (q:draft)
zukham = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:drunk/drunken/intoxicated) (d:overcome by <zu>, alcoholic drink; also used for a drunk person, a drunkard) (s:kham) (q:draft)
zukhamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:drunk/in a drunken state) (d:<zukham>, drunk, with the linking ending <in>) (b:zukham) (q:draft)
zukhamna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drunkenness/intoxication) (d:the state of being drunk; {zukhamna pan a pilvan} is to wake from a drunken sleep) (s:khamna) (b:zukham) (q:draft)
zukhampa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drunkard/drunken man) (d:<zukham> drunk with <pa> marking a male person) (s:zuhai/khampa) (b:zukham) (q:draft)
zukhamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make drunk/intoxicate) (d:<zukham> drunk with <sak>, cause to be) (s:khamsak) (b:zukham) (q:draft)
zukhamte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drunkards) (d:<zukham>, drunk, with the plural <te>: people who get drunk) (s:guite) (b:zukham) (q:draft)
zukna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:raining/falling of rain) (d:<zuk> fall, of rain, with the noun suffix <na>; {guah zukna ding mun} is the place where rain is to fall) (s:guahzukna) (b:zuk) (q:draft)
zuksak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:make rain/send rain/bring rain) (d:<zuk>, fall as rain, with the causative <sak>: make rain fall, used with <guah>, rain) (s:guahzusak) (b:zuk) (q:draft)
zuksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:sending of rain/making rain fall) (d:<zuksak>, make rain fall, with the noun suffix <na>: the sending of rain; {guah zuksakna ding} is in order to send rain) (b:zuksak) (q:draft)
zul = (t:todo) (r:26.15.4) (q:draft, one verse only, in {a zul kat teng} for the charred middle part of a stick whose ends are burnt; the meaning of {zul} alone is not clear)
zulesa = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drink and meat) (d:apparently <zu>, drink, <le>, and, <sa>, meat: strong drink and meat as at a feast; {zulesa tawh kidiah}, soaked with drink and meat, describes people who are drunk) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulhtat = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:unruly/undisciplined/disorderly) (d:lacking restraint or discipline; {khuaval zulhtat lo} is sober and self-controlled, and {thadah zulhtat mite} are people who are idle and disorderly) (q:draft)
zulhtatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:in a disorderly way/idly) (d:<zulhtat>, unruly, with the adverb ending <in>; {thadah zulhtatin gamta} is behave in an idle and disorderly way) (b:zulhtat) (q:draft)
zulhtatna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:unruliness/wantonness/lack of restraint) (d:<zulhtat> unruly with the noun suffix <na>; in the verse the unrestrained conduct of youth that brings shame) (b:zulhtat) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulhzau = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:faithless/backsliding/unfaithful) (d:turning away from the one to whom loyalty is owed and not keeping faith; in Jeremiah said of Israel and of other peoples addressed as an unfaithful daughter) (a:cihtak/citak) (q:draft)
zulhzauna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:backsliding/faithlessness) (d:<zulhzau>, faithless, with the noun suffix <na>: turning away from God, backsliding) (s:cihtaklohna) (a:cihtakna) (b:zulhzau) (q:draft)
zulim = (i:1) (t:n) (w:good wine/choice wine) (d:<zu> wine with <lim> tasty, parallel to <anlim> choice food; the verse has new wine) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulkatteng = (i:1) (t:n) (w:charred part/burnt remainder) (d:apparently <zul> with <kat> burn and <teng> all, the whole: the remaining middle of a stick that the fire has charred; written as three words {a zul kat teng} in the other text) (q:draft, low confidence)
zum = (i:1) (t:v) (w:be ashamed/feel shame/be put to shame) (d:feel shame; often with <mai>, face: {mai zum} is be ashamed or be put to shame, and {zum kei} is not be ashamed) (s:zahla/kisuang/zahhuai) (r:60.4.16) (q:draft)
zum = (i:2) (t:n) (w:court/office/law court) (d:government office or court of law, as in {zum inn}, court house, {thukhen zum}, law court, and {zum nasemte}, officials) (r:18.9.32) (q:draft)
zum = (i:3) (t:adj) (w:pointed/sharp) (d:tapering to a point: {mualdawn zum} is a mountain peak, {ciangkhut zum} a pointed goad) (q:draft)
zuma = (i:1) (t:n) (w:of the court/at the court) (d:<zum> court or office with the marker <a>, of or at: {zuma thukhente} are the judges of the court) (b:zum) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumah = (i:1) (t:n) (w:in court/at the court) (d:<zum>, court or office, with the place marker <ah>; {thukhen zumah} is in the law court) (b:zum) (r:30.5.10) (q:draft)
zumcingte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:guards/court guards) (d:apparently <zum> court or office with <cing> guard and the plural <te>: those who guard the court; {zumcingte omna} is the court of the guard) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:shameful/disgraceful) (d:causing shame, disgraceful; {zumhuai-in gamta} is act shamefully) (s:mindaihuai/maizumhuai) (a:zahtakhuai) (q:draft)
zumhuaina = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace/nakedness) (d:<zumhuai>, shameful, with the noun suffix <na>: a shameful thing, a disgrace; also the shame of being seen naked) (s:maizumna/mindaina/zumna/minsiatna) (a:pahtawina/minthanna) (b:zumhuai) (r:34.3.5) (q:draft)
zumhuaipi = (t:see) <zumhuaipi-in>
zumhuaipi-in = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:shamefully/disgracefully) (d:<zumhuaipi>, very shameful, with the adverb ending {-in}: in a shameful way) (q:draft)
zumhuaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:disgrace/put to shame) (d:<zumhuai>, shameful, with the causative suffix <sak>: make shameful, bring disgrace on) (s:maizumsak/mindaisak/zumsak/minsiasak) (a:pahtawi/minthangsak) (b:zumhuai) (q:draft)
zumin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:being ashamed/in shame) (d:<zum>, be ashamed, with the linking ending <in>; {mai zumin} is with shame of face, put to shame) (b:zum) (q:draft)
zumkhak = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holiday) (d:apparently <zum> office with <khak> shut, a day on which business is closed; in the verse {zumkhak hun} stands for the New Moon festival when grain could not be sold) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:holiday/day off) (d:<zumkhak> holiday with the noun suffix <na>: the keeping of a holiday, with work stopped) (b:zumkhak) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumlai = (i:1) (t:n) (w:office records/register) (d:apparently <zum> office with <lai> writing: {galkap zumlai a kem} is the one who keeps the army records, the officer who enrols the people) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace) (d:<zum>, be ashamed, with the noun suffix <na>: shame or disgrace; {zumna thuak} is be put to shame) (s:maizumna/mindaina/zumhuaina/minsiatna) (a:pahtawina/minthanna) (b:zum) (q:draft)
Zumna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:shame) (d:<zumna>, shame, written with a capital at the start of a line or sentence; {zumna mel thei lo} is shameless) (b:zumna) (q:draft)
zumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:shame/put to shame/humiliate) (d:<zum>, be ashamed, with the causative <sak>: make someone ashamed) (s:maizumsak/mindaisak/zumhuaisak/minsiasak) (a:pahtawi/minthangsak) (b:zum) (q:draft)
zun = (i:1) (t:n) (w:urine) (d:the liquid waste of the body; in the verses paired with <ek>, excrement) (q:draft)
zun = (i:2) (t:v) (w:be ripe/be fully ripe) (d:of fruit on the tree or vine, often after <min> ripe: {a min a zun}, {min zun mahmah}, very ripe; used where the English has first ripe or early fruit; exact sense not certain) (s:minta) (q:draft, low confidence)
zune = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink/feast/carouse) (d:drink liquor, from <zu>, fermented drink, and <ne>, consume; mostly in the pair {anne zune}, eat and drink) (r:21.10.16/40.24.38) (q:draft)
zunek = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drink liquor/drink wine) (d:form of <zune>, drink liquor, used before another word: {zunek a hatte} is those strong at drinking, {zunek ding} is what is to be drunk) (b:zune) (q:draft)
zunekna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:drinking/wine drinking/drunkenness) (d:<zunek>, drink liquor, with the noun suffix <na>: the drinking of wine or other alcoholic drink, also heavy drinking) (b:zunek) (q:draft)
zung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:root) (d:the part of a plant or tree that grows in the ground; {zung kha} means take root) (s:singzung/zungpi) (r:23.11.10) (q:draft)
Zung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:root) (d:<zung>, root, written with a capital in the title {David’ Zung}, the Root of David, and at the start of a quotation) (b:zung) (q:draft)
zungbawh = (i:1) (t:v) (w:uproot/pull up by the roots) (d:<zung>, root, with <bawh>, pull up: tear a plant out with its roots) (s:zunglot/botkhia/bawhkhiat) (a:suan) (q:draft)
zungbawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:uprooting/pulling up by the roots) (d:<zungbawh>, uproot, with the linking ending <in>: uprooting and then) (b:zungbawh) (q:draft)
zungbuh = (i:1) (t:n) (w:ring/signet ring) (d:a ring worn on the finger; {min gelhna zungbuh} or {min thuhna zungbuh} is a signet ring used for sealing) (s:khutbuh) (r:17.8.2) (q:draft)
zungbuhin = (i:1) (t:n) (w:as a ring/as a signet ring) (d:<zungbuh> ring with the marker <in>, here as or like: make someone as a signet ring) (b:zungbuh) (q:draft)
zungbuhte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:rings) (d:plural of <zungbuh> finger ring; {min gelhna zungbuhte} are signet rings) (b:zungbuh) (q:draft)
zungkha = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take root/be rooted) (d:<zung>, root, with <kha>: strike root, become firmly fixed; also written apart as {zung kha}) (s:zungthuk) (q:draft)
zungkha = (i:2) (t:n) (w:bitter root) (d:apparently <zung>, root, with <kha>, bitter: in Hebrews 12.15 {zungkha a nei singkung} is a plant with a bitter root that grows up and harms many, where the other text has {a kha kung a zung}) (q:draft, low confidence)
zunglot = (i:1) (t:v) (w:uproot/pluck up/root out) (d:pull out by the roots; of people, remove them completely from their land) (s:zungbawh/botkhia/bawhkhiat) (a:suan) (q:draft)
zungpi = (i:1) (t:n) (w:root/main root) (d:<zung>, root, with <pi>, great: the main root that keeps the branches alive) (s:zung) (b:zung) (q:draft)
zungte = (i:1) (t:n) (w:roots) (d:plural of <zung>: the roots of a tree or plant) (b:zung) (q:draft)
zungthuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:take root/be rooted) (d:<zung>, root, with <thuk>, deep, used with <kha>: strike deep roots, be firmly rooted) (s:zungkha) (q:draft)
zungzung = (i:1) (t:adv) (w:very/exceedingly/so) (d:intensifier placed after a describing word: {nuam zungzung} very pleasant, {lim zungzung} very tasty, {khum zungzung} very sweet, {gim zungzung} very tiring) (s:mahmah) (q:draft)
zuphung = (i:1) (t:n) (w:banquet/feast) (d:found only in {zuphung pa}, the man in charge of a wedding feast, master of the banquet; <zu> is wine) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zur) (d:name of two men: a Midianite chief, father of Kozbi, killed by the Israelites, and a Benjamite of Gibeon, a brother of Kish) (r:4.31.8/13.8.30) (q:draft)
Zuriel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zuriel) (d:son of Abihail, leader of the Merarite clans of the Levites) (r:4.3.35)
Zurishaddai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zurishaddai) (d:father of Shelumiel, the leader of the tribe of Simeon in the wilderness) (r:4.1.6/4.10.19)
zusa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (w:mouse/rat) (d:small gnawing animal, a rat or mouse, counted among the unclean animals) (s:simbeng)
zusak = (i:1) (t:v) (w:drop/let fall/send down) (d:<zu>, fall, with the causative <sak>: make rain, hail or food fall from the sky) (s:zuksak/guahzusak) (b:zu)
zusak = (i:2) (t:v) (w:cause) (d:cause something to fall or come down from above, said of God sending rain, fire or manna) (b:zu)
zusakin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:raining down/sending rain/making fall) (d:<zusak>, cause to fall or rain, with the linking ending <in>: sending down, and so) (b:zusak) (q:draft)
zusuk = (i:1) (t:v) (w:fall/rain down/pour down) (d:<zu>, fall, said of rain, with <suk>, downward: pour down) (b:zu) (q:draft)
zut = (i:1) (t:n) (w:paint/coat/smear) (d:coat or smear a surface with pitch, plaster or the like)
zut = (i:2) (t:n) (w:cover/overlay/plate) (d:cover a surface with a layer of gold or bronze)
zute = (i:1) (t:n) (w:wines/drinks) (d:<zu> wine or fermented drink with the plural <te>; {leenggah zute} is wine of grapes) (b:zu) (q:draft)
zuthawl = (i:1) (t:n) (w:betrothal pledge/engagement) (d:pledge given to seal a promise of marriage, literally a flask of <zu>, rice beer; {zuthawl piaksa} means pledged to be married, betrothed) (q:draft, low confidence)
zutin = (i:1) (t:v) (w:overlay/smear/rub/paint) (d:<zut>, overlay or smear, with the linking ending {-in}: coat with gold, rub with oil, paint the eyes) (b:zut) (q:draft)
zutkhat = (t:todo) (r:24.46.22) (q:draft, one verse only, said of Egypt becoming like a fleeing snake where the NIV has hiss; cannot tell whether it names the sound or the gliding movement)
zutkhia = (t:see) <zutkhia-in>
zutkhia-in = (i:1) (t:v) (w:strip off/pull off) (d:connective form of <zutkhia>, from <zut> rub or strip with <khia> out: stripping fruit off a plant and then) (q:draft, low confidence)
zutna = (i:1) (t:n) (w:plaster/coating) (d:<zut>, smear, plaster or overlay, with the noun suffix <na>; the material for plastering a wall, or the overlaying of a surface) (s:kizutna) (b:zut) (q:draft)
zutsiang = (i:1) (t:adj) (w:burnished/polished) (d:apparently <zut> rub with <siang> clean: rubbed bright, said of bronze) (s:kinawtngil) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zuzim = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (w:Zuzites) (d:people living in Ham, east of the Jordan, who were defeated by Kedorlaomer) (r:1.14.5)
